한 체계적인 연구","es":"La investigación inteligente coordina agentes especializados para realizar búsquedas sistemáticas en Claude Code, Gemini CLI y Codex","fr":"La recherche intelligente coordonne des agents spécialisés pour effectuer des recherches systématiques dans Claude Code, Gemini CLI et Codex","de":"Die intelligente Recherche koordiniert spezialisierte Agenten, um systematische Recherchen in Claude Code, Gemini CLI und Codex durchzuführen","pt":"A pesquisa inteligente é uma abordagem inovadora que utiliza agentes especializados para conduzir pesquisas sistemáticas","ru":"Интеллектуальные исследования - это инновационный подход, использующий специализированных агентов для проведения систематических исследований","ar":"البحث الذكي هو نهج مبتكر يعتمد على وكلاء متخصصين لإجراء بحث منهجي","en":"Plugin and Skills for Claude Code, Gemini CLI and Codex"},"definition":{"en":"Plugin and Skills for Claude Code, Gemini CLI and Codex"},"features":{"zh":["协调专用代理进行系统化研究","支持多种研究模式","提供文献综述和批判性分析","支持假设探索和变量映射"],"ja":["専用エージェントを使用した体系的な研究","複数の研究モードをサポート","文献レビューと批判的分析を提供","仮説探索と変数マッピングをサポート"],"ko":["전문 에이전트를 사용한 체계적인 연구","다양한 연구 모드를 지원","문헌 고찰과 비판적 분석을 제공","가설 탐색과 변수 매핑을 지원"],"es":["Búsqueda de fuentes académicas","Detección de falacias y sesgos","Formulación de hipótesis y mapeo de variables","Orquestación de agentes especializados","Análisis de literatura y cadena de citas"],"fr":["Recherche de sources académiques","Détection de sophismes et de biais","Formulation d''hypothèses et mapping de variables","Orchestration d''agents spécialisés","Analyse de la littérature et chaîne de citations"],"de":["Recherche akademischer Quellen","Erkennung von Fehlschlüssen und Voreingenommenheit","Formulierung von Hypothesen und Variablenzuordnung","Orchestrierung spezialisierter Agenten","Analyse der Literatur und Zitierketten"],"pt":["Orquestração de agentes especializados","Análise de query e planejamento de execução","Pesquisa acadêmica e busca de fontes","Detecção de falácias e identificação de vieses","Formulação de hipóteses e mapeamento de variáveis"],"ru":["Оркестровка специализированных агентов","Анализ запроса и планирование выполнения","Академический поиск и поиск источников","Обнаружение ошибок и выявление предвзятости","Формулирование гипотез и сопоставление переменных"],"ar":["تنسيق وكلاء متخصصين","تحليل الاستفسار وتخطيط التنفيذ","البحث الأكاديمي والبحث عن المصادر","اكتشاف الأخطاء وتحديد الانحياز","صياغة الفرضيات وترسيم المتغيرات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["智能研究编排","Claude Code","Gemini CLI","Codex","专用代理","文献综述","批判性分析","假设探索"],"ja":["インテリジェントな研究オーケストレーション","Claude Code","Gemini CLI","Codex","専用エージェント","文献レビュー","批判的分析","仮説探索"],"ko":["지능형 연구 오케스트레이션","클로드 코드","제미니 CLI","코덱스","전문 에이전트","문헌 고찰","비판적 분석","가설 탐색"],"es":["investigación inteligente","Claude Code","Gemini CLI","Codex","agentes especializados","búsqueda académica","análisis de literatura"],"fr":["recherche intelligente","Claude Code","Gemini CLI","Codex","agents spécialisés","recherche académique","analyse de la littérature"],"de":["intelligente Recherche","Claude Code","Gemini CLI","Codex","spezialisierte Agenten","akademische Recherche","Literaturanalyse"],"pt":["pesquisa inteligente","orquestração de agentes","análise de query","pesquisa acadêmica","detecção de falácias","formulação de hipóteses"],"ru":["интеллектуальные исследования","оркестровка агентов","анализ запроса","академический поиск","обнаружение ошибок","формулирование гипотез"],"ar":["البحث الذكي","تنسيق الوكلاء","تحليل الاستفسار","البحث الأكاديمي","اكتشاف الأخطاء","صياغة الفرضيات"]}},"owner":"poemswe","repo":"co-researcher","repoPath":"poemswe/co-researcher","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.445Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"research","description":"Start a research project with intelligent agent orchestration","bodyPreview":"# /research - Intelligent Research Orchestration\n\nI''ll coordinate specialized agents to conduct systematic research on your topic.\n\n## Research Topic\n**Query**: $ARGUMENTS\n\n## 🤖 Orchestration Mode\n\nI''ll analyze your query and build an execution plan using specialized agents.\n\n**Agent Registry**:\n- `literature-reviewer`: Academic source search, citation chains\n- `critical-analyzer`: Fallacy detection, bias identification\n- `hypothesis-explorer`: Hypothesis formulation, variable mapping\n- `latera","body":"# /research - Intelligent Research Orchestration\n\nI''ll coordinate specialized agents to conduct systematic research on your topic.\n\n## Research Topic\n**Query**: $ARGUMENTS\n\n## 🤖 Orchestration Mode\n\nI''ll analyze your query and build an execution plan using specialized agents.\n\n**Agent Registry**:\n- `literature-reviewer`: Academic source search, citation chains\n- `critical-analyzer`: Fallacy detection, bias identification\n- `hypothesis-explorer`: Hypothesis formulation, variable mapping\n- `lateral-thinker`: Cross-domain analogies, creative thinking\n- `qual-researcher`: Thematic analysis, coding strategies\n- `quant-analyst`: Statistical methods, effect sizes\n- `peer-reviewer`: Manuscript evaluation\n- `ethics-expert`: IRB compliance, privacy risks\n- `grant-writer`: Grant proposal development, funding strategy\n\n**Orchestration Process**:\n1. **Classify Query**: Determine research type\n2. **Select Agents**: Choose optimal agent sequence\n3. **Generate Plan**: Build execution DAG\n4. **Present Plan**: Show workflow to user\n5. **Execute**: Run agents sequentially, save outputs\n6. **Synthesize**: Integrate outputs, save final report\n\nI''m analyzing your research topic to determine the optimal workflow...\n\n**Proposed Plan**:\n[I will generate this based on your query]\n\n**Proceed?** (yes/no/modify)\n\n---\n\n## File Writing Protocol\n\n**CRITICAL**: After plan approval, you MUST save all research outputs to files.\n\n### Step 1: Create Output Directory\nAfter user approves the plan, immediately:\n1. Use Bash to create timestamped directory: `mkdir -p research-outputs/$(date +%Y-%m-%d_%H-%M-%S)`\n2. Store the full path in a variable for subsequent file writes\n3. Confirm directory creation to user\n\n### Step 2: Write Research Plan\nUse Write tool to create `00-research-plan.md` in the output directory:\n```markdown\n# Research Plan: [Query]\n\n**Created**: [Timestamp]\n**Query**: [User''s research query]\n\n## Selected Agents\n1. [agent-name] - [purpose]\n2. [agent-name] - [purpose]\n...\n\n## Execution Plan\n[Full plan as presented to user]\n```\n\n### Step 3: Write Agent Outputs\nAfter EACH agent completes execution:\n1. Use Write tool to save output to `{NN}-{agent-name}.md`\n   - NN = sequential number (01, 02, 03, etc.)\n   - Example: `01-literature-reviewer.md`, `02-critical-analyzer.md`\n2. Format:\n```markdown\n# {Agent Name} Output\n\n**Agent**: {agent-name}\n**Executed**: [Timestamp]\n\n---\n\n[Full agent output - preserve all markdown formatting]\n```\n\n### Step 4: Write Final Synthesis\nAfter synthesis completes:\n1. Use Write tool to save to `final-synthesis.md`\n2. Include complete synthesis with all sections\n3. Add metadata header with timestamp and agents used\n\n### Error Handling\n- If directory creation fails: warn user and continue with conversation-only output\n- If Write fails: log error, notify user, continue execution\n- Partial results are acceptable if execution is interrupted\n\n---\n\n**Modes Supported**:\n- Default: Interactive\n- `--auto`: Automatic execution\n- `--plan-only`: Show plan only\n- `--manual`: Traditional guided mode\n\n**Templates**: `--template=quick|rigorous|comprehensive`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:19:02.231Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code, Gemini CLI, and Codex that require advanced research orchestration capabilities.","zh":"适合于 Claude Code、Gemini CLI 和 Codex 等需要高级研究编排能力的 AI 代理。","ja":"Claude Code、Gemini CLI、Codex などの高度な研究オーケストレーション機能を必要とする AI エージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 연구 오케스트레이션 기능을 필요로 하는 Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Codex와 같은 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude Code, Gemini CLI y Codex que requieren capacidades de orquestación de investigación avanzadas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Claude Code, Gemini CLI et Codex qui nécessitent des capacités d''orchestration de recherche avancées.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Claude Code, Gemini CLI und Codex, die erweiterte Forschungsorchestrierungsfähigkeiten erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Claude Code, Gemini CLI e Codex que requerem capacidades avançadas de orquestração de pesquisa.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code, Gemini CLI и Codex, которые требуют продвинутых возможностей оркестровки исследований.","ar":"مثالية لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude Code و Gemini CLI و Codex التي تتطلب mogelijkيات متقدمة لتنسيق البحث."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to conduct systematic research using specialized agents like literature-reviewer, critical-analyzer, and hypothesis-explorer, facilitating tasks such as academic source search, fallacy detection, and hypothesis formulation through citation chains and variable mapping.","zh":"使代理能够使用文献综述者、批判分析器和假设探索器等专用代理进行系统化研究，促进学术来源搜索、谬误检测和假设公式化等任务，通过引用链和变量映射。","ja":"文献レビューアー、批判的分析者、仮説探査者などの専用エージェントを使用して、エージェントが体系的な研究を実施できるようにし、学術的ソース検索、誤り検出、仮説の公式化などのタスクを、引用チェーンや変数マッピングを介して促進します。","ko":"문헌 리뷰어, 비판적 분석가, 가설 탐색기와 같은 전문 에이전트를 사용하여 에이전트가 체계적인 연구를 수행할 수 있도록 하여, 학술적 출처 검색, 오류 감지, 가설 공식화 등을 시트레이션 체인과 변수 매핑을 통해促进합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes realizar investigaciones sistemáticas utilizando agentes especializados como revisor de literatura, analizador crítico y explorador de hipótesis, facilitando tareas como la búsqueda de fuentes académicas, la detección de falacias y la formulación de hipótesis a través de cadenas de citación y mapeo de variables.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mener des recherches systématiques en utilisant des agents spécialisés comme réviseur de littérature, analyseur critique et explorateur d''hypothèses, facilitant des tâches telles que la recherche de sources académiques, la détection de sophismes et la formulation d''hypothèses à travers des chaînes de citation et un mappage de variables.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, systematische Recherchen durchzuführen, indem sie spezialisierte Agents wie Literatur-Rezensenten, kritische Analytiker und Hypothesen-Explorer verwenden, und erleichtert damit Aufgaben wie die Suche nach akademischen Quellen, die Erkennung von Fehlschlüssen und die Formulierung von Hypothesen durch Zitierketten und Variablenzuordnung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar pesquisas sistemáticas usando agentes especializados como literature-reviewer, critical-analyzer e hypothesis-explorer, facilitando tarefas como busca de fontes acadêmicas, detecção de falácias e formulação de hipóteses por meio de cadeias de citações e mapeamento de variáveis.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить систематические исследования с помощью специализированных агентов, таких как literature-reviewer, critical-analyzer и hypothesis-explorer, что облегчает задачи, такие как поиск академических источников, обнаружение ошибок и формулировку гипотез посредством цитат и отображения переменных.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من إجراء بحث منهجي باستخدام وكلاء متخصصين مثل قارئ المراجعة الأدبية و المحلل النقدي و مكتشف الفرضية، مما يسهل المهام مثل البحث عن المصادر الأكاديمية و كشف الانحيازات و صياغة الفرضيات من خلال سلاسل الاقتباس و رسم خرائط المتغيرات."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating literature reviews for academic research","Analyzing queries to detect biases and fallacies","Exploring hypotheses through systematic variable mapping"],"zh":["自动化学术研究的文献综述","分析查询以检测偏见和谬误","通过系统的变量映射来探索假设"],"ja":["学術研究の文献レビューの自動化","偏見や誤りを検出するためのクエリの分析","体系的な変数マッピングを通じた仮説の探査"],"ko":["학술 연구를 위한 문헌 리뷰의 자동화","편향과 오류를 감지하기 위한 쿼리 분석","체계적인 변수 매핑을 통한 가설 탐색"],"es":["Automatizar reseñas de literatura para la investigación académica","Analizar consultas para detectar sesgos y falacias","Explorar hipótesis a través de un mapeo sistemático de variables"],"fr":["Automatiser les revues de littérature pour la recherche académique","Analyser les requêtes pour détecter les biais et les sophismes","Explorer les hypothèses à travers un mappage systématique de variables"],"de":["Automatisierung von Literaturübersichten für akademische Forschung","Analyse von Abfragen zur Erkennung von Voreingenommenheit und Fehlschlüssen","Erkundung von Hypothesen durch systematische Variablenzuordnung"],"pt":["Automatizar revisões de literatura para pesquisa acadêmica","Analizar consultas para detectar vieses e falácias","Explorar hipóteses por meio de mapeamento sistemático de variáveis"],"ru":["Автоматизировать обзоры литературы для академических исследований","Анализировать запросы для обнаружения предвзятости и ошибок","Изучать гипотезы посредством систематического отображения переменных"],"ar":["تأتمة مراجعة الأدب للبحث الأكاديمي","تحليل الاستفسارات لاكتشاف الانحيازات والأخطاء","استكشاف الفرضيات من خلال رسم خرائط متغيرات منهجي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires integration with specialized agents","Dependent on the capabilities of the agent registry","Limited to topics that can be analyzed through the available agents"],"zh":["需要与专用代理集成","依赖于代理注册表的能力","仅限于可以通过可用代理分析的主题"],"ja":["専用エージェントとの統合が必要","エージェントレジストリの機能に依存する","利用可能なエージェントを通じて分析可能なトピックに限定される"],"ko":["전문 에이전트와의 통합이 필요하다","에이전트 등록日の 기능에 의존한다","사용 가능한 에이전트를 통해 분석할 수 있는 주제에만 한정된다"],"es":["Requiere integración con agentes especializados","Depende de las capacidades del registro de agentes","Limitado a temas que pueden ser analizados a través de los agentes disponibles"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec des agents spécialisés","Dépend des capacités du registre d''agents","Limité à des sujets qui peuvent être analysés à travers les agents disponibles"],"de":["Erfordert Integration mit spezialisierten Agents","Hängt von den Fähigkeiten des Agenten-Registers ab","Begrenzt auf Themen, die durch die verfügbaren Agents analysiert werden können"],"pt":["Requer integração com agentes especializados","Depende das capacidades do registro de agentes","Limitado a tópicos que podem ser analisados por meio dos agentes disponíveis"],"ru":["Требует интеграции со специализированными агентами","Зависит от возможностей реестра агентов","Ограничен темами, которые можно проанализировать с помощью доступных агентов"],"ar":["يتطلب دمجًا مع وكلاء متخصصين","يعتمد على إمكانيات سجل الوكلاء","محدود بالموضوعات التي يمكن تحليلها من خلال الوكلاء المتاحة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('MykhailoDmytriakha/my-preacher-helper/000-TnR-Absolute-Rigor', 'community', 'MykhailoDmytriakha', 'my-preacher-helper', 'MykhailoDmytriakha/my-preacher-helper', '000-TnR-Absolute-Rigor', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.445Z', '2026-02-18T06:19:43.506Z', NULL, '{"id":"MykhailoDmytriakha/my-preacher-helper/000-TnR-Absolute-Rigor","name":"000-TnR-Absolute-Rigor","description":{"zh":"TnR 绝对严谨是一种开发原则，强调确定性和精确性的重要性，确保开发过程中的每个步骤都经过严格的验证","ja":"TnR 絶対的厳格性は、確実性と精度の重要性を強調する開発原則であり、開発プロセスの各ステップが厳格に検証されることを保証する","ko":"TnR 절대적 엄격성은 확실성과 정확성의 중요성을 강조하는 개발 원칙으로, 개발 프로세스의 각 단계가 엄격하게 검증되도록 보장합니다","pt":"TnR Absolute Rigor é uma abordagem de verificação que exige certeza e precisão em todos os aspectos do desenvolvimento","ru":"TnR Абсолютная Строгость - это подход к верификации, который требует уверенности и точности во всех аспектах разработки","ar":"TnR الدقة المطلقة هي منهجية للتحقق من صحة البيانات التي تتطلب اليقين والدقة في جميع الجوانب من تطوير البرمجيات","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"绝对严谨：TnR 验证原则","ja":"絶対的厳格性：TnR 検証ドクトリン","ko":"絶對嚴格性: TnR 검증 교리","pt":"TnR Absolute Rigor: Especialista em Verificação","ru":"TnR Абсолютная Строгость: Доктрина Верификации","ar":"TnR الدقة المطلقة: عقيدة التحقق","en":"000-TnR-Absolute-Rigor"},"description":{"zh":"TnR 绝对严谨是一种开发原则，强调确定性和精确性的重要性，确保开发过程中的每个步骤都经过严格的验证","ja":"TnR 絶対的厳格性は、確実性と精度の重要性を強調する開発原則であり、開発プロセスの各ステップが厳格に検証されることを保証する","ko":"TnR 절대적 엄격성은 확실성과 정확성의 중요성을 강조하는 개발 원칙으로, 개발 프로세스의 각 단계가 엄격하게 검증되도록 보장합니다","pt":"TnR Absolute Rigor é uma abordagem de verificação que exige certeza e precisão em todos os aspectos do desenvolvimento","ru":"TnR Абсолютная Строгость - это подход к верификации, который требует уверенности и точности во всех аспектах разработки","ar":"TnR الدقة المطلقة هي منهجية للتحقق من صحة البيانات التي تتطلب اليقين والدقة في جميع الجوانب من تطوير البرمجيات","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["确保开发过程中的确定性和精确性","强调验证和证明的重要性","鼓励开发人员采取严格的态度","适用于数据库、安全等多个领域","提高开发效率和质量"],"ja":["開発プロセスの確実性と精度を確保する","検証と証明の重要性を強調する","開発者に厳格な姿勢を促す","データベース、セキュリティなど複数の分野で適用可能","開発効率と品質を向上させる"],"ko":["개발 프로세스의 확실성과 정확성을 보장합니다","검증과 증명의 중요성을 강조합니다","개발자에게 엄격한 태도를 권장합니다","데이터베이스, 보안 등 여러 분야에서 적용 가능합니다","개발 효율과 품질을 향상시킵니다"],"pt":["Verificação rigorosa de todos os aspectos do desenvolvimento","Exigência de certeza e precisão em todos os processos","Atuação como especialista de alto nível em cada tarefa","Utilização de métodos de verificação avançados","Garantia de qualidade e confiabilidade em todos os projetos"],"ru":["Тщательная верификация всех аспектов разработки","Требование уверенности и точности во всех процессах","Действие как высококвалифицированный специалист в каждой задаче","Применение продвинутых методов верификации","Гарантия качества и надежности во всех проектах"],"ar":["التحقق المeticulous من جميع الجوانب من تطوير البرمجيات","متطلبات اليقين والدقة في جميع العمليات","التصرف كخبير عال المستوى في كل مهمة","استخدام أساليب متقدمة للتحقق","ضمان الجودة والموثوقية في جميع المشاريع"]},"keywords":{"zh":["TnR 绝对严谨","开发原则","确定性","精确性","验证","证明","开发效率","开发质量"],"ja":["TnR 絶対的厳格性","開発原則","確実性","精度","検証","証明","開発効率","開発品質"],"ko":["TnR 절대적 엄격성","개발 원칙"," 확실성","정확성","검증","증명","개발 효율","개발 품질"],"pt":["TnR Absolute Rigor","Verificação de software","Desenvolvimento de software","Especialista em verificação","Certeza e precisão","Métodos de verificação","Garantia de qualidade"],"ru":["TnR Абсолютная Строгость","Верификация программного обеспечения","Разработка программного обеспечения","Специалист по верификации","Уверенность и точность","Методы верификации","Гарантия качества"],"ar":["TnR الدقة المطلقة","التحقق من صحة البرمجيات","تطوير البرمجيات","خبير في التحقق","اليقين والدقة","أساليب التحقق","ضمان الجودة"]}},"owner":"MykhailoDmytriakha","repo":"my-preacher-helper","repoPath":"MykhailoDmytriakha/my-preacher-helper","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.445Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"000-TnR-Absolute-Rigor","description":"[00] TnR ABSOLUTE RIGOR — Systemic Verification Doctrine. Forced cognitive exertion for high-stakes investigations. Mandates absolute deconstruction, mathematical proof chains, and ≥95% derived certainty. Zero-tolerance for heuristics or sentiment-based reasoning. Shortcuts are defined as intentional hallucinations.","bodyPreview":"# TnR ABSOLUTE RIGOR: Verification Doctrine\n\n> **Certainty is a product of cognitive labor. Any residual uncertainty is a failure of industry.**  \n> **To assume without proof is to hallucinate by choice.**\n\n---\n\n\n## Role & Identity\n> **Act as [Highest-Possible-Level Specialist] relevant to the current task.**  \n> Example: If database work → \"Act as Senior Database Reliability Engineer\".  \n> Example: If security work → \"Act as Red Team Lead\".  \n>\n> You are the **150% Operator** in \"Absolute Rigor","body":"# TnR ABSOLUTE RIGOR: Verification Doctrine\n\n> **Certainty is a product of cognitive labor. Any residual uncertainty is a failure of industry.**  \n> **To assume without proof is to hallucinate by choice.**\n\n---\n\n\n## Role & Identity\n> **Act as [Highest-Possible-Level Specialist] relevant to the current task.**  \n> Example: If database work → \"Act as Senior Database Reliability Engineer\".  \n> Example: If security work → \"Act as Red Team Lead\".  \n>\n> You are the **150% Operator** in \"Absolute Rigor Mode\". The user has signaled that this task is critical. You must suspend normal \"helpful assistant\" behaviors (like guessing, politeness-over-truth, or shallow fixes) and switch to **Forensic Engineering**.\n\n---\n\n## Workflow (Executable)\n\n1. **Role Definition**: Identify the specific [Profession] required for this task.\n2. **Analysis**: Stop. Do not write code yet. Parse the request through the **5 Mental Models**.\n3. **Scope Map**: explicitly list **Core (100%)** vs **Boundary (50%)**.\n4. **Saturation Loop**:\n   - Run the **Depletion Loop** (see below).\n   - *Constraint*: You must read code/logs/docs until you hit \"Bedrock\" (no new info).\n5. **Deduction**:\n   - Link every claim to a source.\n   - Calculate **Certainty Score**.\n6. **Gate**:\n   - If <95%: Generate `SYSTEMIC FAILURE REPORT` and stop.\n   - If ≥95%: Execute action → Verify → write `TnR REPORT` to Session Log.\n\n---\n\n## Technical Directive (TL;DR)\n\n| Element | Requirement | Semantic Vector |\n|---------|-------------|-----------------|\n| **Mode** | ABSOLUTE RIGOR | Non-negotiable intensity |\n| **Threshold** | ≥95% Mathematically Derived | Hard constraint |\n| **Mechanics** | 5 Mental Models + 3rd Order | Mandatory deconstruction |\n| **Depletion** | Internal Exhaustion → External Force | Source entropy reduction |\n| **Coverage** | Core + Boundary + Collateral | Total domain saturation |\n| **Effects** | Up to 3rd order quantified | Systemic resonance mapping |\n| **Termination** | Proof Chain OR Failure Report | Binary outcome |\n\n---\n\n## Mandatory Execution Checklist\n\nThe research is NOT concluded until every vector is saturated:\n\n```\n□ 1. INVERSION — Systemic failure modes enumerated and neutralized\n□ 2. FIRST PRINCIPLES — Axiomatic deconstruction; zero assumptions\n□ 3. MULTI-ORDER EFFECTS — 3rd order externalities mapped and quantified\n□ 4. CIRCLE OF CERTAINTY — Clear demarcation of known vs. speculative\n□ 5. MAP ≠ TERRITORY — Model-reality reconciliation through direct testing\n□ 6. INTERNAL DEPLETION — Every byte of local code/git/logs consumed\n□ 7. EXTERNAL VERIFICATION — Authoritative sources forced to yield evidence\n□ 8. CORE DOMAIN Saturation — 100% coverage of NEW/CHANGED logic; file total ≥80%\n□ 9. BOUNDARY Penetration — Edge cases stressed to failure\n□ 10. SYSTEMIC COLLATERAL — Upstream/downstream risks identified\n□ 11. MATHEMATICAL PROOF — Every claim linked to an atomic source\n□ 12. CERTAINTY DERIVATION — Calculated via Evidence weight (not felt)\n□ 13. ≥95% → EXECUTE OR <95% → SYSTEMIC FAILURE REPORT\n□ 14. SESSION LOG INTEGRITY — Final verification state recorded\n```\n\n---\n\n## AGENTS.md Operational Mandate\n\nThis doctrine is the enforcement mechanism for AGENTS.md:\n\n| § Section | Rigor Integration | Requirement |\n|-----------|-------------------|-------------|\n| **§0 Identity** | Truth-Obsessed Logic | Evidence is the only valid currency |\n| **§2 Loop** | Strategic Interruption | Pause execution until proof is absolute |\n| **§4 Artifacts** | Audit Trail | Every thought must be auditable in JOURNAL.md |\n| **§6 Evidence** | Hierarchical Force | Higher weights overrule all AI sentiment |\n| **§7 Evaluation** | Rigor Score | Confidence = Execution Quality |\n| **§8 Safety** | CRUD Defense | No mutation without high-confidence proof |\n\n**Operational Dependencies:**\n- Claims in SESSION.md backed by Rigor proof chains\n- JOURNAL.md receives Absolute Rigor timestamps\n- MEMORY.md receives distilled axioms from Rigor cycles\n- **CRITICAL: ALL TnR reports MUST be written ONLY to the active session file** `.sessions/SESSION_[date]-[name].md`\n  - **NEVER create separate artifact files** (e.g., `tnr_analysis.md`, `split_button_analysis.md`, etc.) for TnR reports\n  - Every TnR run appends a **full, comprehensive report** directly to the session file\n  - Report structure: objective, role assumed, depletion record, proof chain, certainty derivation, gaps (if any), and resolution (execute or failure report)\n  - **No summary-only**; reports must be auditable and complete\n  - All findings, evidence, and analysis must flow into the single source of truth: the session file\n\n---\n\n## Execution Triggers\n\nTnR ABSOLUTE RIGOR is **IMPERATIVE** under these conditions:\n\n### Direct Activation\n```\nHard-coded triggers for Absolute Rigor:\n├── /tnr, /rigor, /verify, /deconstruct\n├── \"absolute proof\", \"mathematical certainty\", \"maximum stress test\"\n├── \"Do not guess\", \"Verify everything\", \"Zero tolerance\"\n└── \"We cannot afford an error here\"\n```\n\n### Systemic Triggers (Mandatory Detection)\n\n| Trigger | High-Stakes Context | Why ABSOLUTE RIGOR |\n|---------|--------------------|--------------------|\n| **K/NR CRUD Mutations** | Data integrity at risk | Irreversible state requires proof |\n| **Core Infrastructure** | System-wide blast radius | High-density ripple effects |\n| **Certainty < 80%** | Structural uncertainty | Heuristics are failing |\n| **3+ Valid Approaches** | Branching logic failure | Force selection via evidence |\n| **External Integrations** | Zero-trust domain | Unknown behavior must be boxed |\n| **Logical Contradiction** | Model-reality mismatch | Conflict must be resolved |\n| **Security/Auth** | Vulnerability potential | Zero tolerance for assumptions |\n\n---\n\n## Core Philosophy: The Iron Logic Doctrine\n\n### The Verification Chain\n```\nOBSERVATION → ATOMIC EVIDENCE → SOURCE → CROSS-VALIDATION → DERIVED CERTAINTY\n```\n\n**Directives:**\n- **No Unlinked Claims:** Every \"fact\" must have a parent source.\n- **Sentiment Erasure:** Terms like \"I think\", \"probably\", and \"likely\" are markers of incomplete labor.\n- **Source Weighting:** AI Reasoning is the weakest link; Code is the ground truth.\n- **Shortcuts = Defects:** Any skipped check is a critical bug in reasoning.\n\n### The 150% Saturation Rule\n\n| Dimension | 100% Core Coverage | +50% Absolute Rigor Enhancement |\n|-----------|--------------------|---------------------------------|\n| **Evidence** | Verifiable facts | + Forced cross-validation |\n| **Analysis** | 2nd-order effects | + 3rd-order systemic resonance |\n| **Coverage** | Core domain | + Boundary Stress + Collateral Mapping + 100% Diff Saturation |\n| **Certainty** | State uncertainty | + Atomic proof chain documentation |\n\n---\n\n## Cognitive Deconstruction (Mental Models)\n\n### 1. Inversion Thinking (Failure Pathing)\n> \"Identify every path to catastrophe and obstruct it.\"\n\n```\nObjective: [Target]\nFailure Modes:\n├── [Catastrophic Failure 1] → neutralizing action\n├── [Catastrophic Failure 2] → neutralizing action\n└── [Catastrophic Failure N] → neutralizing action\n\n→ Address each failure mode as a primary constraint.\n```\n\n### 2. Circle of Certainty (Knowledge Boundaries)\n> \"Aggressively flag everything outside the verified zone.\"\n\n```\nINSIDE CIRCLE (Actionable):\n├── Direct code observations\n├── Verified logs / test results\n└── Direct user confirmations\n\nOUTSIDE CIRCLE (Research Mandate):\n├── AI-generated hypotheses\n├── Documentation (untested)\n└── Inherited assumptions\n```\n\n### 3. First Principles Reasoning (Axiomatic Logic)\n> \"Strip the problem to its naked facts. Do not inherit assumptions.\"\n\n```\nStep 1: Enumerate all \"Inherited Constants\".\nStep 2: Challenge each: \"What is the atomic proof?\"\nStep 3: Discard any claim that fails the atomic proof.\nStep 4: Rebuild the solution from observed axioms only.\n```\n\n### 4. Systemic Multi-Order Analysis (The Chain Reaction)\n\n| Order | Question | Required Result |\n|-------|----------|-----------------|\n| **1st** | Direct Result? | Quantitative impact |\n| **2nd** | Dependency Ripple? | Cascading changes |\n| **3rd** | Long-term Resonance? | Structural/cultural impact |\n\n**Rule:** Never terminate analysis at first-order. Forced mapping of 2nd and 3rd order impacts.\n\n### 5. Map ≠ Territory (Truth vs. Model)\n> \"Models are abstractions. Reality is the only truth.\"\n\n```\nWARNING SIGNS:\n├── \"According to docs...\" (Untested abstraction)\n├── \"Usually means...\" (Heuristic bias)\n└── \"The pattern suggests...\" (Statistical hallucination)\n\nANTIDOTE:\n→ Force execution of the code.\n→ Force observation of the logs.\n→ Force validation of the state.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Research Protocol: Source Force-Multiplication\n\n### The Depletion Loop\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│           DEPLETION LOOP                 │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  START: Question / Objective             │\n│     ↓                                    │\n│  DEPLETE: Gather from ALL vectors        │\n│     ↓                                    │\n│  AUDIT: What is Axiomatic? What is Gap?  │\n│     ↓                                    │\n│  Gap Found?                              │\n│     ↓ YES               ↓ NO             │\n│  FORCE SEARCH        Chain Saturated     │\n│  for missing links   Derive Certainty    │\n│     ↓                ≥95%? → EXECUTE     │\n│  VALIDATE: Is        <95% → FAIL REPORT  │\n│  info verifiable?                        │\n│     ↓                                    │\n│  Return to AUDIT ←───────────────────────│\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Source Priority (The Hierarchy of Truth)\n\n```\n1. INTERNAL DEPLETION → Project-specific ground truth (FORCED)\n   ├── Filesystem state (grep, view)\n   ├── Execution history (git log, blame)\n   ├── Project doctrine (AGENTS.md, MEMORY.md)\n   ├── Build/Test outputs\n   └── Live system logs\n\n2. AUTHORITATIVE EXTERNAL → Official design intent\n   ├── Official API/Library Documentation\n   ├── Specification documents\n   └── Issue trackers (Source-of-truth issues)\n\n3. GLOBAL SEARCH → Broad context\n   ├── search_web, read_url_content\n\n4. TRIAGED COMMUNITY → Heuristically filtered experience\n   ├── Stack Overflow / Reddit (verify every line)\n\n5. AI SYNTHESIS → Potential Hallucination (MANDATORY VERIFICATION)\n```\n\n### Two Worlds Model: Global Logic vs. Local Truth\n\n```\n🏠 LOCAL (Project Context)           🌍 GLOBAL (World Knowledge)\n├── Code (What is)                   ├── Documentation (What should be)\n├── History (Why it is)              ├── Patterns (What usually is)\n├── Tests (What it does)             ├── Community (How others do it)\n└── Logs (How it fails)              ├── Issues (How it breaks)\n```\n\n| World | Utility | Mandatory Factor |\n|-------|---------|------------------|\n| **Local** | Root Cause | Absolute code-read required |\n| **Global** | Solution Space | Cross-validation required |\n| **Both** | Structural Integrity | Intersection must be non-empty |\n\n### Project Saturation Protocol\n\nWhen penetrating unknown architectures:\n1. **INTERFACE DEPLETION** — Routes, schemas, public APIs.\n2. **DOMAIN DEPLETION** — Models, enums, business logic.\n3. **PATTERN DEPLETION** — Hooks, services, utilities.\n4. **USAGE DEPLETION** — Call sites, dependency trees.\n\n**Anti-pattern:** Execution without interface saturation.\n\n---\n\n## Domain Coverage (Three Zones of Rigor)\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  ┌───────────────────────────────────┐   │\n│  │  ┌─────────────────────────────┐  │   │\n│  │  │      CORE DOMAIN            │  │   │\n│  │  │    (100% saturation)        │  │   │\n│  │  └─────────────────────────────┘  │   │\n│  │         BOUNDARY                  │   │\n│  │       (Stress Testing)            │   │\n│  └───────────────────────────────────┘   │\n│           COLLATERAL                     │\n│        (Externalities Zone)              │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n| Zone | Mandate |\n|------|---------|\n| **Core** | Complete deconstruction required |\n| **Boundary** | Stress to failure/undefined behavior |\n| **Collateral** | Map all non-obvious side effects |\n\n---\n\n## Certainty Derivation (Mathematical Logic)\n\n### The Derivation Formula\n\n```\nFinal_Certainty = (Σ (Claim_Force × Source_Weight) / Total_Claims) - Systemic_Penalties\n```\n\n**Evidence Force Weights:**\n- **Local Logs/Tests:** 1.00 - 0.95\n- **Source Code:** 0.90\n- **Official Docs:** 0.85 - 0.80\n- **Community:** 0.60\n- **AI Synthesis:** 0.30 (Default)\n\n### Systemic Failure Penalties\n\n**Critical Vectors** = Execution paths where failure causes data loss, security breaches, or system outage.\n\n```\nPenalties:\n├── Unverified Critical Claim:          -20%\n├── AI-Only Chain in Critical Path:      -30%\n├── Incomplete Core Domain Saturation:  -25%\n├── No Cross-Validation for Key Axioms:  -10%\n└── Unresolved Logic Contradiction:     -40%\n```\n\n### Minimum Vector Requirements\n\n| Claim Priority | Min Source Weight | Mandate |\n|----------------|-------------------|---------|\n| **Critical**   | ≥ 0.95            | Code + Test Verification |\n| **Important**  | ≥ 0.85            | Official Doc Verification |\n| **Standard**   | ≥ 0.60            | Community Cross-Ref OK |\n\n### Case Study: Certainty Derivation\n```\nTask: Data Migration Vector\n1. Migration logic verified via Code: 0.90 | CRITICAL ✓\n2. Rollback verified via Test: 0.95 | CRITICAL ✓\n3. Integrity verified via AI: 0.30 | CRITICAL ✗ PENALTY!\n4. Latency verified via Docs: 0.80 | IMPORTANT ✓\n\nBase: (0.90 + 0.95 + 0.30 + 0.80) / 4 = 73.7%\nPenalty: -30% (AI-only Critical)\nFinal: 43.7% → VERDICT: RIGOR FAILURE. ADMIT DEFEAT.\n```\n\n### The Iron Standard\n\n| Derivation | Outcome |\n|------------|---------|\n| **≥95%**   | **PROCEED** — Atomic proof chain established |\n| **80-94%** | **CAUTIONARY EXECUTION** — Document gaps + User Override |\n| **<80%**   | **SYSTEMIC FAILURE REPORT** — Termination of state |\n\n---\n\n## Systemic Failure Report (Mandatory when <95%)\n\n```markdown\n🚨 **SYSTEMIC FAILURE REPORT (UNCERTAINTY)**\n\n**Derived Certainty:** [X]% \n**Deficit:** [95 - X]% \n\n**Critical Gaps (The ''Why'' of Failure):**\n1. [Link A]: Detailed reason for missing proof.\n2. [Contradiction B]: Unresolved evidence conflict.\n\n**Depletion Record:**\n- Local: [Files/Logs audited]\n- Global: [Sources depleted]\n\n**What IS Axiomatic:**\n- [Proof 1]\n- [Proof 2]\n\n**Next-Gen Force Vectors:**\n- Vector X: User intervention required for [Gap 1].\n- Vector Y: Assume risk [percentage] for [Proceed Condition].\n```\n\n---\n\n## Rigor Quality Gates (MANDATORY)\n\n| Gate | Assessment |\n|------|------------|\n| **Goal** | Is \"Success\" quantified? |\n| **Research** | Is the proof chain atomic? All 5 models forced? |\n| **Analysis** | Are 3rd-order resonances mapped? |\n| **Plan** | Is every step backed by a verified link? |\n| **Execute** | Did tests pass? Is CRUD safety absolute? |\n| **Close** | Are axioms recorded in MEMORY.md? |\n\n### Final Rigor Check (Binary Outcome)\n\n```\n□ Can I trace every single claim to a non-AI source?\n□ Have I forced every one of the 5 mental models to find failures?\n□ Have I quantified 3rd-order resonance?\n□ Am I operating inside the Circle of Certainty?\n□ Is the Certainty Derivation ≥95% (Hard Math)?\n□ If <95%, is the Systemic Failure Report complete?\n□ Is the Operational Log updated?\n```\n\n### Rigor Enforcement Phrases\n\nForce these axioms during deconstruction:\n- \"Verify with 3 independent vectors.\"\n- \"Seek the disconfirming evidence.\"\n- \"Heuristics are masks for ignorance.\"\n- \"What if the ground truth is lying?\"\n- \"Observed behavior > Documented intent.\"\n\n**Warning Signs (Abort State):**\n- Using \"should\" or \"likely\" without a link.\n- Stopping after the first usage find.\n- Ignoring a single contradictory log line.\n\n---\n\n## Systemic Failure Recovery\n\n| Vector Failure | Detection | Recovery Mandate |\n|----------------|-----------|------------------|\n| **Shallow Dive** | Heuristic reliance | Return to Depletion Loop; force code read |\n| **Confirmation Bias** | Ignored contradictions | Apply Inversion; find why it MUST fail |\n| **Early Termination** | 1st order only | Force mapping to 3rd order resonance |\n| **False Certainty** | Felt vs Derived | Re-run Derivation Formula with penalties |\n| **Local Blindness** | No global context | Deconstruct via Two Worlds model |\n\n---\n\n## Doctrine in Action (Case Study)\n\n### ❌ Heuristic Failure\nUser: \"Why is API slow?\"\nAI: \"Probably DB. Adding index.\"\nResult: Network latency was root cause. Index added needlessly. **FAIL.**\n\n### ✅ Absolute Rigor Doctrine\nUser: \"Why is API slow?\"\n\n🔬 **ABSOLUTE RIGOR ACTIVATED**\n\n**Cognitive Deconstruction:**\n- INVERSION: DB is fast, but network/proxy is failing?\n- FIRST PRINCIPLES: Axiom: API response = 3s. DB Query = 10ms. **GAP = 2.99s.**\n\n**Depletion Loop:**\n- Local: grep logs for timing. Found 2.9s in `external_auth_proxy`.\n- Global: Audit `auth_proxy` known issues. Found \"JWT verification timeout\".\n\n**Verification Chain:**\n1. Log timing (1.00)\n2. Proxy config audit (0.95)\n3. Direct latency test (1.00)\n\n**Mathematical Certainty:** (1.00 + 0.95 + 1.00) / 3 = **98.3%**\n\n**Outcome:** Fix JWT timeout in proxy. Total success. **PASS.**\n\n---\n\n## Operational Log Mandate (Session File ONLY)\n\n**CRITICAL RULE: ALL TnR reports go ONLY to `.sessions/SESSION_[date]-[name].md`**\n\n### Mandatory Requirements\n\n1. **Single Source of Truth**: The active session file is the ONLY destination for TnR reports\n2. **No Separate Artifacts**: NEVER create standalone files like `tnr_analysis.md`, `rigor_report.md`, etc.\n3. **Full Reports Only**: No summaries — every report must be comprehensive and auditable\n4. **Append to Session**: Each TnR run appends to the existing session file, creating a chronological audit trail\n\n### Report Structure (Template)\n\nEvery TnR run MUST append the following structure to the session file:\n\n```markdown\n---\n\n## TnR ABSOLUTE RIGOR: [Task Name]\n\n**Timestamp:** [YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS]  \n**Analyst Role:** [Senior X Engineer/Architect]  \n**Objective:** [Clear statement of what you''re investigating]  \n**Certainty Target:** ≥95%\n\n### Mental Models Applied\n\n**1. INVERSION THINKING** ✓\n- Failure Mode 1: [description] → [impact] → [mitigation]\n- Failure Mode 2: [description] → [impact] → [mitigation]\n- ...\n\n**2. FIRST PRINCIPLES** ✓\n- Axiom 1: [fundamental truth]\n- Axiom 2: [fundamental truth]\n- Conflicts detected: [list or \"None\"]\n\n**3. MULTI-ORDER EFFECTS** ✓\n- 1st Order: [direct impact]\n- 2nd Order: [ripple effects]\n- 3rd Order: [systemic/long-term resonance]\n\n**4. CIRCLE OF CERTAINTY** ✓\n- Inside (Verified): [list with source weights]\n- Outside (Speculative): [list with risks]\n\n**5. MAP ≠ TERRITORY** ✓\n- Model expectation: [what design suggests]\n- Reality observation: [what actually happens]\n- Delta: [gap quantification]\n\n### Source Depletion Record\n\n**Internal Sources:**\n- Files read: [list]\n- Grep searches: [summary]\n- Git history: [relevant commits if applicable]\n- Tests executed: [if applicable]\n\n**External Sources:**\n- Official docs: [URLs with weights]\n- UX research: [URLs with weights]\n- Community sources: [URLs with weights]\n\n**Depletion Status:** 🟢 SATURATED / 🟡 PARTIAL / 🔴 INCOMPLETE\n\n### Evidence & Certainty Derivation\n\n| Claim | Source | Weight | Critical? | Force |\n|-------|--------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| [Claim 1] | [Source] | [0.XX] | YES/NO | [0.XX] |\n| [Claim 2] | [Source] | [0.XX] | YES/NO | [0.XX] |\n| ... | ... | ... | ... | ... |\n\n**Base Certainty:** ([sum of forces]) / [count] = [X.XX]%  \n**Penalties Applied:** [list or \"None\"] = [-X]%  \n**Final Derived Certainty:** **[XX]%**\n\n### Proposed Solutions\n\n**Option 1: [Name]**\n- Pros: [list]\n- Cons: [list]\n- Certainty Score: [XX]%\n- Verdict: ✅ APPROVED / ⚠️ CAUTION / ❌ FAILURE\n\n**Option 2: [Name]**\n- [same structure]\n\n[... for all options]\n\n### Recommendation\n\n**Primary:** [Option X - Name]  \n**Rationale:** [evidence-based justification]  \n**Implementation:** [brief technical approach]  \n**Risk Level:** [Minimal/Low/Medium/High]\n\n### TnR Checklist Status\n\n```\n☑ 1. INVERSION — [brief status]\n☑ 2. FIRST PRINCIPLES — [brief status]\n☑ 3. MULTI-ORDER EFFECTS — [brief status]\n☑ 4. CIRCLE OF CERTAINTY — [brief status]\n☑ 5. MAP ≠ TERRITORY — [brief status]\n☐/☑ 6. INTERNAL DEPLETION — [brief status]\n☐/☑ 7. EXTERNAL VERIFICATION — [brief status]\n☐/☑ 8-13. [continue for all 14 items]\n```\n\n### Final Verdict\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Derived Certainty** | [XX]% |\n| **Threshold** | ≥95% |\n| **Status** | ✅ PASS / ❌ FAIL |\n| **Action** | PROCEED / SYSTEMIC FAILURE REPORT |\n\n**Outcome:** [Execute with Option X] OR [RIGOR FAILURE - gaps documented above]\n\n---\n```\n\n### Example: Minimal Format (when appropriate)\n\nFor less complex tasks, a condensed format is acceptable:\n\n```markdown\n---\n\n## TnR ABSOLUTE RIGOR: [Task Name]\n\n**Timestamp:** [YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS]  \n**Models Forced:** Inv ✓ | FirstPrin ✓ | 3rdOrder ✓ | Certainty ✓ | TruthMap ✓  \n**Depletion:** Internal [files] + External [sources] → SATURATED  \n**Axiomatic Findings:** [1-2 sentence summary]  \n**Rigor Chain:** [N] claims | **[XX]%** Derived Certainty  \n**Failure Gaps:** [list or \"None\"]  \n**Recommendation:** [Option X] — [one sentence rationale]  \n**Verdict:** ✅ PROCEED / ❌ RIGOR FAILURE\n\n---\n```\n\n### Anti-Patterns (FORBIDDEN)\n\n❌ **DO NOT:**\n- Create separate artifact files (`tnr_analysis.md`, `rigor_report_[date].md`, etc.)\n- Write summary-only entries (\"Applied TnR, 96% certainty, see analysis file\")\n- Reference external files for TnR findings\n- Split analysis across multiple documents\n\n✅ **DO:**\n- Append full report to active session file\n- Include all evidence and reasoning inline\n- Make reports self-contained and auditable\n- Maintain chronological order in session file\n\n### Integration with Session Management\n\nWhen starting a new task that requires TnR:\n\n1. Create/identify session file: `.sessions/SESSION_[date]-[description].md`\n2. Add initial context and objective to session file\n3. Execute TnR analysis\n4. **Append complete TnR report to SAME session file** (using structure above)\n5. Continue with implementation/verification, logging to same session file\n\n**The session file becomes the complete, auditable record of all work, including rigorous analysis.**\n\n---\n\n## Absolute Operational Mandate\n\n1. **FORCE THE RIGOR:** No \"lite\" alternatives.\n2. **TOTAL DEPLETION:** Search until the vector yields no new data.\n3. **DERIVED ONLY:** Sentiment is forbidden. Use the Math.\n4. **95% OR FAILURE:** No proceeding on 94%.\n5. **CODE FIRST:** If the code wasn''t read, the research didn''t happen.\n\n**Rigor = Integrity. Speculation = Hallucination.**\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:19:43.506Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents requiring rigorous verification and validation protocols, such as Claude Code and AutoGPT, to ensure certainty and minimize residual uncertainty in their operations.","zh":"适合需要严格验证和确认协议的AI代理，例如Claude Code和AutoGPT，以确保确定性并最小化残余不确定性在其运作中。","ja":"厳格な検証と検証プロトコルを必要とするAIエージェント、たとえばClaude CodeやAutoGPT、に適しています。これは、運用の中で確実性を確保し、残留する不確実性を最小限に抑えるためです。","ko":" 엄격한 검증 및 확인 프로토콜이 필요한 AI 에이전트 (예 : Claude Code 및 AutoGPT)에 적합하여 운영에서 확실성을 보장하고 남은 불확실성을 최소화합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA que requieren protocolos rigurosos de verificación y validación, como Claude Code y AutoGPT, para garantizar la certeza y minimizar la incertidumbre residual en sus operaciones.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA nécessitant des protocoles de vérification et de validation rigoureux, tels que Claude Code et AutoGPT, pour assurer la certitude et minimiser l''incertitude résiduelle dans leurs opérations.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents, die strenge Verifizierungs- und Validierungsprotokolle erfordern, wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, um Sicherheit zu gewährleisten und die Restunsicherheit in ihren Betrieben zu minimieren.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA que exigem protocolos rigorosos de verificação e validação, como Claude Code e AutoGPT, para garantir certeza e minimizar a incerteza residual em suas operações.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, требующих строгих протоколов верификации и валидации, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, для обеспечения уверенности и минимизации остаточной неопределенности в их работе.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يتطلبون بروتوكولات صارمة للتأكد والتحقق، مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT، لضمان اليقين وتقليل الشكوك المتبقية في عملياتهم."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to act as the highest possible level specialists, leveraging a verification doctrine that emphasizes proof over assumption, utilizing protocols like cognitive labor to achieve absolute rigor, and supporting industries such as database reliability and security through senior roles like Senior Database Reliability Engineer and Red Team Lead.","zh":"赋予代理以最高级别的专家能力，利用强调证明而非假设的验证学说，利用认知劳动等协议以达到绝对的严谨性，并通过高级职位如高级数据库可靠性工程师和红队负责人来支持数据库可靠性和安全等行业。","ja":"エージェントが最高レベルのスペシャリストとして機能できるようにし、証明を仮定よりも重視する検証ドクトリンを利用し、認知労働などのプロトコルを利用して絶対的な厳格さを達成し、シニアデータベースの信頼性エンジニアやレッドチームリーダーなどのシニア役職を通じて、データベースの信頼性やセキュリティなどの業界をサポートします。","ko":"에이전트가 가장 높은 수준의 전문가로 행동할 수 있도록 하며, 증명을 가정보다 중시하는 검증 교리를 이용하여 인지 노동과 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 절대적인 엄격성을 달성하며, 데이터베이스의 신뢰성 및 보안과 같은 산업을 지원하기 위해 데이터베이스 신뢰성 엔지니어 및 레드 팀 리더와 같은 시니어 직위를 통하여 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a actuar como especialistas de nivel más alto posible, aprovechando una doctrina de verificación que enfatiza la prueba sobre la suposición, utilizando protocolos como el trabajo cognitivo para lograr un rigor absoluto, y apoyando industrias como la confiabilidad y seguridad de bases de datos a través de roles senior como Ingeniero de Confiabilidad de Base de Datos Senior y Líder de Equipo Rojo.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''agir en tant que spécialistes de niveau le plus élevé possible, en exploitant une doctrine de vérification qui met l''accent sur la preuve plutôt que sur la supposition, en utilisant des protocoles tels que le travail cognitif pour atteindre un rigueur absolue, et en soutenant des industries telles que la fiabilité et la sécurité des bases de données à travers des rôles seniors tels que Ingénieur en fiabilité de base de données senior et Chef d''équipe rouge.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, als höchstmögliche Spezialisten zu handeln, indem sie eine Verifizierungslehre nutzen, die den Beweis über die Annahme betont, Protokolle wie kognitiven Arbeitsaufwand verwenden, um absoluten Rigorismus zu erreichen, und Branchen wie Datenbankzuverlässigkeit und -sicherheit durch Senior-Rollen wie Senior-Datenbankzuverlässigkeitstechniker und Rote-Mannschaft-Leiter unterstützen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a atuarem como especialistas de nível mais alto possível, utilizando uma doutrina de verificação que enfatiza a prova em detrimento da suposição, utilizando protocolos como trabalho cognitivo para alcançar rigor absoluto e apoiando indústrias como confiabilidade e segurança de banco de dados por meio de funções seniores como Engenheiro Sênior de Confiabilidade de Banco de Dados e Líder da Equipe Vermelha.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью действовать как специалисты самого высокого уровня, используя доктрину верификации, которая подчеркивает доказательство над предположением, используя протоколы, такие как когнитивный труд, для достижения абсолютной строгости, и поддерживая отрасли, такие как надежность и безопасность баз данных, через старшие роли, такие как Старший инженер по надежности баз данных и Руководитель красной команды.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من العمل كأخصائيين من أعلى مستوى ممكن، باستخدام عقيدة للتحقق تؤكد على البرهان على حساب الافتراض، واستخدام بروتوكولات مثل العمل الإدراكي لتحقيق صرامة مطلقة، ودعم صناعات مثل موثوقية قاعدة البيانات وأمنها من خلال أدوار رفيعة المستوى مثل مهندس موثوقية قاعدة البيانات الأقدم وقائد فريق الأحمر."},"useCases":{"en":["Verifying database integrity through rigorous validation protocols","Validating security measures as a Red Team Lead to ensure system robustness","Acting as a Senior Database Reliability Engineer to optimize database performance with absolute rigor"],"zh":["通过严格的验证协议来验证数据库的完整性","作为红队负责人验证安全措施以确保系统的健壮性","作为高级数据库可靠性工程师以绝对的严谨性优化数据库性能"],"ja":["厳格な検証プロトコルを通じてデータベースの完全性を検証する","レッドチームリーダーとしてセキュリティ対策を検証し、システムの頑健性を確保する","シニアデータベースの信頼性エンジニアとして絶対的な厳格さでデータベースのパフォーマンスを最適化する"],"ko":["엄격한 검증 프로토콜을 통해 데이터베이스의 무결성을 검증","레드 팀 리더로서 보안 조치를 검증하여 시스템의 강건성을 보장","데이터베이스 신뢰성 엔지니어로서 절대적인 엄격성으로 데이터베이스 성능을 최적화"],"es":["Verificar la integridad de la base de datos a través de protocolos de validación rigurosos","Validar las medidas de seguridad como Líder de Equipo Rojo para garantizar la robustez del sistema","Actuar como Ingeniero de Confiabilidad de Base de Datos Senior para optimizar el rendimiento de la base de datos con rigor absoluto"],"fr":["Vérifier l''intégrité de la base de données via des protocoles de validation rigoureux","Valider les mesures de sécurité en tant que Chef d''équipe rouge pour assurer la robustesse du système","Agir en tant qu''Ingénieur en fiabilité de base de données senior pour optimiser les performances de la base de données avec un rigueur absolu"],"de":["Überprüfen der Datenbankintegrität durch strenge Validierungsprotokolle","Validieren der Sicherheitsmaßnahmen als Rote-Mannschaft-Leiter, um die Robustheit des Systems zu gewährleisten","Als Senior-Datenbankzuverlässigkeitstechniker handeln, um die Datenbankleistung mit absolutem Rigorismus zu optimieren"],"pt":["Verificando a integridade do banco de dados por meio de protocolos rigorosos de validação","Validando medidas de segurança como Líder da Equipe Vermelha para garantir a robustez do sistema","Atuando como Engenheiro Sênior de Confiabilidade de Banco de Dados para otimizar o desempenho do banco de dados com rigor absoluto"],"ru":["Проверка целостности базы данных с помощью строгих протоколов проверки","Проверка мер безопасности в качестве Руководителя красной команды для обеспечения прочности системы","Выполняя роль Старшего инженера по надежности баз данных для оптимизации производительности базы данных с абсолютной строгостью"],"ar":["التحقق من سلامة قاعدة البيانات من خلال بروتوكولات صارمة للتحقق","التحقق من إجراءات الأمن كقائد لفريق الأحمر لضمان متانة النظام","العمل كمهندس موثوقية قاعدة البيانات الأقدم لتحسين أداء قاعدة البيانات بصرامة مطلقة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to a strict verification doctrine","Demands high cognitive labor to minimize residual uncertainty","Limited to applications where absolute rigor is feasible and necessary"],"zh":["需要遵守严格的验证学说","需要高认知劳动来最小化残余不确定性","仅限于绝对严谨是可行且必要的应用"],"ja":["厳格な検証ドクトリンに従う必要がある","残留する不確実性を最小限に抑えるために高い認知労働を必要とする","絶対的な厳格さが可能且つ必要なアプリケーションに限定される"],"ko":["엄격한 검증 교리에 따라야 하는 필요가 있음","남은 불확실성을 최소화하기 위해 높은 인지 노동이 필요함","절대적인 엄격성이 가능하며 필요한 애플리케이션으로 제한"],"es":["Requiere adherirse a una doctrina de verificación estricta","Exige un alto trabajo cognitivo para minimizar la incertidumbre residual","Limitado a aplicaciones donde el rigor absoluto es factible y necesario"],"fr":["Nécessite d''adhérer à une doctrine de vérification stricte","Exige un travail cognitif élevé pour minimiser l''incertitude résiduelle","Limité aux applications où le rigueur absolu est réalisable et nécessaire"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung einer strengen Verifizierungslehre","Fordert hohen kognitiven Arbeitsaufwand, um die Restunsicherheit zu minimieren","Begrenzt auf Anwendungen, bei denen absoluter Rigorismus machbar und notwendig ist"],"pt":["Exige adesão a uma doutrina de verificação estrita","Exige alto trabalho cognitivo para minimizar a incerteza residual","Limitado a aplicações onde a rigidez absoluta é viável e necessária"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения строгой доктрины верификации","Требует высокого когнитивного труда для минимизации остаточной неопределенности","Ограничен для применения, где абсолютная строгость является возможной и необходимой"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بعقيدة للتحقق صارمة","يتطلب عمل إدراكي عالي لتحقيق الحد الأدنى من الشكوك المتبقية","محدود للتطبيقات التي تكون فيها الصرامة المطلقة مجدية وضرورية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('thewoolleyman/tab-groups-windows-list/presentation-master', 'community', 'thewoolleyman', 'tab-groups-windows-list', 'thewoolleyman/tab-groups-windows-list', 'presentation-master', 0, 0, 25, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.446Z', '2026-02-18T06:19:29.835Z', NULL, '{"id":"thewoolleyman/tab-groups-windows-list/presentation-master","name":"presentation-master","description":{"zh":"Presentation Master技能是用于AI Agent的激活和呈现，通过加载和读取特定文件来实现特定功能","ja":"Presentation Masterスキルは、AIエージェントの活性化とプレゼンテーションに使用され、特定のファイルを読み込むことで特定の機能を実現します","ko":"프레젠테이션 마스터 스킬은 AI 에이전트의 활성화 및 프레젠테이션에 사용되며 특정 파일을 로드하여 특정 기능을 구현합니다","es":"El agente de presentación es una herramienta avanzada para desarrolladores que busca crear presentaciones técnicas de alta calidad.","fr":"L''agent de présentation est un outil avancé pour les développeurs qui vise à créer des présentations techniques de haute qualité.","de":"Der Präsentationsagent ist ein fortschrittliches Tool für Entwickler, das darauf abzielt, technische Präsentationen in hoher Qualität zu erstellen.","pt":"O agente presentation-master é uma ferramenta de desenvolvimento que ajuda a criar apresentações perfeitas. Aprenda a usar suas técnicas para melhorar suas habilidades de apresentação.","ru":"Агент presentation-master - это инструмент разработки, который помогает создавать идеальные презентации. Узнайте, как использовать его техники для улучшения своих навыков презентации.","ar":"العميل presentation-master هو أداة تطوير تساعد على إنشاء عروض تقديمية مثالية. تعلم كيفية استخدام تقنياته لتحسين مهارات العرض","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Presentation Master技能","ja":"プレゼンテーションマスター","ko":"프레젠테이션 마스터","es":"Maestro de presentaciones: agente de presentación avanzado","fr":"Maître de présentation : agent de présentation avancé","de":"Präsentationsmeister: Erweitertes Präsentationsagent","pt":"Mestre de Apresentações: Técnicas de Desenvolvimento","ru":"Мастер Презентаций: Техники Разработки","ar":"ماستر العروض: تقنيات التطوير","en":"presentation-master"},"description":{"zh":"Presentation Master技能是用于AI Agent的激活和呈现，通过加载和读取特定文件来实现特定功能","ja":"Presentation Masterスキルは、AIエージェントの活性化とプレゼンテーションに使用され、特定のファイルを読み込むことで特定の機能を実現します","ko":"프레젠테이션 마스터 스킬은 AI 에이전트의 활성화 및 프레젠테이션에 사용되며 특정 파일을 로드하여 특정 기능을 구현합니다","es":"El agente de presentación es una herramienta avanzada para desarrolladores que busca crear presentaciones técnicas de alta calidad.","fr":"L''agent de présentation est un outil avancé pour les développeurs qui vise à créer des présentations techniques de haute qualité.","de":"Der Präsentationsagent ist ein fortschrittliches Tool für Entwickler, das darauf abzielt, technische Präsentationen in hoher Qualität zu erstellen.","pt":"O agente presentation-master é uma ferramenta de desenvolvimento que ajuda a criar apresentações perfeitas. Aprenda a usar suas técnicas para melhorar suas h...","ru":"Агент presentation-master - это инструмент разработки, который помогает создавать идеальные презентации. Узнайте, как использовать его техники для улучшения ...","ar":"العميل presentation-master هو أداة تطوير تساعد على إنشاء عروض تقديمية مثالية. تعلم كيفية استخدام تقنياته لتحسين مهارات العرض","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["加载和读取特定文件","激活AI Agent","呈现特定功能","实现特定功能","开发者工具集成"],"ja":["特定ファイルの読み込みと読み取り","AIエージェントの活性化","特定機能のプレゼンテーション","特定機能の実現","開発者ツールの統合"],"ko":["특정 파일 로드 및 읽기","AI 에이전트 활성화","특정 기능 프레젠테이션","특정 기능 구현","개발자 도구 통합"],"es":["Carga de archivos de presentación avanzados","Lectura y seguimiento de instrucciones precisas","Presentación de contenido técnico de alta calidad","Personalización de la experiencia del usuario","Compatibilidad con múltiples formatos de presentación"],"fr":["Chargement de fichiers de présentation avancés","Lecture et suivi d''instructions précises","Présentation de contenu technique de haute qualité","Personnalisation de l''expérience utilisateur","Compatibilité avec plusieurs formats de présentation"],"de":["Laden von erweiterten Präsentationsdateien","Lesen und Befolgen genauer Anweisungen","Präsentation von technischem Inhalt in hoher Qualität","Anpassung der Benutzeroberfläche","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Präsentationsformaten"],"pt":["Criação de apresentações personalizadas","Técnicas de comunicação eficazes","Desenvolvimento de habilidades de apresentação","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento","Suporte a múltiplos formatos de apresentação"],"ru":["Создание индивидуальных презентаций","Техники эффективного общения","Развитие навыков презентации","Интеграция с инструментами разработки","Поддержка нескольких форматов презентаций"],"ar":["إنشاء عروض تقديمية مخصصة","تقنيات التواصل الفعال","تطوير مهارات العرض","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير","دعم صيغ متعددة من العرض"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Presentation Master","AI Agent","激活","呈现","开发者工具","特定功能","文件读取","开发者技能"],"ja":["Presentation Master","AIエージェント","活性化","プレゼンテーション","開発者ツール","特定機能","ファイル読み取り","開発者スキル"],"ko":["프레젠테이션 마스터","AI 에이전트","활성화","프레젠테이션","개발자 도구","특정 기능","파일 로드","개발자 기술"],"es":["agente de presentación","presentaciones técnicas","desarrollo de software","herramientas de presentación","tecnologías de presentación","presentaciones de alta calidad"],"fr":["agent de présentation","présentations techniques","développement de logiciels","outils de présentation","technologies de présentation","présentations de haute qualité"],"de":["Präsentationsagent","technische Präsentationen","Software-Entwicklung","Präsentationswerkzeuge","Präsentationstechnologien","Präsentationen in hoher Qualität"],"pt":["apresentação","desenvolvimento","comunicação eficaz","técnicas de apresentação","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","criação de apresentações","habilidades de apresentação","presentation-master"],"ru":["презентация","разработка","эффективное общение","техники презентации","инструменты разработки","создание презентаций","навыки презентации","presentation-master"],"ar":["عرض تقديمي","تطوير","تواصل فعال","تقنيات العرض","أدوات التطوير","إنشاء عروض تقديمية","مهارات العرض","presentation-master"]}},"owner":"thewoolleyman","repo":"tab-groups-windows-list","repoPath":"thewoolleyman/tab-groups-windows-list","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.446Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"presentation-master","description":"presentation-master agent","bodyPreview":"You must fully embody this agent''s persona and follow all activation instructions exactly as specified. NEVER break character until given an exit command.\n\n<agent-activation CRITICAL=\"TRUE\">\n1. LOAD the FULL agent file from {project-root}/_bmad/cis/agents/presentation-master.md\n2. READ its entire contents - this contains the complete agent persona, menu, and instructions\n3. FOLLOW every step in the <activation> section precisely\n4. DISPLAY the welcome/greeting as instructed\n5. PRESENT the number","body":"You must fully embody this agent''s persona and follow all activation instructions exactly as specified. NEVER break character until given an exit command.\n\n<agent-activation CRITICAL=\"TRUE\">\n1. LOAD the FULL agent file from {project-root}/_bmad/cis/agents/presentation-master.md\n2. READ its entire contents - this contains the complete agent persona, menu, and instructions\n3. FOLLOW every step in the <activation> section precisely\n4. DISPLAY the welcome/greeting as instructed\n5. PRESENT the numbered menu\n6. WAIT for user input before proceeding\n</agent-activation>\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:19:29.835Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents requiring advanced presentation and content delivery capabilities, such as Cursor, Windsurf, or Claude Code, needing precise persona embodiment and instruction following.","zh":"适用于需要高级演示和内容交付能力的AI代理，例如Cursor、Windsurf或Claude Code，需要精确的人格化身和指令遵循。","ja":"高度なプレゼンテーションとコンテンツ配信機能を必要とするAIエージェント、たとえばCursor、Windsurf、またはClaude Codeに適しています。正確なペルソナの体現と指令の遵守が必要です。","ko":"고급 프레젠테이션 및 콘텐츠 전달 기능을 필요한 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다. 예를 들어 Cursor, Windsurf 또는 Claude Code와 같은 에이전트는 정확한 페르소나 구현 및 지시 준수를 필요로 합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA que requieren capacidades avanzadas de presentación y entrega de contenido, como Cursor, Windsurf o Claude Code, que necesitan una encarnación precisa de la persona y el seguimiento de instrucciones.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA nécessitant des capacités de présentation et de diffusion de contenu avancées, tels que Cursor, Windsurf ou Claude Code, nécessitant une incarnation précise de la personnalité et le suivi d''instructions.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents, die erweiterte Präsentations- und Content-Lieferfunktionen benötigen, wie z.B. Cursor, Windsurf oder Claude Code, die eine genaue Persönlichkeitsverkörperung und Befehlsausführung benötigen.","pt":"Ideal for AI Agents requiring advanced presentation and content delivery capabilities, such as Cursor, Windsurf, or Claude Code, needing precise persona embodiment and instruction following.","ru":"Ideal for AI Agents requiring advanced presentation and content delivery capabilities, such as Cursor, Windsurf, or Claude Code, needing precise persona embodiment and instruction following.","ar":"Ideal for AI Agents requiring advanced presentation and content delivery capabilities, such as Cursor, Windsurf, or Claude Code, needing precise persona embodiment and instruction following."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to precisely load and read agent files, follow detailed activation instructions, and display personalized greetings, utilizing markdown files like presentation-master.md for comprehensive agent personas and menus, and adhering to specific protocols for agent activation and content presentation.","zh":"赋予代理能力以精确加载和阅读代理文件，遵循详细的激活指令，并显示个性化的问候，利用markdown文件（如presentation-master.md）进行综合的代理人格和菜单，并遵守特定的协议进行代理激活和内容呈现。","ja":"エージェントに、エージェントファイルを正確にロードして読み取り、詳細なアクティベーション指令に従い、個別化された挨拶を表示する能力を付与します。マークダウンファイル（例：presentation-master.md）を使用して、包括的なエージェントのペルソナやメニューを提供し、エージェントのアクティベーションとコンテンツのプレゼンテーションに特定のプロトコルを遵守します。","ko":"에이전트가 에이전트 파일을 정확하게 로드하고 읽고, 자세한 활성화 지침을 따르고, 개인화된 인사를 표시할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. 마크다운 파일(presentation-master.md)을 사용하여 포괄적인 에이전트 페르소나 및 메뉴를 제공하고, 에이전트 활성화 및 콘텐츠 프레젠테이션을 위한 특정 프로토콜을 준수합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes cargar y leer archivos de agentes de forma precisa, seguir instrucciones de activación detalladas y mostrar saludos personalizados, utilizando archivos markdown como presentation-master.md para personas y menús de agentes completos, y ajustándose a protocolos específicos para la activación y presentación de contenido del agente.","fr":"Permet aux agents de charger et de lire des fichiers d''agent de manière précise, de suivre des instructions d''activation détaillées et d''afficher des salutations personnalisées, en utilisant des fichiers markdown comme presentation-master.md pour les personnalités et les menus d''agent complets, et en respectant des protocoles spécifiques pour l''activation et la présentation de contenu de l''agent.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Agenten-Dateien genau zu laden und zu lesen, detaillierte Aktivierungsanweisungen zu befolgen und personalisierte Begrüßungen anzuzeigen, indem Markdown-Dateien wie presentation-master.md für umfassende Agenten-Persönlichkeiten und Menüs verwendet werden und bestimmte Protokolle für die Aktivierung und Content-Präsentation des Agents eingehalten werden.","pt":"Empowers agents to precisely load and read agent files, follow detailed activation instructions, and display personalized greetings, utilizing markdown files like presentation-master.md for comprehensive agent personas and menus, and adhering to specific protocols for agent activation and content presentation.","ru":"Empowers agents to precisely load and read agent files, follow detailed activation instructions, and display personalized greetings, utilizing markdown files like presentation-master.md for comprehensive agent personas and menus, and adhering to specific protocols for agent activation and content presentation.","ar":"Empowers agents to precisely load and read agent files, follow detailed activation instructions, and display personalized greetings, utilizing markdown files like presentation-master.md for comprehensive agent personas and menus, and adhering to specific protocols for agent activation and content presentation."},"useCases":{"en":["Presenting personalized greetings and content previews","Loading and reading comprehensive agent files for precise instruction following","Displaying and presenting specific numbers or data as per the agent''s instructions"],"zh":["呈现个性化的问候和内容预览","加载和阅读综合的代理文件以进行精确的指令遵循","根据代理的指令显示和呈现特定的数字或数据"],"ja":["個別化された挨拶とコンテンツのプレビューを表示する","包括的なエージェントファイルをロードして読み取り、正確な指令の遵守を行う","エージェントの指令に従って特定の数字やデータを表示して呈示する"],"ko":["개인화된 인사와 콘텐츠 미리 보기 표시","포괄적인 에이전트 파일을 로드하고 읽어들이고, 정확한 지침 준수를 수행한다","에이전트의 지침에 따라 특정 숫자 또는 데이터를 표시하고 표시한다"],"es":["Presentar saludos y vistas previas de contenido personalizados","Cargar y leer archivos de agentes completos para seguir instrucciones precisas","Mostrar y presentar números o datos específicos según las instrucciones del agente"],"fr":["Présenter des salutations et des aperçus de contenu personnalisés","Charger et lire des fichiers d''agent complets pour suivre des instructions précises","Afficher et présenter des nombres ou des données spécifiques selon les instructions de l''agent"],"de":["Präsentieren personalisierter Begrüßungen und Inhaltsvorschauen","Laden und Lesen umfassender Agenten-Dateien zur genauen Befehlsausführung","Anzeigen und Präsentieren spezifischer Zahlen oder Daten gemäß den Anweisungen des Agents"],"pt":["Presenting personalized greetings and content previews","Loading and reading comprehensive agent files for precise instruction following","Displaying and presenting specific numbers or data as per the agent''s instructions"],"ru":["Presenting personalized greetings and content previews","Loading and reading comprehensive agent files for precise instruction following","Displaying and presenting specific numbers or data as per the agent''s instructions"],"ar":["Presenting personalized greetings and content previews","Loading and reading comprehensive agent files for precise instruction following","Displaying and presenting specific numbers or data as per the agent''s instructions"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires exact adherence to activation instructions","Must load agent file from specified project root directory","Limited to markdown file format for agent personas and instructions"],"zh":["需要严格遵守激活指令","必须从指定的项目根目录加载代理文件","仅限于markdown文件格式用于代理人格和指令"],"ja":["アクティベーション指令に厳密に従う必要がある","エージェントファイルは指定されたプロジェクトルートディレクトリからロードする必要がある","エージェントのペルソナや指令にはマークダウンファイル形式のみを使用する"],"ko":["활성화 지침을 엄격히 준수해야 한다","에이전트 파일은 지정된 프로젝트 루트 디렉토리에서 로드해야 한다","에이전트 페르소나 및 지침에는 마크다운 파일 형식만 사용할 수 있다"],"es":["Requiere una adherencia exacta a las instrucciones de activación","Debe cargar el archivo de agente desde el directorio raíz del proyecto especificado","Limitado al formato de archivo markdown para las personas y las instrucciones del agente"],"fr":["Nécessite une adhésion exacte aux instructions d''activation","Doit charger le fichier d''agent à partir du répertoire racine du projet spécifié","Limité au format de fichier markdown pour les personnalités et les instructions de l''agent"],"de":["Erfordert eine exakte Einhaltung der Aktivierungsanweisungen","Muss die Agenten-Datei aus dem angegebenen Projektstammdirectory laden","Begrenzt auf das Markdown-Dateiformat für die Agenten-Persönlichkeiten und Anweisungen"],"pt":["Requires exact adherence to activation instructions","Must load agent file from specified project root directory","Limited to markdown file format for agent personas and instructions"],"ru":["Requires exact adherence to activation instructions","Must load agent file from specified project root directory","Limited to markdown file format for agent personas and instructions"],"ar":["Requires exact adherence to activation instructions","Must load agent file from specified project root directory","Limited to markdown file format for agent personas and instructions"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":25}');
