ung von Web-Animationen, die sich richtig anfühlen, basierend auf dem Kurs ''Animations on the Web'' von Emil Kowalski","pt":"Guia completo para criação de animações web que funcionam bem, baseado no curso de Emil Kowalski","ru":"Полное руководство по созданию анимаций на сайте, основанное на курсе Эмиля Ковальски","ar":"دليل شامل لتصميم الرسوم المتحركة على الويب بناءً على دورة إميل كووالسكي","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["Web ","Emil Kowalski","Markdown","Web "],"ja":["Web","Emil Kowalski","Markdown","Web"],"ko":["Web ","Emil Kowalski","Markdown","Web "],"es":["Creación de animaciones personalizadas","Uso de tecnologías web como CSS y JavaScript","Implementación de efectos de transición y movimiento","Mejora de la experiencia del usuario con animaciones","Optimización de rendimiento para animaciones web"],"fr":["Création d''animations personnalisées","Utilisation de technologies web comme CSS et JavaScript","Mise en œuvre d''effets de transition et de mouvement","Amélioration de l''expérience utilisateur avec des animations","Optimisation des performances pour les animations web"],"de":["Erstellung von benutzerdefinierten Animationen","Verwendung von Web-Technologien wie CSS und JavaScript","Implementierung von Übergangs- und Bewegungseffekten","Verbesserung der Benutzererfahrung mit Animationen","Leistungsoptimierung für Web-Animationen"],"pt":["Criação de animações personalizadas","Otimização de desempenho de animações","Integração com tecnologias web","Desenvolvimento de efeitos visuais","Uso de bibliotecas de animação","Criação de experiências de usuário interativas"],"ru":["Создание кастомных анимаций","Оптимизация производительности анимаций","Интеграция с веб-технологиями","Разработка визуальных эффектов","Использование библиотек анимации","Создание интерактивных пользовательских trải nghiệm"],"ar":["تصميم الرسوم المتحركة المخصصة","تحسين أداء الرسوم المتحركة","التكامل مع تقنيات الويب","تصميم التأثيرات البصرية","استخدام مكتبات الرسوم المتحركة","إنشاء تجارب مستخدم تفاعلية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Web ","Web ","Emil Kowalski","Web ","Web ","Web "],"ja":["Web","Web","Emil Kowalski","Web","Web","Web"],"ko":["Web ","Web ","Emil Kowalski","Web ","Web ","Web "],"es":["diseño de animaciones web","animaciones web","css animations","javascript animations","experiencia del usuario","optimización de rendimiento","tecnologías web"],"fr":["conception d''animations web","animations web","animations css","animations javascript","expérience utilisateur","optimisation des performances","technologies web"],"de":["web-animation-design","web-animationen","css-animationen","javascript-animationen","benutzererfahrung","leistungsoptimierung","web-technologien"],"pt":["animação web","desenvolvimento de animação","efeitos visuais","tecnologias web","bibliotecas de animação","experiência de usuário","desenvolvimento de software","design de interface"],"ru":["веб-анимация","дизайн анимации","визуальные эффекты","веб-технологии","библиотеки анимации","пользовательский опыт","разработка программного обеспечения","дизайн интерфейса"],"ar":["الرسوم المتحركة على الويب","تصميم الرسوم المتحركة","التأثيرات البصرية","تقنيات الويب","مكتبات الرسوم المتحركة","تجربة المستخدم","تطوير البرمجيات","تصميم الواجهة"]}},"owner":"segersniels","repo":"dotfiles","repoPath":"segersniels/dotfiles","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.446Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"web-animation-design","description":"Design and implement web animations that feel natural and purposeful. Use this skill proactively whenever the user asks questions about animations, motion, easing, timing, duration, springs, transitions, or animation performance. This includes questions about how to animate specific UI elements, which easing to use, animation best practices, or accessibility considerations for motion. Triggers on: easing, ease-out, ease-in, ease-in-out, cubic-bezier, bounce, spring physics, keyframes, transform, opacity, fade, slide, scale, hover effects, microinteractions, Framer Motion, React Spring, GSAP, CSS transitions, entrance/exit animations, page transitions, stagger, will-change, GPU acceleration, prefers-reduced-motion, modal/dropdown/tooltip/popover/drawer animations, gesture animations, drag interactions, button press feel, feels janky, make it smooth.","bodyPreview":"# Web Animation Design\n\nA comprehensive guide for creating animations that feel right, based on Emil Kowalski''s \"Animations on the Web\" course.\n\n## Review Format (Required)\n\nWhen reviewing animations, you MUST use a markdown table. Do NOT use a list with \"Before:\" and \"After:\" on separate lines. Always output an actual markdown table like this:\n\n| Before                            | After                                           |\n| --------------------------------- | --------------------------","body":"# Web Animation Design\n\nA comprehensive guide for creating animations that feel right, based on Emil Kowalski''s \"Animations on the Web\" course.\n\n## Review Format (Required)\n\nWhen reviewing animations, you MUST use a markdown table. Do NOT use a list with \"Before:\" and \"After:\" on separate lines. Always output an actual markdown table like this:\n\n| Before                            | After                                           |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `transform: scale(0)`             | `transform: scale(0.95)`                        |\n| `animation: fadeIn 400ms ease-in` | `animation: fadeIn 200ms ease-out`              |\n| No reduced motion support         | `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {...}` |\n\nWrong format (never do this):\n\n```\nBefore: transform: scale(0)\nAfter: transform: scale(0.95)\n────────────────────────────\nBefore: 400ms duration\nAfter: 200ms\n```\n\nCorrect format: A single markdown table with | Before | After | columns, one row per issue.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nEvery animation decision starts with these questions:\n\n1. **Is this element entering or exiting?** → Use `ease-out`\n2. **Is an on-screen element moving?** → Use `ease-in-out`\n3. **Is this a hover/color transition?** → Use `ease`\n4. **Will users see this 100+ times daily?** → Don''t animate it\n\n## The Easing Blueprint\n\n### ease-out (Most Common)\n\nUse for **user-initiated interactions**: dropdowns, modals, tooltips, any element entering or exiting the screen.\n\n```css\n/* Sorted weak to strong */\n--ease-out-quad: cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.46, 0.45, 0.94);\n--ease-out-cubic: cubic-bezier(0.215, 0.61, 0.355, 1);\n--ease-out-quart: cubic-bezier(0.165, 0.84, 0.44, 1);\n--ease-out-quint: cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1);\n--ease-out-expo: cubic-bezier(0.19, 1, 0.22, 1);\n--ease-out-circ: cubic-bezier(0.075, 0.82, 0.165, 1);\n```\n\nWhy it works: Acceleration at the start creates an instant, responsive feeling. The element \"jumps\" toward its destination then settles in.\n\n### ease-in-out (For Movement)\n\nUse when **elements already on screen need to move or morph**. Mimics natural motion like a car accelerating then braking.\n\n```css\n/* Sorted weak to strong */\n--ease-in-out-quad: cubic-bezier(0.455, 0.03, 0.515, 0.955);\n--ease-in-out-cubic: cubic-bezier(0.645, 0.045, 0.355, 1);\n--ease-in-out-quart: cubic-bezier(0.77, 0, 0.175, 1);\n--ease-in-out-quint: cubic-bezier(0.86, 0, 0.07, 1);\n--ease-in-out-expo: cubic-bezier(1, 0, 0, 1);\n--ease-in-out-circ: cubic-bezier(0.785, 0.135, 0.15, 0.86);\n```\n\n### ease (For Hover Effects)\n\nUse for **hover states and color transitions**. The asymmetrical curve (faster start, slower end) feels elegant for gentle animations.\n\n```css\ntransition: background-color 150ms ease;\n```\n\n### linear (Avoid in UI)\n\nOnly use for:\n\n- Constant-speed animations (marquees, tickers)\n- Time visualization (hold-to-delete progress indicators)\n\nLinear feels robotic and unnatural for interactive elements.\n\n### ease-in (Almost Never)\n\n**Avoid for UI animations.** Makes interfaces feel sluggish because the slow start delays visual feedback.\n\n### Paired Elements Rule\n\nElements that animate together must use the same easing and duration. Modal + overlay, tooltip + arrow, drawer + backdrop—if they move as a unit, they should feel like a unit.\n\n```css\n/* Both use the same timing */\n.modal {\n  transition: transform 200ms ease-out;\n}\n.overlay {\n  transition: opacity 200ms ease-out;\n}\n```\n\n## Timing and Duration\n\n## Duration Guidelines\n\n| Element Type                      | Duration  |\n| --------------------------------- | --------- |\n| Micro-interactions                | 100-150ms |\n| Standard UI (tooltips, dropdowns) | 150-250ms |\n| Modals, drawers                   | 200-300ms |\n\n**Rules:**\n- UI animations should stay under 300ms\n- Larger elements animate slower than smaller ones\n- Exit animations can be ~20% faster than entrance\n- Match duration to distance - longer travel = longer duration\n\n### The Frequency\n\nDetermine how often users will see the animation:\n\n- **100+ times/day** → No animation (or drastically reduced)\n- **Occasional use** → Standard animation\n- **Rare/first-time** → Can be more special\n\n**Example:** Raycast never animates because users open it hundreds of times a day.\n\n## When to Animate\n\n**Do animate:**\n\n- Enter/exit transitions for spatial consistency\n- State changes that benefit from visual continuity\n- Responses to user actions (feedback)\n- Rarely-used interactions where delight adds value\n\n**Don''t animate:**\n\n- Keyboard-initiated actions\n- Hover effects on frequently-used elements\n- Anything users interact with 100+ times daily\n- When speed matters more than smoothness\n\n**Marketing vs. Product:**\n\n- Marketing: More elaborate, longer durations allowed\n- Product: Fast, purposeful, never frivolous\n\n## Spring Animations\n\nSprings feel more natural because they don''t have fixed durations—they simulate real physics.\n\n### When to Use Springs\n\n- Drag interactions with momentum\n- Elements that should feel \"alive\" (Dynamic Island)\n- Gestures that can be interrupted mid-animation\n- Organic, playful interfaces\n\n### Configuration\n\n**Apple''s approach (recommended):**\n\n```js\n// Duration + bounce (easier to understand)\n{ type: \"spring\", duration: 0.5, bounce: 0.2 }\n```\n\n**Traditional physics:**\n\n```js\n// Mass, stiffness, damping (more complex)\n{ type: \"spring\", mass: 1, stiffness: 100, damping: 10 }\n```\n\n### Bounce Guidelines\n\n- **Avoid bounce** in most UI contexts\n- **Use bounce** for drag-to-dismiss, playful interactions\n- Keep bounce subtle (0.1-0.3) when used\n\n### Interruptibility\n\nSprings maintain velocity when interrupted—CSS animations restart from zero. This makes springs ideal for gestures users might change mid-motion.\n\n## Performance\n\n### The Golden Rule\n\nOnly animate `transform` and `opacity`. These skip layout and paint stages, running entirely on the GPU.\n\n**Avoid animating:**\n\n- `padding`, `margin`, `height`, `width` (trigger layout)\n- `blur` filters above 20px (expensive, especially Safari)\n- CSS variables in deep component trees\n\n### Optimization Techniques\n\n```css\n/* Force GPU acceleration */\n.animated-element {\n  will-change: transform;\n}\n```\n\n**React-specific:**\n\n- Animate outside React''s render cycle when possible\n- Use refs to update styles directly instead of state\n- Re-renders on every frame = dropped frames\n\n**Framer Motion:**\n\n```jsx\n// Hardware accelerated (transform as string)\n<motion.div animate={{ transform: \"translateX(100px)\" }} />\n\n// NOT hardware accelerated (more readable)\n<motion.div animate={{ x: 100 }} />\n```\n\n### CSS vs. JavaScript\n\n- CSS animations run off main thread (smoother under load)\n- JS animations (Framer Motion, React Spring) use `requestAnimationFrame`\n- CSS better for simple, predetermined animations\n- JS better for dynamic, interruptible animations\n\n## Accessibility\n\nAnimations can cause motion sickness or distraction for some users.\n\n### prefers-reduced-motion\n\nWhenever you add an animation, also add a media query to disable it:\n\n```css\n.modal {\n  animation: fadeIn 200ms ease-out;\n}\n\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n  .modal {\n    animation: none;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Reduced Motion Guidelines\n\n- Every animated element needs its own `prefers-reduced-motion` media query\n- Set `animation: none` or `transition: none` (no `!important`)\n- No exceptions for opacity or color - disable all animations\n- Show play buttons instead of autoplay videos\n\n### Framer Motion Implementation\n\n```jsx\nimport { useReducedMotion } from \"framer-motion\";\n\nfunction Component() {\n  const shouldReduceMotion = useReducedMotion();\n\n  return (\n    <motion.div\n      initial={shouldReduceMotion ? false : { opacity: 0, y: 20 }}\n      animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }}\n    />\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Touch Device Considerations\n\n```css\n/* Disable hover animations on touch devices */\n@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {\n  .element:hover {\n    transform: scale(1.05);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nTouch devices trigger hover on tap, causing false positives.\n\n## Practical Tips\n\nQuick reference for common scenarios. See [PRACTICAL-TIPS.md](PRACTICAL-TIPS.md) for detailed implementations.\n\n| Scenario                        | Solution                                        |\n| ------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| Make buttons feel responsive    | Add `transform: scale(0.97)` on `:active`       |\n| Element appears from nowhere    | Start from `scale(0.95)`, not `scale(0)`        |\n| Shaky/jittery animations        | Add `will-change: transform`                    |\n| Hover causes flicker            | Animate child element, not parent               |\n| Popover scales from wrong point | Set `transform-origin` to trigger location      |\n| Sequential tooltips feel slow   | Skip delay/animation after first tooltip        |\n| Small buttons hard to tap       | Use 44px minimum hit area (pseudo-element)      |\n| Something still feels off       | Add subtle blur (under 20px) to mask it         |\n| Hover triggers on mobile        | Use `@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)` |\n\n## Easing Decision Flowchart\n\nIs the element entering or exiting the viewport?\n├── Yes → ease-out\n└── No\n├── Is it moving/morphing on screen?\n│ └── Yes → ease-in-out\n└── Is it a hover change?\n├── Yes → ease\n└── Is it constant motion?\n├── Yes → linear\n└── Default → ease-out\n\n## Reference Files\n\n- [PRACTICAL-TIPS.md](PRACTICAL-TIPS.md) - Detailed implementations for common animation scenarios\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:20:50.450Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing advanced web animation design capabilities based on Emil Kowalski''s principles.","zh":"非常适合需要基于Emil Kowalski原理的高级网页动画设计能力的前端代理","ja":"Emil Kowalskiの原則に基づいた高度なWebアニメーションデザイン機能が必要なフロントエンドエージェントに最適","ko":"Emil Kowalski의 원리에 기반한 고급 웹 애니메이션 디자인 기능이 필요한 프론트엔드 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes frontend que necesitan capacidades de diseño de animación web avanzadas basadas en los principios de Emil Kowalski.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents frontend ayant besoin de capacités de conception d''animation web avancées basées sur les principes d''Emil Kowalski.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agenten, die erweiterte Web-Animations-Designfunktionen auf der Grundlage der Prinzipien von Emil Kowalski benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que precisam de capacidades avançadas de design de animação web baseadas nos princípios de Emil Kowalski.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Frontend, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности дизайна веб-анимации на основе принципов Эмиля Ковальски.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأماميين الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات تصميم متقدمة للرسوم المتحركة على الويب dựa على مبادئ إميل كوفالسكي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create animations that feel right, utilizing markdown tables for review and feedback, and leveraging web-specific animation techniques, including SVG and CSS animations, to generate engaging web content.","zh":"赋予代理创建感觉正确的动画的能力，利用Markdown表格进行审查和反馈，并利用Web特定的动画技术，包括SVG和CSS动画，生成吸引人的Web内容","ja":"エージェントが正しさを感じるアニメーションを作成する能力を与え、レビューとフィードバックにMarkdownテーブルを利用し、SVGおよびCSSアニメーションなどのWeb固有のアニメーション技術を利用して、魅力的なWebコンテンツを生成する","ko":"에이전트가 올바른 느낌의 애니메이션을 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하고,審查와 피드백에 마크다운 표를 활용하며, SVG 및 CSS 애니메이션などの 웹 고유의 애니메이션 기술을 활용하여 매력적인 웹 콘텐츠를 생성","es":"Permite a los agentes crear animaciones que se sienten bien, utilizando tablas de markdown para revisión y comentarios, y aprovechando técnicas de animación específicas de la web, incluyendo animaciones SVG y CSS, para generar contenido web atractivo.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des animations qui se sentent bien, en utilisant des tableaux markdown pour la révision et les commentaires, et en exploitant des techniques d''animation spécifiques au web, y compris les animations SVG et CSS, pour générer du contenu web engageant.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Animations zu erstellen, die sich richtig anfühlen, indem sie Markdown-Tabellen für die Überprüfung und das Feedback nutzen und web-spezifische AnimationsTechniken, einschließlich SVG- und CSS-Animationen, einsetzen, um ansprechende Webinhalte zu generieren.","pt":"Permite que os agentes criem animações que se sentem certas, utilizando tabelas markdown para revisão e feedback, e aproveitando técnicas de animação específicas da web, incluindo animações SVG e CSS, para gerar conteúdo web atraente.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать анимации, которые кажутся правильными, используя таблицы markdown для обзора и обратной связи, а также использует веб-специфические техники анимации, включая анимацию SVG и CSS, для генерации привлекательного веб-контента.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من إنشاء رسوم متحركة تظهر بشكل صحيح، باستخدام جداول markdown للrevision و Feedback، واستخدام تقنيات الرسوم المتحركة المحددة للويب، بما في ذلك رسوم متحركة SVG و CSS، لإنشاء محتوى ويب جذاب."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing interactive web animations for landing pages","Generating animations for hero sections using SVG and CSS","Reviewing and providing feedback on web animation designs using markdown tables"],"zh":["为着陆页设计交互式网页动画","使用SVG和CSS为英雄区生成动画","使用Markdown表格审查和提供对网页动画设计的反馈"],"ja":["ランディングページのインタラクティブWebアニメーションを設計する","SVGおよびCSSを使用してヒーローセクションのアニメーションを生成する","Markdownテーブルを使用してWebアニメーションデザインのレビューとフィードバックを提供する"],"ko":["랜딩 페이지를 위한 인터랙티브 웹 애니메이션을 설계","SVG 및 CSS를 사용하여 히어로 섹션의 애니메이션을 생성","마크다운 표를 사용하여 웹 애니메이션 설계에 대한 리뷰 및 피드백을 제공"],"es":["Diseñar animaciones web interactivas para páginas de aterrizaje","Generar animaciones para secciones de héroe utilizando SVG y CSS","Revisar y proporcionar comentarios sobre diseños de animación web utilizando tablas de markdown"],"fr":["Concevoir des animations web interactives pour les pages d''atterrissage","Générer des animations pour les sections de héros en utilisant SVG et CSS","Réviser et fournir des commentaires sur les conceptions d''animation web en utilisant des tableaux markdown"],"de":["Interaktive Web-Animationen für Landingpages entwerfen","Animationen für Hero-Sectionen mit SVG und CSS generieren","Web-Animations-Entwürfe überprüfen und Feedback in Markdown-Tabellen bereitstellen"],"pt":["Criar animações interativas da web para páginas de destino","Gerar animações para seções de heróis usando SVG e CSS","Revisar e fornecer feedback sobre designs de animação da web usando tabelas markdown"],"ru":["Создание интерактивных веб-анимаций для целевых страниц","Генерация анимаций для секций героев с использованием SVG и CSS","Просмотр и предоставление обратной связи по дизайну веб-анимации с помощью таблиц markdown"],"ar":["إنشاء رسوم متحركة تفاعلية على الويب للصفحات المستهدفة","إنشاء رسوم متحركة لقطع البطل باستخدام SVG و CSS","مراجعة وتقديم反馈 حول تصميمات الرسوم المتحركة على الويب باستخدام جداول markdown"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of web animation principles and design","Limited to web-based animations, not applicable to other mediums like video or mobile apps","Output must be in markdown table format for review and feedback"],"zh":["需要了解网页动画原理和设计","仅限于基于Web的动画，不适用于其他媒体，如视频或移动应用","输出必须以Markdown表格格式进行审查和反馈"],"ja":["Webアニメーションの原理とデザインの理解が必要","Webベースのアニメーションに限定され、ビデオやモバイルアプリなどの他のメディアには適用できない","出力はレビューとフィードバックのためにMarkdownテーブル形式でなければならない"],"ko":["웹 애니메이션 원리와 설계에 대한 이해가 필요","웹 기반 애니메이션에만 국한되며, 비디오 또는 모바일 앱과 같은 기타 매체에는 적용할 수 없음","출력은 리뷰 및 피드백을 위해 마크다운 표 형식이어야 함"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los principios de animación web y diseño","Limitado a animaciones basadas en la web, no aplicable a otros medios como video o aplicaciones móviles","La salida debe estar en formato de tabla de markdown para revisión y comentarios"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des principes d''animation web et de conception","Limité aux animations basées sur le web, non applicable à d''autres médias tels que la vidéo ou les applications mobiles","La sortie doit être au format de tableau markdown pour la révision et les commentaires"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis für Web-Animations-Prinzipien und Design","Begrenzt auf webbasierte Animationen, nicht anwendbar auf andere Medien wie Video oder Mobile Apps","Die Ausgabe muss im Markdown-Tabellen-Format für die Überprüfung und das Feedback bereitgestellt werden"],"pt":["Requer entendimento dos princípios de animação da web e design","Limitado a animações baseadas na web, não aplicável a outros meios como vídeo ou aplicativos móveis","A saída deve estar no formato de tabela markdown para revisão e feedback"],"ru":["Требует понимания принципов веб-анимации и дизайна","Ограничен анимациями, основанными на вебе, не применимо к другим средствам, таким как видео или мобильные приложения","Выходные данные должны быть в формате таблицы markdown для обзора и обратной связи"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مبادئ الرسوم المتحركة على الويب وتصميم","محدود بالرسوم المتحركة المبنية على الويب، 