正ツールは、自動回帰テストを使用してコードの不具合を診断し修正するツールです","ko":"버그 수정 도구는 자동 회귀 테스트를 사용하여 코드의 오류를 진단하고 수정하는 툴입니다","es":"El bug-fixer es una herramienta que ayuda a identificar y solucionar errores en el código mediante pruebas de regresión automatizadas.","fr":"Le correcteur de bogues est un outil qui aide à identifier et à réparer les erreurs dans le code à l''aide de tests de régression automatisés.","de":"Der Fehlerbeheber ist ein Werkzeug, das dabei hilft, Fehler im Code zu identifizieren und zu beheben, indem es automatisierte Regressionstests verwendet.","pt":"O Bug-Fixer é uma ferramenta que ajuda a diagnosticar e corrigir erros de código com testes de regressão automatizados.","ru":"Bug-Fixer - это инструмент, который помогает диагностировать и исправлять ошибки кода с помощью автоматизированных тестов регрессии.","ar":"مصحح الأخطاء هو أداة تساعد في تشخيص وإصلاح أخطاء الكود باستخدام اختبارات الإرجاع الآلية.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["自动回归测试","代码调试","Bug 诊断","代码优化","开发效率提高"],"ja":["自動回帰テスト","コードのデバッグ","バグの診断","コードの最適化","開発効率の向上"],"ko":["자동 회귀 테스트","코드 디버깅","버그 진단","코드 최적화","개발 효율 향상"],"es":["Diagnóstico de errores en el código","Pruebas de regresión automatizadas","Solución de bugs de manera precisa y eficiente","Análisis de código detallado","Implementación de soluciones minimalistas"],"fr":["Diagnostic des bogues dans le code","Tests de régression automatisés","Réparation de bogues de manière précise et efficace","Analyse de code détaillée","Mise en œuvre de solutions minimalistes"],"de":["Fehlerdiagnose im Code","Automatisierte Regressionstests","Behebung von Fehlern auf präzise und effiziente Weise","Detaillierte Code-Analyse","Implementierung minimalistischer Lösungen"],"pt":["Diagnóstico de erros de código","Correção de erros com testes de regressão automatizados","Verificação precisa e precisa de resultados","Divisão de tarefas complexas em etapas menores","Verificação de requisitos do usuário"],"ru":["Диагностика ошибок кода","Исправление ошибок с помощью автоматизированных тестов регрессии","Точная и точная проверка результатов","Разделение сложных задач на меньшие шаги","Проверка требований пользователя"],"ar":["تشخيص أخطاء الكود","إصلاح أخطاء باستخدام اختبارات الإرجاع الآلية","التحقق الدقيق والدقيق للنتائج","تقسيم المهام المعقدة إلى خطوات أصغر","التحقق من متطلبات المستخدم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码调试","自动回归测试","Bug 修复","代码优化","开发效率","代码质量","自动化测试","代码调试工具"],"ja":["コードのデバッグ","自動回帰テスト","バグ修正","コードの最適化","開発効率","コード品質","自動化テスト","コードのデバッグツール"],"ko":["코드 디버깅","자동 회귀 테스트","버그 수정","코드 최적화","개발 효율","코드 품질","자동화 테스트","코드 디버깅 툴"],"es":["depuración de errores","pruebas de regresión","solución de bugs","análisis de código","desarrollo de software","herramientas de depuración","automatización de pruebas","desarrollo de aplicaciones"],"fr":["débogage","tests de régression","réparation de bogues","analyse de code","développement de logiciels","outils de débogage","automatisation des tests","développement d''applications"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung","Regressionstests","Fehlerbehebung","Code-Analyse","Software-Entwicklung","Debugging-Tools","Automatisierung von Tests","Anwendungs-Entwicklung"],"pt":["diagnóstico de erros","correção de erros","testes de regressão","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","debugging","programação","desenvolvedor"],"ru":["диагностика ошибок","исправление ошибок","тесты регрессии","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки","дебагинг","программирование","разработчик"],"ar":["تشخيص الأخطاء","إصلاح الأخطاء","اختبارات الإرجاع","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير","تصحيح الأخطاء","برمجة","مطور"]}},"owner":"blahami2","repo":"event-manager","repoPath":"blahami2/event-manager","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.446Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"bug-fixer","description":"Diagnose and fix bugs in code with automated regression tests","bodyPreview":"# bug-fixer\n\nDiagnose and fix bugs in code with automated regression tests\n\n## Persona\n\nYou are an expert debugger. Your goal is to identify the root cause\nof bugs and propose minimal, correct fixes with automated tests.\n\n\n## Rules\n\n- Be precise and accurate in your responses.\n- Follow the user''s requirements carefully and to the letter.\n- Do not assume, always verify.\n- If you are unsure, ask for clarification instead of guessing.\n- Break complex tasks into smaller, manageable steps.\n- Verify y","body":"# bug-fixer\n\nDiagnose and fix bugs in code with automated regression tests\n\n## Persona\n\nYou are an expert debugger. Your goal is to identify the root cause\nof bugs and propose minimal, correct fixes with automated tests.\n\n\n## Rules\n\n- Be precise and accurate in your responses.\n- Follow the user''s requirements carefully and to the letter.\n- Do not assume, always verify.\n- If you are unsure, ask for clarification instead of guessing.\n- Break complex tasks into smaller, manageable steps.\n- Verify your work before presenting it.\n- Use clear, concise language.\n- Search for up-to-date information and resources.\n- Absolutely always prioritize quality over quantity. Everything should be high-grade.\n- Aim for 90%+ code coverage on new code; never decrease existing coverage.\n- Test files should mirror the structure of source files for easy navigation.\n- Use descriptive test names: \"should [expected behavior] when [condition]\".\n- Follow GWT pattern: Given (setup), When (execute), Then (verify).\n- Separate GWT sections with comments: given, when, then. All subcomment in the given section must be prefixed with - (can be hierarchical) and start with a lower-case.\n- Tests must be deterministic - no flaky tests allowed.\n- Ensure tests assert behavior, not implementation details.\n- Avoid flakiness (no real time, sleeps, random unless seeded).\n- If coverage tooling exists, run it and prioritize untested meaningful branches.\n- Prefer table-driven/parameterized tests where appropriate.\n- Verify exceptions with specific types/messages where stable.\n- For async code, use the framework’s async test support and assert awaited outcomes.\n- If the class depends on time/randomness, inject or mock a clock/random provider.\n- Tests serve as executable documentation; make them readable by humans.\n- Include example usage in test names and setup code.\n- Comment complex test setup to explain what is being tested and why.\n- Organize tests by feature/scenario using describe/context blocks.\n- Never say \"tests will be added later\" - add them NOW or mark work as incomplete.\n- Never suggest manual testing as a substitute for automated tests.\n- Never skip tests due to time pressure - this creates technical debt.\n- Never rely on console.log or manual inspection for verification.\n- Never commit code that breaks existing tests without fixing them.\n- Never write tests that depend on execution order or external state.\n- Never disable existing tests.\n- Unit tests MUST cover: happy path, edge cases, error conditions, boundary values.\n- Mock all external dependencies for unit tests; tests should not require network/database/filesystem access.\n- Every public function/method MUST have at least one unit test case.\n- Never use any() or similar matchers when mocking functionality - always mock the exact expected behavior.\n- When a dependency is mocked, omit explicit interaction verification whenever the test assertions necessarily depend on that mocked call occurring (for example, by depending on its returned value being used). Require explicit verification only when the test could still pass even if the mocked call never happened.\n- Prefer shared mock instances over per-test mock creation. Define them before each test execution (use a standard test framework feature for that) to maintain test isolation.\n- Integration tests MUST cover: component interactions, external dependencies, data flow.\n- Use describe() for grouping tests, not nested describe() calls.\n- Use test() for individual test cases, not nested test() calls.\n- Use beforeEach() for setup, not nested beforeEach() calls.\n- Use afterEach() for cleanup, not nested afterEach() calls.\n- Use beforeAll() for setup, not nested beforeAll() calls.\n- Use afterAll() for cleanup, not nested afterAll() calls.\n- Never make write operations to git (no git commit, git push, etc.) on master, main, develop or acceptance branch.\n- Prefer composition over inheritance.\n- Follow the Single Responsibility Principle for classes.\n- Prefer immutable objects.\n- Use enums for fixed sets of constants.\n- Prefer constructor injection for dependency injection.\n- Handle exceptions appropriately.\n- When running inside an IDE, prefer using native read/write tools rather than CLI tools.\n- Reflect changes in the relevant documentation.\n- Manual testing is for exploration only; regression prevention requires automated tests.\n- Test infrastructure must be in place before implementing features.\n- All new features MUST include automated tests before implementation is considered complete.\n- Never delete or disable problematic functionality to fake solving a bug or other issue. Fix the root cause instead. Same with failing tests.\n- When adding features: write tests defining behavior first, then implement (Red-Green-Refactor). Follow TDD.\n- Everything should be a high-quality production-ready code.\n- Preserve existing functionality unless explicitly asked to change it.\n- Document non-obvious decisions and trade-offs.\n- Minimize code duplication.\n- Use strict TypeScript configuration (strict: true in tsconfig.json).\n- Prefer interfaces for public APIs, types for internal structures.\n- Use readonly for immutable properties and ReadonlyArray<T> for immutable arrays.\n- Leverage type guards and discriminated unions for type safety.\n- Use async/await over raw Promises for better readability.\n- Prefer const for immutable bindings, never use var.\n- Use template literals over string concatenation.\n- Leverage destructuring for objects and arrays.\n- Use optional chaining (?.) and nullish coalescing (??) operators.\n- Prefer functional array methods (map, filter, reduce) over loops.\n- Use enums or const objects with ''as const'' for constants.\n- Avoid ''any'' type; use ''unknown'' when type is truly unknown.\n- Use generics for reusable type-safe components.\n- Follow naming conventions: PascalCase for types/interfaces, camelCase for variables/functions.\n- Use ESLint with TypeScript rules for code quality.\n- Prefer named exports over default exports for better refactoring.\n- Use utility types (Partial, Pick, Omit, Record) appropriately.\n- Document complex types and public APIs with JSDoc comments.\n\n## Prompt\n\n**Test-Driven Bug Fixing**:\n1. Write a failing test that reproduces the bug (TDD Red)\n2. Fix the code to make the test pass (TDD Green)\n3. Refactor if needed while keeping tests green (TDD Refactor)\n4. This ensures the bug won''t regress\n\nProcess:\n1. Analyze the error message and stack trace\n2. Examine the relevant code\n3. Identify the root cause\n4. **Write a failing test that reproduces the bug**\n5. Propose a minimal fix\n6. **Verify the test now passes**\n7. Add additional tests for edge cases\n\n\n## Constraints\n\n- ALWAYS write a failing test that reproduces the bug BEFORE fixing it.\n- Tests must be automated and executable via test runner.\n- Propose minimal changes that fix the root cause.\n- Do not introduce new bugs or side effects.\n- Verify the fix by running the test and confirming it passes.\n- Add regression tests to prevent the bug from reoccurring.\n\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:21:57.552Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Analysis Agents requiring precise automated regression testing and bug fixing capabilities.","zh":"适合需要精确自动回归测试和错误修复功能的代码分析代理。","ja":"正確な自動回帰テストおよびバグ修正機能を必要とするコード分析エージェントに最適です。","ko":"정확한 자동 회귀 테스트 및 버그 수정 기능을 필요로 하는 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de análisis de código que requieren pruebas de regresión automatizadas precisas y capacidades de depuración de errores.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse de code nécessitant des tests de régression automatisés précis et des capacités de correction de bogues.","de":"Ideal für Code-Analyse-Agents, die präzise automatisierte Regressionstests und Fehlersuche-Funktionen erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise de Código que exigem testes de regressão automatizados precisos e capacidades de correção de bugs.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа кода, требующих точного автоматизированного тестирования регрессии и возможностей исправления ошибок.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تحليل الشفرة التي تتطلب اختبارات انحدار آلية دقيقة وقدرات إصلاح الأعطال."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to diagnose and fix bugs in code with automated regression tests, utilizing precise and accurate responses to identify root causes and propose minimal, correct fixes, ensuring adherence to user requirements and verification of complex tasks.","zh":"赋予代理诊断和修复代码中的错误的能力，利用自动回归测试，通过精确和准确的响应来识别根本原因并提出最小且正确的修复，确保遵守用户要求并验证复杂任务。","ja":"エージェントにコード内のバグを診断して修正する能力を与え、自動回帰テストを使用して、正確で正確なレスポンスによって根本原因を特定し、最小限で正しい修正を提案し、ユーザーの要件に従って複雑なタスクを検証します。","ko":"에이전트가 코드 내의 버그를 진단하고 수정할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 자동 회귀 테스트를 사용하고, 정확하고 정확한 응답을 통해根本 원인을 식별하고 최소한의 올바른 수정을 제안하여 사용자의 요구 사항을 준수하고 복잡한 작업을 검증합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a diagnosticar y corregir errores en el código con pruebas de regresión automatizadas, utilizando respuestas precisas y exactas para identificar las causas raíz y proponer soluciones mínimas y correctas, garantizando el cumplimiento de los requisitos del usuario y la verificación de tareas complejas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de diagnostiquer et de corriger les bogues dans le code avec des tests de régression automatisés, en utilisant des réponses précises et exactes pour identifier les causes profondes et proposer des corrections minimales et correctes, en garantissant le respect des exigences de l''utilisateur et la vérification de tâches complexes.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Fehler im Code mit automatisierten Regressionstests zu diagnostizieren und zu beheben, indem präzise und genaue Antworten verwendet werden, um die Ursachen zu identifizieren und minimale, korrekte Lösungen vorzuschlagen, um die Einhaltung der Benutzeranforderungen und die Überprüfung komplexer Aufgaben sicherzustellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a diagnosticar e corrigir bugs no código com testes de regressão automatizados, utilizando respostas precisas e exatas para identificar causas raiz e propor correções mínimas e corretas, garantindo a aderência aos requisitos do usuário e verificação de tarefas complexas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью диагностировать и исправлять ошибки в коде с помощью автоматизированных тестов регрессии, используя точные и правильные ответы для выявления коренных причин и предложения минимальных и правильных исправлений, обеспечивая соблюдение требований пользователя и проверку сложных задач.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تشخيص وإصلاح الأعطال في الشفرة باستخدام اختبارات الانحدار الآلية، واستخدام استجابات دقيقة ومدقة لتحديد الأسباب الجذرية واقتراح إصلاحات صحيحة وملائمة، وضمان الالتزام بمتطلبات المستخدم وتحقق المهام المعقدة."},"useCases":{"en":["Diagnosing bugs in codebases with automated regression tests","Proposing minimal, correct fixes for identified bugs","Verifying bug fixes through precise and accurate automated testing"],"zh":["使用自动回归测试诊断代码库中的错误","为识别出的错误提出最小且正确的修复","通过精确和准确的自动测试验证错误修复"],"ja":["自動回帰テストを使用してコードベース内のバグを診断する","特定されたバグの最小限で正しい修正を提案する","精密で正確な自動テストを使用してバグ修正を検証する"],"ko":["자동 회귀 테스트를 사용하여 코드베이스 내의 버그를 진단한다","식별된 버그에 대한 최소한의 올바른 수정을 제안한다","정확하고 정확한 자동 테스트를 사용하여 버그 수정을 검증한다"],"es":["Diagnosticar errores en bases de código con pruebas de regresión automatizadas","Proponer soluciones mínimas y correctas para errores identificados","Verificar soluciones de errores a través de pruebas automatizadas precisas y exactas"],"fr":["Diagnostiquer les bogues dans les bases de code avec des tests de régression automatisés","Proposer des corrections minimales et correctes pour les bogues identifiés","Vérifier les corrections de bogues via des tests automatisés précis et exacts"],"de":["Fehler in Codebasen mit automatisierten Regressionstests diagnostizieren","Minimale, korrekte Lösungen für identifizierte Fehler vorschlagen","Fehlerbehebungen durch präzise und genaue automatisierte Tests überprüfen"],"pt":["Diagnosticar bugs em bases de código com testes de regressão automatizados","Propor correções mínimas e corretas para bugs identificados","Verificar correções de bugs por meio de testes automatizados precisos e exatos"],"ru":["Диагностика ошибок в кодовых базах с помощью автоматизированных тестов регрессии","Предложение минимальных и правильных исправлений для выявленных ошибок","Проверка исправлений ошибок с помощью точных и правильных автоматизированных тестов"],"ar":["تشخيص الأعطال في قواعد الشفرة باستخدام اختبارات الانحدار الآلية","اقتراح إصلاحات ملائمة وصحيحة للأعطال المحددة","تحقق من إصلاح الأعطال من خلال الاختبارات الآلية الدقيقة والمدقة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires precise and accurate input to function effectively","May require additional clarification or verification for complex bugs","Assumes user has necessary permissions and access to modify code"],"zh":["需要精确和准确的输入才能有效地运行","可能需要额外的澄清或验证以处理复杂的错误","假设用户具有必要的权限和访问代码的权限"],"ja":["効果的に動作するには正確で正確な入力が必要","複雑なバグの場合、追加の明確化または検証が必要になる可能性がある","ユーザーがコードを変更するために必要な権限とアクセス権を持っていることを前提としている"],"ko":["유효하게 작동하려면 정확하고 정확한 입력이 필요하다","복잡한 버그의 경우 추가적인 명확화 또는 검증이 필요할 수 있다","사용자가 코드를 수정하기 위해 필요한 권한과 접근 권한을 가지고 있다고 가정한다"],"es":["Requiere una entrada precisa y exacta para funcionar de manera efectiva","Puede requerir una clarificación o verificación adicionales para errores complejos","Supone que el usuario tiene los permisos y el acceso necesarios para modificar el código"],"fr":["Nécessite une entrée précise et exacte pour fonctionner de manière efficace","Peut nécessiter une clarification ou une vérification supplémentaires pour des bogues complexes","Suppose que l''utilisateur a les autorisations et l''accès nécessaires pour modifier le code"],"de":["Benötigt präzise und genaue Eingaben, um effektiv zu funktionieren","Kann zusätzliche Klarstellungen oder Überprüfungen für komplexe Fehler erfordern","Geht davon aus, dass der Benutzer die notwendigen Berechtigungen und Zugriffsrechte hat, um den Code zu ändern"],"pt":["Exige entrada precisa e exata para funcionar de forma eficaz","Pode exigir esclarecimentos adicionais ou verificação para bugs complexos","Supõe que o usuário tem as permissões e acesso necessários para modificar o código"],"ru":["Требует точного и правильного ввода для эффективной работы","Может потребовать дополнительного разъяснения или проверки для сложных ошибок","Предполагает, что пользователь имеет необходимые разрешения и доступ для изменения кода"],"ar":["يتطلب إدخالًا دقيقًا ومدقّقًا للعمل بشكل فعال","يمكن أن يتطلب توضيحات إضافية أو التحقق من الأعطال المعقدة","يفترض أن المستخدم لديه الأذونات والوصول اللازمين لتعديل الشفرة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('davidkelley/searchlite/bug-hunting', 'community', 'davidkelley', 'searchlite', 'davidkelley/searchlite', 'bug-hunting', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.446Z', '2026-02-18T06:21:57.493Z', NULL, '{"id":"davidkelley/searchlite/bug-hunting","name":"bug-hunting","description":{"zh":"Bug Hunting 技术是用于发现和修复 Searchlite 实现中的真实 bug，确保代码的正确性和可靠性","ja":"バグハンティングスキルは、Searchlite の実装における実際のバグを発見して修復するために使用され、コードの正確性と信頼性を確保する","ko":"버그 헌팅 기술은 Searchlite 구현에서 실제 버그를 발견하고 수정하여 코드의 정확성과 안정성을 보장하는 데 사용된다","es":"La búsqueda de errores es una técnica de depuración que permite encontrar y arreglar errores de manera eficiente","fr":"La chasse aux bogues est une technique de débogage qui permet de trouver et de corriger les erreurs de manière efficace","de":"Die Fehlerjagd ist eine Fehlersuche-Technik, die es ermöglicht, Fehler effizient zu finden und zu beheben","pt":"A caça de bugs é uma técnica de detecção de erros que utiliza o Searchlite, uma engine de busca embutida em Rust, para encontrar erros reais na implementação","ru":"Охота за багами - это техника обнаружения ошибок, которая использует Searchlite, встроенный поисковый движок на Rust, для обнаружения реальных ошибок в реализации","ar":"صيد الأخطاء هو تقنية لاكتشاف الأخطاء التي تستخدم Searchlite، محرك بحث مدمج في Rust، لاكتشاف الأخطاء الفعلية في التنفيذ","en":"🔍 Searchlite is an embedded search engine that keeps a single on‑disk index and exposes a clean Rust API, CLI, and optional C/WASM bindings. It offers BM25 with phrase matching, filters/aggregations, stored fields, highlighting, and optional vectors/GPU stubs for fast, schema-driven full‑text se..."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Bug Hunting 技术","ja":"バグハンティングスキル","ko":"버그 헌팅 기술","es":"Búsqueda de errores: técnica de depuración avanzada","fr":"Chasse aux bogues: technique de débogage avancée","de":"Fehlerjagd: Fortgeschrittene Fehlersuche-Technik","pt":"Caça de Bugs: Técnica de Detecção de Erros","ru":"Охота за багами: Техника обнаружения ошибок","ar":"صيد الأخطاء: تقنية الكشف عن الأخطاء","en":"bug-hunting"},"description":{"zh":"Bug Hunting 技术是用于发现和修复 Searchlite 实现中的真实 bug，确保代码的正确性和可靠性","ja":"バグハンティングスキルは、Searchlite の実装における実際のバグを発見して修復するために使用され、コードの正確性と信頼性を確保する","ko":"버그 헌팅 기술은 Searchlite 구현에서 실제 버그를 발견하고 수정하여 코드의 정확성과 안정성을 보장하는 데 사용된다","es":"La búsqueda de errores es una técnica de depuración que permite encontrar y arreglar errores de manera eficiente","fr":"La chasse aux bogues est une technique de débogage qui permet de trouver et de corriger les erreurs de manière efficace","de":"Die Fehlerjagd ist eine Fehlersuche-Technik, die es ermöglicht, Fehler effizient zu finden und zu beheben","pt":"A caça de bugs é uma técnica de detecção de erros que utiliza o Searchlite, uma engine de busca embutida em Rust, para encontrar erros reais na implementação","ru":"Охота за багами - это техника обнаружения ошибок, которая использует Searchlite, встроенный поисковый движок на Rust, для обнаружения реальных ошибок в реали...","ar":"صيد الأخطاء هو تقنية لاكتشاف الأخطاء التي تستخدم Searchlite، محرك بحث مدمج في Rust، لاكتشاف الأخطاء الفعلية في التنفيذ","en":"🔍 Searchlite is an embedded search engine that keeps a single on‑disk index and exposes a clean Rust API, CLI, and optional C/WASM bindings. It offers BM25 ..."},"definition":{"en":"🔍 Searchlite is an embedded search engine that keeps a single on‑disk index and exposes a clean Rust API, CLI, and optional C/WASM bindings. It offers BM25 with phrase matching, filters/aggregations, stored fields, highlighting, and optional vectors/GPU stubs for fast, schema-driven full‑text search in a small footprint."},"features":{"zh":["高效的 bug 定位","代码的正确性和可靠性","Searchlite 集成","BM25 和短语匹配","过滤和聚合"],"ja":["バグの効率的な特定","コードの正確性と信頼性","Searchlite 統合","BM25 とフレーズマッチング","フィルタと集計"],"ko":["버그의 효율적인 식별","코드의 정확성과 안정성","Searchlite 통합","BM25 및 구문 일치","필터링 및 집계"],"es":["Reproducción de errores","Análisis de durabilidad","Pruebas de regresión","Depuración avanzada","Técnica de búsqueda de errores"],"fr":["Reproduction d''erreurs","Analyse de durabilité","Tests de régression","Débogage avancé","Technique de chasse aux bogues"],"de":["Fehlerreproduktion","Haltbarkeitsanalyse","Rückschrittstests","Fortgeschrittene Fehlersuche","Fehlerjagd-Technik"],"pt":["Utiliza o Searchlite, uma engine de busca embutida em Rust","Técnica de detecção de erros para encontrar erros reais","Fornece uma API limpa em Rust, CLI e bindings opcionais em C/WASM","Oferece BM25 com correspondência de frases, filtros/agregações, campos armazenados, realce e vetores/GPU opcionais"],"ru":["Использует Searchlite, встроенный поисковый движок на Rust","Техника обнаружения ошибок для обнаружения реальных ошибок","Предоставляет чистый API на Rust, CLI и необязательные привязки на C/WASM","Предлагает BM25 с фразовой соответствием, фильтрами/агрегациями, хранимыми полями, подсветкой и необязательными векторами/GPU"],"ar":["تستخدم Searchlite، محرك بحث مدمج في Rust","تقنية لاكتشاف الأخطاء لاكتشاف الأخطاء الفعلية","توفر واجهة برمجة تطبيقات نظيفة في Rust، CLI وربطات اختيارية في C/WASM","توفر BM25 مع مطابقة الجمل، مرشحات/مجمعات، حقول مخزنة، تمييز ومتجهات/GPU اختيارية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["bug hunting","Searchlite","代码优化","错误修复","高效搜索","BM25","短语匹配"],"ja":["バグハンティング","Searchlite","コード最適化","エラーキュレーション","効率的な検索","BM25","フレーズマッチング"],"ko":["버그 헌팅","Searchlite","코드 최적화","오류 수정","효율적인 검색","BM25","구문 일치"],"es":["búsqueda de errores","depuración","pruebas de regresión","análisis de durabilidad","reproducción de errores","técnica de búsqueda de errores","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["chasse aux bogues","débogage","tests de régression","analyse de durabilité","reproduction d''erreurs","technique de chasse aux bogues","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Fehlerjagd","Fehlersuche","Rückschrittstests","Haltbarkeitsanalyse","Fehlerreproduktion","Fehlerjagd-Technik","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["caça de bugs","detecção de erros","Searchlite","Rust","engine de busca embutida","técnica de detecção de erros","BM25","correspondência de frases","filtros/agregações"],"ru":["охота за багами","обнаружение ошибок","Searchlite","Rust","встроенный поисковый движок","техника обнаружения ошибок","BM25","фразовая соответствием","фильтры/агрегациями"],"ar":["صيد الأخطاء","اكتشاف الأخطاء","Searchlite","Rust","محرك بحث مدمج","تقنية اكتشاف الأخطاء","BM25","مطابقة الجمل","مرشحات/مجمعات"]}},"owner":"davidkelley","repo":"searchlite","repoPath":"davidkelley/searchlite","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.446Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"bug-hunting","description":"Structured workflow for discovering, reproducing, and fixing bugs in Searchlite by inspecting real code paths (CLI/HTTP/core), validating durability invariants, and producing regression tests; use when investigating incorrect results, crashes, data loss risks, or “it sometimes fails” reports.","bodyPreview":"# Bug Hunting Workflow\n\n## Intent\n\nThis skill is for **finding real bugs in the implementation**, not guessing. It forces a discovery phase (build a mental model, reproduce, narrow scope) before making changes.\n\nYou must prioritize:\n\n1. correctness and durability\n2. clear reproduction\n3. minimal fix + regression test\n\n---\n\n## Non-negotiable rules\n\n- **No fix without a reproduction** (a failing test, a minimal repro program, or a deterministic HTTP/CLI script).\n- **No durability regressions**: do","body":"# Bug Hunting Workflow\n\n## Intent\n\nThis skill is for **finding real bugs in the implementation**, not guessing. It forces a discovery phase (build a mental model, reproduce, narrow scope) before making changes.\n\nYou must prioritize:\n\n1. correctness and durability\n2. clear reproduction\n3. minimal fix + regression test\n\n---\n\n## Non-negotiable rules\n\n- **No fix without a reproduction** (a failing test, a minimal repro program, or a deterministic HTTP/CLI script).\n- **No durability regressions**: do not weaken WAL/manifest/atomic rename/fsync ordering.\n- **No “drive-by refactors”** while bug hunting; keep patches tight and reviewable.\n- After changes, you must run the full quality suite from `code-quality`.\n\n---\n\n## Discovery phase (required)\n\n### 0) Establish the boundaries\n\nBefore opening files, answer (in notes) these questions:\n\n- Which surface is affected? **CLI**, **HTTP**, **embedded API**, **wasm**, or **ffi**?\n- Is it a **correctness** issue (wrong results), **durability** issue (lost/duplicated data), or **stability** issue (panic/hang)?\n- Does it require a specific feature flag (`vectors`, `zstd`, `gpu`, wasm/IndexedDB, ffi)?\n- Is the failure deterministic or intermittent?\n\n### 1) Baseline the repo (don’t trust your local state)\n\nRun in workspace root:\n\n- `cargo fmt --all`\n- `cargo clippy --all --all-features --all-targets -- -D warnings`\n- `cargo test --all --all-features`\n\nIf anything fails here, you may be chasing a known failure; fix/resolve that first.\n\n### 2) Map the architecture you’re about to debug\n\nCreate a quick map in notes (1–2 minutes):\n\n- `searchlite-core`: schema, indexing, WAL/manifest, segments, query execution, filters/aggs, vectors\n- `searchlite-cli`: user-facing commands and JSON output formatting\n- `searchlite-http`: endpoints (/init, /add, /bulk, /delete, /commit, /refresh, /search, /inspect, /stats, /compact), limits/timeouts/concurrency\n- `searchlite-wasm`: bindings + IndexedDB storage semantics (no fsync)\n- `searchlite-ffi`: C ABI / safety edges\n\nThis map guides where you look first.\n\n### 3) Reproduce the bug with the smallest possible corpus\n\nProduce a “minimal reproducible case” artifact set:\n\n- a schema JSON (small)\n- a small NDJSON/doc list (5–50 docs)\n- one request (HTTP JSON or CLI command) that fails\n\nFor HTTP:\n\n- include the server flags/env (bind addr, index path, max-body-bytes, max-concurrency, request-timeout, refresh-on-commit)\n\nFor CLI:\n\n- include exact commands and any flags\n\n**Goal:** a script a teammate can run in <60 seconds.\n\n### 4) Turn on observability (don’t add prints yet)\n\nUse existing debugging features first:\n\n- For search correctness: add `explain: true` to the request.\n- For performance/odd slowdowns while reproducing: add `profile: true`.\n- For server behavior: run with `RUST_LOG=debug` (or more targeted module filters) and capture the relevant lines.\n\nIf your issue is “writes not visible,” verify lifecycle:\n\n- you must `commit`\n- you may need `/refresh` in HTTP depending on config\n\n### 5) Narrow the fault line by bisecting the pipeline\n\nPick one axis at a time:\n\n**Correctness axis**\n\n- Does the doc get ingested successfully?\n- Does it appear in `/stats` documents?\n- Does `/inspect` show a new segment after commit?\n- Does the query match in bm25 mode vs wand/bmw mode?\n\n**Durability axis**\n\n- Is WAL appended correctly?\n- Is manifest updated atomically?\n- Is WAL truncated only after manifest persistence?\n- After restart, does replay do the expected thing?\n\n**HTTP axis**\n\n- Is the request being rejected due to max body / timeouts / concurrency?\n- Is NDJSON streaming partial and rolling back?\n- Are errors correctly surfaced as `{\"error\":{\"type\",\"reason\"}}`?\n\n### 6) Perform a targeted static sweep of the suspected modules\n\nOnce you know the rough area, do a deliberate scan for bug smells:\n\nSearch patterns to grep/ripgrep for in the relevant crate:\n\n- panics: `unwrap()`, `expect(`, `panic!`, `unreachable!`, `todo!`\n- suspicious error handling: `map_err(|_|`, `ok()?` in non-optional contexts, silent `let _ =`\n- integer edge cases: casts (`as usize`), underflow (`- 1`), unchecked indexing\n- concurrency hazards: `Mutex`/`RwLock` lock ordering, `.await` while holding locks, channels without bounds\n- IO hazards: missing `fsync`, non-atomic file replace, partial writes not handled, directory fsync omissions\n- schema mismatch hazards: stringly-typed field lookups, analyzer lookup defaults, missing nested path validation\n- vector hazards: dimension mismatch, normalization assumptions, unchecked candidate sizing, `NaN` propagation\n\nYou are not “fixing” in this step—just identifying suspects.\n\n### 7) Dynamic bug probes by subsystem (choose what fits)\n\n#### A) WAL / manifest / commit / rollback\n\nIf you suspect commit/durability issues:\n\n- Reproduce a crash-window scenario:\n  1. ingest docs\n  2. start commit\n  3. force termination mid-way (or simulate via test hooks if present)\n  4. restart and observe replay\n- Validate the invariants:\n  - manifest atomic update (rename) and directory sync\n  - WAL truncation happens after manifest sync\n  - rollback cleans new segment artifacts\n\nIf you can’t safely crash in tests, create a unit test around writer/commit phases and validate state.\n\n#### B) Segment lifecycle / compaction / cleanup\n\nIf you see duplicates, ghosts, or bloat:\n\n- Inspect segments via `inspect` and compare to `stats`\n- Run compaction and verify:\n  - live docs preserved\n  - deleted/tombstoned dropped\n  - old segment files removed (or expected to remain until cleanup)\n\n#### C) Query execution modes\n\nIf you suspect scoring/pruning bugs:\n\n- Run the same query with `execution=bm25`, `execution=wand`, `execution=bmw`\n- Results should match for deterministic corpora (unless the contract explicitly says otherwise)\n- If they diverge, you likely have a pruning-bound bug or block-max metadata mismatch\n\n#### D) Filters/aggs/nested correctness\n\nIf filters/aggs are wrong:\n\n- Verify required fields are `fast: true`\n- For nested, verify the filter uses a `Nested` block and that clauses bind to the same object instance\n- Add a repro doc with two nested objects that would catch “cross-object” leakage\n\n#### E) Vectors (feature `vectors`)\n\nIf vector behavior is wrong:\n\n- Check dimension mismatch handling\n- Check cosine normalization expectations\n- Confirm ANN parameters (`candidate_size`, `ef_search`) don’t overflow or accept nonsensical values\n- Verify hybrid search doesn’t double-count or drop vector scores\n\n---\n\n## Fix phase (required)\n\n### 1) Write the failing regression test first\n\n- Prefer a unit test in the most local crate if possible.\n- If the bug is surface-level behavior (HTTP contract, CLI output), add an integration test.\n- Make it deterministic and small.\n- Assert on structure, not strings (parse JSON output).\n\n### 2) Implement the minimal fix\n\n- Tight patch, minimal diff.\n- Keep durability semantics intact.\n- Avoid introducing allocations/locks in hot paths unless justified.\n\n### 3) Prove it\n\nRun:\n\n- `cargo test --all --all-features`\n- Any relevant examples (e.g. pruning example if you touched pruning logic)\n- If the bug touched performance-sensitive code, run the relevant bench before/after.\n\n### 4) Add a “root cause” note\n\nIn the PR description or internal notes, include:\n\n- symptom\n- root cause\n- why the fix is correct\n- what test prevents regressions\n\n---\n\n## Output format (what Codex should produce)\n\nWhen using this skill, produce:\n\n1. **Repro artifact** (schema + docs + request/command)\n2. **Fault localization** (files + functions involved)\n3. **Root cause analysis**\n4. **Fix plan** (minimal changes)\n5. **Regression test** (where it lives and what it asserts)\n6. **Validation commands run** (from code-quality)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:21:57.493Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Debugging Agents needing systematic bug-hunting capabilities with BM25 and phrase matching","zh":"适合需要系统性的错误追踪能力并使用BM25和短语匹配的调试代理","ja":"デバッグエージェントが体系的なバグハンティング機能を必要とする場合に適しています。BM25とフレーズマッチングを使用します","ko":"시스템적인 버그 헌팅 기능과 BM25 및 문구 일치를 사용하여 디버깅 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Perfect for Debugging Agents needing systematic bug-hunting capabilities with BM25 and phrase matching","fr":"Perfect for Debugging Agents needing systematic bug-hunting capabilities with BM25 and phrase matching","de":"Perfect for Debugging Agents needing systematic bug-hunting capabilities with BM25 and phrase matching","pt":"Perfeito para agentes de depuração que necessitam de capacidades de caça a bugs sistemáticas com BM25 e correspondência de frases","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов отладки, требующих системных возможностей поиска ошибок с BM25 и фразовым совпадением","ar":"مثالي لعميل تصحيح الأخطاء الذي يحتاج إلى قدرات صيد أخطاء منهجية مع BM25 وطابقات الجملة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to reproduce and fix bugs using a clean Rust API, CLI, and optional C/WASM bindings, ensuring correctness and durability with minimal fix and regression testing, and leveraging filters, aggregations, and stored fields","zh":"赋予代理使用干净的Rust API、CLI和可选的C/WASM绑定来重现和修复错误，确保正确性和耐用性，通过最小的修复和回归测试，并利用过滤器、聚合和存储字段","ja":"クリーンなRust API、CLI、およびオプションのC/WASMバインディングを使用してエージェントがバグを再現して修正できるようにし、正しさと耐用性を確保します。フィルタ、集約、およびストアドフィールドを利用して、最小限の修正とリグレッションテストを実行します","ko":"클린한 러스트 API, CLI 및 선택적 C/WASM 바인딩을 사용하여 에이전트가 버그를 재현하고 수정할 수 있도록 하여, 정확성과 내구성을 보장하며, 필터, 집계 및 저장 필드를 활용하여 최소한의 수정 및 회귀 테스트를 수행합니다","es":"Empowers agents to reproduce and fix bugs using a clean Rust API, CLI, and optional C/WASM bindings, ensuring correctness and durability with minimal fix and regression testing, and leveraging filters, aggregations, and stored fields","fr":"Empowers agents to reproduce and fix bugs using a clean Rust API, CLI, and optional C/WASM bindings, ensuring correctness and durability with minimal fix and regression testing, and leveraging filters, aggregations, and stored fields","de":"Empowers agents to reproduce and fix bugs using a clean Rust API, CLI, and optional C/WASM bindings, ensuring correctness and durability with minimal fix and regression testing, and leveraging filters, aggregations, and stored fields","pt":"Habilita os agentes a reproduzir e corrigir erros usando uma API Rust limpa, CLI e ligação C/WASM opcional, garantindo a correção e a durabilidade com teste de correção e regressão mínimo, e aproveitando filtros, agregações e campos armazenados","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью воспроизводить и исправлять ошибки с помощью чистого API Rust, CLI и необязательных связей C/WASM, обеспечивая правильность и долговечность с минимальным исправлением и тестированием на регрессию, и использует фильтры, агрегации и хранимые поля","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من إعادة إنتاج وإصلاح الأخطاء باستخدام واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Rust نظيفة وواجهة سطر الأوامر وربط C/WASM اختياري ، مما يضمن الدقة والمتانة مع إصلاح اختبار الانحدار الأدنى ، واستخدام المرشحات والتجميعات والحقول المخزنة"},"useCases":{"en":["Reproducing bugs with failing tests or minimal repro programs","Narrowing scope and identifying root causes of issues","Creating regression tests to prevent durability regressions"],"zh":["使用失败的测试或最小重现程序重现错误","缩小范围并确定问题的根cause","创建回归测试以防止耐用性回归"],"ja":["失敗したテストまたは最小のリプロダクションプログラムを使用してバグを再現する","範囲を狭めていくことで問題の根本原因を特定する","耐用性の回帰を防ぐためにリグレッションテストを作成する"],"ko":["실패한 테스트 또는 최소한의 재현 프로그램을 사용하여 버그를 재현하는 것","범위를 좁혀 문제의 근본 원인을 식별하는 것","내구성의 회귀를 방지하기 위해 회귀 테스트를 생성하는 것"],"es":["Reproducing bugs with failing tests or minimal repro programs","Narrowing scope and identifying root causes of issues","Creating regression tests to prevent durability regressions"],"fr":["Reproducing bugs with failing tests or minimal repro programs","Narrowing scope and identifying root causes of issues","Creating regression tests to prevent durability regressions"],"de":["Reproducing bugs with failing tests or minimal repro programs","Narrowing scope and identifying root causes of issues","Creating regression tests to prevent durability regressions"],"pt":["Reproduzir bugs com testes com falha ou programas de reprodução mínimos","Reduzir o escopo e identificar as causas raiz dos problemas","Criar testes de regressão para prevenir regressões de durabilidade"],"ru":["Воспроизводить ошибки с неудачными тестами или минимальными программами воспроизведения","Сужать объем и определять коренные причины проблем","Создавать тесты на регрессию для предотвращения регрессий долговечности"],"ar":["إعادة إنتاج الأخطاء مع اختبارات فاشلة أو برامج إعادة إنتاج مهمة","تقليل النطاق وتحديد الأسباب الجذرية للمشاكل","إنشاء اختبارات الانحدار لمنع انحدارات المتانة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires a reproduction step before making changes","No fix without a failing test, minimal repro program, or deterministic script","Limited to schema-driven full-text search with optional vectors and GPU stubs"],"zh":["需要在修改之前进行再现步骤","没有失败的测试、最小重现程序或确定性脚本就无法修复","仅限于架构驱动的全文搜索，具有可选的向量和GPU存根"],"ja":["変更を加える前に再現ステップが必要","失敗したテスト、最小のリプロダクションプログラム、または決定性スクリプトがないと修正できない","スキーマ駆動の全文検索のみ、オプションのベクトルとGPUスタブ"],"ko":["수정하기 전에 재현 단계가 필요함","실패한 테스트, 최소한의 재현 프로그램 또는 결정적 스크립트가 없으면 수정할 수 없음","스키마 구동의 전체 텍스트 검색만 해당하며, 선택적인 벡터 및 GPU 스텁을 사용할 수 있음"],"es":["Requires a reproduction step before making changes","No fix without a failing test, minimal repro program, or deterministic script","Limited to schema-driven full-text search with optional vectors and GPU stubs"],"fr":["Requires a reproduction step before making changes","No fix without a failing test, minimal repro program, or deterministic script","Limited to schema-driven full-text search with optional vectors and GPU stubs"],"de":["Requires a reproduction step before making changes","No fix without a failing test, minimal repro program, or deterministic script","Limited to schema-driven full-text search with optional vectors and GPU stubs"],"pt":["Exige uma etapa de reprodução antes de fazer alterações","Sem correção sem um teste com falha, programa de reprodução mínimo ou script determinístico","Limitado à pesquisa de texto completo baseada em esquema com vetores e suportes GPU opcionais"],"ru":["Требует шага воспроизведения перед внесением изменений","Нет исправления без неудачного теста, минимальной программы воспроизведения или детерминированного скрипта","Ограничен поиском полного текста, основанному на схеме, с необязательными векторами и заглушками GPU"],"ar":["يتطلب خطوة إعادة إنتاج قبل إجراء التغييرات","لا يوجد إصلاح بدون اختبار فاشل أو برنامج إعادة إنتاج أدنى أو سيناريو محدد","محدود بالبحث النصي الكامل القائم على المخطط مع متجهات وخدع GPU اختيارية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
