ra convertir libros en datos de entrenamiento y modelos de transferencia de estilo","fr":"La pipeline de livre SFT est un système complet pour convertir des livres en données d''entraînement et des modèles de transfert de style","de":"Die Buch-SFT-Pipeline ist ein vollständiges System zur Umwandlung von Büchern in Trainingsdaten und Stil-Transfer-Modelle","pt":"O pipeline de livros SFT é um sistema completo para converter livros em conjuntos de dados SFT e treinar modelos de transferência de estilo.","ru":"Конвейер книг SFT - это полная система для преобразования книг в наборы данных SFT и обучения моделей переноса стиля.","ar":"pipeline كتاب SFT هو نظام كامل لتحويل الكتب إلى مجموعات بيانات SFT وتدريب نماذج نقل الأسلوب.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["ePubSFT","SFT","TinkerSFT","SFT","SFT","SFT"],"ja":["ePubSFT","SFT","TinkerSFT","SFT","SFT","SFT"],"ko":["ePubSFT","SFT","TinkerSFT","SFT","SFT","SFT"],"es":["Conversión de libros en datos de entrenamiento","Creación de modelos de transferencia de estilo","Preparación de datos de entrenamiento para plataformas de SFT","Diseño de pipelines de segmentación de texto para contenido de larga forma","Entrenamiento de modelos de lenguaje pequeños"],"fr":["Conversion de livres en données d''entraînement","Création de modèles de transfert de style","Préparation de données d''entraînement pour les plateformes de SFT","Conception de pipelines de segmentation de texte pour le contenu de longue forme","Entraînement de modèles de langage petits"],"de":["Umwandlung von Büchern in Trainingsdaten","Erstellung von Stil-Transfer-Modellen","Vorbereitung von Trainingsdaten für SFT-Plattformen","Entwurf von Textsegmentierungspipelines für Langform-Inhalte","Training von kleinen Sprachmodellen"],"pt":["Conversão de livros em conjuntos de dados SFT","Treinamento de modelos de transferência de estilo","Criação de pipelines de processamento de texto para conteúdo de longa forma","Preparação de dados para plataformas de treinamento de modelos","Segmentação de texto para conteúdo de longa forma"],"ru":["Преобразование книг в наборы данных SFT","Обучение моделей переноса стиля","Разработка конвейеров обработки текста для контента большой длины","Подготовка данных для платформ обучения моделей","Сегментация текста для контента большой длины"],"ar":["تحويل الكتب إلى مجموعات بيانات SFT","تدريب نماذج نقل الأسلوب","إنشاء أنابيب معالجة النصوص لل nội dung الطويل","إعداد بيانات لمنصات تدريب النماذج","تقسيم النصوص لل nội dung الطويل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Book SFT Pipeline","SFT","ePubSFT","TinkerSFT","SFT","SFT","SFT","SFT"],"ja":["Book SFT Pipeline","SFT","ePubSFT","TinkerSFT","SFT","SFT","SFT","SFT"],"ko":["Book SFT Pipeline","SFT","ePubSFT","TinkerSFT","SFT","SFT","SFT","SFT"],"es":["pipeline de libro SFT","conversión de libros","datos de entrenamiento","modelos de transferencia de estilo","plataformas de SFT","segmentación de texto","entrenamiento de modelos de lenguaje"],"fr":["pipeline de livre SFT","conversion de livres","données d''entraînement","modèles de transfert de style","plateformes de SFT","segmentation de texte","entraînement de modèles de langage"],"de":["Buch-SFT-Pipeline","Umwandlung von Büchern","Trainingsdaten","Stil-Transfer-Modelle","SFT-Plattformen","Textsegmentierung","Training von Sprachmodellen"],"pt":["pipeline de livros SFT","transferência de estilo","treinamento de modelos","processamento de texto","conteúdo de longa forma","plataformas de treinamento de modelos"],"ru":["конвейер книг SFT","перенос стиля","обучение моделей","обработка текста","контент большой длины","платформы обучения моделей"],"ar":["pipeline كتاب SFT","نقل الأسلوب","تدريب النماذج","معالجة النصوص","نội dung الطويل","منصات تدريب النماذج"]}},"owner":"goodnight000","repo":"KittyCourt","repoPath":"goodnight000/KittyCourt","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.446Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"book-sft-pipeline","description":"End-to-end system for creating supervised fine-tuning datasets from books and training style-transfer models. Covers text extraction, intelligent segmentation, synthetic instruction generation, Tinker-compatible output, LoRA training, and validation.","version":"2.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Book SFT Pipeline\n\nA complete system for converting books into SFT datasets and training style-transfer models. This skill teaches the pipeline from raw ePub to a model that writes in any author''s voice.\n\n## When to Activate\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- Building fine-tuning datasets from literary works\n- Creating author-voice or style-transfer models\n- Preparing training data for Tinker or similar SFT platforms\n- Designing text segmentation pipelines for long-form content\n- Training small mode","body":"# Book SFT Pipeline\n\nA complete system for converting books into SFT datasets and training style-transfer models. This skill teaches the pipeline from raw ePub to a model that writes in any author''s voice.\n\n## When to Activate\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- Building fine-tuning datasets from literary works\n- Creating author-voice or style-transfer models\n- Preparing training data for Tinker or similar SFT platforms\n- Designing text segmentation pipelines for long-form content\n- Training small models (8B or less) on limited data\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### The Three Pillars of Book SFT\n\n**1. Intelligent Segmentation**\nText chunks must be semantically coherent. Breaking mid-sentence teaches the model to produce fragmented output. Target: 150-400 words per chunk, always at natural boundaries.\n\n**2. Diverse Instruction Generation**\nUse multiple prompt templates and system prompts to prevent overfitting. A single prompt style leads to memorization. Use 15+ prompt templates with 5+ system prompts.\n\n**3. Style Over Content**\nThe goal is learning the author''s rhythm and vocabulary patterns, not memorizing plots. Synthetic instructions describe what happens without quoting the text.\n\n## Pipeline Architecture\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    ORCHESTRATOR AGENT                           │\n│  Coordinates pipeline phases, manages state, handles failures   │\n└──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                       │\n       ┌───────────────┼───────────────┬───────────────┐\n       ▼               ▼               ▼               ▼\n┌──────────────┐ ┌──────────────┐ ┌──────────────┐ ┌──────────────┐\n│  EXTRACTION  │ │ SEGMENTATION │ │  INSTRUCTION │ │   DATASET    │\n│    AGENT     │ │    AGENT     │ │    AGENT     │ │   BUILDER    │\n│ ePub → Text  │ │ Text → Chunks│ │ Chunks →     │ │ Pairs →      │\n│              │ │ 150-400 words│ │ Prompts      │ │ JSONL        │\n└──────────────┘ └──────────────┘ └──────────────┘ └──────────────┘\n                       │\n       ┌───────────────┴───────────────┐\n       ▼                               ▼\n┌──────────────┐               ┌──────────────┐\n│   TRAINING   │               │  VALIDATION  │\n│    AGENT     │               │    AGENT     │\n│ LoRA on      │               │ AI detector  │\n│ Tinker       │               │ Originality  │\n└──────────────┘               └──────────────┘\n```\n\n## Phase 1: Text Extraction\n\n### Critical Rules\n1. **Always source ePub over PDF** - OCR errors become learned patterns\n2. **Use paragraph-level extraction** - Extract from `<p>` tags to preserve breaks\n3. **Remove front/back matter** - Copyright and TOC pollute the dataset\n\n```python\n# Extract text from ePub paragraphs\nfrom epub2 import EPub\nfrom bs4 import BeautifulSoup\n\ndef extract_epub(path):\n    book = EPub(path)\n    chapters = []\n    for item in book.flow:\n        html = book.get_chapter(item.id)\n        soup = BeautifulSoup(html, ''html.parser'')\n        paragraphs = [p.get_text().strip() for p in soup.find_all(''p'')]\n        chapters.append(''\\n\\n''.join(p for p in paragraphs if p))\n    return ''\\n\\n''.join(chapters)\n```\n\n## Phase 2: Intelligent Segmentation\n\n### Smaller Chunks + Overlap\n\nSmaller chunks (150-400 words) produce more training examples and better style transfer than larger chunks (250-650).\n\n```python\ndef segment(text, min_words=150, max_words=400):\n    paragraphs = text.split(''\\n\\n'')\n    chunks, buffer, buffer_words = [], [], 0\n    \n    for para in paragraphs:\n        words = len(para.split())\n        if buffer_words + words > max_words and buffer_words >= min_words:\n            chunks.append(''\\n\\n''.join(buffer))\n            # Keep last paragraph for overlap\n            buffer = [buffer[-1], para] if buffer else [para]\n            buffer_words = sum(len(p.split()) for p in buffer)\n        else:\n            buffer.append(para)\n            buffer_words += words\n    \n    if buffer:\n        chunks.append(''\\n\\n''.join(buffer))\n    return chunks\n```\n\n### Expected Results\n\nFor an 86,000-word book:\n- Old method (250-650 words): ~150 chunks\n- New method (150-400 + overlap): ~300 chunks\n- With 2 variants per chunk: 600+ training examples\n\n## Phase 3: Diverse Instruction Generation\n\n### The Key Insight\n\nUsing a single prompt template causes memorization. Diverse templates teach the underlying style.\n\n```python\nSYSTEM_PROMPTS = [\n    \"You are an expert creative writer capable of emulating specific literary styles.\",\n    \"You are a literary writer with deep knowledge of classic prose styles.\",\n    \"You are a creative writer skilled at emulating distinctive authorial voices.\",\n    \"You write prose that captures the essence of modernist literature.\",\n    \"You are a talented writer who can channel classic American authors.\",\n]\n\nPROMPT_TEMPLATES = [\n    \"Write a passage in the style of {author}: {desc}\",\n    \"Channel {author}''s voice to write about: {desc}\",\n    \"In {author}''s distinctive prose style, describe: {desc}\",\n    \"Write this scene as {author} would have: {desc}\",\n    \"Using {author}''s repetitive technique, describe: {desc}\",\n    \"Capture the rhythm of {author} in this passage: {desc}\",\n    \"Write like {author}: {desc}\",\n    \"In the voice of {author}, write: {desc}\",\n    \"This is a literary exercise. Write like {author}: {desc}\",\n    \"Can you write in {author}''s style? {desc}\",\n]\n```\n\n### Instruction Generation\n\n```python\nINSTRUCTION_PROMPT = \"\"\"Describe what is happening in this excerpt in 2-3 sentences.\nFocus on: characters present, actions, emotions, setting.\nDo NOT quote the text directly.\n\nExcerpt:\n{text}\n\"\"\"\n\n# Use a fast, cheap LLM (e.g., Gemini Flash)\ninstruction = llm_call(INSTRUCTION_PROMPT.format(text=chunk))\n```\n\n## Phase 4: Dataset Construction\n\n### Message Format\n\n```json\n{\n    \"messages\": [\n        {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are an expert creative writer...\"},\n        {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Write in the style of Author: Scene description...\"},\n        {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"The actual book text from chunk...\"}\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n### Multiple Variants Per Chunk\n\n```python\ndef build_examples(chunk, instruction, author, variants=2):\n    examples = []\n    for i in range(variants):\n        system = SYSTEM_PROMPTS[i % len(SYSTEM_PROMPTS)]\n        template = PROMPT_TEMPLATES[(chunk.id + i) % len(PROMPT_TEMPLATES)]\n        user = template.format(author=author, desc=instruction)\n        examples.append({\"messages\": [\n            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": system},\n            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": user},\n            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": chunk.text}\n        ]})\n    return examples\n```\n\n## Phase 5: LoRA Training on Tinker\n\n### Configuration\n\n```python\nCONFIG = {\n    \"model_name\": \"Qwen/Qwen3-8B-Base\",  # Base, not instruct\n    \"lora_rank\": 32,                      # 352MB adapter\n    \"learning_rate\": 5e-4,                # Higher for LoRA\n    \"batch_size\": 4,\n    \"epochs\": 3,\n}\n```\n\n### Why Base Model?\n\nUse **base** (pretrained) models, not instruction-tuned versions:\n- Base models are more malleable for new styles\n- Instruct models have patterns that resist overwriting\n- Style is a low-level pattern that base models capture better\n\n### Training Loop\n\n```python\nimport tinker\nfrom tinker import types\n\ntraining_client = await service_client.create_lora_training_client_async(\n    base_model=\"Qwen/Qwen3-8B-Base\",\n    rank=32\n)\n\nfor epoch in range(3):\n    for batch in batches:\n        await training_client.forward_backward_async(batch, loss_fn=\"cross_entropy\")\n        await training_client.optim_step_async(types.AdamParams(learning_rate=5e-4))\n\nresult = await training_client.save_weights_for_sampler_async(name=\"final\")\n```\n\n## Phase 6: Validation\n\n### Modern Scenario Test\n\nTest with scenarios that couldn''t exist in the original book:\n\n```python\nTEST_PROMPTS = [\n    \"Write about a barista making lattes\",\n    \"Describe lovers communicating through text messages\",\n    \"Write about someone anxious about climate change\",\n]\n```\n\nIf the model applies style markers to modern scenarios, it learned **style**, not **content**.\n\n### Originality Verification\n\n```bash\n# Search training data for output phrases\ngrep \"specific phrase from output\" dataset.jsonl\n# Should return: No matches\n```\n\n### AI Detector Testing\n\nTest outputs with GPTZero, Pangram, or ZeroGPT.\n\n## Known Issues and Solutions\n\n### Character Name Leakage\n\n**Symptom**: Model uses original character names in new scenarios.\n**Cause**: Limited name diversity from one book.\n**Solution**: Train on multiple books or add synthetic examples.\n\n### Model Parrots Exact Phrases\n\n**Symptom**: Outputs contain exact sentences from training data.\n**Cause**: Too few prompt variations or too many epochs.\n**Solution**: Use 15+ templates, limit to 3 epochs.\n\n### Fragmented Outputs\n\n**Symptom**: Sentences feel incomplete.\n**Cause**: Poor segmentation breaking mid-thought.\n**Solution**: Always break at paragraph boundaries.\n\n## Guidelines\n\n1. **Always source ePub over PDF** - OCR errors become learned patterns\n2. **Never break mid-sentence** - Boundaries must be grammatically complete\n3. **Use diverse prompts** - 15+ templates, 5+ system prompts\n4. **Use base models** - Not instruct versions\n5. **Use smaller chunks** - 150-400 words for more examples\n6. **Reserve test set** - 50 examples minimum\n7. **Test on modern scenarios** - Proves style transfer vs memorization\n8. **Verify originality** - Grep training data for output phrases\n\n## Expected Results\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| Training examples | 500-1000 per book |\n| Model | Qwen/Qwen3-8B-Base |\n| LoRA rank | 32 |\n| Adapter size | ~350 MB |\n| Training time | ~15 min |\n| Loss reduction | 90%+ |\n| Style transfer success | ~50% perfect |\n\n## Cost Estimate\n\n| Component | Cost |\n|-----------|------|\n| LLM (instruction generation) | ~$0.50 |\n| Tinker training (15 min) | ~$1.50 |\n| **Total** | **~$2.00** |\n\n## Integration with Context Engineering Skills\n\nThis example applies several skills from the Agent Skills for Context Engineering collection:\n\n### project-development\nThe pipeline follows the staged, idempotent architecture pattern:\n- **Acquire**: Extract text from ePub\n- **Prepare**: Segment into training chunks\n- **Process**: Generate synthetic instructions\n- **Parse**: Build message format\n- **Render**: Output Tinker-compatible JSONL\n- **Train**: LoRA fine-tuning\n- **Validate**: Modern scenario testing\n\nEach phase is resumable and produces intermediate artifacts for debugging.\n\n### context-compression\nSegmentation is a form of context compression for training. The core insight from context-compression applies: information density matters more than information quantity. Smaller, coherent chunks (150-400 words) produce better style transfer than larger, diluted chunks.\n\nThe two-tier strategy mirrors context compression evaluation:\n- Tier 1: Fast, deterministic compression\n- Tier 2: LLM-assisted for edge cases\n\n### multi-agent-patterns\nThe pipeline uses the **supervisor/orchestrator** pattern:\n- Orchestrator coordinates phases and manages state\n- Specialized agents (Extraction, Segmentation, Instruction, Builder) have isolated contexts\n- Each agent receives only the information needed for its task\n\nThis matches the principle that sub-agents exist primarily to isolate context rather than simulate roles.\n\n### evaluation\nValidation follows the **end-state evaluation** pattern:\n- Functional testing: Does output match expected style markers?\n- Originality verification: Is content genuinely generated?\n- External validation: AI detector scores\n\nThe \"modern scenario\" test is a form of out-of-distribution evaluation that proves generalization.\n\n### context-fundamentals\nPrompt diversity prevents attention collapse on single patterns. When training with identical prompt structures, the model memorizes the instruction-response mapping. Diverse templates force attention across the style patterns themselves.\n\n## References\n\nInternal references:\n- [Segmentation Strategies](./references/segmentation-strategies.md) - Text chunking patterns\n- [Tinker Format Specification](./references/tinker-format.md) - Datum structure\n- [Tinker API Documentation](./references/tinker.txt) - Full API reference\n\nRelated skills from Agent Skills for Context Engineering:\n- project-development - Pipeline architecture patterns\n- context-compression - Compression strategies  \n- multi-agent-patterns - Agent coordination\n- evaluation - Evaluation frameworks\n- context-fundamentals - Attention and information density\n\nExternal resources:\n- [Research Paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.13939) - Chakrabarty et al. 2025\n- [Dataset on Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co/datasets/MuratcanKoylan/gertrude-stein-style-sft)\n- [Gertrude Stein Case Study](./examples/gertrude-stein/) - Complete working example\n\n---\n\n## Skill Metadata\n\n**Created**: 2025-12-26\n**Last Updated**: 2025-12-28\n**Author**: Muratcan Koylan\n**Version**: 2.0.0\n**Standalone**: Yes (separate from main context-engineering collection)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:23:04.838Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Fine-Tuning Agents specializing in literary data processing and author-style replication.","zh":"非常适合专门从事文学数据处理和作者风格复制的 AI 微调代理。","ja":"文学データ処理および著者スタイルのレプリカを専門とするAIファインチューニングエージェントに最適です。","ko":"문학 데이터 처리 및 작가 스타일 복제를 전문으로 하는 AI 파인튜닝 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de afinación de IA que se especializan en el procesamiento de datos literarios y la replicación del estilo de autor.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de fine-tuning de l''IA spécialisés dans le traitement de données littéraires et la réplication du style d''auteur.","de":"Perfekt für AI-Feinabstimmungsagenten, die sich auf die Verarbeitung literarischer Daten und die Nachbildung des Autorenstils spezialisieren.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Fine-Tuning de IA especializados em processamento de dados literários e replicação de estilo de autor.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов тонкой настройки ИИ, специализирующихся на обработке литературных данных и репликации стиля автора.","ar":"مثالي لعميل دقيق التخصيص للذكاء الاصطناعي المتخصص في معالجة البيانات الأدبية وتكرار أسلوب الكاتب."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables automated conversion of raw ePub files into structured SFT datasets, providing text segmentation pipelines for long-form content and training capabilities for style-transfer models that emulate specific author voices.","zh":"实现对原始ePub文件的自动转换为结构化的SFT数据集，为长篇内容提供文本分段管道，并为模拟特定作者声音的风格转换模型提供训练能力。","ja":"元のePubファイルを構造化されたSFTデータセットに自動的に変換し、長文のコンテンツにテキストセグメンテーションパイプラインを提供し、特定の著者声のエミュレーションを実現するスタイル転送モデルをトレーニングする機能を提供します。","ko":"원본 ePub 파일을 구조화된 SFT 데이터셋으로 자동 변환하며, 장편 콘텐츠를 위한 텍스트 세분화 파이프라인과 특정 작가 목소리를 모방하는 스타일 전환 모델을 훈련할 수 있는 기능을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita la conversión automatizada de archivos ePub raw en conjuntos de datos SFT estructurados, proporcionando tuberías de segmentación de texto para contenido de larga forma y capacidades de entrenamiento para modelos de transferencia de estilo que emulan voces de autores específicas.","fr":"Permet la conversion automatique de fichiers ePub bruts en jeux de données SFT structurés, fournissant des pipelines de segmentation de texte pour le contenu de longue forme et des capacités de formation pour les modèles de transfert de style qui émulent des voix d''auteurs spécifiques.","de":"Ermöglicht die automatische Umwandlung von rohen ePub-Dateien in strukturierte SFT-Datensätze, indem Textsegmentierungspipelines für Langforminhalte und Trainingsfähigkeiten für Style-Transfer-Modelle bereitgestellt werden, die spezifische Autorenstimmen emulieren.","pt":"Permite a conversão automatizada de arquivos ePub brutos em conjuntos de dados SFT estruturados, fornecendo pipelines de segmentação de texto para conteúdo de longa forma e capacidades de treinamento para modelos de transferência de estilo que emulam vozes de autores específicos.","ru":"Позволяет автоматически преобразовывать сырые файлы ePub в структурированные наборы данных SFT, предоставляя конвейеры сегментации текста для контента большой длины и возможности обучения для моделей переноса стиля, имитирующих конкретные голоса авторов.","ar":"تمكن من تحويل الملفات الأصلية لتنسيق ePub إلى مجموعات بيانات SFT منظمّة، وتوفير خطوط أنابيب لتقسيم النصوص لل 内容 على المدى الطويل وسمات تدريب لطرازات نقل الأسلوب التي تقلد أصوات المؤلفين المحددة."},"useCases":{"en":["Processing raw ePub files into fine-tuning datasets","Training author-voice style-transfer models","Preparing training data for Tinker SFT platforms","Segmenting long-form literary content for model training"],"zh":["将原始ePub文件处理为微调数据集","训练作者语音风格转换模型","为Tinker SFT平台准备训练数据","为模型训练分段长篇文学内容"],"ja":["元のePubファイルをファインチューニングデータセットに処理する","著者ボイススタイル転送モデルをトレーニングする","Tinker SFTプラットフォームのトレーニングデータを準備する","モデルトレーニングのための長文文学コンテンツをセグメント化する"],"ko":["원본 ePub 파일을 파인튜닝 데이터셋으로 처리하기","작가 보이스 스타일 전환 모델을 훈련시키기","Tinker SFT 플랫폼을 위한 훈련 데이터 준비하기","모델 훈련을 위한 장편 문학 콘텐츠 분할하기"],"es":["Procesamiento de archivos ePub raw en conjuntos de datos de afinación","Entrenamiento de modelos de transferencia de estilo de voz de autor","Preparación de datos de entrenamiento para plataformas Tinker SFT","Segmentación de contenido literario de larga forma para el entrenamiento de modelos"],"fr":["Traitement de fichiers ePub bruts en jeux de données de fine-tuning","Formation de modèles de transfert de style de voix d''auteur","Préparation de données de formation pour les plates-formes Tinker SFT","Segmentation de contenu littéraire de longue forme pour la formation de modèles"],"de":["Verarbeitung von rohen ePub-Dateien in Feinabstimmungsdatensätze","Training von Style-Transfer-Modellen für Autorenstimmen","Vorbereitung von Trainingsdaten für Tinker-SFT-Plattformen","Segmentierung von Langformliteraturinhalten für das Modelltraining"],"pt":["Processamento de arquivos ePub brutos em conjuntos de dados de fine-tuning","Treinamento de modelos de transferência de estilo de voz de autor","Preparação de dados de treinamento para plataformas Tinker SFT","Segmentação de conteúdo literário de longa forma para treinamento de modelos"],"ru":["Обработка сырых файлов ePub в наборы данных для тонкой настройки","Обучение моделей переноса стиля голоса автора","Подготовка данных для обучения на платформах Tinker SFT","Сегментация литературного контента большой длины для обучения моделей"],"ar":["معالجة الملفات الأصلية لتنسيق ePub إلى مجموعات بيانات دقيقة التخصيص","تدريب طرازات نقل أسلوب صوت الكاتب","إعداد بيانات التدريب منصات Tinker SFT","تقسيم المحتوى الأدبي على المدى الطويل لتدريب الطرازات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires ePub source files","Designed specifically for literary content processing","Optimized for SFT (Supervised Fine-Tuning) workflows"],"zh":["需要ePub源文件","专门为文学内容处理而设计","针对SFT（监督微调）工作流进行优化"],"ja":["ePubソースファイルが必要","文学コンテンツ処理専用に設計された","SFT（監視ファインチューニング）ワークフローに最適化"],"ko":["ePub 소스 파일이 필요합니다.","문학 콘텐츠 처리를専門으로 설계되었습니다.","SFT(Supervised Fine-Tuning) 워크플로우에 최적화"],"es":["Requiere archivos fuente ePub","Diseñado específicamente para el procesamiento de contenido literario","Optimizado para flujos de trabajo de Afinación Fina Supervisada (SFT)"],"fr":["Nécessite des fichiers source ePub","Conçu spécifiquement pour le traitement de contenu littéraire","Optimisé pour les flux de travail de fine-tuning supervisée (SFT)"],"de":["Benötigt ePub-Quelldateien","Speziell für die Verarbeitung von Literaturinhalten konzipiert","Optimiert für SFT- (Supervised Fine-Tuning) Arbeitsabläufe"],"pt":["Requer arquivos de origem no formato ePub","Projetado especificamente para processamento de conteúdo literário","Otimizado para fluxos de trabalho SFT (Supervised Fine-Tuning)"],"ru":["Требует исходных файлов в формате ePub","Разработан специально для обработки литературного контента","Оптимизирован для рабочих процессов SFT (Supervised Fine-Tuning)"],"ar":["يتطلب ملفات مصدر بتنسيق ePub","صُمّم خصيصًا لمعالجة المحتوى الأدبي","مُثّبت لتدفقات العمل SFT (التحكم الدقيق في التخصيص)"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
