 Descoberta de Código","ru":"Context Hunter: Инструмент для поиска кода","ar":"context hunter: أداة لاكتشاف الكود","en":"context-hunter"},"description":{"zh":"Context Hunter是一种优化代码发现和任务复杂性分类的工具，帮助开发人员提高效率","ja":"Context Hunterはコードの発見とタスクの複雑性分類を最適化するツールで、開発者の効率を向上させる","ko":"Context Hunter는 코드 발견과 작업 복잡도 분류를 최적화하는 도구로 개발자의 효율성을 높여줍니다","es":"Context Hunter es una herramienta para gestionar la colaboración de proyectos entre humanos y agentes de IA en un ecosistema Git, mejorando la eficiencia y r...","fr":"Context Hunter est un outil pour gérer la collaboration de projets entre humains et agents IA dans un écosystème Git, améliorant l''efficacité et réduisant la...","de":"Context Hunter ist ein Tool zur Verwaltung der Projektzusammenarbeit zwischen Menschen und KI-Agents in einem Git-Ökosystem, das die Effizienz verbessert und...","pt":"O Context Hunter é uma ferramenta para gerenciar a colaboração de projetos entre humanos e agentes de IA no ecossistema Git.","ru":"Context Hunter — это инструмент для управления сотрудничеством в проектах между людьми и агентами ИИ в экосистеме Git.","ar":"Context Hunter هو أداة لإدارة التعاون في المشاريع بين البشر ووكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي في نظام جيت","en":"Backlog.md - A tool for managing project collaboration between humans and AI Agents in a git ecosystem"},"definition":{"en":"Backlog.md - A tool for managing project collaboration between humans and AI Agents in a git ecosystem"},"features":{"zh":["优化代码发现","任务复杂性分类","支持L0、L1、L2复杂性级别","提高开发效率","简化代码管理"],"ja":["コードの発見を最適化","タスクの複雑性分類","L0、L1、L2複雑性レベルのサポート","開発効率の向上","コード管理の簡素化"],"ko":["코드 발견 최적화","작업 복잡도 분류","L0, L1, L2 복잡도 레벨 지원","개발 효율성 향상","코드 관리 간소화"],"es":["Gestión de proyectos en un ecosistema Git","Colaboración entre humanos y agentes de IA","Clasificación de la complejidad de las tareas","Descubrimiento enfocado de archivos relevantes","Reducción de la complejidad y mejora de la eficiencia"],"fr":["Gestion de projets dans un écosystème Git","Collaboration entre humains et agents IA","Classification de la complexité des tâches","Découverte ciblée de fichiers pertinents","Réduction de la complexité et amélioration de l''efficacité"],"de":["Projektverwaltung in einem Git-Ökosystem","Zusammenarbeit zwischen Menschen und KI-Agents","Klassifizierung der Aufgabenkomplexität","Fokussierte Entdeckung von relevanten Dateien","Komplexitätsreduktion und Effizienzsteigerung"],"pt":["Ferramenta de descoberta de código","Classificação de complexidade de tarefas","Suporte a colaboração entre humanos e agentes de IA","Integração com o ecossistema Git","Ajuda a encontrar os arquivos certos","Reduz a complexidade do código"],"ru":["Инструмент для поиска кода","Классификация сложности задач","Поддержка сотрудничества между людьми и агентами ИИ","Интеграция с экосистемой Git","Помогает найти нужные файлы","Уменьшает сложность кода"],"ar":["أداة لاكتشاف الكود","تصنيف تعقيد المهام","دعم التعاون بين البشر ووكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","التكامل مع نظام جيت","تساعد في العثور على الملفات الصحيحة","تقلل من تعقيد الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码发现","任务复杂性分类","Context Hunter","开发效率","代码管理","L0复杂性","L1复杂性","L2复杂性"],"ja":["コードの発見","タスクの複雑性分類","Context Hunter","開発効率","コード管理","L0複雑性","L1複雑性","L2複雑性"],"ko":["코드 발견","작업 복잡도 분류","Context Hunter","개발 효율성","코드 관리","L0 복잡도","L1 복잡도","L2 복잡도"],"es":["Context Hunter","colaboración de proyectos","ecosistema Git","agentes de IA","gestión de proyectos","desarrollo de software","eficiencia en el desarrollo","reducción de la complejidad"],"fr":["Context Hunter","collaboration de projets","écosystème Git","agents IA","gestion de projets","développement de logiciels","efficacité dans le développement","réduction de la complexité"],"de":["Context Hunter","Projektzusammenarbeit","Git-Ökosystem","KI-Agents","Projektverwaltung","Software-Entwicklung","Effizienz im Entwicklung","Komplexitätsreduktion"],"pt":["Context Hunter","ferramenta de descoberta de código","colaboração entre humanos e agentes de IA","ecossistema Git","classificação de complexidade de tarefas","desenvolvimento de software","engenharia de software","gerenciamento de projetos"],"ru":["Context Hunter","инструмент для поиска кода","сотрудничество между людьми и агентами ИИ","экосистема Git","классификация сложности задач","разработка программного обеспечения","инженерия программного обеспечения","управление проектами"],"ar":["Context Hunter","أداة لاكتشاف الكود","التعاون بين البشر ووكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","نظام جيت","تصنيف تعقيد المهام","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة البرمجيات","إدارة المشاريع"]}},"owner":"MrLesk","repo":"Backlog.md","repoPath":"MrLesk/Backlog.md","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"context-hunter","description":"MUST run before any code implementation task. Classifies complexity, discovers local conventions, finds reusable patterns, and prevents blind coding. Invoke this skill before writing or modifying code.","bodyPreview":"# Context Hunter\n\nBefore writing code, run a focused discovery loop.\nDo not load everything. Find the right files.\n\n## Complexity Gate\n\nClassify task complexity first:\n\n- `L0 (trivial)`: typos, renames, copy-only edits, obvious single-line fixes with no behavior change.\n- `L1 (moderate)`: behavior changes in one bounded area.\n- `L2 (high-risk)`: cross-module changes, data semantics, refactors, architecture-impacting work.\n\nOutput by level:\n- `L0`: no context brief, proceed directly.\n- `L1`: writ","body":"# Context Hunter\n\nBefore writing code, run a focused discovery loop.\nDo not load everything. Find the right files.\n\n## Complexity Gate\n\nClassify task complexity first:\n\n- `L0 (trivial)`: typos, renames, copy-only edits, obvious single-line fixes with no behavior change.\n- `L1 (moderate)`: behavior changes in one bounded area.\n- `L2 (high-risk)`: cross-module changes, data semantics, refactors, architecture-impacting work.\n\nOutput by level:\n- `L0`: no context brief, proceed directly.\n- `L1`: write a micro-brief.\n- `L2`: write a full context brief.\n\nRe-evaluate level during discovery and implementation.\nIf new evidence shows higher complexity than initially classified, upgrade the level and apply the stricter workflow.\n\n## Core Behavior\n\nAct like a senior engineer who asks the next useful question:\n1. **Assess completeness**: Check whether the request omits expected concerns seen in analogous code.\n2. **Discover selectively**: Read the minimum set of relevant files.\n3. **Validate assumptions**: Confirm with tests/config/history.\n4. **Synthesize**: Capture findings before coding for `L1/L2`.\n\n## Discovery Workflow (Before Coding)\n\n### 1) Assess Request Completeness\n\nAsk: \"What is likely missing?\"\n\nExamples:\n- Similar endpoints include auth/validation. Is that expected here?\n- This area uses soft-delete semantics. Should this operation follow that?\n- Similar flows emit telemetry/error states. Should this change do the same?\n- Existing module boundaries suggest a different placement. Is current request still correct?\n\n### 2) Run Targeted Discovery\n\nPrioritize these in order:\n1. Find analogous implementations and copy their structure.\n2. Trace data flow for similar features end-to-end.\n3. Identify reusable utilities before creating new helpers.\n4. Inspect nearby tests to infer team priorities and edge cases.\n5. Read recent commits in the same area for current direction.\n\nPortable discovery actions:\n- Search for feature/domain terms in relevant directories.\n- Enumerate nearby files in the affected area.\n- Inspect recent change history for touched paths.\n- Run targeted validation first, then broader project checks as needed.\n\n### 3) Probe for Silent Knowledge\n\nLook for implicit rules encoded in code:\n- Soft-delete, audit, or historical retention patterns (for data-touching changes).\n- Naming conventions (`userId` vs `user_id`) and file placement norms.\n- Existing design system choices (for this repo: Nuxt + Vue + Tailwind 4.1 patterns).\n- “Dead but dangerous” APIs/functions that exist but are no longer preferred.\n\n### 4) Confidence-Based Stop Rule\n\nStop discovery when confidence is high enough to predict likely review feedback.\nIf you cannot anticipate reviewer concerns yet, keep looking.\n\n### 5) Produce Scaled Discovery Output\n\nFor `L1`, write a micro-brief:\n- Closest analog and chosen pattern.\n- Main risk or ambiguity.\n\nFor `L2`, write a full context brief:\n- Analogous files reviewed (with paths).\n- Patterns to follow (state/data/error handling/naming).\n- Reusable utilities/components/composables identified.\n- Risks and unknowns.\n\nFor `L1/L2`, keep an internal discovery log:\n- Files checked.\n- Patterns inferred.\n- Decisions made from evidence.\n- Naming evidence for new identifiers (`new name -> analog paths -> extracted pattern`).\n\n## Clarification Policy\n\n- Prefer fewer questions.\n- Ask only when the answer would change implementation approach.\n- If convention is clear, proceed silently.\n- Escalate only genuine ambiguity/conflict or product-level tradeoffs.\n\n## During Implementation\n\nChanges should look native to the codebase:\n- Reuse existing abstractions first.\n- Match existing module boundaries and naming.\n- Follow established error-handling and testing style.\n- Prefer consistency over novelty.\n\nNaming derivation rule:\n- Do not invent names from general priors.\n- For each new identifier family (file/function/variable/class/route), derive naming from closest local analogs.\n- Use at least 2 analogous examples when available before finalizing a new naming pattern.\n- If no analog exists, introduce the new term explicitly and record it as a no-analog exception.\n\nIf requirements conflict with discovered conventions:\n- Flag the conflict explicitly.\n- Propose 1-2 alternatives aligned with existing patterns.\n- Ask for decision when tradeoffs are product/architecture-level.\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter coding:\n- Run targeted validation for changed area first.\n- Run broader checks appropriate for risk (`typecheck`, lint/check, tests as needed).\n- Confirm no new pattern drift was introduced.\n\n## Checklist\n\n`L0`:\n- [ ] Confirmed change is truly trivial and safe to execute without full discovery.\n\n`L1/L2`:\n- [ ] Classified complexity (`L0/L1/L2`) before discovery\n- [ ] Studied analogous features in the codebase\n- [ ] Checked for reusable utilities\n- [ ] Reviewed test patterns for similar functionality\n- [ ] Assessed request completeness before implementation\n- [ ] Identified at least one silent convention/risk\n- [ ] Produced the required artifact for the chosen level\n- [ ] Kept an internal discovery log for `L1/L2`\n- [ ] All new names were derived from codebase analogs, or marked as intentional no-analog exceptions\n- [ ] Verified final approach matches existing patterns\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:25:47.010Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Analysis Agents needing efficient project collaboration and complexity classification in git ecosystems","zh":"非常适合需要在 git 生态系统中实现高效项目协作和复杂性分类的代码分析代理","ja":"Git エコシステムでのプロジェクトの共同作業と複雑さの分類に効率的なコード分析エージェントを必要とする場合に最適","ko":"GIT 생태계에서 프로젝트 협업 및 복잡성 분류가 효율적으로 필요한 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de análisis de código que necesitan una colaboración de proyecto eficiente y clasificación de complejidad en ecosistemas git","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de code ayant besoin d''une collaboration de projet efficace et d''une classification de complexité dans les écosystèmes git","de":"Perfekt für Code-Analyse-Agents, die eine effiziente Projektzusammenarbeit und Komplexitätsklassifizierung in Git-Ökosystemen benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Código que necessitam de colaboração de projeto eficiente e classificação de complexidade em ecossistemas git","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа кода, которым требуется эффективное сотрудничество в проекте и классификация сложности в экосистемах git","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل التعليمات البرمجية الذي يحتاج إلى تعاون فعال في المشروع وتصنيف التعقيد في بيئات جيت"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform focused discovery loops, classify task complexity using levels such as L0, L1, and L2, and optimize context brief generation for behavior changes and cross-module modifications in git repositories","zh":"赋予代理执行专注的发现循环，使用诸如 L0、L1 和 L2 之类的级别对任务复杂性进行分类，并针对行为更改和跨模块修改在 git 仓库中优化上下文简报生成","ja":"エージェントに、L0、L1、L2 などのレベルを使用したタスクの複雑さの分類や、Git リポジトリでの動作の変更やモジュール間の変更に対するコンテキストブリーフの生成を最適化することに焦点を当てた発見ループの実行を可能にする","ko":"에이전트가 집중적인 발견 루프를 수행하고 L0, L1 및 L2와 같은 수준으로 작업 복잡성을 분류하며 GIT 저장소에서 동작 변경 및 모듈 간 수정에 대한 문맥 브리핑 생성을 최적화하는 것을 가능하게 함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar bucles de descubrimiento enfocados, clasificar la complejidad de las tareas utilizando niveles como L0, L1 y L2, y optimizar la generación de breves contextuales para cambios de comportamiento y modificaciones entre módulos en repositorios git","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer des boucles de découverte ciblées, de classer la complexité des tâches en utilisant des niveaux tels que L0, L1 et L2, et d''optimiser la génération de brèves contextuelles pour les changements de comportement et les modifications entre modules dans les référentiels git","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, fokussierte Entdeckungsschleifen durchzuführen, die Komplexität von Aufgaben mithilfe von Ebenen wie L0, L1 und L2 zu klassifizieren und die Generierung von Kontextzusammenfassungen für Verhaltensänderungen und Modifikationen zwischen Modulen in Git-Repositorys zu optimieren","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar loops de descoberta focados, classificar a complexidade das tarefas usando níveis como L0, L1 e L2 e otimizar a geração de breves contextuais para alterações de comportamento e modificações entre módulos em repositórios git","ru":"Позволяет агентам выполнять сфокусированные циклы обнаружения, классифицировать сложность задач с использованием уровней, таких как L0, L1 и L2, и оптимизировать генерацию контекстных кратких сообщений для изменений поведения и межмодульных изменений в репозиториях git","ar":"تمكّن العميل من إجراء دورات اكتشاف محددة، وتصنيف تعقيد المهام باستخدام مستويات مثل L0 و L1 و L2، وتحسين توليد ملخصات سياقية لتغييرات السلوك والتحديثات عبر الوحدات في مستودعات جيت"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating task complexity classification for collaborative projects","Generating context briefs for L1 and L2 level tasks","Optimizing code review workflows by identifying trivial, moderate, and high-risk changes"],"zh":["为协作项目自动化任务复杂性分类","为 L1 和 L2 级任务生成上下文简报","通过识别琐碎、适中和高风险的更改来优化代码审查工作流"],"ja":["共同作業プロジェクトのタスクの複雑さの分類を自動化する","L1 および L2 レベルのタスクのコンテキストブリーフを生成する","微小、適度、ハイリスクの変更を識別することでコードレビューのワークフローを最適化する"],"ko":["협력 프로젝트를 위한 작업 복잡성 분류 자동화","L1 및 L2 수준 작업을 위한 문맥 브리핑 생성","코드 리뷰 워크플로우를 하이리스크 변경 사항 식별을 통해 최적화"],"es":["Automatizar la clasificación de la complejidad de las tareas para proyectos colaborativos","Generar breves contextuales para tareas de nivel L1 y L2","Optimizar los flujos de trabajo de revisión de código al identificar cambios triviales, moderados y de alto riesgo"],"fr":["Automatiser la classification de la complexité des tâches pour les projets collaboratifs","Générer des brèves contextuelles pour les tâches de niveau L1 et L2","Optimiser les flux de travail de révision de code en identifiant les changements triviaux, modérés et à haut risque"],"de":["Automatisieren der Komplexitätsklassifizierung von Aufgaben für kollaborative Projekte","Generieren von Kontextzusammenfassungen für Aufgaben der Ebenen L1 und L2","Optimieren der Code-Review-Workflows durch Identifizierung von trivialen, moderaten und hochriskanten Änderungen"],"pt":["Automatizar a classificação da complexidade das tarefas para projetos colaborativos","Gerar breves contextuais para tarefas de nível L1 e L2","Otimizar fluxos de trabalho de revisão de código identificando alterações triviais, moderadas e de alto risco"],"ru":["Автоматизировать классификацию сложности задач для совместных проектов","Генерировать контекстные краткие сообщения для задач уровня L1 и L2","Оптимизировать рабочие процессы проверки кода, выявляя тривиальные, умеренные и высокорисковые изменения"],"ar":["توسيع تلقائي لتصنيف تعقيد المهام للمشاريع التعاونية","توليد ملخصات سياقية لمهام مستوى L1 و L2","تحسين سير عمل مراجعة التعليمات البرمجية عن طريق تحديد التغييرات التافئة والمتوسطة والخطر العالي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires integration with git ecosystem","Limited to classification of task complexity into predefined levels"],"zh":["需要与 git 生态系统集成","仅限于将任务复杂性分类到预定义级别"],"ja":["Git エコシステムとの統合が必要","タスクの複雑さの分類が予め定義されたレベルに限定される"],"ko":["GIT 생태계와의 통합이 필요","작업 복잡성 분류가 미리 정의된 수준으로 제한"],"es":["Requiere integración con el ecosistema git","Limitado a la clasificación de la complejidad de las tareas en niveles predefinidos"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec l''écosystème git","Limité à la classification de la complexité des tâches en niveaux prédéfinis"],"de":["Erfordert Integration in das Git-Ökosystem","Begrenzt auf die Klassifizierung der Aufgabenkomplexität in vordefinierte Ebenen"],"pt":["Requer integração com o ecossistema git","Limitado à classificação da complexidade da tarefa em níveis predefinidos"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с экосистемой git","Ограничен классификацией сложности задач на предварительно определенных уровнях"],"ar":["يتطلب التكامل مع بيئة جيت","محدود بتصنيف تعقيد المهام على مستويات محددة مسبقا"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
