om ShardingSphere","Suporte a SQL distribuído"],"ru":["Анализ коренной причины","Логика откат","Решения о слиянии","Комментарии к запросу изменения тона","Интеграция с ShardingSphere","Поддержка распределенного SQL"],"ar":["تحليل السبب الأساسي","لوجيستي الفallback","قرارات الدمج","تعليقات طلب تغيير النبرة","التكامل مع ShardingSphere","دعم SQL موزع"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Review PR","分布式 SQL","分片","可扩展性","安全性","代码合并决策","根因修复"],"ja":["Review PR","分散 SQL","シャーディング","スケーラビリティ","セキュリティ","コードのマージ決定","根本原因の修復"],"ko":["리뷰 PR","분산 SQL","샤딩","확장성","보안","코드 병합 결정","根本 원인 수정"],"es":["revisión de PR","SQL distribuido","escalabilidad","seguridad","bases de datos","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software"],"fr":["révision de PR","SQL réparti","évolutivité","sécurité","bases de données","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de logiciels"],"de":["PR-Überprüfung","verteiltes SQL","Skalierbarkeit","Sicherheit","Datenbanken","Softwareentwicklung","Softwareingenieurwesen"],"pt":["Review PR","inteligência de dados","SQL distribuído","ShardingSphere","decisões de merge","causa raiz","lógica de fallback","comentários de solicitação de alteração de tom","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["Просмотр PR","интеллект данных","распределенный SQL","ShardingSphere","решения о слиянии","коренная причина","логика откат","комментарии к запросу изменения тона","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["مراجعة PR","ذكاء البيانات","SQL موزع","ShardingSphere","قرارات الدمج","السبب الأساسي","لوجيستي الفallback","تعليقات طلب تغيير النبرة","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"apache","repo":"shardingsphere","repoPath":"apache/shardingsphere","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"review-pr","description":">-","bodyPreview":"# Review PR\n\n## Objective\n\n- Make merge decisions for ShardingSphere PRs with a \"root-cause-first, evidence-first\" approach.\n- Output a single merge decision:\n  - `Merge Verdict`: `Mergeable` / `Not Mergeable`\n\n## Trigger Scenarios\n\n- The user asks you to review a PR.\n- The user asks whether a PR \"can be merged\" or \"fixes the root cause.\"\n- The user asks you to generate committer-tone change request comments.\n\n## Mandatory Constraints\n\n1. Verify root-cause repair first, then fallback logic; do n","body":"# Review PR\n\n## Objective\n\n- Make merge decisions for ShardingSphere PRs with a \"root-cause-first, evidence-first\" approach.\n- Output a single merge decision:\n  - `Merge Verdict`: `Mergeable` / `Not Mergeable`\n\n## Trigger Scenarios\n\n- The user asks you to review a PR.\n- The user asks whether a PR \"can be merged\" or \"fixes the root cause.\"\n- The user asks you to generate committer-tone change request comments.\n\n## Mandatory Constraints\n\n1. Verify root-cause repair first, then fallback logic; do not accept \"fallback only\" as a substitute for root-cause repair.\n2. You must scan side effects and risks:\n   - Design consistency\n   - Performance (complexity, hot paths, memory, and I/O)\n   - Compatibility (behavior, config, API-SPI, SQL dialect)\n   - Functional degradation and regression surface\n3. You must provide exactly one `Merge Verdict`.\n4. If evidence is insufficient, risk is unclear, or validation is incomplete, always set `Merge Verdict: Not Mergeable`,\n   and list the minimum additional information required.\n5. Change request replies must be gentle in tone and contain no emojis.\n6. If unrelated changes exist, you must explicitly ask for rollback; if none exist, do not output that section.\n7. Any \"fallback-only without root-cause repair\" or \"unresolved risk\" must not receive `Merge Verdict: Mergeable`.\n8. Review only the PR''s latest code version; do not reuse conclusions from older versions.\n\n## Execution Boundary\n\n- Review output only; do not modify code.\n\n## Evidence Source Strategy\n\nPriority from high to low:\n\n1. PR facts: diff, commit history, review comments, CI status, check results.\n2. Related issues in the same repo, relevant module code/tests, historical behavior (optional git blame/log).\n3. ShardingSphere official docs and official repo conventions.\n4. External authoritative specs only when necessary (official standards/docs only).\n\nForbidden sources:\n\n- Unverifiable blogs, forum posts, or AI-reposted content.\n\n## Review Efficiency Rules\n\n- In the current reply, prioritize blocking issues and `Merge Verdict`.\n- If the PR is obviously too large (too many files or too much churn), suggest splitting first.\n- If full review cannot be completed immediately, provide high-risk blockers first to avoid blocking the delivery chain.\n\n## Quick Triage\n\nBefore deep review, answer:\n\n1. Does the PR clearly state the problem and expected behavior?\n2. Do current changes directly touch the suspected root-cause path?\n3. Is there corresponding validation (unit/integration/regression tests)?\n4. Are there file changes unrelated to the stated goal?\n\nTriage policy:\n\n- Information complete: proceed with full review.\n- Missing evidence: mark as \"not mergeable\" and request minimum additional info.\n- Any off-topic/unrelated changes: mark as \"not mergeable\" and require scope narrowing.\n- Change set too large: request split first, and provide only blocker-level feedback for current version.\n\n## Minimum Additional Information List (Fixed Template)\n\nWhen information gaps block mergeability, request at least:\n\n- Recheck scope for the PR latest version (files/modules).\n- ShardingSphere version and runtime topology (JDBC/Proxy + Standalone/Cluster).\n- Database type and version.\n- Minimal reproducible input (SQL/request/config snippet) with expected vs actual behavior.\n- Key logs or stack traces.\n- Test evidence mapped one-to-one with fix points (new or adjusted tests).\n\n## Review Workflow\n\n1. Define target and boundary: restate PR goal, impacted modules, target topology (JDBC or Proxy, Standalone or Cluster).\n2. Root-cause modeling: reconstruct \"trigger condition -> failure path -> result\" from issue and code path.\n3. Fix mapping: verify each change covers the root-cause chain, not just symptoms.\n4. Risk scan:\n   - Design: abstraction level, responsibility boundaries, temporary compatibility branches\n   - Performance: new loops/remote calls/object allocations on hot paths\n   - Compatibility: behavior/config/API-SPI/SQL dialect versions\n   - Regression: similar statements, adjacent features, exception branches\n5. Test adequacy:\n   - Is there a failing case first or reproducible steps?\n   - Are major branches, boundaries, and counterexamples covered?\n   - Are tests mapped one-to-one with fix points?\n6. Supply-chain and license gates (triggered by changes):\n   - If dependency manifests or lockfiles changed, check vulnerability severity and license constraints\n   - Mark whether extra security review is required\n7. Unrelated-change screening: identify code/format/refactor changes not directly tied to PR goal; require removal or rollback.\n8. Version baseline control:\n   - Base conclusion only on PR latest code version\n   - If new commits are added, current conclusion becomes invalid and must be re-reviewed on latest version\n9. Merge decision: output `Merge Verdict`.\n10. Generate feedback: follow the output template below.\n\n## Root-Cause Validation Checklist (Must Answer Each)\n\n- Was the true trigger point identified (not just the final error point)?\n- Do changes directly fix the trigger point or key propagation path?\n- Is it only adding null checks/defaults/try-catch without fixing root cause?\n- Does it introduce silent error swallowing or downgrade to wrong semantics?\n- Are adjacent paths sharing the same root cause also validated?\n\nIf the root-cause chain cannot be fully proven fixed, set `Merge Verdict: Not Mergeable`.\n\n## Risk Checklist (Must Cover)\n\n- Design risk: broken layering, duplicated logic, bypassed SPI/metadata cache, implicit state.\n- Performance risk: complexity increase, extra hot-path allocations, unbounded retries, blocking I/O.\n- Compatibility risk:\n  - Behavior compatibility\n  - Config compatibility\n  - API/SPI compatibility\n  - SQL compatibility (database/version/dialect)\n- Functional degradation risk: old-scenario regression, boundary input behavior changes, error-code/exception semantic drift.\n- Operational risk: config migration complexity, gray-release and rollback complexity.\n- Supply-chain risk: vulnerabilities, licenses, transitive dependency changes from new deps.\n\n## Coverage Statement (Required in Every Review)\n\nEach review must declare:\n\n- `Reviewed Scope`: files/modules actually reviewed this round.\n- `Not Reviewed Scope`: unreviewed or only superficially reviewed areas.\n- `Need Expert Review`: whether domain reviewers are required (security, concurrency, performance, protocol, etc.).\n\n## Multi-Round Change Request Comparison Rules\n\nWhen the user provides previous-round feedback or PR adds new commits, perform incremental comparison:\n\n1. Build a \"previous issues list\" and mark each as:\n   - Fixed\n   - Partially fixed\n   - Not fixed\n   - Newly introduced issue\n2. Keep only unresolved and newly introduced items as current focus; do not repeat closed items.\n3. Every suggestion must cite corresponding diff evidence.\n4. For partially fixed items, specify exactly what is still needed to close.\n5. If new commits were added, continue review only on the latest version; no need to output historical commit SHA.\n\n## Output Structure\n\n### A. Not Mergeable (Change Request)\n\nUse committer tone, gentle wording, no emojis; structure:\n\n1. Decision block\n   - `Merge Verdict: Not Mergeable`\n   - `Reviewed Scope / Not Reviewed Scope / Need Expert Review`\n2. Positive feedback (optional)\n   - Include only when there are genuinely correct direction-aligned changes.\n   - Omit if none.\n3. Major issues\n   - List unreasonable/incorrect points by severity.\n   - Each issue includes: label, symptom, risk, recommended action (fix or rollback).\n4. Newly introduced issues\n   - Point out defects/regression risks introduced by this PR.\n   - Clearly require fix or rollback.\n5. Unrelated changes (output only when present)\n   - List changes unrelated to this PR goal and request rollback.\n6. Next-step suggestions\n   - Provide executable fix checklist and encourage next revision.\n7. Multi-round comparison (only when history exists)\n   - Versus previous round: closed, unresolved, and new items.\n8. Evidence supplement (only when information is insufficient)\n   - Explicitly list minimum additional information and review entry points.\n\n### B. Mergeable\n\n1. Decision block\n   - `Merge Verdict: Mergeable`\n   - `Reviewed Scope / Not Reviewed Scope / Need Expert Review`\n2. Basis\n   - Root-cause fix evidence.\n   - Risk assessment results (proving no unresolved risk).\n3. Pre-merge checks\n   - CI, tests, compatibility confirmations.\n\n## Change Request Tone Guidelines\n\n- Use \"suggest / please / need\" rather than accusatory commands.\n- Facts first, judgment second; avoid emotional wording.\n- Suggested sentence patterns:\n  - \"This part is in the right direction, especially ...\"\n  - \"There are still several issues affecting mergeability; please address them first: ...\"\n  - \"This introduces new risk; please fix or roll back this part.\"\n  - \"Please continue refining it, and I will do another focused review after that.\"\n\n## Prohibited Items\n\n- Do not output `Mergeable` when evidence is insufficient or risks are unclear.\n- Do not use \"fallback logic passes tests\" to replace proof of root-cause repair.\n- Do not ignore unrelated changes.\n- Do not reuse old conclusions after new commits are added without re-review.\n- Do not include emojis in change request text.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:25:36.881Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing advanced Distributed SQL analysis for Sharding and Scalability decisions.","zh":"非常适合需要高级分布式SQL分析以进行分片和可扩展性决策的代码审查代理。","ja":"コードレビューエージェントが分片とスケーラビリティの決定に先進的な分散SQL分析を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"코드 리뷰 에이전트가 샤딩 및 확장성 결정을 위해 고급 분산 SQL 분석이 필요한 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan un análisis de SQL distribuido avanzado para decisiones de fragmentación y escalabilidad.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de révision de code nécessitant une analyse de SQL distribué avancée pour les décisions de partitionnement et de scalabilité.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agents, die eine erweiterte Analyse von verteiltem SQL für Entscheidungen zu Sharding und Skalierbarkeit benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de análise avançada de SQL distribuído para decisões de fragmentação e escalabilidade.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов проверки кода, которым требуется продвинутый анализ распределенного SQL для принятия решений по шардированию и масштабируемости.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء مراجعة الشفرة الذين يحتاجون إلى تحليل متقدم ل SQL الموزع لاتخاذ قرارات بشأن تقطيع البيانات ومقاييس التوسع."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to make informed merge decisions using a ''root-cause-first, evidence-first'' approach, ensuring data intelligence and security across all databases with ShardingSphere PRs, and providing committer-tone change request comments.","zh":"使得代理能够使用''根因优先，证据优先''的方法做出明智的合并决策，确保所有数据库的数据智能和安全，包括ShardingSphere PR，并提供提交者语气的更改请求评论。","ja":"エージェントがルート原因優先、証拠優先のアプローチを使用して情報に基づいたマージの決定を下し、ShardingSphere PRを含むすべてのデータベースのデータインテリジェンスとセキュリティを確保し、コミッターのトーンの変更リクエストコメントを提供できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 ''근본 원인 우선, 증거 우선'' 접근 방식을 사용하여 정보에基づいた 병합 결정을 내릴 수 있도록 하며, ShardingSphere PR를 포함한 모든 데이터베이스의 데이터 지능과 보안을 보장하고, 커미터의 トーン의 변경 요청 댓글을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a tomar decisiones informadas de fusión utilizando un enfoque ''causa raíz primero, evidencia primero'', garantizando la inteligencia y seguridad de los datos en todas las bases de datos con solicitudes de extracción de ShardingSphere y proporcionando comentarios de solicitud de cambio de tono de confirmador.","fr":"Permet aux agents de prendre des décisions éclairées de fusion en utilisant une approche ''cause première, preuve première'', en garantissant l''intelligence et la sécurité des données sur toutes les bases de données avec les demandes d''extraction de ShardingSphere et en fournissant des commentaires de demande de modification de ton de validateur.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, fundierte Entscheidungen über die Zusammenführung zu treffen, indem sie einen Ansatz ''Ursache-wegen-erst, Beweis-erst'' verwenden, der die Datenintelligenz und -sicherheit in allen Datenbanken mit ShardingSphere-PRs gewährleistet und Änderungsanforderungskommentare im Ton des Committers bereitstellt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a tomar decisões de mesclagem informadas utilizando uma abordagem ''causa-raiz-primeiro, evidência-primeiro'', garantindo inteligência e segurança de dados em todos os bancos de dados com PRs ShardingSphere e fornecendo comentários de solicitação de alteração de tom de comitente.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью принимать обоснованные решения о слиянии, используя подход ''причина корень-сначала, доказательства-сначала'', гарантируя интеллект и безопасность данных во всех базах данных с PR ShardingSphere и предоставляя комментарии к запросам на изменение тона коммитера.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من اتخاذ قرارات دمج مستنيرة باستخدام نهج ''السبب الأساسي أولاً، الأدلة أولاً''، وضمان ذكاء البيانات وأمنها عبر جميع قواعد البيانات مع طلبات الشardingSphere وتمكين طلبات تغيير النغمة الملتزمة."},"useCases":{"en":["Verifying root-cause repair for PRs","Generating merge verdicts with fallback logic","Automating PR reviews for ShardingSphere"],"zh":["验证PR的根因修复","使用备用逻辑生成合并裁决","自动化ShardingSphere的PR审查"],"ja":["PRの根本原因の修復を検証する","フォールバックロジックを使用してマージの判決を生成する","ShardingSphereのPRレビューを自動化する"],"ko":["PR의 근본 원인 修复를 검증하는 것","备用 로직을 사용하여 合并 裁定을 생성하는 것","ShardingSphere의 PR 리뷰를 자동화하는 것"],"es":["Verificar la reparación de la causa raíz para las solicitudes de extracción","Generar veredictos de fusión con lógica de reserva","Automatizar las revisiones de solicitudes de extracción para ShardingSphere"],"fr":["Vérifier la réparation de la cause première pour les demandes d''extraction","Générer des verdicts de fusion avec une logique de secours","Automatiser les examens des demandes d''extraction pour ShardingSphere"],"de":["Überprüfen der Ursachenreparatur für Pull-Requests","Erzeugen von Merge-Urteilen mit Fallback-Logik","Automatisieren von Pull-Request-Überprüfungen für ShardingSphere"],"pt":["Verificar reparo de causa-raiz para PRs","Gerar verdicatos de mesclagem com lógica de fallback","Automatizar revisões de PR para ShardingSphere"],"ru":["Проверка ремонта коренной причины для PR","Генерация вердиктов слияния с логикой отallback","Автоматизация обзоров PR для ShardingSphere"],"ar":["التحقق من إصلاح السبب الأساسي ل PRs","توليد أحكام الدمج مع منطق الإصدار الخلفي","أتمتة استعراض PRs ل ShardingSphere"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires ShardingSphere PR access","Distributed SQL knowledge necessary","Root-cause-first approach mandatory"],"zh":["需要ShardingSphere PR访问","需要分布式SQL知识","根因优先方法是强制性的"],"ja":["ShardingSphere PRへのアクセスが必要","分散SQLの知識が必要","根本原因優先の方法は必須"],"ko":["ShardingSphere PR 접근이 필요","분산 SQL 지식이 필요","근본 원인 우선 방법이 필수"],"es":["Requiere acceso a las solicitudes de extracción de ShardingSphere","Conocimiento de SQL distribuido necesario","Enfoque de causa raíz primero obligatorio"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès aux demandes d''extraction de ShardingSphere","Connaissances de SQL distribué nécessaires","Approche de cause première obligatoire"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf ShardingSphere-Pull-Requests","Verteiltes SQL-Wissen erforderlich","Ursachen-erst-Ansatz obligatorisch"],"pt":["Requer acesso PR ShardingSphere","Conhecimento de SQL distribuído necessário","Abordagem de causa-raiz-primeiro obrigatória"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к PR ShardingSphere","Необходимо знание распределенного SQL","Подход корень-причина-сначала обязательный"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى PR ShardingSphere","مطلوب معرفة SQL الموزع","نهج السبب الأساسي أولاً إلزامي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
