, design, and optimization in complex real-world scenarios."},"features":{"zh":["使用 FFI 调用 C 代码","实现低级抽象","性能优化","逃避借用检查","安全注释要求"],"ja":["FFI を使用して C コードを呼び出す","低レベルの抽象化を実装する","パフォーマンス最適化","借用チェッカーを回避する","安全注釈の要件"],"ko":["FFI를 사용하여 C 코드 호출","저수준 추상화 구현","성능 최적화","대출检查 회피","안전 주석 요구사항"],"es":["Orquestación de habilidades modulares","Cadenas de ejecución colaborativas","Unidades de razonamiento y decisión llamables","Diagnóstico y optimización en escenarios complejos","Cumplimiento de los requisitos de comentarios de seguridad"],"fr":["Orchestration d''habiletés modulaires","Chaînes d''exécution collaboratives","Unités de raisonnement et de décision appelables","Diagnostic et optimisation dans des scénarios complexes","Respect des exigences de commentaires de sécurité"],"de":["Modulare Fähigkeitsorchestrierung","Kollaborative Ausführungsketten","Aufrufbare Reasoning- und Entscheidungseinheiten","Diagnose und Optimierung in komplexen Szenarien","Erfüllung der Sicherheitsanforderungen für Kommentare"],"pt":["Uso de código não seguro com controles rigorosos","Diagnóstico e design de sistemas complexos","Otimização de desempenho em cenários críticos","Integração com bibliotecas C","Controle de acesso à memória"],"ru":["Использование небезопасного кода с жесткими контролями","Диагностика и проектирование сложных систем","Оптимизация производительности в критических сценариях","Интеграция с библиотеками C","Контроль доступа к памяти"],"ar":["استخدام رمز غير آمن مع ضوابط صارمة","التشخيص والتصميم لأنظمة معقدة","تحسين الأداء في سناريوهات حرجة","التكامل مع مكتبات سي","مراقبة الوصول إلى الذاكرة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Rust 不安全代码","unsafe 关键字","FFI","低级抽象","性能优化","借用检查","安全注释"],"ja":["Rust 不安全コード","unsafe キーワード","FFI","低レベルの抽象化","パフォーマンス最適化","借用チェッカー","安全注釈"],"ko":["Rust 안전하지 않은 코드","unsafe 키워드","FFI","저수준 추상화","성능 최적화","대출检查","안전 주석"],"es":["Rust Unsafe","prácticas de ingeniería de Rust","inteligencia artificial","orquestación de habilidades modulares","cumplimiento de los requisitos de comentarios de seguridad","desarrollo de software seguro"],"fr":["Rust Unsafe","pratiques d''ingénierie Rust","intelligence artificielle","orchestration d''habiletés modulaires","respect des exigences de commentaires de sécurité","développement de logiciels sûrs"],"de":["Rust Unsafe","Rust-Ingenieurpraktiken","künstliche Intelligenz","modulare Fähigkeitsorchestrierung","Erfüllung der Sicherheitsanforderungen für Kommentare","sichere Softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["Rust Unsafe","código não seguro","segurança em Rust","desenvolvimento de software","otimização de desempenho","bibliotecas C","controle de acesso à memória"],"ru":["Rust Unsafe","небезопасный код","безопасность в Rust","разработка программного обеспечения","оптимизация производительности","библиотеки C","контроль доступа к памяти"],"ar":["رست غير آمن","رمز غير آمن","أمان في رست","تطوير البرمجيات","تحسين الأداء","مكتبات سي","مراقبة الوصول إلى الذاكرة"]}},"owner":"huiali","repo":"rust-skills","repoPath":"huiali/rust-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"rust-unsafe","description":"Unsafe code and FFI expert covering raw pointers (*mut, *const), FFI patterns, transmute, union, #[repr(C)], SAFETY comments, soundness rules, and undefined behavior prevention.","bodyPreview":"## When Unsafe is Justified\n\n| Use Case | Example | Justified? |\n|----------|---------|-----------|\n| FFI calls to C | `extern \"C\" { fn libc_malloc(size: usize) -> *mut c_void; }` | ✅ Yes |\n| Low-level abstractions | Internal implementation of `Vec`, `Arc` | ✅ Yes |\n| Performance optimization (measured) | Hot path with proven bottleneck | ⚠️ Verify first |\n| Escaping borrow checker | Don''t know why you need it | ❌ No |\n\n\n## SAFETY Comment Requirements\n\n**Every unsafe block must include a SAFETY","body":"## When Unsafe is Justified\n\n| Use Case | Example | Justified? |\n|----------|---------|-----------|\n| FFI calls to C | `extern \"C\" { fn libc_malloc(size: usize) -> *mut c_void; }` | ✅ Yes |\n| Low-level abstractions | Internal implementation of `Vec`, `Arc` | ✅ Yes |\n| Performance optimization (measured) | Hot path with proven bottleneck | ⚠️ Verify first |\n| Escaping borrow checker | Don''t know why you need it | ❌ No |\n\n\n## SAFETY Comment Requirements\n\n**Every unsafe block must include a SAFETY comment:**\n\n```rust\n// SAFETY: ptr must be non-null and properly aligned.\n// This function is only called after a null check.\nunsafe { *ptr = value; }\n\n/// # Safety\n///\n/// * `ptr` must be properly aligned and not null\n/// * `ptr` must point to initialized memory of type T\n/// * The memory must not be accessed after this function returns\npub unsafe fn write(ptr: *mut T, value: &T) { ... }\n```\n\n\n## Solution Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: FFI with Safe Wrapper\n\n```rust\nuse std::ffi::{CStr, CString};\nuse std::os::raw::c_char;\n\nextern \"C\" {\n    fn c_function(s: *const c_char) -> i32;\n}\n\n// ✅ Safe wrapper\npub fn safe_c_function(s: &str) -> Result<i32, Box<dyn Error>> {\n    let c_str = CString::new(s)?;\n    // SAFETY: c_str is a valid null-terminated string created from Rust data.\n    // The pointer is valid for the duration of this call.\n    let result = unsafe { c_function(c_str.as_ptr()) };\n    Ok(result)\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Raw Pointer with Validation\n\n```rust\nuse std::ptr::NonNull;\n\nstruct Buffer {\n    ptr: NonNull<u8>,\n    len: usize,\n}\n\nimpl Buffer {\n    pub fn write(&mut self, index: usize, value: u8) -> Result<(), String> {\n        if index >= self.len {\n            return Err(\"index out of bounds\".to_string());\n        }\n\n        // SAFETY: We''ve checked index is within bounds.\n        // ptr is NonNull and points to valid memory.\n        unsafe {\n            self.ptr.as_ptr().add(index).write(value);\n        }\n        Ok(())\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Uninitialized Memory\n\n```rust\nuse std::mem::MaybeUninit;\n\n// ✅ Safe uninitialized memory handling\nfn create_buffer(size: usize) -> Vec<u8> {\n    let mut buffer: Vec<MaybeUninit<u8>> = Vec::with_capacity(size);\n\n    for i in 0..size {\n        buffer.push(MaybeUninit::new(0));\n    }\n\n    // SAFETY: All elements have been initialized to 0.\n    unsafe { std::mem::transmute(buffer) }\n}\n\n// ❌ Avoid: deprecated pattern\nfn bad_buffer(size: usize) -> Vec<u8> {\n    let mut v = Vec::with_capacity(size);\n    unsafe { v.set_len(size); }  // UB if not initialized!\n    v\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: Repr(C) for FFI\n\n```rust\n#[repr(C)]\npub struct Point {\n    pub x: f64,\n    pub y: f64,\n}\n\n#[repr(C)]\npub enum Status {\n    Success = 0,\n    Error = 1,\n}\n\n// SAFETY: Layout matches C struct exactly\nextern \"C\" {\n    fn process_point(p: *const Point) -> Status;\n}\n```\n\n\n## 47 Unsafe Rules Reference\n\n### General Principles (3 rules)\n\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| G-01 | Don''t use unsafe to escape compiler safety checks |\n| G-02 | Don''t blindly use unsafe for performance |\n| G-03 | Don''t create \"Unsafe\" aliases for types/methods |\n\n### Memory Layout (6 rules)\n\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| M-01 | Choose appropriate memory layout for struct/tuple/enum |\n| M-02 | Don''t modify memory variables of other processes |\n| M-03 | Don''t let String/Vec auto-deallocate memory from other processes |\n| M-04 | Prefer reentrant versions of C-API or syscalls |\n| M-05 | Use third-party crates for bit fields |\n| M-06 | Use `MaybeUninit<T>` for uninitialized memory |\n\n### Raw Pointers (6 rules)\n\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| P-01 | Don''t share raw pointers across threads |\n| P-02 | Prefer `NonNull<T>` over `*mut T` |\n| P-03 | Use `PhantomData<T>` to mark variance and ownership |\n| P-04 | Don''t dereference pointers cast to misaligned types |\n| P-05 | Don''t manually convert immutable pointers to mutable |\n| P-06 | Use `ptr::cast` instead of `as` for pointer casts |\n\n### Unions (2 rules)\n\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| U-01 | Avoid unions except for C interop |\n| U-02 | Don''t use union variants with different lifetimes |\n\n### FFI (18 rules)\n\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| F-01 | Avoid passing strings directly to C |\n| F-02 | Carefully read `std::ffi` types documentation |\n| F-03 | Implement Drop for wrapped C pointers |\n| F-04 | Handle panics across FFI boundaries |\n| F-05 | Use portable type aliases from `std` or `libc` |\n| F-06 | Ensure C-ABI string compatibility |\n| F-07 | Don''t implement Drop for types passed to extern code |\n| F-08 | Handle errors properly in FFI |\n| F-09 | Use references instead of raw pointers in safe wrappers |\n| F-10 | Exported functions must be thread-safe |\n| F-11 | Be careful with references to `repr(packed)` fields |\n| F-12 | Document invariant assumptions for C parameters |\n| F-13 | Ensure consistent data layout for custom types |\n| F-14 | FFI types should have stable layout |\n| F-15 | Validate robustness of external values |\n| F-16 | Separate data and code for C closures |\n| F-17 | Use opaque types instead of `c_void` |\n| F-18 | Avoid passing trait objects to C |\n\n### Safe Abstractions (11 rules)\n\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| S-01 | Be aware of memory safety issues from panics |\n| S-02 | Unsafe code authors must verify safety invariants |\n| S-03 | Don''t expose uninitialized memory in public APIs |\n| S-04 | Avoid double-free from panics |\n| S-05 | Consider safety when manually implementing Auto Traits |\n| S-06 | Don''t expose raw pointers in public APIs |\n| S-07 | Provide safe alternatives for performance |\n| S-08 | Returning mutable reference from immutable parameter is wrong |\n| S-09 | Add SAFETY comment before each unsafe block |\n| S-10 | Add Safety section to public unsafe function docs |\n| S-11 | Use `assert!` instead of `debug_assert!` in unsafe functions |\n\n### I/O Safety (1 rule)\n\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| I-01 | Ensure I/O safety when using raw handles |\n\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Question the Need\n\n```\nDo I really need unsafe?\n  → Can I use safe abstractions?\n  → Is this for FFI? (justified)\n  → Is this for measured performance? (profile first)\n  → Am I fighting the borrow checker? (redesign instead)\n```\n\n### Step 2: Write SAFETY Comments\n\n```\nFor every unsafe block:\n1. Document preconditions\n2. Explain why they hold\n3. Reference invariants maintained\n\nFor public unsafe functions:\n1. Add /// # Safety section\n2. List all requirements\n3. Document consequences of violations\n```\n\n### Step 3: Validate with Tools\n\n```bash\n# Detect undefined behavior\ncargo +nightly miri test\n\n# Memory leak detection\nvalgrind ./target/release/program\n\n# Data race detection\nRUST_BACKTRACE=1 cargo test --features tsan\n```\n\n### Step 4: Build Safe Wrappers\n\n```\nRaw unsafe code\n  ↓\nSafe private functions (validate inputs)\n  ↓\nSafe public API (no unsafe visible)\n```\n\n\n## Common Errors and Fixes\n\n| Error | Fix |\n|-------|-----|\n| Null pointer dereference | Check for null before dereferencing |\n| Use after free | Ensure lifetime validity |\n| Data race | Add synchronization |\n| Alignment violation | Use `#[repr(C)]`, check alignment |\n| Invalid bit pattern | Use `MaybeUninit` |\n| Missing SAFETY comment | Add comment |\n\n\n## Deprecated Patterns\n\n| Deprecated | Modern Alternative |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| `mem::uninitialized()` | `MaybeUninit<T>` |\n| `mem::zeroed()` (for reference types) | `MaybeUninit<T>` |\n| Raw pointer arithmetic | `NonNull<T>`, `ptr::add` |\n| `CString::new().unwrap().as_ptr()` | Store `CString` first |\n| `static mut` | `AtomicT` or `Mutex` |\n| Manual extern declarations | `bindgen` |\n\n\n## FFI Tools\n\n| Direction | Tool |\n|-----------|------|\n| C → Rust | `bindgen` |\n| Rust → C | `cbindgen` |\n| Python | `PyO3` |\n| Node.js | `napi-rs` |\n| C++ | `cxx` |\n\n\n## Review Checklist\n\nWhen reviewing unsafe code:\n\n- [ ] Unsafe usage is justified (FFI, low-level abstraction, measured perf)\n- [ ] Every unsafe block has SAFETY comment\n- [ ] Public unsafe functions document Safety requirements\n- [ ] Raw pointers are validated before dereferencing\n- [ ] No raw pointer sharing across threads without sync\n- [ ] FFI boundaries properly handle panics\n- [ ] Memory layout explicitly specified for FFI types\n- [ ] Uninitialized memory uses `MaybeUninit`\n- [ ] Safe public API wraps unsafe internals\n- [ ] Tested with Miri for undefined behavior\n\n\n## Verification Commands\n\n```bash\n# Check for undefined behavior\ncargo +nightly miri test\n\n# Run with address sanitizer\nRUSTFLAGS=\"-Z sanitizer=address\" cargo +nightly test\n\n# Check FFI bindings\ncargo check --features ffi\n\n# Verify memory safety\nvalgrind --leak-check=full ./target/release/program\n\n# Documentation check\ncargo doc --no-deps --open\n```\n\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n### 1. Dangling Pointers\n\n**Symptom**: Use-after-free, segfault\n\n```rust\n// ❌ Bad: pointer outlives data\nfn bad() -> *const i32 {\n    let x = 42;\n    &x as *const i32  // Dangling!\n}\n\n// ✅ Good: proper lifetime management\nfn good(x: &i32) -> *const i32 {\n    x as *const i32  // Lifetime tied to input\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Uninitialized Memory\n\n**Symptom**: Undefined behavior, random values\n\n```rust\n// ❌ Bad: reading uninitialized memory\nlet x: i32;\nunsafe { println!(\"{}\", x); }  // UB!\n\n// ✅ Good: use MaybeUninit\nlet mut x = MaybeUninit::<i32>::uninit();\nx.write(42);\nlet x = unsafe { x.assume_init() };  // Safe\n```\n\n### 3. Invalid Repr\n\n**Symptom**: FFI crashes, data corruption\n\n```rust\n// ❌ Bad: default repr with FFI\nstruct Point { x: f64, y: f64 }\nextern \"C\" { fn use_point(p: Point); }\n\n// ✅ Good: explicit C layout\n#[repr(C)]\nstruct Point { x: f64, y: f64 }\nextern \"C\" { fn use_point(p: Point); }\n```\n\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **rust-ownership** - Lifetime and borrowing fundamentals\n- **rust-ffi** - Advanced FFI patterns\n- **rust-performance** - When unsafe optimization is justified\n- **rust-coding** - SAFETY comment conventions\n- **rust-concurrency** - Thread-safe unsafe patterns\n\n\n## Localized Reference\n\n- **Chinese version**: [SKILL_ZH.md](./SKILL_ZH.md) - 完整中文版本，包含所有内容\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:26:43.659Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Systems Programming Agents needing low-level memory management and performance optimization with Rust''s unsafe capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要低级内存管理和性能优化的系统编程代理，利用Rust的不安全功能。","ja":"システムプログラミングエージェントが低レベルのメモリ管理とパフォーマンス最適化を必要とする場合に適しています。Rustの不安全な機能を使用します。","ko":"시스템 프로그래밍 에이전트가 저수준 메모리 관리와 성능 최적화가 필요한 경우 적합합니다. 러스트의 안전하지 않은 기능을 사용합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Programación de Sistemas que necesitan gestión de memoria de bajo nivel y optimización del rendimiento con las capacidades no seguras de Rust.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Programmation de Systèmes ayant besoin d''une gestion de la mémoire de bas niveau et d''une optimisation des performances avec les fonctionnalités non sécurisées de Rust.","de":"Perfekt für Systemprogrammierungsagenten, die eine niedrigstufige Speicherverwaltung und Leistungsoptimierung mit den unsicheren Funktionen von Rust benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes de programação de sistemas que necessitam de gerenciamento de memória de baixo nível e otimização de desempenho com as capacidades não seguras do Rust.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов системного программирования, которым требуется управление памятью низкого уровня и оптимизация производительности с помощью возможностей Rust, не связанных с безопасностью.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات برمجة النظم التي تحتاج إلى إدارة ذاكرة منخفضة المستوى وتحسين الأداء باستخدام возможности رست غير الآمنة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to utilize Rust''s unsafe features for Foreign Function Interface (FFI) calls to C, low-level abstractions, and performance-critical code optimization, all while ensuring safety through meticulous documentation and verification, including the use of SAFETY comments and justified unsafe blocks.","zh":"赋予代理使用Rust的不安全功能进行外部函数接口（FFI）调用、低级抽象和性能关键代码优化的能力，同时通过仔细的文档和验证确保安全性，包括使用SAFETY注释和合理的不安全代码块。","ja":"エージェントがRustの安全でない機能を使用して外部関数インターフェイス（FFI）呼び出し、低レベルの抽象化、パフォーマンスクリティカルコードの最適化を行うことができるようにします。同時に、安全性を確保するために、慎重な文書化と検証、SAFETYコメントと正当化された安全でないブロックの使用を行います。","ko":"외부 함수 인터페이스(FFI) 호출, 저수준 추상화 및 성능 임계 코드 최적화를 위해 러스트의 안전하지 않은 기능을 사용할 수 있는 에이전트를赋予합니다.同時に, 안전성을 보장하기 위해 주의 깊은 문서화 및 검증, SAFETY 주석 및 정당한 안전하지 않은 블록을 사용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a utilizar las características no seguras de Rust para llamadas de interfaz de función externa (FFI) a C, abstracciones de bajo nivel y optimización de código crítico de rendimiento, todo mientras se garantiza la seguridad a través de una documentación y verificación exhaustivas, incluyendo el uso de comentarios de SEGURIDAD y bloques no seguros justificados.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''utiliser les fonctionnalités non sécurisées de Rust pour les appels d''interface de fonction étrangère (FFI) vers C, les abstractions de bas niveau et l''optimisation de code critique de performances, tout en garantissant la sécurité grâce à une documentation et une vérification minutieuses, y compris l''utilisation de commentaires de SÉCURITÉ et de blocs non sécurisés justifiés.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Rusts unsichere Funktionen für Aufrufe der Fremdfunktionsschnittstelle (FFI) an C, niedrigstufige Abstraktionen und leistungskritische Codeoptimierung zu nutzen, während die Sicherheit durch sorgfältige Dokumentation und Überprüfung gewährleistet wird, einschließlich der Verwendung von SICHERHEITS-Kommentaren und gerechtfertigten unsicheren Blöcken.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a utilizar os recursos não seguros do Rust para chamadas de Interface de Função Estrangeira (FFI) para C, abstrações de baixo nível e otimização de código crítico de desempenho, garantindo a segurança por meio de documentação meticulosa e verificação, incluindo o uso de comentários de SEGURANÇA e blocos não seguros justificados.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью использовать небезопасные функции Rust для вызовов иностранных функций (FFI) в C, абстракций низкого уровня и оптимизации критического кода, обеспечивая безопасность за счет тщательной документации и верификации, включая использование комментариев SAFETY и оправданных небезопасных блоков.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من استخدام ميزات رست غير الآمنة لأداء مكالمات واجهة الدوال الأجنبية (FFI) إلى سي، ومحاكاة منخفضة المستوى، وتحسين كود حرج الأداء، مع ضمان السلامة من خلال التوثيق المeticulous والتحقق، بما في ذلك استخدام تعليقات السلامة والكتل غير الآمنة المبررة."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing FFI calls to C libraries for enhanced functionality","Optimizing performance-critical code paths using unsafe Rust","Creating low-level abstractions for efficient data structures and algorithms"],"zh":["实现FFI调用以增强C库的功能","使用不安全的Rust优化性能关键代码路径","创建低级抽象以实现高效的数据结构和算法"],"ja":["Cライブラリの機能を強化するためのFFI呼び出しを実装する","パフォーマンスクリティカルコードパスの最適化に安全でないRustを使用する","効率的なデータ構造とアルゴリズムを実現するための低レベルの抽象化を作成する"],"ko":["함수성 기능을 강화하기 위한 C 라이브러리의 FFI 호출 구현","성능 임계 코드 경로 최적화를 위해 안전하지 않은 러스트 사용","효율적인 데이터 구조 및 알고리즘을 구현하기 위한 저수준 추상화 생성"],"es":["Implementar llamadas de FFI a bibliotecas de C para una funcionalidad mejorada","Optimizar caminos de código críticos de rendimiento utilizando Rust no seguro","Crear abstracciones de bajo nivel para estructuras de datos y algoritmos eficientes"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des appels FFI vers des bibliothèques C pour une fonctionnalité améliorée","Optimiser les chemins de code critiques de performances en utilisant Rust non sécurisé","Créer des abstractions de bas niveau pour des structures de données et des algorithmes efficaces"],"de":["Implementierung von FFI-Aufrufen an C-Bibliotheken für erweiterte Funktionalität","Optimierung von leistungskritischen Codepfaden unter Verwendung von unsicheren Rust","Erstellung von niedrigstufigen Abstraktionen für effiziente Datenstrukturen und Algorithmen"],"pt":["Implementação de chamadas de FFI para bibliotecas C para funcionalidades aprimoradas","Otimização de caminhos de código críticos de desempenho usando Rust não seguro","Criação de abstrações de baixo nível para estruturas de dados e algoritmos eficientes"],"ru":["Реализация вызовов FFI для библиотек C для расширенной функциональности","Оптимизация критических путей кода с помощью небезопасного Rust","Создание абстракций низкого уровня для эффективных структур данных и алгоритмов"],"ar":["تنفيذ مكالمات FFI إلى مكتبات سي لتحسين الوظائف","تحسين مسارات الكود الحرجة للأداء باستخدام رست غير آمن","إنشاء محاكاة منخفضة المستوى لتحسين هياكل البيانات والخوارزميات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires meticulous documentation and verification of unsafe code","Demands a deep understanding of Rust''s memory model and borrow checker","Should be used judiciously and only when justified, with a focus on measured performance optimization"],"zh":["需要对不安全代码进行仔细的文档和验证","需要深入了解Rust的内存模型和借用检查器","应该谨慎使用并仅在必要时使用，重点是衡量性能优化"],"ja":["安全でないコードの慎重な文書化と検証が必要","Rustのメモリモデルと借用チェッカーの深い理解が必要","慎重に使用し、必要な場合のみ使用する必要があり、重点は測定されたパフォーマンス最適化"],"ko":["안전하지 않은 코드에 대한 주의 깊은 문서화 및 검증이 필요합니다","러스트의 메모리 모델 및 대출 검사기에 대한 깊은 이해가 필요합니다","신중하게 사용하고 필요한 경우에만 사용해야 하며 중점은 측정된 성능 최적화"],"es":["Requiere una documentación y verificación exhaustivas del código no seguro","Exige un profundo conocimiento del modelo de memoria de Rust y del prestamista de préstamos","Debería usarse con juicio y solo cuando esté justificado, con un enfoque en la optimización del rendimiento medido"],"fr":["Nécessite une documentation et une vérification minutieuses du code non sécurisé","Exige une compréhension approfondie du modèle de mémoire de Rust et du vérificateur d''emprunt","Devrait être utilisé avec jugement et uniquement lorsqu''il est justifié, avec un focus sur l''optimisation des performances mesurées"],"de":["Erfordert eine sorgfältige Dokumentation und Überprüfung des unsicheren Codes","Fordert ein tiefes Verständnis des Rust-Speichermodells und des Borrow-Checkers","Sollte nur mit Bedacht und nur wenn gerechtfertigt eingesetzt werden, mit Fokus auf die gemessene Leistungsoptimierung"],"pt":["Exige documentação e verificação meticulosas de código não seguro","Exige uma compreensão profunda do modelo de memória do Rust e do empréstimo de verificação","Deve ser usado comedido e apenas quando justificado, com foco na otimização de desempenho medida"],"ru":["Требует тщательной документации и верификации небезопасного кода","Требует глубокого понимания модели памяти Rust и заимствования проверки","Должно использоваться осторожно и только при наличии обоснования, с фокусом на измеренной оптимизации производительности"],"ar":["يتطلب توثيقًا وتحققًا دقيقين للكود غير الآمن","يتطلب فهمًا عميقًا لنموذج الذاكرة رست ومراجعة الإقراض","يجب استخدامه بحذر وเฉพาะ عند التبرير، مع التركيز على تحسين الأداء المقاس"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
