지 확인합니다","es":"La revisión de planes de implementación es crucial para garantizar la cobertura, corrección y ajuste con el código base actual","fr":"La révision des plans d''implémentation est essentielle pour garantir la couverture, la correction et l''ajustement avec le code base actuel","de":"Die Überprüfung von Implementierungsplänen ist entscheidend, um die Abdeckung, Korrektheit und Anpassung an den aktuellen Codebase zu gewährleisten","pt":"Revisão de plano de implementação para garantir cobertura, correção e compatibilidade com o código atual","ru":"Проверка плана реализации для обеспечения покрытия, корректности и совместимости с текущим кодом","ar":"استعراض خطة التنفيذ لضمان التغطية والصحة والتوافق مع الكود الحالي","en":"Wraps Blockscout APIs and exposes blockchain data by Model Context Protocol"},"definition":{"en":"Wraps Blockscout APIs and exposes blockchain data by Model Context Protocol"},"features":{"zh":["审查实现计划","检查覆盖范围和正确性","检查代码库适配性","支持本地文件路径和GitHub问题编号","使用Model Context Protocol暴露区块链数据"],"ja":["実装計画をレビューする","カバレッジと正確性を確認する","コードベースへの適合性を確認する","ローカルファイルパスとGitHubの問題番号をサポートする","Model Context Protocolを使用してブロックチェーンデータを公開する"],"ko":["구현 계획을 검토합니다","범위와 정확성을 확인합니다","코드베이스 적합성을 확인합니다","로컬 파일 경로와 GitHub 문제 번호를 지원합니다","Model Context Protocol을 사용하여 블록체인 데이터를 공개합니다"],"es":["Revisión de planes de implementación para blockchain","Integración con Model Context Protocol","Uso de Blockscout APIs para exponer datos de blockchain","Análisis de cobertura y corrección del plan","Ajuste con el código base actual"],"fr":["Révision des plans d''implémentation pour blockchain","Intégration avec Model Context Protocol","Utilisation de Blockscout APIs pour exposer des données de blockchain","Analyse de la couverture et de la correction du plan","Ajustement avec le code base actuel"],"de":["Überprüfung von Implementierungsplänen für Blockchain","Integration mit Model Context Protocol","Verwendung von Blockscout APIs zur Exposition von Blockchain-Daten","Analyse der Abdeckung und Korrektheit des Plans","Anpassung an den aktuellen Codebase"],"pt":["Análise de plano de implementação","Verificação de cobertura e correção","Compatibilidade com o código atual","Suporte a GitHub","Análise de requisitos e problemas"],"ru":["Анализ плана реализации","Проверка покрытия и корректности","Совместимость с текущим кодом","Поддержка GitHub","Анализ требований и проблем"],"ar":["استعراض خطة التنفيذ","تحليل التغطية والصحة","التوافق مع الكود الحالي","دعم GitHub","تحليل المتطلبات والمشاكل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["区块链实现计划","代码库适配性","Model Context Protocol","ブロックチェーンデータ","实现计划审查","代码审查"],"ja":["ブロックチェーン実装計画","コードベース適合性","Model Context Protocol","ブロックチェーンデータ","実装計画レビュー","コードレビュー"],"ko":["블록체인 구현 계획","코드베이스 적합성","Model Context Protocol","블록체인 데이터","구현 계획 검토","코드 검토"],"es":["revisión de planes de implementación","blockchain","Model Context Protocol","Blockscout APIs","desarrollo de software","implementación de blockchain"],"fr":["révision des plans d''implémentation","blockchain","Model Context Protocol","Blockscout APIs","développement de logiciels","implémentation de blockchain"],"de":["Überprüfung von Implementierungsplänen","Blockchain","Model Context Protocol","Blockscout APIs","Softwareentwicklung","Implementierung von Blockchain"],"pt":["revisão de plano de implementação","análise de código","desenvolvimento de software","github","requisitos de software","problemas de software","planejamento de implementação"],"ru":["проверка плана реализации","анализ кода","разработка программного обеспечения","github","требования программного обеспечения","проблемы программного обеспечения","планирование реализации"],"ar":["استعراض خطة التنفيذ","تحليل الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","github","متطلبات البرمجيات","مشاكل البرمجيات","تخطيط التنفيذ"]}},"owner":"blockscout","repo":"mcp-server","repoPath":"blockscout/mcp-server","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"implementation-plan-review","description":"Expert review of an implementation plan against a GitHub issue/enhancement description (provided as a local file or a GitHub issue URL) and the current repository codebase. Use when asked to critique a plan for correctness, completeness, codebase alignment, risks, and test/rollout readiness (do not implement).","bodyPreview":"# Implementation Plan Review (Expert)\n\nReview an implementation plan for coverage, correctness, and fit with the current codebase. Do not implement.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Implementation plan: a local file path.\n- Issue/requirements: either (a) a local file path, or (b) a GitHub issue number (run from the target repo so `gh` resolves it).\n\nIf the user provides a GitHub issue number, prefer fetching it into a local file using the bundled script (requires `gh` auth and network access; otherwise ask for a l","body":"# Implementation Plan Review (Expert)\n\nReview an implementation plan for coverage, correctness, and fit with the current codebase. Do not implement.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Implementation plan: a local file path.\n- Issue/requirements: either (a) a local file path, or (b) a GitHub issue number (run from the target repo so `gh` resolves it).\n\nIf the user provides a GitHub issue number, prefer fetching it into a local file using the bundled script (requires `gh` auth and network access; otherwise ask for a local issue description file):\n\n```bash\nbash .codex/skills/implementation-plan-review/scripts/fetch_github_issue.sh <issue-number> --out /tmp/issue.md\n```\n\nIf the script reports that `gh` is not authenticated (exit code `3`), ask the user to run:\n\n```bash\ngh auth login\n```\n\n## Workflow\n\n1) Ensure repo startup constraints are satisfied:\n   - In this repository, run `$codex-session-bootstrap` before doing any other work.\n\n2) Read the two inputs in full:\n   - Plan file\n   - Issue description file (or the fetched `/tmp/issue.md`)\n\n3) Apply strict versioning-comment policy:\n   - Do **not** request or suggest any version bump (package version, `server.json`, etc.) unless the **issue description explicitly requires** a version bump/release/publish/tag.\n   - Even if the plan changes externally-consumed surfaces (tool schemas, REST/OpenAPI, manifests), treat missing version bump steps as **intentional** unless the issue says otherwise.\n\n4) Validate codebase reality (start targeted, expand as needed):\n   - Start by finding referenced modules/configs/env vars/tests with `rg` (fast and low-noise).\n   - Prefer opening the minimal set of files *first* to confirm patterns and naming, but broaden freely if you suspect hidden coupling or cross-cutting behavior (e.g., shared helpers, config loading, response models, pagination, truncation).\n   - If the plan touches MCP tools, REST API, docs, or tests, cross-check relevant `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` guidance.\n   - If it improves confidence, use any other repo investigation strategy (e.g., inspect docs like `SPEC.md`/`API.md`, check tests, use `git blame`, or run unit tests/lint locally).\n\nSuggested commands (adapt as needed):\n\n```bash\nrg -n \"name_in_plan|function_in_plan|ENV_VAR_IN_PLAN\" -S .\nrg -n \"ToolResponse\\\\[|@mcp\\\\.tool\\\\(|log_tool_invocation\" blockscout_mcp_server -S\nrg -n \"ServerConfig\\\\(|BaseSettings\\\\(|BLOCKSCOUT_\" blockscout_mcp_server/config.py -S\nrg -n \"pytest\\\\.mark\\\\.integration|tests/integration|tests/tools\" tests -S\n```\n\n1) Produce the review in the required format (next section).\n\n## Required output format\n\nProduce a review with these sections:\n\n### 1) Understanding\n\n- Issue summary\n- Acceptance criteria (bulleted)\n\n### 2) Plan ↔ Requirements coverage\n\n- What is covered well\n- What is missing / ambiguous\n\n### 3) Codebase alignment\n\n- Key files/modules you inspected (with paths)\n- Assumptions in the plan that match the codebase\n- Assumptions that don’t match (explain and suggest correction)\n\n### 4) Review comments (actionable)\n\nProvide comments as a list. Each comment must include:\n\n- Severity: `Blocker | Major | Minor | Question | Nit`\n- Location: plan section/step + (when relevant) repo file/function/class\n- Problem: what’s wrong / missing\n- Recommendation: concrete change to the plan\n- Rationale: why it matters (bug risk / security / perf / maintainability)\n\n**Testing gaps rule:**\n\n- List every specific missing/incorrect test as an actionable comment in **§4**.\n- In **§6**, provide a consolidated checklist that references those items **without repeating full explanations**.\n\n### 5) Junior-dev readiness check\n\n- Missing prerequisites, commands, step ordering, “how to verify”\n- Where the plan needs more explicit detail\n\n### 6) Test & rollout strategy\n\n- Consolidated test checklist (Unit / Integration / E2E / Negative & security / Performance & regression), referencing §4 test comments\n- Migration/rollback plan if applicable\n- Feature flags / safe rollout suggestions if applicable\n\n## Review focus checklist (use as prompts, not new requirements)\n\n- Coverage: every acceptance criterion mapped to plan steps.\n- Codebase alignment: paths, module structure, naming, existing helpers and patterns.\n- Edge cases & compatibility: pagination, timeouts, empty results, truncation limits, backward compatibility.\n- Security: input validation, SSRF/DNS rebinding boundaries, secrets handling, logging redaction, auth assumptions.\n- Performance/scale: API call counts, caching, pagination strategy, long-running tasks/progress updates.\n- Ops/observability: error handling, logs, metrics/telemetry/analytics implications, rollout/rollback.\n- Versioning: only comment if explicitly required by the issue description; otherwise assume omission is intentional.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:26:45.385Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing advanced implementation plan analysis capabilities via Model Context Protocol","zh":"非常适合需要通过模型上下文协议进行高级实现计划分析的代码审查代理","ja":"コードレビューエージェントがモデルコンテキストプロトコルを介して高度な実装計画分析機能を必要とする場合に最適","ko":"코드 리뷰 에이전트가 모델 컨텍스트 프로토콜을 통해 고급 구현 계획 분석 기능을 필요로 하는 경우에 가장 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan capacidades de análisis de planes de implementación avanzados a través del Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de révision de code nécessitant des capacités d''analyse de plans d''implémentation avancées via le Protocole de Contexte de Modèle","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agenten, die erweiterte Implementierungsplananalysefunktionen über das Modellkontextprotokoll benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de análise de planos de implementação via Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов кодового обзора, которым требуются расширенные возможности анализа планов реализации через Протокол контекста модели","ar":"مثالي لعمليات المراجعة الكودية التي تحتاج إلى خيارات متقدمة لتحليلخطط التنفيذ من خلال بروتوكول سياق النموذج"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to review implementation plans for coverage, correctness, and fit with the current codebase, utilizing Blockscout APIs and handling local file paths or GitHub issue numbers with gh authentication","zh":"赋予代理审查实现计划的覆盖范围、正确性和与当前代码库的兼容性，利用Blockscout API并处理本地文件路径或GitHub问题号，使用gh身份验证","ja":"エージェントが実装計画のカバレッジ、正しさ、現在のコードベースとの適合性をレビューできるようにし、Blockscout APIを利用し、ローカルファイルパスまたはGitHubの問題番号をgh認証で処理","ko":"에이전트가 구현 계획의 범위, 정확성 및 현재 코드베이스와의 적합성을 검토할 수 있도록 하며, Blockscout API를 활용하고 로컬 파일 경로 또는 GitHub 이슈 번호를 gh 인증으로 처리","es":"Habilita a los agentes a revisar los planes de implementación para cobertura, corrección y ajuste con la base de código actual, utilizando las APIs de Blockscout y manejando rutas de archivo locales o números de problema de GitHub con autenticación gh","fr":"Permet aux agents de réviser les plans d''implémentation pour la couverture, la correction et l''ajustement avec la base de code actuelle, en utilisant les API Blockscout et en gérant les chemins de fichiers locaux ou les numéros de problème GitHub avec l''authentification gh","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Implementierungspläne für Abdeckung, Richtigkeit und Anpassung an die aktuelle Codebasis zu überprüfen, indem sie die Blockscout-APIs nutzen und lokale Dateipfade oder GitHub-Problemmnummern mit gh-Authentifizierung verarbeiten","pt":"Habilita os agentes a revisar planos de implementação para cobertura, correção e adequação à base de código atual, utilizando APIs do Blockscout e lidando com caminhos de arquivos locais ou números de problemas do GitHub com autenticação gh","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью рассматривать планы реализации для покрытия, правильности и соответствия текущей базе кода, используя API Blockscout и обрабатывая локальные пути файлов или номера проблем GitHub с аутентификацией gh","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من مراجعة خطط التنفيذ لتغطية الصحة والملاءمة مع قاعدة الشفرة الحالية، باستخدام واجهات برمجة تطبيقات Blockscout ومعالجة مسارات الملفات المحلية أو أرقام المشكلات في GitHub مع المصادقة gh"},"useCases":{"en":["Reviewing implementation plans for new feature integration","Validating correctness of code changes against issue requirements","Analyzing coverage of implementation plans against existing codebase"],"zh":["审查新功能集成的实现计划","验证代码更改的正确性与问题要求","分析实现计划的覆盖范围与现有代码库"],"ja":["新しい機能統合のための実装計画のレビュー","コード変更の正しさを問題要件と比較検証","実装計画のカバレッジを既存のコードベースと分析"],"ko":["새로운 기능 통합을 위한 구현 계획의 검토","코드 변경의 정확성을 문제 요구 사항과 확인","구현 계획의 범위를 기존 코드베이스와 분석"],"es":["Revisar planes de implementación para la integración de nuevas características","Validar la corrección de los cambios de código frente a los requisitos del problema","Analizar la cobertura de los planes de implementación frente a la base de código existente"],"fr":["Réviser les plans d''implémentation pour l''intégration de nouvelles fonctionnalités","Valider la correction des modifications de code par rapport aux exigences du problème","Analyser la couverture des plans d''implémentation par rapport à la base de code existante"],"de":["Überprüfung von Implementierungsplänen für die Integration neuer Funktionen","Überprüfung der Richtigkeit von Codeänderungen gegenüber den Problemvoraussetzungen","Analyse der Abdeckung von Implementierungsplänen gegenüber der bestehenden Codebasis"],"pt":["Revisar planos de implementação para integração de recursos novos","Validar a correção das alterações de código em relação aos requisitos da issue","Analizar a cobertura dos planos de implementação em relação à base de código existente"],"ru":["Просмотр планов реализации для интеграции новых функций","Проверка правильности изменений кода относительно требований проблемы","Анализ покрытия планов реализации относительно существующей базы кода"],"ar":["مراجعة خطط التنفيذ لتكامل الميزات الجديدة","التحقق من صحة تغييرات الشفرة فيما يتعلق بمتطلبات المشكلة","تحليل تغطية خطط التنفيذ فيما يتعلق بقاعدة الشفرة الحالية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires gh authentication and network access for GitHub issue resolution","Limited to handling local file paths or GitHub issue numbers as input"],"zh":["需要gh身份验证和网络访问以解决GitHub问题","仅限处理本地文件路径或GitHub问题号作为输入"],"ja":["GitHubの問題解決のためにgh認証とネットワークアクセスが必要","入力としてローカルファイルパスまたはGitHubの問題番号のみを処理"],"ko":["GitHub 이슈 해결을 위해 gh 인증 및 네트워크 액세스가 필요","로컬 파일 경로 또는 GitHub 이슈 번호만 입력으로 처리"],"es":["Requiere autenticación gh y acceso a la red para la resolución de problemas de GitHub","Limitado a la gestión de rutas de archivo locales o números de problema de GitHub como entrada"],"fr":["Nécessite une authentification gh et un accès au réseau pour la résolution des problèmes GitHub","Limité à la gestion des chemins de fichiers locaux ou des numéros de problème GitHub comme entrée"],"de":["Erfordert gh-Authentifizierung und Netzwerkzugriff für die Auflösung von GitHub-Problemen","Begrenzt auf die Verarbeitung von lokalen Dateipfaden oder GitHub-Problemmnummern als Eingabe"],"pt":["Exige autenticação gh e acesso à rede para resolução de problemas do GitHub","Limitado a lidar com caminhos de arquivos locais ou números de problemas do GitHub como entrada"],"ru":["Требует аутентификации gh и доступа к сети для решения проблем GitHub","Ограничен обработкой локальных путей файлов или номеров проблем GitHub в качестве входных данных"],"ar":["يتطلب مصادقة gh ووصول إلى الشبكة لحل مشكلات GitHub","محدود بمعالجة مسارات الملفات المحلية أو أرقام مشكلات GitHub كمدخلات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('EricOo0/stock-trading-platform/systematic-debugging', 'community', 'EricOo0', 'stock-trading-platform', 'EricOo0/stock-trading-platform', 'systematic-debugging', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z', '2026-02-18T06:26:57.186Z', NULL, '{"id":"EricOo0/stock-trading-platform/systematic-debugging","name":"systematic-debugging","description":{"zh":"系统化调试是一种通过找到根因来解决技术问题的方法，提高代码质量和效率","ja":"体系的なデバッグは、根本原因を特定して技術的な問題を解決する方法で、コードの品質と効率を向上させる","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 근본 원인을 찾아 기술적인 문제를 해결하는 방법으로 코드 품질과 효율성을 향상시킵니다","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque estructurado para identificar y solucionar errores de software. Siempre encuentra la causa raíz antes de proponer soluciones.","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche structurée pour identifier et résoudre les erreurs de logiciel. Trouvez toujours la cause profonde avant de proposer des solutions.","de":"Die systematische Fehlersuche ist ein strukturierter Ansatz, um Softwarefehler zu identifizieren und zu beheben. Finden Sie immer die Ursache, bevor Sie Lösungen vorschlagen.","pt":"A depuração sistemática é uma abordagem que enfatiza a importância de encontrar a causa raiz dos problemas técnicos antes de propor soluções","ru":"Системная отладка - это подход, который подчеркивает важность нахождения коренной причины технических проблем перед предложением решений","ar":"تصحيح 系统ي هو نهج يؤكد على أهمية العثور على السبب الجذري للمشاكل الفنية قبل تقديم الحلول","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"系统化调试技术","ja":"体系的なデバッグ","ko":"시스템 디버깅","es":"Depuración Sistemática: Encontrar la Causa Raíz","fr":"Débogage Systématique: Trouver la Cause Profonde","de":"Systematische Fehlersuche: Die Ursache Finden","pt":"Depuração Sistemática: Encontre a Causa Raiz","ru":"Системная отладка: найдите коренную причину","ar":"تصحيح 系统ي: العثور على السبب الجذري","en":"systematic-debugging"},"description":{"zh":"系统化调试是一种通过找到根因来解决技术问题的方法，提高代码质量和效率","ja":"体系的なデバッグは、根本原因を特定して技術的な問題を解決する方法で、コードの品質と効率を向上させる","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 근본 원인을 찾아 기술적인 문제를 해결하는 방법으로 코드 품질과 효율성을 향상시킵니다","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque estructurado para identificar y solucionar errores de software. Siempre encuentra la causa raíz antes de proponer sol...","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche structurée pour identifier et résoudre les erreurs de logiciel. Trouvez toujours la cause profonde avant de propose...","de":"Die systematische Fehlersuche ist ein strukturierter Ansatz, um Softwarefehler zu identifizieren und zu beheben. Finden Sie immer die Ursache, bevor Sie Lösu...","pt":"A depuração sistemática é uma abordagem que enfatiza a importância de encontrar a causa raiz dos problemas técnicos antes de propor soluções","ru":"Системная отладка - это подход, который подчеркивает важность нахождения коренной причины технических проблем перед предложением решений","ar":"تصحيح 系统ي هو نهج يؤكد على أهمية العثور على السبب الجذري للمشاكل الفنية قبل تقديم الحلول","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["找到根因","提高代码质量","提高效率","解决技术问题","遵循铁律"],"ja":["根本原因の特定","コード品質の向上","効率の向上","技術的な問題の解決","鉄則の遵守"],"ko":["근본 원인 찾기","코드 품질 향상","효율성 향상","기술적인 문제 해결","철칙 준수"],"es":["Enfoque estructurado para la depuración","Identificación de la causa raíz de los errores","Evitación de soluciones temporales","Aplicación a cualquier problema técnico","Incluye fases de investigación y solución","Mejora la eficiencia en la resolución de errores"],"fr":["Approche structurée pour le débogage","Identification de la cause profonde des erreurs","Évitement des solutions temporaires","Application à tout problème technique","Comprend des phases d''investigation et de solution","Améliore l''efficacité dans la résolution des erreurs"],"de":["Strukturierter Ansatz für die Fehlersuche","Identifizierung der Ursache von Fehlern","Vermeidung von temporären Lösungen","Anwendung auf jedes technische Problem","Umfasst Phasen der Untersuchung und Lösung","Verbessert die Effizienz bei der Fehlerbehebung"],"pt":["Identificação da causa raiz dos problemas técnicos","Análise sistemática de problemas","Proposta de soluções eficazes","Redução de tempo e esforço para resolver problemas","Melhoria da qualidade do código"],"ru":["Определение коренной причины технических проблем","Системный анализ проблем","Предложение эффективных решений","Сокращение времени и усилий для решения проблем","Улучшение качества кода"],"ar":["تحديد السبب الجذري للمشاكل الفنية","تحليل منهجي للمشاكل","تقديم حلول فعالة","تقليل الوقت والجهد لแก้ไข المشاكل","تحسين جودة الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["系统化调试","技术问题解决","代码质量","效率提高","调试技巧","编码最佳实践"],"ja":["体系的なデバッグ","技術的な問題の解決","コード品質","効率の向上","デバッグテクニック","コーディングベストプラクティス"],"ko":["시스템 디버깅","기술적인 문제 해결","코드 품질","효율성 향상","디버깅 기술","코딩最佳实践"],"es":["depuración sistemática","causa raíz","errores de software","solución de errores","eficiencia en la depuración","enfoque estructurado","investigación de errores","solución de problemas técnicos"],"fr":["débogage systématique","cause profonde","erreurs de logiciel","résolution d''erreurs","efficacité dans le débogage","approche structurée","investigation d''erreurs","résolution de problèmes techniques"],"de":["systematische Fehlersuche","Ursache","Softwarefehler","Fehlerbehebung","Effizienz bei der Fehlersuche","strukturierter Ansatz","Fehleruntersuchung","Lösung technischer Probleme"],"pt":["depuração sistemática","resolução de problemas","análise de problemas","causa raiz","soluções eficazes","qualidade do código"],"ru":["системная отладка","решение проблем","анализ проблем","коренная причина","эффективные решения","качество кода"],"ar":["تصحيح 系统ي","حل المشاكل","تحليل المشاكل","السبب الجذري","حلول فعالة","جودة الكود"]}},"owner":"EricOo0","repo":"stock-trading-platform","repoPath":"EricOo0/stock-trading-platform","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"systematic-debugging","description":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes","bodyPreview":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs","body":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs in production\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Performance problems\n- Build failures\n- Integration issues\n\n**Use this ESPECIALLY when:**\n- Under time pressure (emergencies make guessing tempting)\n- \"Just one quick fix\" seems obvious\n- You''ve already tried multiple fixes\n- Previous fix didn''t work\n- You don''t fully understand the issue\n\n**Don''t skip when:**\n- Issue seems simple (simple bugs have root causes too)\n- You''re in a hurry (rushing guarantees rework)\n- Manager wants it fixed NOW (systematic is faster than thrashing)\n\n## The Four Phases\n\nYou MUST complete each phase before proceeding to the next.\n\n### Phase 1: Root Cause Investigation\n\n**BEFORE attempting ANY fix:**\n\n1. **Read Error Messages Carefully**\n   - Don''t skip past errors or warnings\n   - They often contain the exact solution\n   - Read stack traces completely\n   - Note line numbers, file paths, error codes\n\n2. **Reproduce Consistently**\n   - Can you trigger it reliably?\n   - What are the exact steps?\n   - Does it happen every time?\n   - If not reproducible → gather more data, don''t guess\n\n3. **Check Recent Changes**\n   - What changed that could cause this?\n   - Git diff, recent commits\n   - New dependencies, config changes\n   - Environmental differences\n\n4. **Gather Evidence in Multi-Component Systems**\n\n   **WHEN system has multiple components (CI → build → signing, API → service → database):**\n\n   **BEFORE proposing fixes, add diagnostic instrumentation:**\n   ```\n   For EACH component boundary:\n     - Log what data enters component\n     - Log what data exits component\n     - Verify environment/config propagation\n     - Check state at each layer\n\n   Run once to gather evidence showing WHERE it breaks\n   THEN analyze evidence to identify failing component\n   THEN investigate that specific component\n   ```\n\n   **Example (multi-layer system):**\n   ```bash\n   # Layer 1: Workflow\n   echo \"=== Secrets available in workflow: ===\"\n   echo \"IDENTITY: ${IDENTITY:+SET}${IDENTITY:-UNSET}\"\n\n   # Layer 2: Build script\n   echo \"=== Env vars in build script: ===\"\n   env | grep IDENTITY || echo \"IDENTITY not in environment\"\n\n   # Layer 3: Signing script\n   echo \"=== Keychain state: ===\"\n   security list-keychains\n   security find-identity -v\n\n   # Layer 4: Actual signing\n   codesign --sign \"$IDENTITY\" --verbose=4 \"$APP\"\n   ```\n\n   **This reveals:** Which layer fails (secrets → workflow ✓, workflow → build ✗)\n\n5. **Trace Data Flow**\n\n   **WHEN error is deep in call stack:**\n\n   See `root-cause-tracing.md` in this directory for the complete backward tracing technique.\n\n   **Quick version:**\n   - Where does bad value originate?\n   - What called this with bad value?\n   - Keep tracing up until you find the source\n   - Fix at source, not at symptom\n\n### Phase 2: Pattern Analysis\n\n**Find the pattern before fixing:**\n\n1. **Find Working Examples**\n   - Locate similar working code in same codebase\n   - What works that''s similar to what''s broken?\n\n2. **Compare Against References**\n   - If implementing pattern, read reference implementation COMPLETELY\n   - Don''t skim - read every line\n   - Understand the pattern fully before applying\n\n3. **Identify Differences**\n   - What''s different between working and broken?\n   - List every difference, however small\n   - Don''t assume \"that can''t matter\"\n\n4. **Understand Dependencies**\n   - What other components does this need?\n   - What settings, config, environment?\n   - What assumptions does it make?\n\n### Phase 3: Hypothesis and Testing\n\n**Scientific method:**\n\n1. **Form Single Hypothesis**\n   - State clearly: \"I think X is the root cause because Y\"\n   - Write it down\n   - Be specific, not vague\n\n2. **Test Minimally**\n   - Make the SMALLEST possible change to test hypothesis\n   - One variable at a time\n   - Don''t fix multiple things at once\n\n3. **Verify Before Continuing**\n   - Did it work? Yes → Phase 4\n   - Didn''t work? Form NEW hypothesis\n   - DON''T add more fixes on top\n\n4. **When You Don''t Know**\n   - Say \"I don''t understand X\"\n   - Don''t pretend to know\n   - Ask for help\n   - Research more\n\n### Phase 4: Implementation\n\n**Fix the root cause, not the symptom:**\n\n1. **Create Failing Test Case**\n   - Simplest possible reproduction\n   - Automated test if possible\n   - One-off test script if no framework\n   - MUST have before fixing\n   - Use the `superpowers:test-driven-development` skill for writing proper failing tests\n\n2. **Implement Single Fix**\n   - Address the root cause identified\n   - ONE change at a time\n   - No \"while I''m here\" improvements\n   - No bundled refactoring\n\n3. **Verify Fix**\n   - Test passes now?\n   - No other tests broken?\n   - Issue actually resolved?\n\n4. **If Fix Doesn''t Work**\n   - STOP\n   - Count: How many fixes have you tried?\n   - If < 3: Return to Phase 1, re-analyze with new information\n   - **If ≥ 3: STOP and question the architecture (step 5 below)**\n   - DON''T attempt Fix #4 without architectural discussion\n\n5. **If 3+ Fixes Failed: Question Architecture**\n\n   **Pattern indicating architectural problem:**\n   - Each fix reveals new shared state/coupling/problem in different place\n   - Fixes require \"massive refactoring\" to implement\n   - Each fix creates new symptoms elsewhere\n\n   **STOP and question fundamentals:**\n   - Is this pattern fundamentally sound?\n   - Are we \"sticking with it through sheer inertia\"?\n   - Should we refactor architecture vs. continue fixing symptoms?\n\n   **Discuss with your human partner before attempting more fixes**\n\n   This is NOT a failed hypothesis - this is a wrong architecture.\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Follow Process\n\nIf you catch yourself thinking:\n- \"Quick fix for now, investigate later\"\n- \"Just try changing X and see if it works\"\n- \"Add multiple changes, run tests\"\n- \"Skip the test, I''ll manually verify\"\n- \"It''s probably X, let me fix that\"\n- \"I don''t fully understand but this might work\"\n- \"Pattern says X but I''ll adapt it differently\"\n- \"Here are the main problems: [lists fixes without investigation]\"\n- Proposing solutions before tracing data flow\n- **\"One more fix attempt\" (when already tried 2+)**\n- **Each fix reveals new problem in different place**\n\n**ALL of these mean: STOP. Return to Phase 1.**\n\n**If 3+ fixes failed:** Question the architecture (see Phase 4.5)\n\n## your human partner''s Signals You''re Doing It Wrong\n\n**Watch for these redirections:**\n- \"Is that not happening?\" - You assumed without verifying\n- \"Will it show us...?\" - You should have added evidence gathering\n- \"Stop guessing\" - You''re proposing fixes without understanding\n- \"Ultrathink this\" - Question fundamentals, not just symptoms\n- \"We''re stuck?\" (frustrated) - Your approach isn''t working\n\n**When you see these:** STOP. Return to Phase 1.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Issue is simple, don''t need process\" | Simple issues have root causes too. Process is fast for simple bugs. |\n| \"Emergency, no time for process\" | Systematic debugging is FASTER than guess-and-check thrashing. |\n| \"Just try this first, then investigate\" | First fix sets the pattern. Do it right from the start. |\n| \"I''ll write test after confirming fix works\" | Untested fixes don''t stick. Test first proves it. |\n| \"Multiple fixes at once saves time\" | Can''t isolate what worked. Causes new bugs. |\n| \"Reference too long, I''ll adapt the pattern\" | Partial understanding guarantees bugs. Read it completely. |\n| \"I see the problem, let me fix it\" | Seeing symptoms ≠ understanding root cause. |\n| \"One more fix attempt\" (after 2+ failures) | 3+ failures = architectural problem. Question pattern, don''t fix again. |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Phase | Key Activities | Success Criteria |\n|-------|---------------|------------------|\n| **1. Root Cause** | Read errors, reproduce, check changes, gather evidence | Understand WHAT and WHY |\n| **2. Pattern** | Find working examples, compare | Identify differences |\n| **3. Hypothesis** | Form theory, test minimally | Confirmed or new hypothesis |\n| **4. Implementation** | Create test, fix, verify | Bug resolved, tests pass |\n\n## When Process Reveals \"No Root Cause\"\n\nIf systematic investigation reveals issue is truly environmental, timing-dependent, or external:\n\n1. You''ve completed the process\n2. Document what you investigated\n3. Implement appropriate handling (retry, timeout, error message)\n4. Add monitoring/logging for future investigation\n\n**But:** 95% of \"no root cause\" cases are incomplete investigation.\n\n## Supporting Techniques\n\nThese techniques are part of systematic debugging and available in this directory:\n\n- **`root-cause-tracing.md`** - Trace bugs backward through call stack to find original trigger\n- **`defense-in-depth.md`** - Add validation at multiple layers after finding root cause\n- **`condition-based-waiting.md`** - Replace arbitrary timeouts with condition polling\n\n**Related skills:**\n- **superpowers:test-driven-development** - For creating failing test case (Phase 4, Step 1)\n- **superpowers:verification-before-completion** - Verify fix worked before claiming success\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging sessions:\n- Systematic approach: 15-30 minutes to fix\n- Random fixes approach: 2-3 hours of thrashing\n- First-time fix rate: 95% vs 40%\n- New bugs introduced: Near zero vs common\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:26:57.186Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Technical Agents needing structured issue resolution through systematic debugging","zh":"非常适合需要通过系统调试解决结构化问题的技术代理","ja":"構造化された問題を体系的なデバッグを通じて解決する必要があるテクニカルエージェントに最適","ko":"체계적인 디버깅을 통해 구조화된 문제를 해결해야 하는 기술 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Técnicos que necesitan resolución de problemas estructurada a través de depuración sistemática","fr":"Parfait pour les agents techniques ayant besoin d''une résolution de problèmes structurée grâce à un débogage systématique","de":"Perfekt für technische Agenten, die eine strukturierte Problemlösung durch systematisches Debugging benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Técnicos que necessitam de resolução de problemas estruturada por meio de depuração sistemática","ru":"Идеально для технических агентов, которым требуется структурированное решение проблем посредством системной отладки","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الفنيين الذين بحاجة إلى حل مشكلات منظم من خلال تحديد الأعطال المنهجي"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to identify root causes of technical issues using the Iron Law of NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST, ensuring thorough investigation of test failures and bugs before proposing fixes","zh":"赋予代理识别技术问题的根因，使用没有根因调查就没有修复的铁律，确保在提出修复方案之前彻底调查测试失败和漏洞","ja":"エージェントが技術的な問題の根本原因を特定できるようにし、根本原因の調査がなければ修復はできないという鉄則を使用して、修復を提案する前にテストの失敗やバグを徹底的に調査する","ko":"에이전트가 기술적인 문제의 근본 원인을 식별할 수 있도록 하며, 근본 원인 조사가 없으면 수정이 불가능한 철칙을 사용하여 수정을 제안하기 전에 테스트 실패와 버그를 철저히 조사","es":"Habilita a los agentes a identificar las causas raíz de los problemas técnicos utilizando la Ley de Hierro de NO SOLUCIONES SIN INVESTIGACIÓN DE CAUSA RAÍZ PRIMERO, garantizando una investigación exhaustiva de los fallos de prueba y errores antes de proponer soluciones","fr":"Permet aux agents d''identifier les causes profondes des problèmes techniques en utilisant la Loi de Fer de PAS DE CORRECTIONS SANS ENQUÊTE SUR LA CAUSE PROFONDE D''ABORD, garantissant une enquête approfondie des défaillances de test et des bogues avant de proposer des correctifs","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Ursachen von technischen Problemen unter Verwendung des Eisernen Gesetzes von KEINE REPARATUREN OHNE URSACHENFORSCHUNG ERST zu identifizieren, indem sie eine gründliche Untersuchung von Testfehlern und Fehlern vor der Vorschlag von Reparaturen gewährleisten","pt":"Habilita os agentes a identificar as causas raiz dos problemas técnicos usando a Lei de Ferro de NENHUMA CORREÇÃO SEM INVESTIGAÇÃO DA CAUSA RAIZ EM PRIMEIRO LUGAR, garantindo uma investigação minuciosa das falhas de teste e bugs antes de propor correções","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выявлять коренные причины технических проблем, используя Железный закон НИКАКИХ ИСПРАВЛЕНИЙ БЕЗ РАССЛЕДОВАНИЯ КОРЕННОЙ ПРИЧИНЫ СНАЧАЛА, обеспечивая тщательное расследование неисправностей тестирования и ошибок перед предложением исправлений","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تحديد الأسباب الجذرية للمشكلات الفنية باستخدام قانون الحديد لعدم إصلاح بدون تحقيق السبب الجذري أولا، مما يضمن調査 شاملة لفشل الاختبارات والحشرات قبل اقتراح الإصلاحات"},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging complex software issues","Investigating test failures","Identifying root causes of recurring bugs"],"zh":["调试复杂的软件问题","调查测试失败","确定反复出现的错误的根因"],"ja":["複雑なソフトウェアの問題をデバッグする","テストの失敗を調査する","繰り返し発生するバグの根本原因を特定する"],"ko":["복잡한 소프트웨어 문제를 디버깅","테스트 실패를 조사","반복되는 버그의 근본 원인을 식별"],"es":["Depuración de problemas de software complejos","Investigación de fallos de prueba","Identificación de causas raíz de errores recurrentes"],"fr":["Débogage de problèmes de logiciel complexes","Enquête sur les défaillances de test","Identification des causes profondes des bogues récurrents"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung komplexer Softwareprobleme","Untersuchung von Testfehlern","Identifizierung von Ursachen für wiederkehrende Fehler"],"pt":["Depuração de problemas de software complexos","Investigação de falhas de teste","Identificação de causas raiz de bugs recorrentes"],"ru":["Отладка сложных проблем программного обеспечения","Расследование неисправностей тестирования","Выявление коренных причин повторяющихся ошибок"],"ar":["تحديد الأعطال البرمجيات المعقدة","تحقيق فشل الاختبارات","تحديد الأسباب الجذرية للحشرات المتكررة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to the core principle of finding root cause before attempting fixes","Violating the letter of the systematic debugging process is considered a violation of the spirit of debugging"],"zh":["需要遵守在尝试修复之前找到根因的核心原则","违反系统调试过程的字母被认为是违反调试的精神"],"ja":["修復を試みる前に根本原因を見つけるというコアな原則に従う必要がある","体系的なデバッグプロセスの文字を違反することはデバッグの精神を違反することとみなされる"],"ko":["수정하기 전에 근본 원인을 찾는 핵심 원칙을 준수해야 함","체계적인 디버깅 프로세스의 문자를 위반하는 것은 디버깅의 정신을 위반하는 것으로 간주"],"es":["Requiere adherencia al principio fundamental de encontrar la causa raíz antes de intentar soluciones","Violación de la letra del proceso de depuración sistemática se considera una violación del espíritu de la depuración"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion au principe fondamental de recherche de la cause profonde avant de tenter des corrections","La violation de la lettre du processus de débogage systématique est considérée comme une violation de l''esprit du débogage"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung des grundlegenden Prinzips, die Ursache vor der Fehlerbehebung zu finden","Verletzung des Buchstabens des systematischen Fehlersuchprozesses gilt als Verletzung des Geistes der Fehlersuche"],"pt":["Exige adesão ao princípio básico de encontrar a causa raiz antes de tentar correções","Violar a letra do processo de depuração sistemática é considerado uma violação do espírito da depuração"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения основного принципа нахождения коренной причины до попытки исправлений","Нарушение буквы системного процесса отладки считается нарушением духа отладки"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بالمبدأ الأساسي لإيجاد السبب الجذري قبل محاولة الإصلاحات","مخالفة حرفية عملية تحديد الأعطال المنهجي يعتبر انتهاكا لروح تحديد الأعطال"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('kriegcloud/beep-effect/domain-modeling', 'community', 'kriegcloud', 'beep-effect', 'kriegcloud/beep-effect', 'domain-modeling', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z', '2026-02-18T06:26:22.549Z', NULL, '{"id":"kriegcloud/beep-effect/domain-modeling","name":"domain-modeling","description":{"zh":"Effect领域建模技能用于创建领域模型，实体，值对象和核心业务概念","ja":"Effectドメインモデリングスキルは、ドメインモデル、エンティティ、値オブジェクト、またはコアビジネス概念を表すタイプを作成するために使用されます","ko":"Effect 도메인 모델링 스킬은 도메인 모델, 엔티티, 값 객체 및 핵심 비즈니스 개념을 생성하는 데 사용됩니다","es":"El modelado de dominio es una habilidad fundamental para crear software robusto y escalable. Nuestra habilidad de modelado de dominio te ayuda a definir y implementar modelos de dominio efectivos","fr":"La modélisation de domaine est une compétence fondamentale pour créer des logiciels robustes et évolutifs. Notre compétence en modélisation de domaine vous aide à définir et à mettre en œuvre des modèles de domaine efficaces","de":"Die Domänenmodellierung ist eine grundlegende Fähigkeit, um robuste und skalierbare Software zu erstellen. Unsere Domänenmodellierungs-Fähigkeit hilft Ihnen, effektive Domänenmodelle zu definieren und umzusetzen","pt":"O Effect Domain Modeling Skill é usado para criar modelos de domínio, entidades e objetos de valor que representam conceitos comerciais centrais.","ru":"Навык Effect Domain Modeling используется для создания моделей домена, сущностей и объектов значения, которые представляют основные бизнес-концепции.","ar":"وتستخدم مهارة نمذجة المجال Effect لإنشاء نماذج المجال والكيانات وأجسام القيمة التي تمثل المفاهيم التجارية الأساسية.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"领域建模技能 - Effect Domain Modeling","ja":"ドメインモデリングスキル - Effect Domain Modeling","ko":"도메인 모델링 스킬 - Effect Domain Modeling","es":"Modelado de Dominio Efectivo","fr":"Modélisation de Domaine Efficace","de":"Effektives Domain-Modellierung","pt":"Modelagem de Domínio de Effect","ru":"Доменное Моделирование Effect","ar":"نمذجة المجال Effect","en":"domain-modeling"},"description":{"zh":"Effect领域建模技能用于创建领域模型，实体，值对象和核心业务概念","ja":"Effectドメインモデリングスキルは、ドメインモデル、エンティティ、値オブジェクト、またはコアビジネス概念を表すタイプを作成するために使用されます","ko":"Effect 도메인 모델링 스킬은 도메인 모델, 엔티티, 값 객체 및 핵심 비즈니스 개념을 생성하는 데 사용됩니다","es":"El modelado de dominio es una habilidad fundamental para crear software robusto y escalable. Nuestra habilidad de modelado de dominio te ayuda a definir y im...","fr":"La modélisation de domaine est une compétence fondamentale pour créer des logiciels robustes et évolutifs. Notre compétence en modélisation de domaine vous a...","de":"Die Domänenmodellierung ist eine grundlegende Fähigkeit, um robuste und skalierbare Software zu erstellen. Unsere Domänenmodellierungs-Fähigkeit hilft Ihnen,...","pt":"O Effect Domain Modeling Skill é usado para criar modelos de domínio, entidades e objetos de valor que representam conceitos comerciais centrais.","ru":"Навык Effect Domain Modeling используется для создания моделей домена, сущностей и объектов значения, которые представляют основные бизнес-концепции.","ar":"وتستخدم مهارة نمذجة المجال Effect لإنشاء نماذج المجال والكيانات وأجسام القيمة التي تمثل المفاهيم التجارية الأساسية.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["自动_tag辨别器","自动Equal实现","Schema.TaggedStruct","Schema.Data","核心业务概念表示"],"ja":["自動_tag識別器","自動Equal実装","Schema.TaggedStruct","Schema.Data","コアビジネス概念表現"],"ko":["자동 태그 식별자","자동 동등성 구현","Schema.TaggedStruct","Schema.Data","핵심 비즈니스 개념 표현"],"es":["Schema.TaggedStruct para tipos de unión","Schema.Data para implementación automática de Equal","Definición de tipos y utilidades de tiempo de ejecución","Cobertura del ciclo de vida completo del modelo de dominio","Mejora de la robustez y escalabilidad del software"],"fr":["Schema.TaggedStruct pour les types d''union","Schema.Data pour la mise en œuvre automatique de Equal","Définition de types et utilitaires de temps d''exécution","Couverture du cycle de vie complet du modèle de domaine","Amélioration de la robustesse et de l''évolutivité du logiciel"],"de":["Schema.TaggedStruct für Union-Typen","Schema.Data für automatische Implementierung von Equal","Definition von Typen und Laufzeit-Utilities","Abdeckung des gesamten Lebenszyklus des Domänenmodells","Verbesserung der Robustheit und Skalierbarkeit der Software"],"pt":["Schema.TaggedStruct para tipos de união","Schema.Data para implementação automática de igualdade","Ciclo de vida completo para definição de tipos e utilitários de tempo de execução","Suporte a conceitos comerciais centrais","Integração com outras habilidades do Effect"],"ru":["Schema.TaggedStruct для объединенных типов","Schema.Data для автоматической реализации равенства","Полный цикл жизни для определения типов и утилит времени выполнения","Поддержка основных бизнес-концепций","Интеграция с другими навыками Effect"],"ar":["Schema.TaggedStruct لانواع الاتحاد","Schema.Data لتنفيذ المساواة التلقائي","دورة حياة كاملة لتعريف الأنواع وبرامج المساعدة في وقت التشغيل","دعم المفاهيم التجارية الأساسية","التكامل مع مهارات Effect الأخرى"]},"keywords":{"zh":["领域建模","Effect Domain Modeling","Schema.TaggedStruct","Schema.Data","核心业务概念","自动_tag辨别器","自动Equal实现"],"ja":["ドメインモデリング","Effectドメインモデリング","Schema.TaggedStruct","Schema.Data","コアビジネス概念","自動_tag識別器","自動Equal実装"],"ko":["도메인 모델링","Effect 도메인 모델링","Schema.TaggedStruct","Schema.Data","핵심 비즈니스 개념","자동 태그 식별자","자동 동등성 구현"],"es":["modelado de dominio","desarrollo de software","dominio efectivo","Schema.TaggedStruct","Schema.Data","tipos de unión","implementación de Equal","robustez y escalabilidad"],"fr":["modélisation de domaine","développement de logiciels","domaine efficace","Schema.TaggedStruct","Schema.Data","types d''union","mise en œuvre de Equal","robustesse et évolutivité"],"de":["Domänenmodellierung","Softwareentwicklung","effektives Domänenmodell","Schema.TaggedStruct","Schema.Data","Union-Typen","Implementierung von Equal","Robustheit und Skalierbarkeit"],"pt":["modelagem de domínio","effect domain modeling","desenvolvimento de software","conceitos comerciais","tipos de união","igualdade automática"],"ru":["доменное моделирование","effect domain modeling","разработка программного обеспечения","бизнес-концепции","объединенные типы","автоматическая реализация равенства"],"ar":["نمذجة المجال","effect domain modeling","تطوير البرمجيات","مفاهيم تجارية","انواع الاتحاد","تنفيذ المساواة التلقائي"]}},"owner":"kriegcloud","repo":"beep-effect","repoPath":"kriegcloud/beep-effect","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"domain-modeling","description":"Create production-ready Effect domain models using Schema.TaggedStruct for ADTs, Schema.Data for automatic equality, with comprehensive predicates, orders, guards, and match functions. Use when modeling domain entities, value objects, or any discriminated union types.","bodyPreview":"# Effect Domain Modeling Skill\n\nUse this skill when creating domain models, entities, value objects, or any types that represent core business concepts. This skill covers the complete lifecycle from type definition to runtime utilities.\n\n## Core Pattern: Schema.TaggedStruct + Schema.Data\n\nThe foundation of Effect domain modeling combines three key features:\n\n1. **Schema.TaggedStruct** - Automatic `_tag` discriminator for union types\n2. **Schema.Data** - Automatic `Equal` implementation for struc","body":"# Effect Domain Modeling Skill\n\nUse this skill when creating domain models, entities, value objects, or any types that represent core business concepts. This skill covers the complete lifecycle from type definition to runtime utilities.\n\n## Core Pattern: Schema.TaggedStruct + Schema.Data\n\nThe foundation of Effect domain modeling combines three key features:\n\n1. **Schema.TaggedStruct** - Automatic `_tag` discriminator for union types\n2. **Schema.Data** - Automatic `Equal` implementation for structural equality\n3. **Schema.decodeSync** - Type-safe constructors with validation\n\n```typescript\nimport { Schema, Equal } from \"effect\"\n\n// Define each variant with TaggedStruct\nexport const Pending = Schema.TaggedStruct(\"pending\", {\n  id: Schema.String,\n  createdAt: Schema.DateTimeUtcFromSelf,\n}).pipe(\n  Schema.Data, // Automatic Equal.Symbol implementation\n  Schema.annotations({\n    identifier: \"Pending\",\n    title: \"Pending Task\",\n    description: \"A task that has been created but not yet started\",\n  })\n)\n\nexport const Active = Schema.TaggedStruct(\"active\", {\n  id: Schema.String,\n  createdAt: Schema.DateTimeUtcFromSelf,\n  startedAt: Schema.DateTimeUtcFromSelf,\n}).pipe(\n  Schema.Data,\n  Schema.annotations({\n    identifier: \"Active\",\n    title: \"Active Task\",\n    description: \"A task that is currently being worked on\",\n  })\n)\n\nexport const Completed = Schema.TaggedStruct(\"completed\", {\n  id: Schema.String,\n  createdAt: Schema.DateTimeUtcFromSelf,\n  completedAt: Schema.DateTimeUtcFromSelf,\n}).pipe(\n  Schema.Data,\n  Schema.annotations({\n    identifier: \"Completed\",\n    title: \"Completed Task\",\n    description: \"A task that has been finished\",\n  })\n)\n\n// Union type\nexport const Task = Schema.Union(Pending, Active, Completed).pipe(\n  Schema.annotations({\n    identifier: \"Task\",\n    title: \"Task\",\n    description: \"A task can be pending, active, or completed\",\n  })\n)\n\nexport type Task = Schema.Schema.Type<typeof Task>\n\n// Export member types for refinements\nexport type Pending = Schema.Schema.Type<typeof Pending>\nexport type Active = Schema.Schema.Type<typeof Active>\nexport type Completed = Schema.Schema.Type<typeof Completed>\n```\n\n## Why This Pattern?\n\n**Schema.TaggedStruct Benefits:**\n- Automatically adds `_tag` discriminator (no manual `Schema.Literal`)\n- The `_tag` is applied automatically in constructors\n- Cleaner than `Schema.Struct` with manual tag fields\n- Enables exhaustive pattern matching\n\n**Schema.Data Benefits:**\n- Implements `Equal.Symbol` automatically\n- Enables `Equal.equals(a, b)` for structural equality\n- No manual equality implementation needed\n- Works correctly with nested structures\n\n**Schema.annotations Benefits:**\n- Self-documenting schemas with identifier, title, description\n- Better error messages in validation failures\n- Enables schema introspection\n\n## Mandatory Module Exports\n\nEvery domain model module MUST include:\n\n### 1. Type Definition with Schemas\n\n```typescript\nimport { Schema } from \"effect\"\n\n// Export both schema and type for each variant\nexport const Admin = Schema.TaggedStruct(\"Admin\", {\n  id: Schema.String,\n  name: Schema.String,\n  permissions: Schema.Array(Schema.String),\n}).pipe(Schema.Data)\n\nexport type Admin = Schema.Schema.Type<typeof Admin>\n\nexport const Customer = Schema.TaggedStruct(\"Customer\", {\n  id: Schema.String,\n  name: Schema.String,\n  tier: Schema.Union(\n    Schema.Literal(\"free\"),\n    Schema.Literal(\"premium\")\n  ),\n}).pipe(Schema.Data)\n\nexport type Customer = Schema.Schema.Type<typeof Customer>\n\n// Union schema\nexport const User = Schema.Union(Admin, Customer).pipe(\n  Schema.annotations({\n    identifier: \"User\",\n    title: \"User\",\n    description: \"A user can be an admin or a customer\",\n  })\n)\n\nexport type User = Schema.Schema.Type<typeof User>\n```\n\n### 2. Constructors Using Schema.decodeSync\n\n```typescript\nimport { Schema } from \"effect\"\nimport * as DateTime from \"effect/DateTime\"\n\n// Assume we have these schemas from previous section\ndeclare const Pending: Schema.Schema<any, any, never>\ndeclare const Active: Schema.Schema<any, any, never>\ndeclare const Completed: Schema.Schema<any, any, never>\n\n/**\n * Create a pending task.\n *\n * Note: _tag is automatically applied by TaggedStruct.\n *\n * @category Constructors\n * @since 0.1.0\n * @example\n * import * as Task from \"@/schemas/Task\"\n * import * as DateTime from \"effect/DateTime\"\n *\n * const task = Task.makePending({\n *   id: \"task-123\",\n *   createdAt: DateTime.unsafeNow()\n * })\n * // Result: { _tag: \"pending\", id: \"task-123\", createdAt: ... }\n *\n * // Structural equality from Schema.Data:\n * const another = Task.makePending({\n *   id: \"task-123\",\n *   createdAt: DateTime.unsafeNow()\n * })\n * Equal.equals(task, another) // true if all fields match\n */\nexport const makePending = Schema.decodeSync(Pending)\n\n/**\n * Create an active task.\n *\n * @category Constructors\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const makeActive = Schema.decodeSync(Active)\n\n/**\n * Create a completed task.\n *\n * @category Constructors\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const makeCompleted = Schema.decodeSync(Completed)\n```\n\n**Why decodeSync?**\n- `Schema.Data` returns a schema that needs decoding\n- `decodeSync` creates a validated constructor\n- Automatically applies the `_tag` discriminator\n- Throws on invalid input (use `decodeUnknownSync` for unknown data)\n\n### 3. Guards and Type Predicates\n\n```typescript\nimport { Schema } from \"effect\"\n\n// Assume Task type from previous section\ndeclare type Task =\n  | { readonly _tag: \"pending\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any }\n  | { readonly _tag: \"active\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any; readonly startedAt: any }\n  | { readonly _tag: \"completed\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any; readonly completedAt: any }\n\ndeclare type Pending = Extract<Task, { readonly _tag: \"pending\" }>\ndeclare type Active = Extract<Task, { readonly _tag: \"active\" }>\ndeclare type Completed = Extract<Task, { readonly _tag: \"completed\" }>\n\ndeclare const Task: Schema.Schema<Task, any, never>\n\n/**\n * Type guard for Task union.\n *\n * @category Guards\n * @since 0.1.0\n * @example\n * import * as Task from \"@/schemas/Task\"\n *\n * if (Task.isTask(value)) {\n *   // value is Task\n * }\n */\nexport const isTask = Schema.is(Task)\n\n/**\n * Refine to Pending variant.\n *\n * @category Guards\n * @since 0.1.0\n * @example\n * import * as Task from \"@/schemas/Task\"\n *\n * if (Task.isPending(task)) {\n *   // task is Pending, access startedAt safely\n *   console.log(task.createdAt)\n * }\n */\nexport const isPending = (self: Task): self is Pending => self._tag === \"pending\"\n\n/**\n * Refine to Active variant.\n *\n * @category Guards\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const isActive = (self: Task): self is Active => self._tag === \"active\"\n\n/**\n * Refine to Completed variant.\n *\n * @category Guards\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const isCompleted = (self: Task): self is Completed => self._tag === \"completed\"\n```\n\n### 4. Match Function (Pattern Matching)\n\n```typescript\nimport * as Match from \"effect/Match\"\n\n// Assume Task type from previous section\ndeclare type Task =\n  | { readonly _tag: \"pending\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any }\n  | { readonly _tag: \"active\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any; readonly startedAt: any }\n  | { readonly _tag: \"completed\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any; readonly completedAt: any }\n\n/**\n * Pattern match on Task using Match.typeTags.\n *\n * @category Pattern Matching\n * @since 0.1.0\n * @example\n * import * as Task from \"@/schemas/Task\"\n *\n * const status = Task.match({\n *   pending: (t) => `Pending: ${t.id}`,\n *   active: (t) => `Active since ${t.startedAt}`,\n *   completed: (t) => `Completed at ${t.completedAt}`\n * })\n *\n * const result = status(task)\n */\nexport const match = Match.typeTags<Task>()\n```\n\n**Match.typeTags Usage:**\n- Primary pattern for discriminated unions\n- Type-safe and exhaustive\n- Works with any `_tag` discriminator\n\n### 5. Equivalence (Usually Automatic via Schema.Data)\n\n```typescript\nimport { Schema } from \"effect\"\nimport * as Equal from \"effect/Equal\"\nimport * as Equivalence from \"effect/Equivalence\"\n\n// Assume Task type and schema from previous section\ndeclare type Task =\n  | { readonly _tag: \"pending\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any }\n  | { readonly _tag: \"active\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any; readonly startedAt: any }\n  | { readonly _tag: \"completed\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any; readonly completedAt: any }\n\ndeclare const Task: Schema.Schema<Task, any, never>\n\n/**\n * Primary approach: Use Equal.equals() from Schema.Data\n *\n * @example\n * import * as Equal from \"effect/Equal\"\n *\n * const task1 = Task.makePending({ ... })\n * const task2 = Task.makePending({ ... })\n *\n * // Structural equality (automatic from Schema.Data)\n * if (Equal.equals(task1, task2)) {\n *   // Tasks are structurally equal\n * }\n */\n\n/**\n * Field-based equivalence using Equivalence.mapInput\n *\n * Compare by specific fields when structural equality isn''t appropriate.\n *\n * @category Equivalence\n * @since 0.1.0\n * @example\n * import * as Task from \"@/schemas/Task\"\n *\n * // Compare by ID only\n * const areTasksSame = Task.EquivalenceById(task1, task2)\n */\nexport const EquivalenceById = Equivalence.mapInput(\n  Equivalence.string,\n  (task: Task) => task.id\n)\n```\n\n**When to Export Custom Equivalence:**\n- You need multiple comparison strategies (by ID, by group, etc.)\n- Field-based equality is semantically meaningful\n- Business logic requires custom equality checks\n\n**When NOT to Export Custom Equivalence:**\n- You only need structural equality (use `Equal.equals()` directly)\n- No custom comparison logic is needed\n\n## Conditional Module Exports\n\nInclude these when semantically appropriate:\n\n### Identity Values\n\nWhen the type has a natural \"zero\" or \"empty\" value:\n\n```typescript\n// Assume Cents and List types exist\ndeclare type Cents = bigint\ndeclare function make(value: bigint): Cents\ndeclare type List<T> = ReadonlyArray<T>\ndeclare function makeEmpty<T>(): List<T>\n\n/**\n * Zero value for monetary amounts.\n *\n * @category Identity\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const zero: Cents = make(0n)\n\n/**\n * Empty list.\n *\n * @category Identity\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const empty: List<never> = makeEmpty()\n```\n\n### Combinators\n\nFunctions that combine or transform values:\n\n```typescript\nimport { dual } from \"effect/Function\"\n\n// Assume Cents type exists\ndeclare type Cents = bigint\ndeclare function make(value: bigint): Cents\n\n/**\n * Add two monetary values.\n *\n * @category Combinators\n * @since 0.1.0\n * @example\n * import * as Cents from \"@/schemas/Cents\"\n * import { pipe } from \"effect/Function\"\n *\n * const total = pipe(price, Cents.add(tax))\n */\nexport const add: {\n  (that: Cents): (self: Cents) => Cents\n  (self: Cents, that: Cents): Cents\n} = dual(2, (self: Cents, that: Cents): Cents => make(self + that))\n\n/**\n * Get minimum of two values.\n *\n * @category Combinators\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const min = (a: Cents, b: Cents): Cents => a < b ? a : b\n\n/**\n * Get maximum of two values.\n *\n * @category Combinators\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const max = (a: Cents, b: Cents): Cents => a > b ? a : b\n```\n\n### Order Instances\n\nProvide sorting capabilities using `Order.mapInput`:\n\n```typescript\nimport * as Order from \"effect/Order\"\nimport * as DateTime from \"effect/DateTime\"\n\n// Assume Task type from previous section\ndeclare type Task =\n  | { readonly _tag: \"pending\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: DateTime.DateTime.Utc }\n  | { readonly _tag: \"active\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: DateTime.DateTime.Utc; readonly startedAt: DateTime.DateTime.Utc }\n  | { readonly _tag: \"completed\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: DateTime.DateTime.Utc; readonly completedAt: DateTime.DateTime.Utc }\n\n/**\n * Order by tag (pending < active < completed).\n *\n * Uses Order.mapInput to compose from Order.number.\n *\n * @category Orders\n * @since 0.1.0\n * @example\n * import * as Task from \"@/schemas/Task\"\n * import * as Array from \"effect/Array\"\n * import { pipe } from \"effect/Function\"\n *\n * const sorted = pipe(tasks, Array.sort(Task.OrderByTag))\n */\nexport const OrderByTag: Order.Order<Task> = Order.mapInput(\n  Order.number,\n  (task) => {\n    const priorities = { pending: 0, active: 1, completed: 2 }\n    return priorities[task._tag]\n  }\n)\n\n/**\n * Order by ID.\n *\n * @category Orders\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const OrderById: Order.Order<Task> =\n  Order.mapInput(Order.string, (task) => task.id)\n\n/**\n * Order by creation date.\n *\n * @category Orders\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const OrderByCreatedAt: Order.Order<Task> =\n  Order.mapInput(DateTime.Order, (task) => task.createdAt)\n\n/**\n * Combine multiple orders for multi-criteria sorting.\n *\n * Sorts by tag first, then by creation date.\n *\n * @category Orders\n * @since 0.1.0\n * @example\n * import * as Task from \"@/schemas/Task\"\n * import * as Array from \"effect/Array\"\n *\n * const sorted = Array.sort(tasks, Task.OrderByTagThenDate)\n */\nexport const OrderByTagThenDate: Order.Order<Task> = Order.combine(\n  OrderByTag,\n  OrderByCreatedAt\n)\n```\n\n**Key Pattern: Order.mapInput**\n- Compose orders from simpler base orders\n- Map domain type to comparable value\n- Signature: `Order.mapInput(baseOrder, (value) => extractField)`\n\n**Key Pattern: Order.combine**\n- Combine multiple orders for multi-criteria sorting\n- First order takes precedence, then second, etc.\n\n### Destructors (Getters)\n\nSafe extraction of inner values:\n\n```typescript\nimport * as DateTime from \"effect/DateTime\"\n\n// Assume Task type from previous section\ndeclare type Task =\n  | { readonly _tag: \"pending\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: DateTime.DateTime.Utc }\n  | { readonly _tag: \"active\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: DateTime.DateTime.Utc; readonly startedAt: DateTime.DateTime.Utc }\n  | { readonly _tag: \"completed\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: DateTime.DateTime.Utc; readonly completedAt: DateTime.DateTime.Utc }\n\n/**\n * Get the ID from any Task variant.\n *\n * @category Destructors\n * @since 0.1.0\n * @example\n * import * as Task from \"@/schemas/Task\"\n *\n * const id = Task.getId(task) // Works for any variant\n */\nexport const getId = (self: Task): string => self.id\n\n/**\n * Get creation date.\n *\n * @category Destructors\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const getCreatedAt = (self: Task): DateTime.DateTime.Utc =>\n  self.createdAt\n```\n\n### Setters (Immutable Updates)\n\n```typescript\nimport { dual } from \"effect/Function\"\n\n// Assume Task type from previous section\ndeclare type Task =\n  | { readonly _tag: \"pending\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any }\n  | { readonly _tag: \"active\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any; readonly startedAt: any }\n  | { readonly _tag: \"completed\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any; readonly completedAt: any }\n\n/**\n * Update a field immutably.\n *\n * @category Setters\n * @since 0.1.0\n * @example\n * import * as Task from \"@/schemas/Task\"\n * import { pipe } from \"effect/Function\"\n *\n * const updated = pipe(task, Task.setId(\"new-id\"))\n */\nexport const setId: {\n  (id: string): (self: Task) => Task\n  (self: Task, id: string): Task\n} = dual(2, (self: Task, id: string): Task => ({ ...self, id }))\n```\n\n## Advanced Patterns\n\n### Recursive Schemas with Schema.suspend\n\nUse for self-referencing types (trees, graphs, nested structures):\n\n```typescript\nimport { Schema } from \"effect\"\n\n/**\n * Recursive domain type: Category with subcategories.\n */\n\n// Separate base fields from recursive field\nconst baseFields = {\n  id: Schema.String,\n  name: Schema.String,\n}\n\n// Define the recursive type\ninterface Category extends Schema.Struct.Type<typeof baseFields> {\n  readonly subcategories: ReadonlyArray<Category>\n}\n\n// Create schema with Schema.suspend for recursion\nexport const Category = Schema.Struct({\n  ...baseFields,\n  subcategories: Schema.Array(\n    Schema.suspend((): Schema.Schema<Category> => Category)\n  ),\n}).pipe(\n  Schema.Data,\n  Schema.annotations({\n    identifier: \"Category\",\n    title: \"Category\",\n    description: \"A category that can contain nested subcategories\",\n  })\n)\n\nexport type Category = Schema.Schema.Type<typeof Category>\nexport const make = Schema.decodeSync(Category)\n\n/**\n * Example usage:\n *\n * const root = Category.make({\n *   id: \"1\",\n *   name: \"Electronics\",\n *   subcategories: [\n *     Category.make({ id: \"2\", name: \"Phones\", subcategories: [] }),\n *     Category.make({ id: \"3\", name: \"Laptops\", subcategories: [] })\n *   ]\n * })\n */\n```\n\n**Key Pattern: Schema.suspend**\n- Use for self-referencing types\n- Separate base fields for clarity\n- Define interface first, then schema with `Schema.suspend`\n\n### Branded Types\n\nFor types that need additional runtime guarantees:\n\n```typescript\nimport * as Brand from \"effect/Brand\"\nimport { Schema } from \"effect\"\n\n/**\n * Email branded type with validation.\n */\nexport type Email = Brand.Branded<string, \"Email\">\n\nexport const Email = Brand.refined<Email>(\n  (s) => /^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/.test(s),\n  (s) => Brand.error(`\"${s}\" is not a valid email`)\n)\n\n/**\n * Schema for Email serialization/deserialization.\n */\nexport const EmailSchema: Schema.BrandSchema<Email, string> =\n  Schema.String.pipe(Schema.fromBrand(Email))\n\n/**\n * @example\n * const email = Email(\"user@example.com\")\n * const decoded = Schema.decodeSync(EmailSchema)(\"user@example.com\")\n */\n```\n\n### Typeclass Instances\n\n**Only implement typeclasses that are semantically appropriate.**\n\nCheck the project''s `@/typeclass/` directory for available typeclasses:\n\n```typescript\n// Assume Schedulable typeclass exists\ndeclare namespace Schedulable$ {\n  function make<A>(\n    get: (self: A) => any,\n    set: (self: A, date: any) => A\n  ): any\n  function isScheduledBefore(instance: any): (a: any, b: any) => boolean\n  function OrderByScheduledDate(instance: any): any\n}\n\n// Assume Task type from previous section\ndeclare type Task =\n  | { readonly _tag: \"pending\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any }\n  | { readonly _tag: \"active\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any; readonly startedAt: any }\n  | { readonly _tag: \"completed\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any; readonly completedAt: any }\n\n/**\n * Schedulable instance for Task.\n *\n * @category Typeclasses\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const Schedulable = Schedulable$.make<Task>(\n  (self) => self.createdAt,\n  (self, date) => ({ ...self, createdAt: date })\n)\n\n// Re-export derived predicates\nexport const isScheduledBefore = Schedulable$.isScheduledBefore(Schedulable)\n\n// Re-export derived orders\nexport const OrderByScheduledDate = Schedulable$.OrderByScheduledDate(Schedulable)\n```\n\n**Common typeclass examples:**\n- **Schedulable**: For types with date/time properties\n- **Durable**: For types with duration properties\n- **Priceable**: For types with price properties\n- **Identifiable**: For types with ID properties\n\n## Import Patterns\n\n**CRITICAL**: Always use namespace imports:\n\n```typescript\n// CORRECT\nimport * as Task from \"@/schemas/Task\"\nimport * as DateTime from \"effect/DateTime\"\nimport * as Array from \"effect/Array\"\nimport * as Order from \"effect/Order\"\nimport * as Equal from \"effect/Equal\"\n\ndeclare const tasks: ReadonlyArray<Task.Task>\ndeclare const task1: Task.Task\ndeclare const task2: Task.Task\n\nconst task = Task.makePending({\n  id: \"123\",\n  createdAt: DateTime.unsafeNow()\n})\nconst isPending = Task.isPending(task)\nconst sorted = Array.sort(tasks, Task.OrderByTag)\nconst areEqual = Equal.equals(task1, task2)\n```\n\n**NEVER** do this:\n\n```typescript\n// WRONG - loses context, causes name clashes\nimport { makePending, isPending } from \"@/schemas/Task\"\n```\n\n**Namespace Import Benefits:**\n- Clear context for all functions\n- Prevents name clashes\n- Enables `Task.Pending`, `Task.Active` schema access\n- Natural organization: `Task.makePending`, `Task.isPending`\n\n## Temporal Data\n\nAlways use DateTime and Duration, never Date or number:\n\n```typescript\n// CORRECT\nimport { Schema } from \"effect\"\nimport * as DateTime from \"effect/DateTime\"\nimport * as Duration from \"effect/Duration\"\n\nexport const Task = Schema.TaggedStruct(\"task\", {\n  createdAt: Schema.DateTimeUtcFromSelf,  // UTC datetime\n  duration: Schema.Duration,               // Duration type\n}).pipe(Schema.Data)\n\n// WRONG\nexport const TaskBad = Schema.TaggedStruct(\"task\", {\n  createdAt: Schema.Date,        // Native Date\n  duration: Schema.Number,       // Number milliseconds\n})\n```\n\n## Immutability\n\nUse the Data module for immutable operations:\n\n```typescript\nimport { Data } from \"effect\"\n\n// Assume Task type from previous section\ndeclare type Task =\n  | { readonly _tag: \"pending\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any }\n  | { readonly _tag: \"active\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any; readonly startedAt: any }\n  | { readonly _tag: \"completed\"; readonly id: string; readonly createdAt: any; readonly completedAt: any }\n\n/**\n * Immutable update.\n *\n * @category Setters\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const updateStatus = (self: Task, newTag: Task[\"_tag\"]): Task =>\n  Data.struct({ ...self, _tag: newTag })\n```\n\n## Documentation Standards\n\nEvery exported member MUST have:\n\n- JSDoc with description\n- `@category` tag (Constructors, Guards, Pattern Matching, Orders, etc.)\n- `@since` tag (version number)\n- `@example` with fully working code including all imports\n\n```typescript\nimport { Schema } from \"effect\"\nimport * as DateTime from \"effect/DateTime\"\n\ndeclare const Pending: Schema.Schema<any, any, never>\n\n/**\n * Create a pending task.\n *\n * Note: _tag is automatically applied by TaggedStruct.\n *\n * @category Constructors\n * @since 0.1.0\n * @example\n * import * as Task from \"@/schemas/Task\"\n * import * as DateTime from \"effect/DateTime\"\n *\n * const task = Task.makePending({\n *   id: \"task-123\",\n *   createdAt: DateTime.unsafeNow()\n * })\n */\nexport const makePending = Schema.decodeSync(Pending)\n```\n\n## Quality Checklist\n\n### Mandatory - Every Domain Model\n\n- [ ] Type definition using `Schema.TaggedStruct` for each variant\n- [ ] `.pipe(Schema.Data)` for automatic `Equal` implementation\n- [ ] Schema annotations (identifier, title, description) on all schemas\n- [ ] Constructor functions using `Schema.decodeSync`\n- [ ] Type guard using `Schema.is` for union\n- [ ] Refinement predicates for each variant (e.g., `isPending`)\n- [ ] Match function using `Match.typeTags`\n- [ ] Export all union member schemas and types\n- [ ] All exports use namespace pattern (`import * as`)\n- [ ] Full JSDoc with @category, @since, @example\n- [ ] DateTime/Duration for temporal data (not Date/number)\n- [ ] Data module for immutability\n- [ ] Examples compile and run\n- [ ] Format and typecheck pass\n\n### Conditional - Include When Appropriate\n\n- [ ] Identity values (`zero`, `empty`, `unit`)\n- [ ] Combinators (`add`, `min`, `max`, `combine`)\n- [ ] Order instances using `Order.mapInput` for common sorting needs\n- [ ] `Order.combine` for multi-criteria sorting\n- [ ] Custom Equivalence via `Schema.equivalence()` or `Equivalence.mapInput`\n- [ ] Destructors (getters for common fields)\n- [ ] Setters (immutable update helpers)\n- [ ] Recursive schemas with `Schema.suspend` (for self-referencing types)\n- [ ] Branded types for validation constraints\n- [ ] Typeclass instances (check `@/typeclass/` directory first)\n- [ ] Derived predicates from typeclasses\n- [ ] Derived orders from typeclasses\n\n## Complete Example\n\n```typescript\n/**\n * User domain model demonstrating all patterns.\n *\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nimport { Schema, Equal, Match, Data } from \"effect\"\nimport * as DateTime from \"effect/DateTime\"\nimport * as Order from \"effect/Order\"\nimport * as Equivalence from \"effect/Equivalence\"\nimport { dual } from \"effect/Function\"\n\n// =============================================================================\n// Models\n// =============================================================================\n\nexport const Admin = Schema.TaggedStruct(\"Admin\", {\n  id: Schema.String,\n  name: Schema.String,\n  createdAt: Schema.DateTimeUtcFromSelf,\n  permissions: Schema.Array(Schema.String),\n}).pipe(\n  Schema.Data,\n  Schema.annotations({\n    identifier: \"Admin\",\n    title: \"Administrator\",\n    description: \"A user with administrative privileges\",\n  })\n)\n\nexport type Admin = Schema.Schema.Type<typeof Admin>\n\nexport const Customer = Schema.TaggedStruct(\"Customer\", {\n  id: Schema.String,\n  name: Schema.String,\n  createdAt: Schema.DateTimeUtcFromSelf,\n  tier: Schema.Union(Schema.Literal(\"free\"), Schema.Literal(\"premium\")),\n}).pipe(\n  Schema.Data,\n  Schema.annotations({\n    identifier: \"Customer\",\n    title: \"Customer\",\n    description: \"A customer user\",\n  })\n)\n\nexport type Customer = Schema.Schema.Type<typeof Customer>\n\nexport const User = Schema.Union(Admin, Customer).pipe(\n  Schema.annotations({\n    identifier: \"User\",\n    title: \"User\",\n    description: \"A user can be an admin or a customer\",\n  })\n)\n\nexport type User = Schema.Schema.Type<typeof User>\n\n// =============================================================================\n// Constructors\n// =============================================================================\n\n/**\n * Create an admin user.\n *\n * @category Constructors\n * @since 0.1.0\n * @example\n * import * as User from \"@/schemas/User\"\n * import * as DateTime from \"effect/DateTime\"\n *\n * const admin = User.makeAdmin({\n *   id: \"admin-1\",\n *   name: \"Alice\",\n *   createdAt: DateTime.unsafeNow(),\n *   permissions: [\"read\", \"write\"]\n * })\n */\nexport const makeAdmin = Schema.decodeSync(Admin)\n\n/**\n * Create a customer user.\n *\n * @category Constructors\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const makeCustomer = Schema.decodeSync(Customer)\n\n// =============================================================================\n// Guards\n// =============================================================================\n\n/**\n * Type guard for User.\n *\n * @category Guards\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const isUser = Schema.is(User)\n\n/**\n * Refine to Admin.\n *\n * @category Guards\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const isAdmin = (self: User): self is Admin => self._tag === \"Admin\"\n\n/**\n * Refine to Customer.\n *\n * @category Guards\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const isCustomer = (self: User): self is Customer => self._tag === \"Customer\"\n\n// =============================================================================\n// Pattern Matching\n// =============================================================================\n\n/**\n * Pattern match on User.\n *\n * @category Pattern Matching\n * @since 0.1.0\n * @example\n * import * as User from \"@/schemas/User\"\n *\n * const greeting = User.match({\n *   Admin: (u) => `Hello Admin ${u.name}`,\n *   Customer: (u) => `Hello ${u.tier} customer ${u.name}`\n * })\n *\n * const message = greeting(user)\n */\nexport const match = Match.typeTags<User>()\n\n// =============================================================================\n// Equivalence\n// =============================================================================\n\n/**\n * Compare users by ID only.\n *\n * @category Equivalence\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const EquivalenceById = Equivalence.mapInput(\n  Equivalence.string,\n  (user: User) => user.id\n)\n\n// =============================================================================\n// Orders\n// =============================================================================\n\n/**\n * Order by name.\n *\n * @category Orders\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const OrderByName: Order.Order<User> =\n  Order.mapInput(Order.string, (user) => user.name)\n\n/**\n * Order by creation date.\n *\n * @category Orders\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const OrderByCreatedAt: Order.Order<User> =\n  Order.mapInput(DateTime.Order, (user) => user.createdAt)\n\n/**\n * Order by tag (Admin < Customer).\n *\n * @category Orders\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const OrderByTag: Order.Order<User> = Order.mapInput(\n  Order.number,\n  (user) => (user._tag === \"Admin\" ? 0 : 1)\n)\n\n// =============================================================================\n// Destructors\n// =============================================================================\n\n/**\n * Get user ID.\n *\n * @category Destructors\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const getId = (self: User): string => self.id\n\n/**\n * Get user name.\n *\n * @category Destructors\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const getName = (self: User): string => self.name\n\n/**\n * Get creation date.\n *\n * @category Destructors\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const getCreatedAt = (self: User): DateTime.DateTime.Utc => self.createdAt\n\n// =============================================================================\n// Setters\n// =============================================================================\n\n/**\n * Update user name immutably.\n *\n * @category Setters\n * @since 0.1.0\n */\nexport const setName: {\n  (name: string): (self: User) => User\n  (self: User, name: string): User\n} = dual(2, (self: User, name: string): User => ({ ...self, name }))\n```\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Creating domain entities (User, Product, Order)\n- Modeling value objects (Email, Money, Address)\n- Defining discriminated unions (states, events, commands)\n- Implementing ADTs (algebraic data types)\n- Building type-safe domain models with validation\n- Ensuring structural equality with automatic Equal\n- Creating self-documenting schemas\n\n## Key Principles Summary\n\n1. **Schema.TaggedStruct** - Use for all tagged union variants\n2. **Schema.Data** - Apply for automatic Equal implementation\n3. **Schema.decodeSync** - Create type-safe constructors\n4. **Schema.annotations** - Document all schemas\n5. **Order.mapInput** - Compose orders from base orders\n6. **Match.typeTags** - Pattern match on discriminated unions\n7. **Schema.suspend** - Handle recursive types\n8. **Namespace imports** - Always use `import * as`\n9. **DateTime/Duration** - Never use Date/number for temporal data\n10. **Equal.equals()** - Primary equality check (from Schema.Data)\n\nYour domain models should be production-ready, type-safe, and provide excellent developer experience.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:26:22.549Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Type-Definition Agents requiring advanced domain modeling capabilities with automatic discriminator and Equal implementation","zh":"适用于需要高级域模型能力的类型定义代理，包括自动鉴别器和相等实现","ja":"高度なドメインモデリング機能を必要とするType-Definitionエージェントに適しています。自動判別器とEqual実装が含まれます","ko":"고급 도메인 모델링 기능이 필요한 유형 정의 에이전트에 적합합니다. 자동 판별기 및 동등한 구현이 포함됩니다","es":"Ideal para agentes de definición de tipo que requieren capacidades de modelado de dominio avanzadas con discriminador automático y implementación de igualdad","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de définition de type nécessitant des capacités de modélisation de domaine avancées avec un discriminateur automatique et une implémentation d''égalité","de":"Ideal für Type-Definition-Agents, die erweiterte Domänenmodellierungs-Funktionen mit automatischem Diskriminanz und Gleichheitsimplementierung erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Definição de Tipo que requerem capacidades avançadas de modelagem de domínio com discriminador automático e implementação Equal","ru":"Идеально для агентов определения типа, требующих продвинутых возможностей моделирования области с автоматическим дискриминатором и реализацией Equal","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تعريف النوع التي تتطلبقدرات متقدمة في نمذجة النطاق مع تمييز التمييز التلقائي وتنفيذ المساواة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create robust domain models using Schema.TaggedStruct and Schema.Data, enabling automatic _tag discrimination for union types and Equal implementation for structs, streamlining the development of core business concepts","zh":"赋予代理创建强大的域模型的能力，使用Schema.TaggedStruct和Schema.Data，实现联合类型的自动标签判别和结构的Equal实现，从而简化核心业务概念的开发","ja":"エージェントに強力なドメインモデルを作成する能力を与え、Schema.TaggedStructとSchema.Dataを使用して、共用体型の自動タグ判別と構造体のEqual実装を可能にし、コアビジネス概念の開発を合理化する","ko":"에이전트가 강력한 도메인 모델을 만들 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 Schema.TaggedStruct 및 Schema.Data를 사용하여 유니온 유형의 자동 태그 판별 및 구조체의 동등한 구현을 가능하게 하여 핵심 비즈니스 개념의 개발을 간소화합니다","es":"Permite a los agentes crear modelos de dominio robustos utilizando Schema.TaggedStruct y Schema.Data, lo que permite la discriminación automática de etiquetas para los tipos de unión y la implementación de igualdad para estructuras, lo que simplifica el desarrollo de conceptos comerciales básicos","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des modèles de domaine robustes en utilisant Schema.TaggedStruct et Schema.Data, ce qui permet la discrimination automatique des balises pour les types d''union et l''implémentation d''égalité pour les structures, ce qui simplifie le développement des concepts commerciaux de base","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, robuste Domänenmodelle mit Schema.TaggedStruct und Schema.Data zu erstellen, wodurch die automatische Tag-Diskriminierung für Union-Typen und die Gleichheitsimplementierung für Strukturen ermöglicht wird, was die Entwicklung von Kerngeschäftskonzepten vereinfacht","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar modelos de domínio robustos usando Schema.TaggedStruct e Schema.Data, permitindo a discriminação automática de tags para tipos de união e implementação de Equal para structs, simplificando o desenvolvimento de conceitos comerciais centrais","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать прочные модели области с помощью Schema.TaggedStruct и Schema.Data, обеспечивая автоматическое различие тегов для объединенных типов и реализацию Equal для структур, упрощая разработку основных бизнес-концепций","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إنشاء نماذج نطاق متينة باستخدام Schema.TaggedStruct و Schema.Data، وتمكين التمييز التلقائي للعلامات لانواع الاتحاد وتنفيذ المساواة للهياكل، وبذلك يُبسّط تطوير المفاهيم التجارية الأساسية"},"useCases":{"en":["Defining entity relationships with automatic _tag discriminators","Generating Equal implementations for complex data structures","Creating runtime utilities for domain models with Schema.Data"],"zh":["使用自动标签判别器定义实体关系","为复杂数据结构生成Equal实现","使用Schema.Data为域模型创建运行时实用程序"],"ja":["自動タグ判別器を使用してエンティティ関係を定義する","複雑なデータ構造用のEqual実装を生成する","Schema.Dataを使用してドメインモデル用のランタイムユーティリティを作成する"],"ko":["자동 태그 판별기를 사용하여 엔터티 관계를 정의합니다","복잡한 데이터 구조에 대한 동등한 구현을 생성합니다","Schema.Data를 사용하여 도메인 모델에 대한 런타임 유틸리티를 생성합니다"],"es":["Definir relaciones de entidad con discriminadores de etiquetas automáticos","Generar implementaciones de igualdad para estructuras de datos complejas","Crear utilidades de tiempo de ejecución para modelos de dominio con Schema.Data"],"fr":["Définir les relations d''entité avec des discriminateurs de balises automatiques","Générer des implémentations d''égalité pour des structures de données complexes","Créer des utilitaires de runtime pour les modèles de domaine avec Schema.Data"],"de":["Entitätsbeziehungen mit automatischen Tag-Diskriminatoren definieren","Gleichheitsimplementierungen für komplexe Datenstrukturen generieren","Laufzeit-Utilities für Domänenmodelle mit Schema.Data erstellen"],"pt":["Definir relacionamentos de entidades com discriminadores de tag automáticos","Gerar implementações de Equal para estruturas de dados complexas","Criar utilitários de tempo de execução para modelos de domínio com Schema.Data"],"ru":["Определение отношений сущностей с автоматическим дискриминатором тегов","Генерация реализаций Equal для сложных структур данных","Создание утилит времени выполнения для моделей области с Schema.Data"],"ar":["تحديد علاقات الكيانات مع تمييز العلامات التلقائي","إنتاج تنفيذات المساواة للتعقيدات الهيكلية للمعلومات","creating أدوات وقت التشغيل لنماذج النطاق مع Schema.Data"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Schema.TaggedStruct and Schema.Data patterns","Limited to domain modeling use cases"],"zh":["需要理解Schema.TaggedStruct和Schema.Data模式","仅限域模型用例"],"ja":["Schema.TaggedStructとSchema.Dataのパターンを理解する必要がある","ドメインモデリングのユースケースに限定される"],"ko":["Schema.TaggedStruct 및 Schema.Data 패턴을 이해해야 함","도메인 모델링 사용 사례에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los patrones Schema.TaggedStruct y Schema.Data","Limitado a casos de uso de modelado de dominio"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des modèles Schema.TaggedStruct et Schema.Data","Limité aux cas d''utilisation de modélisation de domaine"],"de":["Erfordert das Verständnis der Muster Schema.TaggedStruct und Schema.Data","Begrenzt auf Domänenmodellierungs-Anwendungsfälle"],"pt":["Exige compreensão dos padrões Schema.TaggedStruct e Schema.Data","Limitado a casos de uso de modelagem de domínio"],"ru":["Требует понимания шаблонов Schema.TaggedStruct и Schema.Data","Ограничен случаи использования моделирования области"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم أنماط Schema.TaggedStruct و Schema.Data","محدود لاستخدامات نمذجة النطاق"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Pauli-Group/Hegemon/hegemon-testnet-join', 'community', 'Pauli-Group', 'Hegemon', 'Pauli-Group/Hegemon', 'hegemon-testnet-join', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z', '2026-02-18T06:27:06.604Z', NULL, '{"id":"Pauli-Group/Hegemon/hegemon-testnet-join","name":"hegemon-testnet-join","description":{"zh":"Hegemon测试网是一个量子抗性和私有的区块链，用于连接新节点和挖矿","ja":"Hegemonテストネットは量子耐性とプライベートなブロックチェーンで、新しいノードを接続し、マイニングを行うために使用されます","ko":"헤게몬 테스트넷은 양자 저항과 프라이빗한 블록체인으로 새로운 노드를 연결하고 채굴을 수행하는 데 사용됩니다","es":"Hegemon testnet es una blockchain resistente a cuánticos y privada. Conecta un nuevo nodo y verifica la cadena canónica","fr":"Hegemon testnet est une blockchain résistante aux quantiques et privée. Connectez un nouveau nœud et vérifiez la chaîne canonique","de":"Hegemon Testnet ist eine quantenresistente und private Blockchain. Verbinden Sie einen neuen Knoten und überprüfen Sie die kanonische Kette","pt":"A Hegemon Testnet é uma blockchain resistente ao quantum e privada, permitindo a conexão de novos nós e a verificação da cadeia canônica","ru":"Hegemon Testnet — это квантово-устойчивая и частная блокчейн-сеть, которая позволяет подключать новые ноды и проверять каноническую цепочку","ar":"Hegemon Testnet هي شبكة بلوكشين مقاومة للكميات وخاصة، تسمح بالاتصال بنقاط جديدة والتحقق من السلسلة المعتمدة","en":"Quantum resistant and private blockchain"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"加入Hegemon测试网 - 量子抗性私有区块链","ja":"Hegemonテストネットに接続 - 量子耐性のプライベートブロックチェーン","ko":"헤게몬 테스트넷에 연결 - 양자 저항 프라이빗 블록체인","es":"Únete a Hegemon Testnet: blockchain resistente a cuánticos","fr":"Rejoindre Hegemon Testnet: blockchain résistant aux quant...","de":"Hegemon Testnet beitreten: quantenresistente Blockchain","pt":"Conecte-se à Hegemon Testnet","ru":"Присоединяйтесь к Hegemon Testnet","ar":"انضم إلى Hegemon Testnet","en":"hegemon-testnet-join"},"description":{"zh":"Hegemon测试网是一个量子抗性和私有的区块链，用于连接新节点和挖矿","ja":"Hegemonテストネットは量子耐性とプライベートなブロックチェーンで、新しいノードを接続し、マイニングを行うために使用されます","ko":"헤게몬 테스트넷은 양자 저항과 프라이빗한 블록체인으로 새로운 노드를 연결하고 채굴을 수행하는 데 사용됩니다","es":"Hegemon testnet es una blockchain resistente a cuánticos y privada. Conecta un nuevo nodo y verifica la cadena canónica","fr":"Hegemon testnet est une blockchain résistante aux quantiques et privée. Connectez un nouveau nœud et vérifiez la chaîne canonique","de":"Hegemon Testnet ist eine quantenresistente und private Blockchain. Verbinden Sie einen neuen Knoten und überprüfen Sie die kanonische Kette","pt":"A Hegemon Testnet é uma blockchain resistente ao quantum e privada, permitindo a conexão de novos nós e a verificação da cadeia canônica","ru":"Hegemon Testnet — это квантово-устойчивая и частная блокчейн-сеть, которая позволяет подключать новые ноды и проверять каноническую цепочку","ar":"Hegemon Testnet هي شبكة بلوكشين مقاومة للكميات وخاصة، تسمح بالاتصال بنقاط جديدة والتحقق من السلسلة المعتمدة","en":"Quantum resistant and private blockchain"},"definition":{"en":"Quantum resistant and private blockchain"},"features":{"zh":["量子抗性","私有区块链","新节点连接","规范链验证","同步完成后挖矿"],"ja":["量子耐性","プライベートブロックチェーン","新しいノードの接続","規範チェーンの検証","同期完了後のマイニング"],"ko":["양자 저항","프라이빗 블록체인","새로운 노드 연결","규범 체인 검증","동기화 완료 후 채굴"],"es":["Blockchain resistente a cuánticos","Privacidad garantizada","Conexión de nuevos nodos","Verificación de la cadena canónica","Minado seguro después de la sincronización","Configuración personalizable"],"fr":["Blockchain résistante aux quantiques","Confidentialité garantie","Connexion de nouveaux nœuds","Vérification de la chaîne canonique","Minage sécurisé après synchronisation","Configuration personnalisable"],"de":["Quantenresistente Blockchain","Garantierte Privatsphäre","Verbindung neuer Knoten","Überprüfung der kanonischen Kette","Sicheres Mining nach Synchronisation","Anpassbare Konfiguration"],"pt":["Blockchain resistente ao quantum","Conexão de novos nós","Verificação da cadeia canônica","Mineração após sincronização","Configuração personalizada","Suporte a RPC e P2P"],"ru":["Квантово-устойчивая блокчейн-сеть","Подключение новых нод","Проверка канонической цепочки","Майнинг после синхронизации","Настройка по умолчанию","Поддержка RPC и P2P"],"ar":["بلوكشين مقاوم للكميات","الاتصال بنقاط جديدة","التحقق من السلسلة المعتمدة","التعدين بعد الانتهاء من التزامن","الإعدادات المخصصة","دعم RPC و P2P"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Hegemon测试网","量子抗性","私有区块链","区块链开发","节点连接","挖矿"],"ja":["Hegemonテストネット","量子耐性","プライベートブロックチェーン","ブロックチェーン開発","ノード接続","マイニング"],"ko":["헤게몬 테스트넷","양자 저항","프라이빗 블록체인","블록체인 개발","노드 연결","채굴"],"es":["Hegemon testnet","blockchain resistente a cuánticos","privacidad en blockchain","conexión de nodos","verificación de cadena canónica","minado seguro","desarrollo de blockchain","quantum resistant blockchain"],"fr":["Hegemon testnet","blockchain résistante aux quantiques","confidentialité dans la blockchain","connexion de nœuds","vérification de chaîne canonique","minage sécurisé","développement de blockchain","blockchain résistante aux quantiques"],"de":["Hegemon Testnet","quantenresistente Blockchain","Privatsphäre in der Blockchain","Verbindung von Knoten","Überprüfung der kanonischen Kette","sicheres Mining","Blockchain-Entwicklung","quantenresistente Blockchain"],"pt":["Hegemon Testnet","Blockchain resistente ao quantum","Conexão de nós","Verificação da cadeia canônica","Mineração de blockchain","Desenvolvimento de blockchain","Blockchain privada","Resistência ao quantum"],"ru":["Hegemon Testnet","Квантово-устойчивая блокчейн-сеть","Подключение нод","Проверка канонической цепочки","Майнинг блокчейн","Разработка блокчейн","Частная блокчейн-сеть","Устойчивость к квантовым атакам"],"ar":["Hegemon Testnet","بلوكشين مقاوم للكميات","الاتصال بنقاط","التحقق من السلسلة المعتمدة","التعدين البلوكشين","تطوير البلوكشين","بلوكشين خاصة","مقاومة الكميات"]}},"owner":"Pauli-Group","repo":"Hegemon","repoPath":"Pauli-Group/Hegemon","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"hegemon-testnet-join","description":"Join the Hegemon testnet using the shared chainspec, verify genesis, sync to the tip, and enable mining safely.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"# Goal\nConnect a new node to the Hegemon testnet, verify it is on the canonical chain, and mine only after sync completes.\n\n# Defaults\n- Boot node: hegemon.pauli.group:30333\n- Chain spec: config/dev-chainspec.json\n- Genesis hash: 0xcaa718106d1530705c53a99628d929cd78d47a0bf06b177aa4853962b47c637d\n- RPC port: 9944\n- P2P listen: /ip4/0.0.0.0/tcp/30333\n\n# Steps\n1. Ensure binaries exist (fresh clones must run make setup and make node):\n   - make setup\n   - make node\n   - cargo build --release -p wall","body":"# Goal\nConnect a new node to the Hegemon testnet, verify it is on the canonical chain, and mine only after sync completes.\n\n# Defaults\n- Boot node: hegemon.pauli.group:30333\n- Chain spec: config/dev-chainspec.json\n- Genesis hash: 0xcaa718106d1530705c53a99628d929cd78d47a0bf06b177aa4853962b47c637d\n- RPC port: 9944\n- P2P listen: /ip4/0.0.0.0/tcp/30333\n\n# Steps\n1. Ensure binaries exist (fresh clones must run make setup and make node):\n   - make setup\n   - make node\n   - cargo build --release -p walletd\n2. Verify the shared chainspec matches the boot node. Do not use --chain dev.\n   - shasum -a 256 config/dev-chainspec.json\n3. Create or open a wallet and export the shielded mining address:\n   - export HEGEMON_MINER_ADDRESS=$(printf ''%s\\n{\"id\":1,\"method\":\"status.get\",\"params\":{}}\\n'' \"YOUR_PASSPHRASE\" \\\n     | ./target/release/walletd --store ~/.hegemon-wallet --mode open \\\n     | jq -r ''.result.primaryAddress'')\n4. Start the node with the shared chainspec and seed:\n   - HEGEMON_MINE=1 \\\n     HEGEMON_SEEDS=\"hegemon.pauli.group:30333\" \\\n     HEGEMON_MINER_ADDRESS=\"$HEGEMON_MINER_ADDRESS\" \\\n     ./target/release/hegemon-node \\\n       --dev \\\n       --base-path ~/.hegemon-node \\\n       --chain config/dev-chainspec.json \\\n       --listen-addr /ip4/0.0.0.0/tcp/30333 \\\n       --rpc-port 9944 \\\n       --rpc-external \\\n       --rpc-methods safe \\\n       --name \"TestnetNode\"\n5. Monitor sync status and height. Mining pauses while syncing and resumes once caught up.\n   - curl -s -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d ''{\"id\":1,\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"method\":\"system_health\"}'' \\\n     http://127.0.0.1:9944 | jq\n   - curl -s -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d ''{\"id\":1,\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"method\":\"hegemon_consensusStatus\"}'' \\\n     http://127.0.0.1:9944 | jq\n   - curl -s -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d ''{\"id\":1,\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"method\":\"chain_getHeader\"}'' \\\n     http://127.0.0.1:9944 | jq\n6. If height stalls, check peers and genesis hash:\n   - curl -s -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d ''{\"id\":1,\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"method\":\"chain_getBlockHash\",\"params\":[0]}'' \\\n     http://127.0.0.1:9944 | jq\n\n# Notes\n- If the genesis hash or chainspec differ, stop the node and wipe the base path before restarting.\n- Keep RPC access locked down if you expose it beyond localhost.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:27:06.604Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Blockchain Agents requiring secure and private testnet integration with Quantum-resistant capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要安全且私有的区块链测试网络集成和抗量子能力的区块链代理。","ja":"ブロックチェーンエージェントが安全でプライベートなテストネットワーク統合と量子耐性機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"보안 및 사적인 블록체인 테스트 네트워크 통합 및 양자 저항 기능이 필요한 블록체인 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Blockchain que requieren una integración de testnet segura y privada con capacidades resistentes a Quantum.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de blockchain nécessitant une intégration de testnet sécurisée et privée avec des capacités résistantes au Quantum.","de":"Ideal für Blockchain-Agenten, die eine sichere und private Testnet-Integration mit quantenresistenten Fähigkeiten erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Blockchain que exigem integração de testnet segura e privada com capacidades resistentes a Quantum.","ru":"Идеально для агентов блокчейна, требующих безопасной и частной интеграции тестовой сети с квантово-устойчивыми возможностями.","ar":"مثالي لعميل بلوكشين الذي يتطلب تكامل شبكة اختبار آمن وخاص مع قدرات مقاومة للكمون."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to connect nodes to the Hegemon testnet, utilizing a canonical chain and mining after sync completion, via protocols such as RPC and P2P, with specific configurations like chain spec and genesis hash.","zh":"使代理能够连接节点到Hegemon测试网络，利用规范链和同步完成后的挖矿，通过诸如RPC和P2P的协议，以特定的配置，如链规格和创世区块哈希。","ja":"Hegemonテストネットワークにノードを接続し、同期完了後のマイニングを実行するエージェントを可能にします。RPCやP2Pなどのプロトコルを使用し、チェーン仕様やジェネシスハッシュなどの特定の設定で、規範チェーンを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 헤게몬 테스트 네트워크에 노드를 연결하고 동기화 완료 후 마이닝을 수행할 수 있도록 합니다. RPC 및 P2P와 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 체인 규격 및 생성기 해시와 같은 특정 구성으로 규범 체인을 활용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes conectar nodos a la testnet de Hegemon, utilizando una cadena canónica y minería después de la finalización de la sincronización, a través de protocolos como RPC y P2P, con configuraciones específicas como especificación de cadena y hash de génesis.","fr":"Permet aux agents de se connecter aux nœuds de la testnet Hegemon, en utilisant une chaîne canonique et une extraction après l''achèvement de la synchronisation, via des protocoles tels que RPC et P2P, avec des configurations spécifiques comme spécification de chaîne et hachage de génèse.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Knoten mit der Hegemon-Testnet zu verbinden, indem sie eine kanonische Kette und Bergbau nach Abschluss der Synchronisierung verwenden, über Protokolle wie RPC und P2P, mit spezifischen Konfigurationen wie Chain-Spezifikation und Genesis-Hash.","pt":"Permite que os agentes conectem nós à rede de teste Hegemon, utilizando uma cadeia canônica e mineração após a conclusão da sincronização, por meio de protocolos como RPC e P2P, com configurações específicas como especificação de cadeia e hash de gênese.","ru":"Позволяет агентам подключать узлы к тестовой сети Hegemon, используя каноническую цепь и майнинг после завершения синхронизации, через протоколы такие как RPC и P2P, с конкретными конфигурациями как спецификация цепи и хеш генезиса.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من kết nối العقد إلى شبكة اختبار هيجيمون، باستخدام سلسلة معيارية وتعدين بعد إكمال التزامن، من خلال بروتوكولات مثل RPC و P2P، مع تكوينات محددة مثل مواصفات السلسلة وهاش الجينيس."},"useCases":{"en":["Connecting new nodes to the Hegemon testnet for expanded network capabilities","Verifying node synchronization with the canonical chain for data consistency","Mining on the testnet after successful node setup and sync for blockchain development"],"zh":["将新节点连接到Hegemon测试网络以扩展网络功能","验证节点与规范链的同步以确保数据一致性","在成功设置和同步节点后，在测试网络上进行挖矿以进行区块链开发"],"ja":["ヘゲモンテストネットワークに新しいノードを接続してネットワーク機能を拡張する","ノードの同期を規範チェーンで検証してデータの一貫性を確保する","ノードのセットアップと同期に成功した後、ブロックチェーン開発のためにテストネットワークでマイニングを行う"],"ko":["헤게몬 테스트 네트워크에 새로운 노드를 연결하여 네트워크 기능을 확장하는 것","노드가 규범 체인과 동기화되는 것을 검증하여 데이터 일관성을 보장하는 것","노드 설정 및 동기화에 성공한 후 블록체인 개발을 위해 테스트 네트워크에서 마이닝을 수행하는 것"],"es":["Conectar nuevos nodos a la testnet de Hegemon para ampliar las capacidades de la red","Verificar la sincronización del nodo con la cadena canónica para la coherencia de los datos","Minar en la testnet después de la configuración y sincronización del nodo exitoso para el desarrollo de blockchain"],"fr":["Se connecter à de nouveaux nœuds de la testnet Hegemon pour étendre les capacités du réseau","Vérifier la synchronisation du nœud avec la chaîne canonique pour la cohérence des données","Extraire de la testnet après la configuration et la synchronisation du nœud réussie pour le développement de blockchain"],"de":["Neue Knoten mit der Hegemon-Testnet verbinden, um die Netzwerkkapazitäten zu erweitern","Überprüfen der Knotensynchronisierung mit der kanonischen Kette für die Datenkonsistenz","Im Testnet abbauen, nachdem das Knoten-Setup und die Synchronisierung erfolgreich waren, für die Blockchain-Entwicklung"],"pt":["Conectar novos nós à rede de teste Hegemon para capacidades de rede expandidas","Verificar a sincronização do nó com a cadeia canônica para consistência de dados","Minerar na rede de teste após a configuração e sincronização bem-sucedida do nó para desenvolvimento de blockchain"],"ru":["Подключение новых узлов к тестовой сети Hegemon для расширенных возможностей сети","Проверка синхронизации узла с канонической цепью для согласованности данных","Майнинг в тестовой сети после успешной настройки и синхронизации узла для разработки блокчейна"],"ar":[" kết nối العقد الجديدة إلى شبكة اختبار هيجيمون لتحسين إمكانيات الشبكة","التحقق من مزامنة العقد مع السلسلة المعيارية لاتساق البيانات","التعدين في شبكة الاختبار بعد إعداد وتزامن العقد بنجاح لتطوير بلوكشين"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires binaries setup via make setup and make node","Dependent on specific chain spec and genesis hash configurations","Limited to Hegemon testnet environment"],"zh":["需要通过make setup和make node设置二进制文件","依赖于特定的链规格和创世区块哈希配置","仅限于Hegemon测试网络环境"],"ja":["make setupとmake nodeを使用してバイナリファイルをセットアップする必要がある","特定のチェーン仕様とジェネシスハッシュの設定に依存している","ヘゲモンテストネットワーク環境のみに制限される"],"ko":["make setup 및 make node를 사용하여 바이너리 파일을 설정해야 함","특정 체인 규격 및 생성기 해시 구성에 의존","헤게몬 테스트 네트워크 환경만으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere configuración de binarios a través de make setup y make node","Dependiente de configuraciones específicas de especificación de cadena y hash de génesis","Limitado al entorno de testnet de Hegemon"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de binaires via make setup et make node","Dépendant de configurations spécifiques de spécification de chaîne et de hachage de génèse","Limité à l''environnement de testnet Hegemon"],"de":["Benötigt Binär-Setup über make setup und make node","Abhängig von spezifischen Konfigurationen von Chain-Spezifikation und Genesis-Hash","Begrenzt auf die Hegemon-Testnet-Umgebung"],"pt":["Exige configuração de binários via make setup e make node","Dependente de configurações específicas de especificação de cadeia e hash de gênese","Limitado ao ambiente de rede de teste Hegemon"],"ru":["Требует настройки бинарных файлов через make setup и make node","Зависит от конкретных конфигураций спецификации цепи и хеша генезиса","Ограничен средой тестовой сети Hegemon"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد ثنائيات عبر make setup و make node","يعتمد على تكوينات محددة لمواصفات السلسلة وهاش الجينيس","محدود بيئة شبكة اختبار هيجيمون"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('CongDon1207/AGENTS.md/research', 'community', 'CongDon1207', 'AGENTS.md', 'CongDon1207/AGENTS.md', 'research', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z', '2026-02-18T06:27:47.828Z', NULL, '{"id":"CongDon1207/AGENTS.md/research","name":"research","description":{"zh":"研究技能是一种系统化的信息收集方法，遵循YAGNI、KISS、DRY原则","ja":"研究スキルは、YAGNI、KISS、DRY原則に基づいた体系的な情報収集方法です","ko":"연구 스킬은 YAGNI, KISS, DRY 원칙을 따르는 체계적인 정보 수집 방법입니다","es":"Nuestra guía de investigación te muestra cómo definir el alcance, evaluar fuentes y establecer criterios de evaluación","fr":"Notre guide de recherche vous montre comment définir la portée, évaluer les sources et établir des critères d''évaluation","de":"Unser Forschungsleitfaden zeigt Ihnen, wie Sie den Umfang definieren, Quellen bewerten und Bewertungskriterien festlegen","en":"Copy .* folder and AGENTS.md then paste  /root of project "},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"研究技能：系统化信息收集","ja":"研究スキル：体系的な情報収集","ko":"연구 스킬: 체계적인 정보 수집","es":"Investigación Efectiva","fr":"Recherche Éfficace","de":"Effektive Recherche","en":"research"},"description":{"zh":"研究技能是一种系统化的信息收集方法，遵循YAGNI、KISS、DRY原则","ja":"研究スキルは、YAGNI、KISS、DRY原則に基づいた体系的な情報収集方法です","ko":"연구 스킬은 YAGNI, KISS, DRY 원칙을 따르는 체계적인 정보 수집 방법입니다","es":"Nuestra guía de investigación te muestra cómo definir el alcance, evaluar fuentes y establecer criterios de evaluación","fr":"Notre guide de recherche vous montre comment définir la portée, évaluer les sources et établir des critères d''évaluation","de":"Unser Forschungsleitfaden zeigt Ihnen, wie Sie den Umfang definieren, Quellen bewerten und Bewertungskriterien festlegen","en":"Copy .* folder and AGENTS.md then paste  /root of project "},"definition":{"en":"Copy .* folder and AGENTS.md then paste  /root of project "},"features":{"zh":["遵循YAGNI、KISS、DRY原则","系统化的信息收集方法","清晰定义研究范围","确定评估标准","设定信息深度边界"],"ja":["YAGNI、KISS、DRY原則に基づく","体系的な情報収集方法","研究範囲の明確な定義","評価基準の決定","情報の深度の境界の設定"],"ko":["YAGNI, KISS, DRY 원칙 준수","체계적인 정보 수집 방법","연구 범위의 명확한 정의","평가 기준의 결정","정보의 깊이 경계 설정"],"es":["Definición del alcance de la investigación","Evaluación de fuentes y establecimiento de criterios","Aplicación de principios YAGNI, KISS y DRY","Enfoque en la honestidad, la brutalidad y la concisión","Focalización en la recencia y la profundidad de la investigación"],"fr":["Définition de la portée de la recherche","Évaluation des sources et établissement de critères","Application des principes YAGNI, KISS et DRY","Accent sur l''honnêteté, la brutalité et la concision","Focalisation sur la récence et la profondeur de la recherche"],"de":["Definition des Forschungsumfangs","Bewertung von Quellen und Festlegung von Kriterien","Anwendung der Prinzipien YAGNI, KISS und DRY","Fokus auf Ehrlichkeit, Brutalität und Prägnanz","Fokussierung auf die Aktualität und Tiefe der Forschung"]},"keywords":{"zh":["研究技能","系统化信息收集","YAGNI","KISS","DRY","开发效率","信息评估"],"ja":["研究スキル","体系的な情報収集","YAGNI","KISS","DRY","開発効率","情報評価"],"ko":["연구 스킬","체계적인 정보 수집","YAGNI","KISS","DRY","개발 효율성","정보 평가"],"es":["investigación efectiva","definición del alcance","evaluación de fuentes","YAGNI","KISS","DRY","recencia","profundidad","honestidad","brutalidad"],"fr":["recherche efficace","définition de la portée","évaluation des sources","YAGNI","KISS","DRY","récence","profondeur","honnêteté","brutalité"],"de":["effektive Forschung","Definition des Forschungsumfangs","Bewertung von Quellen","YAGNI","KISS","DRY","Aktualität","Tiefe","Ehrlichkeit","Brutalität"]}},"owner":"CongDon1207","repo":"AGENTS.md","repoPath":"CongDon1207/AGENTS.md","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"research","description":"Use when you need to research, analyze, and plan technical solutions that are scalable, secure, and maintainable.","bodyPreview":"# Research\n\n## Research Methodology\n\nAlways honoring **YAGNI**, **KISS**, and **DRY** principles.\n**Be honest, be brutal, straight to the point, and be concise.**\n\n### Phase 1: Scope Definition\n\nFirst, you will clearly define the research scope by:\n- Identifying key terms and concepts to investigate\n- Determining the recency requirements (how current must information be)\n- Establishing evaluation criteria for sources\n- Setting boundaries for the research depth\n\n### Phase 2: Systematic Informatio","body":"# Research\n\n## Research Methodology\n\nAlways honoring **YAGNI**, **KISS**, and **DRY** principles.\n**Be honest, be brutal, straight to the point, and be concise.**\n\n### Phase 1: Scope Definition\n\nFirst, you will clearly define the research scope by:\n- Identifying key terms and concepts to investigate\n- Determining the recency requirements (how current must information be)\n- Establishing evaluation criteria for sources\n- Setting boundaries for the research depth\n\n### Phase 2: Systematic Information Gathering\n\nYou will employ a multi-source research strategy:\n\n1. **Search Strategy**:\n   - Check if `gemini` bash command is available, if so, execute `gemini -m gemini-2.5-flash -p \"...your search prompt...\"` bash command (timeout: 10 minutes) and save the output using `Report:` path from `## Naming` section (including all citations).\n   - If `gemini` bash command is not available, fallback to `WebSearch` tool.\n   - Run multiple `gemini` bash commands or `WebSearch` tools in parallel to search for relevant information.\n   - Craft precise search queries with relevant keywords\n   - Include terms like \"best practices\", \"2024\", \"latest\", \"security\", \"performance\"\n   - Search for official documentation, GitHub repositories, and authoritative blogs\n   - Prioritize results from recognized authorities (official docs, major tech companies, respected developers)\n   - **IMPORTANT:** You are allowed to perform at most **5 researches (max 5 tool calls)**, user might request less than this amount, **strictly respect it**, think carefully based on the task before performing each related research topic.\n\n2. **Deep Content Analysis**:\n   - When you found a potential Github repository URL, use `docs-seeker` skill to find read it.\n   - Focus on official documentation, API references, and technical specifications\n   - Analyze README files from popular GitHub repositories\n   - Review changelog and release notes for version-specific information\n\n3. **Video Content Research**:\n   - Prioritize content from official channels, recognized experts, and major conferences\n   - Focus on practical demonstrations and real-world implementations\n\n4. **Cross-Reference Validation**:\n   - Verify information across multiple independent sources\n   - Check publication dates to ensure currency\n   - Identify consensus vs. controversial approaches\n   - Note any conflicting information or debates in the community\n\n### Phase 3: Analysis and Synthesis\n\nYou will analyze gathered information by:\n- Identifying common patterns and best practices\n- Evaluating pros and cons of different approaches\n- Assessing maturity and stability of technologies\n- Recognizing security implications and performance considerations\n- Determining compatibility and integration requirements\n\n### Phase 4: Report Generation\n\n**Notes:**\n- Research reports are saved using `Report:` path from `## Naming` section.\n- If `## Naming` section is not available, ask main agent to provide the output path.\n\nYou will create a comprehensive markdown report with the following structure:\n\n```markdown\n# Research Report: [Topic]\n\n## Executive Summary\n[2-3 paragraph overview of key findings and recommendations]\n\n## Research Methodology\n- Sources consulted: [number]\n- Date range of materials: [earliest to most recent]\n- Key search terms used: [list]\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### 1. Technology Overview\n[Comprehensive description of the technology/topic]\n\n### 2. Current State & Trends\n[Latest developments, version information, adoption trends]\n\n### 3. Best Practices\n[Detailed list of recommended practices with explanations]\n\n### 4. Security Considerations\n[Security implications, vulnerabilities, and mitigation strategies]\n\n### 5. Performance Insights\n[Performance characteristics, optimization techniques, benchmarks]\n\n## Comparative Analysis\n[If applicable, comparison of different solutions/approaches]\n\n## Implementation Recommendations\n\n### Quick Start Guide\n[Step-by-step getting started instructions]\n\n### Code Examples\n[Relevant code snippets with explanations]\n\n### Common Pitfalls\n[Mistakes to avoid and their solutions]\n\n## Resources & References\n\n### Official Documentation\n- [Linked list of official docs]\n\n### Recommended Tutorials\n- [Curated list with descriptions]\n\n### Community Resources\n- [Forums, Discord servers, Stack Overflow tags]\n\n### Further Reading\n- [Advanced topics and deep dives]\n\n## Appendices\n\n### A. Glossary\n[Technical terms and definitions]\n\n### B. Version Compatibility Matrix\n[If applicable]\n\n### C. Raw Research Notes\n[Optional: detailed notes from research process]\n```\n\n## Quality Standards\n\nYou will ensure all research meets these criteria:\n- **Accuracy**: Information is verified across multiple sources\n- **Currency**: Prioritize information from the last 12 months unless historical context is needed\n- **Completeness**: Cover all aspects requested by the user\n- **Actionability**: Provide practical, implementable recommendations\n- **Clarity**: Use clear language, define technical terms, provide examples\n- **Attribution**: Always cite sources and provide links for verification\n\n## Special Considerations\n\n- When researching security topics, always check for recent CVEs and security advisories\n- For performance-related research, look for benchmarks and real-world case studies\n- When investigating new technologies, assess community adoption and support levels\n- For API documentation, verify endpoint availability and authentication requirements\n- Always note deprecation warnings and migration paths for older technologies\n\n## Output Requirements\n\nYour final report must:\n1. Be saved using the `Report:` path from `## Naming` section with a descriptive filename\n2. Include a timestamp of when the research was conducted\n3. Provide clear section navigation with a table of contents for longer reports\n4. Use code blocks with appropriate syntax highlighting\n5. Include diagrams or architecture descriptions where helpful (in mermaid or ASCII art)\n6. Conclude with specific, actionable next steps\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Sacrifice grammar for the sake of concision when writing reports.\n**IMPORTANT:** In reports, list any unresolved questions at the end, if any.\n\n**Remember:** You are not just collecting information, but providing strategic technical intelligence that enables informed decision-making. Your research should anticipate follow-up questions and provide comprehensive coverage of the topic while remaining focused and practical."},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:27:47.828Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Research Agents requiring systematic information gathering and analysis with strict adherence to YAGNI, KISS, and DRY principles.","zh":"非常适合需要系统信息收集和分析的研究代理，严格遵循YAGNI、KISS和DRY原则。","ja":"YAGNI、KISS、DRY原則に厳格に従って体系的な情報収集と分析を必要とする研究エージェントに最適。","ko":"체계적인 정보 수집 및 분석이 필요한 연구 에이전트에게 적합하며, YAGNI, KISS, DRY 원칙을 엄격하게 따름.","es":"Ideal para agentes de investigación que requieren una recopilación y análisis de información sistemáticos con una adhesión estricta a los principios de YAGNI, KISS y DRY.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de recherche nécessitant une collecte et une analyse d''informations systématiques avec une adhésion stricte aux principes YAGNI, KISS et DRY.","de":"Ideal für Forschungsagenten, die eine systematische Informationsbeschaffung und -analyse mit strenger Einhaltung der YAGNI-, KISS- und DRY-Prinzipien erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Pesquisa que necessitam de coleta e análise de informações sistemáticas com adesão estrita aos princípios YAGNI, KISS e DRY.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов-исследователей, требующих системного сбора и анализа информации с строгим соблюдением принципов YAGNI, KISS и DRY.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء البحثيين الذين يتطلبون جمع معلومات منهجي وتحليله مع اتباع صارم لمبادئ YAGNI و KISS و DRY."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables structured research methodology implementation including scope definition, systematic information analysis, and source evaluation. Provides framework for key term identification, recency requirements determination, and research boundary setting.","zh":"实现结构化研究方法论，包括范围定义、系统信息分析和来源评估。为关键词识别、时效性要求确定和研究边界设置提供框架。","ja":"構造化された研究方法論の実装を可能にし、範囲の定義、体系的な情報分析、出典の評価を行う。重要用語の特定、時効要件の決定、研究境界の設定のためのフレームワークを提供する。","ko":"구조화된 연구 방법론을 구현하여 범위 정의, 체계적인 정보 분석 및 출처 평가를 수행함. 핵심 용어 식별, 시効성 요구 사항 결정 및 연구 경계 설정을 위한 프레임워크를 제공함.","es":"Permite la implementación de una metodología de investigación estructurada, incluyendo la definición del alcance, el análisis sistemático de la información y la evaluación de las fuentes. Proporciona un marco para la identificación de términos clave, la determinación de los requisitos de actualidad y la configuración de los límites de la investigación.","fr":"Permet la mise en œuvre d''une méthodologie de recherche structurée, y compris la définition de la portée, l''analyse systématique de l''information et l''évaluation des sources. Fournit un cadre pour l''identification des termes clés, la détermination des exigences de récence et la définition des limites de la recherche.","de":"Ermöglicht die Implementierung einer strukturierten Forschungsmethodik, einschließlich der Definition des Umfangs, der systematischen Informationsanalyse und der Quellenbewertung. Bietet einen Rahmen für die Identifizierung von Schlüsselbegriffen, die Bestimmung der Aktualitätsanforderungen und die Festlegung der Forschungsgrenzen.","pt":"Permite a implementação de metodologia de pesquisa estruturada, incluindo definição de escopo, análise sistemática de informações e avaliação de fontes. Fornece estrutura para identificação de termos-chave, determinação de requisitos de recência e definição de limites de pesquisa.","ru":"Позволяет реализовать структурированную методологию исследования, включая определение объема, системный анализ информации и оценку источников. Предоставляет основу для выявления ключевых терминов, определения требований к актуальности и установления границ исследования.","ar":"يمكن تنفيذ منهجية بحثية منظمة، بما في ذلك تعريف النطاق وتحليل المعلومات النظامي وتقييم المصادر. يوفر إطارًا لتحديد المصطلحات الرئيسية وتحديد متطلبات الحداثة وضبط حدود البحث."},"useCases":{"en":["Defining research scope with clear boundaries","Evaluating source credibility using established criteria","Conducting systematic information analysis","Maintaining research documentation integrity through AGENTS.md preservation"],"zh":["定义研究范围和明确边界","使用既定标准评估来源可信度","进行系统信息分析","通过AGENTS.md保存维护研究文档完整性"],"ja":["研究範囲の定義と明確な境界の設定","既定の基準を使用した出典の信頼性評価","体系的な情報分析の実施","AGENTS.mdの保存を通じて研究文書の完全性の維持"],"ko":["연구 범위 정의 및明確한 경계 설정","既定 기준을 사용한 출처 신뢰도 평가","체계적인 정보 분석 수행","AGENTS.md 보존을 통한 연구 문서 완전성 유지"],"es":["Definir el alcance de la investigación con límites claros","Evaluar la credibilidad de las fuentes utilizando criterios establecidos","Realizar un análisis sistemático de la información","Mantener la integridad de la documentación de investigación a través de la preservación de AGENTS.md"],"fr":["Définir la portée de la recherche avec des limites claires","Évaluer la crédibilité des sources en utilisant des critères établis","Effectuer une analyse systématique de l''information","Maintenir l''intégrité de la documentation de recherche grâce à la préservation de AGENTS.md"],"de":["Definieren des Forschungsumfangs mit klaren Grenzen","Bewerten der Quellenverlässlichkeit unter Verwendung etablierter Kriterien","Durchführen einer systematischen Informationsanalyse","Aufrechterhalten der Integrität der Forschungsdokumentation durch die Erhaltung von AGENTS.md"],"pt":["Definir escopo de pesquisa com limites claros","Avaliar credibilidade de fontes usando critérios estabelecidos","Realizar análise sistemática de informações","Manter integridade da documentação de pesquisa por meio da preservação do AGENTS.md"],"ru":["Определение объема исследования с четкими границами","Оценка достоверности источников с использованием установленных критериев","Проведение системного анализа информации","Поддержание целостности документации исследования путем сохранения AGENTS.md"],"ar":["تحديد نطاق البحث مع حدود واضحة","تقييم مصداقية المصادر باستخدام معايير محددة","إجراء تحليل منهجي للمعلومات","الحفاظ على سلامة توثيق البحث من خلال الحفاظ على AGENTS.md"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires project folder structure access","Dependent on existing AGENTS.md documentation","Limited to predefined research methodology framework"],"zh":["需要访问项目文件夹结构","依赖于现有的AGENTS.md文档","仅限于预定义的研究方法论框架"],"ja":["プロジェクトフォルダ構造へのアクセスが必要","既存のAGENTS.md文書への依存","事前に定義された研究方法論フレームワークのみに限定"],"ko":["프로젝트 폴더 구조에 대한 액세스가 필요함","既存의 AGENTS.md 문서에 의존","사전에 정의된 연구 방법론 프레임워크로만 제한"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la estructura de carpetas del proyecto","Depende de la documentación existente de AGENTS.md","Limitado al marco de metodología de investigación predefinido"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la structure de dossiers du projet","Dépend de la documentation existante de AGENTS.md","Limité au cadre de méthodologie de recherche prédéfini"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Projektordnerstruktur","Hängt von der bestehenden AGENTS.md-Dokumentation ab","Begrenzt auf den vorgegebenen Forschungsmethodikrahmen"],"pt":["Requer acesso à estrutura de pasta do projeto","Depende da documentação existente do AGENTS.md","Limitado ao quadro de metodologia de pesquisa predefinido"],"ru":["Требует доступа к структуре папок проекта","Зависит от существующей документации AGENTS.md","Ограничен предопределенным框ом методологии исследования"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى هيكل مجلدات المشروع","يعتمد على توثيق AGENTS.md الحالي","محدود بالإطار المحدد مسبقًا لمنهجية البحث"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
