 avec des outils de planification et de suivi","Génération de rapports au format JSON, Markdown et HTML","Compatibilité avec plusieurs langues et formats de fichier"],"de":["Automatisierung der Überprüfung und Berichterstellung","Verwendung von KI zur Zusammenfassung und Analyse von Informationen","Integration mit Planungs- und Überwachungstools","Generierung von Berichten im JSON-, Markdown- und HTML-Format","Kompatibilität mit mehreren Sprachen und Dateiformaten"],"pt":["Automatização da busca e extração de informações de artigos de arXiv","Geração de relatórios em JSON, Markdown e HTML","Revisão dupla para garantir a qualidade das informações","Integração com regras de código e estrutura de revisão","Suporte a múltiplos formatos de saída"],"ru":["Автоматизация поиска и извлечения информации из статей arXiv","Генерация отчетов в форматах JSON, Markdown и HTML","Двойной обзор для обеспечения качества информации","Интеграция с правилами кода и структурой обзора","Поддержка нескольких форматов вывода"],"ar":["ت autoComplete البحث واستخراج المعلومات من المقالات من arXiv","توليد تقارير ب形式 JSON و Markdown و HTML","المراجعة المزدوجة لضمان جودة المعلومات","التكامل مع قواعد الكود وهيكل المراجعة","دعم عدة صيغ للخرج"]},"keywords":{"zh":["双重审查计划实施","AI 代码审查","代码结构性审查","代码自修复","自动化代码审查","代码质量","开发效率"],"ja":["デュアルレビュー計画実装","AI コードレビュー","コード構造的レビュー","コード自修復","自動化コードレビュー","コード品質","開発効率"],"ko":["이중 검토 계획 구현","AI 코드 검토","코드 구조적 검토","코드 자가 수리","자동화 코드 검토","코드 품질","개발 효율성"],"es":["planificación de revisión dual","implementación de revisión dual","automatización de la revisión","generación de informes","IA para la revisión","herramientas de planificación","seguimiento de proyectos","análisis de información"],"fr":["planification de revue double","mise en œuvre de revue double","automatisation de la revue","génération de rapports","IA pour la revue","outils de planification","suivi de projets","analyse d''informations"],"de":["Planung der dualen Überprüfung","Implementierung der dualen Überprüfung","Automatisierung der Überprüfung","Berichterstellung","KI für die Überprüfung","Planungstools","Projektverfolgung","Informationsanalyse"],"pt":["planejamento e implementação de revisão dupla","automatização de revisão de artigos","arXiv","AI","revisão de código","estrutura de revisão","relatórios em JSON","relatórios em Markdown","relatórios em HTML"],"ru":["планирование и реализация двойного обзора","автоматизация обзора статей","arXiv","ИИ","обзор кода","структура обзора","отчеты в JSON","отчеты в Markdown","отчеты в HTML"],"ar":["تخطيط وتنفيذ المراجعة المزدوجة","ت autoComplete المراجعة للمقالات","arXiv","الذكاء الاصطناعي","مراجعة الكود","هيكل المراجعة","التقارير ب形式 JSON","التقارير ب形式 Markdown","التقارير ب形式 HTML"]}},"owner":"RainerSeventeen","repo":"paper-tracker","repoPath":"RainerSeventeen/paper-tracker","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"plan-implement-dual-review","description":"当用户提供项目计划文件并希望按计划落地代码时使用。该技能用于主agent编排两个subagent：subagent1读取计划并在新分支实现代码、随后依据 .ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md 自审并直接修复；subagent2再依据 .ai_docs/rules/code_review_structure_rules.md 做结构性审查并上报问题；主agent最终仅向用户汇报第三步的结构性问题。","bodyPreview":"# Plan Implement Dual Review\n\n## Overview\n\n将“按计划实现代码 + 规则自修复 + 结构性复审 + 主线程最小汇报”变成固定流程。\n目标是让主线程只承载高价值决策信息，不重复展开实现细节。\n其中：\n- 撰写/实现阶段统一遵守 `.ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md`。\n- 结构性审查阶段统一遵守 `.ai_docs/rules/code_review_structure_rules.md`。\n\n## Required Inputs\n\n在开始前收集并确认：\n- 计划文件路径（用户提供）\n- 是否允许创建并切换新分支（默认允许）\n- 验证方式（优先执行计划中要求的测试；若未定义，执行项目默认测试）\n\n若计划缺失关键约束，先补最少问题；其余采用显式假设并继续。\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Subagent1 implement plan on a new branch\n\n创建 `subagent1` 并分配唯一职责：按计划实现。\n\n对 `subagent1` 的明确要求：\n- 完整阅读计划文件，不得只读摘要","body":"# Plan Implement Dual Review\n\n## Overview\n\n将“按计划实现代码 + 规则自修复 + 结构性复审 + 主线程最小汇报”变成固定流程。\n目标是让主线程只承载高价值决策信息，不重复展开实现细节。\n其中：\n- 撰写/实现阶段统一遵守 `.ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md`。\n- 结构性审查阶段统一遵守 `.ai_docs/rules/code_review_structure_rules.md`。\n\n## Required Inputs\n\n在开始前收集并确认：\n- 计划文件路径（用户提供）\n- 是否允许创建并切换新分支（默认允许）\n- 验证方式（优先执行计划中要求的测试；若未定义，执行项目默认测试）\n\n若计划缺失关键约束，先补最少问题；其余采用显式假设并继续。\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Subagent1 implement plan on a new branch\n\n创建 `subagent1` 并分配唯一职责：按计划实现。\n\n对 `subagent1` 的明确要求：\n- 完整阅读计划文件，不得只读摘要\n- 开始实现前先阅读 `.ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md`，并在整个实现阶段持续遵守\n- 基于计划创建新分支并实现代码改动\n- 分支命名优先遵循计划内约定；若计划未给出，使用 `codex/<feature-summary>`\n- 在实现过程中记录：改动文件、关键设计决策、测试结果\n\n可直接复用的指令模板：\n\n```text\n你负责按计划落地实现，不做结构性审查。请完成：\n1) 读取计划文件：<PLAN_PATH>\n2) 阅读并严格遵守 .ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md\n3) 创建并切换新分支（遵循计划命名；无命名时用需要遵守 .ai_docs/rules/git_rules.md）\n4) 按计划完成代码修改并执行必要测试\n5) 输出：分支名、变更文件列表、测试结果、剩余风险\n```\n\n### Step 2: Subagent1 self-review by code rules and fix directly\n\n在 Step 1 完成后，继续让 `subagent1` 执行规则自审并直接修复问题。\n\n对 `subagent1` 的明确要求：\n- 读取并严格遵守 `.ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md`\n- 逐项检查刚完成的改动，发现问题直接修复，不进入上报\n- 修复后重新执行受影响测试\n- 输出：自审发现项、对应修复、最终测试结果\n\n可直接复用的指令模板：\n\n```text\n继续处理你刚才的改动：\n1) 阅读 .ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md\n2) 按规则审查你的所有改动\n3) 有问题直接修正并重新测试\n4) 输出：发现的问题与修复清单、最终测试结果\n```\n\n### Step 3: Subagent2 perform structural review and report\n\n创建 `subagent2`，只做结构性审查，不直接改代码。\n\n对 `subagent2` 的明确要求：\n- 阅读 `.ai_docs/rules/code_review_structure_rules.md`\n- 审查范围仅限当前分支改动\n- 仅输出“结构性问题”与证据，不输出风格性建议\n- 每条问题包含：严重级别、文件路径、问题描述、影响、建议方向\n\n可直接复用的指令模板：\n\n```text\n你只做结构性审查，不要修改代码：\n1) 阅读 .ai_docs/rules/code_review_structure_rules.md\n2) 仅审查当前分支改动的结构性问题\n3) 输出问题清单：severity/file/issue/impact/suggestion\n4) 若无结构性问题，明确输出“无结构性问题”\n```\n\n### Step 4: Main agent report only structural issues\n\n主agent只向用户汇报 Step 3 的结果。\n\n必须遵守：\n- 仅汇报结构性问题清单（或“无结构性问题”）\n- 不展开 Step 1/2 的实现过程细节\n- 不追加与结构无关的建议\n\n## Output Contract\n\n主线程固定输出：\n\n1. `结构性问题`：按严重级别排序（高 -> 中 -> 低）\n2. `结论`：\n   - 有问题：`请你拍板是否先修复以上结构性问题再继续。`\n   - 无问题：`本轮结构性审查通过。`\n\n## Standard Reply Template\n\n在主线程汇报时，直接套用以下模板之一。\n\n### Template A: 有结构性问题\n\n```markdown\n结构性问题\n1. [高|中|低] <问题标题>\n   - 文件: `<absolute-or-workspace-path>:<line>`\n   - 问题: <结构性问题描述>\n   - 影响: <可能导致的行为/维护风险>\n   - 建议方向: <修复方向，不展开实现细节>\n\n2. [高|中|低] <问题标题>\n   - 文件: `<absolute-or-workspace-path>:<line>`\n   - 问题: <结构性问题描述>\n   - 影响: <可能导致的行为/维护风险>\n   - 建议方向: <修复方向，不展开实现细节>\n\n结论\n请你拍板是否先修复以上结构性问题再继续。\n```\n\n### Template B: 无结构性问题\n\n```markdown\n结构性问题\n无结构性问题。\n\n结论\n本轮结构性审查通过。\n```\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Step 1 的实现必须以 `.ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md` 为编码准绳，不能跳过。\n- Step 2 必须由 `subagent1` 执行且“发现即修复”，不能跳过。\n- Step 3 必须以 `.ai_docs/rules/code_review_structure_rules.md` 为审查准绳，且由独立的 `subagent2` 执行，不能复用 `subagent1` 结论替代。\n- 主agent最终输出不得混入实现细节、风格性意见、或非结构问题。\n- 若 Step 3 证据不足，标记为“待确认”，不得伪造确定性结论。\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:28:27.390Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Review Agents requiring structured implementation and dual-review workflows","zh":"适用于需要结构化实现和双重审查工作流的代码审查代理","ja":"コードレビュー エージェントが構造化された実装とデュアルレビュー ワークフローを必要とする場合に最適","ko":"구조화된 구현 및 이중 검토 워크플로가 필요한 코드 검토 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de revisión de código que requieren una implementación estructurada y flujos de trabajo de revisión dual","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de révision de code nécessitant une mise en œuvre structurée et des flux de travail de révision double","de":"Ideal für Code-Review-Agents, die eine strukturierte Implementierung und Dual-Review-Workflows erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Revisão de Código que requerem implementação estruturada e fluxos de trabalho de revisão dupla","ru":"Идеально для агентов проверки кода, требующих структурированной реализации и двойных потоков проверки","ar":"مثالي لعميل مراجعة الكود الذي يحتاج إلى تنفيذ منظم وعمليات مراجعة مزدوجة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automate code implementation and review processes using JSON and Markdown reports, enforcing rules from `.ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md` and `.ai_docs/rules/code_review_structure_rules.md`","zh":"赋予代理人使用 JSON 和 Markdown 报表自动执行代码实现和审查流程的能力，强制执行 `.ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md` 和 `.ai_docs/rules/code_review_structure_rules.md` 中的规则","ja":"JSON と Markdown レポートを使用してコードの実装とレビュー プロセスを自動化するエージェントを可能にし、`.ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md` と `.ai_docs/rules/code_review_structure_rules.md` のルールを適用","ko":"JSON 및 Markdown 보고서를 사용하여 코드 구현 및 검토 프로세스를 자동화하고 `.ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md` 및 `.ai_docs/rules/code_review_structure_rules.md`의 규칙을 적용하는 에이전트를 가능하게 함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a automatizar los procesos de implementación y revisión de código utilizando informes JSON y Markdown, aplicando reglas de `.ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md` y `.ai_docs/rules/code_review_structure_rules.md`","fr":"Permet aux agents d''automatiser les processus de mise en œuvre et de révision de code en utilisant des rapports JSON et Markdown, en appliquant les règles de `.ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md` et `.ai_docs/rules/code_review_structure_rules.md`","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Code-Implementierungs- und Überprüfungsprozesse mithilfe von JSON- und Markdown-Berichten zu automatisieren, wobei Regeln aus `.ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md` und `.ai_docs/rules/code_review_structure_rules.md` angewendet werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a automatizar a implementação de código e processos de revisão usando relatórios JSON e Markdown, aplicando regras de `.ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md` e `.ai_docs/rules/code_review_structure_rules.md`","ru":"Позволяет агентам автоматизировать реализацию кода и процессы проверки, используя отчеты JSON и Markdown, применяя правила из `.ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md` и `.ai_docs/rules/code_review_structure_rules.md`","ar":"يمكن العميل من توفير آلي لتنفيذ الكود وعمليات المراجعة باستخدام تقارير JSON و Markdown ، وتنفيذ القواعد من `.ai_docs/rules/code_rules.md` و `.ai_docs/rules/code_review_structure_rules.md`"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating arXiv paper summaries with metadata extraction","Implementing code review structures with minimal main thread reporting","Generating HTML reports for code implementation and review"],"zh":["使用元数据提取自动化 arXiv 论文摘要","实现代码审查结构，具有最小的主线程报告","生成代码实现和审查的 HTML 报告"],"ja":["メタデータ抽出を使用して arXiv 論文のサマリーを自動化","コードレビュー構造を実装し、最小のメインスレッド レポートを使用","コード実装とレビューの HTML レポートを生成"],"ko":["메타데이터 추출을 사용하여 arXiv 논문의 요약을 자동화","코드 검토 구조를 구현하고 최소한의 메인 스레드 보고서를 사용","코드 구현 및 검토를 위한 HTML 보고서 생성"],"es":["Automatización de resúmenes de artículos de arXiv con extracción de metadatos","Implementación de estructuras de revisión de código con informes de subprocesos mínimos","Generación de informes HTML para implementación y revisión de código"],"fr":["Automatisation des résumés d''articles arXiv avec extraction de métadonnées","Mise en œuvre de structures de révision de code avec des rapports de threads principaux minimaux","Génération de rapports HTML pour la mise en œuvre et la révision de code"],"de":["Automatisierung von Zusammenfassungen von arXiv-Artikeln mit Metadatenextraktion","Implementierung von Code-Review-Strukturen mit minimalen Hauptthread-Berichten","Generierung von HTML-Berichten für Code-Implementierung und -Überprüfung"],"pt":["Automatizar resumos de artigos do arXiv com extração de metadados","Implementar estruturas de revisão de código com relatórios de thread principal mínimos","Gerar relatórios HTML para implementação e revisão de código"],"ru":["Автоматизировать резюме статей arXiv с извлечением метаданных","Реализовывать структуры проверки кода с минимальным отчетом основного потока","Генерировать отчеты HTML для реализации и проверки кода"],"ar":["توفير ملخصات آلية لأوراق arXiv مع استخراج البيانات الوصفية","تنفيذ هياكل مراجعة الكود مع تقارير线 رئيسية قليلة","توليد تقارير HTML لتنفيذ الكود ومراجعته"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to arXiv and specific file paths for plan implementation","Dependent on `.ai_docs/rules` directory for code and review rules","Limited to JSON, Markdown, and HTML report formats"],"zh":["需要访问 arXiv 和特定的文件路径以实施计划","依赖于 `.ai_docs/rules` 目录中的代码和审查规则","仅限于 JSON、Markdown 和 HTML 报表格式"],"ja":["計画の実施には arXiv と特定のファイル パスへのアクセスが必要","`.ai_docs/rules` ディレクトリ内のコードとレビュー ルールに依存","JSON、Markdown、HTML レポート形式のみに限定"],"ko":["계획을 구현하려면 arXiv 및 특정 파일 경로에 대한 액세스가 필요함","`.ai_docs/rules` 디렉토리 내의 코드 및 검토 규칙에 종속됨","JSON, Markdown, HTML 보고서 형식만으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere acceso a arXiv y rutas de archivo específicas para la implementación del plan","Dependiente del directorio `.ai_docs/rules` para reglas de código y revisión","Limitado a formatos de informe JSON, Markdown y HTML"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à arXiv et des chemins de fichiers spécifiques pour la mise en œuvre du plan","Dépendant du répertoire `.ai_docs/rules` pour les règles de code et de révision","Limité aux formats de rapport JSON, Markdown et HTML"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf arXiv und spezifische Dateipfade für die Planimplementierung","Abhängig vom Verzeichnis `.ai_docs/rules` für Code- und Review-Regeln","Begrenzt auf JSON-, Markdown- und HTML-Berichtsformate"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao arXiv e caminhos de arquivo específicos para implementação do plano","Dependente do diretório `.ai_docs/rules` para regras de código e revisão","Limitado a formatos de relatório JSON, Markdown e HTML"],"ru":["Требует доступа к arXiv и определенных путей файлов для реализации плана","Зависит от директории `.ai_docs/rules` для правил кода и проверки","Ограничен форматами отчетов JSON, Markdown и HTML"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى arXiv ومسارات الملفات المحددة لتنفيذ الخطة","يعتمد على الدليل `.ai_docs/rules` لقواعد الكود ومراجعته","محدود بالتنسيقات التقارير JSON و Markdown و HTML"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('jaxxstorm/landlord/openspec-onboard', 'community', 'jaxxstorm', 'landlord', 'jaxxstorm/landlord', 'openspec-onboard', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z', '2026-02-18T06:28:38.575Z', NULL, '{"id":"jaxxstorm/landlord/openspec-onboard","name":"openspec-onboard","description":{"zh":"OpenSpec 入门指南，引导您完成第一个工作流程周期","ja":"OpenSpec のガイドを通じて、最初のワークフロー サイクルを完了","ko":"OpenSpec 시작하기 가이드, 첫 번째 워크플로 사이클을 완료","es":"OpenSpec es una herramienta que te guía a través de tu primer ciclo de trabajo completo. Inicializa OpenSpec y comienza a trabajar en tu código.","fr":"OpenSpec est un outil qui vous guide à travers votre premier cycle de travail complet. Initialiser OpenSpec et commencez à travailler sur votre code.","de":"OpenSpec ist ein Tool, das Sie durch Ihren ersten vollständigen Arbeitszyklus führt. Initialisieren Sie OpenSpec und beginnen Sie mit der Arbeit an Ihrem Code.","pt":"O OpenSpec Onboard é um guia que o ajuda a configurar e iniciar o workflow do OpenSpec. Aprenda a inicializar e começar a trabalhar em seu código","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard — это руководство, которое помогает настроить и начать рабочий процесс OpenSpec. Узнайте, как инициализировать и начать работать с вашим кодом","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard هو دليل يساعدك على ضبط وبدء دورة العمل OpenSpec. تعلم كيف تُشغل وتبدأ العمل على كودك","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"OpenSpec 入门指南","ja":"OpenSpec を使い始める","ko":"OpenSpec 시작하기","es":"Guía de OpenSpec: Inicio y configuración","fr":"Guide OpenSpec : Premiers pas et configuration","de":"OpenSpec-Anleitung: Ersteinrichtung und Konfiguration","pt":"OpenSpec Onboard: Guia de Inicialização","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard: Руководство по настройке","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard: دليل الإعداد","en":"openspec-onboard"},"description":{"zh":"OpenSpec 入门指南，引导您完成第一个工作流程周期","ja":"OpenSpec のガイドを通じて、最初のワークフロー サイクルを完了","ko":"OpenSpec 시작하기 가이드, 첫 번째 워크플로 사이클을 완료","es":"OpenSpec es una herramienta que te guía a través de tu primer ciclo de trabajo completo. Inicializa OpenSpec y comienza a trabajar en tu código.","fr":"OpenSpec est un outil qui vous guide à travers votre premier cycle de travail complet. Initialiser OpenSpec et commencez à travailler sur votre code.","de":"OpenSpec ist ein Tool, das Sie durch Ihren ersten vollständigen Arbeitszyklus führt. Initialisieren Sie OpenSpec und beginnen Sie mit der Arbeit an Ihrem Code.","pt":"O OpenSpec Onboard é um guia que o ajuda a configurar e iniciar o workflow do OpenSpec. Aprenda a inicializar e começar a trabalhar em seu código","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard — это руководство, которое помогает настроить и начать рабочий процесс OpenSpec. Узнайте, как инициализировать и начать работать с вашим кодом","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard هو دليل يساعدك على ضبط وبدء دورة العمل OpenSpec. تعلم كيف تُشغل وتبدأ العمل على كودك","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["OpenSpec 初始化","工作流程周期引导","代码库操作","实时反馈","步骤解释"],"ja":["OpenSpec 初期化","ワークフロー サイクル ガイド","コードベース操作","リアルタイム フィードバック","ステップ説明"],"ko":["OpenSpec 초기화","워크플로 사이클 가이드","코드베이스操作","실시간 피드백","단계 설명"],"es":["Guía de inicio para OpenSpec","Configuración y inicialización de OpenSpec","Ciclo de trabajo completo de OpenSpec","Trabajo real en el código del proyecto","Explicación de cada paso del proceso"],"fr":["Guide de démarrage pour OpenSpec","Configuration et initialisation d''OpenSpec","Cycle de travail complet d''OpenSpec","Travail réel sur le code du projet","Explication de chaque étape du processus"],"de":["Ersteinrichtungsanleitung für OpenSpec","Konfiguration und Initialisierung von OpenSpec","Vollständiger Arbeitszyklus von OpenSpec","Echte Arbeit am Projektcode","Erklärung jedes Schritts im Prozess"],"pt":["Guia de inicialização","Configuração do OpenSpec","Início do workflow","Trabalho em código","Verificação de inicialização"],"ru":["Руководство по настройке","Настройка OpenSpec","Начало рабочего процесса","Работа с кодом","Проверка инициализации"],"ar":["دليل الإعداد","ضبط OpenSpec","بدء الدورةالعمل","العمل على الكود","فحص التشغيل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["OpenSpec","开发工作流","代码库管理","工作流程周期","开发工具"],"ja":["OpenSpec","開発ワークフロー","コードベース管理","ワークフロー サイクル","開発ツール"],"ko":["OpenSpec","개발 워크플로","코드베이스 관리","워크플로 사이클","개발 도구"],"es":["OpenSpec","configuración de OpenSpec","inicio de OpenSpec","ciclo de trabajo de OpenSpec","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo","flujo de trabajo de desarrollo"],"fr":["OpenSpec","configuration d''OpenSpec","démarrage d''OpenSpec","cycle de travail d''OpenSpec","développement de logiciels","outils de développement","flux de travail de développement"],"de":["OpenSpec","OpenSpec-Konfiguration","OpenSpec-Ersteinrichtung","OpenSpec-Arbeitszyklus","Softwareentwicklung","Entwicklungstools","Entwicklungsarbeitsablauf"],"pt":["OpenSpec","Onboard","inicialização","workflow","desenvolvimento","código","configuração"],"ru":["OpenSpec","Onboard","настройка","рабочий процесс","разработка","код","конфигурация"],"ar":["OpenSpec","Onboard","إعداد","دورة العمل","التطوير","الكود","ضبط"]}},"owner":"jaxxstorm","repo":"landlord","repoPath":"jaxxstorm/landlord","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-onboard","description":"Guided onboarding for OpenSpec - walk through a complete workflow cycle with narration and real codebase work.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay","body":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay:\n\n```\n## Welcome to OpenSpec!\n\nI''ll walk you through a complete change cycle—from idea to implementation—using a real task in your codebase. Along the way, you''ll learn the workflow by doing it.\n\n**What we''ll do:**\n1. Pick a small, real task in your codebase\n2. Explore the problem briefly\n3. Create a change (the container for our work)\n4. Build the artifacts: proposal → specs → design → tasks\n5. Implement the tasks\n6. Archive the completed change\n\n**Time:** ~15-20 minutes\n\nLet''s start by finding something to work on.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Task Selection\n\n### Codebase Analysis\n\nScan the codebase for small improvement opportunities. Look for:\n\n1. **TODO/FIXME comments** - Search for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `HACK`, `XXX` in code files\n2. **Missing error handling** - `catch` blocks that swallow errors, risky operations without try-catch\n3. **Functions without tests** - Cross-reference `src/` with test directories\n4. **Type issues** - `any` types in TypeScript files (`: any`, `as any`)\n5. **Debug artifacts** - `console.log`, `console.debug`, `debugger` statements in non-debug code\n6. **Missing validation** - User input handlers without validation\n\nAlso check recent git activity:\n```bash\ngit log --oneline -10 2>/dev/null || echo \"No git history\"\n```\n\n### Present Suggestions\n\nFrom your analysis, present 3-4 specific suggestions:\n\n```\n## Task Suggestions\n\nBased on scanning your codebase, here are some good starter tasks:\n\n**1. [Most promising task]**\n   Location: `src/path/to/file.ts:42`\n   Scope: ~1-2 files, ~20-30 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**2. [Second task]**\n   Location: `src/another/file.ts`\n   Scope: ~1 file, ~15 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**3. [Third task]**\n   Location: [location]\n   Scope: [estimate]\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**4. Something else?**\n   Tell me what you''d like to work on.\n\nWhich task interests you? (Pick a number or describe your own)\n```\n\n**If nothing found:** Fall back to asking what the user wants to build:\n> I didn''t find obvious quick wins in your codebase. What''s something small you''ve been meaning to add or fix?\n\n### Scope Guardrail\n\nIf the user picks or describes something too large (major feature, multi-day work):\n\n```\nThat''s a valuable task, but it''s probably larger than ideal for your first OpenSpec run-through.\n\nFor learning the workflow, smaller is better—it lets you see the full cycle without getting stuck in implementation details.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Slice it smaller** - What''s the smallest useful piece of [their task]? Maybe just [specific slice]?\n2. **Pick something else** - One of the other suggestions, or a different small task?\n3. **Do it anyway** - If you really want to tackle this, we can. Just know it''ll take longer.\n\nWhat would you prefer?\n```\n\nLet the user override if they insist—this is a soft guardrail.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Explore Demo\n\nOnce a task is selected, briefly demonstrate explore mode:\n\n```\nBefore we create a change, let me quickly show you **explore mode**—it''s how you think through problems before committing to a direction.\n```\n\nSpend 1-2 minutes investigating the relevant code:\n- Read the file(s) involved\n- Draw a quick ASCII diagram if it helps\n- Note any considerations\n\n```\n## Quick Exploration\n\n[Your brief analysis—what you found, any considerations]\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│   [Optional: ASCII diagram if helpful]  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nExplore mode (`/opsx:explore`) is for this kind of thinking—investigating before implementing. You can use it anytime you need to think through a problem.\n\nNow let''s create a change to hold our work.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user acknowledgment before proceeding.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Create the Change\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Creating a Change\n\nA \"change\" in OpenSpec is a container for all the thinking and planning around a piece of work. It lives in `openspec/changes/<name>/` and holds your artifacts—proposal, specs, design, tasks.\n\nLet me create one for our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the change with a derived kebab-case name:\n```bash\nopenspec new change \"<derived-name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nCreated: `openspec/changes/<name>/`\n\nThe folder structure:\n```\nopenspec/changes/<name>/\n├── proposal.md    ← Why we''re doing this (empty, we''ll fill it)\n├── design.md      ← How we''ll build it (empty)\n├── specs/         ← Detailed requirements (empty)\n└── tasks.md       ← Implementation checklist (empty)\n```\n\nNow let''s fill in the first artifact—the proposal.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Proposal\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## The Proposal\n\nThe proposal captures **why** we''re making this change and **what** it involves at a high level. It''s the \"elevator pitch\" for the work.\n\nI''ll draft one based on our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft the proposal content (don''t save yet):\n\n```\nHere''s a draft proposal:\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n[1-2 sentences explaining the problem/opportunity]\n\n## What Changes\n\n[Bullet points of what will be different]\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n- `<capability-name>`: [brief description]\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n<!-- If modifying existing behavior -->\n\n## Impact\n\n- `src/path/to/file.ts`: [what changes]\n- [other files if applicable]\n\n---\n\nDoes this capture the intent? I can adjust before we save it.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user approval/feedback.\n\nAfter approval, save the proposal:\n```bash\nopenspec instructions proposal --change \"<name>\" --json\n```\nThen write the content to `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`.\n\n```\nProposal saved. This is your \"why\" document—you can always come back and refine it as understanding evolves.\n\nNext up: specs.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Specs\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Specs\n\nSpecs define **what** we''re building in precise, testable terms. They use a requirement/scenario format that makes expected behavior crystal clear.\n\nFor a small task like this, we might only need one spec file.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the spec file:\n```bash\nmkdir -p openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability-name>\n```\n\nDraft the spec content:\n\n```\nHere''s the spec:\n\n---\n\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: <Name>\n\n<Description of what the system should do>\n\n#### Scenario: <Scenario name>\n\n- **WHEN** <trigger condition>\n- **THEN** <expected outcome>\n- **AND** <additional outcome if needed>\n\n---\n\nThis format—WHEN/THEN/AND—makes requirements testable. You can literally read them as test cases.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability>/spec.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Design\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Design\n\nThe design captures **how** we''ll build it—technical decisions, tradeoffs, approach.\n\nFor small changes, this might be brief. That''s fine—not every change needs deep design discussion.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft design.md:\n\n```\nHere''s the design:\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\n[Brief context about the current state]\n\n## Goals / Non-Goals\n\n**Goals:**\n- [What we''re trying to achieve]\n\n**Non-Goals:**\n- [What''s explicitly out of scope]\n\n## Decisions\n\n### Decision 1: [Key decision]\n\n[Explanation of approach and rationale]\n\n---\n\nFor a small task, this captures the key decisions without over-engineering.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Tasks\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Tasks\n\nFinally, we break the work into implementation tasks—checkboxes that drive the apply phase.\n\nThese should be small, clear, and in logical order.\n```\n\n**DO:** Generate tasks based on specs and design:\n\n```\nHere are the implementation tasks:\n\n---\n\n## 1. [Category or file]\n\n- [ ] 1.1 [Specific task]\n- [ ] 1.2 [Specific task]\n\n## 2. Verify\n\n- [ ] 2.1 [Verification step]\n\n---\n\nEach checkbox becomes a unit of work in the apply phase. Ready to implement?\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user to confirm they''re ready to implement.\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 9: Apply (Implementation)\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Implementation\n\nNow we implement each task, checking them off as we go. I''ll announce each one and occasionally note how the specs/design informed the approach.\n```\n\n**DO:** For each task:\n\n1. Announce: \"Working on task N: [description]\"\n2. Implement the change in the codebase\n3. Reference specs/design naturally: \"The spec says X, so I''m doing Y\"\n4. Mark complete in tasks.md: `- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n5. Brief status: \"✓ Task N complete\"\n\nKeep narration light—don''t over-explain every line of code.\n\nAfter all tasks:\n\n```\n## Implementation Complete\n\nAll tasks done:\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n- [x] ...\n\nThe change is implemented! One more step—let''s archive it.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 10: Archive\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Archiving\n\nWhen a change is complete, we archive it. This moves it from `openspec/changes/` to `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`.\n\nArchived changes become your project''s decision history—you can always find them later to understand why something was built a certain way.\n```\n\n**DO:**\n```bash\nopenspec archive \"<name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nArchived to: `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`\n\nThe change is now part of your project''s history. The code is in your codebase, the decision record is preserved.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 11: Recap & Next Steps\n\n```\n## Congratulations!\n\nYou just completed a full OpenSpec cycle:\n\n1. **Explore** - Thought through the problem\n2. **New** - Created a change container\n3. **Proposal** - Captured WHY\n4. **Specs** - Defined WHAT in detail\n5. **Design** - Decided HOW\n6. **Tasks** - Broke it into steps\n7. **Apply** - Implemented the work\n8. **Archive** - Preserved the record\n\nThis same rhythm works for any size change—a small fix or a major feature.\n\n---\n\n## Command Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems before/during work |\n| `/opsx:new` | Start a new change, step through artifacts |\n| `/opsx:ff` | Fast-forward: create all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue` | Continue working on an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply` | Implement tasks from a change |\n| `/opsx:verify` | Verify implementation matches artifacts |\n| `/opsx:archive` | Archive a completed change |\n\n---\n\n## What''s Next?\n\nTry `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff` on something you actually want to build. You''ve got the rhythm now!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Graceful Exit Handling\n\n### User wants to stop mid-way\n\nIf the user says they need to stop, want to pause, or seem disengaged:\n\n```\nNo problem! Your change is saved at `openspec/changes/<name>/`.\n\nTo pick up where we left off later:\n- `/opsx:continue <name>` - Resume artifact creation\n- `/opsx:apply <name>` - Jump to implementation (if tasks exist)\n\nThe work won''t be lost. Come back whenever you''re ready.\n```\n\nExit gracefully without pressure.\n\n### User just wants command reference\n\nIf the user says they just want to see the commands or skip the tutorial:\n\n```\n## OpenSpec Quick Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems (no code changes) |\n| `/opsx:new <name>` | Start a new change, step by step |\n| `/opsx:ff <name>` | Fast-forward: all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue <name>` | Continue an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply <name>` | Implement tasks |\n| `/opsx:verify <name>` | Verify implementation |\n| `/opsx:archive <name>` | Archive when done |\n\nTry `/opsx:new` to start your first change, or `/opsx:ff` if you want to move fast.\n```\n\nExit gracefully.\n\n---\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- **Follow the EXPLAIN → DO → SHOW → PAUSE pattern** at key transitions (after explore, after proposal draft, after tasks, after archive)\n- **Keep narration light** during implementation—teach without lecturing\n- **Don''t skip phases** even if the change is small—the goal is teaching the workflow\n- **Pause for acknowledgment** at marked points, but don''t over-pause\n- **Handle exits gracefully**—never pressure the user to continue\n- **Use real codebase tasks**—don''t simulate or use fake examples\n- **Adjust scope gently**—guide toward smaller tasks but respect user choice\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:28:38.575Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Analysis Agents needing guided OpenSpec workflow integration.","zh":"适合需要引导式OpenSpec工作流集成的代码分析代理。","ja":"OpenSpecワークフロー統合を必要とするコード分析エージェントに最適です。","ko":"가이드된 OpenSpec 워크플ロー 통합을 필요로 하는 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de análisis de código que necesitan una integración de flujo de trabajo OpenSpec guiada.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de code nécessitant une intégration de workflow OpenSpec guidée.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Analyse-Agents, die eine guidierte OpenSpec-Workflow-Integration benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Código que necessitam de integração de fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec orientada.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа кода, которым необходима интеграция рабочего процесса OpenSpec с пошаговым руководством.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء تحليل الشفرة الذين يحتاجون إلى تكامل تدفق عمل OpenSpec الموجه."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to initialize and manage OpenSpec projects, providing JSON status checks and step-by-step workflow guidance through the command line using openspec init and openspec status commands.","zh":"赋予代理初始化和管理OpenSpec项目的能力，提供JSON状态检查和通过命令行使用openspec init和openspec status命令的逐步工作流指导。","ja":"エージェントにOpenSpecプロジェクトを初期化および管理する能力を与え、JSONステータスチェックとコマンドラインを使用したopenspec initおよびopenspec statusコマンドによるステップバイステップのワークフローガイダンスを提供します。","ko":"에이전트에게 OpenSpec 프로젝트를 초기화하고 관리하는 능력을 부여하며, JSON 상태检查과 명령줄을 통한 openspec init 및 openspec status 명령어를 사용한 단계별 워크플로우 가이드를 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a inicializar y gestionar proyectos OpenSpec, proporcionando comprobaciones de estado JSON y orientación de flujo de trabajo paso a paso a través de la línea de comandos utilizando los comandos openspec init y openspec status.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''initialiser et de gérer des projets OpenSpec, en fournissant des vérifications d''état JSON et une orientation de workflow étape par étape via la ligne de commande en utilisant les commandes openspec init et openspec status.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agents, OpenSpec-Projekte zu initialisieren und zu verwalten, und bietet JSON-Statusprüfungen und schrittweise Workflow-Anleitung über die Kommandozeile mithilfe der Befehle openspec init und openspec status.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a inicializar e gerenciar projetos OpenSpec, fornecendo verificações de status JSON e orientação de fluxo de trabalho passo a passo através da linha de comando usando os comandos openspec init e openspec status.","ru":"Позволяет агентам инициализировать и управлять проектами OpenSpec, обеспечивая проверки статуса JSON и пошаговое руководство рабочим процессом через командную строку с помощью команд openspec init и openspec status.","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من 초기ته وتشغيل مشاريع OpenSpec، ويوفر فحوصات حالة JSON وتوجيه خطوة بخطوة للتدفقالعمل عبر سطر الأوامر باستخدام أوامر openspec init وopenspec status."},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing OpenSpec in new projects","Guiding users through their first OpenSpec workflow cycle","Checking OpenSpec initialization status via JSON output"],"zh":["在新项目中初始化OpenSpec","引导用户完成第一个OpenSpec工作流周期","通过JSON输出检查OpenSpec初始化状态"],"ja":["新しいプロジェクトでOpenSpecを初期化する","ユーザーを最初のOpenSpecワークフローサイクルに導く","JSON出力でOpenSpec初期化状態を確認する"],"ko":["새 프로젝트에서 OpenSpec 초기화","사용자를 첫 번째 OpenSpec 워크플로우 사이클로 안내","JSON 출력을 통해 OpenSpec 초기화 상태 확인"],"es":["Inicializar OpenSpec en nuevos proyectos","Guía a los usuarios a través de su primer ciclo de flujo de trabajo OpenSpec","Comprobación del estado de inicialización de OpenSpec a través de la salida JSON"],"fr":["Initialiser OpenSpec dans de nouveaux projets","Guider les utilisateurs à travers leur premier cycle de workflow OpenSpec","Vérification de l''état d''initialisation OpenSpec via la sortie JSON"],"de":["OpenSpec in neuen Projekten initialisieren","Benutzer durch ihren ersten OpenSpec-Workflow-Zyklus führen","Überprüfung des OpenSpec-Initialisierungsstatus über die JSON-Ausgabe"],"pt":["Inicializar OpenSpec em novos projetos","Orientar usuários através do seu primeiro ciclo de fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec","Verificar status de inicialização OpenSpec via saída JSON"],"ru":["Инициализация OpenSpec в новых проектах","Помощь пользователям в их первом цикле рабочего процесса OpenSpec","Проверка статуса инициализации OpenSpec через вывод JSON"],"ar":["تحرير OpenSpec في مشاريع جديدة","توجيه المستخدمين خلال دورة تدفق العمل OpenSpec الأولى","تحقق من حالة بدء تشغيل OpenSpec من خلال الإخراج JSON"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires openspec command-line tool installation","Needs project setup with openspec init before use"],"zh":["需要安装openspec命令行工具","需要在使用前使用openspec init设置项目"],"ja":["openspecコマンドラインツールのインストールが必要","使用前にopenspec initでプロジェクトを設定する必要がある"],"ko":["openspec 명령줄 도구 설치가 필요","사용 전에 openspec init로 프로젝트 설정이 필요"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de la herramienta de línea de comandos openspec","Necesita la configuración del proyecto con openspec init antes de su uso"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de l''outil de ligne de commande openspec","Nécessite la configuration du projet avec openspec init avant utilisation"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation des openspec-Kommandozeilen-Tools","Benötigt die Projektkonfiguration mit openspec init vor der Verwendung"],"pt":["Requer instalação da ferramenta de linha de comando openspec","Necessita de configuração do projeto com openspec init antes do uso"],"ru":["Требует установки инструмента командной строки openspec","Требует настройки проекта с помощью openspec init перед использованием"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت أداة سطر الأوامر openspec","يحتاج إلى إعداد المشروع مع openspec init قبل الاستخدام"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
