Sie .NET-Anwendungen entwickeln können, mit unseren E...","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["CLI 工具","测试框架","SOLID 原则","描述性变量","方法排序","避免魔术数"],"ja":["CLI ツール","テストフレームワーク","SOLID 原則","記述的変数","メソッドの並び","マジックナンバーの回避"],"ko":["CLI 도구","테스트 프레임워크","SOLID 원칙","설명적 변수","메서드 정렬","마법 数의 回避"],"es":["Estructura de código clara y mantenible","Seguimiento de los principios SOLID","Uso de variables descriptivas y claras","Evitación de números y cadenas mágicas","Orden de métodos en clases: público, protegido y privado"],"fr":["Structure de code claire et maintenable","Respect des principes SOLID","Utilisation de variables descriptives et claires","Évitement des nombres et des chaînes magiques","Ordre des méthodes dans les classes : public, protégé et privé"],"de":["Klare und wartbare Code-Struktur","Einhalten der SOLID-Prinzipien","Verwendung von beschreibenden und klaren Variablen","Vermeidung von magischen Zahlen und Zeichenfolgen","Reihenfolge der Methoden in Klassen: öffentlich, geschützt und privat"]},"keywords":{"zh":[".NET","CLI 工具","测试框架","SOLID 原则","变量命名","方法排序","魔术数","C#","开发框架"],"ja":[".NET","CLI ツール","テストフレームワーク","SOLID 原則","変数命名","メソッドの並び","マジックナンバー","C#","開発フレームワーク"],"ko":[".NET","CLI 도구","테스트 프레임워크","SOLID 원칙","변수 이름","메서드 정렬","마법 数","C#","개발 프레임워크"],"es":["desarrollo de aplicaciones .NET","mejores prácticas .NET","estructura de código .NET","principios SOLID","variables descriptivas","números mágicos","cadenas mágicas"],"fr":["développement d''applications .NET","meilleures pratiques .NET","structure de code .NET","principes SOLID","variables descriptives","nombres magiques","chaînes magiques"],"de":[".NET-Anwendungsentwicklung","beste Praktiken .NET","Code-Struktur .NET","SOLID-Prinzipien","beschreibende Variablen","magische Zahlen","magische Zeichenfolgen"]}},"owner":"PinedaTec-EU","repo":"SphereIntegrationHub","repoPath":"PinedaTec-EU/SphereIntegrationHub","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.448Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"dotnet","description":"Work on the .NET solution for SphereIntegrationHub. Use this when editing services, components, JSON data, or tests.","bodyPreview":"# .NET\n\n## Main structure\n\n- CLI tool: `src/SphereIntegrationHub` (Application).\n- Tests: `tests/SphereIntegrationHub.cli.tests` (xUnit).\n\n## Considerations\n\n- If a method has a `CancellationToken`, it must be the last parameter in the method signature.\n- SOLID principles must be followed.\n- Variables must be descriptive and clear, without being excessively long.\n- The order of methods in classes must be: public, protected, then private.\n- Magic numbers, strings, etc. must be avoided. Use `priva","body":"# .NET\n\n## Main structure\n\n- CLI tool: `src/SphereIntegrationHub` (Application).\n- Tests: `tests/SphereIntegrationHub.cli.tests` (xUnit).\n\n## Considerations\n\n- If a method has a `CancellationToken`, it must be the last parameter in the method signature.\n- SOLID principles must be followed.\n- Variables must be descriptive and clear, without being excessively long.\n- The order of methods in classes must be: public, protected, then private.\n- Magic numbers, strings, etc. must be avoided. Use `private const` when elements are exclusive to a class, or, if shared, a `XxxxConsts` class with `internal const` members and reduced visibility.\n- When possible, components should use a fluent style for construction/configuration.\n- Methods must have clearly bounded responsibilities; actions should be focused and the code readable, split into small chunks (ideally no more than 50 lines of code).\n\n## Tests\n\n- Reusable, associated fixtures must be used, with methods that create common elements for multiple tests, reducing complexity and improving readability.\n- Tests must be unit tests, using mocks or WireMock (for endpoints).\n- Interfaces of the elements under test must be used, for example:  \n  `IWorkflowExecutor executor = new WorkflowExecutor()`, ensuring that the interface is fully implemented and complete.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:30:34.052Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for CLI-based Agents needing robust .NET integration and SOLID principle adherence.","zh":"适合需要强大 .NET 集成和 SOLID 原则遵守的基于 CLI 的代理。","ja":"CLI ベースのエージェントが強力な .NET 統合と SOLID 原則の遵守を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"강력한 .NET 통합과 SOLID 원칙 준수를 필요로 하는 CLI 기반 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes basados en CLI que necesitan una integración robusta de .NET y adherencia al principio SOLID.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents basés sur CLI nécessitant une intégration robuste de .NET et l''adhésion au principe SOLID.","de":"Perfekt für CLI-basierte Agenten, die eine robuste .NET-Integration und die Einhaltung des SOLID-Prinzips benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes baseados em CLI que necessitam de integração robusta do .NET e aderência aos princípios SOLID.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов, основанных на CLI, требующих надежной интеграции с .NET и соблюдения принципов SOLID.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء القائمين على CLI الذين يحتاجون إلى تكامل قوي مع .NET وامتثال لمبدأ SOLID."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to develop scalable .NET applications using CLI tools like `dotnet`, following best practices with descriptive variable naming and avoiding magic numbers, while leveraging xUnit for test-driven development and ensuring adherence to SOLID principles.","zh":"赋予代理开发可扩展的 .NET 应用程序的能力，使用像 `dotnet` 这样的 CLI 工具，遵循最佳实践，使用描述性变量命名，避免魔术数字，同时利用 xUnit 进行测试驱动开发，确保遵守 SOLID 原则。","ja":"エージェントが `dotnet` などの CLI ツールを使用して拡張可能な .NET アプリケーションを開発する能力を与え、ベストプラクティスに従い、記述的な変数命名を使用し、マジックナンバーを避け、xUnit を使用してテスト駆動開発を行い、SOLID 原則の遵守を確保します。","ko":"에이전트가 `dotnet`과 같은 CLI 도구를 사용하여 확장 가능한 .NET 애플리케이션을 개발할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 최고의 관행을 따르고 설명적인 변수 이름을 사용하며 마법숫자를 피하고 xUnit을 사용하여 테스트 주도 개발을 수행하며 SOLID 원칙을 준수합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes desarrollar aplicaciones .NET escalables utilizando herramientas de CLI como `dotnet`, siguiendo las mejores prácticas con nombres de variables descriptivos y evitando números mágicos, mientras aprovecha xUnit para el desarrollo dirigido por pruebas y garantiza el cumplimiento de los principios SOLID.","fr":"Permet aux agents de développer des applications .NET évolutives en utilisant des outils CLI tels que `dotnet`, en suivant les meilleures pratiques avec une dénomination de variables descriptive et en évitant les nombres magiques, tout en exploitant xUnit pour le développement piloté par les tests et en garantissant le respect des principes SOLID.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, skalierbare .NET-Anwendungen mithilfe von CLI-Tools wie `dotnet` zu entwickeln, indem sie bewährte Verfahren mit beschreibenden Variablenbezeichnungen und der Vermeidung von Magischen Zahlen befolgen und xUnit für testgetriebene Entwicklung nutzen und die Einhaltung der SOLID-Prinzipien sicherstellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a desenvolver aplicações .NET escaláveis usando ferramentas CLI como `dotnet`, seguindo as melhores práticas com nomes de variáveis descritivos e evitando números mágicos, ao mesmo tempo em que aproveita o xUnit para desenvolvimento orientado a testes e garantindo a aderência aos princípios SOLID.","ru":"Позволяет агентам разрабатывать масштабируемые приложения .NET, используя инструменты CLI, такие как `dotnet`, следуя лучшим практикам с описательными именами переменных и избегая магических чисел, а также использует xUnit для разработки, ориентированной на тестирование, и обеспечивает соблюдение принципов SOLID.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من تطوير تطبيقات .NET قابلة للتوسيع باستخدام أدوات CLI مثل `dotnet` ، متبعة أفضل الممارسات بأسماء متغيرات وصفية وتجنب الأرقام السحرية ، وفي الوقت نفسه يستفيد من xUnit لتطوير قائم على الاختبار وضمان الامتثال لمبدأ SOLID."},"useCases":{"en":["Developing scalable .NET applications","Implementing unit tests with xUnit","Integrating CLI tools for streamlined development"],"zh":["开发可扩展的 .NET 应用程序","使用 xUnit 实现单元测试","集成 CLI 工具以实现流畅的开发"],"ja":["拡張可能な .NET アプリケーションの開発","xUnit を使用したユニットテストの実装","CLI ツールの統合によるスムーズな開発"],"ko":["확장 가능한 .NET 애플리케이션 개발","xUnit을 사용한 유닛 테스트 구현","CLI 도구 통합을 통한 원활한 개발"],"es":["Desarrollar aplicaciones .NET escalables","Implementar pruebas unitarias con xUnit","Integrar herramientas de CLI para un desarrollo optimizado"],"fr":["Développer des applications .NET évolutives","Mettre en œuvre des tests unitaires avec xUnit","Intégrer des outils CLI pour un développement rationalisé"],"de":["Skalierbare .NET-Anwendungen entwickeln","Einheitliche Tests mit xUnit implementieren","CLI-Tools für ein optimiertes Entwicklung integrieren"],"pt":["Desenvolver aplicações .NET escaláveis","Implementar testes unitários com xUnit","Integrar ferramentas CLI para desenvolvimento otimizado"],"ru":["Разработка масштабируемых приложений .NET","Реализация модульных тестов с помощью xUnit","Интеграция инструментов CLI для оптимизированного развития"],"ar":["تطوير تطبيقات .NET قابلة للتوسيع","تنفيذ اختبارات الوحدة مع xUnit","دمج أدوات CLI لتطوير متسلسل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires .NET Core installation","xUnit testing framework dependency","Adherence to specific coding standards"],"zh":[".NET Core 安装要求","xUnit 测试框架依赖","特定编码标准的遵守"],"ja":[".NET Core のインストール要件","xUnit テストフレームワークの依存","特定のコーディング規約の遵守"],"ko":[".NET Core 설치 요구 사항","xUnit 테스트 프레임워크 종속성","특정 코딩 표준 준수"],"es":["Requiere instalación de .NET Core","Dependencia del marco de pruebas xUnit","Adhesión a normas de codificación específicas"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de .NET Core","Dépendance du framework de test xUnit","Adhésion à des normes de codage spécifiques"],"de":["Benötigt .NET Core-Installation","Abhängigkeit vom xUnit-Testframework","Einhaltung spezifischer Kodierungsstandards"],"pt":["Requer instalação do .NET Core","Dependência do framework de teste xUnit","Aderência a padrões de codificação específicos"],"ru":["Требуется установка .NET Core","Зависимость от фреймворка тестирования xUnit","Соблюдение конкретных стандартов кодирования"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت .NET Core","اعتماد إطار اختبار xUnit","امتثال لمعايير برمجة محددة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":20}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ShalomObongo/nanoclaw/add-telegram', 'community', 'ShalomObongo', 'nanoclaw', 'ShalomObongo/nanoclaw', 'add-telegram', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z', '2026-02-18T06:29:35.899Z', NULL, '{"id":"ShalomObongo/nanoclaw/add-telegram","name":"add-telegram","description":{"zh":"add-telegram技能为NanoClaw添加Telegram支持，提供多种消息传递方式","ja":"add-telegramスキルはNanoClawにTelegramサポートを追加し、複数のメッセージングオプションを提供します","ko":"add-telegram 스킬은 NanoClaw에 텔레그램 지원을 추가하여 여러 가지 메시지 전달 방식을 제공합니다","es":"Add-telegram es una habilidad que agrega soporte de Telegram a NanoClaw, permitiendo a los usuarios elegir entre diferentes modos de uso","fr":"Add-telegram est une compétence qui ajoute la prise en charge de Telegram à NanoClaw, permettant aux utilisateurs de choisir entre différents modes d''utilisation","de":"Add-telegram ist eine Fähigkeit, die die Unterstützung von Telegram zu NanoClaw hinzufügt, wodurch Benutzer zwischen verschiedenen Verwendungsmöglichkeiten wählen können","pt":"O skill add-telegram adiciona suporte ao Telegram ao NanoClaw, permitindo que os usuários escolham como utilizar o canal de mensagens","ru":"Навык add-telegram добавляет поддержку Telegram в NanoClaw, позволяя пользователям выбирать, как использовать канал обмена сообщениями","ar":"مهارة add-telegram تضيف دعم Telegram إلى NanoClaw، مما يسمح للمستخدمين باختيار كيفية استخدام قناة المراسلة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"添加Telegram支持 - NanoClaw","ja":"Telegramを追加する - NanoClaw","ko":"텔레그램 지원 추가 - NanoClaw","es":"Agregar soporte de Telegram con add-telegram","fr":"Ajouter la prise en charge de Telegram avec add-telegram","de":"Telegram-Unterstützung mit add-telegram hinzufügen","pt":"Adicione Suporte ao Telegram com o Skill add-telegram","ru":"Добавьте поддержку Telegram с помощью навыка add-telegram","ar":"أضف دعم Telegram باستخدام مهارة add-telegram","en":"add-telegram"},"description":{"zh":"add-telegram技能为NanoClaw添加Telegram支持，提供多种消息传递方式","ja":"add-telegramスキルはNanoClawにTelegramサポートを追加し、複数のメッセージングオプションを提供します","ko":"add-telegram 스킬은 NanoClaw에 텔레그램 지원을 추가하여 여러 가지 메시지 전달 방식을 제공합니다","es":"Add-telegram es una habilidad que agrega soporte de Telegram a NanoClaw, permitiendo a los usuarios elegir entre diferentes modos de uso","fr":"Add-telegram est une compétence qui ajoute la prise en charge de Telegram à NanoClaw, permettant aux utilisateurs de choisir entre différents modes d''utilisa...","de":"Add-telegram ist eine Fähigkeit, die die Unterstützung von Telegram zu NanoClaw hinzufügt, wodurch Benutzer zwischen verschiedenen Verwendungsmöglichkeiten w...","pt":"O skill add-telegram adiciona suporte ao Telegram ao NanoClaw, permitindo que os usuários escolham como utilizar o canal de mensagens","ru":"Навык add-telegram добавляет поддержку Telegram в NanoClaw, позволяя пользователям выбирать, как использовать канал обмена сообщениями","ar":"مهارة add-telegram تضيف دعم Telegram إلى NanoClaw، مما يسمح للمستخدمين باختيار كيفية استخدام قناة المراسلة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["替换WhatsApp","与WhatsApp同时使用","控制频道","通知频道"],"ja":["WhatsAppの置き換え","WhatsAppと同時に使用","コントロールチャンネル","通知チャンネル"],"ko":["WhatsApp 대체","WhatsApp와 함께 사용","제어 채널","알림 채널"],"es":["Reemplazar WhatsApp como canal de mensajería","Agregar Telegram como canal de mensajería adicional","Controlar el canal de Telegram","Recibir notificaciones a través de Telegram"],"fr":["Remplacer WhatsApp par Telegram comme canal de messagerie","Ajouter Telegram comme canal de messagerie supplémentaire","Contrôler le canal Telegram","Recevoir des notifications via Telegram"],"de":["WhatsApp als Nachrichtenkanal ersetzen","Telegram als zusätzlichen Nachrichtenkanal hinzufügen","Telegram-Kanal steuern","Benachrichtigungen über Telegram erhalten"],"pt":["Substitui o WhatsApp como canal de mensagens","Adiciona o Telegram como canal de mensagens adicional","Controla o canal de mensagens","Recebe notificações limitadas"],"ru":["Заменяет WhatsApp в качестве канала обмена сообщениями","Добавляет Telegram в качестве дополнительного канала обмена сообщениями","Контролирует канал обмена сообщениями","Получает ограниченные уведомления"],"ar":["يستبدل WhatsApp كقناة مراسلة","يضيف Telegram كقناة مراسلة إضافية","يحكم قناة المراسلة","يستلم إشعارات محدودة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["NanoClaw","Telegram","add-telegram","消息传递","WhatsApp","Grammy"],"ja":["NanoClaw","Telegram","add-telegram","メッセージング","WhatsApp","Grammy"],"ko":["NanoClaw","텔레그램","add-telegram","메시지 전달","WhatsApp","Grammy"],"es":["add-telegram","Telegram","NanoClaw","integración de Telegram","desarrollo de chatbots","canal de mensajería","Grammy","TypeScript"],"fr":["add-telegram","Telegram","NanoClaw","intégration de Telegram","développement de chatbots","canal de messagerie","Grammy","TypeScript"],"de":["add-telegram","Telegram","NanoClaw","Telegram-Integration","Chatbot-Entwicklung","Nachrichtenkanal","Grammy","TypeScript"],"pt":["skill add-telegram","suporte ao Telegram","NanoClaw","canal de mensagens","desenvolvimento de aplicativos","Telegram bot"],"ru":["навык add-telegram","поддержка Telegram","NanoClaw","канал обмена сообщениями","разработка приложений","бот Telegram"],"ar":["مهارة add-telegram","دعم Telegram","NanoClaw","قناة المراسلة","تطوير التطبيقات","бот Telegram"]}},"owner":"ShalomObongo","repo":"nanoclaw","repoPath":"ShalomObongo/nanoclaw","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"add-telegram","description":"Add Telegram as a channel. Can replace WhatsApp entirely or run alongside it. Also configurable as a control-only channel (triggers actions) or passive channel (receives notifications only).","bodyPreview":"# Add Telegram Channel\n\nThis skill adds Telegram support to NanoClaw. Users can choose to:\n\n1. **Replace WhatsApp** - Use Telegram as the only messaging channel\n2. **Add alongside WhatsApp** - Both channels active\n3. **Control channel** - Telegram triggers agent but doesn''t receive all outputs\n4. **Notification channel** - Receives outputs but limited triggering\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n### 1. Install Grammy\n\n```bash\nnpm install grammy\n```\n\nGrammy is a modern, TypeScript-first Telegram bot framework.","body":"# Add Telegram Channel\n\nThis skill adds Telegram support to NanoClaw. Users can choose to:\n\n1. **Replace WhatsApp** - Use Telegram as the only messaging channel\n2. **Add alongside WhatsApp** - Both channels active\n3. **Control channel** - Telegram triggers agent but doesn''t receive all outputs\n4. **Notification channel** - Receives outputs but limited triggering\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n### 1. Install Grammy\n\n```bash\nnpm install grammy\n```\n\nGrammy is a modern, TypeScript-first Telegram bot framework.\n\n### 2. Create Telegram Bot\n\nTell the user:\n\n> I need you to create a Telegram bot:\n>\n> 1. Open Telegram and search for `@BotFather`\n> 2. Send `/newbot` and follow prompts:\n>    - Bot name: Something friendly (e.g., \"Andy Assistant\")\n>    - Bot username: Must end with \"bot\" (e.g., \"andy_ai_bot\")\n> 3. Copy the bot token (looks like `123456:ABC-DEF1234ghIkl-zyx57W2v1u123ew11`)\n\nWait for user to provide the token.\n\n### 3. Get Chat ID\n\nTell the user:\n\n> To register a chat, you need its Chat ID. Here''s how:\n>\n> **For Private Chat (DM with bot):**\n> 1. Search for your bot in Telegram\n> 2. Start a chat and send any message\n> 3. I''ll add a `/chatid` command to help you get the ID\n>\n> **For Group Chat:**\n> 1. Add your bot to the group\n> 2. Send any message\n> 3. Use the `/chatid` command in the group\n\n### 4. Disable Group Privacy (for group chats)\n\nTell the user:\n\n> **Important for group chats**: By default, Telegram bots in groups only receive messages that @mention the bot or are commands. To let the bot see all messages (needed for `requiresTrigger: false` or trigger-word detection):\n>\n> 1. Open Telegram and search for `@BotFather`\n> 2. Send `/mybots` and select your bot\n> 3. Go to **Bot Settings** > **Group Privacy**\n> 4. Select **Turn off**\n>\n> Without this, the bot will only see messages that directly @mention it.\n\nThis step is optional if the user only wants trigger-based responses via @mentioning the bot.\n\n## Questions to Ask\n\nBefore making changes, ask:\n\n1. **Mode**: Replace WhatsApp or add alongside it?\n   - If replace: Set `TELEGRAM_ONLY=true`\n   - If alongside: Both will run\n\n2. **Chat behavior**: Should this chat respond to all messages or only when @mentioned?\n   - Main chat: Responds to all (set `requiresTrigger: false`)\n   - Other chats: Default requires trigger (`requiresTrigger: true`)\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Step 1: Update Configuration\n\nRead `src/config.ts` and add Telegram config exports:\n\n```typescript\nexport const TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN = process.env.TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN || \"\";\nexport const TELEGRAM_ONLY = process.env.TELEGRAM_ONLY === \"true\";\n```\n\nThese should be added near the top with other configuration exports.\n\n### Step 2: Add storeMessageDirect to Database\n\nRead `src/db.ts` and add this function (place it near the `storeMessage` function):\n\n```typescript\n/**\n * Store a message directly (for non-WhatsApp channels that don''t use Baileys proto).\n */\nexport function storeMessageDirect(msg: {\n  id: string;\n  chat_jid: string;\n  sender: string;\n  sender_name: string;\n  content: string;\n  timestamp: string;\n  is_from_me: boolean;\n}): void {\n  db.prepare(\n    `INSERT OR REPLACE INTO messages (id, chat_jid, sender, sender_name, content, timestamp, is_from_me) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)`,\n  ).run(\n    msg.id,\n    msg.chat_jid,\n    msg.sender,\n    msg.sender_name,\n    msg.content,\n    msg.timestamp,\n    msg.is_from_me ? 1 : 0,\n  );\n}\n```\n\nThis uses the existing `db` instance from `db.ts`. No additional imports needed.\n\n### Step 3: Create Telegram Module\n\nCreate `src/telegram.ts`. The Telegram module is a thin layer that stores incoming messages to the database. It does NOT call the agent directly — the existing `startMessageLoop()` in `src/index.ts` polls all registered group JIDs and picks up Telegram messages automatically.\n\n```typescript\nimport { Bot } from \"grammy\";\nimport {\n  ASSISTANT_NAME,\n  TRIGGER_PATTERN,\n} from \"./config.js\";\nimport {\n  getAllRegisteredGroups,\n  storeChatMetadata,\n  storeMessageDirect,\n} from \"./db.js\";\nimport { logger } from \"./logger.js\";\n\nlet bot: Bot | null = null;\n\n/** Store a placeholder message for non-text content (photos, voice, etc.) */\nfunction storeNonTextMessage(ctx: any, placeholder: string): void {\n  const chatId = `tg:${ctx.chat.id}`;\n  const registeredGroups = getAllRegisteredGroups();\n  if (!registeredGroups[chatId]) return;\n\n  const timestamp = new Date(ctx.message.date * 1000).toISOString();\n  const senderName =\n    ctx.from?.first_name || ctx.from?.username || ctx.from?.id?.toString() || \"Unknown\";\n  const caption = ctx.message.caption ? ` ${ctx.message.caption}` : \"\";\n\n  storeChatMetadata(chatId, timestamp);\n  storeMessageDirect({\n    id: ctx.message.message_id.toString(),\n    chat_jid: chatId,\n    sender: ctx.from?.id?.toString() || \"\",\n    sender_name: senderName,\n    content: `${placeholder}${caption}`,\n    timestamp,\n    is_from_me: false,\n  });\n}\n\nexport async function connectTelegram(botToken: string): Promise<void> {\n  bot = new Bot(botToken);\n\n  // Command to get chat ID (useful for registration)\n  bot.command(\"chatid\", (ctx) => {\n    const chatId = ctx.chat.id;\n    const chatType = ctx.chat.type;\n    const chatName =\n      chatType === \"private\"\n        ? ctx.from?.first_name || \"Private\"\n        : (ctx.chat as any).title || \"Unknown\";\n\n    ctx.reply(\n      `Chat ID: \\`tg:${chatId}\\`\\nName: ${chatName}\\nType: ${chatType}`,\n      { parse_mode: \"Markdown\" },\n    );\n  });\n\n  // Command to check bot status\n  bot.command(\"ping\", (ctx) => {\n    ctx.reply(`${ASSISTANT_NAME} is online.`);\n  });\n\n  bot.on(\"message:text\", async (ctx) => {\n    // Skip commands\n    if (ctx.message.text.startsWith(\"/\")) return;\n\n    const chatId = `tg:${ctx.chat.id}`;\n    let content = ctx.message.text;\n    const timestamp = new Date(ctx.message.date * 1000).toISOString();\n    const senderName =\n      ctx.from?.first_name ||\n      ctx.from?.username ||\n      ctx.from?.id.toString() ||\n      \"Unknown\";\n    const sender = ctx.from?.id.toString() || \"\";\n    const msgId = ctx.message.message_id.toString();\n\n    // Determine chat name\n    const chatName =\n      ctx.chat.type === \"private\"\n        ? senderName\n        : (ctx.chat as any).title || chatId;\n\n    // Translate Telegram @bot_username mentions into TRIGGER_PATTERN format.\n    // Telegram @mentions (e.g., @andy_ai_bot) won''t match TRIGGER_PATTERN\n    // (e.g., ^@Andy\\b), so we prepend the trigger when the bot is @mentioned.\n    const botUsername = ctx.me?.username?.toLowerCase();\n    if (botUsername) {\n      const entities = ctx.message.entities || [];\n      const isBotMentioned = entities.some((entity) => {\n        if (entity.type === \"mention\") {\n          const mentionText = content\n            .substring(entity.offset, entity.offset + entity.length)\n            .toLowerCase();\n          return mentionText === `@${botUsername}`;\n        }\n        return false;\n      });\n      if (isBotMentioned && !TRIGGER_PATTERN.test(content)) {\n        content = `@${ASSISTANT_NAME} ${content}`;\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Store chat metadata for discovery\n    storeChatMetadata(chatId, timestamp, chatName);\n\n    // Check if this chat is registered\n    const registeredGroups = getAllRegisteredGroups();\n    const group = registeredGroups[chatId];\n\n    if (!group) {\n      logger.debug(\n        { chatId, chatName },\n        \"Message from unregistered Telegram chat\",\n      );\n      return;\n    }\n\n    // Store message — startMessageLoop() will pick it up\n    storeMessageDirect({\n      id: msgId,\n      chat_jid: chatId,\n      sender,\n      sender_name: senderName,\n      content,\n      timestamp,\n      is_from_me: false,\n    });\n\n    logger.info(\n      { chatId, chatName, sender: senderName },\n      \"Telegram message stored\",\n    );\n  });\n\n  // Handle non-text messages with placeholders so the agent knows something was sent\n  bot.on(\"message:photo\", (ctx) => storeNonTextMessage(ctx, \"[Photo]\"));\n  bot.on(\"message:video\", (ctx) => storeNonTextMessage(ctx, \"[Video]\"));\n  bot.on(\"message:voice\", (ctx) => storeNonTextMessage(ctx, \"[Voice message]\"));\n  bot.on(\"message:audio\", (ctx) => storeNonTextMessage(ctx, \"[Audio]\"));\n  bot.on(\"message:document\", (ctx) => {\n    const name = ctx.message.document?.file_name || \"file\";\n    storeNonTextMessage(ctx, `[Document: ${name}]`);\n  });\n  bot.on(\"message:sticker\", (ctx) => {\n    const emoji = ctx.message.sticker?.emoji || \"\";\n    storeNonTextMessage(ctx, `[Sticker ${emoji}]`);\n  });\n  bot.on(\"message:location\", (ctx) => storeNonTextMessage(ctx, \"[Location]\"));\n  bot.on(\"message:contact\", (ctx) => storeNonTextMessage(ctx, \"[Contact]\"));\n\n  // Handle errors gracefully\n  bot.catch((err) => {\n    logger.error({ err: err.message }, \"Telegram bot error\");\n  });\n\n  // Start polling\n  bot.start({\n    onStart: (botInfo) => {\n      logger.info(\n        { username: botInfo.username, id: botInfo.id },\n        \"Telegram bot connected\",\n      );\n      console.log(`\\n  Telegram bot: @${botInfo.username}`);\n      console.log(\n        `  Send /chatid to the bot to get a chat''s registration ID\\n`,\n      );\n    },\n  });\n}\n\nexport async function sendTelegramMessage(\n  chatId: string,\n  text: string,\n): Promise<void> {\n  if (!bot) {\n    logger.warn(\"Telegram bot not initialized\");\n    return;\n  }\n\n  try {\n    const numericId = chatId.replace(/^tg:/, \"\");\n\n    // Telegram has a 4096 character limit per message — split if needed\n    const MAX_LENGTH = 4096;\n    if (text.length <= MAX_LENGTH) {\n      await bot.api.sendMessage(numericId, text);\n    } else {\n      for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i += MAX_LENGTH) {\n        await bot.api.sendMessage(numericId, text.slice(i, i + MAX_LENGTH));\n      }\n    }\n    logger.info({ chatId, length: text.length }, \"Telegram message sent\");\n  } catch (err) {\n    logger.error({ chatId, err }, \"Failed to send Telegram message\");\n  }\n}\n\nexport async function setTelegramTyping(chatId: string): Promise<void> {\n  if (!bot) return;\n  try {\n    const numericId = chatId.replace(/^tg:/, \"\");\n    await bot.api.sendChatAction(numericId, \"typing\");\n  } catch (err) {\n    logger.debug({ chatId, err }, \"Failed to send Telegram typing indicator\");\n  }\n}\n\nexport function isTelegramConnected(): boolean {\n  return bot !== null;\n}\n\nexport function stopTelegram(): void {\n  if (bot) {\n    bot.stop();\n    bot = null;\n    logger.info(\"Telegram bot stopped\");\n  }\n}\n```\n\nKey differences from WhatsApp message handling:\n- No `onMessage` callback — messages are stored to DB and the existing message loop picks them up\n- Registration check uses `getAllRegisteredGroups()` from `db.ts` directly\n- Trigger matching is handled by `startMessageLoop()` / `processGroupMessages()`, not the Telegram module\n\n### Step 4: Update Main Application\n\nModify `src/index.ts`:\n\n1. **Add imports** at the top:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  connectTelegram,\n  sendTelegramMessage,\n  setTelegramTyping,\n  stopTelegram,\n} from \"./telegram.js\";\nimport { TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, TELEGRAM_ONLY } from \"./config.js\";\n```\n\n2. **Update `sendMessage` function** to route Telegram messages. Find the `sendMessage` function and add a `tg:` prefix check before the WhatsApp path:\n\n```typescript\nasync function sendMessage(jid: string, text: string): Promise<void> {\n  // Route Telegram messages directly (no outgoing queue needed)\n  if (jid.startsWith(\"tg:\")) {\n    await sendTelegramMessage(jid, text);\n    return;\n  }\n\n  // WhatsApp path (with outgoing queue for reconnection)\n  if (!waConnected) {\n    outgoingQueue.push({ jid, text });\n    logger.info({ jid, length: text.length, queueSize: outgoingQueue.length }, ''WA disconnected, message queued'');\n    return;\n  }\n  try {\n    await sock.sendMessage(jid, { text });\n    logger.info({ jid, length: text.length }, ''Message sent'');\n  } catch (err) {\n    outgoingQueue.push({ jid, text });\n    logger.warn({ jid, err, queueSize: outgoingQueue.length }, ''Failed to send, message queued'');\n  }\n}\n```\n\n3. **Update `setTyping` function** to route Telegram typing indicators:\n\n```typescript\nasync function setTyping(jid: string, isTyping: boolean): Promise<void> {\n  if (jid.startsWith(\"tg:\")) {\n    if (isTyping) await setTelegramTyping(jid);\n    return;\n  }\n  try {\n    await sock.sendPresenceUpdate(isTyping ? ''composing'' : ''paused'', jid);\n  } catch (err) {\n    logger.debug({ jid, err }, ''Failed to update typing status'');\n  }\n}\n```\n\n4. **Update `main()` function**. Add Telegram startup before `connectWhatsApp()` and wrap WhatsApp in a `TELEGRAM_ONLY` check:\n\n```typescript\nasync function main(): Promise<void> {\n  ensureContainerSystemRunning();\n  initDatabase();\n  logger.info(''Database initialized'');\n  loadState();\n\n  // Graceful shutdown handlers\n  const shutdown = async (signal: string) => {\n    logger.info({ signal }, ''Shutdown signal received'');\n    stopTelegram();\n    await queue.shutdown(10000);\n    process.exit(0);\n  };\n  process.on(''SIGTERM'', () => shutdown(''SIGTERM''));\n  process.on(''SIGINT'', () => shutdown(''SIGINT''));\n\n  // Start Telegram bot if configured (independent of WhatsApp)\n  const hasTelegram = !!TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN;\n  if (hasTelegram) {\n    await connectTelegram(TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN);\n  }\n\n  if (!TELEGRAM_ONLY) {\n    await connectWhatsApp();\n  } else {\n    // Telegram-only mode: start all services that WhatsApp''s connection.open normally starts\n    startSchedulerLoop({\n      registeredGroups: () => registeredGroups,\n      getSessions: () => sessions,\n      queue,\n      onProcess: (groupJid, proc, containerName, groupFolder) =>\n        queue.registerProcess(groupJid, proc, containerName, groupFolder),\n      sendMessage,\n      assistantName: ASSISTANT_NAME,\n    });\n    startIpcWatcher();\n    queue.setProcessMessagesFn(processGroupMessages);\n    recoverPendingMessages();\n    startMessageLoop();\n    logger.info(\n      `NanoClaw running (Telegram-only, trigger: @${ASSISTANT_NAME})`,\n    );\n  }\n}\n```\n\nNote: When running alongside WhatsApp, the `connection.open` handler in `connectWhatsApp()` already starts the scheduler, IPC watcher, queue, and message loop — no duplication needed.\n\n5. **Update `getAvailableGroups` function** to include Telegram chats. The current filter only shows WhatsApp groups (`@g.us`). Update it to also include `tg:` chats so the agent can discover and register Telegram chats via IPC:\n\n```typescript\nfunction getAvailableGroups(): AvailableGroup[] {\n  const chats = getAllChats();\n  const registeredJids = new Set(Object.keys(registeredGroups));\n\n  return chats\n    .filter((c) => c.jid !== ''__group_sync__'' && (c.jid.endsWith(''@g.us'') || c.jid.startsWith(''tg:'')))\n    .map((c) => ({\n      jid: c.jid,\n      name: c.name,\n      lastActivity: c.last_message_time,\n      isRegistered: registeredJids.has(c.jid),\n    }));\n}\n```\n\n### Step 5: Update Environment\n\nAdd to `.env`:\n\n```bash\nTELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=YOUR_BOT_TOKEN_HERE\n\n# Optional: Set to \"true\" to disable WhatsApp entirely\n# TELEGRAM_ONLY=true\n```\n\n**Important**: After modifying `.env`, sync to the container environment:\n\n```bash\ncp .env data/env/env\n```\n\nThe container reads environment from `data/env/env`, not `.env` directly.\n\n### Step 6: Register a Telegram Chat\n\nAfter installing and starting the bot, tell the user:\n\n> 1. Send `/chatid` to your bot (in private chat or in a group)\n> 2. Copy the chat ID (e.g., `tg:123456789` or `tg:-1001234567890`)\n> 3. I''ll register it for you\n\nRegistration uses the `registerGroup()` function in `src/index.ts`, which writes to SQLite and creates the group folder structure. Call it like this (or add a one-time script):\n\n```typescript\n// For private chat (main group):\nregisterGroup(\"tg:123456789\", {\n  name: \"Personal\",\n  folder: \"main\",\n  trigger: `@${ASSISTANT_NAME}`,\n  added_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n  requiresTrigger: false, // main group responds to all messages\n});\n\n// For group chat (note negative ID for Telegram groups):\nregisterGroup(\"tg:-1001234567890\", {\n  name: \"My Telegram Group\",\n  folder: \"telegram-group\",\n  trigger: `@${ASSISTANT_NAME}`,\n  added_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n  requiresTrigger: true, // only respond when triggered\n});\n```\n\nThe `RegisteredGroup` type requires a `trigger` string field and has an optional `requiresTrigger` boolean (defaults to `true`). Set `requiresTrigger: false` for chats that should respond to all messages.\n\nAlternatively, if the agent is already running in the main group, it can register new groups via IPC using the `register_group` task type.\n\n### Step 7: Build and Restart\n\n```bash\nnpm run build\nlaunchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.nanoclaw\n```\n\nOr for systemd:\n\n```bash\nnpm run build\nsystemctl --user restart nanoclaw\n```\n\n### Step 8: Test\n\nTell the user:\n\n> Send a message to your registered Telegram chat:\n> - For main chat: Any message works\n> - For non-main: `@Andy hello` or @mention the bot\n>\n> Check logs: `tail -f logs/nanoclaw.log`\n\n## Replace WhatsApp Entirely\n\nIf user wants Telegram-only:\n\n1. Set `TELEGRAM_ONLY=true` in `.env`\n2. Run `cp .env data/env/env` to sync to container\n3. The WhatsApp connection code is automatically skipped\n4. All services (scheduler, IPC watcher, queue, message loop) start independently\n5. Optionally remove `@whiskeysockets/baileys` dependency (but it''s harmless to keep)\n\n## Features\n\n### Chat ID Formats\n\n- **WhatsApp**: `120363336345536173@g.us` (groups) or `1234567890@s.whatsapp.net` (DM)\n- **Telegram**: `tg:123456789` (positive for private) or `tg:-1001234567890` (negative for groups)\n\n### Trigger Options\n\nThe bot responds when:\n1. Chat has `requiresTrigger: false` in its registration (e.g., main group)\n2. Bot is @mentioned in Telegram (translated to TRIGGER_PATTERN automatically)\n3. Message matches TRIGGER_PATTERN directly (e.g., starts with @Andy)\n\nTelegram @mentions (e.g., `@andy_ai_bot`) are automatically translated: if the bot is @mentioned and the message doesn''t already match TRIGGER_PATTERN, the trigger prefix is prepended before storing. This ensures @mentioning the bot always triggers a response.\n\n**Group Privacy**: The bot must have Group Privacy disabled in BotFather to see non-mention messages in groups. See Prerequisites step 4.\n\n### Commands\n\n- `/chatid` - Get chat ID for registration\n- `/ping` - Check if bot is online\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Bot not responding\n\nCheck:\n1. `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` is set in `.env` AND synced to `data/env/env`\n2. Chat is registered in SQLite (check with: `sqlite3 store/messages.db \"SELECT * FROM registered_groups WHERE jid LIKE ''tg:%''\"`)\n3. For non-main chats: message includes trigger pattern\n4. Service is running: `launchctl list | grep nanoclaw`\n\n### Bot only responds to @mentions in groups\n\nThe bot has Group Privacy enabled (default). It can only see messages that @mention it or are commands. To fix:\n1. Open `@BotFather` in Telegram\n2. `/mybots` > select bot > **Bot Settings** > **Group Privacy** > **Turn off**\n3. Remove and re-add the bot to the group (required for the change to take effect)\n\n### Getting chat ID\n\nIf `/chatid` doesn''t work:\n- Verify bot token is valid: `curl -s \"https://api.telegram.org/bot${TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN}/getMe\"`\n- Check bot is started: `tail -f logs/nanoclaw.log`\n\n### Service conflicts\n\nIf running `npm run dev` while launchd service is active:\n```bash\nlaunchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.nanoclaw.plist\nnpm run dev\n# When done testing:\nlaunchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.nanoclaw.plist\n```\n\n## Agent Swarms (Teams)\n\nAfter completing the Telegram setup, ask the user:\n\n> Would you like to add Agent Swarm support? Without it, Agent Teams still work — they just operate behind the scenes. With Swarm support, each subagent appears as a different bot in the Telegram group so you can see who''s saying what and have interactive team sessions.\n\nIf they say yes, invoke the `/add-telegram-swarm` skill.\n\n## Removal\n\nTo remove Telegram integration:\n\n1. Delete `src/telegram.ts`\n2. Remove Telegram imports from `src/index.ts`\n3. Remove `sendTelegramMessage` / `setTelegramTyping` routing from `sendMessage()` and `setTyping()` functions\n4. Remove `connectTelegram()` / `stopTelegram()` calls from `main()`\n5. Remove `TELEGRAM_ONLY` conditional in `main()`\n6. Revert `getAvailableGroups()` filter to only include `@g.us` chats\n7. Remove `storeMessageDirect` from `src/db.ts`\n8. Remove Telegram config (`TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`, `TELEGRAM_ONLY`) from `src/config.ts`\n9. Remove Telegram registrations from SQLite: `sqlite3 store/messages.db \"DELETE FROM registered_groups WHERE jid LIKE ''tg:%''\"`\n10. Uninstall: `npm uninstall grammy`\n11. Rebuild: `npm run build && launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.nanoclaw`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:29:35.899Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Multi-Channel Agents seeking to integrate Telegram messaging capabilities alongside or instead of WhatsApp.","zh":"适合于寻求将Telegram消息功能与WhatsApp一起或取代WhatsApp的多渠道代理商。","ja":"WhatsAppと並んで、または代わりにTelegramのメッセージング機能を統合したいマルチチャネルエージェントに最適です。","ko":"WhatsApp와 함께 또는 대신 Telegram 메시징 기능을 통합하려는 멀티 채널 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de varios canales que buscan integrar capacidades de mensajería de Telegram junto con o en lugar de WhatsApp.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents à plusieurs canaux qui cherchent à intégrer les capacités de messagerie Telegram aux côtés de ou au lieu de WhatsApp.","de":"Ideal für Multi-Channel-Agents, die Telegram-Messaging-Funktionen neben oder anstelle von WhatsApp integrieren möchten.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Multi-Canal que buscam integrar capacidades de mensagens do Telegram ao lado ou em vez do WhatsApp.","ru":"Идеально для Многоканальных Агентов, стремящихся интегрировать возможности обмена сообщениями Telegram наряду или вместо WhatsApp.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء متعددة القنوات الذين يسعون إلى دمج قدرات مراسلة Telegram جنبًا إلى جنب أو بدلاً من WhatsApp."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage the Grammy Telegram bot framework, enabling advanced messaging channel control, including replacing, adding, or limiting channel functionality, all while utilizing TypeScript-first development.","zh":"赋予代理商利用Grammy Telegram机器人框架的能力，实现高级消息通道控制，包括替换、添加或限制通道功能，同时利用TypeScript第一开发。","ja":"Grammy Telegramボットフレームワークを利用することで、エージェントは高度なメッセージチャネルコントロールを実現でき、チャネル機能の置き換え、追加、または制限を行うことができ、TypeScript第一開発を利用します。","ko":"Grammy Telegram 봇 프레임워크를 활용하여 에이전트가 고급 메시지 채널 제어를 가능하게 하며, 채널 기능의 교체, 추가 또는 제한을 수행할 수 있으며, TypeScript 첫 개발을 활용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes aprovechar el marco de trabajo de bot de Grammy Telegram, lo que permite un control avanzado del canal de mensajería, incluida la sustitución, adición o limitación de la funcionalidad del canal, todo mientras se utiliza el desarrollo de TypeScript en primer lugar.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exploiter le cadre de bot Grammy Telegram, ce qui permet un contrôle avancé du canal de messagerie, y compris le remplacement, l''ajout ou la limitation de la fonctionnalité du canal, le tout en utilisant le développement TypeScript en premier lieu.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, das Grammy-Telegram-Bot-Framework zu nutzen, wodurch ein erweitertes Messaging-Kanal-Steuerung ermöglicht wird, einschließlich Ersetzen, Hinzufügen oder Einschränken der Kanalfunktionalität, und all dies während der Verwendung von TypeScript-First-Entwicklung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aproveitar o framework de bot do Telegram Grammy, permitindo controle avançado do canal de mensagens, incluindo substituir, adicionar ou limitar a funcionalidade do canal, tudo isso utilizando o desenvolvimento TypeScript-first.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью использовать фреймворк Telegram-бота Grammy, обеспечивающий расширенный контроль над каналом обмена сообщениями, включая замену, добавление или ограничение функциональности канала, все это при использовании разработки на основе TypeScript.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من الاستفادة من إطار عمل.bot Grammy لبرامج Telegram، مما يتيح التحكم المتقدم في قناة المراسلة، بما في ذلك استبدال أو إضافة أو تقييد وظائف القناة، وكل ذلك باستخدام التطوير من النوع الأول TypeScript."},"useCases":{"en":["Replacing WhatsApp with Telegram for unified messaging","Adding Telegram alongside WhatsApp for multi-channel support","Controlling agent triggers through Telegram without receiving all outputs","Setting up Telegram as a notification channel for selective output reception"],"zh":["用Telegram替换WhatsApp实现统一消息","在WhatsApp旁边添加Telegram以实现多渠道支持","通过Telegram控制代理商触发器而不接收所有输出","设置Telegram作为选择性输出接收的通知渠道"],"ja":["WhatsAppをTelegramに置き換えて統一メッセージングを実現する","WhatsAppの隣にTelegramを追加してマルチチャネルサポートを実現する","Telegramを介してエージェントトリガーを制御し、すべての出力を受信しない","Telegramを選択的出力受信の通知チャネルとして設定する"],"ko":["WhatsApp를 Telegram으로 대체하여 통일 메시징을 구현하는 것","WhatsApp旁에 Telegram을 추가하여 멀티 채널 지원을 구현하는 것","Telegram을 통해 에이전트 트리거를 제어하여 모든 출력을 받지 않는 것","Telegram을 선택적 출력 수신의 알림 채널로 설정하는 것"],"es":["Reemplazar WhatsApp con Telegram para la mensajería unificada","Agregar Telegram junto con WhatsApp para el soporte de varios canales","Controlar los disparadores de los agentes a través de Telegram sin recibir todas las salidas","Configurar Telegram como un canal de notificación para la recepción selectiva de salidas"],"fr":["Remplacer WhatsApp par Telegram pour la messagerie unifiée","Ajouter Telegram aux côtés de WhatsApp pour le support à plusieurs canaux","Contrôler les déclencheurs des agents via Telegram sans recevoir toutes les sorties","Configurer Telegram en tant que canal de notification pour la réception sélective des sorties"],"de":["WhatsApp durch Telegram für die einheitliche Messaging ersetzen","Telegram neben WhatsApp für die Unterstützung mehrerer Kanäle hinzufügen","Agenten-Trigger über Telegram steuern, ohne alle Ausgaben zu erhalten","Telegram als Benachrichtigungs-Kanal für die selektive Ausgaberezeption einrichten"],"pt":["Substituir o WhatsApp pelo Telegram para mensagens unificadas","Adicionar o Telegram ao lado do WhatsApp para suporte a vários canais","Controlar gatilhos de agente por meio do Telegram sem receber todas as saídas","Configurar o Telegram como um canal de notificação para recebimento de saída seletiva"],"ru":["Заменить WhatsApp на Telegram для унифицированных сообщений","Добавить Telegram наряду с WhatsApp для поддержки нескольких каналов","Контролировать триггеры агента через Telegram без получения всех выходных данных","Настроить Telegram в качестве канала уведомлений для выборочного приема выходных данных"],"ar":["استبدال WhatsApp بالبريد Telegram للمراسلات الموحدة","إضافة Telegram إلى جانب WhatsApp لدعم عدة قنوات","التحكم في محفزات الوكيل من خلال Telegram دون استلام جميع الإخراج","تكوين Telegram كقناة إعلامية لاستلام الإخراج الانتقائي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires installation of Grammy via npm","Dependent on Telegram bot framework capabilities and limitations"],"zh":["需要通过npm安装Grammy","依赖于Telegram机器人框架的能力和限制"],"ja":["npmを介してGrammyをインストールする必要がある","Telegramボットフレームワークの能力と制限に依存する"],"ko":["npm을 통해 Grammy를 설치해야 함","Telegram 봇 프레임워크의 능력과 제한에 의존함"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de Grammy a través de npm","Dependiente de las capacidades y limitaciones del marco de trabajo de bot de Telegram"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de Grammy via npm","Dépend des capacités et des limitations du cadre de bot Telegram"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation von Grammy über npm","Abhängig von den Fähigkeiten und Einschränkungen des Telegram-Bot-Frameworks"],"pt":["Exige a instalação do Grammy via npm","Dependente das capacidades e limitações do framework de bot do Telegram"],"ru":["Требует установки Grammy через npm","Зависит от возможностей и ограничений фреймворка Telegram-бота"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت Grammy من خلال npm","يعتمد على قدرات وقيود إطار عمل برامج Telegram"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
