","품질 게이트와 토큰 예산","감사 가능한 아티팩트","세맨틱 버ージョ닝","헬스 체크와 릴리즈 태그","포괄적인 모니터링"],"es":["Flujos de trabajo de despliegue de producción repeatibles","Puertas de calidad y presupuestos de tokens","Artículos auditables y versiones semánticas","Monitoreo exhaustivo y salud de la aplicación","Promoción de versiones validadas de staging a producción"],"fr":["Flux de travail de déploiement de production répétitifs","Portes de qualité et budgets de jetons","Artéfacts auditable et versions sémantiques","Monitoring exhaustif et santé de l''application","Promotion de versions validées de staging en production"],"de":["Wiederholbare Produktionsbereitstellungs-Workflows","Qualitätstore und Token-Budgets","Auditable Artefakte und semantische Versionen","Umfassendes Monitoring und Anwendungsgesundheit","Überführung von validierten Staging-Versionen in die Produktion"],"pt":["Fluxo de trabalho de implantação de produção","Desenvolvimento dirigido por especificações","Geração de versões semânticas","Verificação de validação de staging","Criação de tags de lançamento"],"ru":["Рабочий процесс развертывания в производство","Разработка на основе спецификаций","Управление семантическими версиями","Проверка валидации staging","Создание тегов выпуска"],"ar":["سير عمل نشر الإنتاج","تطوير مدفوع بالمواصفات","ادارة الإصدارات الدلالية","التحقق من صحة المراحل","إنشاء علامات الإصدار"]},"keywords":{"zh":["生产部署","Spec-Driven Development","Claude Code","质量门控","语义版本控制","健康检查","发布标签","综合监控"],"ja":["プロダクションデプロイメント","Spec-Driven Development","Claude Code","品質ゲート","セマンティックバージョニング","ヘルスチェック","リリースタグ","包括的な監視"],"ko":["생산 배포","Spec-Driven Development","Claude Code","품질 게이트","세맨틱 버ージョ닝","헬스 체크","릴리즈 태그","포괄적인 모니터링"],"es":["despliegue de producción","automatización de lanzamientos","Spec-Driven Development","Claude Code","versiones semánticas","monitoreo de aplicaciones"],"fr":["déploiement de production","automatisation des lancements","Spec-Driven Development","Claude Code","versions sémantiques","monitoring d''applications"],"de":["Produktionsbereitstellung","Automatisierung von Launches","Spec-Driven Development","Claude Code","semantische Versionen","Anwendungsüberwachung"],"pt":["implantação de produção","desenvolvimento dirigido por especificações","versões semânticas","validação de staging","tags de lançamento","fluxo de trabalho de implantação"],"ru":["развертывание в производство","разработка на основе спецификаций","семантические версии","валидация staging","теги выпуска","рабочий процесс развертывания"],"ar":["نشر الإنتاج","تطوير مدفوع بالمواصفات","الإصدارات الدلالية","التحقق من صحة المراحل","علامات الإصدار","سير عمل نشر"]}},"owner":"marcusgoll","repo":"Spec-Flow","repoPath":"marcusgoll/Spec-Flow","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.447Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"production-deployment-phase","description":"Executes production deployment workflow by promoting validated staging builds to production with semantic versioning, health checks, and release tagging. Use when running /ship-prod command, deploying to production after staging validation, or promoting staging builds to production environment.","bodyPreview":"<objective>\nExecute production deployment workflow by promoting validated staging builds to production with semantic versioning, health checks, release tagging, and comprehensive monitoring.\n</objective>\n\n<quick_start>\n<production_deployment_workflow>\n**Prerequisite-driven production promotion:**\n\n1. **Verify staging validation**: Check state.yaml manual_gates.staging_validation.status = approved\n2. **Bump semantic version**: Update package.json/version files (major.minor.patch)\n3. **Create rele","body":"<objective>\nExecute production deployment workflow by promoting validated staging builds to production with semantic versioning, health checks, release tagging, and comprehensive monitoring.\n</objective>\n\n<quick_start>\n<production_deployment_workflow>\n**Prerequisite-driven production promotion:**\n\n1. **Verify staging validation**: Check state.yaml manual_gates.staging_validation.status = approved\n2. **Bump semantic version**: Update package.json/version files (major.minor.patch)\n3. **Create release tag**: Tag git commit with new version\n4. **Deploy to production**: Push to production branch or trigger deployment\n5. **Run health checks**: Verify endpoints, databases, services operational\n6. **Generate ship report**: Document deployment artifacts and metadata\n7. **Monitor post-deploy**: Watch logs, metrics, alerts for 15-30 minutes\n\n**Example workflow:**\n\n```\nVerifying staging validation complete... ✅\nCurrent version: 2.6.0\nBump type: minor (new features added)\nNew version: 2.7.0\n\nCreating git tag v2.7.0... ✅\nPushing to production branch... ✅\nTriggering production deployment... ✅\n\nHealth checks:\n  API endpoints: 200 OK ✅\n  Database connections: healthy ✅\n  Cache: operational ✅\n  CDN: propagated ✅\n\nProduction deployment successful!\nRelease: https://github.com/user/repo/releases/tag/v2.7.0\nShip report: specs/NNN-slug/production-ship-report.md\n```\n\n</production_deployment_workflow>\n\n<trigger_conditions>\n**Auto-invoke when:**\n\n- `/ship-prod` command executed\n- User mentions \"deploy to production\", \"ship to prod\", \"production release\"\n- state.yaml shows current_phase: ship-prod\n\n**Prerequisites required:**\n\n- Staging validation approved (manual_gates.staging_validation.status = approved)\n- Rollback gate passed (quality_gates.rollback.status = passed)\n- Git repository has remote configured\n- Production deployment configuration exists\n  </trigger_conditions>\n  </quick_start>\n\n<workflow>\n<step_1_verify_staging>\n**1. Verify Staging Validation Complete**\n\nCheck workflow state for staging validation approval:\n\n```bash\n# Read workflow state\nSTATE_FILE=\"specs/$(ls -t specs/ | head -1)/state.yaml\"\n\nSTAGING_STATUS=$(grep -A2 \"staging_validation:\" \"$STATE_FILE\" | grep \"status:\" | awk ''{print $2}'')\n\nif [ \"$STAGING_STATUS\" != \"approved\" ]; then\n  echo \"❌ BLOCKED: Staging validation not approved\"\n  echo \"Current status: $STAGING_STATUS\"\n  echo \"Run: /validate-staging to complete manual validation\"\n  exit 1\nfi\n\necho \"✅ Staging validation approved\"\n```\n\n**Blocking conditions:**\n\n- Staging validation status ≠ approved\n- Rollback gate status ≠ passed\n- No staging deployment exists\n  </step_1_verify_staging>\n\n<step_2_bump_version>\n**2. Bump Semantic Version**\n\nDetermine version bump type and update version files:\n\n```bash\n# Read current version\nCURRENT_VERSION=$(node -p \"require(''./package.json'').version\")\n\n# Determine bump type from CHANGELOG or git commits\n# - major: Breaking changes\n# - minor: New features (backward compatible)\n# - patch: Bug fixes only\n\n# Use npm version or manual update\nnpm version minor -m \"chore: bump version to %s for production release\"\n\nNEW_VERSION=$(node -p \"require(''./package.json'').version\")\n\necho \"Version bumped: $CURRENT_VERSION → $NEW_VERSION\"\n```\n\n**Semantic versioning rules:**\n\n- **Major (X.0.0)**: Breaking changes, API contract changes\n- **Minor (0.X.0)**: New features, backward compatible\n- **Patch (0.0.X)**: Bug fixes, no new features\n\n**Files to update:**\n\n- package.json (version field)\n- CHANGELOG.md (unreleased → version section)\n- Any version constants in code\n  </step_2_bump_version>\n\n<step_3_create_release_tag>\n**3. Create Git Release Tag**\n\nTag the commit and push to remote:\n\n```bash\n# Create annotated tag\ngit tag -a \"v${NEW_VERSION}\" -m \"Release v${NEW_VERSION}\n\n$(sed -n \"/## \\[${NEW_VERSION}\\]/,/## \\[/p\" CHANGELOG.md | head -n -1)\"\n\n# Push tag to remote\ngit push origin \"v${NEW_VERSION}\"\n\necho \"✅ Tag created and pushed: v${NEW_VERSION}\"\n```\n\n**Tag format:**\n\n- Annotated tags required (not lightweight)\n- Prefix with \"v\" (e.g., v2.7.0)\n- Include CHANGELOG excerpt in tag message\n  </step_3_create_release_tag>\n\n<step_4_deploy_production>\n**4. Deploy to Production**\n\nTrigger production deployment based on deployment model:\n\n```bash\n# Model 1: Git push to production branch\ngit push origin main:production\n\n# Model 2: GitHub Actions deployment\ngh workflow run deploy-production.yml \\\n  -f version=\"${NEW_VERSION}\" \\\n  -f environment=production\n\n# Model 3: Direct deployment platform (Vercel, Netlify, etc.)\nvercel --prod --yes\n```\n\n**Deployment verification:**\n\n- Wait for deployment to complete\n- Check deployment platform status\n- Verify deployment ID/URL returned\n- Record deployment metadata\n  </step_4_deploy_production>\n\n<step_5_health_checks>\n**5. Run Production Health Checks**\n\nVerify all critical services operational:\n\n```bash\necho \"Running production health checks...\"\n\n# API endpoints\nfor ENDPOINT in /health /api/status /api/version; do\n  STATUS=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" \"https://production.example.com$ENDPOINT\")\n  if [ \"$STATUS\" = \"200\" ]; then\n    echo \"  ✅ $ENDPOINT: $STATUS OK\"\n  else\n    echo \"  ❌ $ENDPOINT: $STATUS FAILED\"\n    HEALTH_FAILED=true\n  fi\ndone\n\n# Database connectivity\n# (Run via deployment platform or SSH to production)\n\n# Cache/Redis\n# CDN propagation\n# Background jobs\n\nif [ \"$HEALTH_FAILED\" = \"true\" ]; then\n  echo \"❌ Health checks failed - initiate rollback\"\n  exit 1\nfi\n\necho \"✅ All health checks passed\"\n```\n\n**Critical checks:**\n\n- API endpoints return 200 OK\n- Database connections healthy\n- Cache/Redis operational\n- CDN serving latest assets\n- Background jobs processing\n  </step_5_health_checks>\n\n<step_6_generate_ship_report>\n**6. Generate Production Ship Report**\n\nCreate production-ship-report.md with deployment metadata:\n\n```bash\ncat > specs/$FEATURE_SLUG/production-ship-report.md <<EOF\n# Production Ship Report: $FEATURE_SLUG\n\n## Deployment Summary\n- **Version**: v${NEW_VERSION}\n- **Deployed at**: $(date -Iseconds)\n- **Deployment ID**: ${DEPLOYMENT_ID}\n- **Production URL**: https://production.example.com\n- **Release URL**: https://github.com/user/repo/releases/tag/v${NEW_VERSION}\n\n## Health Checks\n- API endpoints: ✅ All passing\n- Database: ✅ Healthy\n- Cache: ✅ Operational\n- CDN: ✅ Propagated\n\n## Deployment Artifacts\n- Git tag: v${NEW_VERSION}\n- Commit SHA: ${COMMIT_SHA}\n- Deployment platform: ${PLATFORM}\n\n## Rollback Procedure\n1. Revert git tag: git tag -d v${NEW_VERSION} && git push origin :refs/tags/v${NEW_VERSION}\n2. Deploy previous version: git push origin v${PREVIOUS_VERSION}:production\n3. Monitor health checks\nEOF\n\necho \"✅ Ship report generated\"\n```\n\n**Report contents:**\n\n- Deployment metadata (version, time, ID, URLs)\n- Health check results\n- Rollback procedure\n- Post-deployment monitoring plan\n  </step_6_generate_ship_report>\n\n<step_7_monitor_post_deploy>\n**7. Monitor Post-Deployment**\n\nWatch production for 15-30 minutes after deployment:\n\n```bash\necho \"Monitoring production (15-30 minutes)...\"\necho \"Watch for:\"\necho \"  - Error rate spikes\"\necho \"  - Performance degradation\"\necho \"  - User reports/support tickets\"\necho \"  - Background job failures\"\n\n# Monitor logs (varies by platform)\n# - Vercel: vercel logs --follow\n# - Heroku: heroku logs --tail\n# - AWS: CloudWatch logs\n# - Netlify: Netlify UI\n\necho \"Monitor dashboard: https://monitoring.example.com/dashboard\"\n```\n\n**Monitoring checklist:**\n\n- [ ] Error rates normal (<1% increase)\n- [ ] Response times acceptable (<10% degradation)\n- [ ] No critical alerts triggered\n- [ ] Background jobs processing normally\n- [ ] No user-reported issues in first 30 minutes\n\n**If issues detected:**\n\n1. Assess severity (critical vs minor)\n2. Initiate rollback if critical\n3. Apply hotfix if minor and fixable quickly\n4. Document incident for post-mortem\n   </step_7_monitor_post_deploy>\n   </workflow>\n\n<anti_patterns>\n**Avoid these production deployment mistakes:**\n\n<pitfall name=\"deploy_without_staging_validation\">\n**❌ Deploying to production before staging validation**\n```bash\n# BAD: Skip staging validation\n/ship-prod  # Staging not validated yet\n```\n**✅ Always verify staging validation approved**\n```bash\n# GOOD: Check workflow state first\ngrep -A2 \"staging_validation:\" state.yaml\n# Ensure status: approved before proceeding\n```\n**Impact**: Untested code reaches production, high risk of incidents\n</pitfall>\n\n<pitfall name=\"missing_rollback_verification\">\n**❌ Not verifying rollback procedure before deploy**\n```bash\n# BAD: Deploy without testing rollback\ngit push origin main:production\n# Hope rollback works if needed\n```\n**✅ Verify rollback gate passed**\n```bash\n# GOOD: Ensure rollback tested on staging\ngrep -A2 \"rollback:\" state.yaml | grep \"status: passed\"\n# Confidence that rollback works if needed\n```\n**Impact**: Unable to recover quickly if deployment fails\n</pitfall>\n\n<pitfall name=\"insufficient_health_checks\">\n**❌ Deploying without comprehensive health checks**\n```bash\n# BAD: Only check homepage\ncurl https://production.example.com/  # 200 OK, ship it!\n```\n**✅ Check all critical endpoints and services**\n```bash\n# GOOD: Verify API, database, cache, background jobs\ncurl /health && curl /api/status && check-db && check-redis\n```\n**Impact**: Silent failures in critical services not detected\n</pitfall>\n\n<pitfall name=\"no_post_deploy_monitoring\">\n**❌ Deploying and immediately moving to next task**\n```bash\n# BAD: Deploy and forget\ngit push origin production\n# Move on to next feature immediately\n```\n**✅ Monitor production for 15-30 minutes after deploy**\n```bash\n# GOOD: Watch logs and metrics\nvercel logs --follow &\nwatch -n 10 ''curl -s https://production.example.com/health''\n# Wait 30 minutes before declaring success\n```\n**Impact**: Issues discovered hours later instead of minutes\n</pitfall>\n\n<pitfall name=\"wrong_version_bump\">\n**❌ Using wrong semantic version bump type**\n```bash\n# BAD: Minor bump for breaking change\nnpm version minor  # But API contract changed!\n```\n**✅ Follow semantic versioning strictly**\n```bash\n# GOOD: Major bump for breaking changes\n# Breaking change in API → major bump\nnpm version major -m \"chore: bump to %s (breaking: API v2)\"\n```\n**Impact**: Users experience unexpected breaking changes\n</pitfall>\n\n<pitfall name=\"missing_git_tag\">\n**❌ Deploying without creating git release tag**\n```bash\n# BAD: Just push to production branch\ngit push origin main:production\n# No tag created for version tracking\n```\n**✅ Always create annotated tag before deploy**\n```bash\n# GOOD: Tag first, then deploy\ngit tag -a \"v2.7.0\" -m \"Release v2.7.0\"\ngit push origin v2.7.0\ngit push origin main:production\n```\n**Impact**: Cannot easily track what code is in production, rollback difficult\n</pitfall>\n</anti_patterns>\n\n<success_criteria>\n**Production deployment successful when:**\n\n- ✓ Staging validation approved (state.yaml verified)\n- ✓ Rollback gate passed (confidence in recovery procedure)\n- ✓ Version bumped correctly (semantic versioning followed)\n- ✓ Git tag created and pushed (v${VERSION} format)\n- ✓ Production deployment triggered and completed\n- ✓ Health checks passing (all critical services operational)\n- ✓ Ship report generated (production-ship-report.md created)\n- ✓ Post-deployment monitoring complete (15-30 minutes, no issues)\n- ✓ Release URL accessible (GitHub release created)\n- ✓ Deployment metadata recorded (ID, URLs, timestamps)\n\n**Quality gates passed:**\n\n- No critical errors in first 30 minutes\n- Error rate <1% increase from baseline\n- Response times <10% degradation\n- No user-reported critical issues\n- All background jobs processing normally\n  </success_criteria>\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:29:36.213Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for DevOps Agents requiring automated production deployment workflows with Spec-Driven Development and Claude Code integration.","zh":"适用于需要自动化生产部署工作流的DevOps代理，具有Spec-Driven Development和Claude Code集成。","ja":"Spec-Driven DevelopmentおよびClaude Codeの統合を備えた自動化されたプロダクション展開ワークフローを必要とするDevOpsエージェントに適しています。","ko":"자동화된 프로덕션 배포 워크플로를 필요로 하는 DevOps 에이전트에게 적합하며, Spec-Driven Development와 Claude Code 통합을 지원합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de DevOps que requieren flujos de trabajo de implementación de producción automatizados con Desarrollo impulsado por especificaciones y integración de Claude Code.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents DevOps nécessitant des flux de travail de déploiement de production automatisés avec un développement piloté par des spécifications et une intégration de Claude Code.","de":"Ideal für DevOps-Agents, die automatisierte Produktionsbereitstellungs-Workflows mit spezifikationsgetriebenem Development und Claude-Code-Integration erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes DevOps que exigem fluxos de trabalho de implantação de produção automatizados com Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Especificações e integração com Claude Code.","ru":"Идеально для агентов DevOps, требующих автоматизированных рабочих процессов развертывания в производство с помощью разработки, управляемой спецификациями, и интеграции с Claude Code.","ar":"مثالي لعميل ديڤ اوپس الذي يتطلب سير عمل تثبيت الإنتاج الآلي مع تطوير مدفوع بالمواصفات وتكامل كلود كود."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to execute production deployment workflows with semantic versioning, health checks, and comprehensive monitoring, utilizing token budgets and auditable artifacts for quality assurance, all while promoting validated staging builds to production.","zh":"赋予代理执行生产部署工作流的能力，具有语义版本控制、健康检查和综合监控，利用令牌预算和可审计的工件进行质量保证，同时促进已验证的分段构建发布到生产环境。","ja":"トークン予算と監査可能なアーティファクトを使用した品質保証を行い、セマンティックバージョニング、ヘルスチェック、および包括的な監視を提供することで、エージェントがプロダクション展開ワークフローを実行できるようにし、検証済みのステージングビルドをプロダクションに昇格させる。","ko":"토큰 예산 및 감사 가능한 아티팩트를 사용하여 품질 보증을 수행하고, 의미론적 버전 관리, 헬스 체크 및 포괄적인 모니터링을 제공하여 에이전트가 프로덕션 배포 워크플로를 실행할 수 있도록 하며, 검증된 스테이징 빌드를 프로덕션으로 승격시킵니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a ejecutar flujos de trabajo de implementación de producción con versionado semántico, comprobaciones de estado y monitoreo integral, utilizando presupuestos de tokens y artefactos auditables para garantizar la calidad, al tiempo que promueve versiones de ensamblaje validadas a producción.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter des flux de travail de déploiement de production avec un versionnage sémantique, des vérifications d''état et un monitoring complet, en utilisant des budgets de jetons et des artefacts auditable pour assurer la qualité, tout en promouvant des builds de staging validés en production.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Produktionsbereitstellungs-Workflows mit semantischer Versionierung, Gesundheitschecks und umfassender Überwachung auszuführen, die Token-Budgets und überprüfbare Artefakte für die Qualitätssicherung nutzen und dabei validierte Staging-Builds in die Produktion fördern.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar fluxos de trabalho de implantação de produção com versionamento semântico, verificações de saúde e monitoramento abrangente, utilizando orçamentos de tokens e artefatos auditáveis para garantia de qualidade, ao mesmo tempo em que promove compilações de pré-lançamento validadas para produção.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять рабочие процессы развертывания в производство с семантическим версионированием, проверками здоровья и комплексным мониторингом, используя бюджет токенов и аудиторские артефакты для обеспечения качества, при этом продвигая проверенные сборки на производство.","ar":"يتمكن العملاء من تشغيل سير عمل تثبيت الإنتاج باستخدام إصدار معنوي، وفحوصات الصحة والمراقبة الشاملة، باستخدام ميزانيات الرموز والمكونات القابلة للتدقيق لضمان الجودة، وفي الوقت نفسه تعزيز المجمعات المؤكدة قبل الإصدار إلى الإنتاج."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating production deployment with prerequisite-driven promotion","Generating release tags and updating package.json/version files","Validating staging builds with manual gates and health checks"],"zh":["使用先决条件驱动的促销自动化生产部署","生成发布标签并更新package.json/版本文件","使用手动门槛和健康检查验证分段构建"],"ja":["前提条件駆動のプロモーションを使用した自動化されたプロダクション展開","リリースタグの生成とpackage.json/バージョンファイルの更新","手動ゲートとヘルスチェックを使用したステージングビルドの検証"],"ko":["사전 조건 구동 프로모션을 사용한 자동화된 프로덕션 배포","릴리즈 태그 생성 및 package.json/버전 파일 업데이트","수동 게이트 및 헬스 체크를 사용한 스테이징 빌드 검증"],"es":["Automatizar la implementación de producción con promoción impulsada por requisitos previos","Generar etiquetas de lanzamiento y actualizar archivos package.json/version","Validar ensamblajes de staging con puertas manuales y comprobaciones de estado"],"fr":["Automatiser le déploiement de production avec une promotion basée sur des conditions préalables","Générer des étiquettes de version et mettre à jour les fichiers package.json/version","Valider les builds de staging avec des portes manuelles et des vérifications d''état"],"de":["Automatisieren der Produktionsbereitstellung mit vorbedingungsbasierter Beförderung","Erzeugen von Release-Tags und Aktualisieren von package.json/Version-Dateien","Validieren von Staging-Builds mit manuellen Toren und Gesundheitschecks"],"pt":["Automatizar a implantação de produção com promoção baseada em pré-requisitos","Gerar etiquetas de lançamento e atualizar arquivos package.json/versão","Validar compilações de pré-lançamento com portões manuais e verificações de saúde"],"ru":["Автоматизировать развертывание в производство с промоцией на основе предварительных требований","Генерировать теги выпуска и обновлять файлы package.json/версия","Проверять сборки перед выпуском с помощью ручных воротов и проверок здоровья"],"ar":["تثبيت الإنتاج الآلي مع الترقية القائمة على المتطلبات السابقة","توليد علامات الإصدار وتحديث ملفات package.json/الإصدار","التحقق من المجمعات قبل الإصدار باستخدام بوابات يدوية وفحوصات الصحة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Claude Code workflows and Spec-Driven Development setup","Needs access to state.yaml and package.json files","Dependent on semantic versioning and release tagging protocols"],"zh":["需要Claude Code工作流和Spec-Driven Development设置","需要访问state.yaml和package.json文件","依赖于语义版本控制和发布标签协议"],"ja":["Claude CodeワークフローおよびSpec-Driven Developmentの設定が必要","state.yamlおよびpackage.jsonファイルへのアクセスが必要","セマンティックバージョニングおよびリリースタグ付けプロトコルに依存"],"ko":["Claude Code 워크플로 및 Spec-Driven Development 설정이 필요합니다","state.yaml 및 package.json 파일에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다","의미론적 버전 관리 및 릴리스 태깅 프로토콜에 의존합니다"],"es":["Requiere flujos de trabajo de Claude Code y configuración de Desarrollo impulsado por especificaciones","Necesita acceso a los archivos state.yaml y package.json","Dependiente de protocolos de versionado semántico y etiquetado de lanzamiento"],"fr":["Nécessite des flux de travail de Claude Code et une configuration de développement piloté par des spécifications","A besoin d''accès aux fichiers state.yaml et package.json","Dépendant des protocoles de versionnage sémantique et d''étiquetage de version"],"de":["Benötigt Claude-Code-Workflows und Spezifikationsgetriebenes-Development-Setup","Benötigt Zugriff auf state.yaml- und package.json-Dateien","Abhängig von semantischer Versionierung und Release-Tagging-Protokollen"],"pt":["Exige workflows do Claude Code e configuração de Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Especificações","Necessita acesso a arquivos state.yaml e package.json","Dependente de protocolos de versionamento semântico e marcação de lançamento"],"ru":["Требует рабочих процессов Claude Code и настройки разработки, управляемой спецификациями","Требует доступа к файлам state.yaml и package.json","Зависит от протоколов семантического версионирования и маркировки выпуска"],"ar":["يتطلب سير عمل كلود كود وضبط تطوير مدفوع بالمواصفات","يحتاج إلى الوصول إلى الملفات state.yaml و package.json","يعتمد على بروتوكولات الإصدار المعنوي وتعليم الإصدار"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('MichaelvanLaar/mvlkss/openspec-archive-change', 'community', 'MichaelvanLaar', 'mvlkss', 'MichaelvanLaar/mvlkss', 'openspec-archive-change', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.448Z', '2026-02-18T06:30:23.545Z', NULL, '{"id":"MichaelvanLaar/mvlkss/openspec-archive-change","name":"openspec-archive-change","description":{"zh":"openspec-archive-change技能用于实验工作流归档，支持开发人员高效管理代码变更","ja":"openspec-archive-changeスキルは実験ワークフローをアーカイブし、開発者がコードの変更を効率的に管理できるようにする","ko":"openspec-archive-change 스킬은 실험 워크플로우를 아카이브하고 개발자가 코드 변경을 효율적으로 관리할 수 있도록 한다","es":"El skill openspec-archive-change permite archivar cambios completados en el flujo de trabajo experimental.","fr":"Le skill openspec-archive-change permet d''archiver les modifications terminées dans le flux de travail expérimental.","de":"Das Skill openspec-archive-change ermöglicht das Archivieren abgeschlossener Änderungen im experimentellen Workflow.","pt":"O openspec-archive-change é uma ferramenta para arquivar alterações completas no fluxo de trabalho experimental. Ele permite que os desenvolvedores gerenciem suas alterações de forma eficiente.","ru":"Openspec-archive-change — это инструмент для архивирования завершенных изменений в экспериментальном рабочем процессе. Он позволяет разработчикам эффективно управлять своими изменениями.","ar":"openspec-archive-change هو أداة لأرشفة التغييرات المكتملة في تدفق العمل التجريبي. يسمح للمطورين بإدارة تغييراتهم بفعالية.","en":"Michael van Laar’s Kirby Site Starter"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"openspec-archive-change技能：实验工作流归档","ja":"openspec-archive-changeスキル：実験ワークフローをアーカイブ","ko":"openspec-archive-change 스킬: 실험 워크플로우 아카이브","es":"Archivo de cambios con openspec-archive-change","fr":"Archivez les modifications avec openspec-archive-change","de":"Ändern Sie das Archiv mit openspec-archive-change","pt":"Arquivar Alterações com openspec-archive-change","ru":"Архивирование изменений с openspec-archive-change","ar":"أرشفة التغييرات مع openspec-archive-change","en":"openspec-archive-change"},"description":{"zh":"openspec-archive-change技能用于实验工作流归档，支持开发人员高效管理代码变更","ja":"openspec-archive-changeスキルは実験ワークフローをアーカイブし、開発者がコードの変更を効率的に管理できるようにする","ko":"openspec-archive-change 스킬은 실험 워크플로우를 아카이브하고 개발자가 코드 변경을 효율적으로 관리할 수 있도록 한다","es":"El skill openspec-archive-change permite archivar cambios completados en el flujo de trabajo experimental.","fr":"Le skill openspec-archive-change permet d''archiver les modifications terminées dans le flux de travail expérimental.","de":"Das Skill openspec-archive-change ermöglicht das Archivieren abgeschlossener Änderungen im experimentellen Workflow.","pt":"O openspec-archive-change é uma ferramenta para arquivar alterações completas no fluxo de trabalho experimental. Ele permite que os desenvolvedores gerenciem...","ru":"Openspec-archive-change — это инструмент для архивирования завершенных изменений в экспериментальном рабочем процессе. Он позволяет разработчикам эффективно ...","ar":"openspec-archive-change هو أداة لأرشفة التغييرات المكتملة في تدفق العمل التجريبي. يسمح للمطورين بإدارة تغييراتهم بفعالية.","en":"Michael van Laar’s Kirby Site Starter"},"definition":{"en":"Michael van Laar’s Kirby Site Starter"},"features":{"zh":["实验工作流归档","支持代码变更管理","提高开发效率","可选指定变更名称","支持多语言"],"ja":["実験ワークフローをアーカイブ","コードの変更を管理","開発効率を向上","変更名称を指定可能","多言語対応"],"ko":["실험 워크플로우 아카이브","코드 변경 관리","개발 효율성 향상","변경 이름 지정 가능","다국어 지원"],"es":["Archiva cambios completados","Permite la selección de cambios","Utiliza el comando openspec list","Muestra solo cambios activos","Incluye esquema para cada cambio"],"fr":["Archive les modifications terminées","Permet la sélection de modifications","Utilise la commande openspec list","Affiche uniquement les modifications actives","Inclut un schéma pour chaque modification"],"de":["Änderungen archivieren","Ermöglicht die Auswahl von Änderungen","Verwendet den Befehl openspec list","Zeigt nur aktive Änderungen an","Enthält ein Schema für jede Änderung"],"pt":["Arquivamento de alterações completas","Gerenciamento de alterações no fluxo de trabalho experimental","Integração com o comando openspec list","Seleção de alterações ativas","Uso da ferramenta AskUserQuestion"],"ru":["Архивирование завершенных изменений","Управление изменениями в экспериментальном рабочем процессе","Интеграция с командой openspec list","Выбор активных изменений","Использование инструмента AskUserQuestion"],"ar":["أرشفة التغييرات المكتملة","إدارة التغييرات في تدفق العمل التجريبي","التكامل مع الأمر openspec list","اختيار التغييرات النشطة","استخدام أداة AskUserQuestion"]},"keywords":{"zh":["openspec-archive-change","实验工作流","代码变更管理","开发效率","代码管理","软件开发"],"ja":["openspec-archive-change","実験ワークフロー","コードの変更管理","開発効率","コード管理","ソフトウェア開発"],"ko":["openspec-archive-change","실험 워크플로우","코드 변경 관리","개발 효율성","코드 관리","소프트웨어 개발"],"es":["openspec-archive-change","flujo de trabajo experimental","archivar cambios","seleccionar cambios","comando openspec list","cambios activos"],"fr":["openspec-archive-change","flux de travail expérimental","archiver les modifications","sélectionner les modifications","commande openspec list","modifications actives"],"de":["openspec-archive-change","experimenteller Workflow","Änderungen archivieren","Änderungen auswählen","Befehl openspec list","aktive Änderungen"],"pt":["openspec-archive-change","arquivamento de alterações","fluxo de trabalho experimental","gerenciamento de alterações","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["openspec-archive-change","архивирование изменений","экспериментальный рабочий процесс","управление изменениями","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["openspec-archive-change","أرشفة التغييرات","تدفق العمل التجريبي","إدارة التغييرات","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"MichaelvanLaar","repo":"mvlkss","repoPath":"MichaelvanLaar/mvlkss","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.448Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-archive-change","description":"Archive a completed change in the experimental workflow. Use when the user wants to finalize and archive a change after implementation is complete.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Archive a completed change in the experimental workflow.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes. Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select.\n\n   Show only active changes (not already archived).\n   Include the schema used for eac","body":"Archive a completed change in the experimental workflow.\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes. Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select.\n\n   Show only active changes (not already archived).\n   Include the schema used for each change if available.\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT guess or auto-select a change. Always let the user choose.\n\n2. **Check artifact completion status**\n\n   Run `openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json` to check artifact completion.\n\n   Parse the JSON to understand:\n   - `schemaName`: The workflow being used\n   - `artifacts`: List of artifacts with their status (`done` or other)\n\n   **If any artifacts are not `done`:**\n   - Display warning listing incomplete artifacts\n   - Use **AskUserQuestion tool** to confirm user wants to proceed\n   - Proceed if user confirms\n\n3. **Check task completion status**\n\n   Read the tasks file (typically `tasks.md`) to check for incomplete tasks.\n\n   Count tasks marked with `- [ ]` (incomplete) vs `- [x]` (complete).\n\n   **If incomplete tasks found:**\n   - Display warning showing count of incomplete tasks\n   - Use **AskUserQuestion tool** to confirm user wants to proceed\n   - Proceed if user confirms\n\n   **If no tasks file exists:** Proceed without task-related warning.\n\n4. **Assess delta spec sync state**\n\n   Check for delta specs at `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/`. If none exist, proceed without sync prompt.\n\n   **If delta specs exist:**\n   - Compare each delta spec with its corresponding main spec at `openspec/specs/<capability>/spec.md`\n   - Determine what changes would be applied (adds, modifications, removals, renames)\n   - Show a combined summary before prompting\n\n   **Prompt options:**\n   - If changes needed: \"Sync now (recommended)\", \"Archive without syncing\"\n   - If already synced: \"Archive now\", \"Sync anyway\", \"Cancel\"\n\n   If user chooses sync, execute /opsx:sync logic (use the openspec-sync-specs skill). Proceed to archive regardless of choice.\n\n5. **Perform the archive**\n\n   Create the archive directory if it doesn''t exist:\n   ```bash\n   mkdir -p openspec/changes/archive\n   ```\n\n   Generate target name using current date: `YYYY-MM-DD-<change-name>`\n\n   **Check if target already exists:**\n   - If yes: Fail with error, suggest renaming existing archive or using different date\n   - If no: Move the change directory to archive\n\n   ```bash\n   mv openspec/changes/<name> openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>\n   ```\n\n6. **Display summary**\n\n   Show archive completion summary including:\n   - Change name\n   - Schema that was used\n   - Archive location\n   - Whether specs were synced (if applicable)\n   - Note about any warnings (incomplete artifacts/tasks)\n\n**Output On Success**\n\n```\n## Archive Complete\n\n**Change:** <change-name>\n**Schema:** <schema-name>\n**Archived to:** openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/\n**Specs:** ✓ Synced to main specs (or \"No delta specs\" or \"Sync skipped\")\n\nAll artifacts complete. All tasks complete.\n```\n\n**Guardrails**\n- Always prompt for change selection if not provided\n- Use artifact graph (openspec status --json) for completion checking\n- Don''t block archive on warnings - just inform and confirm\n- Preserve .openspec.yaml when moving to archive (it moves with the directory)\n- Show clear summary of what happened\n- If sync is requested, use openspec-sync-specs approach (agent-driven)\n- If delta specs exist, always run the sync assessment and show the combined summary before prompting\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:30:23.545Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing experimental workflow management and change archival capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要实验工作流管理和变更存档功能的开发代理。","ja":"実験的ワークフロー管理および変更アーカイブ機能を必要とする開発エージェントに最適。","ko":"실험적인 워크플로 관리 및 변경 기록 기능이 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan gestión de flujo de trabajo experimental y capacidades de archivo de cambios.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une gestion de workflow expérimental et de capacités d''archivage de modifications.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die experimentelle Workflow-Verwaltung und Änderungsarchivierungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de gerenciamento de fluxo de trabalho experimental e capacidades de arquivo de alterações.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходимы возможности управления экспериментальным рабочим процессом и архивации изменений.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الذي يحتاج إلى إدارة تدفق العمل التجريبي وقدرات أرشفة التغييرات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to archive completed changes in the experimental workflow using the openspec-archive-change command, leveraging JSON output and the AskUserQuestion tool for seamless user interaction and change selection, including schema utilization.","zh":"赋予代理使用 openspec-archive-change 命令在实验工作流中存档已完成的更改的能力，利用 JSON 输出和 AskUserQuestion 工具实现无缝的用户交互和更改选择，包括模式利用。","ja":"openspec-archive-change コマンドを使用して実験的ワークフローで完了した変更をアーカイブする能力をエージェントに与え、JSON 出力と AskUserQuestion ツールを使用してユーザーとの無邪気なやり取りと変更の選択を実現し、スキーマの利用を含む。","ko":"openspec-archive-change 명령을 사용하여 실험적인 워크플로에서 완료된 변경을 기록할 수 있는 능력을 에이전트에게 부여하며, JSON 출력과 AskUserQuestion 도구를 사용하여 사용자와의 원활한 상호 작용과 변경 선택을实现하며, 스키마 활용을 포함합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a archivar los cambios completados en el flujo de trabajo experimental utilizando el comando openspec-archive-change, aprovechando la salida JSON y la herramienta AskUserQuestion para una interacción del usuario y selección de cambios sin problemas, incluyendo la utilización de esquemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''archiver les modifications terminées dans le flux de travail expérimental en utilisant la commande openspec-archive-change, en exploitant la sortie JSON et l''outil AskUserQuestion pour une interaction utilisateur et une sélection de modifications sans accroc, y compris l''utilisation de schémas.","de":"Ermächtigt die Mittel, die abgeschlossenen Änderungen im experimentellen Workflow mit dem Befehl openspec-archive-change zu archivieren, indem es die JSON-Ausgabe und das Tool AskUserQuestion für eine nahtlose Benutzerinteraktion und Änderungsauswahl nutzt, einschließlich der Verwendung von Schemata.","pt":"Permite que os agentes arquivem alterações concluídas no fluxo de trabalho experimental usando o comando openspec-archive-change, aproveitando a saída JSON e a ferramenta AskUserQuestion para interação do usuário transparente e seleção de alterações, incluindo utilização de esquema.","ru":"Позволяет агентам архивировать завершенные изменения в экспериментальном рабочем процессе, используя команду openspec-archive-change, которая использует выходные данные JSON и инструмент AskUserQuestion для бесшовного взаимодействия с пользователем и выбора изменений, включая использование схемы.","ar":"يمكن للعميل أرشفة التغييرات المكتملة في تدفق العمل التجريبي باستخدام أمر openspec-archive-change، مستفيداً من الإخراج JSON وأداة AskUserQuestion لتفاعل المستخدم الشفاف واختيار التغييرات، بما في ذلك استخدام مخطط."},"useCases":{"en":["Archiving completed changes in the experimental workflow","Prompting users for change selection using the AskUserQuestion tool","Retrieving available changes with openspec list --json"],"zh":["在实验工作流中存档已完成的更改","使用 AskUserQuestion 工具提示用户选择更改","使用 openspec list --json 检索可用的更改"],"ja":["実験的ワークフローで完了した変更をアーカイブする","AskUserQuestion ツールを使用してユーザーに変更の選択を求める","openspec list --json を使用して利用可能な変更を取得する"],"ko":["실험적인 워크플로에서 완료된 변경을 기록する","AskUserQuestion 도구를 사용하여 사용자에게 변경 선택을 요청하는","openspec list --json을 사용하여 사용 가능한 변경을 검색하는"],"es":["Archivar los cambios completados en el flujo de trabajo experimental","Solicitar a los usuarios la selección de cambios con la herramienta AskUserQuestion","Recuperar los cambios disponibles con openspec list --json"],"fr":["Archiver les modifications terminées dans le flux de travail expérimental","Inciter les utilisateurs à sélectionner des modifications à l''aide de l''outil AskUserQuestion","Récupérer les modifications disponibles avec openspec list --json"],"de":["Abgeschlossene Änderungen im experimentellen Workflow archivieren","Benutzer auffordern, Änderungen mit dem Tool AskUserQuestion auszuwählen","Verfügbare Änderungen mit openspec list --json abrufen"],"pt":["Arquivar alterações concluídas no fluxo de trabalho experimental","Solicitar aos usuários a seleção de alterações usando a ferramenta AskUserQuestion","Recuperar alterações disponíveis com openspec list --json"],"ru":["Архивировать завершенные изменения в экспериментальном рабочем процессе","Просить пользователей выбрать изменения, используя инструмент AskUserQuestion","Получать доступные изменения с помощью openspec list --json"],"ar":["أرشفة التغييرات المكتملة في تدفق العمل التجريبي","تحفيز المستخدمين على اختيار التغييرات باستخدام أداة AskUserQuestion","استرجاع التغييرات المتاحة مع openspec list --json"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires openspec command-line tool access","Limited to active changes only","May prompt for user input if change name is omitted or ambiguous"],"zh":["需要 openspec 命令行工具访问","仅限于活动更改","如果更改名称省略或模糊，可能会提示用户输入"],"ja":["openspec コマンドラインツールへのアクセスが必要","アクティブな変更のみに限定","変更名が省略または曖昧な場合、ユーザー入力を求めることがある"],"ko":["openspec 명령줄 도구에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다.","활성 변경만 제한됨","변경 이름이省略되거나 모호한 경우 사용자 입력을 요청할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la herramienta de línea de comandos openspec","Limitado a cambios activos solo","Puede solicitar la entrada del usuario si el nombre del cambio se omite o es ambiguo"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès à l''outil de ligne de commande openspec","Limité aux modifications actives uniquement","Peut demander une saisie utilisateur si le nom de la modification est omis ou ambigu"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf das Befehlszeilen-Tool openspec","Begrenzt auf aktive Änderungen","Kann Benutzereingabe anfordern, wenn der Änderungsname weggelassen oder mehrdeutig ist"],"pt":["Requer acesso à ferramenta de linha de comando openspec","Limitado a alterações ativas apenas","Pode solicitar entrada do usuário se o nome da alteração for omitido ou ambíguo"],"ru":["Требует доступа к командной строке openspec","Ограничен только активными изменениями","Может запросить ввод пользователя, если имя изменения не указано или неоднозначно"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى أداة سطر الأوامر openspec","محدود بالتغييرات النشطة فقط","يمكن أن يحفز entrada من المستخدم إذا تم استبعاد اسم التغيير أو إذا كان غامضاً"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Tupatuko2023/Python-R-Scripts/fof-qc-summarizer', 'community', 'Tupatuko2023', 'Python-R-Scripts', 'Tupatuko2023/Python-R-Scripts', 'fof-qc-summarizer', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.448Z', '2026-02-18T06:30:30.318Z', NULL, '{"id":"Tupatuko2023/Python-R-Scripts/fof-qc-summarizer","name":"fof-qc-summarizer","description":{"zh":"fof-qc-summarizer技能用于总结质量控制输出，通过运行R脚本提高开发效率","ja":"fof-qc-summarizerスキルは、品質管理の出力を要約し、Rスクリプトを実行して開発の効率を向上させるために使用されます","ko":"fof-qc-summarizer 기능은 품질 관리 출력을 요약하고 R 스크립트를 실행하여 개발 효율성을 높이는 데 사용됩니다","es":"El resumen de QC de Fear-of-Falling es una herramienta para analizar resultados de QC de forma eficiente.","fr":"Le résumé de QC de Fear-of-Falling est un outil pour analyser les résultats de QC de manière efficace.","de":"Die QC-Zusammenfassung von Fear-of-Falling ist ein Tool zum effizienten Analysieren von QC-Ergebnissen.","pt":"O fof-qc-summarizer é uma ferramenta para resumir resultados de controle de qualidade em projetos de desenvolvimento","ru":"fof-qc-summarizer - это инструмент для суммирования результатов контроля качества в проектах разработки","ar":"fof-qc-summarizer هو أداة لتلخيص نتائج تحكم الجودة في مشاريع التطوير","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"fof-qc-summarizer技能：恐惧坠落质量控制总结","ja":"fof-qc-summarizerスキル：恐怖の落下品質管理サマリー","ko":"fof-qc-summarizer 기능: 공포의 떨어짐 품질 관리 요약","es":"Resumen de QC de Fear-of-Falling","fr":"Résumé de QC de Fear-of-Falling","de":"QC-Zusammenfassung von Fear-of-Falling","pt":"Resumo de Controle de Qualidade fof-qc-summarizer","ru":"Суммаризатор контроля качества fof-qc-summarizer","ar":"موجز تحكم الجودة fof-qc-summarizer","en":"fof-qc-summarizer"},"description":{"zh":"fof-qc-summarizer技能用于总结质量控制输出，通过运行R脚本提高开发效率","ja":"fof-qc-summarizerスキルは、品質管理の出力を要約し、Rスクリプトを実行して開発の効率を向上させるために使用されます","ko":"fof-qc-summarizer 기능은 품질 관리 출력을 요약하고 R 스크립트를 실행하여 개발 효율성을 높이는 데 사용됩니다","es":"El resumen de QC de Fear-of-Falling es una herramienta para analizar resultados de QC de forma eficiente.","fr":"Le résumé de QC de Fear-of-Falling est un outil pour analyser les résultats de QC de manière efficace.","de":"Die QC-Zusammenfassung von Fear-of-Falling ist ein Tool zum effizienten Analysieren von QC-Ergebnissen.","pt":"O fof-qc-summarizer é uma ferramenta para resumir resultados de controle de qualidade em projetos de desenvolvimento","ru":"fof-qc-summarizer - это инструмент для суммирования результатов контроля качества в проектах разработки","ar":"fof-qc-summarizer هو أداة لتلخيص نتائج تحكم الجودة في مشاريع التطوير","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["运行R脚本总结质量控制输出","支持可选参数覆盖","自动发现manifest helpers","支持多语言开发"],"ja":["Rスクリプトを実行して品質管理の出力を要約","オプションパラメータのオーバーライドをサポート","マニフェストヘルパーの自動発見","多言語開発をサポート"],"ko":["R 스크립트를 실행하여 품질 관리 출력을 요약","옵션 매개 변수 오버라이드를 지원","매니페스트 헬퍼의 자동 검색","다국어 개발을 지원"],"es":["Análisis de resultados de QC","Compatibilidad con Rscript","Opciones de configuración personalizables","Compatibilidad con directorios de salida personalizados","Detección automática de archivos de manifiesto"],"fr":["Analyse des résultats de QC","Compatibilité avec Rscript","Options de configuration personnalisables","Compatibilité avec des répertoires de sortie personnalisés","Détection automatique des fichiers de manifeste"],"de":["Analyse von QC-Ergebnissen","Kompatibilität mit Rscript","Anpassbare Konfigurationsoptionen","Kompatibilität mit benutzerdefinierten Ausgabeverzeichnissen","Automatische Erkennung von Manifestdateien"],"pt":["Resumo de resultados de controle de qualidade","Execução via Rscript","Opções de substituição para diretórios e rótulos","Leitura de saídas de controle de qualidade","Geração de relatórios personalizados"],"ru":["Суммирование результатов контроля качества","Выполнение через Rscript","Возможность переопределения директорий и меток","Чтение выходных данных контроля качества","Генерация индивидуальных отчетов"],"ar":["تلخيص نتائج تحكم الجودة","التشغيل عبر Rscript","خيار التغيير لمسارات الملفات والأوسمة","قراءة مخرجات تحكم الجودة","توليد تقارير مخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["fof-qc-summarizer","质量控制","R脚本","开发效率","总结输出","可选参数"],"ja":["fof-qc-summarizer","品質管理","Rスクリプト","開発効率","出力の要約","オプションパラメータ"],"ko":["fof-qc-summarizer","품질 관리","R 스크립트","개발 효율성","출력 요약","옵션 매개 변수"],"es":["resumen de QC","Fear-of-Falling","análisis de resultados","Rscript","configuración personalizable","directorios de salida personalizados","detección de archivos de manifiesto"],"fr":["résumé de QC","Fear-of-Falling","analyse de résultats","Rscript","configuration personnalisable","répertoires de sortie personnalisés","détection de fichiers de manifeste"],"de":["QC-Zusammenfassung","Fear-of-Falling","Analyse von Ergebnissen","Rscript","anpassbare Konfiguration","benutzerdefinierte Ausgabeverzeichnisse","Erkennung von Manifestdateien"],"pt":["fof-qc-summarizer","controle de qualidade","desenvolvimento de software","Rscript","relatórios personalizados","análise de dados"],"ru":["fof-qc-summarizer","контроль качества","разработка программного обеспечения","Rscript","индивидуальные отчеты","анализ данных"],"ar":["fof-qc-summarizer","تحكم الجودة","تطوير البرمجيات","Rscript","تقارير مخصصة","تحليل البيانات"]}},"owner":"Tupatuko2023","repo":"Python-R-Scripts","repoPath":"Tupatuko2023/Python-R-Scripts","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.448Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"fof-qc-summarizer","description":"Aggregate-only summarizer for K18 QC artifacts; produces summary outputs and appends manifest rows when format is confirmed.","bodyPreview":"## How to use\n\nRun from the Fear-of-Falling subproject root or repo root.\n\nExample:\n\n```bash\nRscript .codex/skills/fof-qc-summarizer/scripts/qc_summarize.R\n```\n\nOptional overrides:\n\n```bash\nRscript .codex/skills/fof-qc-summarizer/scripts/qc_summarize.R --qc-dir PATH --out-dir PATH --script-label K18_QC_SUMMARY\n```\n\n## Inputs\n\n- QC outputs under `Fear-of-Falling/R-scripts/K18/outputs/K18_QC/qc/`.\n- Manifest helpers discovered by scanning for `init.R` with `append_manifest()` and `manifest_row()`.","body":"## How to use\n\nRun from the Fear-of-Falling subproject root or repo root.\n\nExample:\n\n```bash\nRscript .codex/skills/fof-qc-summarizer/scripts/qc_summarize.R\n```\n\nOptional overrides:\n\n```bash\nRscript .codex/skills/fof-qc-summarizer/scripts/qc_summarize.R --qc-dir PATH --out-dir PATH --script-label K18_QC_SUMMARY\n```\n\n## Inputs\n\n- QC outputs under `Fear-of-Falling/R-scripts/K18/outputs/K18_QC/qc/`.\n- Manifest helpers discovered by scanning for `init.R` with `append_manifest()` and `manifest_row()`.\n- Policy sources: `Fear-of-Falling/CLAUDE.md`, `Fear-of-Falling/QC_CHECKLIST.md`.\n\n## Outputs\n\n- `Fear-of-Falling/R-scripts/K18/outputs/K18_QC/qc_summary/qc_summary.csv`\n- `Fear-of-Falling/R-scripts/K18/outputs/K18_QC/qc_summary/qc_summary.txt`\n- One manifest row per new artifact (if manifest format is confirmed).\n\n## Failure modes\n\n- Fear-of-Falling project root not found.\n- QC outputs directory missing.\n- Manifest helpers missing.\n- Manifest header mismatch (fail closed).\n- No eligible aggregate QC artifacts to summarize.\n\n## Safety/guardrails\n\n- FAIL CLOSED: if manifest helpers or format are not verifiable, the script exits 1.\n- Privacy: skips any file with `ids`, `row_level`, or `participant` in the name or\n  an `id`-like column; never writes participant-level rows.\n- No external APIs or network calls.\n- Does not modify raw data or QC inputs.\n\nSources: `Fear-of-Falling/CLAUDE.md`, `Fear-of-Falling/QC_CHECKLIST.md`.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:30:30.318Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Bioinformatics Analysis Agents specializing in R-based quality control workflows for Fear-of-Falling research data.","zh":"适用于生物信息学分析代理，专注于 R 基础的质量控制工作流，用于恐惧跌倒研究数据。","ja":"バイオインフォマティクス分析エージェントに適しています。Rベースの品質管理ワークフローを専門とし、恐怖の落下研究データを扱います。","ko":"생물 정보학 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다. R 기반의 품질 관리 워크플로를 전문으로 하며, 공포의 낙하 연구 데이터를 처리합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Análisis de Bioinformática especializados en flujos de trabajo de control de calidad basados en R para datos de investigación de miedo a caer.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse de bioinformatique spécialisés dans les flux de travail de contrôle de qualité basés sur R pour les données de recherche sur la peur de tomber.","de":"Ideal für Bioinformatik-Analyse-Agents, die auf R-basierte Qualitätskontroll-Workflows für Angst-vor-dem-Fallen-Forschungsdaten spezialisiert sind.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise de Bioinformática especializados em fluxos de trabalho de controle de qualidade baseados em R para dados de pesquisa de Medo de Queda.","ru":"Идеально для агентов анализа биоинформатики, специализирующихся на потоках контроля качества на основе R для исследования данных Страха падения.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تحليل المعلومات الحيوية المتخصصة في تدفقات عمل مراقبة الجودة القائمة على R لبيانات البحث حول خوف السقوط."},"recommendation":{"en":"Automates aggregation and summarization of QC outputs from K18_QC directories, leveraging manifest helpers discovered through init.R scanning with append_manifest() and manifest_row() functions. Enables batch processing of quality control results with customizable output paths and script labels via command-line arguments.","zh":"自动化 K18_QC 目录中的 QC 输出的聚合和总结，利用通过 init.R 扫描和 append_manifest() 和 manifest_row() 函数发现的 manifest 辅助工具。通过命令行参数启用批处理质量控制结果，具有可定制的输出路径和脚本标签。","ja":"K18_QC ディレクトリ内の QC 出力の集約と概要の自動化を実行し、init.R スキャニングと append_manifest() および manifest_row() 関数で発見されたマニフェスト ヘルパーを利用する。コマンドライン引数を介して、カスタマイズ可能な出力パスとスクリプト ラベルを備えたバッチ処理の品質管理結果を有効にします。","ko":"K18_QC 디렉토리의 QC 출력의 집계와 요약을 자동화하고, init.R 스캔과 append_manifest() 및 manifest_row() 함수를 통해 발견된 매니페스트 도우미를 활용합니다. 명령줄 인수를 통해 출력 경로와 스크립트 레이블을 사용자 정의하여 일괄 처리 품질 관리 결과를 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Automatiza la agregación y resumen de resultados de control de calidad de los directorios K18_QC, aprovechando los ayudantes de manifiesto descubiertos a través de la exploración de init.R con las funciones append_manifest() y manifest_row(). Permite el procesamiento por lotes de resultados de control de calidad con rutas de salida personalizables y etiquetas de script a través de argumentos de línea de comandos.","fr":"Automatise l''agrégation et la synthèse des résultats de contrôle de qualité des répertoires K18_QC, en exploitant les aides de manifeste découvertes grâce à l''analyse de init.R avec les fonctions append_manifest() et manifest_row(). Permet le traitement par lots des résultats de contrôle de qualité avec des chemins de sortie personnalisables et des libellés de script via des arguments de ligne de commande.","de":"Automatisiert die Aggregation und Zusammenfassung von Qualitätskontroll-Ergebnissen aus K18_QC-Verzeichnissen, indem es Manifest-Helferleistungen nutzt, die durch init.R-Scanning mit append_manifest()- und manifest_row()-Funktionen entdeckt wurden. Ermöglicht den Batch-Prozess von Qualitätskontroll-Ergebnissen mit anpassbaren Ausgabepfaden und Skriptetiketten über Befehlszeilenargumente.","pt":"Automatiza a agregação e a resumo das saídas de QC dos diretórios K18_QC, utilizando os ajudantes de manifesto descobertos por meio da varredura init.R com as funções append_manifest() e manifest_row(). Permite o processamento em lote dos resultados de controle de qualidade com caminhos de saída personalizáveis e rótulos de script via argumentos de linha de comando.","ru":"Автоматизирует агрегацию и суммирование выходных данных QC из каталогов K18_QC, используя помощников манифеста, обнаруженных путем сканирования init.R с функциями append_manifest() и manifest_row(). Позволяет выполнять пакетную обработку результатов контроля качества с настраиваемыми путями вывода и метками сценариев через аргументы командной строки.","ar":"يتم Automatiza تجميع وتلخيص مخرجات QC من مكاتب K18_QC ، باستخدام مساعدات البيان المكتشفة من خلال مسح init.R مع وظائف append_manifest() و manifest_row() . يسمح بمعالجة الدُفعات من نتائج مراقبة الجودة بمسارات مخرجات قابلة للتخصيص وملصقات البرامج النصية عبر حُجج سطر الأوامر."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating QC report generation for Fear-of-Falling datasets","Aggregating multiple QC outputs into comprehensive summaries","Processing manifest data from init.R files for workflow integration"],"zh":["自动化恐惧跌倒数据集的 QC 报告生成","将多个 QC 输出聚合为综合摘要","处理 init.R 文件的清单数据以实现工作流集成"],"ja":["恐怖の落下データセットの QC レポート生成の自動化","複数の QC 出力を包括的な概要に集約する","init.R ファイルのマニフェスト データを処理してワークフロー統合を実現する"],"ko":["공포의 낙하 데이터셋의 QC 보고서 생성 자동화","여러 개의 QC 출력을 종합적인 요약으로 집계","init.R 파일의 매니페스트 데이터를 처리하여 워크플로 통합을 구현"],"es":["Automatizar la generación de informes de control de calidad para conjuntos de datos de miedo a caer","Agregar múltiples resultados de control de calidad en resúmenes comprehensivos","Procesar datos de manifiesto de archivos init.R para la integración de flujos de trabajo"],"fr":["Automatiser la génération de rapports de contrôle de qualité pour les jeux de données de peur de tomber","Aggréger plusieurs résultats de contrôle de qualité en synthèses complètes","Traiter les données de manifeste des fichiers init.R pour l''intégration de flux de travail"],"de":["Automatisieren der Erstellung von Qualitätskontroll-Berichten für Angst-vor-dem-Fallen-Datensätze","Zusammenfassen mehrerer Qualitätskontroll-Ergebnisse in umfassende Zusammenfassungen","Verarbeiten von Manifest-Daten aus init.R-Dateien für die Workflow-Integration"],"pt":["Automatizar a geração de relatórios de QC para conjuntos de dados de Medo de Queda","Agregando várias saídas de QC em resumos abrangentes","Processando dados de manifesto de arquivos init.R para integração de fluxos de trabalho"],"ru":["Автоматизация генерации отчетов QC для наборов данных Страха падения","Агрегация нескольких выходных данных QC в комплексные сводки","Обработка данных манифеста из файлов init.R для интеграции рабочих процессов"],"ar":["توفير آلي لتوليد تقارير QC لdatasets خوف السقوط","تجميع مخرجات QC المتعددة في تلخيصات شاملة","معالجة بيانات البيان من الملفات init.R لتكامل تدفقات العمل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires specific directory structure (Fear-of-Falling/R-scripts/K18/outputs/K18_QC/qc/)","Dependent on R environment and script execution capabilities","Needs manifest helpers with append_manifest() and manifest_row() functions"],"zh":["需要特定的目录结构（恐惧跌倒/R-scripts/K18/outputs/K18_QC/qc/）","依赖于 R 环境和脚本执行能力","需要具有 append_manifest() 和 manifest_row() 函数的 manifest 辅助工具"],"ja":["特定のディレクトリ構造（恐怖の落下/R-scripts/K18/outputs/K18_QC/qc/）を必要とする","R 環境とスクリプト実行能力に依存する","append_manifest() および manifest_row() 関数を備えたマニフェスト ヘルパーを必要とする"],"ko":["특정 디렉토리 구조(공포의 낙하/R-scripts/K18/outputs/K18_QC/qc/)가 필요","R 환경과 스크립트 실행 능력에 의존","append_manifest() 및 manifest_row() 함수를 갖춘 매니페스트 도우미가 필요"],"es":["Requiere una estructura de directorio específica (Fear-of-Falling/R-scripts/K18/outputs/K18_QC/qc/)","Dependiente del entorno R y de las capacidades de ejecución de scripts","Necesita ayudantes de manifiesto con funciones append_manifest() y manifest_row()"],"fr":["Nécessite une structure de répertoire spécifique (Fear-of-Falling/R-scripts/K18/outputs/K18_QC/qc/)","Dépendant de l''environnement R et des capacités d''exécution de scripts","A besoin d''aides de manifeste avec les fonctions append_manifest() et manifest_row()"],"de":["Benötigt eine spezifische Verzeichnisstruktur (Fear-of-Falling/R-scripts/K18/outputs/K18_QC/qc/)","Abhängig von der R-Umgebung und den Skript-Ausführungsfähigkeiten","Benötigt Manifest-Helfer mit append_manifest()- und manifest_row()-Funktionen"],"pt":["Exige estrutura de diretório específica (Fear-of-Falling/R-scripts/K18/outputs/K18_QC/qc/)","Depende do ambiente R e capacidades de execução de scripts","Necessita de ajudantes de manifesto com as funções append_manifest() e manifest_row()"],"ru":["Требует конкретной структуры каталога (Fear-of-Falling/R-scripts/K18/outputs/K18_QC/qc/)","Зависит от среды R и возможностей выполнения сценариев","Требует помощников манифеста с функциями append_manifest() и manifest_row()"],"ar":["يتطلب هيكلا مديرا محددا (Fear-of-Falling/R-scripts/K18/outputs/K18_QC/qc/)","يعتمد على بيئة R وقدرات تشغيل البرامج النصية","يحتاج إلى مساعدات البيان مع وظائف append_manifest() و manifest_row()"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('HerbertGao/qsl-cardhub/openspec-onboard', 'community', 'HerbertGao', 'qsl-cardhub', 'HerbertGao/qsl-cardhub', 'openspec-onboard', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.448Z', '2026-02-18T06:29:45.455Z', NULL, '{"id":"HerbertGao/qsl-cardhub/openspec-onboard","name":"openspec-onboard","description":{"zh":"本教程将引导您完成一个完整的OpenSpec工作流周期，包括初始化、创建变更、构建产出物和实现任务","ja":"OpenSpecのワークフローを通して、初心者でも簡単に学べます","ko":"OpenSpec 작업 흐름을 통해 변경 관리를 진행하는 방법을 배웁니다","es":"El onboarding de OpenSpec te guía a través de un ciclo de trabajo completo, desde la idea hasta la implementación, utilizando tareas reales de tu código","fr":"L''onboarding OpenSpec vous guide à travers un cycle de travail complet, de l''idée à la mise en œuvre, en utilisant des tâches réelles de votre code","de":"Das Onboarding von OpenSpec führt Sie durch einen vollständigen Arbeitszyklus, von der Idee bis zur Implementierung, unter Verwendung von echten Aufgaben aus Ihrem Code","pt":"O OpenSpec Onboard é um guia de integração que ajuda desenvolvedores a aprender workflows de código práticos.","ru":"OpenSpec Онбординг - это руководство по интеграции, которое помогает разработчикам изучать практические кодовые рабочие процессы.","ar":"توجيه OpenSpec هو دليل إعداد يساعد المطورين على تعلم سير عمل الكود العملي.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"OpenSpec入门指南","ja":"OpenSpecを始める","ko":"OpenSpec 시작하기","es":"Onboarding de OpenSpec: primer ciclo de trabajo","fr":"Onboarding OpenSpec : premier cycle de travail","de":"OpenSpec-Onboarding: Erster Arbeitszyklus","pt":"OpenSpec Onboard: Guia de Integração","ru":"OpenSpec Онбординг: Руководство по Интеграции","ar":"توجيه OpenSpec: دليل الإعداد","en":"openspec-onboard"},"description":{"zh":"本教程将引导您完成一个完整的OpenSpec工作流周期，包括初始化、创建变更、构建产出物和实现任务","ja":"OpenSpecのワークフローを通して、初心者でも簡単に学べます","ko":"OpenSpec 작업 흐름을 통해 변경 관리를 진행하는 방법을 배웁니다","es":"El onboarding de OpenSpec te guía a través de un ciclo de trabajo completo, desde la idea hasta la implementación, utilizando tareas reales de tu código","fr":"L''onboarding OpenSpec vous guide à travers un cycle de travail complet, de l''idée à la mise en œuvre, en utilisant des tâches réelles de votre code","de":"Das Onboarding von OpenSpec führt Sie durch einen vollständigen Arbeitszyklus, von der Idee bis zur Implementierung, unter Verwendung von echten Aufgaben aus...","pt":"O OpenSpec Onboard é um guia de integração que ajuda desenvolvedores a aprender workflows de código práticos.","ru":"OpenSpec Онбординг - это руководство по интеграции, которое помогает разработчикам изучать практические кодовые рабочие процессы.","ar":"توجيه OpenSpec هو دليل إعداد يساعد المطورين على تعلم سير عمل الكود العملي.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["初始化OpenSpec","创建变更","构建产出物","实现任务","归档完成的变更"],"ja":["OpenSpecの初期化","変更の作成","成果物の構築","タスクの実装","完了した変更のアーカイブ"],"ko":["OpenSpec 초기화","변경 생성","산출물 구축","작업 구현","완료된 변경 보관"],"es":["Selección de tareas reales","Creación de un cambio","Construcción de resultados","Implementación de tareas","Archivo de cambios completados","Guía interactiva"],"fr":["Sélection de tâches réelles","Création d''un changement","Construction de résultats","Mise en œuvre de tâches","Archivage de changements terminés","Guide interactif"],"de":["Auswahl von echten Aufgaben","Erstellung einer Änderung","Erstellung von Ergebnissen","Implementierung von Aufgaben","Archivierung abgeschlossener Änderungen","Interaktive Anleitung"],"pt":["Integração passo-a-passo","Desenvolvimento de habilidades práticas","Ciclo de trabalho completo","Aprendizado de workflows de código","Guia interativo"],"ru":["Пошаговая интеграция","Развитие практических навыков","Полный цикл работы","Обучение кодовым рабочим процессам","Интерактивное руководство"],"ar":["دمج خطوة بخطوة","تطوير مهارات عملية","دورة عمل كاملة","تعلم سير عمل الكود","دليل تفاعلي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["OpenSpec入门","OpenSpec工作流","变更管理","代码库管理","开发者工具"],"ja":["OpenSpecを始める","OpenSpecワークフロー","変更管理","コードライブラリ管理","開発者ツール"],"ko":["OpenSpec 시작","OpenSpec 작업 흐름","변경 관리","코드 라이브러리 관리","개발자 도구"],"es":["OpenSpec","onboarding","ciclo de trabajo","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo","guía interactiva","tareas reales"],"fr":["OpenSpec","onboarding","cycle de travail","développement de logiciels","outils de développement","guide interactif","tâches réelles"],"de":["OpenSpec","Onboarding","Arbeitszyklus","Softwareentwicklung","Entwicklungstools","interaktive Anleitung","echte Aufgaben"],"pt":["OpenSpec","integração","desenvolvimento de software","workflows de código","guia de integração","aprendizado prático"],"ru":["OpenSpec","интеграция","разработка программного обеспечения","кодовые рабочие процессы","руководство по интеграции","практическое обучение"],"ar":["OpenSpec","دمج","تطوير البرمجيات","سير عمل الكود","دليل الإعداد","التعلم العملي"]}},"owner":"HerbertGao","repo":"qsl-cardhub","repoPath":"HerbertGao/qsl-cardhub","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.448Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-onboard","description":"OpenSpec 引导式入门 - 通过讲解与在真实代码库中动手，走完一个完整的工作流周期。","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"引导用户完成他们的第一个完整OpenSpec工作流周期。这是一个教学体验——你将在他们的代码库中完成实际工作，同时解释每个步骤。\n\n---\n\n## 准备阶段\n\n开始前，检查OpenSpec是否已初始化：\n\n```bash\nopenspec-cn status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**如果未初始化：**\n> OpenSpec尚未在此项目中设置。请先运行 `openspec-cn init`，然后返回 `/opsx:onboard`。\n\n如果未初始化，请在此停止。\n\n---\n\n## 阶段1：欢迎\n\n显示：\n\n```\n## 欢迎使用OpenSpec！\n\n我将引导您完成一个完整的变更周期——从想法到实现——使用您代码库中的真实任务。在此过程中，您将通过实践学习工作流程。\n\n**我们将要做的事情：**\n1. 在您的代码库中选择一个小的真实任务\n2. 简要探索问题\n3. 创建一个变更（我们工作的容器）\n4. 构建产出物：提案 → 规格说明 → 设计 → 任务\n5. 实现任务\n6. 归档完成的变更\n\n**时间：** ~15-20分钟","body":"引导用户完成他们的第一个完整OpenSpec工作流周期。这是一个教学体验——你将在他们的代码库中完成实际工作，同时解释每个步骤。\n\n---\n\n## 准备阶段\n\n开始前，检查OpenSpec是否已初始化：\n\n```bash\nopenspec-cn status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**如果未初始化：**\n> OpenSpec尚未在此项目中设置。请先运行 `openspec-cn init`，然后返回 `/opsx:onboard`。\n\n如果未初始化，请在此停止。\n\n---\n\n## 阶段1：欢迎\n\n显示：\n\n```\n## 欢迎使用OpenSpec！\n\n我将引导您完成一个完整的变更周期——从想法到实现——使用您代码库中的真实任务。在此过程中，您将通过实践学习工作流程。\n\n**我们将要做的事情：**\n1. 在您的代码库中选择一个小的真实任务\n2. 简要探索问题\n3. 创建一个变更（我们工作的容器）\n4. 构建产出物：提案 → 规格说明 → 设计 → 任务\n5. 实现任务\n6. 归档完成的变更\n\n**时间：** ~15-20分钟\n\n让我们开始寻找要处理的内容。\n```\n\n---\n\n## 阶段2：任务选择\n\n### 代码库分析\n\n扫描代码库寻找小的改进机会。寻找：\n\n1. **TODO/FIXME注释** - 在代码文件中搜索 `TODO`、`FIXME`、`HACK`、`XXX`\n2. **缺少错误处理** - 吞没错误的 `catch` 块，没有try-catch的风险操作\n3. **没有测试的函数** - 交叉引用 `src/` 和测试目录\n4. **类型问题** - TypeScript文件中的 `any` 类型（`: any`、`as any`）\n5. **调试产出物** - 非调试代码中的 `console.log`、`console.debug`、`debugger` 语句\n6. **缺少验证** - 没有验证的用户输入处理程序\n\n同时检查最近的git活动：\n```bash\ngit log --oneline -10 2>/dev/null || echo \"No git history\"\n```\n\n### 提出建议\n\n根据您的分析，提出3-4个具体建议：\n\n```\n## 任务建议\n\n基于扫描您的代码库，以下是一些好的入门任务：\n\n**1. [最有希望的任务]**\n   位置：`src/path/to/file.ts:42`\n   范围：~1-2个文件，~20-30行\n   为什么好：[简要原因]\n\n**2. [第二个任务]**\n   位置：`src/another/file.ts`\n   范围：~1个文件，~15行\n   为什么好：[简要原因]\n\n**3. [第三个任务]**\n   位置：[位置]\n   范围：[估计]\n   为什么好：[简要原因]\n\n**4. 其他内容？**\n   告诉我您想要处理什么。\n\n哪个任务让您感兴趣？（选择一个数字或描述您自己的）\n```\n\n**如果未找到任何内容：** 回退到询问用户想要构建什么：\n> 我在您的代码库中没有找到明显的快速改进机会。您一直想要添加或修复什么小东西？\n\n### 范围护栏\n\n如果用户选择或描述的内容太大（主要功能，多天工作）：\n\n```\n这是一个有价值的任务，但对于您的第一次OpenSpec体验来说可能太大了。\n\n对于学习工作流程，越小越好——它让您能够看到完整周期而不会陷入实现细节。\n\n**选项：**\n1. **切分成更小的部分** - [他们的任务]中最小的有用部分是什么？也许只是[具体切片]？\n2. **选择其他内容** - 其他建议之一，或不同的任务？\n3. **无论如何都做** - 如果您真的想处理这个，我们可以做。只是要知道需要更长时间。\n\n您更喜欢哪种？\n```\n\n如果用户坚持，让他们覆盖——这是一个软护栏。\n\n---\n\n## 阶段3：探索演示\n\n一旦选择了任务，简要演示探索模式：\n\n```\n在我们创建变更之前，让我快速向您展示**探索模式**——这是在承诺方向之前思考问题的方式。\n```\n\n花1-2分钟调查相关代码：\n- 阅读涉及的文件\n- 如果需要，绘制快速ASCII图表\n- 注意任何考虑事项\n\n```\n## 快速探索\n\n[您的简要分析——您发现了什么，任何考虑事项]\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│   [可选：如果有帮助的ASCII图表]          │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n探索模式（`/opsx:explore`）用于这种思考——在实现之前进行调查。您可以在需要思考问题时随时使用它。\n\n现在让我们创建一个变更来保存我们的工作。\n```\n\n**暂停** - 等待用户确认后再继续。\n\n---\n\n## 阶段4：创建变更\n\n**解释：**\n```\n## 创建变更\n\nOpenSpec中的\"变更\"是围绕一项工作的所有思考和规划的容器。它位于 `openspec/changes/<name>/` 中，保存您的产出物——提案、规格说明、设计、任务。\n\n让我为我们的任务创建一个。\n```\n\n**执行：** 使用派生的kebab-case名称创建变更：\n```bash\nopenspec-cn new change \"<derived-name>\"\n```\n\n**显示：**\n```\n已创建：`openspec/changes/<name>/`\n\n文件夹结构：\n```\nopenspec/changes/<name>/\n├── proposal.md    ← 为什么我们要做这个（空，我们将填充它）\n├── design.md      ← 我们将如何构建它（空）\n├── specs/         ← 详细需求（空）\n└── tasks.md       ← 实现检查清单（空）\n```\n\n现在让我们填充第一个产出物——提案。\n```\n\n---\n\n## 阶段5：提案\n\n**解释：**\n```\n## 提案\n\n提案捕获**为什么**我们要进行此变更以及**什么**在高层级上涉及。这是工作的\"电梯演讲\"。\n\n我将根据我们的任务起草一个。\n```\n\n**执行：** 起草提案内容（暂时不保存）：\n\n```\n这是一个草案提案：\n\n---\n\n## 为什么\n\n[1-2句话解释问题/机会]\n\n## 什么变化\n\n[将要不同的要点]\n\n## 能力\n\n### 新能力\n- `<能力名称>`: [简要描述]\n\n### 修改的能力\n<!-- 如果修改现有行为 -->\n\n## 影响\n\n- `src/path/to/file.ts`: [什么变化]\n- [其他文件如果适用]\n\n---\n\n这能捕捉意图吗？我可以在保存前调整。\n```\n\n**暂停** - 等待用户批准/反馈。\n\n批准后，保存提案：\n```bash\nopenspec-cn instructions proposal --change \"<name>\" --json\n```\n然后将内容写入 `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`。\n\n```\n提案已保存。这是您的\"为什么\"文档——您随时可以回来在理解发展时完善它。\n\n接下来：规格说明。\n```\n\n---\n\n## 阶段6：规格说明\n\n**解释：**\n```\n## 规格说明\n\n规格说明以精确、可测试的术语定义**什么**我们正在构建。它们使用需求/场景格式，使预期行为清晰明了。\n\n对于像这样的小任务，我们可能只需要一个规格说明文件。\n```\n\n**执行：** 创建规格说明文件：\n```bash\nmkdir -p openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability-name>\n```\n\n起草规格说明内容：\n\n```\n这是规格说明：\n\n---\n\n## 新增需求\n\n### 需求：<名称>\n\n<系统应该做什么的描述>\n\n#### 场景：<场景名称>\n\n- **当** <触发条件>\n- **那么** <预期结果>\n- **并且** <如果需要额外结果>\n\n---\n\n这种格式——当/那么/并且——使需求可测试。您可以将它们字面地读作测试用例。\n```\n\n保存到 `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability>/spec.md`。\n\n---\n\n## 阶段7：设计\n\n**解释：**\n```\n## 设计\n\n设计捕获**如何**我们将构建它——技术决策、权衡、方法。\n\n对于小变更，这可能很简短。没关系——不是每个变更都需要深入的设计讨论。\n```\n\n**执行：** 起草design.md：\n\n```\n这是设计：\n\n---\n\n## 上下文\n\n[关于当前状态的简要上下文]\n\n## 目标/非目标\n\n**目标：**\n- [我们试图实现什么]\n\n**非目标：**\n- [明确超出范围的内容]\n\n## 决策\n\n### 决策1：[关键决策]\n\n[方法解释和理由]\n\n---\n\n对于小任务，这捕获了关键决策而不过度工程化。\n```\n\n保存到 `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`。\n\n---\n\n## 阶段8：任务\n\n**解释：**\n```\n## 任务\n\n最后，我们将工作分解为实现任务——驱动应用阶段的复选框。\n\n这些应该小、清晰且逻辑顺序。\n```\n\n**执行：** 基于规格说明和设计生成任务：\n\n```\n这是实现任务：\n\n---\n\n## 1. [类别或文件]\n\n- [ ] 1.1 [具体任务]\n- [ ] 1.2 [具体任务]\n\n## 2. 验证\n\n- [ ] 2.1 [验证步骤]\n\n---\n\n每个复选框成为应用阶段的工作单元。准备好实现了吗？\n```\n\n**暂停** - 等待用户确认他们准备好实现。\n\n保存到 `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`。\n\n---\n\n## 阶段9：应用（实现）\n\n**解释：**\n```\n## 实现\n\n现在我们实现每个任务，在过程中勾选它们。我将宣布每个任务，并偶尔注意规格说明/设计如何影响方法。\n```\n\n**执行：** 对于每个任务：\n\n1. 宣布：\"正在处理任务N：[描述]\"\n2. 在代码库中实现变更\n3. 自然地引用规格说明/设计：\"规格说明说X，所以我做Y\"\n4. 在tasks.md中标记完成：`- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n5. 简要状态：\"✓ 任务N完成\"\n\n保持叙述轻量——不要过度解释每一行代码。\n\n所有任务后：\n\n```\n## 实现完成\n\n所有任务完成：\n- [x] 任务1\n- [x] 任务2\n- [x] ...\n\n变更已实现！还有一个步骤——让我们归档它。\n```\n\n---\n\n## 阶段10：归档\n\n**解释：**\n```\n## 归档\n\n当变更完成时，我们归档它。这将把它从 `openspec/changes/` 移动到 `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`。\n\n归档的变更成为您项目的决策历史——您随时可以找到它们来理解为什么某物以某种方式构建。\n```\n\n**执行：**\n```bash\nopenspec-cn archive \"<name>\"\n```\n\n**显示：**\n```\n已归档到：`openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`\n\n变更现在是您项目历史的一部分。代码在您的代码库中，决策记录被保留。\n```\n\n---\n\n## 阶段11：回顾与下一步\n\n```\n## 恭喜！\n\n您刚刚完成了一个完整的OpenSpec周期：\n\n1. **探索** - 思考问题\n2. **新建** - 创建变更容器\n3. **提案** - 捕获为什么\n4. **规格说明** - 详细定义什么\n5. **设计** - 决定如何\n6. **任务** - 分解为步骤\n7. **应用** - 实现工作\n8. **归档** - 保留记录\n\n同样的节奏适用于任何大小的变更——小修复或主要功能。\n\n---\n\n## 命令参考\n\n| 命令 | 做什么 |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | 在工作之前/期间思考问题 |\n| `/opsx:new` | 开始新变更，逐步通过产出物 |\n| `/opsx:ff` | 快进：一次创建所有产出物 |\n| `/opsx:continue` | 继续处理现有变更 |\n| `/opsx:apply` | 实现变更中的任务 |\n| `/opsx:verify` | 验证实现是否匹配产出物 |\n| `/opsx:archive` | 归档完成的变更 |\n\n---\n\n## 下一步是什么？\n\n尝试 `/opsx:new` 或 `/opsx:ff` 在您实际想要构建的内容上。您现在掌握了节奏！\n```\n\n---\n\n## 优雅退出处理\n\n### 用户想要中途停止\n\n如果用户说他们需要停止、想要暂停或似乎不投入：\n\n```\n没问题！您的变更保存在 `openspec/changes/<name>/`。\n\n要在以后继续：\n- `/opsx:continue <name>` - 恢复产出物创建\n- `/opsx:apply <name>` - 跳转到实现（如果任务存在）\n\n工作不会丢失。随时回来。\n```\n\n优雅退出，不施加压力。\n\n### 用户只想要命令参考\n\n如果用户说他们只想看命令或跳过教程：\n\n```\n## OpenSpec快速参考\n\n| 命令 | 做什么 |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | 思考问题（无代码更改） |\n| `/opsx:new <name>` | 开始新变更，逐步进行 |\n| `/opsx:ff <name>` | 快进：一次创建所有产出物 |\n| `/opsx:continue <name>` | 继续现有变更 |\n| `/opsx:apply <name>` | 实现任务 |\n| `/opsx:verify <name>` | 验证实现 |\n| `/opsx:archive <name>` | 完成后归档 |\n\n尝试 `/opsx:new` 开始您的第一个变更，或 `/opsx:ff` 如果您想快速移动。\n```\n\n优雅退出。\n\n---\n\n## 护栏\n\n- **遵循解释→执行→显示→暂停模式**在关键转换点（探索后、提案草案后、任务后、归档后）\n- **在实现期间保持叙述轻量**——教学而不说教\n- **不要跳过阶段**即使变更很小——目标是教学工作流程\n- **在标记点暂停等待确认**，但不要过度暂停\n- **优雅处理退出**——从不施压用户继续\n- **使用真实代码库任务**——不模拟或使用虚假示例\n- **温和调整范围**——引导向更小任务但尊重用户选择\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:29:45.455Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing guided workflow integration with OpenSpec","zh":"非常适合需要引导式工作流集成的 OpenSpec 开发代理","ja":"OpenSpec とのワークフロー統合を必要とする開発エージェントに最適","ko":"OpenSpec 의 가이드 된 워크플로 통합이 필요한 개발 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan integración de flujo de trabajo guiada con OpenSpec","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement nécessitant une intégration de workflow guidée avec OpenSpec","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine geschützte Workflow-Integration mit OpenSpec benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de integração de fluxo de trabalho orientada com OpenSpec","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, которым требуется интеграция рабочего процесса с руководством OpenSpec","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى دمج تدفق العمل الإرشادي مع OpenSpec"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to initiate and manage complete OpenSpec workflow cycles, including initialization, change creation, and task implementation, utilizing openspec-cn commands and JSON output for seamless interaction","zh":"赋予代理人启动和管理完整的 OpenSpec 工作流周期的能力，包括初始化、更改创建和任务实施，利用 openspec-cn 命令和 JSON 输出实现无缝交互","ja":"OpenSpec の完全なワークフロー周期を開始して管理するエージェントを可能にし、初期化、変更の作成、タスクの実装を openspec-cn コマンドと JSON 出力でシームレスに実行","ko":"에이전트가 OpenSpec 의 전체 워크플로 사이클을 시작하