ppement de logiciels","Rust"],"de":["rust-actor","KI für Rust","Software-Engineering","modulare Orchestrierung","kollaborative Ausführung","Reasoning-Einheiten","Software-Entwicklung","Rust"],"pt":["Rust Actor","IA","Engenharia Rust","Solucções escaláveis","Modular skill orchestration","Tokio","Async/await"],"ru":["Rust Actor","ИИ","Инженерия Rust","Масштабируемые решения","Модульная оркестрация навыков","Tokio","Async/await"],"ar":["Rust Actor","الذكاء الاصطناعي","هندسة Rust","حلول قابلة للتحسين","التحكم المتناسق للمهارات القابلة للتحسين","Tokio","Async/await"]}},"owner":"huiali","repo":"rust-skills","repoPath":"huiali/rust-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.449Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"rust-actor","description":"Actor model expert covering message passing, state isolation, supervision trees, deadlock prevention, fault tolerance, Actix framework, and Erlang-style concurrency patterns.","bodyPreview":"## Solution Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Basic Actor Implementation\n\n```rust\nuse tokio::sync::mpsc::{channel, Sender, Receiver};\nuse std::collections::HashMap;\n\n// Actor trait\ntrait Actor: Send + ''static {\n    type Message: Send + ''static;\n    type Error: std::error::Error;\n\n    fn receive(&mut self, ctx: &mut Context<Self>, msg: Self::Message);\n}\n\n// Actor context\nstruct Context<A: Actor> {\n    mailbox: Receiver<A::Message>,\n    sender: Sender<A::Message>,\n    state: ActorState,\n    supervisor: Opt","body":"## Solution Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Basic Actor Implementation\n\n```rust\nuse tokio::sync::mpsc::{channel, Sender, Receiver};\nuse std::collections::HashMap;\n\n// Actor trait\ntrait Actor: Send + ''static {\n    type Message: Send + ''static;\n    type Error: std::error::Error;\n\n    fn receive(&mut self, ctx: &mut Context<Self>, msg: Self::Message);\n}\n\n// Actor context\nstruct Context<A: Actor> {\n    mailbox: Receiver<A::Message>,\n    sender: Sender<A::Message>,\n    state: ActorState,\n    supervisor: Option<SupervisorAddr>,\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\nenum ActorState {\n    Starting,\n    Running,\n    Restarting,\n    Stopping,\n    Stopped,\n}\n\n// Address handle for sending messages\n#[derive(Clone)]\nstruct Addr<A: Actor> {\n    sender: Sender<A::Message>,\n}\n\nimpl<A: Actor> Addr<A> {\n    pub async fn send(&self, msg: A::Message) -> Result<(), SendError> {\n        self.sender.send(msg).await\n            .map_err(|_| SendError::Disconnected)\n    }\n}\n\n// Example actor\nstruct CounterActor {\n    count: usize,\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug)]\nenum CounterMessage {\n    Increment,\n    Decrement,\n    GetCount(Sender<usize>),\n}\n\nimpl Actor for CounterActor {\n    type Message = CounterMessage;\n    type Error = std::io::Error;\n\n    fn receive(&mut self, ctx: &mut Context<Self>, msg: Self::Message) {\n        match msg {\n            CounterMessage::Increment => {\n                self.count += 1;\n            }\n            CounterMessage::Decrement => {\n                self.count = self.count.saturating_sub(1);\n            }\n            CounterMessage::GetCount(reply) => {\n                let _ = reply.try_send(self.count);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Request-Response Pattern\n\n```rust\nuse tokio::sync::oneshot;\nuse std::time::Duration;\n\n// Request wrapper with response channel\nstruct Request<M, R> {\n    payload: M,\n    response: oneshot::Sender<R>,\n}\n\n// Synchronous request with timeout\nasync fn request<A: Actor, R>(\n    actor: &Addr<A>,\n    msg: A::Message,\n    timeout: Duration,\n) -> Result<R, RequestError> {\n    let (tx, rx) = oneshot::channel();\n\n    let request = Request {\n        payload: msg,\n        response: tx,\n    };\n\n    actor.send(request).await\n        .map_err(|_| RequestError::SendFailed)?;\n\n    tokio::time::timeout(timeout, rx).await\n        .map_err(|_| RequestError::Timeout)?\n        .map_err(|_| RequestError::Canceled)\n}\n\n// Usage example\nasync fn example_request_response() {\n    let (tx, rx) = oneshot::channel();\n\n    let addr = counter_actor.start();\n    addr.send(CounterMessage::GetCount(tx)).await.unwrap();\n\n    let count = rx.await.unwrap();\n    println!(\"Count: {}\", count);\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Supervision Tree\n\n```rust\nuse std::collections::HashMap;\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\nenum SupervisionStrategy {\n    OneForOne,    // Only restart failed child\n    AllForOne,    // Restart all children if one fails\n    RestForOne,   // Restart failed child and all after it\n}\n\nstruct Supervisor {\n    children: HashMap<ChildId, Child>,\n    strategy: SupervisionStrategy,\n    max_restarts: u32,\n    window: Duration,\n}\n\nstruct Child {\n    id: ChildId,\n    addr: Box<dyn std::any::Any + Send>,\n    restart_count: u32,\n    last_restart: Option<Instant>,\n    spec: ChildSpec,\n}\n\nstruct ChildSpec {\n    factory: Box<dyn Fn() -> Box<dyn std::any::Any + Send>>,\n    restart_strategy: RestartStrategy,\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\nenum RestartStrategy {\n    Permanent,   // Always restart\n    Temporary,   // Never restart\n    Transient,   // Restart only on abnormal exit\n}\n\nimpl Supervisor {\n    fn new(strategy: SupervisionStrategy, max_restarts: u32, window: Duration) -> Self {\n        Self {\n            children: HashMap::new(),\n            strategy,\n            max_restarts,\n            window,\n        }\n    }\n\n    async fn handle_child_error(&mut self, child_id: ChildId, error: &dyn std::error::Error) {\n        log::warn!(\"Child {} failed: {}\", child_id, error);\n\n        match self.strategy {\n            SupervisionStrategy::OneForOne => {\n                self.restart_child(child_id).await;\n            }\n            SupervisionStrategy::AllForOne => {\n                for id in self.children.keys().cloned().collect::<Vec<_>>() {\n                    self.stop_child(id).await;\n                }\n                for id in self.children.keys().cloned().collect::<Vec<_>>() {\n                    self.restart_child(id).await;\n                }\n            }\n            SupervisionStrategy::RestForOne => {\n                let ids: Vec<_> = self.children.keys()\n                    .filter(|&&id| id >= child_id)\n                    .cloned()\n                    .collect();\n\n                for id in ids {\n                    self.stop_child(id).await;\n                    self.restart_child(id).await;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    async fn restart_child(&mut self, child_id: ChildId) -> bool {\n        if let Some(child) = self.children.get_mut(&child_id) {\n            child.restart_count += 1;\n\n            // Check restart rate limit\n            if self.should_give_up(child) {\n                log::error!(\"Child {} exceeded max restarts, giving up\", child_id);\n                self.stop_child(child_id).await;\n                return false;\n            }\n\n            child.last_restart = Some(Instant::now());\n            log::info!(\"Restarting child {}\", child_id);\n\n            // Factory creates new instance\n            let new_instance = (child.spec.factory)();\n            child.addr = new_instance;\n\n            true\n        } else {\n            false\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn should_give_up(&self, child: &Child) -> bool {\n        if child.restart_count > self.max_restarts {\n            if let Some(last_restart) = child.last_restart {\n                if last_restart.elapsed() < self.window {\n                    return true;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        false\n    }\n\n    async fn stop_child(&mut self, child_id: ChildId) {\n        if let Some(child) = self.children.remove(&child_id) {\n            log::info!(\"Stopping child {}\", child_id);\n            // Send stop signal\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: Deadlock Prevention with Bounded Mailboxes\n\n```rust\nuse tokio::sync::mpsc;\n\nstruct BoundedMailbox<A: Actor> {\n    receiver: mpsc::Receiver<A::Message>,\n    sender: mpsc::Sender<A::Message>,\n    capacity: usize,\n}\n\nimpl<A: Actor> BoundedMailbox<A> {\n    fn new(capacity: usize) -> Self {\n        let (sender, receiver) = mpsc::channel(capacity);\n        Self {\n            receiver,\n            sender,\n            capacity,\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn capacity(&self) -> usize {\n        self.capacity\n    }\n\n    async fn send_with_backpressure(&self, msg: A::Message) -> Result<(), SendError> {\n        // Will wait if mailbox is full (backpressure)\n        self.sender.send(msg).await\n            .map_err(|_| SendError::Disconnected)\n    }\n\n    fn try_send(&self, msg: A::Message) -> Result<(), TrySendError<A::Message>> {\n        // Returns immediately if mailbox is full\n        self.sender.try_send(msg)\n            .map_err(|e| match e {\n                mpsc::error::TrySendError::Full(msg) => TrySendError::Full(msg),\n                mpsc::error::TrySendError::Closed(msg) => TrySendError::Disconnected(msg),\n            })\n    }\n}\n\n// Usage\nasync fn example_bounded_mailbox() {\n    let mailbox: BoundedMailbox<CounterActor> = BoundedMailbox::new(100);\n\n    // This will block if mailbox is full\n    mailbox.send_with_backpressure(CounterMessage::Increment).await.unwrap();\n\n    // This returns error immediately if full\n    match mailbox.try_send(CounterMessage::Increment) {\n        Ok(_) => println!(\"Sent\"),\n        Err(TrySendError::Full(_)) => println!(\"Mailbox full\"),\n        Err(TrySendError::Disconnected(_)) => println!(\"Actor stopped\"),\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 5: Actor Lifecycle Management\n\n```rust\ntrait LifecycleHandler: Actor {\n    fn pre_start(&mut self, ctx: &mut Context<Self>) {\n        // Initialize resources\n        log::info!(\"Actor starting\");\n    }\n\n    fn post_start(&mut self, ctx: &mut Context<Self>) {\n        // Start timers, establish connections\n        log::info!(\"Actor started\");\n    }\n\n    fn pre_restart(&mut self, ctx: &mut Context<Self>, error: &dyn std::error::Error) {\n        // Clean up resources before restart\n        log::warn!(\"Actor restarting due to: {}\", error);\n    }\n\n    fn post_restart(&mut self, ctx: &mut Context<Self>) {\n        // Reinitialize after restart\n        log::info!(\"Actor restarted\");\n    }\n\n    fn post_stop(&mut self) {\n        // Save state, close connections\n        log::info!(\"Actor stopped\");\n    }\n}\n\n// Example with lifecycle hooks\nstruct DatabaseActor {\n    connection: Option<DatabaseConnection>,\n}\n\nimpl LifecycleHandler for DatabaseActor {\n    fn pre_start(&mut self, ctx: &mut Context<Self>) {\n        // Establish database connection\n        self.connection = Some(DatabaseConnection::new());\n    }\n\n    fn pre_restart(&mut self, ctx: &mut Context<Self>, error: &dyn std::error::Error) {\n        // Close existing connection\n        if let Some(conn) = self.connection.take() {\n            conn.close();\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn post_stop(&mut self) {\n        // Ensure connection is closed\n        if let Some(conn) = self.connection.take() {\n            conn.close();\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n\n## Actor vs Thread Model\n\n| Feature | Thread Model | Actor Model |\n|---------|-------------|-------------|\n| State sharing | Shared memory + locks | Isolated, message passing |\n| Deadlock risk | High (lock ordering) | Low (message queues) |\n| Scalability | Limited by thread count | Millions of actors possible |\n| Fault handling | Manual | Supervision trees |\n| Debugging | Hard (race conditions) | Easier (message sequence) |\n| Memory | Shared | Isolated per actor |\n\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Design Actor Hierarchy\n\n```\nDesign questions:\n  → What state needs isolation? Each isolated state = 1 actor\n  → What operations need sequential processing? Group in same actor\n  → What can fail independently? Separate actors with supervision\n  → What needs to scale? Use actor pool pattern\n```\n\n### Step 2: Choose Messaging Pattern\n\n```\nMessage patterns:\n  → Fire-and-forget: Async send, no response\n  → Request-response: Oneshot channel for reply\n  → Streaming: Channel for multiple responses\n  → Broadcast: Multiple recipients\n```\n\n### Step 3: Set Up Supervision\n\n```\nSupervision strategy:\n  → OneForOne: Independent actors (default choice)\n  → AllForOne: Tightly coupled actors needing consistent state\n  → RestForOne: Sequential dependencies\n\nRestart policy:\n  → Permanent: Critical actors (always restart)\n  → Temporary: One-time tasks (never restart)\n  → Transient: Restart on errors only\n```\n\n\n## Review Checklist\n\nWhen implementing actor systems:\n\n- [ ] Each actor has clear single responsibility\n- [ ] Mailboxes have bounded capacity (prevent memory leaks)\n- [ ] Message types are Send + ''static\n- [ ] No shared mutable state between actors\n- [ ] Supervision strategy appropriate for error handling\n- [ ] Actor lifecycle properly managed (cleanup in post_stop)\n- [ ] No circular message dependencies (deadlock risk)\n- [ ] Timeouts on request-response patterns\n- [ ] Monitoring tracks mailbox size and message latency\n- [ ] Backpressure handled when mailbox is full\n\n\n## Verification Commands\n\n```bash\n# Run tests with actor system\ncargo test --test actor_tests\n\n# Check for deadlocks with timeout\ncargo test --test deadlock_tests -- --test-threads=1 --nocapture\n\n# Profile actor message throughput\ncargo bench --bench actor_bench\n\n# Check memory usage under load\ncargo run --release --bin load_test\n\n# Monitor actor lifecycle events\nRUST_LOG=debug cargo run\n```\n\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n### 1. Circular Message Dependencies (Deadlock)\n\n**Symptom**: Actors waiting for each other''s responses\n\n```rust\n// ❌ Bad: Actor A waits for Actor B, Actor B waits for Actor A\nasync fn actor_a_handler(&mut self, msg: Message) {\n    let response = self.actor_b.request(msg).await;  // Blocks\n    // Actor A is blocked, can''t process Actor B''s request\n}\n\nasync fn actor_b_handler(&mut self, msg: Message) {\n    let response = self.actor_a.request(msg).await;  // Blocks\n    // Deadlock!\n}\n\n// ✅ Good: Use timeouts and avoid circular dependencies\nasync fn actor_a_handler(&mut self, msg: Message) {\n    match tokio::time::timeout(\n        Duration::from_secs(5),\n        self.actor_b.request(msg)\n    ).await {\n        Ok(response) => { /* handle response */ }\n        Err(_) => { /* timeout, handle error */ }\n    }\n}\n\n// Better: redesign to avoid circular dependency\n```\n\n### 2. Unbounded Mailbox Growth\n\n**Symptom**: Memory grows unbounded, OOM crashes\n\n```rust\n// ❌ Bad: unbounded channel\nlet (tx, rx) = mpsc::unbounded_channel();\n\n// Slow consumer can''t keep up, mailbox grows forever\n\n// ✅ Good: bounded channel with backpressure\nlet (tx, rx) = mpsc::channel(100);  // Max 100 messages\n\n// Sender will wait when mailbox is full (backpressure)\ntx.send(msg).await?;\n```\n\n### 3. Blocking Operations in Actor\n\n**Symptom**: Actor becomes unresponsive, messages pile up\n\n```rust\n// ❌ Bad: blocking I/O in actor\nimpl Actor for MyActor {\n    fn receive(&mut self, ctx: &mut Context<Self>, msg: Self::Message) {\n        // Blocks entire actor!\n        let data = std::fs::read(\"file.txt\").unwrap();\n        // Other messages can''t be processed\n    }\n}\n\n// ✅ Good: use async I/O or spawn blocking task\nimpl Actor for MyActor {\n    fn receive(&mut self, ctx: &mut Context<Self>, msg: Self::Message) {\n        let addr = ctx.address();\n        tokio::spawn(async move {\n            // Runs in separate task\n            let data = tokio::fs::read(\"file.txt\").await.unwrap();\n            addr.send(ProcessData(data)).await;\n        });\n        // Actor continues processing messages\n    }\n}\n```\n\n\n## Actix Framework Example\n\n```rust\nuse actix::{Actor, Handler, Message, Context};\n\nstruct MyActor {\n    counter: usize,\n}\n\nimpl Actor for MyActor {\n    type Context = Context<Self>;\n\n    fn started(&mut self, _ctx: &mut Self::Context) {\n        println!(\"Actor started\");\n    }\n\n    fn stopped(&mut self, _ctx: &mut Self::Context) {\n        println!(\"Actor stopped\");\n    }\n}\n\n#[derive(Message)]\n#[rtype(result = \"usize\")]\nstruct Increment;\n\nimpl Handler<Increment> for MyActor {\n    type Result = usize;\n\n    fn handle(&mut self, _msg: Increment, _ctx: &mut Self::Context) -> Self::Result {\n        self.counter += 1;\n        self.counter\n    }\n}\n\n// Usage\n#[actix_rt::main]\nasync fn main() {\n    let actor = MyActor { counter: 0 }.start();\n    let result = actor.send(Increment).await.unwrap();\n    println!(\"Counter: {}\", result);\n}\n```\n\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **rust-concurrency** - Concurrency primitives and patterns\n- **rust-async** - Async message handling\n- **rust-error** - Error propagation in actor systems\n- **rust-channel** - Channel-based communication\n- **rust-performance** - Actor system optimization\n\n\n## Localized Reference\n\n- **Chinese version**: [SKILL_ZH.md](./SKILL_ZH.md) - 完整中文版本，包含所有内容\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:40:48.467Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Systems Programming Agents requiring modular and concurrent execution chains in Rust, leveraging tokio and async/await capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要利用 tokio 和 async/await 功能在 Rust 中构建模块化并发执行链的系统编程智能体。","ja":"Rustにおいて、tokioとasync/await機能を活用したモジュール式で並行実行チェーンを必要とするシステムプログラミングエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Rust에서 tokio와 async/await 기능을 활용하여 모듈화되고 동시 실행 체인이 필요한 시스템 프로그래밍 에이전트에 이상적입니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Programación de Sistemas que requieren cadenas de ejecución modulares y concurrentes en Rust, aprovechando las capacidades de tokio y async/await.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Programmation de Systèmes nécessitant des chaînes d''exécution modulaires et concurrentes en Rust, en exploitant les capacités de tokio et async/await.","de":"Ideal für Systemprogrammierungsagenten, die modulare und konkurrierende Ausführungsketten in Rust benötigen, die die Fähigkeiten von tokio und async/await nutzen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Programação de Sistemas que exigem cadeias de execução modulares e concorrentes em Rust, aproveitando as capacidades do tokio e async/await.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов системного программирования, требующих модульных и параллельных цепочек выполнения в Rust, использующих возможности tokio и async/await.","ar":"مثالي لعميل برمجة الأنظمة التي تتطلب سلاسل تنفيذ متوافقة ومتزامنة في Rust، مستفيدا من قدرات tokio و async/await."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create scalable and fault-tolerant systems by leveraging the rust-actor framework, utilizing tokio''s mpsc channels for message passing and enabling modular skill orchestration through the Actor trait and Context struct, while also supporting async/await for concurrent execution.","zh":"通过利用 rust-actor 框架，使用 tokio 的 mpsc 通道进行消息传递，并通过 Actor trait 和 Context 结构实现模块化技能编排，同时支持 async/await 以实现并发执行，从而使智能体能够创建可扩展且容错的系统。","ja":"rust-actorフレームワークを活用し、メッセージパッシングにtokioのmpscチャネルを利用し、ActorトレイトとContext構造体によるモジュール式スキルオーケストレーションを可能にすることで、エージェントがスケーラブルでフォールトトレラントなシステムを作成できるようにします。また、並行実行のためにasync/awaitもサポートします。","ko":"rust-actor 프레임워크를 활용하고, 메시지 전달을 위해 tokio의 mpsc 채널을 사용하며, Actor 트레이트와 Context 구조체를 통해 모듈식 기술 오케스트레이션을 가능하게 함으로써 에이전트가 확장 가능하고 내결함성 있는 시스템을 생성할 수 있도록 합니다. 또한 동시 실행을 위한 async/await도 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear sistemas escalables y tolerantes a fallos aprovechando el marco de trabajo rust-actor, utilizando canales mpsc de tokio para el paso de mensajes y habilitando la orquestación de habilidades modulares a través del rasgo Actor y la estructura Context, mientras también admite async/await para la ejecución concurrente.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des systèmes évolutifs et tolérants aux défaillances en exploitant le framework rust-actor, en utilisant les canaux mpsc de tokio pour le passage de messages et en permettant l''orchestration modulaire des compétences via le trait Actor et la structure Context, tout en prenant en charge async/await pour l''exécution concurrente.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, skalierbare und fehlertolerante Systeme zu erstellen, indem sie das rust-actor-Framework nutzen, tokio''s mpsc-Kanäle für die Nachrichtenübermittlung verwenden und eine modulare Fähigkeitsorchestrierung durch das Actor-Merkmal und den Context-Baustein ermöglichen, während auch async/await für die konkurrierende Ausführung unterstützt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar sistemas escaláveis e tolerantes a falhas, aproveitando o framework rust-actor, utilizando canais mpsc do tokio para passagem de mensagens e habilitando orquestração de habilidades modulares por meio do traço Actor e struct Context, além de suportar async/await para execução concorrente.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать масштабируемые и отказоустойчивые системы, используя фреймворк rust-actor, а также каналы mpsc от tokio для обмена сообщениями и обеспечивая модульную оркестрацию навыков через трейт Actor и структуру Context, а также поддержку async/await для параллельного выполнения.","ar":"يتمكن العملاء من إنشاء أنظمة قابلة للتوسيع ومدى تحمل الأخطاء، مستفدين من إطار عمل rust-actor، واستخدام قنوات mpsc من tokio لنقل الرسائل، وتمكين تنسيق المهارات المتنقلة من خلال سمة Actor وهيكل Context، بالإضافة إلى دعم async/await للتنفيذ المتزامن."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing concurrent execution chains for complex systems","Building modular and scalable actor-based systems in Rust","Designing fault-tolerant and async-capable actor implementations"],"zh":["为复杂系统实现并发执行链","在 Rust 中构建模块化且可扩展的基于 Actor 的系统","设计具有容错和异步能力的 Actor 实现"],"ja":["複雑なシステムのための並行実行チェーンの実装","Rustにおけるモジュール式でスケーラブルなアクターベースのシステムの構築","フォールトトレラントで非同期対応可能なアクター実装の設計"],"ko":["복잡한 시스템을 위한 동시 실행 체인 구현","Rust에서 모듈화되고 확장 가능한 액터 기반 시스템 구축","내결함성 및 비동기 기능을 갖춘 액터 구현 설계"],"es":["Implementar cadenas de ejecución concurrentes para sistemas complejos","Crear sistemas modulares y escalables basados en actores en Rust","Diseñar implementaciones de actores tolerantes a fallos y capaces de async"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des chaînes d''exécution concurrentes pour des systèmes complexes","Construire des systèmes modulaires et évolutifs basés sur des acteurs en Rust","Concevoir des implémentations d''acteurs tolérantes aux défaillances et capables d''async"],"de":["Implementierung konkurrierender Ausführungsketten für komplexe Systeme","Erstellung modularer und skalierbarer aktorbasierter Systeme in Rust","Entwurf fehlertoleranter und async-fähiger Aktorimplementierungen"],"pt":["Implementação de cadeias de execução concorrentes para sistemas complexos","Construção de sistemas modulares e escaláveis baseados em atores em Rust","Projeto de implementações de atores tolerantes a falhas e capazes de async"],"ru":["Реализация параллельных цепочек выполнения для сложных систем","Построение модульных и масштабируемых систем на основе акторов в Rust","Проектирование реализаций акторов, устойчивых к сбоям и поддерживающих async"],"ar":["تنفيذ سلاسل تنفيذ متوافقة لأنظمة معقدة","بناء أنظمة قابلة للتوسيع ومتوافقة على أساس ممثلين في Rust","تصميم تنفيذات الممثلين مدى تحمل الأخطاء وقادرة على async"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Rust 1.64+ and tokio 1.20+","Limited to Rust ecosystem and async/await runtime","Dependent on tokio''s sync and async primitives"],"zh":["需要 Rust 1.64+ 和 tokio 1.20+","仅限于 Rust 生态系统和 async/await 运行时","依赖于 tokio 的同步和异步原语"],"ja":["Rust 1.64+ および tokio 1.20+ が必要","Rustエコシステムとasync/awaitランタイムに限定される","tokioの同期および非同期プリミティブに依存"],"ko":["Rust 1.64+ 및 tokio 1.20+ 필요","Rust 생태계 및 async/await 런타임으로 제한됨","tokio의 동기 및 비동기 프리미티브에 종속적"],"es":["Requiere Rust 1.64+ y tokio 1.20+","Limitado al ecosistema de Rust y al tiempo de ejecución async/await","Dependiente de los primitivos sincrónicos y asíncrónicos de tokio"],"fr":["Nécessite Rust 1.64+ et tokio 1.20+","Limité à l''écosystème Rust et au runtime async/await","Dépendant des primitives synchrones et asynchrones de tokio"],"de":["Benötigt Rust 1.64+ und tokio 1.20+","Begrenzt auf das Rust-Ökosystem und die async/await-Laufzeit","Abhängig von den synchronen und asynchronen Primitiven von tokio"],"pt":["Exige Rust 1.64+ e tokio 1.20+","Limitado ao ecossistema Rust e tempo de execução async/await","Dependente dos primitivos sync e async do tokio"],"ru":["Требует Rust 1.64+ и tokio 1.20+","Ограничен экосистемой Rust и средой выполнения async/await","Зависит от синхронных и асинхронных примитивов tokio"],"ar":["يتطلب Rust 1.64+ و tokio 1.20+","محدود بنظام Rust و وقت تشغيل async/await","يعتمد على البدائيات المتزامنة وغير المتزامنة من tokio"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
