ciona recomendaciones para mejorar el rendimiento en los resultados de búsqueda orgánica","fr":"L''audit SEO identifie les problèmes et fournit des recommandations pour améliorer les performances dans les résultats de recherche organique","de":"Das SEO-Audit identifiziert Probleme und liefert Empfehlungen, um die Leistung in den organischen Suchergebnissen zu verbessern","pt":"Análise SEO para identificar problemas e melhorar o desempenho de busca orgânica","ru":"Аудит SEO для выявления проблем и улучшения результатов поиска","ar":"فحص تحسين محركات البحث لتحديد المشاكل و تحسين أداء البحث العضوي","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["网站分析","SEO 问题识别","改进建议","搜索引擎排名优化","网站可见性提高"],"ja":["サイト分析","SEO 問題の特定","改善策の提供","検索エンジンランキングの最適化","サイトの可視性の向上"],"ko":["웹사이트 분석","SEO 문제 식별","개선策 제공","검색 엔진 순위 최적화","웹사이트 가시성 향상"],"es":["Identificación de problemas de SEO","Análisis de la estructura del sitio web","Evaluación de la optimización de contenido","Recomendaciones para mejorar el rendimiento","Análisis de palabras clave y competidores","Informes personalizados y detallados"],"fr":["Identification des problèmes de SEO","Analyse de la structure du site web","Évaluation de l''optimisation du contenu","Recommandations pour améliorer les performances","Analyse des mots-clés et des concurrents","Rapports personnalisés et détaillés"],"de":["Identifizierung von SEO-Problemen","Analyse der Website-Struktur","Bewertung der Inhalts-Optimierung","Empfehlungen zur Leistungsverbesserung","Analyse von Schlüsselwörtern und Wettbewerbern","Individuelle und detaillierte Berichte"],"pt":["Identificação de problemas de SEO","Análise de desempenho de busca orgânica","Otimização de conteúdo e estrutura de site","Melhoria da experiência do usuário","Aumento da visibilidade nos resultados de busca"],"ru":["Выявление проблем SEO","Анализ результатов поиска","Оптимизация контента и структуры сайта","Улучшение пользовательского опыта","Повышение видимости в результатах поиска"],"ar":["تحديد مشاكل تحسين محركات البحث","تحليل أداء البحث العضوي","تحسين المحتوى و هيكل الموقع","تحسين تجربة المستخدم","زيادة الظهور في نتائج البحث"]},"keywords":{"zh":["SEO 审计","网站优化","搜索引擎排名","SEO 问题","网站可见性"],"ja":["SEO オーディット","サイト最適化","検索エンジンランキング","SEO 問題","サイトの可視性"],"ko":["SEO 감사","웹사이트 최적화","검색 엔진 순위","SEO 문제","웹사이트 가시성"],"es":["análisis de SEO","optimización de sitios web","mejora de la posición en buscadores","SEO para desarrolladores","herramientas de SEO","audit de SEO","informes de SEO","recomendaciones de SEO","estrategias de SEO"],"fr":["audit SEO","optimisation de sites web","amélioration de la position dans les moteurs de recherche","SEO pour les développeurs","outils de SEO","analyse de SEO","rapports de SEO","recommandations de SEO","stratégies de SEO"],"de":["SEO-Audit","Optimierung von Websites","Verbesserung der Suchmaschinen-Position","SEO für Entwickler","SEO-Tools","SEO-Analyse","SEO-Berichte","SEO-Empfehlungen","SEO-Strategien"],"pt":["análise SEO","otimização de busca","desempenho de busca orgânica","problemas de SEO","melhoria da visibilidade","experiência do usuário"],"ru":["Аудит SEO","Оптимизация поиска","Результаты поиска","Проблемы SEO","Улучшение видимости","Пользовательский опыт"],"ar":["فحص تحسين محركات البحث","تحسين البحث","أداء البحث العضوي","مشاكل تحسين محركات البحث","تحسين الظهور","تجربة المستخدم"]}},"owner":"arditlleshi","repo":"alex-electric","repoPath":"arditlleshi/alex-electric","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.449Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"seo-audit","description":"When the user wants to audit, review, or diagnose SEO issues on their site. Also use when the user mentions SEO audit, technical SEO, why am I not ranking, SEO issues, on-page SEO, meta tags review, or SEO health check. For building pages at scale to target keywords, see programmatic-seo. For adding structured data, see schema-markup.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# SEO Audit\n\nYou are an expert in search engine optimization. Your goal is to identify SEO issues and provide actionable recommendations to improve organic search performance.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore auditing, understand:\n\n1. **Site Context**\n   - What type of site? (Sa","body":"# SEO Audit\n\nYou are an expert in search engine optimization. Your goal is to identify SEO issues and provide actionable recommendations to improve organic search performance.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore auditing, understand:\n\n1. **Site Context**\n   - What type of site? (SaaS, e-commerce, blog, etc.)\n   - What''s the primary business goal for SEO?\n   - What keywords/topics are priorities?\n\n2. **Current State**\n   - Any known issues or concerns?\n   - Current organic traffic level?\n   - Recent changes or migrations?\n\n3. **Scope**\n   - Full site audit or specific pages?\n   - Technical + on-page, or one focus area?\n   - Access to Search Console / analytics?\n\n---\n\n## Audit Framework\n\n### Priority Order\n1. **Crawlability & Indexation** (can Google find and index it?)\n2. **Technical Foundations** (is the site fast and functional?)\n3. **On-Page Optimization** (is content optimized?)\n4. **Content Quality** (does it deserve to rank?)\n5. **Authority & Links** (does it have credibility?)\n\n---\n\n## Technical SEO Audit\n\n### Crawlability\n\n**Robots.txt**\n- Check for unintentional blocks\n- Verify important pages allowed\n- Check sitemap reference\n\n**XML Sitemap**\n- Exists and accessible\n- Submitted to Search Console\n- Contains only canonical, indexable URLs\n- Updated regularly\n- Proper formatting\n\n**Site Architecture**\n- Important pages within 3 clicks of homepage\n- Logical hierarchy\n- Internal linking structure\n- No orphan pages\n\n**Crawl Budget Issues** (for large sites)\n- Parameterized URLs under control\n- Faceted navigation handled properly\n- Infinite scroll with pagination fallback\n- Session IDs not in URLs\n\n### Indexation\n\n**Index Status**\n- site:domain.com check\n- Search Console coverage report\n- Compare indexed vs. expected\n\n**Indexation Issues**\n- Noindex tags on important pages\n- Canonicals pointing wrong direction\n- Redirect chains/loops\n- Soft 404s\n- Duplicate content without canonicals\n\n**Canonicalization**\n- All pages have canonical tags\n- Self-referencing canonicals on unique pages\n- HTTP → HTTPS canonicals\n- www vs. non-www consistency\n- Trailing slash consistency\n\n### Site Speed & Core Web Vitals\n\n**Core Web Vitals**\n- LCP (Largest Contentful Paint): < 2.5s\n- INP (Interaction to Next Paint): < 200ms\n- CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift): < 0.1\n\n**Speed Factors**\n- Server response time (TTFB)\n- Image optimization\n- JavaScript execution\n- CSS delivery\n- Caching headers\n- CDN usage\n- Font loading\n\n**Tools**\n- PageSpeed Insights\n- WebPageTest\n- Chrome DevTools\n- Search Console Core Web Vitals report\n\n### Mobile-Friendliness\n\n- Responsive design (not separate m. site)\n- Tap target sizes\n- Viewport configured\n- No horizontal scroll\n- Same content as desktop\n- Mobile-first indexing readiness\n\n### Security & HTTPS\n\n- HTTPS across entire site\n- Valid SSL certificate\n- No mixed content\n- HTTP → HTTPS redirects\n- HSTS header (bonus)\n\n### URL Structure\n\n- Readable, descriptive URLs\n- Keywords in URLs where natural\n- Consistent structure\n- No unnecessary parameters\n- Lowercase and hyphen-separated\n\n---\n\n## On-Page SEO Audit\n\n### Title Tags\n\n**Check for:**\n- Unique titles for each page\n- Primary keyword near beginning\n- 50-60 characters (visible in SERP)\n- Compelling and click-worthy\n- Brand name placement (end, usually)\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Duplicate titles\n- Too long (truncated)\n- Too short (wasted opportunity)\n- Keyword stuffing\n- Missing entirely\n\n### Meta Descriptions\n\n**Check for:**\n- Unique descriptions per page\n- 150-160 characters\n- Includes primary keyword\n- Clear value proposition\n- Call to action\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Duplicate descriptions\n- Auto-generated garbage\n- Too long/short\n- No compelling reason to click\n\n### Heading Structure\n\n**Check for:**\n- One H1 per page\n- H1 contains primary keyword\n- Logical hierarchy (H1 → H2 → H3)\n- Headings describe content\n- Not just for styling\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Multiple H1s\n- Skip levels (H1 → H3)\n- Headings used for styling only\n- No H1 on page\n\n### Content Optimization\n\n**Primary Page Content**\n- Keyword in first 100 words\n- Related keywords naturally used\n- Sufficient depth/length for topic\n- Answers search intent\n- Better than competitors\n\n**Thin Content Issues**\n- Pages with little unique content\n- Tag/category pages with no value\n- Doorway pages\n- Duplicate or near-duplicate content\n\n### Image Optimization\n\n**Check for:**\n- Descriptive file names\n- Alt text on all images\n- Alt text describes image\n- Compressed file sizes\n- Modern formats (WebP)\n- Lazy loading implemented\n- Responsive images\n\n### Internal Linking\n\n**Check for:**\n- Important pages well-linked\n- Descriptive anchor text\n- Logical link relationships\n- No broken internal links\n- Reasonable link count per page\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Orphan pages (no internal links)\n- Over-optimized anchor text\n- Important pages buried\n- Excessive footer/sidebar links\n\n### Keyword Targeting\n\n**Per Page**\n- Clear primary keyword target\n- Title, H1, URL aligned\n- Content satisfies search intent\n- Not competing with other pages (cannibalization)\n\n**Site-Wide**\n- Keyword mapping document\n- No major gaps in coverage\n- No keyword cannibalization\n- Logical topical clusters\n\n---\n\n## Content Quality Assessment\n\n### E-E-A-T Signals\n\n**Experience**\n- First-hand experience demonstrated\n- Original insights/data\n- Real examples and case studies\n\n**Expertise**\n- Author credentials visible\n- Accurate, detailed information\n- Properly sourced claims\n\n**Authoritativeness**\n- Recognized in the space\n- Cited by others\n- Industry credentials\n\n**Trustworthiness**\n- Accurate information\n- Transparent about business\n- Contact information available\n- Privacy policy, terms\n- Secure site (HTTPS)\n\n### Content Depth\n\n- Comprehensive coverage of topic\n- Answers follow-up questions\n- Better than top-ranking competitors\n- Updated and current\n\n### User Engagement Signals\n\n- Time on page\n- Bounce rate in context\n- Pages per session\n- Return visits\n\n---\n\n## Common Issues by Site Type\n\n### SaaS/Product Sites\n- Product pages lack content depth\n- Blog not integrated with product pages\n- Missing comparison/alternative pages\n- Feature pages thin on content\n- No glossary/educational content\n\n### E-commerce\n- Thin category pages\n- Duplicate product descriptions\n- Missing product schema\n- Faceted navigation creating duplicates\n- Out-of-stock pages mishandled\n\n### Content/Blog Sites\n- Outdated content not refreshed\n- Keyword cannibalization\n- No topical clustering\n- Poor internal linking\n- Missing author pages\n\n### Local Business\n- Inconsistent NAP\n- Missing local schema\n- No Google Business Profile optimization\n- Missing location pages\n- No local content\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Audit Report Structure\n\n**Executive Summary**\n- Overall health assessment\n- Top 3-5 priority issues\n- Quick wins identified\n\n**Technical SEO Findings**\nFor each issue:\n- **Issue**: What''s wrong\n- **Impact**: SEO impact (High/Medium/Low)\n- **Evidence**: How you found it\n- **Fix**: Specific recommendation\n- **Priority**: 1-5 or High/Medium/Low\n\n**On-Page SEO Findings**\nSame format as above\n\n**Content Findings**\nSame format as above\n\n**Prioritized Action Plan**\n1. Critical fixes (blocking indexation/ranking)\n2. High-impact improvements\n3. Quick wins (easy, immediate benefit)\n4. Long-term recommendations\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n- [AI Writing Detection](references/ai-writing-detection.md): Common AI writing patterns to avoid (em dashes, overused phrases, filler words)\n- [AEO & GEO Patterns](references/aeo-geo-patterns.md): Content patterns optimized for answer engines and AI citation\n\n---\n\n## Tools Referenced\n\n**Free Tools**\n- Google Search Console (essential)\n- Google PageSpeed Insights\n- Bing Webmaster Tools\n- Rich Results Test\n- Mobile-Friendly Test\n- Schema Validator\n\n**Paid Tools** (if available)\n- Screaming Frog\n- Ahrefs / Semrush\n- Sitebulb\n- ContentKing\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What pages/keywords matter most?\n2. Do you have Search Console access?\n3. Any recent changes or migrations?\n4. Who are your top organic competitors?\n5. What''s your current organic traffic baseline?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **programmatic-seo**: For building SEO pages at scale\n- **schema-markup**: For implementing structured data\n- **page-cro**: For optimizing pages for conversion (not just ranking)\n- **analytics-tracking**: For measuring SEO performance\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:41:45.482Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Digital Marketing Agents requiring in-depth SEO analysis and optimization capabilities.","zh":"适合需要深入SEO分析和优化能力的数字营销代理。","ja":"デジタルマーケティングエージェントが詳細なSEO分析および最適化機能を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"디지털 마케팅 에이전트가 심도 있는 SEO 분석 및 최적화 기능을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de marketing digital que requieren un análisis y capacidades de optimización de SEO en profundidad.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de marketing numérique nécessitant une analyse et des capacités d''optimisation de SEO en profondeur.","de":"Ideal für digitale Marketingagenten, die eine umfassende SEO-Analyse und Optimierungsfähigkeiten erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Marketing Digital que exigem análise e capacidades de otimização de SEO aprofundadas.","ru":"Идеально для цифровых маркетинговых агентов, требующих глубокого анализа и возможностей оптимизации SEO.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التسويق الرقمي الذين يحتاجون إلى تحليل متعمق وقدرات تحسين SEO."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to identify SEO issues and provide actionable recommendations to improve organic search performance, utilizing site context and product marketing context files like `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` for informed audits.","zh":"赋予代理识别SEO问题的能力，并提供可行的建议以提高有机搜索性能，利用`.claude/product-marketing-context.md`等站点上下文和产品营销上下文文件进行信息审计。","ja":"SEOの問題を特定し、`.claude/product-marketing-context.md`などのサイトコンテキストと製品マーケティングコンテキストファイルを使用して情報に基づいた監査を行うことで、有機検索のパフォーマンスを改善するための実行可能な推奨事項を提供する機能をエージェントに与えます。","ko":"에이전트가 SEO 문제를 식별하고 `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`와 같은 사이트 contexto 및 제품 마케팅 contexto 파일을 사용하여 정보에 기반한 감사를 수행함으로써 유기적인 검색 성능을 개선하기 위한 실행 가능한 추천을 제공할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a identificar problemas de SEO y proporcionar recomendaciones accionables para mejorar el rendimiento de búsqueda orgánica, utilizando archivos de contexto de sitio y contexto de marketing de productos como `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` para auditorías informadas.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''identifier les problèmes de SEO et de fournir des recommandations actionnables pour améliorer les performances de recherche organique, en utilisant des fichiers de contexte de site et de contexte de marketing de produits comme `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` pour des audits éclairés.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, SEO-Probleme zu identifizieren und handhabbare Empfehlungen zur Verbesserung der organischen Suchleistung zu geben, indem sie Kontextdateien für Website und Produktmarketing wie `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` für fundierte Audits nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a identificar problemas de SEO e fornecer recomendações práticas para melhorar o desempenho de busca orgânica, utilizando arquivos de contexto do site e contexto de marketing de produtos como `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` para auditorias informadas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выявлять проблемы SEO и предоставлять действенные рекомендации для улучшения органического поискового показателя, используя контекст сайта и контекст маркетинга продукции, как `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`, для информированных аудитов.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تحديد مشاكل SEO وتقديم توصيات قابلة للتنفيذ لتحسين أداء البحث العضوي، باستخدام ملفات سياق الموقع وسياق تسويق المنتج مثل `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` لفحوصات مدروسة."},"useCases":{"en":["Auditing website structures for SEO compliance","Generating recommendations for keyword optimization","Analyzing site performance metrics for improvement"],"zh":["审计网站结构以符合SEO标准","生成关键词优化建议","分析网站性能指标以改进"],"ja":["SEOコンプライアンスのためにウェブサイト構造を監査する","キーワード最適化のための勧告を生成する","改善のためにサイトパフォーマンスメトリックを分析する"],"ko":["SEO 규정을 준수하기 위한 웹사이트 구조 감사","키워드 최적화를 위한 추천 생성","개선을 위한 사이트 성능 지표 분석"],"es":["Auditoría de estructuras de sitios web para cumplimiento de SEO","Generación de recomendaciones para la optimización de palabras clave","Análisis de métricas de rendimiento de sitio para mejorar"],"fr":["Audit des structures de sites web pour la conformité aux normes SEO","Génération de recommandations pour l''optimisation des mots-clés","Analyse des métriques de performance de site pour l''amélioration"],"de":["Auditing von Website-Strukturen für SEO-Konformität","Erstellung von Empfehlungen für die Optimierung von Schlüsselwörtern","Analyse von Site-Performancemetriken für die Verbesserung"],"pt":["Auditoria de estruturas de sites para conformidade com SEO","Geração de recomendações para otimização de palavras-chave","Análise de métricas de desempenho do site para melhoria"],"ru":["Проверка структуры сайта на соответствие требованиям SEO","Генерация рекомендаций для оптимизации ключевых слов","Анализ метрик производительности сайта для улучшения"],"ar":["فحص هيكل الموقع لامتثاله لمتطلبات SEO","توليد توصيات لتحسين الكلمات الرئيسية","تحليل معايير أداء الموقع لتحسينه"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to site context and product marketing context files","Limited to organic search performance optimization"],"zh":["需要访问站点上下文和产品营销上下文文件","仅限于有机搜索性能优化"],"ja":["サイトコンテキストと製品マーケティングコンテキストファイルへのアクセスが必要","有機検索のパフォーマンス最適化のみに限定される"],"ko":["사이트 contexto 및 제품 마케팅 contexto 파일에 대한 액세스가 필요함","유기적인 검색 성능 최적화에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere acceso a archivos de contexto de sitio y contexto de marketing de productos","Limitado a la optimización del rendimiento de búsqueda orgánica"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès aux fichiers de contexte de site et de contexte de marketing de produits","Limité à l''optimisation des performances de recherche organique"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf Kontextdateien für Website und Produktmarketing","Begrenzt auf die Optimierung der organischen Suchleistung"],"pt":["Exige acesso a arquivos de contexto do site e contexto de marketing de produtos","Limitado à otimização do desempenho de busca orgânica"],"ru":["Требует доступа к контексту сайта и контексту маркетинга продукции","Ограничен оптимизацией органического поискового показателя"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى ملفات سياق الموقع وسياق تسويق المنتج","محدود بتحسين أداء البحث العضوي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('maskelog/Daegu_bus_flutter_app/systematic-debugging', 'community', 'maskelog', 'Daegu_bus_flutter_app', 'maskelog/Daegu_bus_flutter_app', 'systematic-debugging', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.449Z', '2026-02-18T06:41:50.018Z', NULL, '{"id":"maskelog/Daegu_bus_flutter_app/systematic-debugging","name":"systematic-debugging","description":{"zh":"系统化调试是一种通过找到根源来解决技术问题的方法。它强调在提出解决方案之前必须进行彻底的调查","ja":"体系的デバッグは、根本原因を発見することでテクニカルイシューを解決する方法です。解決策を提案する前に徹底的な調査を行うことを強調しています","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 근본 원인을 찾아 기술 문제를 해결하는 방법입니다. 해결책을 제안하기 전에 철저한 조사해야 함을 강조합니다","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque para identificar y solucionar problemas de manera eficiente. Siempre encuentra la causa raíz antes de intentar soluciones.","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche pour identifier et résoudre les problèmes de manière efficace. Trouvez toujours la cause profonde avant d''essayer des solutions.","de":"Das systematische Debugging ist ein Ansatz, um Probleme effizient zu identifizieren und zu lösen. Finden Sie immer die Ursache, bevor Sie Lösungen versuchen.","pt":"A depuração sistemática é uma abordagem eficaz para resolver problemas técnicos, focando na identificação da causa raiz antes de propor soluções.","ru":"Системная отладка - это эффективный подход к решению технических проблем, основанный на идентификации коренной причины перед предложением решений.","ar":"التصحيح المنهجي هو نهج فعال لحل المشكلات الفنية، يركز على تحديد السبب الجذري قبل اقتراح الحلول.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"系统化调试技术","ja":"体系的デバッグ手法","ko":"시스템 디버깅 기법","es":"Depuración Sistemática: Encontrar la Causa Raíz","fr":"Débogage Systématique: Trouver la Cause Profonde","de":"Systematisches Debugging: Die Ursache Finden","pt":"Depuração Sistemática: Encontre a Causa Raiz","ru":"Системная отладка: найдите коренную причину","ar":"التصحيح المنهجي: اكتشف السبب الجذري","en":"systematic-debugging"},"description":{"zh":"系统化调试是一种通过找到根源来解决技术问题的方法。它强调在提出解决方案之前必须进行彻底的调查","ja":"体系的デバッグは、根本原因を発見することでテクニカルイシューを解決する方法です。解決策を提案する前に徹底的な調査を行うことを強調しています","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 근본 원인을 찾아 기술 문제를 해결하는 방법입니다. 해결책을 제안하기 전에 철저한 조사해야 함을 강조합니다","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque para identificar y solucionar problemas de manera eficiente. Siempre encuentra la causa raíz antes de intentar soluci...","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche pour identifier et résoudre les problèmes de manière efficace. Trouvez toujours la cause profonde avant d''essayer d...","de":"Das systematische Debugging ist ein Ansatz, um Probleme effizient zu identifizieren und zu lösen. Finden Sie immer die Ursache, bevor Sie Lösungen versuchen.","pt":"A depuração sistemática é uma abordagem eficaz para resolver problemas técnicos, focando na identificação da causa raiz antes de propor soluções.","ru":"Системная отладка - это эффективный подход к решению технических проблем, основанный на идентификации коренной причины перед предложением решений.","ar":"التصحيح المنهجي هو نهج فعال لحل المشكلات الفنية، يركز على تحديد السبب الجذري قبل اقتراح الحلول.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["找到根源","彻底调查","不提出随机解决方案","遵循铁律原则","适用于任何技术问题"],"ja":["根本原因の特定","徹底的な調査","ランダムな解決策の提出なし","鉄則原則の遵守","あらゆるテクニカルイシューに適用"],"ko":["근본 원인 찾기","철저한 조사","임의의 해결책 제안 안 함","철칙 원칙 준수","모든 기술 문제에 적용"],"es":["Identificación de la causa raíz","Solución de problemas de manera eficiente","Evitación de soluciones temporales","Aplicación a cualquier problema técnico","Inclusión de pruebas y depuración"],"fr":["Identification de la cause profonde","Résolution de problèmes de manière efficace","Évitement de solutions temporaires","Application à tout problème technique","Inclusion de tests et de débogage"],"de":["Identifizierung der Ursache","Lösung von Problemen auf effiziente Weise","Vermeidung von temporären Lösungen","Anwendung auf jedes technische Problem","Einschließlich Tests und Debugging"],"pt":["Identificação da causa raiz","Análise sistemática de problemas","Resolução eficaz de problemas técnicos","Redução de tempo e esforço","Melhoria da qualidade do código"],"ru":["Идентификация коренной причины","Системный анализ проблем","Эффективное решение технических проблем","Сокращение времени и усилий","Улучшение качества кода"],"ar":["تحديد السبب الجذري","تحليل منهجي للمشكلات","حل فعال للمشكلات الفنية","تقليل الوقت والجهد","تحسين جودة الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["系统化调试","技术问题解决","根源分析","调试方法","软件开发","编程调试"],"ja":["体系的デバッグ","テクニカルイシュー解決","根本原因分析","デバッグ手法","ソフトウェア開発","プログラミングデバッグ"],"ko":["시스템 디버깅","기술 문제 해결","근본 원인 분석","디버깅 방법","소프트웨어 개발","프로그래밍 디버깅"],"es":["depuración sistemática","causa raíz","solución de problemas","eficiencia","debugging","pruebas","tecnología"],"fr":["débogage systématique","cause profonde","résolution de problèmes","efficacité","débogage","tests","technologie"],"de":["systematisches Debugging","Ursache","Fehlerbehebung","Effizienz","Debugging","Tests","Technologie"],"pt":["depuração sistemática","resolução de problemas","causa raiz","análise de problemas","desenvolvimento de software","qualidade do código"],"ru":["системная отладка","решение проблем","коренная причина","анализ проблем","разработка программного обеспечения","качество кода"],"ar":["التصحيح المنهجي","حل المشكلات","السبب الجذري","تحليل المشكلات","تطوير البرمجيات","جودة الكود"]}},"owner":"maskelog","repo":"Daegu_bus_flutter_app","repoPath":"maskelog/Daegu_bus_flutter_app","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.449Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"systematic-debugging","description":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes","bodyPreview":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs","body":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs in production\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Performance problems\n- Build failures\n- Integration issues\n\n**Use this ESPECIALLY when:**\n- Under time pressure (emergencies make guessing tempting)\n- \"Just one quick fix\" seems obvious\n- You''ve already tried multiple fixes\n- Previous fix didn''t work\n- You don''t fully understand the issue\n\n**Don''t skip when:**\n- Issue seems simple (simple bugs have root causes too)\n- You''re in a hurry (rushing guarantees rework)\n- Manager wants it fixed NOW (systematic is faster than thrashing)\n\n## The Four Phases\n\nYou MUST complete each phase before proceeding to the next.\n\n### Phase 1: Root Cause Investigation\n\n**BEFORE attempting ANY fix:**\n\n1. **Read Error Messages Carefully**\n   - Don''t skip past errors or warnings\n   - They often contain the exact solution\n   - Read stack traces completely\n   - Note line numbers, file paths, error codes\n\n2. **Reproduce Consistently**\n   - Can you trigger it reliably?\n   - What are the exact steps?\n   - Does it happen every time?\n   - If not reproducible → gather more data, don''t guess\n\n3. **Check Recent Changes**\n   - What changed that could cause this?\n   - Git diff, recent commits\n   - New dependencies, config changes\n   - Environmental differences\n\n4. **Gather Evidence in Multi-Component Systems**\n\n   **WHEN system has multiple components (CI → build → signing, API → service → database):**\n\n   **BEFORE proposing fixes, add diagnostic instrumentation:**\n   ```\n   For EACH component boundary:\n     - Log what data enters component\n     - Log what data exits component\n     - Verify environment/config propagation\n     - Check state at each layer\n\n   Run once to gather evidence showing WHERE it breaks\n   THEN analyze evidence to identify failing component\n   THEN investigate that specific component\n   ```\n\n   **Example (multi-layer system):**\n   ```bash\n   # Layer 1: Workflow\n   echo \"=== Secrets available in workflow: ===\"\n   echo \"IDENTITY: ${IDENTITY:+SET}${IDENTITY:-UNSET}\"\n\n   # Layer 2: Build script\n   echo \"=== Env vars in build script: ===\"\n   env | grep IDENTITY || echo \"IDENTITY not in environment\"\n\n   # Layer 3: Signing script\n   echo \"=== Keychain state: ===\"\n   security list-keychains\n   security find-identity -v\n\n   # Layer 4: Actual signing\n   codesign --sign \"$IDENTITY\" --verbose=4 \"$APP\"\n   ```\n\n   **This reveals:** Which layer fails (secrets → workflow ✓, workflow → build ✗)\n\n5. **Trace Data Flow**\n\n   **WHEN error is deep in call stack:**\n\n   See `root-cause-tracing.md` in this directory for the complete backward tracing technique.\n\n   **Quick version:**\n   - Where does bad value originate?\n   - What called this with bad value?\n   - Keep tracing up until you find the source\n   - Fix at source, not at symptom\n\n### Phase 2: Pattern Analysis\n\n**Find the pattern before fixing:**\n\n1. **Find Working Examples**\n   - Locate similar working code in same codebase\n   - What works that''s similar to what''s broken?\n\n2. **Compare Against References**\n   - If implementing pattern, read reference implementation COMPLETELY\n   - Don''t skim - read every line\n   - Understand the pattern fully before applying\n\n3. **Identify Differences**\n   - What''s different between working and broken?\n   - List every difference, however small\n   - Don''t assume \"that can''t matter\"\n\n4. **Understand Dependencies**\n   - What other components does this need?\n   - What settings, config, environment?\n   - What assumptions does it make?\n\n### Phase 3: Hypothesis and Testing\n\n**Scientific method:**\n\n1. **Form Single Hypothesis**\n   - State clearly: \"I think X is the root cause because Y\"\n   - Write it down\n   - Be specific, not vague\n\n2. **Test Minimally**\n   - Make the SMALLEST possible change to test hypothesis\n   - One variable at a time\n   - Don''t fix multiple things at once\n\n3. **Verify Before Continuing**\n   - Did it work? Yes → Phase 4\n   - Didn''t work? Form NEW hypothesis\n   - DON''T add more fixes on top\n\n4. **When You Don''t Know**\n   - Say \"I don''t understand X\"\n   - Don''t pretend to know\n   - Ask for help\n   - Research more\n\n### Phase 4: Implementation\n\n**Fix the root cause, not the symptom:**\n\n1. **Create Failing Test Case**\n   - Simplest possible reproduction\n   - Automated test if possible\n   - One-off test script if no framework\n   - MUST have before fixing\n   - Use the `superpowers:test-driven-development` skill for writing proper failing tests\n\n2. **Implement Single Fix**\n   - Address the root cause identified\n   - ONE change at a time\n   - No \"while I''m here\" improvements\n   - No bundled refactoring\n\n3. **Verify Fix**\n   - Test passes now?\n   - No other tests broken?\n   - Issue actually resolved?\n\n4. **If Fix Doesn''t Work**\n   - STOP\n   - Count: How many fixes have you tried?\n   - If < 3: Return to Phase 1, re-analyze with new information\n   - **If ≥ 3: STOP and question the architecture (step 5 below)**\n   - DON''T attempt Fix #4 without architectural discussion\n\n5. **If 3+ Fixes Failed: Question Architecture**\n\n   **Pattern indicating architectural problem:**\n   - Each fix reveals new shared state/coupling/problem in different place\n   - Fixes require \"massive refactoring\" to implement\n   - Each fix creates new symptoms elsewhere\n\n   **STOP and question fundamentals:**\n   - Is this pattern fundamentally sound?\n   - Are we \"sticking with it through sheer inertia\"?\n   - Should we refactor architecture vs. continue fixing symptoms?\n\n   **Discuss with your human partner before attempting more fixes**\n\n   This is NOT a failed hypothesis - this is a wrong architecture.\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Follow Process\n\nIf you catch yourself thinking:\n- \"Quick fix for now, investigate later\"\n- \"Just try changing X and see if it works\"\n- \"Add multiple changes, run tests\"\n- \"Skip the test, I''ll manually verify\"\n- \"It''s probably X, let me fix that\"\n- \"I don''t fully understand but this might work\"\n- \"Pattern says X but I''ll adapt it differently\"\n- \"Here are the main problems: [lists fixes without investigation]\"\n- Proposing solutions before tracing data flow\n- **\"One more fix attempt\" (when already tried 2+)**\n- **Each fix reveals new problem in different place**\n\n**ALL of these mean: STOP. Return to Phase 1.**\n\n**If 3+ fixes failed:** Question the architecture (see Phase 4.5)\n\n## your human partner''s Signals You''re Doing It Wrong\n\n**Watch for these redirections:**\n- \"Is that not happening?\" - You assumed without verifying\n- \"Will it show us...?\" - You should have added evidence gathering\n- \"Stop guessing\" - You''re proposing fixes without understanding\n- \"Ultrathink this\" - Question fundamentals, not just symptoms\n- \"We''re stuck?\" (frustrated) - Your approach isn''t working\n\n**When you see these:** STOP. Return to Phase 1.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Issue is simple, don''t need process\" | Simple issues have root causes too. Process is fast for simple bugs. |\n| \"Emergency, no time for process\" | Systematic debugging is FASTER than guess-and-check thrashing. |\n| \"Just try this first, then investigate\" | First fix sets the pattern. Do it right from the start. |\n| \"I''ll write test after confirming fix works\" | Untested fixes don''t stick. Test first proves it. |\n| \"Multiple fixes at once saves time\" | Can''t isolate what worked. Causes new bugs. |\n| \"Reference too long, I''ll adapt the pattern\" | Partial understanding guarantees bugs. Read it completely. |\n| \"I see the problem, let me fix it\" | Seeing symptoms ≠ understanding root cause. |\n| \"One more fix attempt\" (after 2+ failures) | 3+ failures = architectural problem. Question pattern, don''t fix again. |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Phase | Key Activities | Success Criteria |\n|-------|---------------|------------------|\n| **1. Root Cause** | Read errors, reproduce, check changes, gather evidence | Understand WHAT and WHY |\n| **2. Pattern** | Find working examples, compare | Identify differences |\n| **3. Hypothesis** | Form theory, test minimally | Confirmed or new hypothesis |\n| **4. Implementation** | Create test, fix, verify | Bug resolved, tests pass |\n\n## When Process Reveals \"No Root Cause\"\n\nIf systematic investigation reveals issue is truly environmental, timing-dependent, or external:\n\n1. You''ve completed the process\n2. Document what you investigated\n3. Implement appropriate handling (retry, timeout, error message)\n4. Add monitoring/logging for future investigation\n\n**But:** 95% of \"no root cause\" cases are incomplete investigation.\n\n## Supporting Techniques\n\nThese techniques are part of systematic debugging and available in this directory:\n\n- **`root-cause-tracing.md`** - Trace bugs backward through call stack to find original trigger\n- **`defense-in-depth.md`** - Add validation at multiple layers after finding root cause\n- **`condition-based-waiting.md`** - Replace arbitrary timeouts with condition polling\n\n**Related skills:**\n- **superpowers:test-driven-development** - For creating failing test case (Phase 4, Step 1)\n- **superpowers:verification-before-completion** - Verify fix worked before claiming success\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging sessions:\n- Systematic approach: 15-30 minutes to fix\n- Random fixes approach: 2-3 hours of thrashing\n- First-time fix rate: 95% vs 40%\n- New bugs introduced: Near zero vs common\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:41:50.018Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Technical Troubleshooting Agents needing advanced systematic-debugging capabilities to resolve complex issues","zh":"非常适合需要高级系统调试能力来解决复杂问题的技术故障排除代理","ja":"高度なシステムデバッグ機能を必要とするテクニカルトラブルシューティングエージェントに最適","ko":"복잡한 문제를 해결하기 위해 고급 시스템 디버깅 기능이 필요한 기술적인 문제 해결 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Solución de Problemas Técnicos que necesitan capacidades de depuración sistemática avanzadas para resolver problemas complejos","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Dépannage Technique ayant besoin de capacités de débogage systématique avancées pour résoudre des problèmes complexes","de":"Perfekt für technische Troubleshooting-Agenten, die erweiterte systematische Fehlersuche-Funktionen benötigen, um komplexe Probleme zu lösen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Resolução Técnica que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de depuração sistemática para resolver problemas complexos","ru":"Идеально для технических агентов по устранению неисправностей, которым необходимы продвинутые системные возможности отладки для решения сложных проблем","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الفنيين لحل المشكلات الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات حدسية متقدمة لتحليل المشكلات لفهم المشكلات المعقدة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to identify root causes of technical issues using the Iron Law, ensuring NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST, and providing a systematic approach to debugging test failures and bugs","zh":"赋予代理识别技术问题的根因，使用铁律，确保在调查根因之前不实施修复，并提供一种系统化的方法来调试测试失败和错误","ja":"エージェントが技術的な問題の根本原因を特定することを可能にし、鉄則を使用して根本原因の調査を行わない限り修正を行わないことを保証し、テストの失敗やバグのデバッグに系統的なアプローチを提供する","ko":"에이전트가 기술적인 문제의 근본 원인을 식별할 수 있도록 하며, 철의 법칙을 사용하여 근본 원인 조사를 먼저 수행하지 않으면 수정을 수행하지 않음을 보장하며, 테스트 실패와 버그의 디버깅에 대한 체계적인 접근 방식을 제공","es":"Habilita a los agentes a identificar las causas raíz de los problemas técnicos utilizando la Ley de Hierro, asegurando QUE NO HAYA REPARACIONES SIN INVESTIGACIÓN DE LA CAUSA RAÍZ PRIMERO, y proporcionando un enfoque sistemático para depurar fallos de prueba y errores","fr":"Habilite les agents à identifier les causes profondes des problèmes techniques en utilisant la Loi de Fer, en assurant AUCUNE CORRECTION SANS ENQUÊTE SUR LA CAUSE PROFONDE D''ABORD, et en fournissant une approche systématique pour déboguer les échecs de test et les bogues","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Ursachen von technischen Problemen unter Verwendung des Eisernen Gesetzes zu identifizieren, sicherzustellen, dass ES KEINE REPARATUREN OHNE URSACHENFORSCHUNG ERST GIBT, und bietet einen systematischen Ansatz zur Fehlersuche bei Testfehlern und Fehlern","pt":"Habilita os agentes a identificar as causas raiz dos problemas técnicos usando a Lei de Ferro, garantindo NENHUMA CORREÇÃO SEM INVESTIGAÇÃO DA CAUSA RAIZ EM PRIMEIRO LUGAR, e fornecendo uma abordagem sistemática para depurar falhas de teste e bugs","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выявлять коренные причины технических проблем с помощью Железного закона, гарантируя НИКАКИХ ИСПРАВЛЕНИЙ БЕЗ РАССЛЕДОВАНИЯ КОРЕННОЙ ПРИЧИНЫ СНАЧАЛА, и предоставляя системный подход к отладке сбоев тестирования и ошибок","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تحديد الأسباب الجذرية للمشكلات الفنية باستخدام القانون الحديدي، وضمان عدم وجود إصلاحات بدون تحقيق في السبب الجذري أولاً، وتوفير نهج منهجي لتحليل اختبار الفشل والخروقات"},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging test failures using a systematic approach","Identifying root causes of complex technical issues","Resolving bugs without introducing new issues"],"zh":["使用系统化的方法调试测试失败","识别复杂技术问题的根因","在不引入新问题的情况下解决错误"],"ja":["系統的なアプローチを使用してテストの失敗をデバッグする","複雑な技術的な問題の根本原因を特定する","新しい問題を導入せずにバグを解決する"],"ko":["체계적인 방법을 사용하여 테스트 실패를 디버깅","복잡한 기술적인 문제의 근본 원인을 식별","새로운 문제를 도입하지 않고 버그를 해결"],"es":["Depuración de fallos de prueba utilizando un enfoque sistemático","Identificación de las causas raíz de problemas técnicos complejos","Resolución de errores sin introducir nuevos problemas"],"fr":["Débogage des échecs de test à l''aide d''une approche systématique","Identification des causes profondes de problèmes techniques complexes","Résolution de bogues sans introduire de nouveaux problèmes"],"de":["Fehlersuche bei Testfehlern unter Verwendung eines systematischen Ansatzes","Identifizierung der Ursachen von komplexen technischen Problemen","Behebung von Fehlern ohne neue Probleme einzuführen"],"pt":["Depuração de falhas de teste usando uma abordagem sistemática","Identificação das causas raiz de problemas técnicos complexos","Resolução de bugs sem introduzir novos problemas"],"ru":["Отладка сбоев тестирования с помощью системного подхода","Выявление коренных причин сложных технических проблем","Исправление ошибок без введения новых проблем"],"ar":["تحليل اختبار الفشل باستخدام نهج منهجي","تحديد الأسباب الجذرية للمشكلات الفنية المعقدة","حل الخروقات بدون إدخال مشكلات جديدة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to the Iron Law","Violating the letter of the process is considered violating the spirit of debugging"],"zh":["需要遵守铁律","违反流程的字面意义被认为是违反调试的精神"],"ja":["鉄則に従う必要がある","プロセスの文字通りに違反することはデバッグの精神に違反するものとみなされる"],"ko":["철의 법칙을 준수해야 함","프로세스의 문자를 위반하는 것은 디버깅의 정신을 위반하는 것으로 간주됨"],"es":["Requiere adherirse a la Ley de Hierro","Violación de la letra del proceso se considera violación del espíritu de la depuración"],"fr":["Exige l''adhésion à la Loi de Fer","La violation de la lettre du processus est considérée comme une violation de l''esprit du débogage"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung des Eisernen Gesetzes","Verletzung des Wortlautes des Prozesses gilt als Verletzung des Geistes der Fehlersuche"],"pt":["Exige aderência à Lei de Ferro","Violar a letra do processo é considerado violar o espírito da depuração"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения Железного закона","Нарушение буквы процесса считается нарушением духа отладки"],"ar":["يتطلب امتثالاً للقانون الحديدي","ينظر إلى انتهاك حرفية العملية على أنه انتهاك لروح التحليل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('nadavyigal/Running-coach-/seo-audit', 'community', 'nadavyigal', 'Running-coach-', 'nadavyigal/Running-coach-', 'seo-audit', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.449Z', '2026-02-18T06:42:01.369Z', NULL, '{"id":"nadavyigal/Running-coach-/seo-audit","name":"seo-audit","description":{"zh":"SEO审计是一种专家级的搜索引擎优化技术，通过识别网站的问题并提供改进建议来提高搜索引擎排名","ja":"SEO監査は、ウェブサイトの問題点を特定し、改善策を提供して検索エンジンランキングを上げるための専門家レベルの検索エンジン最適化技術です","ko":"SEO 감사는 웹사이트의 문제점을 식별하고 개선 전략을 제공하여 검색 엔진 순위를 높이기 위한 전문가 수준의 검색 엔진 최적화 기술입니다","es":"El análisis de SEO identifica problemas y proporciona recomendaciones para mejorar el rendimiento en búsquedas orgánicas","fr":"L''audit SEO identifie les problèmes et fournit des recommandations pour améliorer les performances de recherche organique","de":"Das SEO-Audit identifiziert Probleme und liefert Empfehlungen zur Verbesserung der Leistung in organischen Suchanfragen","pt":"A análise de SEO é um processo que ajuda a identificar problemas de otimização e melhorar o desempenho de busca orgânica.","ru":"Аудит SEO - это процесс, который помогает выявить проблемы оптимизации и улучшить органические результаты поиска.","ar":"فحص تحسين محركات البحث هو عملية تساعد على تحديد مشاكل التحسين وتحسين أداء البحث العضوي.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"SEO审计工具","ja":"SEO監査ツール","ko":"SEO 감사 도구","es":"Análisis de SEO: Mejora tu posición en buscadores","fr":"Audit SEO: Améliorez votre référencement","de":"SEO-Audit: Verbessern Sie Ihre Suchmaschinen-Position","pt":"Análise de SEO: Otimização de Desempenho de Busca","ru":"Аудит SEO: Оптимизация результатов поиска","ar":"فحص تحسين محركات البحث: تحسين أداء البحث","en":"seo-audit"},"description":{"zh":"SEO审计是一种专家级的搜索引擎优化技术，通过识别网站的问题并提供改进建议来提高搜索引擎排名","ja":"SEO監査は、ウェブサイトの問題点を特定し、改善策を提供して検索エンジンランキングを上げるための専門家レベルの検索エンジン最適化技術です","ko":"SEO 감사는 웹사이트의 문제점을 식별하고 개선 전략을 제공하여 검색 엔진 순위를 높이기 위한 전문가 수준의 검색 엔진 최적화 기술입니다","es":"El análisis de SEO identifica problemas y proporciona recomendaciones para mejorar el rendimiento en búsquedas orgánicas","fr":"L''audit SEO identifie les problèmes et fournit des recommandations pour améliorer les performances de recherche organique","de":"Das SEO-Audit identifiziert Probleme und liefert Empfehlungen zur Verbesserung der Leistung in organischen Suchanfragen","pt":"A análise de SEO é um processo que ajuda a identificar problemas de otimização e melhorar o desempenho de busca orgânica.","ru":"Аудит SEO - это процесс, который помогает выявить проблемы оптимизации и улучшить органические результаты поиска.","ar":"فحص تحسين محركات البحث هو عملية تساعد على تحديد مشاكل التحسين وتحسين أداء البحث العضوي.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["识别网站SEO问题","提供改进建议","提高搜索引擎排名","分析网站结构","优化网站内容"],"ja":["ウェブサイトのSEO問題を特定する","改善策を提供する","検索エンジンランキングを上げる","ウェブサイト構造を分析する","ウェブサイトコンテンツを最適化する"],"ko":["웹사이트의 SEO 문제를 식별한다","개선 전략을 제공한다","검색 엔진 순위를 높인다","웹사이트 구조를 분석한다","웹사이트 콘텐츠를 최적화한다"],"es":["Identificación de problemas de SEO","Análisis de la estructura del sitio web","Optimización de metadatos y encabezados","Mejora de la velocidad de carga del sitio web","Análisis de enlaces y redirecciones"],"fr":["Identification des problèmes de SEO","Analyse de la structure du site web","Optimisation des métadonnées et des en-têtes","Amélioration de la vitesse de chargement du site web","Analyse des liens et des redirections"],"de":["Identifizierung von SEO-Problemen","Analyse der Website-Struktur","Optimierung von Metadaten und Headern","Verbesserung der Ladezeit der Website","Analyse von Links und Umleitungen"],"pt":["Identificação de problemas de otimização","Análise de desempenho de busca orgânica","Recomendações práticas para melhoria","Análise de site e contexto","Verificação de marketing de produto"],"ru":["Выявление проблем оптимизации","Анализ органических результатов поиска","Практические рекомендации для улучшения","Анализ сайта и контекста","Проверка маркетинга продукта"],"ar":["تحديد مشاكل التحسين","تحليل أداء البحث العضوي","توصيات عملية لتحسين","تحليل الموقع والسياق","فحص تسويق المنتج"]},"keywords":{"zh":["SEO审计","搜索引擎优化","网站优化","搜索引擎排名","网站分析","SEO工具"],"ja":["SEO監査","検索エンジン最適化","ウェブサイト最適化","検索エンジンランキング","ウェブサイト分析","SEOツール"],"ko":["SEO 감사","검색 엔진 최적화","웹사이트 최적화","검색 엔진 순위","웹사이트 분석","SEO 도구"],"es":["análisis de SEO","optimización de sitio web","mejora de búsqueda orgánica","posicionamiento en buscadores","SEO técnico","auditoría de SEO"],"fr":["audit SEO","optimisation de site web","amélioration de recherche organique","positionnement dans les moteurs de recherche","SEO technique","audit de SEO"],"de":["SEO-Audit","Website-Optimierung","Verbesserung von organischen Suchanfragen","Suchmaschinen-Positionierung","technisches SEO","SEO-Prüfung"],"pt":["análise de SEO","otimização de busca","desempenho de busca orgânica","recomendações de SEO","análise de site","marketing de produto"],"ru":["аудит SEO","оптимизация поиска","органические результаты поиска","рекомендации SEO","анализ сайта","маркетинг продукта"],"ar":["فحص تحسين محركات البحث","تحسين البحث","أداء البحث العضوي","توصيات تحسين محركات البحث","تحليل الموقع","تسويق المنتج"]}},"owner":"nadavyigal","repo":"Running-coach-","repoPath":"nadavyigal/Running-coach-","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.449Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"seo-audit","description":"When the user wants to audit, review, or diagnose SEO issues on their site. Also use when the user mentions SEO audit, technical SEO, why am I not ranking, SEO issues, on-page SEO, meta tags review, or SEO health check. For building pages at scale to target keywords, see programmatic-seo. For adding structured data, see schema-markup.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# SEO Audit\n\nYou are an expert in search engine optimization. Your goal is to identify SEO issues and provide actionable recommendations to improve organic search performance.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore auditing, understand:\n\n1. **Site Context**\n   - What type of site? (Sa","body":"# SEO Audit\n\nYou are an expert in search engine optimization. Your goal is to identify SEO issues and provide actionable recommendations to improve organic search performance.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore auditing, understand:\n\n1. **Site Context**\n   - What type of site? (SaaS, e-commerce, blog, etc.)\n   - What''s the primary business goal for SEO?\n   - What keywords/topics are priorities?\n\n2. **Current State**\n   - Any known issues or concerns?\n   - Current organic traffic level?\n   - Recent changes or migrations?\n\n3. **Scope**\n   - Full site audit or specific pages?\n   - Technical + on-page, or one focus area?\n   - Access to Search Console / analytics?\n\n---\n\n## Audit Framework\n\n### Priority Order\n1. **Crawlability & Indexation** (can Google find and index it?)\n2. **Technical Foundations** (is the site fast and functional?)\n3. **On-Page Optimization** (is content optimized?)\n4. **Content Quality** (does it deserve to rank?)\n5. **Authority & Links** (does it have credibility?)\n\n---\n\n## Technical SEO Audit\n\n### Crawlability\n\n**Robots.txt**\n- Check for unintentional blocks\n- Verify important pages allowed\n- Check sitemap reference\n\n**XML Sitemap**\n- Exists and accessible\n- Submitted to Search Console\n- Contains only canonical, indexable URLs\n- Updated regularly\n- Proper formatting\n\n**Site Architecture**\n- Important pages within 3 clicks of homepage\n- Logical hierarchy\n- Internal linking structure\n- No orphan pages\n\n**Crawl Budget Issues** (for large sites)\n- Parameterized URLs under control\n- Faceted navigation handled properly\n- Infinite scroll with pagination fallback\n- Session IDs not in URLs\n\n### Indexation\n\n**Index Status**\n- site:domain.com check\n- Search Console coverage report\n- Compare indexed vs. expected\n\n**Indexation Issues**\n- Noindex tags on important pages\n- Canonicals pointing wrong direction\n- Redirect chains/loops\n- Soft 404s\n- Duplicate content without canonicals\n\n**Canonicalization**\n- All pages have canonical tags\n- Self-referencing canonicals on unique pages\n- HTTP → HTTPS canonicals\n- www vs. non-www consistency\n- Trailing slash consistency\n\n### Site Speed & Core Web Vitals\n\n**Core Web Vitals**\n- LCP (Largest Contentful Paint): < 2.5s\n- INP (Interaction to Next Paint): < 200ms\n- CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift): < 0.1\n\n**Speed Factors**\n- Server response time (TTFB)\n- Image optimization\n- JavaScript execution\n- CSS delivery\n- Caching headers\n- CDN usage\n- Font loading\n\n**Tools**\n- PageSpeed Insights\n- WebPageTest\n- Chrome DevTools\n- Search Console Core Web Vitals report\n\n### Mobile-Friendliness\n\n- Responsive design (not separate m. site)\n- Tap target sizes\n- Viewport configured\n- No horizontal scroll\n- Same content as desktop\n- Mobile-first indexing readiness\n\n### Security & HTTPS\n\n- HTTPS across entire site\n- Valid SSL certificate\n- No mixed content\n- HTTP → HTTPS redirects\n- HSTS header (bonus)\n\n### URL Structure\n\n- Readable, descriptive URLs\n- Keywords in URLs where natural\n- Consistent structure\n- No unnecessary parameters\n- Lowercase and hyphen-separated\n\n---\n\n## On-Page SEO Audit\n\n### Title Tags\n\n**Check for:**\n- Unique titles for each page\n- Primary keyword near beginning\n- 50-60 characters (visible in SERP)\n- Compelling and click-worthy\n- Brand name placement (end, usually)\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Duplicate titles\n- Too long (truncated)\n- Too short (wasted opportunity)\n- Keyword stuffing\n- Missing entirely\n\n### Meta Descriptions\n\n**Check for:**\n- Unique descriptions per page\n- 150-160 characters\n- Includes primary keyword\n- Clear value proposition\n- Call to action\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Duplicate descriptions\n- Auto-generated garbage\n- Too long/short\n- No compelling reason to click\n\n### Heading Structure\n\n**Check for:**\n- One H1 per page\n- H1 contains primary keyword\n- Logical hierarchy (H1 → H2 → H3)\n- Headings describe content\n- Not just for styling\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Multiple H1s\n- Skip levels (H1 → H3)\n- Headings used for styling only\n- No H1 on page\n\n### Content Optimization\n\n**Primary Page Content**\n- Keyword in first 100 words\n- Related keywords naturally used\n- Sufficient depth/length for topic\n- Answers search intent\n- Better than competitors\n\n**Thin Content Issues**\n- Pages with little unique content\n- Tag/category pages with no value\n- Doorway pages\n- Duplicate or near-duplicate content\n\n### Image Optimization\n\n**Check for:**\n- Descriptive file names\n- Alt text on all images\n- Alt text describes image\n- Compressed file sizes\n- Modern formats (WebP)\n- Lazy loading implemented\n- Responsive images\n\n### Internal Linking\n\n**Check for:**\n- Important pages well-linked\n- Descriptive anchor text\n- Logical link relationships\n- No broken internal links\n- Reasonable link count per page\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Orphan pages (no internal links)\n- Over-optimized anchor text\n- Important pages buried\n- Excessive footer/sidebar links\n\n### Keyword Targeting\n\n**Per Page**\n- Clear primary keyword target\n- Title, H1, URL aligned\n- Content satisfies search intent\n- Not competing with other pages (cannibalization)\n\n**Site-Wide**\n- Keyword mapping document\n- No major gaps in coverage\n- No keyword cannibalization\n- Logical topical clusters\n\n---\n\n## Content Quality Assessment\n\n### E-E-A-T Signals\n\n**Experience**\n- First-hand experience demonstrated\n- Original insights/data\n- Real examples and case studies\n\n**Expertise**\n- Author credentials visible\n- Accurate, detailed information\n- Properly sourced claims\n\n**Authoritativeness**\n- Recognized in the space\n- Cited by others\n- Industry credentials\n\n**Trustworthiness**\n- Accurate information\n- Transparent about business\n- Contact information available\n- Privacy policy, terms\n- Secure site (HTTPS)\n\n### Content Depth\n\n- Comprehensive coverage of topic\n- Answers follow-up questions\n- Better than top-ranking competitors\n- Updated and current\n\n### User Engagement Signals\n\n- Time on page\n- Bounce rate in context\n- Pages per session\n- Return visits\n\n---\n\n## Common Issues by Site Type\n\n### SaaS/Product Sites\n- Product pages lack content depth\n- Blog not integrated with product pages\n- Missing comparison/alternative pages\n- Feature pages thin on content\n- No glossary/educational content\n\n### E-commerce\n- Thin category pages\n- Duplicate product descriptions\n- Missing product schema\n- Faceted navigation creating duplicates\n- Out-of-stock pages mishandled\n\n### Content/Blog Sites\n- Outdated content not refreshed\n- Keyword cannibalization\n- No topical clustering\n- Poor internal linking\n- Missing author pages\n\n### Local Business\n- Inconsistent NAP\n- Missing local schema\n- No Google Business Profile optimization\n- Missing location pages\n- No local content\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Audit Report Structure\n\n**Executive Summary**\n- Overall health assessment\n- Top 3-5 priority issues\n- Quick wins identified\n\n**Technical SEO Findings**\nFor each issue:\n- **Issue**: What''s wrong\n- **Impact**: SEO impact (High/Medium/Low)\n- **Evidence**: How you found it\n- **Fix**: Specific recommendation\n- **Priority**: 1-5 or High/Medium/Low\n\n**On-Page SEO Findings**\nSame format as above\n\n**Content Findings**\nSame format as above\n\n**Prioritized Action Plan**\n1. Critical fixes (blocking indexation/ranking)\n2. High-impact improvements\n3. Quick wins (easy, immediate benefit)\n4. Long-term recommendations\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n- [AI Writing Detection](references/ai-writing-detection.md): Common AI writing patterns to avoid (em dashes, overused phrases, filler words)\n- [AEO & GEO Patterns](references/aeo-geo-patterns.md): Content patterns optimized for answer engines and AI citation\n\n---\n\n## Tools Referenced\n\n**Free Tools**\n- Google Search Console (essential)\n- Google PageSpeed Insights\n- Bing Webmaster Tools\n- Rich Results Test\n- Mobile-Friendly Test\n- Schema Validator\n\n**Paid Tools** (if available)\n- Screaming Frog\n- Ahrefs / Semrush\n- Sitebulb\n- ContentKing\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What pages/keywords matter most?\n2. Do you have Search Console access?\n3. Any recent changes or migrations?\n4. Who are your top organic competitors?\n5. What''s your current organic traffic baseline?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **programmatic-seo**: For building SEO pages at scale\n- **schema-markup**: For implementing structured data\n- **page-cro**: For optimizing pages for conversion (not just ranking)\n- **analytics-tracking**: For measuring SEO performance\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:42:01.369Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Digital Marketing Agents needing advanced SEO analysis and optimization capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级SEO分析和优化能力的数字营销代理。","ja":"デジタルマーケティングエージェントが高度なSEO分析および最適化機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 SEO 분석 및 최적화 기능이 필요한 디지털 마케팅 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de marketing digital que necesitan capacidades de análisis y optimización de SEO avanzadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de marketing numérique ayant besoin d''une analyse et d''une optimisation de SEO avancées.","de":"Perfekt für digitale Marketing-Agenten, die erweiterte SEO-Analyse- und Optimierungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Marketing Digital que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de análise e otimização de SEO.","ru":"Идеально для агентов цифрового маркетинга, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности анализа и оптимизации SEO.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تسويق رقمي يحتاج إلى قدرات متقدمة لتحليل وضبط محركات البحث."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to identify SEO issues and provide actionable recommendations using product marketing context, site context, and technical SEO audits, leveraging file formats like ''.md'' and understanding site types.","zh":"赋予代理识别SEO问题和提供可行建议的能力，利用产品营销背景、网站背景和技术SEO审计，利用诸如 ''.md'' 之类的文件格式，并理解网站类型。","ja":"エージェントがSEOの問題を特定し、製品マーケティングのコンテキスト、サイトのコンテキスト、技術SEOオーディットを利用して、実行可能な推奨事項を提供する能力を提供します。ファイル形式 ''.md'' を使用し、サイトの種類を理解します。","ko":"에이전트가 SEO 문제를 식별하고 제품 마케팅 contexto, 사이트 contexto, 기술 SEO 감사를 사용하여 실행 가능한 추천을 제공할 수 있는 능력을 제공하며, ''.md''와 같은 파일 형식을 사용하고 사이트 유형을 이해합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a identificar problemas de SEO y proporcionar recomendaciones concretas utilizando el contexto de marketing de productos, el contexto del sitio y auditorías de SEO técnicas, aprovechando formatos de archivo como ''.md'' y comprendiendo los tipos de sitios.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''identifier les problèmes de SEO et de fournir des recommandations concrètes en utilisant le contexte de marketing de produits, le contexte du site et les audits de SEO techniques, en exploitant des formats de fichiers tels que ''.md'' et en comprenant les types de sites.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, SEO-Probleme zu identifizieren und handhabbare Empfehlungen bereitzustellen, indem sie den Produktmarketing-Kontext, den Seitenkontext und technische SEO-Audits nutzen und Dateiformate wie ''.md'' nutzen und Seitentypen verstehen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a identificar problemas de SEO e fornecer recomendações viáveis usando o contexto de marketing de produtos, contexto do site e auditorias técnicas de SEO, aproveitando formatos de arquivo como ''.md'' e compreendendo tipos de site.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выявлять проблемы SEO и предоставлять действенные рекомендации с использованием контекста маркетинга продукта, контекста сайта и технических аудитов SEO, используя форматы файлов типа ''.md'' и понимая типы сайтов.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على تحديد مشاكل محركات البحث وتقديم توصيات قابلة للتنفيذ باستخدام سياق تسويق المنتج وسياق الموقع وتحليلات ضبط محركات البحث الفنية، مع استخدام أنماط الملفات مثل ''.md'' وفهم أنواع المواقع."},"useCases":{"en":["Auditing website SEO performance","Generating technical SEO recommendations","Analyzing product marketing context for optimization"],"zh":["审计网站SEO性能","生成技术SEO建议","分析产品营销背景以优化"],"ja":["WebサイトのSEOパフォーマンスを監査する","技術SEOの推奨事項を生成する","最適化のために製品マーケティングコンテキストを分析する"],"ko":["웹사이트 SEO 성능 감사","기술 SEO 추천 생성","최적화를 위한 제품 마케팅 컨텍스트 분석"],"es":["Auditoría del rendimiento de SEO del sitio web","Generación de recomendaciones técnicas de SEO","Análisis del contexto de marketing de productos para la optimización"],"fr":["Audit des performances de SEO du site Web","Génération de recommandations techniques de SEO","Analyse du contexte de marketing de produits pour l''optimisation"],"de":["Prüfung der SEO-Leistung der Website","Erstellung technischer SEO-Empfehlungen","Analyse des Produktmarketing-Kontexts für die Optimierung"],"pt":["Auditoria do desempenho de SEO do site","Geração de recomendações técnicas de SEO","Análise do contexto de marketing de produtos para otimização"],"ru":["Аудит производительности SEO сайта","Генерация технических рекомендаций SEO","Анализ контекста маркетинга продукта для оптимизации"],"ar":["تدقيق أداء محركات البحث للموقع","توليد توصيات فنية لضبط محركات البحث","تحليل سياق تسويق المنتج من أجل التحسين"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to site context information","Dependent on existence of ''.claude/product-marketing-context.md'' file"],"zh":["需要访问网站背景信息","依赖于 ''.claude/产品营销背景.md'' 文件的存在"],"ja":["サイトコンテキスト情報へのアクセスが必要"," ''.claude/製品マーケティングコンテキスト.md'' ファイルの存在に依存"],"ko":["사이트 컨텍스트 정보에 대한 액세스가 필요"," ''.claude/제품 마케팅 컨텍스트.md'' 파일의 존재에 의존"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la información del contexto del sitio","Dependiente de la existencia del archivo ''.claude/product-marketing-context.md''"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès aux informations de contexte du site","Dépend de l''existence du fichier ''.claude/product-marketing-context.md''"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Kontextinformationen der Seite","Hängt von der Existenz der Datei ''.claude/product-marketing-context.md'' ab"],"pt":["Requer acesso às informações de contexto do site","Depende da existência do arquivo ''.claude/product-marketing-context.md''"],"ru":["Требует доступа к информации контекста сайта","Зависит от существования файла ''.claude/product-marketing-context.md''"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى معلومات سياق الموقع","يعتمد على وجود ملف ''.claude/product-marketing-context.md''"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('bakwankawa/lazy-code-skill/systematic-debugging', 'community', 'bakwankawa', 'lazy-code-skill', 'bakwankawa/lazy-code-skill', 'systematic-debugging', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.449Z', '2026-02-18T06:42:48.469Z', NULL, '{"id":"bakwankawa/lazy-code-skill/systematic-debugging","name":"systematic-debugging","description":{"es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque metódico para resolver problemas técnicos, enfocándose en encontrar la causa raíz antes de proponer soluciones","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche méthodique pour résoudre les problèmes techniques, en se concentrant sur la recherche de la cause profonde avant de proposer des solutions","de":"Die systematische Fehlersuche ist ein methodischer Ansatz, um technische Probleme zu lösen, indem man sich auf die Suche nach der Ursache konzentriert, bevor man Lösungen vorschlägt","pt":"A depuração sistemática é um processo que ajuda a encontrar a causa raiz dos problemas técnicos, evitando soluções rápidas e ineficazes","ru":"Системная отладка - это процесс, который помогает найти коренную причину технических проблем, избегая быстрых и неэффективных решений","ar":"التصحيح المنهجي هو عملية تساعد على العثور على السبب الجذري للمشاكل الفنية، وتجنب الحلول السريعة وغير الفعالة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"es":"Depuración Sistemática: Encuentra la Causa Raíz","fr":"Débogage Systématique: Trouver la Cause Profonde","de":"Systematische Fehlersuche: Finde die Ursache","pt":"Depuração Sistemática: Encontre a Causa Raiz","ru":"Системная отладка: найдите коренную причину","ar":"التصحيح المنهجي: ابحث عن السبب الجذري","en":"systematic-debugging"},"description":{"es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque metódico para resolver problemas técnicos, enfocándose en encontrar la causa raíz antes de proponer soluciones","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche méthodique pour résoudre les problèmes techniques, en se concentrant sur la recherche de la cause profonde avant de...","de":"Die systematische Fehlersuche ist ein methodischer Ansatz, um technische Probleme zu lösen, indem man sich auf die Suche nach der Ursache konzentriert, bevor...","pt":"A depuração sistemática é um processo que ajuda a encontrar a causa raiz dos problemas técnicos, evitando soluções rápidas e ineficazes","ru":"Системная отладка - это процесс, который помогает найти коренную причину технических проблем, избегая быстрых и неэффективных решений","ar":"التصحيح المنهجي هو عملية تساعد على العثور على السبب الجذري للمشاكل الفنية، وتجنب الحلول السريعة وغير الفعالة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"es":["Enfoque metódico para resolver problemas técnicos","Enfocarse en encontrar la causa raíz antes de proponer soluciones","Aplicación a cualquier problema técnico","Incluye test de fallos y errores","Proceso estructurado para la resolución de problemas"],"fr":["Approche méthodique pour résoudre les problèmes techniques","Se concentrer sur la recherche de la cause profonde avant de proposer des solutions","Application à tout problème technique","Inclut des tests de défaillance et d''erreurs","Processus structuré pour la résolution de problèmes"],"de":["Methodischer Ansatz zur Lösung technischer Probleme","Konzentration auf die Suche nach der Ursache bevor Lösungen vorgeschlagen werden","Anwendung auf jedes technische Problem","Einschließlich Testfehler und Fehler","Strukturierter Prozess zur Problemlösung"],"pt":["Identificação da causa raiz dos problemas","Evita soluções rápidas e ineficazes","Melhora a eficiência do processo de depuração","Reduz a quantidade de bugs e erros","Aumenta a qualidade do código"],"ru":["Определение коренной причины проблем","Избегает быстрых и неэффективных решений","Улучшает эффективность процесса отладки","Снижает количество ошибок и багов","Повышает качество кода"],"ar":["العثور على السبب الجذري للمشاكل","تجنب الحلول السريعة وغير الفعالة","تحسين كفاءة عملية التصحيح","تقليل عدد الأخطاء والعيوب","تحسين جودة الكود"]},"keywords":{"es":["depuración sistemática","resolución de problemas técnicos","causa raíz","test de fallos","errores","proceso de depuración"],"fr":["débogage systématique","résolution de problèmes techniques","cause profonde","test de défaillance","erreurs","processus de débogage"],"de":["systematische Fehlersuche","Lösung technischer Probleme","Ursache","Testfehler","Fehler","Fehlersuchprozess"],"pt":["depuração sistemática","causa raiz","soluções eficazes","processo de depuração","qualidade do código","redução de bugs"],"ru":["системная отладка","коренная причина","эффективные решения","процесс отладки","качество кода","снижение ошибок"],"ar":["التصحيح المنهجي","السبب الجذري","الحلول الفعالة","عملية التصحيح","جودة الكود","تقليل الأخطاء"]}},"owner":"bakwankawa","repo":"lazy-code-skill","repoPath":"bakwankawa/lazy-code-skill","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.449Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"systematic-debugging","description":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes","bodyPreview":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs","body":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs in production\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Performance problems\n- Build failures\n- Integration issues\n\n**Use this ESPECIALLY when:**\n- Under time pressure (emergencies make guessing tempting)\n- \"Just one quick fix\" seems obvious\n- You''ve already tried multiple fixes\n- Previous fix didn''t work\n- You don''t fully understand the issue\n\n**Don''t skip when:**\n- Issue seems simple (simple bugs have root causes too)\n- You''re in a hurry (rushing guarantees rework)\n- Manager wants it fixed NOW (systematic is faster than thrashing)\n\n## The Four Phases\n\nYou MUST complete each phase before proceeding to the next.\n\n### Phase 1: Root Cause Investigation\n\n**BEFORE attempting ANY fix:**\n\n1. **Read Error Messages Carefully**\n   - Don''t skip past errors or warnings\n   - They often contain the exact solution\n   - Read stack traces completely\n   - Note line numbers, file paths, error codes\n\n2. **Reproduce Consistently**\n   - Can you trigger it reliably?\n   - What are the exact steps?\n   - Does it happen every time?\n   - If not reproducible → gather more data, don''t guess\n\n3. **Check Recent Changes**\n   - What changed that could cause this?\n   - Git diff, recent commits\n   - New dependencies, config changes\n   - Environmental differences\n\n4. **Gather Evidence in Multi-Component Systems**\n\n   **WHEN system has multiple components (CI → build → signing, API → service → database):**\n\n   **BEFORE proposing fixes, add diagnostic instrumentation:**\n   ```\n   For EACH component boundary:\n     - Log what data enters component\n     - Log what data exits component\n     - Verify environment/config propagation\n     - Check state at each layer\n\n   Run once to gather evidence showing WHERE it breaks\n   THEN analyze evidence to identify failing component\n   THEN investigate that specific component\n   ```\n\n   **Example (multi-layer system):**\n   ```bash\n   # Layer 1: Workflow\n   echo \"=== Secrets available in workflow: ===\"\n   echo \"IDENTITY: ${IDENTITY:+SET}${IDENTITY:-UNSET}\"\n\n   # Layer 2: Build script\n   echo \"=== Env vars in build script: ===\"\n   env | grep IDENTITY || echo \"IDENTITY not in environment\"\n\n   # Layer 3: Signing script\n   echo \"=== Keychain state: ===\"\n   security list-keychains\n   security find-identity -v\n\n   # Layer 4: Actual signing\n   codesign --sign \"$IDENTITY\" --verbose=4 \"$APP\"\n   ```\n\n   **This reveals:** Which layer fails (secrets → workflow ✓, workflow → build ✗)\n\n5. **Trace Data Flow**\n\n   **WHEN error is deep in call stack:**\n\n   See `root-cause-tracing.md` in this directory for the complete backward tracing technique.\n\n   **Quick version:**\n   - Where does bad value originate?\n   - What called this with bad value?\n   - Keep tracing up until you find the source\n   - Fix at source, not at symptom\n\n### Phase 2: Pattern Analysis\n\n**Find the pattern before fixing:**\n\n1. **Find Working Examples**\n   - Locate similar working code in same codebase\n   - What works that''s similar to what''s broken?\n\n2. **Compare Against References**\n   - If implementing pattern, read reference implementation COMPLETELY\n   - Don''t skim - read every line\n   - Understand the pattern fully before applying\n\n3. **Identify Differences**\n   - What''s different between working and broken?\n   - List every difference, however small\n   - Don''t assume \"that can''t matter\"\n\n4. **Understand Dependencies**\n   - What other components does this need?\n   - What settings, config, environment?\n   - What assumptions does it make?\n\n### Phase 3: Hypothesis and Testing\n\n**Scientific method:**\n\n1. **Form Single Hypothesis**\n   - State clearly: \"I think X is the root cause because Y\"\n   - Write it down\n   - Be specific, not vague\n\n2. **Test Minimally**\n   - Make the SMALLEST possible change to test hypothesis\n   - One variable at a time\n   - Don''t fix multiple things at once\n\n3. **Verify Before Continuing**\n   - Did it work? Yes → Phase 4\n   - Didn''t work? Form NEW hypothesis\n   - DON''T add more fixes on top\n\n4. **When You Don''t Know**\n   - Say \"I don''t understand X\"\n   - Don''t pretend to know\n   - Ask for help\n   - Research more\n\n### Phase 4: Implementation\n\n**Fix the root cause, not the symptom:**\n\n1. **Create Failing Test Case**\n   - Simplest possible reproduction\n   - Automated test if possible\n   - One-off test script if no framework\n   - MUST have before fixing\n   - Use the `superpowers:test-driven-development` skill for writing proper failing tests\n\n2. **Implement Single Fix**\n   - Address the root cause identified\n   - ONE change at a time\n   - No \"while I''m here\" improvements\n   - No bundled refactoring\n\n3. **Verify Fix**\n   - Test passes now?\n   - No other tests broken?\n   - Issue actually resolved?\n\n4. **If Fix Doesn''t Work**\n   - STOP\n   - Count: How many fixes have you tried?\n   - If < 3: Return to Phase 1, re-analyze with new information\n   - **If ≥ 3: STOP and question the architecture (step 5 below)**\n   - DON''T attempt Fix #4 without architectural discussion\n\n5. **If 3+ Fixes Failed: Question Architecture**\n\n   **Pattern indicating architectural problem:**\n   - Each fix reveals new shared state/coupling/problem in different place\n   - Fixes require \"massive refactoring\" to implement\n   - Each fix creates new symptoms elsewhere\n\n   **STOP and question fundamentals:**\n   - Is this pattern fundamentally sound?\n   - Are we \"sticking with it through sheer inertia\"?\n   - Should we refactor architecture vs. continue fixing symptoms?\n\n   **Discuss with your human partner before attempting more fixes**\n\n   This is NOT a failed hypothesis - this is a wrong architecture.\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Follow Process\n\nIf you catch yourself thinking:\n- \"Quick fix for now, investigate later\"\n- \"Just try changing X and see if it works\"\n- \"Add multiple changes, run tests\"\n- \"Skip the test, I''ll manually verify\"\n- \"It''s probably X, let me fix that\"\n- \"I don''t fully understand but this might work\"\n- \"Pattern says X but I''ll adapt it differently\"\n- \"Here are the main problems: [lists fixes without investigation]\"\n- Proposing solutions before tracing data flow\n- **\"One more fix attempt\" (when already tried 2+)**\n- **Each fix reveals new problem in different place**\n\n**ALL of these mean: STOP. Return to Phase 1.**\n\n**If 3+ fixes failed:** Question the architecture (see Phase 4.5)\n\n## your human partner''s Signals You''re Doing It Wrong\n\n**Watch for these redirections:**\n- \"Is that not happening?\" - You assumed without verifying\n- \"Will it show us...?\" - You should have added evidence gathering\n- \"Stop guessing\" - You''re proposing fixes without understanding\n- \"Ultrathink this\" - Question fundamentals, not just symptoms\n- \"We''re stuck?\" (frustrated) - Your approach isn''t working\n\n**When you see these:** STOP. Return to Phase 1.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Issue is simple, don''t need process\" | Simple issues have root causes too. Process is fast for simple bugs. |\n| \"Emergency, no time for process\" | Systematic debugging is FASTER than guess-and-check thrashing. |\n| \"Just try this first, then investigate\" | First fix sets the pattern. Do it right from the start. |\n| \"I''ll write test after confirming fix works\" | Untested fixes don''t stick. Test first proves it. |\n| \"Multiple fixes at once saves time\" | Can''t isolate what worked. Causes new bugs. |\n| \"Reference too long, I''ll adapt the pattern\" | Partial understanding guarantees bugs. Read it completely. |\n| \"I see the problem, let me fix it\" | Seeing symptoms ≠ understanding root cause. |\n| \"One more fix attempt\" (after 2+ failures) | 3+ failures = architectural problem. Question pattern, don''t fix again. |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Phase | Key Activities | Success Criteria |\n|-------|---------------|------------------|\n| **1. Root Cause** | Read errors, reproduce, check changes, gather evidence | Understand WHAT and WHY |\n| **2. Pattern** | Find working examples, compare | Identify differences |\n| **3. Hypothesis** | Form theory, test minimally | Confirmed or new hypothesis |\n| **4. Implementation** | Create test, fix, verify | Bug resolved, tests pass |\n\n## When Process Reveals \"No Root Cause\"\n\nIf systematic investigation reveals issue is truly environmental, timing-dependent, or external:\n\n1. You''ve completed the process\n2. Document what you investigated\n3. Implement appropriate handling (retry, timeout, error message)\n4. Add monitoring/logging for future investigation\n\n**But:** 95% of \"no root cause\" cases are incomplete investigation.\n\n## Supporting Techniques\n\nThese techniques are part of systematic debugging and available in this directory:\n\n- **`root-cause-tracing.md`** - Trace bugs backward through call stack to find original trigger\n- **`defense-in-depth.md`** - Add validation at multiple layers after finding root cause\n- **`condition-based-waiting.md`** - Replace arbitrary timeouts with condition polling\n\n**Related skills:**\n- **superpowers:test-driven-development** - For creating failing test case (Phase 4, Step 1)\n- **superpowers:verification-before-completion** - Verify fix worked before claiming success\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging sessions:\n- Systematic approach: 15-30 minutes to fix\n- Random fixes approach: 2-3 hours of thrashing\n- First-time fix rate: 95% vs 40%\n- New bugs introduced: Near zero vs common\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:42:48.469Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Technical Agents needing structured issue resolution through systematic debugging methodologies.","zh":"非常适合需要通过系统调试方法论来解决结构化问题的技术代理","ja":"技術エージェントがシステム的なデバッグ手法を通じて構造化された問題解決を必要とする場合に最適","ko":"시스템적인 디버깅 방법론을 통해 구조화된 문제를 해결해야 하는 기술 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Técnicos que necesitan una resolución de problemas estructurada a través de metodologías de depuración sistemática.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents techniques ayant besoin d''une résolution de problèmes structurée grâce à des méthodologies de débogage systématiques.","de":"Perfekt für technische Agenten, die eine strukturierte Problemlösung durch systematische Fehlersuche-Methoden benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Técnicos que necessitam de resolução de problemas estruturada por meio de metodologias de depuração sistemáticas.","ru":"Идеально для Технических Агентов, которым требуется структурированное решение проблем посредством систематических методологий отладки.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكلاء الفنية التي تحتاج إلى حل مشكلات منظم من خلال منهجيات فحص منهجية"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to identify root causes of technical issues using the Iron Law, ensuring NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST, and providing a systematic approach to debugging test failures and bugs.","zh":"赋予代理识别技术问题的根因，使用铁律，确保在调查根因之前不进行修复，并提供一种系统性的方法来调试测试失败和bug","ja":"エージェントが技術的な問題の根本原因を特定することを可能にし、鉄の法則を使用して根本原因の調査を最初に行い、修正を試みる前に、テストの失敗やバグをデバッグするための体系的なアプローチを提供する","ko":"에이전트가 기술적인 문제의 근본 원인을 식별할 수 있도록 하며, 철의 법칙을 사용하여 근본 원인을 먼저 조사하고, 수정을 시도하기 전에 테스트 실패와 버그를 디버깅하는 체계적인 방법을 제공","es":"Habilita a los agentes a identificar las causas raíz de los problemas técnicos utilizando la Ley de Hierro, asegurando NO HAY REPARACIONES SIN INVESTIGACIÓN DE LA CAUSA RAÍZ PRIMERO, y proporcionando un enfoque sistemático para depurar fallos de prueba y errores.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''identifier les causes profondes des problèmes techniques en utilisant la Loi de Fer, en garantissant AUCUNE CORRECTION SANS ENQUÊTE SUR LA CAUSE PROFONDE D''ABORD, et en fournissant une approche systématique pour déboguer les défaillances de test et les bogues.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, die Ursachen technischer Probleme mithilfe des Eisernen Gesetzes zu identifizieren, KEINE REPARATUREN OHNE UNTERSUCHUNG DER URSACHE ZUERST sicherzustellen und einen systematischen Ansatz zur Fehlersuche bei Testfehlern und Fehlern zu bieten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a identificar as causas raiz dos problemas técnicos usando a Lei de Ferro, garantindo NENHUMA CORREÇÃO SEM INVESTIGAÇÃO DA CAUSA RAIZ PRIMEIRO, e fornecendo uma abordagem sistemática para depurar falhas de teste e bugs.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выявлять коренные причины технических проблем с помощью Железного Закона, гарантируя НЕТ ИСПРАВЛЕНИЙ БЕЗ РАССЛЕДОВАНИЯ КОРЕННОЙ ПРИЧИНЫ СНАЧАЛА, и предоставляя системный подход к отладке неисправностей тестирования и багов.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تحديد الأسباب الجذرية للمشاكل الفنية باستخدام القانون الحديدي، مما يضمن عدم وجود إصلاحات بدون تحقيق في السبب الجذري أولاً، وتوفير نهج منهجي لتصحيح اختبارات الفشل والاخطاء"},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging complex test failures","Investigating root causes of recurring bugs","Applying the Iron Law to technical issue resolution"],"zh":["调试复杂的测试失败","调查反复出现的bug的根因","将铁律应用于技术问题的解决"],"ja":["複雑なテストの失敗のデバッグ","再発するバグの根本原因の調査","技術的な問題の解決に鉄の法則を適用"],"ko":["복잡한 테스트 실패를 디버깅","재발하는 버그의 근본 원인을 조사","기술적인 문제 해결에 철의 법칙을 적용"],"es":["Depuración de fallos de prueba complejos","Investigación de las causas raíz de errores recurrentes","Aplicación de la Ley de Hierro a la resolución de problemas técnicos"],"fr":["Débogage de défaillances de test complexes","Enquête sur les causes profondes des bogues récurrents","Application de la Loi de Fer à la résolution de problèmes techniques"],"de":["Fehlersuche bei komplexen Testfehlern","Untersuchung der Ursachen von wiederkehrenden Fehlern","Anwendung des Eisernen Gesetzes auf die Lösung technischer Probleme"],"pt":["Depuração de falhas de teste complexas","Investigação de causas raiz de bugs recorrentes","Aplicação da Lei de Ferro à resolução de problemas técnicos"],"ru":["Отладка сложных неисправностей тестирования","Расследование коренных причин повторяющихся багов","Применение Железного Закона к решению технических проблем"],"ar":["تصحيح اختبارات الفشل المعقدة","تحقيق في الأسباب الجذرية للأخطاء المتكررة","تطبيق القانون الحديدي على حل المشاكل الفنية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to the core principle of finding root cause before attempting fixes","Violating the letter of the systematic debugging process is considered violating the spirit of debugging"],"zh":["需要遵守在尝试修复之前找到根因的核心原则","违反系统性的调试过程被认为是违反了调试的精神"],"ja":["修正を試みる前に根本原因を特定するという核心原則に従う必要がある","体系的なデバッグプロセスに違反することはデバッグの精神に違反することとみなされる"],"ko":["수정 시도를 하기 전에 근본 원인을 식별하는 핵심 원칙을 따라야 함","체계적인 디버깅 프로세스를 위반하는 것은 디버깅의 정신을 위반하는 것으로 간주"],"es":["Requiere adherirse al principio fundamental de encontrar la causa raíz antes de intentar reparaciones","Violación de la letra del proceso de depuración sistemática se considera violación del espíritu de la depuración"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion au principe fondamental de trouver la cause profonde avant de tenter des corrections","La violation de la lettre du processus de débogage systématique est considérée comme une violation de l''esprit du débogage"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung des grundlegenden Prinzips, die Ursache vor der Reparatur zu finden","Verletzung des Wortlautes des systematischen Fehlersuchprozesses gilt als Verletzung des Geistes der Fehlersuche"],"pt":["Exige adesão ao princípio fundamental de encontrar a causa raiz antes de tentar correções","Violar a letra do processo de depuração sistemática é considerado violar o espírito da depuração"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения основного принципа нахождения коренной причины до попыток исправления","Нарушение буквы системного процесса отладки считается нарушением духа отладки"],"ar":["يتطلب الامتثال للمبدأ الأساسي لإيجاد السبب الجذري قبل محاولة الإصلاحات","يُعتبر انتهاك حرفية عملية التصحيح المنهجية انتهاكاً لروح التصحيح"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
