a":"体系的デバッグは、テクニカルな問題の根本原因を特定し、修正する方法です。ランダムな修正と新しいバグを避けることができます","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 기술적인 문제의 근본 원인을 찾아서 수정하는 방법으로, 무작위 수정과 새로운 버그를 피할 수 있습니다","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque para encontrar la causa raíz de los errores, evitando soluciones temporales y parches rápidos","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche pour identifier les causes profondes des erreurs, évitant les solutions temporaires et les patchs rapides","de":"Die systematische Fehlersuche ist ein Ansatz, um die Ursache von Fehlern zu finden und vorübergehende Lösungen und schnelle Patches zu vermeiden","pt":"A depuração sistemática é uma abordagem técnica que busca encontrar a causa raiz dos problemas, evitando soluções rápidas e ineficazes","ru":"Системная отладка - это технический подход, направленный на поиск коренной причины проблем, избегая быстрых и неэффективных решений","ar":"تصحيح 系统ي هو نهج تقني يهدف إلى اكتشاف السبب الجذري للمشكلات، وتجنب الحلول السريعة والغير فعالة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["找到技术问题的根源","避免随机修复","减少新bug的产生","提高调试效率","适用于任何技术问题"],"ja":["テクニカルな問題の根本原因を特定する","ランダムな修正を避ける","新しいバグの発生を減らす","デバッグの効率を高める","あらゆるテクニカルな問題に適用可能"],"ko":["기술적인 문제의 근본 원인을 찾는","무작위 수정을 피하는","新的 버그의 발생을 줄이는","디버깅의 효율을 높이는","모든 기술적인 문제에 적용 가능"],"es":["Encontrar la causa raíz de los errores","Evitar soluciones temporales y parches rápidos","Aplicar un enfoque sistemático para la depuración","Identificar y solucionar problemas técnicos de manera efectiva","Reducir el tiempo de depuración y mejorar la productividad"],"fr":["Identifier la cause profonde des erreurs","Éviter les solutions temporaires et les patchs rapides","Appliquer une approche systématique pour le débogage","Identifier et résoudre les problèmes techniques de manière efficace","Réduire le temps de débogage et améliorer la productivité"],"de":["Die Ursache von Fehlern finden","Vorübergehende Lösungen und schnelle Patches vermeiden","Ein systematischer Ansatz für die Fehlersuche anwenden","Technische Probleme effektiv identifizieren und lösen","Die Fehlersuchzeit reduzieren und die Produktivität verbessern"],"pt":["Identificação da causa raiz","Análise sistemática de problemas","Evitação de soluções rápidas e ineficazes","Melhoria da eficiência na resolução de problemas","Redução do tempo de depuração"],"ru":["Определение коренной причины","Системный анализ проблем","Избежание быстрых и неэффективных решений","Улучшение эффективности решения проблем","Сокращение времени отладки"],"ar":["تحديد السبب الجذري","تحليل 系统ي للمشكلات","تجنب الحلول السريعة والغير فعالة","تحسين الكفاءة في حل المشكلات","تقليل وقت تصحيح الأخطاء"]},"keywords":{"zh":["系统调试","技术问题解决","调试方法","根源分析","随机修复","新bug","调试效率"],"ja":["体系的デバッグ","テクニカルな問題解決","デバッグ方法","根本原因分析","ランダムな修正","新しいバグ","デバッグ効率"],"ko":["시스템 디버깅","기술적인 문제 해결","디버깅 방법","근본 원인 분석","무작위 수정","新的 버그","디버깅 효율"],"es":["depuración sistemática","encontrar la causa raíz","soluciones temporales","parches rápidos","desarrollo de software","pruebas de software","depuración de errores"],"fr":["débogage systématique","identifier la cause profonde","solutions temporaires","patchs rapides","développement de logiciels","tests de logiciels","débogage d''erreurs"],"de":["systematische Fehlersuche","die Ursache finden","vorübergehende Lösungen","schnelle Patches","Software-Entwicklung","Software-Tests","Fehlersuche"],"pt":["depuração sistemática","causa raiz","análise de problemas","eficiência na resolução de problemas","melhoria da depuração","resolução de problemas técnicos"],"ru":["системная отладка","коренная причина","анализ проблем","эффективность решения проблем","улучшение отладки","решение технических проблем"],"ar":["تصحيح 系统ي","السبب الجذري","تحليل المشكلات","كفاءة حل المشكلات","تحسين تصحيح الأخطاء","حل المشكلات الفنية"]}},"owner":"Joseph-VJ","repo":"XAI-Threat-Attribution-IDS","repoPath":"Joseph-VJ/XAI-Threat-Attribution-IDS","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.449Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"systematic-debugging","description":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes","bodyPreview":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs","body":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs in production\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Performance problems\n- Build failures\n- Integration issues\n\n**Use this ESPECIALLY when:**\n- Under time pressure (emergencies make guessing tempting)\n- \"Just one quick fix\" seems obvious\n- You''ve already tried multiple fixes\n- Previous fix didn''t work\n- You don''t fully understand the issue\n\n**Don''t skip when:**\n- Issue seems simple (simple bugs have root causes too)\n- You''re in a hurry (rushing guarantees rework)\n- Manager wants it fixed NOW (systematic is faster than thrashing)\n\n## The Four Phases\n\nYou MUST complete each phase before proceeding to the next.\n\n### Phase 1: Root Cause Investigation\n\n**BEFORE attempting ANY fix:**\n\n1. **Read Error Messages Carefully**\n   - Don''t skip past errors or warnings\n   - They often contain the exact solution\n   - Read stack traces completely\n   - Note line numbers, file paths, error codes\n\n2. **Reproduce Consistently**\n   - Can you trigger it reliably?\n   - What are the exact steps?\n   - Does it happen every time?\n   - If not reproducible → gather more data, don''t guess\n\n3. **Check Recent Changes**\n   - What changed that could cause this?\n   - Git diff, recent commits\n   - New dependencies, config changes\n   - Environmental differences\n\n4. **Gather Evidence in Multi-Component Systems**\n\n   **WHEN system has multiple components (CI → build → signing, API → service → database):**\n\n   **BEFORE proposing fixes, add diagnostic instrumentation:**\n   ```\n   For EACH component boundary:\n     - Log what data enters component\n     - Log what data exits component\n     - Verify environment/config propagation\n     - Check state at each layer\n\n   Run once to gather evidence showing WHERE it breaks\n   THEN analyze evidence to identify failing component\n   THEN investigate that specific component\n   ```\n\n   **Example (multi-layer system):**\n   ```bash\n   # Layer 1: Workflow\n   echo \"=== Secrets available in workflow: ===\"\n   echo \"IDENTITY: ${IDENTITY:+SET}${IDENTITY:-UNSET}\"\n\n   # Layer 2: Build script\n   echo \"=== Env vars in build script: ===\"\n   env | grep IDENTITY || echo \"IDENTITY not in environment\"\n\n   # Layer 3: Signing script\n   echo \"=== Keychain state: ===\"\n   security list-keychains\n   security find-identity -v\n\n   # Layer 4: Actual signing\n   codesign --sign \"$IDENTITY\" --verbose=4 \"$APP\"\n   ```\n\n   **This reveals:** Which layer fails (secrets → workflow ✓, workflow → build ✗)\n\n5. **Trace Data Flow**\n\n   **WHEN error is deep in call stack:**\n\n   See `root-cause-tracing.md` in this directory for the complete backward tracing technique.\n\n   **Quick version:**\n   - Where does bad value originate?\n   - What called this with bad value?\n   - Keep tracing up until you find the source\n   - Fix at source, not at symptom\n\n### Phase 2: Pattern Analysis\n\n**Find the pattern before fixing:**\n\n1. **Find Working Examples**\n   - Locate similar working code in same codebase\n   - What works that''s similar to what''s broken?\n\n2. **Compare Against References**\n   - If implementing pattern, read reference implementation COMPLETELY\n   - Don''t skim - read every line\n   - Understand the pattern fully before applying\n\n3. **Identify Differences**\n   - What''s different between working and broken?\n   - List every difference, however small\n   - Don''t assume \"that can''t matter\"\n\n4. **Understand Dependencies**\n   - What other components does this need?\n   - What settings, config, environment?\n   - What assumptions does it make?\n\n### Phase 3: Hypothesis and Testing\n\n**Scientific method:**\n\n1. **Form Single Hypothesis**\n   - State clearly: \"I think X is the root cause because Y\"\n   - Write it down\n   - Be specific, not vague\n\n2. **Test Minimally**\n   - Make the SMALLEST possible change to test hypothesis\n   - One variable at a time\n   - Don''t fix multiple things at once\n\n3. **Verify Before Continuing**\n   - Did it work? Yes → Phase 4\n   - Didn''t work? Form NEW hypothesis\n   - DON''T add more fixes on top\n\n4. **When You Don''t Know**\n   - Say \"I don''t understand X\"\n   - Don''t pretend to know\n   - Ask for help\n   - Research more\n\n### Phase 4: Implementation\n\n**Fix the root cause, not the symptom:**\n\n1. **Create Failing Test Case**\n   - Simplest possible reproduction\n   - Automated test if possible\n   - One-off test script if no framework\n   - MUST have before fixing\n   - Use the `superpowers:test-driven-development` skill for writing proper failing tests\n\n2. **Implement Single Fix**\n   - Address the root cause identified\n   - ONE change at a time\n   - No \"while I''m here\" improvements\n   - No bundled refactoring\n\n3. **Verify Fix**\n   - Test passes now?\n   - No other tests broken?\n   - Issue actually resolved?\n\n4. **If Fix Doesn''t Work**\n   - STOP\n   - Count: How many fixes have you tried?\n   - If < 3: Return to Phase 1, re-analyze with new information\n   - **If ≥ 3: STOP and question the architecture (step 5 below)**\n   - DON''T attempt Fix #4 without architectural discussion\n\n5. **If 3+ Fixes Failed: Question Architecture**\n\n   **Pattern indicating architectural problem:**\n   - Each fix reveals new shared state/coupling/problem in different place\n   - Fixes require \"massive refactoring\" to implement\n   - Each fix creates new symptoms elsewhere\n\n   **STOP and question fundamentals:**\n   - Is this pattern fundamentally sound?\n   - Are we \"sticking with it through sheer inertia\"?\n   - Should we refactor architecture vs. continue fixing symptoms?\n\n   **Discuss with your human partner before attempting more fixes**\n\n   This is NOT a failed hypothesis - this is a wrong architecture.\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Follow Process\n\nIf you catch yourself thinking:\n- \"Quick fix for now, investigate later\"\n- \"Just try changing X and see if it works\"\n- \"Add multiple changes, run tests\"\n- \"Skip the test, I''ll manually verify\"\n- \"It''s probably X, let me fix that\"\n- \"I don''t fully understand but this might work\"\n- \"Pattern says X but I''ll adapt it differently\"\n- \"Here are the main problems: [lists fixes without investigation]\"\n- Proposing solutions before tracing data flow\n- **\"One more fix attempt\" (when already tried 2+)**\n- **Each fix reveals new problem in different place**\n\n**ALL of these mean: STOP. Return to Phase 1.**\n\n**If 3+ fixes failed:** Question the architecture (see Phase 4.5)\n\n## your human partner''s Signals You''re Doing It Wrong\n\n**Watch for these redirections:**\n- \"Is that not happening?\" - You assumed without verifying\n- \"Will it show us...?\" - You should have added evidence gathering\n- \"Stop guessing\" - You''re proposing fixes without understanding\n- \"Ultrathink this\" - Question fundamentals, not just symptoms\n- \"We''re stuck?\" (frustrated) - Your approach isn''t working\n\n**When you see these:** STOP. Return to Phase 1.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Issue is simple, don''t need process\" | Simple issues have root causes too. Process is fast for simple bugs. |\n| \"Emergency, no time for process\" | Systematic debugging is FASTER than guess-and-check thrashing. |\n| \"Just try this first, then investigate\" | First fix sets the pattern. Do it right from the start. |\n| \"I''ll write test after confirming fix works\" | Untested fixes don''t stick. Test first proves it. |\n| \"Multiple fixes at once saves time\" | Can''t isolate what worked. Causes new bugs. |\n| \"Reference too long, I''ll adapt the pattern\" | Partial understanding guarantees bugs. Read it completely. |\n| \"I see the problem, let me fix it\" | Seeing symptoms ≠ understanding root cause. |\n| \"One more fix attempt\" (after 2+ failures) | 3+ failures = architectural problem. Question pattern, don''t fix again. |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Phase | Key Activities | Success Criteria |\n|-------|---------------|------------------|\n| **1. Root Cause** | Read errors, reproduce, check changes, gather evidence | Understand WHAT and WHY |\n| **2. Pattern** | Find working examples, compare | Identify differences |\n| **3. Hypothesis** | Form theory, test minimally | Confirmed or new hypothesis |\n| **4. Implementation** | Create test, fix, verify | Bug resolved, tests pass |\n\n## When Process Reveals \"No Root Cause\"\n\nIf systematic investigation reveals issue is truly environmental, timing-dependent, or external:\n\n1. You''ve completed the process\n2. Document what you investigated\n3. Implement appropriate handling (retry, timeout, error message)\n4. Add monitoring/logging for future investigation\n\n**But:** 95% of \"no root cause\" cases are incomplete investigation.\n\n## Supporting Techniques\n\nThese techniques are part of systematic debugging and available in this directory:\n\n- **`root-cause-tracing.md`** - Trace bugs backward through call stack to find original trigger\n- **`defense-in-depth.md`** - Add validation at multiple layers after finding root cause\n- **`condition-based-waiting.md`** - Replace arbitrary timeouts with condition polling\n\n**Related skills:**\n- **superpowers:test-driven-development** - For creating failing test case (Phase 4, Step 1)\n- **superpowers:verification-before-completion** - Verify fix worked before claiming success\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging sessions:\n- Systematic approach: 15-30 minutes to fix\n- Random fixes approach: 2-3 hours of thrashing\n- First-time fix rate: 95% vs 40%\n- New bugs introduced: Near zero vs common\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:42:04.053Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Technical Agents requiring methodical issue resolution and root cause analysis skills","zh":"适合需要系统性问题解决和根因分析技能的技术代理","ja":"方法的な問題解決とルート要因分析スキルを必要とするテクニカルエージェントに適しています","ko":"체계적인 문제 해결과 근본 원인 분석 技能이 필요한 기술 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes técnicos que requieren resolución de problemas metódica y habilidades de análisis de causa raíz","fr":"Idéal pour les agents techniques nécessitant une résolution de problèmes méthodique et des compétences en analyse de cause profonde","de":"Ideal für technische Agenten, die eine methodische Problemlösung und Fähigkeiten zur Analyse der Ursache erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Técnicos que requerem resolução de problemas metodológica e habilidades de análise de causa raiz","ru":"Идеально для технических агентов, требующих методического решения проблем и навыков анализа коренной причины","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الفنيين الذين يتطلبون حلًا منهجيًا للمشكلات ومهارات تحليل السبب الأساسي"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to conduct thorough root cause investigations using the Iron Law, ensuring NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST, thereby preventing quick patches that mask underlying issues and reducing the introduction of new bugs","zh":"赋予代理进行彻底的根因调查使用铁律，确保在进行任何修复之前先进行根因调查，从而防止掩盖潜在问题的快速补丁并减少新错误的引入","ja":"アイアンロウを使用して徹底的なルート要因の調査を実施し、修復を行う前にルート要因の調査を行うことを保証することで、根本的な問題を隠蔽するパッチを防ぎ、新たなバグの導入を減らします","ko":"철의 법칙을 사용하여 철저한 근본 원인 조사를 수행하고, 수정을 시도하기 전에 근본 원인 조사를 먼저 수행함으로써,根本적인 문제를 가리는 패치를 방지하고 새로운 버그의 도입을 줄입니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar investigaciones exhaustivas de causa raíz utilizando la Ley de Hierro, asegurando NO HAY REPARACIONES SIN INVESTIGACIÓN DE CAUSA RAÍZ PRIMERO, lo que evita soluciones rápidas que ocultan problemas subyacentes y reduce la introducción de nuevos errores","fr":"Permet aux agents de mener des enquêtes approfondies sur les causes profondes en utilisant la Loi de Fer, en garantissant AUCUNE CORRECTION SANS ENQUÊTE SUR LA CAUSE PROFONDE D''ABORD, ce qui empêche les correctifs rapides qui masquent les problèmes sous-jacents et réduit l''introduction de nouveaux bogues","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, gründliche Ursachenanalyse-Untersuchungen unter Verwendung des Eisernen Gesetzes durchzuführen, um KEINE REPARATUREN OHNE URSACHENANALYSE ZUERST sicherzustellen, wodurch schnelle Flickschustereien, die zugrunde liegende Probleme verbergen, verhindert und die Einführung neuer Fehler verringert werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar investigações aprofundadas das causas raiz usando a Lei de Ferro, garantindo NENHUMA CORREÇÃO SEM INVESTIGAÇÃO DE CAUSA RAIZ EM PRIMEIRO LUGAR, prevenindo assim patches rápidos que mascaram problemas subjacentes e reduzindo a introdução de novos bugs","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить тщательные расследования коренной причины с использованием Железного закона, гарантируя НЕТ ИСПРАВЛЕНИЙ БЕЗ РАССЛЕДОВАНИЯ КОРЕННОЙ ПРИЧИНЫ СНАЧАЛА, тем самым предотвращая быстрые исправления, которые маскируют лежащие в основе проблемы и снижают введение новых ошибок","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إجراء تحقيقات شاملة للسبب الأساسي باستخدام قانون الحديد، ضامنًا عدم إصلاح بدون تحقيق في السبب الأساسي أولاً، ومنع التصحيحات السريعة التي تخفي المشكلات الكامنة وخفض إدخال أخطاء جديدة"},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging test failures using systematic approaches","Identifying root causes of bugs before proposing fixes","Applying the Iron Law to prevent premature fixes"],"zh":["使用系统方法调试测试失败","在提出修复之前找出错误的根因","应用铁律以防止过早的修复"],"ja":["体系的なアプローチを使用してテストの失敗をデバッグする","修復を提案する前にバグのルート要因を特定する","アイアンロウを適用して早すぎる修復を防ぐ"],"ko":["체계적인 접근법을 사용하여 테스트 실패를 디버깅하기","수정 제안하기 전에 버그의 근본 원인을 식별하기","철의 법칙을 적용하여 조기 수정을 방지하기"],"es":["Depuración de fallos de prueba utilizando enfoques sistemáticos","Identificación de las causas raíz de los errores antes de proponer soluciones","Aplicación de la Ley de Hierro para prevenir soluciones prematuras"],"fr":["Débogage des échecs de test en utilisant des approches systématiques","Identification des causes profondes des bogues avant de proposer des correctifs","Application de la Loi de Fer pour prévenir les correctifs prématurés"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung bei Testfehlern unter Verwendung systematischer Ansätze","Identifizierung der Ursachen von Fehlern, bevor Korrekturen vorgeschlagen werden","Anwendung des Eisernen Gesetzes, um vorzeitige Korrekturen zu verhindern"],"pt":["Depuração de falhas de teste usando abordagens sistemáticas","Identificação das causas raiz de bugs antes de propor correções","Aplicação da Lei de Ferro para prevenir correções prematuras"],"ru":["Отладка неудач тестирования с использованием системных подходов","Определение коренной причины ошибок перед предложением исправлений","Применение Железного закона для предотвращения преждевременных исправлений"],"ar":["تصحيح أخطاء فشل الاختبار باستخدام مناهج منهجية","تحديد الأسباب الأساسية للأخطاء قبل اقتراح الإصلاحات","تطبيق قانون الحديد لمنع الإصلاحات المبتسرة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to the core principle of finding root cause before attempting fixes","Violating the letter of the systematic debugging process is considered a violation of the spirit of debugging"],"zh":["需要遵守在尝试修复之前找到根因的核心原则","违反系统调试过程的字母是调试精神的违反"],"ja":["修復を試みる前にルート要因を見つけるというコアプリンシプルに従う必要がある","体系的なデバッグプロセスの文字を違反することはデバッグの精神の違反とみなされる"],"ko":["수정 시도 전에 근본 원인을 찾는 핵심 원칙을遵守해야 함","체계적인 디버깅 프로세스의 문자를 위반하는 것은 디버깅의 정신을 위반하는 것으로 간주됨"],"es":["Requiere adherencia al principio fundamental de encontrar la causa raíz antes de intentar soluciones","Violación de la letra del proceso de depuración sistemática se considera una violación del espíritu de la depuración"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion au principe fondamental de trouver la cause profonde avant d''essayer des correctifs","La violation de la lettre du processus de débogage systématique est considérée comme une violation de l''esprit du débogage"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung des grundlegenden Prinzips, die Ursache zuerst zu finden, bevor Reparaturen versucht werden","Verletzung des Wortlautes des systematischen Fehlersuchprozesses gilt als Verletzung des Geistes der Fehlersuche"],"pt":["Exige adesão ao princípio fundamental de encontrar a causa raiz antes de tentar correções","Violar a letra do processo de depuração sistemática é considerado uma violação do espírito da depuração"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения основного принципа нахождения коренной причины перед попыткой исправлений","Нарушение буквы системного процесса отладки считается нарушением духа отладки"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بالمبدأ الأساسي لإيجاد السبب الأساسي قبل محاولة الإصلاحات","مخالفة حرفية عملية التصحيح المنهجي تعتبر مخالفة لروح التصحيح"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('runecalico-ai/second_edition_spellbook/systematic-debugging', 'community', 'runecalico-ai', 'second_edition_spellbook', 'runecalico-ai/second_edition_spellbook', 'systematic-debugging', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.449Z', '2026-02-18T06:42:17.382Z', NULL, '{"id":"runecalico-ai/second_edition_spellbook/systematic-debugging","name":"systematic-debugging","description":{"zh":"系统调试是一种高效的解决技术问题的方法，强调找到问题的根因","ja":"体系的デバッグは、テクニカル問題を効率的に解決する方法で、根本原因を特定することを重視","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 기술 문제를 효율적으로 해결하는 방법으로 문제의 근본 원인을 찾는 것을 강조","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque para resolver problemas técnicos de manera eficiente, encontrando siempre la causa raíz antes de proponer soluciones.","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche pour résoudre les problèmes techniques de manière efficace, en trouvant toujours la cause racine avant de proposer des solutions.","de":"Das systematische Debugging ist ein Ansatz, um technische Probleme effizient zu lösen, indem immer die Ursache gefunden wird, bevor Lösungen vorgeschlagen werden.","pt":"A depuração sistemática é um processo que ajuda a identificar a causa raiz dos problemas técnicos, evitando soluções rápidas e ineficazes.","ru":"Системная отладка - это процесс, который помогает определить коренную причину технических проблем, избегая быстрых и неэффективных решений.","ar":"التصحيح النظامي هو عملية تساعد على تحديد السبب الجذري للمشاكل الفنية، وتجنب الحلول السريعة وغير الفعالة.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"系统调试方法","ja":"体系的デバッグ","ko":"시스템 디버깅","es":"Depuración Sistemática: Resuelve Problemas de Raíz","fr":"Débogage Systématique: Réolvez les Problèmes à la Racine","de":"Systematisches Debugging: Lösen Sie Probleme an der Wurzel","pt":"Depuração Sistemática: Encontre a Causa Raiz","ru":"Системная отладка: найдите коренную причину","ar":"تصحيح سیستماتي: ابحث عن السبب الجذري","en":"systematic-debugging"},"description":{"zh":"系统调试是一种高效的解决技术问题的方法，强调找到问题的根因","ja":"体系的デバッグは、テクニカル問題を効率的に解決する方法で、根本原因を特定することを重視","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 기술 문제를 효율적으로 해결하는 방법으로 문제의 근본 원인을 찾는 것을 강조","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque para resolver problemas técnicos de manera eficiente, encontrando siempre la causa raíz antes de proponer soluciones.","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche pour résoudre les problèmes techniques de manière efficace, en trouvant toujours la cause racine avant de proposer ...","de":"Das systematische Debugging ist ein Ansatz, um technische Probleme effizient zu lösen, indem immer die Ursache gefunden wird, bevor Lösungen vorgeschlagen we...","pt":"A depuração sistemática é um processo que ajuda a identificar a causa raiz dos problemas técnicos, evitando soluções rápidas e ineficazes.","ru":"Системная отладка - это процесс, который помогает определить коренную причину технических проблем, избегая быстрых и неэффективных решений.","ar":"التصحيح النظامي هو عملية تساعد على تحديد السبب الجذري للمشاكل الفنية، وتجنب الحلول السريعة وغير الفعالة.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["找到问题的根因","高效解决技术问题","避免随机修复","遵循铁律"],"ja":["根本原因の特定","テクニカル問題の効率的な解決","ランダム修復の回避","鉄則の遵守"],"ko":["문제의 근본 원인 찾기","기술 문제를 효율적으로 해결","무작위 수정 피하기","철칙 준수"],"es":["Identificación de la causa raíz","Evitación de parches rápidos","Resolución eficiente de problemas técnicos","Aplicación del principio de no soluciones sin investigación","Uso para cualquier problema técnico"],"fr":["Identification de la cause racine","Évitement des correctifs rapides","Résolution efficace des problèmes techniques","Application du principe de pas de solutions sans investigation","Utilisation pour tout problème technique"],"de":["Identifizierung der Ursache","Vermeidung von schnellen Patches","Effiziente Lösung von technischen Problemen","Anwendung des Prinzips keine Lösungen ohne Untersuchung","Verwendung für jedes technische Problem"],"pt":["Identificação da causa raiz","Evita soluções rápidas e ineficazes","Melhora a eficiência do processo de depuração","Reduz a criação de novos bugs","Garante soluções eficazes e duradouras"],"ru":["Определение коренной причины","Избегает быстрых и неэффективных решений","Улучшает эффективность процесса отладки","Снижает создание новых ошибок","Гарантирует эффективные и долговечные решения"],"ar":["تحديد السبب الجذري","تجنب الحلول السريعة وغير الفعالة","تحسين كفاءة عملية التصحيح","تقليل創ation جديدة من الأخطاء","ضمان الحلول الفعالة والمتينة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["系统调试","技术问题解决","效率调试","根本原因","铁律"],"ja":["体系的デバッグ","テクニカル問題解決","効率的デバッグ","根本原因","鉄則"],"ko":["시스템 디버깅","기술 문제 해결","효율적인 디버깅","근본 원인","철칙"],"es":["depuración sistemática","resolución de problemas técnicos","causa raíz","principio de no soluciones sin investigación","debugging","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software"],"fr":["débogage systématique","résolution de problèmes techniques","cause racine","principe de pas de solutions sans investigation","débogage","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de logiciels"],"de":["systematisches Debugging","Lösung von technischen Problemen","Ursache","Prinzip keine Lösungen ohne Untersuchung","Debugging","Softwareentwicklung","Softwareingenieurwesen"],"pt":["depuração sistemática","causa raiz","soluções eficazes","processo de depuração","bugs","desenvolvimento de software","engenharia de software"],"ru":["системная отладка","коренная причина","эффективные решения","процесс отладки","ошибки","разработка программного обеспечения","инженерия программного обеспечения"],"ar":["تصحيح سیستماتي","السبب الجذري","حلول فعالة","عملية التصحيح","أخطاء","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"runecalico-ai","repo":"second_edition_spellbook","repoPath":"runecalico-ai/second_edition_spellbook","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.449Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"systematic-debugging","description":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes","bodyPreview":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs","body":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs in production\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Performance problems\n- Build failures\n- Integration issues\n\n**Use this ESPECIALLY when:**\n- Under time pressure (emergencies make guessing tempting)\n- \"Just one quick fix\" seems obvious\n- You''ve already tried multiple fixes\n- Previous fix didn''t work\n- You don''t fully understand the issue\n\n**Don''t skip when:**\n- Issue seems simple (simple bugs have root causes too)\n- You''re in a hurry (rushing guarantees rework)\n- Manager wants it fixed NOW (systematic is faster than thrashing)\n\n## The Four Phases\n\nYou MUST complete each phase before proceeding to the next.\n\n### Phase 1: Root Cause Investigation\n\n**BEFORE attempting ANY fix:**\n\n1. **Read Error Messages Carefully**\n   - Don''t skip past errors or warnings\n   - They often contain the exact solution\n   - Read stack traces completely\n   - Note line numbers, file paths, error codes\n\n2. **Reproduce Consistently**\n   - Can you trigger it reliably?\n   - What are the exact steps?\n   - Does it happen every time?\n   - If not reproducible → gather more data, don''t guess\n\n3. **Check Recent Changes**\n   - What changed that could cause this?\n   - Git diff, recent commits\n   - New dependencies, config changes\n   - Environmental differences\n\n4. **Gather Evidence in Multi-Component Systems**\n\n   **WHEN system has multiple components (CI → build → signing, API → service → database):**\n\n   **BEFORE proposing fixes, add diagnostic instrumentation:**\n   ```\n   For EACH component boundary:\n     - Log what data enters component\n     - Log what data exits component\n     - Verify environment/config propagation\n     - Check state at each layer\n\n   Run once to gather evidence showing WHERE it breaks\n   THEN analyze evidence to identify failing component\n   THEN investigate that specific component\n   ```\n\n   **Example (multi-layer system):**\n   ```bash\n   # Layer 1: Workflow\n   echo \"=== Secrets available in workflow: ===\"\n   echo \"IDENTITY: ${IDENTITY:+SET}${IDENTITY:-UNSET}\"\n\n   # Layer 2: Build script\n   echo \"=== Env vars in build script: ===\"\n   env | grep IDENTITY || echo \"IDENTITY not in environment\"\n\n   # Layer 3: Signing script\n   echo \"=== Keychain state: ===\"\n   security list-keychains\n   security find-identity -v\n\n   # Layer 4: Actual signing\n   codesign --sign \"$IDENTITY\" --verbose=4 \"$APP\"\n   ```\n\n   **This reveals:** Which layer fails (secrets → workflow ✓, workflow → build ✗)\n\n5. **Trace Data Flow**\n\n   **WHEN error is deep in call stack:**\n\n   See `root-cause-tracing.md` in this directory for the complete backward tracing technique.\n\n   **Quick version:**\n   - Where does bad value originate?\n   - What called this with bad value?\n   - Keep tracing up until you find the source\n   - Fix at source, not at symptom\n\n### Phase 2: Pattern Analysis\n\n**Find the pattern before fixing:**\n\n1. **Find Working Examples**\n   - Locate similar working code in same codebase\n   - What works that''s similar to what''s broken?\n\n2. **Compare Against References**\n   - If implementing pattern, read reference implementation COMPLETELY\n   - Don''t skim - read every line\n   - Understand the pattern fully before applying\n\n3. **Identify Differences**\n   - What''s different between working and broken?\n   - List every difference, however small\n   - Don''t assume \"that can''t matter\"\n\n4. **Understand Dependencies**\n   - What other components does this need?\n   - What settings, config, environment?\n   - What assumptions does it make?\n\n### Phase 3: Hypothesis and Testing\n\n**Scientific method:**\n\n1. **Form Single Hypothesis**\n   - State clearly: \"I think X is the root cause because Y\"\n   - Write it down\n   - Be specific, not vague\n\n2. **Test Minimally**\n   - Make the SMALLEST possible change to test hypothesis\n   - One variable at a time\n   - Don''t fix multiple things at once\n\n3. **Verify Before Continuing**\n   - Did it work? Yes → Phase 4\n   - Didn''t work? Form NEW hypothesis\n   - DON''T add more fixes on top\n\n4. **When You Don''t Know**\n   - Say \"I don''t understand X\"\n   - Don''t pretend to know\n   - Ask for help\n   - Research more\n\n### Phase 4: Implementation\n\n**Fix the root cause, not the symptom:**\n\n1. **Create Failing Test Case**\n   - Simplest possible reproduction\n   - Automated test if possible\n   - One-off test script if no framework\n   - MUST have before fixing\n   - Use the `superpowers:test-driven-development` skill for writing proper failing tests\n\n2. **Implement Single Fix**\n   - Address the root cause identified\n   - ONE change at a time\n   - No \"while I''m here\" improvements\n   - No bundled refactoring\n\n3. **Verify Fix**\n   - Test passes now?\n   - No other tests broken?\n   - Issue actually resolved?\n\n4. **If Fix Doesn''t Work**\n   - STOP\n   - Count: How many fixes have you tried?\n   - If < 3: Return to Phase 1, re-analyze with new information\n   - **If ≥ 3: STOP and question the architecture (step 5 below)**\n   - DON''T attempt Fix #4 without architectural discussion\n\n5. **If 3+ Fixes Failed: Question Architecture**\n\n   **Pattern indicating architectural problem:**\n   - Each fix reveals new shared state/coupling/problem in different place\n   - Fixes require \"massive refactoring\" to implement\n   - Each fix creates new symptoms elsewhere\n\n   **STOP and question fundamentals:**\n   - Is this pattern fundamentally sound?\n   - Are we \"sticking with it through sheer inertia\"?\n   - Should we refactor architecture vs. continue fixing symptoms?\n\n   **Discuss with your human partner before attempting more fixes**\n\n   This is NOT a failed hypothesis - this is a wrong architecture.\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Follow Process\n\nIf you catch yourself thinking:\n- \"Quick fix for now, investigate later\"\n- \"Just try changing X and see if it works\"\n- \"Add multiple changes, run tests\"\n- \"Skip the test, I''ll manually verify\"\n- \"It''s probably X, let me fix that\"\n- \"I don''t fully understand but this might work\"\n- \"Pattern says X but I''ll adapt it differently\"\n- \"Here are the main problems: [lists fixes without investigation]\"\n- Proposing solutions before tracing data flow\n- **\"One more fix attempt\" (when already tried 2+)**\n- **Each fix reveals new problem in different place**\n\n**ALL of these mean: STOP. Return to Phase 1.**\n\n**If 3+ fixes failed:** Question the architecture (see Phase 4.5)\n\n## your human partner''s Signals You''re Doing It Wrong\n\n**Watch for these redirections:**\n- \"Is that not happening?\" - You assumed without verifying\n- \"Will it show us...?\" - You should have added evidence gathering\n- \"Stop guessing\" - You''re proposing fixes without understanding\n- \"Ultrathink this\" - Question fundamentals, not just symptoms\n- \"We''re stuck?\" (frustrated) - Your approach isn''t working\n\n**When you see these:** STOP. Return to Phase 1.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Issue is simple, don''t need process\" | Simple issues have root causes too. Process is fast for simple bugs. |\n| \"Emergency, no time for process\" | Systematic debugging is FASTER than guess-and-check thrashing. |\n| \"Just try this first, then investigate\" | First fix sets the pattern. Do it right from the start. |\n| \"I''ll write test after confirming fix works\" | Untested fixes don''t stick. Test first proves it. |\n| \"Multiple fixes at once saves time\" | Can''t isolate what worked. Causes new bugs. |\n| \"Reference too long, I''ll adapt the pattern\" | Partial understanding guarantees bugs. Read it completely. |\n| \"I see the problem, let me fix it\" | Seeing symptoms ≠ understanding root cause. |\n| \"One more fix attempt\" (after 2+ failures) | 3+ failures = architectural problem. Question pattern, don''t fix again. |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Phase | Key Activities | Success Criteria |\n|-------|---------------|------------------|\n| **1. Root Cause** | Read errors, reproduce, check changes, gather evidence | Understand WHAT and WHY |\n| **2. Pattern** | Find working examples, compare | Identify differences |\n| **3. Hypothesis** | Form theory, test minimally | Confirmed or new hypothesis |\n| **4. Implementation** | Create test, fix, verify | Bug resolved, tests pass |\n\n## When Process Reveals \"No Root Cause\"\n\nIf systematic investigation reveals issue is truly environmental, timing-dependent, or external:\n\n1. You''ve completed the process\n2. Document what you investigated\n3. Implement appropriate handling (retry, timeout, error message)\n4. Add monitoring/logging for future investigation\n\n**But:** 95% of \"no root cause\" cases are incomplete investigation.\n\n## Supporting Techniques\n\nThese techniques are part of systematic debugging and available in this directory:\n\n- **`root-cause-tracing.md`** - Trace bugs backward through call stack to find original trigger\n- **`defense-in-depth.md`** - Add validation at multiple layers after finding root cause\n- **`condition-based-waiting.md`** - Replace arbitrary timeouts with condition polling\n\n**Related skills:**\n- **superpowers:test-driven-development** - For creating failing test case (Phase 4, Step 1)\n- **superpowers:verification-before-completion** - Verify fix worked before claiming success\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging sessions:\n- Systematic approach: 15-30 minutes to fix\n- Random fixes approach: 2-3 hours of thrashing\n- First-time fix rate: 95% vs 40%\n- New bugs introduced: Near zero vs common\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:42:17.382Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Diagnostic Agents requiring a methodical approach to issue resolution, emphasizing root cause analysis over symptomatic fixes.","zh":"适用于需要采取有条不紊的方法来解决问题的诊断代理，强调对根本原因分析而不是症状性修复的重要性。","ja":"根本原因分析よりも症状的修復を重視する問題解決のための体系的なアプローチを必要とする診断エージェントに最適です。","ko":"문제 해결을 위한 체계적인 접근 방식을 필요로 하는 진단 에이전트에게 적합하며, 증상적인 수정보다 근본 원인 분석을 강조합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Diagnóstico que requieren un enfoque metódico para la resolución de problemas, enfatizando el análisis de causa raíz sobre soluciones sintomáticas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de diagnostic nécessitant une approche méthodique pour la résolution des problèmes, en mettant l''accent sur l''analyse de la cause profonde plutôt que sur les solutions symptomatiques.","de":"Ideal für Diagnoseagenten, die einen methodischen Ansatz zur Problemlösung benötigen, wobei die Wurzelursachenanalyse über symptomatische Lösungen priorisiert wird.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Diagnóstico que requerem uma abordagem metódica para resolução de problemas, enfatizando a análise da causa raiz em vez de soluções sintomáticas.","ru":"Идеально для диагностических агентов, требующих системного подхода к решению проблем, подчеркивающих анализ коренной причины над симптоматическим исправлением.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التشخيصيين الذين يحتاجون إلى نهج منهجي لتحليل المشكلات، مع التركيز على تحليل السبب الجذري أكثر من الإصلاحات الأعراضية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to conduct thorough root cause investigations, adhering to the Iron Law of ''NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST'', ensuring that proposed fixes are based on a comprehensive understanding of the underlying issues, utilizing systematic debugging principles to resolve test failures and bugs.","zh":"赋予代理进行彻底的根本原因调查的能力，遵循没有根本原因调查就不进行修复的铁律，确保提出的修复措施基于对潜在问题的全面理解，利用系统化的调试原则来解决测试失败和错误。","ja":"根本原因の調査を徹底的に行うエージェントをEmpowerし、根本原因の調査を行わずに修復を行わないという鉄則に従い、提案された修復が根本的な問題に対する包括的な理解に基づいていることを保証し、体系的なデバッグ原則を使用してテストの失敗とバグを解決します。","ko":"근본 원인 조사를 철저히 수행할 수 있는 에이전트를 강화하여, 근본 원인 조사를 하지 않고 수정을 수행하지 않는다는 철칙을遵守하고, 제안된 수정이 기초가 되는 문제에 대한 포괄적인 이해에 기반하여, 체계적인 디버깅 원리를 사용하여 테스트 실패 및 버그를 해결합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar investigaciones exhaustivas de causa raíz, siguiendo la Ley de Hierro de ''NO SOLUCIONES SIN INVESTIGACIÓN DE CAUSA RAÍZ PRIMERO'', asegurando que las soluciones propuestas se basen en una comprensión integral de los problemas subyacentes, utilizando principios de depuración sistemática para resolver fallos de prueba y errores.","fr":"Habilite les agents à mener des enquêtes approfondies sur les causes profondes, en suivant la Loi de Fer de ''PAS DE CORRECTIONS SANS ENQUÊTE SUR LA CAUSE PROFONDE EN PREMIER'', en garantissant que les correctifs proposés sont basés sur une compréhension exhaustive des problèmes sous-jacents, en utilisant des principes de débogage systématique pour résoudre les échecs de test et les bogues.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, gründliche Wurzelursachenuntersuchungen durchzuführen, indem sie dem Eisernen Gesetz von ''KEINE LÖSUNGEN OHNE WURZELURSACHENUNTERSUCHUNG ZUERST'' folgen, sicherstellend, dass die vorgeschlagenen Lösungen auf einem umfassenden Verständnis der zugrunde liegenden Probleme basieren, wobei systematische Fehlersuche-Prinzipien zur Behebung von Testfehlern und Fehlern verwendet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar investigações minuciosas da causa raiz, aderindo à Lei de Ferro de ''NENHUMA CORREÇÃO SEM INVESTIGAÇÃO DA CAUSA RAIZ EM PRIMEIRO LUGAR'', garantindo que as correções propostas sejam baseadas em uma compreensão abrangente dos problemas subjacentes, utilizando princípios de depuração sistemática para resolver falhas de teste e bugs.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить тщательные расследования коренных причин, следуя Железному Закону ''НЕТ ИСПРАВЛЕНИЙ БЕЗ РАССЛЕДОВАНИЯ КОРЕННОЙ ПРИЧИНЫ СНАЧАЛА'', гарантируя, что предлагаемые исправления основаны на всестороннем понимании лежащих в основе проблем, используя системные отладочные принципы для решения неисправностей и ошибок.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إجراء تحقيقات شاملة للسبب الجذري، والتزام قانون الحديد ل ''لا إصلاح بدون تحقيق في السبب الجذري أولاً''، مما يضمن أن الإصلاحات المقترحة تستند إلى فهم شامل للقضايا الأساسية، واستخدام مبادئ فحص منهجي لتحليل اختبارات الفشل والاخطاء."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging complex test failures","Identifying root causes of recurrent bugs","Implementing systematic fixes for technical issues"],"zh":["调试复杂的测试失败","识别反复出现的错误的根本原因","实施技术问题的系统修复"],"ja":["複雑なテストの失敗のデバッグ","再発するバグの根本原因の特定","技術的な問題の体系的な修復の実施"],"ko":["복잡한 테스트 실패의 디버깅","반복되는 버그의 근본 원인 식별","기술적인 문제의 체계적인 수정 구현"],"es":["Depuración de fallos de prueba complejos","Identificación de causas raíz de errores recurrentes","Implementación de soluciones sistemáticas para problemas técnicos"],"fr":["Débogage de défaillances de test complexes","Identification des causes profondes des bogues récurrents","Mise en œuvre de corrections systématiques pour les problèmes techniques"],"de":["Fehlersuche bei komplexen Testfehlern","Identifizierung der Wurzelursachen wiederkehrender Fehler","Implementierung systematischer Lösungen für technische Probleme"],"pt":["Depuração de falhas de teste complexas","Identificação das causas raiz de bugs recorrentes","Implementação de soluções sistemáticas para problemas técnicos"],"ru":["Отладка сложных неисправностей тестов","Определение коренных причин повторяющихся ошибок","Реализация системных исправлений для технических проблем"],"ar":["فحص اختبارات الفشل المعقدة","تحديد الأسباب الجذري للخطأ المتكرر","تنفيذ إصلاحات منهجية للقضايا الفنية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to the systematic debugging process","Violating the principle of finding root cause before fixes is not allowed"],"zh":["需要遵守系统化的调试过程","不允许违反在修复前找到根本原因的原则"],"ja":["体系的なデバッグプロセスに従う必要がある","修復前に根本原因を見つけるという原則に違反してはならない"],"ko":["체계적인 디버깅 프로세스를 따라야 함","수정 전에 근본 원인을 찾는 원칙을 위반해서는 안 됨"],"es":["Requiere la adhesión al proceso de depuración sistemática","No se permite violar el principio de encontrar la causa raíz antes de las soluciones"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion au processus de débogage systématique","La violation du principe de recherche de la cause profonde avant les corrections n''est pas autorisée"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung des systematischen Fehlersuche-Prozesses","Die Verletzung des Grundsatzes, die Wurzelursache vor den Lösungen zu finden, ist nicht erlaubt"],"pt":["Exige adesão ao processo de depuração sistemática","Violação do princípio de encontrar a causa raiz antes das correções não é permitida"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения системного процесса отладки","Нарушение принципа нахождения коренной причины до исправлений не допускается"],"ar":["يتطلب اتباع عملية فحص منهجي","مخالفة مبدأ إيجاد السبب الجذري قبل الإصلاحات غير مسموح بها"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('hikch/dotfiles/context-loader', 'community', 'hikch', 'dotfiles', 'hikch/dotfiles', 'context-loader', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.450Z', '2026-02-18T06:42:28.014Z', NULL, '{"id":"hikch/dotfiles/context-loader","name":"context-loader","description":{"zh":"Context Loader 技能用于加载共享项目上下文，确保 Codex CLI 与 Claude Code 具有相同的知识。","ja":"Context Loader スキルは、共有プロジェクトコンテキストを読み込み、Codex CLI と Claude Code の知識を同期させます。","ko":"컨텍스트 로더 스킬은 공유 프로젝트 컨텍스트를 로딩하여 Codex CLI와 Claude Code의 지식을 동기화합니다.","es":"El cargador de contexto carga las reglas de codificación desde el directorio `.claude/` para asegurar la consistencia en tus proyectos","fr":"Le chargeur de contexte charge les règles de codage depuis le répertoire `.claude/` pour assurer la cohérence dans vos projets","de":"Der Kontext-Loader lädt die Codierregeln aus dem Verzeichnis `.claude/`, um die Konsistenz in Ihren Projekten sicherzustellen","pt":"O carregador de contexto é uma habilidade que carrega o contexto compartilhado do projeto a partir do diretório `.claude/`","ru":"Контекстный загрузчик - это навык, который загружает общий контекст проекта из директории `.claude/`","ar":"حمل السياق هو مهارة تقوم بتحميل السياق المشترك للمشروع من 目录 `.claude/`","en":"dotfiles."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Context Loader 技能 - 加载共享项目上下文","ja":"Context Loader スキル - 共有プロジェクトコンテキストの読み込み","ko":"컨텍스트 로더 스킬 - 공유 프로젝트 컨텍스트 로딩","es":"Cargador de contexto: carga de reglas de codificación","fr":"Chargeur de contexte : chargement des règles de codage","de":"Kontext-Loader: Laden von Codierregeln","pt":"Carregador de Contexto: Otimização de Projetos","ru":"Контекстный Загрузчик: Оптимизация Проектов","ar":"حمل السياق: تحسين المشاريع","en":"context-loader"},"description":{"zh":"Context Loader 技能用于加载共享项目上下文，确保 Codex CLI 与 Claude Code 具有相同的知识。","ja":"Context Loader スキルは、共有プロジェクトコンテキストを読み込み、Codex CLI と Claude Code の知識を同期させます。","ko":"컨텍스트 로더 스킬은 공유 프로젝트 컨텍스트를 로딩하여 Codex CLI와 Claude Code의 지식을 동기화합니다.","es":"El cargador de contexto carga las reglas de codificación desde el directorio `.claude/` para asegurar la consistencia en tus proyectos","fr":"Le chargeur de contexte charge les règles de codage depuis le répertoire `.claude/` pour assurer la cohérence dans vos projets","de":"Der Kontext-Loader lädt die Codierregeln aus dem Verzeichnis `.claude/`, um die Konsistenz in Ihren Projekten sicherzustellen","pt":"O carregador de contexto é uma habilidade que carrega o contexto compartilhado do projeto a partir do diretório `.claude/`","ru":"Контекстный загрузчик - это навык, который загружает общий контекст проекта из директории `.claude/`","ar":"حمل السياق هو مهارة تقوم بتحميل السياق المشترك للمشروع من 目录 `.claude/`","en":"dotfiles."},"definition":{"en":"dotfiles."},"features":{"zh":["加载共享项目上下文","确保 Codex CLI 与 Claude Code 的知识一致性","支持多种开发环境","自动加载项目规则","提高开发效率"],"ja":["共有プロジェクトコンテキストの読み込み","Codex CLI と Claude Code の知識の一貫性を確保","複数の開発環境をサポート","プロジェクトルールの自動読み込み","開発効率の向上"],"ko":["공유 프로젝트 컨텍스트 로딩","Codex CLI와 Claude Code의 지식 일관성 보장","다양한 개발 환경 지원","프로젝트 규칙 자동 로딩","개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["Carga de reglas de codificación","Compatibilidad con Codex CLI","Carga de contexto de proyecto","Soporte para directorios `.claude/`","Flexibilidad en la configuración de reglas"],"fr":["Chargement des règles de codage","Compatibilité avec Codex CLI","Chargement du contexte de projet","Prise en charge des répertoires `.claude/`","Flexibilité dans la configuration des règles"],"de":["Laden von Codierregeln","Kompatibilität mit Codex CLI","Laden des Projekt-Kontexts","Unterstützung für Verzeichnisse `.claude/`","Flexibilität bei der Konfiguration von Regeln"],"pt":["Carregamento de regras de codificação","Leitura de arquivos de configuração","Compatibilidade com Codex CLI","Melhoria da eficiência do projeto","Suporte a múltiplos diretórios"],"ru":["Загрузка правил кодирования","Чтение файлов конфигурации","Совместимость с Codex CLI","Повышение эффективности проекта","Поддержка нескольких директорий"],"ar":["تحميل قواعد الترميز","قراءة ملفات التهيئة","توافق مع Codex CLI","تحسين كفاءة المشروع","دعم متعدد الدلائل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Context Loader","共享项目上下文","Codex CLI","Claude Code","开发工具","知识一致性","开发环境","项目规则"],"ja":["Context Loader","共有プロジェクトコンテキスト","Codex CLI","Claude Code","開発ツール","知識の一貫性","開発環境","プロジェクトルール"],"ko":["컨텍스트 로더","공유 프로젝트 컨텍스트","Codex CLI","Claude Code","개발 도구","지식 일관성","개발 환경","프로젝트 규칙"],"es":["cargador de contexto","reglas de codificación","Codex CLI","proyecto de código","configuración de reglas","compatibilidad de código"],"fr":["chargeur de contexte","règles de codage","Codex CLI","projet de code","configuration de règles","compatibilité de code"],"de":["Kontext-Loader","Codierregeln","Codex CLI","Code-Projekt","Regel-Konfiguration","Code-Kompatibilität"],"pt":["carregador de contexto","desenvolvimento de software","Codex CLI","regras de codificação","eficiência do projeto","otimização de projetos"],"ru":["контекстный загрузчик","разработка программного обеспечения","Codex CLI","правила кодирования","эффективность проекта","оптимизация проектов"],"ar":["حمل السياق","تطوير البرمجيات","Codex CLI","قواعد الترميز","كفاءة المشروع","تحسين المشاريع"]}},"owner":"hikch","repo":"dotfiles","repoPath":"hikch/dotfiles","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.450Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"context-loader","description":"ALWAYS activate this skill at the start of every task. Load project context from .claude/ directory including coding rules, design decisions, and documentation before executing any task.","bodyPreview":"# Context Loader Skill\n\n## Purpose\n\nLoad shared project context from `.claude/` directory to ensure Codex CLI has the same knowledge as Claude Code.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n**ALWAYS** - This skill must run at the beginning of every task to load project context.\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Load Coding Rules\n\nRead all files in `.claude/rules/`:\n\n```\n.claude/rules/\n├── coding-principles.md   # Simplicity, single responsibility, early return\n├── dev-environment.md     # uv, ruff, ty, pytest requirements","body":"# Context Loader Skill\n\n## Purpose\n\nLoad shared project context from `.claude/` directory to ensure Codex CLI has the same knowledge as Claude Code.\n\n## When to Activate\n\n**ALWAYS** - This skill must run at the beginning of every task to load project context.\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Load Coding Rules\n\nRead all files in `.claude/rules/`:\n\n```\n.claude/rules/\n├── coding-principles.md   # Simplicity, single responsibility, early return\n├── dev-environment.md     # uv, ruff, ty, pytest requirements\n├── language.md            # Think in English, respond in Japanese\n├── security.md            # Secrets, validation, SQLi/XSS prevention\n├── testing.md             # TDD, AAA pattern, 80% coverage\n└── codex-delegation.md    # (skip - not relevant for Codex itself)\n```\n\n### Step 2: Load Design Documentation\n\nRead `.claude/docs/DESIGN.md` for:\n- Architecture decisions\n- Implementation patterns\n- Library choices and constraints\n- TODO items and open questions\n\n### Step 3: Check Library Documentation\n\nIf the task involves specific libraries, read relevant files from:\n```\n.claude/docs/libraries/\n```\n\n### Step 4: Execute Task\n\nWith the loaded context, execute the requested task following:\n- Coding principles from rules\n- Design decisions from DESIGN.md\n- Library constraints from docs\n\n## Key Rules to Remember\n\nAfter loading, always follow these principles:\n\n1. **Simplicity first** - Choose readable code over complex\n2. **Single responsibility** - One function/class does one thing\n3. **Type hints required** - All functions need annotations\n4. **Use uv** - Never use pip directly\n5. **Security** - No hardcoded secrets, validate input, parameterize SQL\n\n## Language Protocol\n\n- **Thinking/Reasoning**: English\n- **Code**: English (variables, functions, comments)\n- **User communication**: Japanese (when reporting back through Claude Code)\n\n## Output\n\nAfter loading context, briefly confirm:\n- Rules loaded\n- Design document status\n- Ready to execute task\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:42:28.014Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Codex CLI Agents needing shared project context synchronization with Claude Code","zh":"非常适合需要与 Claude Code 共享项目上下文同步的 Codex CLI Agent","ja":"Claude Code との共有プロジェクトコンテキストの同期が必要な Codex CLI エージェントに最適","ko":"Claude Code와 공유 프로젝트 컨텍스트 동기화를 필요로 하는 Codex CLI 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de línea de comandos de Codex que necesitan sincronización de contexto de proyecto compartido con Claude Code","fr":"Parfait pour les agents CLI Codex ayant besoin d''une synchronisation de contexte de projet partagé avec Claude Code","de":"Perfekt für Codex-CLI-Agents, die eine gemeinsame Projekt-Kontextsynchronisierung mit Claude Code benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes CLI Codex que precisam de sincronização de contexto de projeto compartilhado com Claude Code","ru":"Идеально для агентов CLI Codex, требующих синхронизации общего контекста проекта с Claude Code","ar":"مثالي لعميل كودكس CLI الذي يحتاج إلى تنسيق سياق المشروع المشترك مع كلود كود"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to load shared project context from `.claude/` directory, ensuring consistency with Claude Code by analyzing files like `coding-principles.md` and `dev-environment.md`","zh":"使得代理能够从 `.claude/` 目录加载共享项目上下文，通过分析 `coding-principles.md` 和 `dev-environment.md` 等文件，确保与 Claude Code的一致性","ja":"エージェントが `.claude/` ディレクトリから共有プロジェクトコンテキストを読み込み、`coding-principles.md` および `dev-environment.md` などのファイルを分析して、Claude Code との一貫性を確保する","ko":"에이전트가 `.claude/` 디렉토리에서 공유 프로젝트 컨텍스트를 로드하고 `coding-principles.md` 및 `dev-environment.md` 등의 파일을 분석하여 Claude Code 와의 일관성을 보장","es":"Habilita a los agentes a cargar el contexto de proyecto compartido desde el directorio `.claude/`, garantizando la coherencia con Claude Code mediante el análisis de archivos como `coding-principles.md` y `dev-environment.md`","fr":"Permet aux agents de charger le contexte de projet partagé à partir du répertoire `.claude/`, en garantissant la cohérence avec Claude Code en analysant des fichiers comme `coding-principles.md` et `dev-environment.md`","de":"Ermächtigt die Agents, den gemeinsamen Projekt-Kontext aus dem Verzeichnis `.claude/` zu laden, wodurch die Konsistenz mit Claude Code durch die Analyse von Dateien wie `coding-principles.md` und `dev-environment.md` sichergestellt wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a carregar o contexto do projeto compartilhado do diretório `.claude/`, garantindo a consistência com o Claude Code, analisando arquivos como `coding-principles.md` e `dev-environment.md`","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью загружать общий контекст проекта из директории `.claude/`, обеспечивая согласованность с Claude Code путем анализа файлов типа `coding-principles.md` и `dev-environment.md`","ar":"يُمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تحميل سياق المشروع المشترك من دليل `.claude/` ، مما يضمن الاتساق مع كلود كود من خلال تحليل الملفات مثل `coding-principles.md` و `dev-environment.md`"},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing project context for coding tasks","Loading custom coding rules for consistency","Ensuring dev environment requirements are met"],"zh":["为编码任务初始化项目上下文","加载自定义编码规则以确保一致性","确保满足开发环境要求"],"ja":["コーディングタスクのプロジェクトコンテキストを初期化する","一貫性を確保するためのカスタムコーディングルールを読み込む","開発環境の要件を満たすことを保証する"],"ko":["코딩 작업을 위한 프로젝트 컨텍스트 초기화","일관성을 보장하기 위한 사용자 지정 코딩 규칙 로드","개발 환경 요구 사항 충족 보장"],"es":["Inicializar el contexto del proyecto para tareas de codificación","Cargar reglas de codificación personalizadas para la coherencia","Garantizar que se cumplan los requisitos del entorno de desarrollo"],"fr":["Initialiser le contexte du projet pour les tâches de codage","Charger les règles de codage personnalisées pour la cohérence","Assurer que les exigences de l''environnement de développement soient respectées"],"de":["Initialisieren des Projekt-Kontexts für Codierungsaufgaben","Laden von benutzerdefinierten Codierregeln für Konsistenz","Sicherstellen, dass die Anforderungen der Entwicklerumgebung erfüllt werden"],"pt":["Inicializar contexto do projeto para tarefas de codificação","Carregar regras de codificação personalizadas para consistência","Garantir que os requisitos do ambiente de desenvolvimento sejam atendidos"],"ru":["Инициализировать контекст проекта для задач кодирования","Загрузить пользовательские правила кодирования для согласованности","Обеспечить выполнение требований среды разработки"],"ar":["ت khởi动 سياق المشروع للمهام البرمجية","تحميل قواعد الترميز المخصصة للاتساق","ضمان 충족 متطلبات بيئة التطوير"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to `.claude/` directory","Must run at the beginning of every task"],"zh":[".claude/ 目录的访问权限","必须在每个任务开始时运行"],"ja":[".claude/ ディレクトリへのアクセス権","各タスクの開始時に実行する必要がある"],"ko":[".claude/ 디렉토리への 액세스 권한","각 태스크 시작 시 실행해야 함"],"es":["Requiere acceso al directorio `.claude/`","Debe ejecutarse al comienzo de cada tarea"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès au répertoire `.claude/`","Doit être exécuté au début de chaque tâche"],"de":["Erfordert den Zugriff auf das Verzeichnis `.claude/`","Muss am Anfang jeder Aufgabe ausgeführt werden"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao diretório `.claude/`","Deve ser executado no início de cada tarefa"],"ru":["Требует доступа к директории `.claude/`","Должно выполняться в начале каждой задачи"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى دليل `.claude/`","يجب تشغيله في بداية كل مهمة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
