ل الإعداد","en":"openspec-onboard"},"description":{"zh":"OpenSpec入门指南，教您如何完成第一个完整的工作流程","ja":"OpenSpecの入門ガイド。最初の完全なワークフローを完了する方法を学ぶ","ko":"OpenSpec 시작하기. 첫 번째 완전한 워크플로우를 완료하는 방법을 배워보세요","es":"OpenSpec es una herramienta para supervisar y notificar cambios en tu tailnet. Esta guía te llevará a través de tu primer ciclo de trabajo completo con OpenSpec","fr":"OpenSpec est un outil pour surveiller et notifier les modifications dans votre tailnet. Ce guide vous accompagnera tout au long de votre premier cycle de tra...","de":"OpenSpec ist ein Tool zur Überwachung und Benachrichtigung von Änderungen in Ihrem Tailnet. Diese Anleitung führt Sie durch Ihren ersten vollständigen OpenSp...","pt":"O OpenSpec Onboard é um guia que auxilia na configuração e inicialização do OpenSpec, permitindo que os desenvolvedores monitorem suas alterações de código d...","ru":"OpenSpec Онбординг - это руководство, которое помогает настроить и инициализировать OpenSpec, позволяя разработчикам эффективно отслеживать изменения в их коде.","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard هو دليل يساعد في إعداد وتشغيل OpenSpec، مما يسمح للمطورين بمراقبة تغييراتهم في الكود بشكل فعال.","en":"Watch over your tailnet and notify of changes"},"definition":{"en":"Watch over your tailnet and notify of changes"},"features":{"zh":["代码库监控","工作流程管理","初始化和运行","代码检查","通知和警报"],"ja":["コードライブラリの監視","ワークフローの管理","初期化と実行","コードのチェック","通知とアラート"],"ko":["코드 라이브러리 모니터링","워크플로우 관리","초기화 및 실행","코드 체크","通知 및 경고"],"es":["Supervisión de cambios en el tailnet","Notificación de actualizaciones","Guía paso a paso para desarrolladores","Integración con el flujo de trabajo de OpenSpec","Verificación del estado de inicialización de OpenSpec"],"fr":["Surveillance des modifications dans le tailnet","Notification des mises à jour","Guide étape par étape pour les développeurs","Intégration avec le flux de travail OpenSpec","Vérification de l''état d''initialisation d''OpenSpec"],"de":["Überwachung von Änderungen im Tailnet","Benachrichtigung bei Updates","Schritt-für-Schritt-Anleitung für Entwickler","Integration in den OpenSpec-Arbeitsablauf","Überprüfung des Initialisierungsstatus von OpenSpec"],"pt":["Guia passo a passo para configuração do OpenSpec","Verificação de inicialização do OpenSpec","Suporte à inicialização do OpenSpec","Monitoramento de alterações de código","Integração com o workflow do desenvolvedor"],"ru":["Пошаговое руководство по настройке OpenSpec","Проверка инициализации OpenSpec","Поддержка инициализации OpenSpec","Отслеживание изменений в коде","Интеграция с рабочим процессом разработчика"],"ar":["دليل خطوة بخطوة لإعداد OpenSpec","تحقق من تشغيل OpenSpec","دعم تشغيل OpenSpec","مراقبة تغييرات الكود","التكامل مع تدفق عمل المطور"]},"keywords":{"zh":["OpenSpec","代码管理","工作流程","监控","通知","代码库","开发工具"],"ja":["OpenSpec","コード管理","ワークフロー","監視","通知","コードライブラリ","開発ツール"],"ko":["OpenSpec","코드 관리","워크플로우","모니터링","通知","코드 라이브러리","개발 도구"],"es":["OpenSpec","tailnet","supervisión de cambios","notificación de actualizaciones","desarrollo de software","integración de OpenSpec","guía para desarrolladores"],"fr":["OpenSpec","tailnet","surveillance de modifications","notification de mises à jour","développement de logiciels","intégration d''OpenSpec","guide pour développeurs"],"de":["OpenSpec","Tailnet","Überwachung von Änderungen","Benachrichtigung bei Updates","Softwareentwicklung","OpenSpec-Integration","Anleitung für Entwickler"],"pt":["OpenSpec","onboard","configuração","inicialização","monitoramento","desenvolvedor","código","workflow"],"ru":["OpenSpec","онбординг","настройка","инициализация","отслеживание","разработчик","код","работа"],"ar":["OpenSpec","إعداد","تشغيل","مراقبة","مطور","كود","تدفق عمل","دليل إعداد"]}},"owner":"jaxxstorm","repo":"sentinel","repoPath":"jaxxstorm/sentinel","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.450Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-onboard","description":"Guided onboarding for OpenSpec - walk through a complete workflow cycle with narration and real codebase work.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay","body":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay:\n\n```\n## Welcome to OpenSpec!\n\nI''ll walk you through a complete change cycle—from idea to implementation—using a real task in your codebase. Along the way, you''ll learn the workflow by doing it.\n\n**What we''ll do:**\n1. Pick a small, real task in your codebase\n2. Explore the problem briefly\n3. Create a change (the container for our work)\n4. Build the artifacts: proposal → specs → design → tasks\n5. Implement the tasks\n6. Archive the completed change\n\n**Time:** ~15-20 minutes\n\nLet''s start by finding something to work on.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Task Selection\n\n### Codebase Analysis\n\nScan the codebase for small improvement opportunities. Look for:\n\n1. **TODO/FIXME comments** - Search for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `HACK`, `XXX` in code files\n2. **Missing error handling** - `catch` blocks that swallow errors, risky operations without try-catch\n3. **Functions without tests** - Cross-reference `src/` with test directories\n4. **Type issues** - `any` types in TypeScript files (`: any`, `as any`)\n5. **Debug artifacts** - `console.log`, `console.debug`, `debugger` statements in non-debug code\n6. **Missing validation** - User input handlers without validation\n\nAlso check recent git activity:\n```bash\ngit log --oneline -10 2>/dev/null || echo \"No git history\"\n```\n\n### Present Suggestions\n\nFrom your analysis, present 3-4 specific suggestions:\n\n```\n## Task Suggestions\n\nBased on scanning your codebase, here are some good starter tasks:\n\n**1. [Most promising task]**\n   Location: `src/path/to/file.ts:42`\n   Scope: ~1-2 files, ~20-30 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**2. [Second task]**\n   Location: `src/another/file.ts`\n   Scope: ~1 file, ~15 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**3. [Third task]**\n   Location: [location]\n   Scope: [estimate]\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**4. Something else?**\n   Tell me what you''d like to work on.\n\nWhich task interests you? (Pick a number or describe your own)\n```\n\n**If nothing found:** Fall back to asking what the user wants to build:\n> I didn''t find obvious quick wins in your codebase. What''s something small you''ve been meaning to add or fix?\n\n### Scope Guardrail\n\nIf the user picks or describes something too large (major feature, multi-day work):\n\n```\nThat''s a valuable task, but it''s probably larger than ideal for your first OpenSpec run-through.\n\nFor learning the workflow, smaller is better—it lets you see the full cycle without getting stuck in implementation details.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Slice it smaller** - What''s the smallest useful piece of [their task]? Maybe just [specific slice]?\n2. **Pick something else** - One of the other suggestions, or a different small task?\n3. **Do it anyway** - If you really want to tackle this, we can. Just know it''ll take longer.\n\nWhat would you prefer?\n```\n\nLet the user override if they insist—this is a soft guardrail.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Explore Demo\n\nOnce a task is selected, briefly demonstrate explore mode:\n\n```\nBefore we create a change, let me quickly show you **explore mode**—it''s how you think through problems before committing to a direction.\n```\n\nSpend 1-2 minutes investigating the relevant code:\n- Read the file(s) involved\n- Draw a quick ASCII diagram if it helps\n- Note any considerations\n\n```\n## Quick Exploration\n\n[Your brief analysis—what you found, any considerations]\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│   [Optional: ASCII diagram if helpful]  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nExplore mode (`/opsx:explore`) is for this kind of thinking—investigating before implementing. You can use it anytime you need to think through a problem.\n\nNow let''s create a change to hold our work.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user acknowledgment before proceeding.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Create the Change\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Creating a Change\n\nA \"change\" in OpenSpec is a container for all the thinking and planning around a piece of work. It lives in `openspec/changes/<name>/` and holds your artifacts—proposal, specs, design, tasks.\n\nLet me create one for our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the change with a derived kebab-case name:\n```bash\nopenspec new change \"<derived-name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nCreated: `openspec/changes/<name>/`\n\nThe folder structure:\n```\nopenspec/changes/<name>/\n├── proposal.md    ← Why we''re doing this (empty, we''ll fill it)\n├── design.md      ← How we''ll build it (empty)\n├── specs/         ← Detailed requirements (empty)\n└── tasks.md       ← Implementation checklist (empty)\n```\n\nNow let''s fill in the first artifact—the proposal.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Proposal\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## The Proposal\n\nThe proposal captures **why** we''re making this change and **what** it involves at a high level. It''s the \"elevator pitch\" for the work.\n\nI''ll draft one based on our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft the proposal content (don''t save yet):\n\n```\nHere''s a draft proposal:\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n[1-2 sentences explaining the problem/opportunity]\n\n## What Changes\n\n[Bullet points of what will be different]\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n- `<capability-name>`: [brief description]\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n<!-- If modifying existing behavior -->\n\n## Impact\n\n- `src/path/to/file.ts`: [what changes]\n- [other files if applicable]\n\n---\n\nDoes this capture the intent? I can adjust before we save it.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user approval/feedback.\n\nAfter approval, save the proposal:\n```bash\nopenspec instructions proposal --change \"<name>\" --json\n```\nThen write the content to `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`.\n\n```\nProposal saved. This is your \"why\" document—you can always come back and refine it as understanding evolves.\n\nNext up: specs.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Specs\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Specs\n\nSpecs define **what** we''re building in precise, testable terms. They use a requirement/scenario format that makes expected behavior crystal clear.\n\nFor a small task like this, we might only need one spec file.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the spec file:\n```bash\nmkdir -p openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability-name>\n```\n\nDraft the spec content:\n\n```\nHere''s the spec:\n\n---\n\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: <Name>\n\n<Description of what the system should do>\n\n#### Scenario: <Scenario name>\n\n- **WHEN** <trigger condition>\n- **THEN** <expected outcome>\n- **AND** <additional outcome if needed>\n\n---\n\nThis format—WHEN/THEN/AND—makes requirements testable. You can literally read them as test cases.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability>/spec.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Design\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Design\n\nThe design captures **how** we''ll build it—technical decisions, tradeoffs, approach.\n\nFor small changes, this might be brief. That''s fine—not every change needs deep design discussion.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft design.md:\n\n```\nHere''s the design:\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\n[Brief context about the current state]\n\n## Goals / Non-Goals\n\n**Goals:**\n- [What we''re trying to achieve]\n\n**Non-Goals:**\n- [What''s explicitly out of scope]\n\n## Decisions\n\n### Decision 1: [Key decision]\n\n[Explanation of approach and rationale]\n\n---\n\nFor a small task, this captures the key decisions without over-engineering.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Tasks\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Tasks\n\nFinally, we break the work into implementation tasks—checkboxes that drive the apply phase.\n\nThese should be small, clear, and in logical order.\n```\n\n**DO:** Generate tasks based on specs and design:\n\n```\nHere are the implementation tasks:\n\n---\n\n## 1. [Category or file]\n\n- [ ] 1.1 [Specific task]\n- [ ] 1.2 [Specific task]\n\n## 2. Verify\n\n- [ ] 2.1 [Verification step]\n\n---\n\nEach checkbox becomes a unit of work in the apply phase. Ready to implement?\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user to confirm they''re ready to implement.\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 9: Apply (Implementation)\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Implementation\n\nNow we implement each task, checking them off as we go. I''ll announce each one and occasionally note how the specs/design informed the approach.\n```\n\n**DO:** For each task:\n\n1. Announce: \"Working on task N: [description]\"\n2. Implement the change in the codebase\n3. Reference specs/design naturally: \"The spec says X, so I''m doing Y\"\n4. Mark complete in tasks.md: `- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n5. Brief status: \"✓ Task N complete\"\n\nKeep narration light—don''t over-explain every line of code.\n\nAfter all tasks:\n\n```\n## Implementation Complete\n\nAll tasks done:\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n- [x] ...\n\nThe change is implemented! One more step—let''s archive it.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 10: Archive\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Archiving\n\nWhen a change is complete, we archive it. This moves it from `openspec/changes/` to `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`.\n\nArchived changes become your project''s decision history—you can always find them later to understand why something was built a certain way.\n```\n\n**DO:**\n```bash\nopenspec archive \"<name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nArchived to: `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`\n\nThe change is now part of your project''s history. The code is in your codebase, the decision record is preserved.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 11: Recap & Next Steps\n\n```\n## Congratulations!\n\nYou just completed a full OpenSpec cycle:\n\n1. **Explore** - Thought through the problem\n2. **New** - Created a change container\n3. **Proposal** - Captured WHY\n4. **Specs** - Defined WHAT in detail\n5. **Design** - Decided HOW\n6. **Tasks** - Broke it into steps\n7. **Apply** - Implemented the work\n8. **Archive** - Preserved the record\n\nThis same rhythm works for any size change—a small fix or a major feature.\n\n---\n\n## Command Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems before/during work |\n| `/opsx:new` | Start a new change, step through artifacts |\n| `/opsx:ff` | Fast-forward: create all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue` | Continue working on an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply` | Implement tasks from a change |\n| `/opsx:verify` | Verify implementation matches artifacts |\n| `/opsx:archive` | Archive a completed change |\n\n---\n\n## What''s Next?\n\nTry `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff` on something you actually want to build. You''ve got the rhythm now!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Graceful Exit Handling\n\n### User wants to stop mid-way\n\nIf the user says they need to stop, want to pause, or seem disengaged:\n\n```\nNo problem! Your change is saved at `openspec/changes/<name>/`.\n\nTo pick up where we left off later:\n- `/opsx:continue <name>` - Resume artifact creation\n- `/opsx:apply <name>` - Jump to implementation (if tasks exist)\n\nThe work won''t be lost. Come back whenever you''re ready.\n```\n\nExit gracefully without pressure.\n\n### User just wants command reference\n\nIf the user says they just want to see the commands or skip the tutorial:\n\n```\n## OpenSpec Quick Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems (no code changes) |\n| `/opsx:new <name>` | Start a new change, step by step |\n| `/opsx:ff <name>` | Fast-forward: all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue <name>` | Continue an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply <name>` | Implement tasks |\n| `/opsx:verify <name>` | Verify implementation |\n| `/opsx:archive <name>` | Archive when done |\n\nTry `/opsx:new` to start your first change, or `/opsx:ff` if you want to move fast.\n```\n\nExit gracefully.\n\n---\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- **Follow the EXPLAIN → DO → SHOW → PAUSE pattern** at key transitions (after explore, after proposal draft, after tasks, after archive)\n- **Keep narration light** during implementation—teach without lecturing\n- **Don''t skip phases** even if the change is small—the goal is teaching the workflow\n- **Pause for acknowledgment** at marked points, but don''t over-pause\n- **Handle exits gracefully**—never pressure the user to continue\n- **Use real codebase tasks**—don''t simulate or use fake examples\n- **Adjust scope gently**—guide toward smaller tasks but respect user choice\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:43:28.931Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for DevOps Agents needing automated workflow cycle management and codebase monitoring.","zh":"非常适合需要自动化工作流周期管理和代码库监控的 DevOps Agents。","ja":"DevOps エージェントが自動化されたワークフロー周期管理とコードベースの監視を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"자동화된 워크플로 사이클 관리 및 코드베이스 모니터링이 필요한 DevOps 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de DevOps que necesitan gestión del ciclo de flujo de trabajo automatizado y monitoreo del código base.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents DevOps ayant besoin d''une gestion automatisée du cycle de workflow et de surveillance du codebase.","de":"Perfekt für DevOps-Agents, die eine automatisierte Workflow-Zyklusverwaltung und Codebase-Überwachung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes DevOps que precisam de gerenciamento de ciclo de trabalho automatizado e monitoramento de codebase.","ru":"Идеально для агентов DevOps, которым необходим автоматизированный менеджмент цикла рабочих процессов и мониторинг кодовой базы.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء DevOps الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة دورة العمل الآلية ومراقبة قاعدة الشفرة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to monitor tailnets and notify of changes, utilizing OpenSpec''s workflow cycle management capabilities and JSON output for seamless integration, while explaining each step in real-time codebase interactions.","zh":"赋予代理监视 tailnets 并在更改时通知的能力，利用 OpenSpec 的工作流周期管理功能和 JSON 输出实现无缝集成，同时实时解释代码库交互中的每个步骤。","ja":"エージェントがテールネットを監視し、変更を通知する機能を提供します。OpenSpec のワークフロー周期管理機能と JSON 出力を使用してシームレスな統合を実現し、リアルタイムのコードベースのやり取りで各ステップを説明します。","ko":"에이전트가 테일넷을 모니터링하고 변경 사항을 알리는 기능을 제공하며, OpenSpec의 워크플로 사이클 관리 기능과 JSON 출력을 사용하여 무결점 통합을 실현하며, 실시간 코드베이스 상호 작용에서 각 단계를 설명합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes para monitorear tailnets y notificar sobre cambios, utilizando las capacidades de gestión del ciclo de flujo de trabajo de OpenSpec y la salida JSON para una integración perfecta, mientras explica cada paso en las interacciones del código base en tiempo real.","fr":"Permet aux agents de surveiller les tailnets et de notifier les modifications, en utilisant les capacités de gestion du cycle de workflow d''OpenSpec et la sortie JSON pour une intégration transparente, tout en expliquant chaque étape dans les interactions du codebase en temps réel.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Tailnets zu überwachen und über Änderungen zu benachrichtigen, indem sie die Workflow-Zyklusverwaltungsfähigkeiten von OpenSpec und die JSON-Ausgabe für eine nahtlose Integration nutzen, während jede Schritt in den Echtzeit-Codebase-Interaktionen erklärt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a monitorar tailnets e notificar sobre alterações, utilizando as capacidades de gerenciamento do ciclo de trabalho do OpenSpec e saída JSON para integração transparente, explicando cada etapa em interações de codebase em tempo real.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью мониторить tailnets и уведомлять о изменениях, используя возможности менеджмента цикла рабочих процессов OpenSpec и вывод JSON для бесшовной интеграции, объясняя каждый шаг в реальных взаимодействиях с кодовой базой.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من مراقبة tailnets وإعلامهم بالتغيرات، باستخدام إمكانيات إدارة دورة العمل مفتوحة المواصفات وخرج JSON من أجل التكامل السلس، مع شرح كل خطوة في تفاعلات قاعدة الشفرة في الوقت الفعلي."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating OpenSpec initialization checks","Monitoring tailnet changes for prompt notifications","Guiding users through complete OpenSpec workflow cycles"],"zh":["自动化 OpenSpec 初始化检查","监视 tailnet 更改以实现及时通知","引导用户完成 OpenSpec 工作流周期"],"ja":["OpenSpec 初期化チェックの自動化","tailnet の変更を監視してタイムリーな通知を行う","OpenSpec ワークフローサイクルを通じてユーザーをガイドする"],"ko":["OpenSpec 초기화 확인 자동화","tailnet 변경 사항을 모니터링하여 즉각적인 알림을 제공하는 것","OpenSpec 워크플로 사이클을 통해 사용자를 안내하는 것"],"es":["Automatización de las comprobaciones de inicialización de OpenSpec","Monitoreo de los cambios en tailnet para notificaciones oportunas","Guía a los usuarios a través de los ciclos de flujo de trabajo de OpenSpec completos"],"fr":["Automatisation des vérifications d''initialisation d''OpenSpec","Surveillance des modifications de tailnet pour des notifications immédiates","Guidage des utilisateurs à travers les cycles de workflow d''OpenSpec complets"],"de":["Automatisierung der Initialisierungsprüfungen von OpenSpec","Überwachung der Änderungen in Tailnet für prompte Benachrichtigungen","Führt Benutzer durch die kompletten OpenSpec-Workflow-Zyklen"],"pt":["Automatizar verificações de inicialização do OpenSpec","Monitorar alterações de tailnet para notificações imediatas","Orientar usuários por meio de ciclos de trabalho completos do OpenSpec"],"ru":["Автоматизировать проверки инициализации OpenSpec","Мониторить изменения tailnet для оперативных уведомлений","Направлять пользователей через полные циклы рабочих процессов OpenSpec"],"ar":["توفير تحقق آلي من عمليات 초기ته مفتوحة المواصفات","مراقبة التغيرات في شبكة التAIL لتنبيهات فورية","توجيه المستخدمين خلال دورات العمل الكاملة لمفتوحة المواصفات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires OpenSpec initialization","Dependent on ''openspec status'' and ''openspec init'' commands"],"zh":["需要 OpenSpec 初始化","依赖于 ''openspec status'' 和 ''openspec init'' 命令"],"ja":["OpenSpec の初期化が必要","''openspec status'' および ''openspec init'' コマンドに依存する"],"ko":["OpenSpec 초기화가 필요함","''openspec status'' 및 ''openspec init'' 명령어에 의존함"],"es":["Requiere inicialización de OpenSpec","Dependiente de los comandos ''openspec status'' y ''openspec init''"],"fr":["Nécessite l''initialisation d''OpenSpec","Dépend des commandes ''openspec status'' et ''openspec init''"],"de":["Erfordert OpenSpec-Initialisierung","Abhängig von den Befehlen ''openspec status'' und ''openspec init''"],"pt":["Exige inicialização do OpenSpec","Dependente dos comandos ''openspec status'' e ''openspec init''"],"ru":["Требует инициализации OpenSpec","Зависит от команд ''openspec status'' и ''openspec init''"],"ar":["يتطلب تهيئة مفتوحة المواصفات","يعتمد على أوامر ''openspec status'' و ''openspec init''"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('carlosapgomes/eqmd/openspec-onboard', 'community', 'carlosapgomes', 'eqmd', 'carlosapgomes/eqmd', 'openspec-onboard', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.450Z', '2026-02-18T06:43:31.514Z', NULL, '{"id":"carlosapgomes/eqmd/openspec-onboard","name":"openspec-onboard","description":{"zh":"本教程将指导用户完成OpenSpec的第一次工作流程，包括初始化和运行","ja":"OpenSpecのワークフローを初めて実行するためのガイド","ko":"OpenSpec의 첫 번째 작업 흐름을 완료하는 방법","es":"El onboarding de OpenSpec te guía a través de tu primer ciclo de trabajo completo","fr":"L''onboarding d''OpenSpec vous guide à travers votre premier cycle de travail complet","de":"Das Onboarding von OpenSpec führt Sie durch Ihren ersten vollständigen Arbeitszyklus","pt":"O OpenSpec Onboard é um guia que o ajuda a configurar e iniciar o OpenSpec em seu projeto.","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard — это руководство, которое помогает вам настроить и запустить OpenSpec в вашем проекте.","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard هو دليل يساعدك على إعداد وتشغيل OpenSpec في مشروعك.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"OpenSpec入门指南","ja":"OpenSpecを始める","ko":"OpenSpec 시작하기","es":"Onboarding con OpenSpec","fr":"Onboarding avec OpenSpec","de":"Onboarding mit OpenSpec","pt":"OpenSpec Onboard: Guia de Inicialização","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard: Руководство по настройке","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard: إرشادات الإعداد","en":"openspec-onboard"},"description":{"zh":"本教程将指导用户完成OpenSpec的第一次工作流程，包括初始化和运行","ja":"OpenSpecのワークフローを初めて実行するためのガイド","ko":"OpenSpec의 첫 번째 작업 흐름을 완료하는 방법","es":"El onboarding de OpenSpec te guía a través de tu primer ciclo de trabajo completo","fr":"L''onboarding d''OpenSpec vous guide à travers votre premier cycle de travail complet","de":"Das Onboarding von OpenSpec führt Sie durch Ihren ersten vollständigen Arbeitszyklus","pt":"O OpenSpec Onboard é um guia que o ajuda a configurar e iniciar o OpenSpec em seu projeto.","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard — это руководство, которое помогает вам настроить и запустить OpenSpec в вашем проекте.","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard هو دليل يساعدك على إعداد وتشغيل OpenSpec في مشروعك.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["OpenSpec初始化","工作流程教程","代码检查","运行OpenSpec","工作流程管理"],"ja":["OpenSpecの初期化","ワークフローの学習","コードのチェック","OpenSpecの実行","ワークフローの管理"],"ko":["OpenSpec 초기화","작업 흐름 가이드","코드 검사","OpenSpec 실행","작업 흐름 관리"],"es":["Guía paso a paso para configurar OpenSpec","Verificación del estado de inicialización de OpenSpec","Incorporación de funcionalidades de OpenSpec en tu proyecto","Explicación detallada de cada paso del ciclo de trabajo","Trabajo práctico en tu código base"],"fr":["Guide étape par étape pour configurer OpenSpec","Vérification de l''état d''initialisation d''OpenSpec","Intégration des fonctionnalités d''OpenSpec dans votre projet","Explication détaillée de chaque étape du cycle de travail","Travail pratique sur votre base de code"],"de":["Schritt-für-Schritt-Anleitung zur Konfiguration von OpenSpec","Überprüfung des Initialisierungsstatus von OpenSpec","Integration von OpenSpec-Funktionen in Ihr Projekt","Detaillierte Erklärung jeder Phase des Arbeitszyklus","Praktische Arbeit in Ihrem Codebase"],"pt":["Configuração inicial do OpenSpec","Verificação do status do OpenSpec","Execução do primeiro ciclo de trabalho do OpenSpec","Explicação passo a passo do processo","Trabalho real no código do usuário","Suporte à inicialização do OpenSpec"],"ru":["Первоначальная настройка OpenSpec","Проверка статуса OpenSpec","Выполнение первого рабочего цикла OpenSpec","Пошаговое объяснение процесса","Реальная работа с кодом пользователя","Поддержка инициализации OpenSpec"],"ar":["إعداد 初يائي ل OpenSpec","فحص حالة OpenSpec","تشغيل الدورة الأولى من عمل OpenSpec","شرح خطوة بخطوة للعملية","العمل الفعلي على كود المستخدم","دعم إعداد OpenSpec"]},"keywords":{"zh":["OpenSpec","代码工作流程","初始化","运行","教程","工作流程管理"],"ja":["OpenSpec","コードワークフロー","初期化","実行","ガイド","ワークフローの管理"],"ko":["OpenSpec","코드 작업 흐름","초기화","실행","가이드","작업 흐름 관리"],"es":["onboarding OpenSpec","tutorial OpenSpec","configuración OpenSpec","ciclo de trabajo OpenSpec","proyectos de código abierto","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["onboarding OpenSpec","tutoriel OpenSpec","configuration OpenSpec","cycle de travail OpenSpec","projets de code ouvert","outils de développement"],"de":["Onboarding OpenSpec","Tutorial OpenSpec","Konfiguration OpenSpec","Arbeitszyklus OpenSpec","Open-Source-Projekte","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["OpenSpec","Onboard","Configuração","Iniciação","Ciclo de trabalho","Desenvolvimento de software","Ferramentas de desenvolvimento","Guia de iniciação","Suporte técnico"],"ru":["OpenSpec","Onboard","Настройка","Инициализация","Рабочий цикл","Разработка программного обеспечения","Инструменты разработки","Руководство по настройке","Техническая поддержка"],"ar":["OpenSpec","Onboard","إعداد","تشغيل","دورة العمل","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير","دليل الإعداد","دعم تقني"]}},"owner":"carlosapgomes","repo":"eqmd","repoPath":"carlosapgomes/eqmd","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.450Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-onboard","description":"Guided onboarding for OpenSpec - walk through a complete workflow cycle with narration and real codebase work.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay","body":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay:\n\n```\n## Welcome to OpenSpec!\n\nI''ll walk you through a complete change cycle—from idea to implementation—using a real task in your codebase. Along the way, you''ll learn the workflow by doing it.\n\n**What we''ll do:**\n1. Pick a small, real task in your codebase\n2. Explore the problem briefly\n3. Create a change (the container for our work)\n4. Build the artifacts: proposal → specs → design → tasks\n5. Implement the tasks\n6. Archive the completed change\n\n**Time:** ~15-20 minutes\n\nLet''s start by finding something to work on.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Task Selection\n\n### Codebase Analysis\n\nScan the codebase for small improvement opportunities. Look for:\n\n1. **TODO/FIXME comments** - Search for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `HACK`, `XXX` in code files\n2. **Missing error handling** - `catch` blocks that swallow errors, risky operations without try-catch\n3. **Functions without tests** - Cross-reference `src/` with test directories\n4. **Type issues** - `any` types in TypeScript files (`: any`, `as any`)\n5. **Debug artifacts** - `console.log`, `console.debug`, `debugger` statements in non-debug code\n6. **Missing validation** - User input handlers without validation\n\nAlso check recent git activity:\n```bash\ngit log --oneline -10 2>/dev/null || echo \"No git history\"\n```\n\n### Present Suggestions\n\nFrom your analysis, present 3-4 specific suggestions:\n\n```\n## Task Suggestions\n\nBased on scanning your codebase, here are some good starter tasks:\n\n**1. [Most promising task]**\n   Location: `src/path/to/file.ts:42`\n   Scope: ~1-2 files, ~20-30 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**2. [Second task]**\n   Location: `src/another/file.ts`\n   Scope: ~1 file, ~15 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**3. [Third task]**\n   Location: [location]\n   Scope: [estimate]\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**4. Something else?**\n   Tell me what you''d like to work on.\n\nWhich task interests you? (Pick a number or describe your own)\n```\n\n**If nothing found:** Fall back to asking what the user wants to build:\n> I didn''t find obvious quick wins in your codebase. What''s something small you''ve been meaning to add or fix?\n\n### Scope Guardrail\n\nIf the user picks or describes something too large (major feature, multi-day work):\n\n```\nThat''s a valuable task, but it''s probably larger than ideal for your first OpenSpec run-through.\n\nFor learning the workflow, smaller is better—it lets you see the full cycle without getting stuck in implementation details.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Slice it smaller** - What''s the smallest useful piece of [their task]? Maybe just [specific slice]?\n2. **Pick something else** - One of the other suggestions, or a different small task?\n3. **Do it anyway** - If you really want to tackle this, we can. Just know it''ll take longer.\n\nWhat would you prefer?\n```\n\nLet the user override if they insist—this is a soft guardrail.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Explore Demo\n\nOnce a task is selected, briefly demonstrate explore mode:\n\n```\nBefore we create a change, let me quickly show you **explore mode**—it''s how you think through problems before committing to a direction.\n```\n\nSpend 1-2 minutes investigating the relevant code:\n- Read the file(s) involved\n- Draw a quick ASCII diagram if it helps\n- Note any considerations\n\n```\n## Quick Exploration\n\n[Your brief analysis—what you found, any considerations]\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│   [Optional: ASCII diagram if helpful]  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nExplore mode (`/opsx:explore`) is for this kind of thinking—investigating before implementing. You can use it anytime you need to think through a problem.\n\nNow let''s create a change to hold our work.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user acknowledgment before proceeding.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Create the Change\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Creating a Change\n\nA \"change\" in OpenSpec is a container for all the thinking and planning around a piece of work. It lives in `openspec/changes/<name>/` and holds your artifacts—proposal, specs, design, tasks.\n\nLet me create one for our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the change with a derived kebab-case name:\n```bash\nopenspec new change \"<derived-name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nCreated: `openspec/changes/<name>/`\n\nThe folder structure:\n```\nopenspec/changes/<name>/\n├── proposal.md    ← Why we''re doing this (empty, we''ll fill it)\n├── design.md      ← How we''ll build it (empty)\n├── specs/         ← Detailed requirements (empty)\n└── tasks.md       ← Implementation checklist (empty)\n```\n\nNow let''s fill in the first artifact—the proposal.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Proposal\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## The Proposal\n\nThe proposal captures **why** we''re making this change and **what** it involves at a high level. It''s the \"elevator pitch\" for the work.\n\nI''ll draft one based on our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft the proposal content (don''t save yet):\n\n```\nHere''s a draft proposal:\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n[1-2 sentences explaining the problem/opportunity]\n\n## What Changes\n\n[Bullet points of what will be different]\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n- `<capability-name>`: [brief description]\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n<!-- If modifying existing behavior -->\n\n## Impact\n\n- `src/path/to/file.ts`: [what changes]\n- [other files if applicable]\n\n---\n\nDoes this capture the intent? I can adjust before we save it.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user approval/feedback.\n\nAfter approval, save the proposal:\n```bash\nopenspec instructions proposal --change \"<name>\" --json\n```\nThen write the content to `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`.\n\n```\nProposal saved. This is your \"why\" document—you can always come back and refine it as understanding evolves.\n\nNext up: specs.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Specs\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Specs\n\nSpecs define **what** we''re building in precise, testable terms. They use a requirement/scenario format that makes expected behavior crystal clear.\n\nFor a small task like this, we might only need one spec file.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the spec file:\n```bash\nmkdir -p openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability-name>\n```\n\nDraft the spec content:\n\n```\nHere''s the spec:\n\n---\n\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: <Name>\n\n<Description of what the system should do>\n\n#### Scenario: <Scenario name>\n\n- **WHEN** <trigger condition>\n- **THEN** <expected outcome>\n- **AND** <additional outcome if needed>\n\n---\n\nThis format—WHEN/THEN/AND—makes requirements testable. You can literally read them as test cases.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability>/spec.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Design\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Design\n\nThe design captures **how** we''ll build it—technical decisions, tradeoffs, approach.\n\nFor small changes, this might be brief. That''s fine—not every change needs deep design discussion.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft design.md:\n\n```\nHere''s the design:\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\n[Brief context about the current state]\n\n## Goals / Non-Goals\n\n**Goals:**\n- [What we''re trying to achieve]\n\n**Non-Goals:**\n- [What''s explicitly out of scope]\n\n## Decisions\n\n### Decision 1: [Key decision]\n\n[Explanation of approach and rationale]\n\n---\n\nFor a small task, this captures the key decisions without over-engineering.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Tasks\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Tasks\n\nFinally, we break the work into implementation tasks—checkboxes that drive the apply phase.\n\nThese should be small, clear, and in logical order.\n```\n\n**DO:** Generate tasks based on specs and design:\n\n```\nHere are the implementation tasks:\n\n---\n\n## 1. [Category or file]\n\n- [ ] 1.1 [Specific task]\n- [ ] 1.2 [Specific task]\n\n## 2. Verify\n\n- [ ] 2.1 [Verification step]\n\n---\n\nEach checkbox becomes a unit of work in the apply phase. Ready to implement?\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user to confirm they''re ready to implement.\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 9: Apply (Implementation)\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Implementation\n\nNow we implement each task, checking them off as we go. I''ll announce each one and occasionally note how the specs/design informed the approach.\n```\n\n**DO:** For each task:\n\n1. Announce: \"Working on task N: [description]\"\n2. Implement the change in the codebase\n3. Reference specs/design naturally: \"The spec says X, so I''m doing Y\"\n4. Mark complete in tasks.md: `- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n5. Brief status: \"✓ Task N complete\"\n\nKeep narration light—don''t over-explain every line of code.\n\nAfter all tasks:\n\n```\n## Implementation Complete\n\nAll tasks done:\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n- [x] ...\n\nThe change is implemented! One more step—let''s archive it.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 10: Archive\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Archiving\n\nWhen a change is complete, we archive it. This moves it from `openspec/changes/` to `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`.\n\nArchived changes become your project''s decision history—you can always find them later to understand why something was built a certain way.\n```\n\n**DO:**\n```bash\nopenspec archive \"<name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nArchived to: `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`\n\nThe change is now part of your project''s history. The code is in your codebase, the decision record is preserved.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 11: Recap & Next Steps\n\n```\n## Congratulations!\n\nYou just completed a full OpenSpec cycle:\n\n1. **Explore** - Thought through the problem\n2. **New** - Created a change container\n3. **Proposal** - Captured WHY\n4. **Specs** - Defined WHAT in detail\n5. **Design** - Decided HOW\n6. **Tasks** - Broke it into steps\n7. **Apply** - Implemented the work\n8. **Archive** - Preserved the record\n\nThis same rhythm works for any size change—a small fix or a major feature.\n\n---\n\n## Command Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems before/during work |\n| `/opsx:new` | Start a new change, step through artifacts |\n| `/opsx:ff` | Fast-forward: create all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue` | Continue working on an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply` | Implement tasks from a change |\n| `/opsx:verify` | Verify implementation matches artifacts |\n| `/opsx:archive` | Archive a completed change |\n\n---\n\n## What''s Next?\n\nTry `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff` on something you actually want to build. You''ve got the rhythm now!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Graceful Exit Handling\n\n### User wants to stop mid-way\n\nIf the user says they need to stop, want to pause, or seem disengaged:\n\n```\nNo problem! Your change is saved at `openspec/changes/<name>/`.\n\nTo pick up where we left off later:\n- `/opsx:continue <name>` - Resume artifact creation\n- `/opsx:apply <name>` - Jump to implementation (if tasks exist)\n\nThe work won''t be lost. Come back whenever you''re ready.\n```\n\nExit gracefully without pressure.\n\n### User just wants command reference\n\nIf the user says they just want to see the commands or skip the tutorial:\n\n```\n## OpenSpec Quick Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems (no code changes) |\n| `/opsx:new <name>` | Start a new change, step by step |\n| `/opsx:ff <name>` | Fast-forward: all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue <name>` | Continue an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply <name>` | Implement tasks |\n| `/opsx:verify <name>` | Verify implementation |\n| `/opsx:archive <name>` | Archive when done |\n\nTry `/opsx:new` to start your first change, or `/opsx:ff` if you want to move fast.\n```\n\nExit gracefully.\n\n---\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- **Follow the EXPLAIN → DO → SHOW → PAUSE pattern** at key transitions (after explore, after proposal draft, after tasks, after archive)\n- **Keep narration light** during implementation—teach without lecturing\n- **Don''t skip phases** even if the change is small—the goal is teaching the workflow\n- **Pause for acknowledgment** at marked points, but don''t over-pause\n- **Handle exits gracefully**—never pressure the user to continue\n- **Use real codebase tasks**—don''t simulate or use fake examples\n- **Adjust scope gently**—guide toward smaller tasks but respect user choice\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:43:31.514Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing guided workflow cycles in OpenSpec","zh":"非常适合需要在 OpenSpec 中引导工作流周期的开发代理","ja":"OpenSpec でガイド付きのワークフロー サイクルを必要とする開発エージェントに最適","ko":"OpenSpec에서 가이드된 워크플로 사이클이 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 완벽함","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan ciclos de flujo de trabajo guiados en OpenSpec","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin de cycles de workflow guidés dans OpenSpec","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die geleitete Workflow-Zyklen in OpenSpec benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de ciclos de fluxo de trabalho orientados no OpenSpec","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, которым необходимы циклы рабочего процесса, управляемые в OpenSpec","ar":"مثالي لعمليات التطوير التي تحتاج إلى دورات عمل إرشادية في OpenSpec"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to initialize and manage OpenSpec projects, providing a seamless workflow experience through JSON status checks and command-line interactions like `openspec init` and `openspec status`","zh":"使代理能够初始化和管理 OpenSpec 项目，通过 JSON 状态检查和命令行交互（如 `openspec init` 和 `openspec status`）提供无缝的工作流体验","ja":"エージェントが OpenSpec プロジェクトを初期化および管理できるようにし、JSON ステータス チェックやコマンド ラインのやり取り（例: `openspec init` および `openspec status`）を介してシームレスなワークフロー エクスペリエンスを提供する","ko":"에이전트가 OpenSpec 프로젝트를 초기화하고 관리할 수 있도록 하며 JSON 상태 확인 및 명령줄 상호 작용(예: `openspec init` 및 `openspec status`)을 통해 무결점의 워크플로우 경험을 제공함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a inicializar y gestionar proyectos de OpenSpec, proporcionando una experiencia de flujo de trabajo sin problemas a través de comprobaciones de estado JSON y interacciones de línea de comandos como `openspec init` y `openspec status`","fr":"Permet aux agents d''initialiser et de gérer des projets OpenSpec, offrant une expérience de workflow fluide grâce aux vérifications de statut JSON et aux interactions de ligne de commande comme `openspec init` et `openspec status`","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, OpenSpec-Projekte zu initialisieren und zu verwalten, und bietet eine nahtlose Workflow-Erfahrung durch JSON-Statusprüfungen und Befehlszeileninteraktionen wie `openspec init` und `openspec status`","pt":"Habilita os agentes a inicializar e gerenciar projetos OpenSpec, fornecendo uma experiência de fluxo de trabalho sem interrupções por meio de verificações de status JSON e interações de linha de comando como `openspec init` e `openspec status`","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью инициализировать и управлять проектами OpenSpec, обеспечивая бесшовный опыт рабочего процесса через проверки статуса JSON и командную строку взаимодействия, такие как `openspec init` и `openspec status`","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من 초기ية وإدارة مشاريع OpenSpec، وتوفير تجربة عمل سلسة من خلال عمليات التحقق من حالة JSON وتفاعلات سطر الأوامر مثل `openspec init` و `openspec status`"},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing OpenSpec in new projects","Guiding users through complete OpenSpec workflow cycles","Debugging OpenSpec initialization issues with `openspec status --json`"],"zh":["在新项目中初始化 OpenSpec","引导用户完成 OpenSpec 工作流周期","使用 `openspec status --json` 调试 OpenSpec 初始化问题"],"ja":["新しいプロジェクトで OpenSpec を初期化する","ユーザーを OpenSpec ワークフロー サイクルに沿って導く","OpenSpec 初期化の問題を `openspec status --json` でデバッグする"],"ko":["새 프로젝트에서 OpenSpec 초기화","사용자를 OpenSpec 워크플로우 사이클을 통해 안내","OpenSpec 초기화 문제를 `openspec status --json`으로 디버깅"],"es":["Inicializar OpenSpec en nuevos proyectos","Guía a los usuarios a través de ciclos de flujo de trabajo de OpenSpec completos","Depurar problemas de inicialización de OpenSpec con `openspec status --json`"],"fr":["Initialiser OpenSpec dans de nouveaux projets","Guider les utilisateurs à travers des cycles de workflow OpenSpec complets","Déboguer les problèmes d''initialisation d''OpenSpec avec `openspec status --json`"],"de":["OpenSpec in neuen Projekten initialisieren","Benutzer durch vollständige OpenSpec-Workflow-Zyklen führen","OpenSpec-Initialisierungsprobleme mit `openspec status --json` debuggen"],"pt":["Inicializando OpenSpec em novos projetos","Orientando os usuários por meio de ciclos de fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec completos","Depurando problemas de inicialização OpenSpec com `openspec status --json`"],"ru":["Инициализация OpenSpec в новых проектах","Направление пользователей через полные циклы рабочего процесса OpenSpec","Отладка проблем инициализации OpenSpec с помощью `openspec status --json`"],"ar":["ت 初يية OpenSpec في مشاريع جديدة","إرشاد المستخدمين من خلال دورات عمل OpenSpec الكاملة","تصحيح أخطاء بدء تشغيل OpenSpec باستخدام `openspec status --json`"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires OpenSpec installation","Needs command-line access for `openspec` commands"],"zh":["需要 OpenSpec 安装","需要命令行访问以执行 `openspec` 命令"],"ja":["OpenSpec のインストールが必要","コマンド ラインへのアクセスが `openspec` コマンドを実行するために必要"],"ko":["OpenSpec 설치가 필요","명령줄 액세스가 `openspec` 명령을 실행하는 데 필요"],"es":["Requiere instalación de OpenSpec","Necesita acceso a la línea de comandos para los comandos `openspec`"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation d''OpenSpec","Nécessite un accès à la ligne de commande pour les commandes `openspec`"],"de":["Benötigt OpenSpec-Installation","Benötigt Befehlszeilenzugriff für `openspec`-Befehle"],"pt":["Exige instalação do OpenSpec","Necessita acesso à linha de comando para comandos `openspec`"],"ru":["Требует установки OpenSpec","Требует доступа к командной строке для команд `openspec`"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت OpenSpec","يحتاج إلى وصول إلى سطر الأوامر لأوامر `openspec`"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
