使用","データの保存と同期のための柔軟性","JSON Canvas Spec 1.0 をサポート","nodes と edges の 2 つのトップレベル配列を含む"],"ko":["유효한 JSON Canvas 파일 생성 및 편집","Obsidian 및 다른 애플리케이션에서 사용","데이터 저장 및 동기화의 유연성","JSON Canvas Spec 1.0 지원","노드 및 에지의 2개 이상의 최상위 배열 포함"],"es":["Creación y edición de archivos de lienzo en formato JSON","Compatibilidad con Obsidian y otras aplicaciones","Formato de archivo abierto para datos de lienzo infinito","Seguimiento de la especificación JSON Canvas 1.0","Estructura de archivo flexible con nodos y aristas"],"fr":["Création et édition de fichiers de canevas au format JSON","Compatibilité avec Obsidian et d''autres applications","Format de fichier ouvert pour les données de canevas infini","Suivi de la spécification JSON Canvas 1.0","Structure de fichier flexible avec des nœuds et des arêtes"],"de":["Erstellung und Bearbeitung von JSON-Canvas-Dateien","Kompatibilität mit Obsidian und anderen Anwendungen","Offenes Dateiformat für infinite Canvas-Daten","Einhaltung der JSON Canvas-Spezifikation 1.0","Flexibles Dateiformat mit Knoten und Kanten"],"pt":["Criação e edição de arquivos de canvas válidos","Utilização do Obsidian como banco de dados e veículo de sincronização de dados","Suporte ao formato de arquivo JSON Canvas","Integração com aplicativos que utilizam o formato JSON Canvas","Edição de nodes e edges em arquivos de canvas"],"ru":["Создание и редактирование допустимых файлов canvas","Использование Obsidian в качестве базы данных и транспортного средства для синхронизации данных","Поддержка формата файла JSON Canvas","Интеграция с приложениями, использующими формат JSON Canvas","Редактирование узлов и ребер в файлах canvas"],"ar":["إنشاء وتحرير ملفات Canvas صالحة","استخدام Obsidian كقاعدة بيانات ووسيلة لنقل البيانات","دعم تنسيق ملف JSON Canvas","التكامل مع التطبيقات التي تستخدم تنسيق JSON Canvas","تحرير العقد والزوايا في ملفات Canvas"]},"keywords":{"zh":["JSON Canvas","Obsidian 插件","无限画布数据","JSON 文件","数据存储","数据同步","开发工具"],"ja":["JSON Canvas","Obsidian プラグイン","無限のキャンバスデータ","JSON ファイル","データの保存","データの同期","開発ツール"],"ko":["JSON Canvas","Obsidian 플러그인","무한한 캔버스 데이터","JSON 파일","데이터 저장","데이터 동기화","개발 도구"],"es":["JSON Canvas","Obsidian","inspección de redes de utilidad","formato de archivo abierto","datos de lienzo infinito","JSON","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["JSON Canvas","Obsidian","inspection de réseaux d''utilité","format de fichier ouvert","données de canevas infini","JSON","développement de logiciels","outils de développement"],"de":["JSON Canvas","Obsidian","Inspektion von Versorgungsnetzen","offenes Dateiformat","infinite Canvas-Daten","JSON","Software-Entwicklung","Entwickler-Tools"],"pt":["JSON Canvas","Obsidian","inspeção de redes de utilidade","arquivos de canvas","formato de arquivo JSON Canvas","desenvolvimento de software","tecnologia de dados","integração de aplicativos"],"ru":["JSON Canvas","Obsidian","осмотр коммунальных сетей","файлы canvas","формат файла JSON Canvas","разработка программного обеспечения","технология данных","интеграция приложений"],"ar":["JSON Canvas","Obsidian","عمليات التفتيش على شبكات المرافق","ملفات Canvas","تنسيق ملف JSON Canvas","تطوير البرمجيات","تكنولوجيا البيانات","التكامل بين التطبيقات"]}},"owner":"rmachado24","repo":"obsidian-inspections","repoPath":"rmachado24/obsidian-inspections","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.450Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"json-canvas","description":"Create and edit JSON Canvas files (.canvas) with nodes, edges, groups, and connections. Use when working with .canvas files, creating visual canvases, mind maps, flowcharts, or when the user mentions Canvas files in Obsidian.","bodyPreview":"# JSON Canvas Skill\n\nThis skill enables skills-compatible agents to create and edit valid JSON Canvas files (`.canvas`) used in Obsidian and other applications.\n\n## Overview\n\nJSON Canvas is an open file format for infinite canvas data. Canvas files use the `.canvas` extension and contain valid JSON following the [JSON Canvas Spec 1.0](https://jsoncanvas.org/spec/1.0/).\n\n## File Structure\n\nA canvas file contains two top-level arrays:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"nodes\": [],\n  \"edges\": []\n}\n```\n\n- `nodes` (optio","body":"# JSON Canvas Skill\n\nThis skill enables skills-compatible agents to create and edit valid JSON Canvas files (`.canvas`) used in Obsidian and other applications.\n\n## Overview\n\nJSON Canvas is an open file format for infinite canvas data. Canvas files use the `.canvas` extension and contain valid JSON following the [JSON Canvas Spec 1.0](https://jsoncanvas.org/spec/1.0/).\n\n## File Structure\n\nA canvas file contains two top-level arrays:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"nodes\": [],\n  \"edges\": []\n}\n```\n\n- `nodes` (optional): Array of node objects\n- `edges` (optional): Array of edge objects connecting nodes\n\n## Nodes\n\nNodes are objects placed on the canvas. There are four node types:\n- `text` - Text content with Markdown\n- `file` - Reference to files/attachments\n- `link` - External URL\n- `group` - Visual container for other nodes\n\n### Z-Index Ordering\n\nNodes are ordered by z-index in the array:\n- First node = bottom layer (displayed below others)\n- Last node = top layer (displayed above others)\n\n### Generic Node Attributes\n\nAll nodes share these attributes:\n\n| Attribute | Required | Type | Description |\n|-----------|----------|------|-------------|\n| `id` | Yes | string | Unique identifier for the node |\n| `type` | Yes | string | Node type: `text`, `file`, `link`, or `group` |\n| `x` | Yes | integer | X position in pixels |\n| `y` | Yes | integer | Y position in pixels |\n| `width` | Yes | integer | Width in pixels |\n| `height` | Yes | integer | Height in pixels |\n| `color` | No | canvasColor | Node color (see Color section) |\n\n### Text Nodes\n\nText nodes contain Markdown content.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"6f0ad84f44ce9c17\",\n  \"type\": \"text\",\n  \"x\": 0,\n  \"y\": 0,\n  \"width\": 400,\n  \"height\": 200,\n  \"text\": \"# Hello World\\n\\nThis is **Markdown** content.\"\n}\n```\n\n#### Newline Escaping (Common Pitfall)\n\nIn JSON, newline characters inside strings **must** be represented as `\\n`. Do **not** use the literal sequence `\\\\n` in a `.canvas` file—Obsidian will render it as the characters `\\` and `n` instead of a line break.\n\nExamples:\n\n```json\n{ \"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Line 1\\nLine 2\" }\n```\n\n```json\n{ \"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Line 1\\\\nLine 2\" }\n```\n\n| Attribute | Required | Type | Description |\n|-----------|----------|------|-------------|\n| `text` | Yes | string | Plain text with Markdown syntax |\n\n### File Nodes\n\nFile nodes reference files or attachments (images, videos, PDFs, notes, etc.).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"a1b2c3d4e5f67890\",\n  \"type\": \"file\",\n  \"x\": 500,\n  \"y\": 0,\n  \"width\": 400,\n  \"height\": 300,\n  \"file\": \"Attachments/diagram.png\"\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"b2c3d4e5f6789012\",\n  \"type\": \"file\",\n  \"x\": 500,\n  \"y\": 400,\n  \"width\": 400,\n  \"height\": 300,\n  \"file\": \"Notes/Project Overview.md\",\n  \"subpath\": \"#Implementation\"\n}\n```\n\n| Attribute | Required | Type | Description |\n|-----------|----------|------|-------------|\n| `file` | Yes | string | Path to file within the system |\n| `subpath` | No | string | Link to heading or block (starts with `#`) |\n\n### Link Nodes\n\nLink nodes display external URLs.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"c3d4e5f678901234\",\n  \"type\": \"link\",\n  \"x\": 1000,\n  \"y\": 0,\n  \"width\": 400,\n  \"height\": 200,\n  \"url\": \"https://obsidian.md\"\n}\n```\n\n| Attribute | Required | Type | Description |\n|-----------|----------|------|-------------|\n| `url` | Yes | string | External URL |\n\n### Group Nodes\n\nGroup nodes are visual containers for organizing other nodes.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"d4e5f6789012345a\",\n  \"type\": \"group\",\n  \"x\": -50,\n  \"y\": -50,\n  \"width\": 1000,\n  \"height\": 600,\n  \"label\": \"Project Overview\",\n  \"color\": \"4\"\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"e5f67890123456ab\",\n  \"type\": \"group\",\n  \"x\": 0,\n  \"y\": 700,\n  \"width\": 800,\n  \"height\": 500,\n  \"label\": \"Resources\",\n  \"background\": \"Attachments/background.png\",\n  \"backgroundStyle\": \"cover\"\n}\n```\n\n| Attribute | Required | Type | Description |\n|-----------|----------|------|-------------|\n| `label` | No | string | Text label for the group |\n| `background` | No | string | Path to background image |\n| `backgroundStyle` | No | string | Background rendering style |\n\n#### Background Styles\n\n| Value | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `cover` | Fills entire width and height of node |\n| `ratio` | Maintains aspect ratio of background image |\n| `repeat` | Repeats image as pattern in both directions |\n\n## Edges\n\nEdges are lines connecting nodes.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"f67890123456789a\",\n  \"fromNode\": \"6f0ad84f44ce9c17\",\n  \"toNode\": \"a1b2c3d4e5f67890\"\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"0123456789abcdef\",\n  \"fromNode\": \"6f0ad84f44ce9c17\",\n  \"fromSide\": \"right\",\n  \"fromEnd\": \"none\",\n  \"toNode\": \"b2c3d4e5f6789012\",\n  \"toSide\": \"left\",\n  \"toEnd\": \"arrow\",\n  \"color\": \"1\",\n  \"label\": \"leads to\"\n}\n```\n\n| Attribute | Required | Type | Default | Description |\n|-----------|----------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `id` | Yes | string | - | Unique identifier for the edge |\n| `fromNode` | Yes | string | - | Node ID where connection starts |\n| `fromSide` | No | string | - | Side where edge starts |\n| `fromEnd` | No | string | `none` | Shape at edge start |\n| `toNode` | Yes | string | - | Node ID where connection ends |\n| `toSide` | No | string | - | Side where edge ends |\n| `toEnd` | No | string | `arrow` | Shape at edge end |\n| `color` | No | canvasColor | - | Line color |\n| `label` | No | string | - | Text label for the edge |\n\n### Side Values\n\n| Value | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `top` | Top edge of node |\n| `right` | Right edge of node |\n| `bottom` | Bottom edge of node |\n| `left` | Left edge of node |\n\n### End Shapes\n\n| Value | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `none` | No endpoint shape |\n| `arrow` | Arrow endpoint |\n\n## Colors\n\nThe `canvasColor` type can be specified in two ways:\n\n### Hex Colors\n\n```json\n{\n  \"color\": \"#FF0000\"\n}\n```\n\n### Preset Colors\n\n```json\n{\n  \"color\": \"1\"\n}\n```\n\n| Preset | Color |\n|--------|-------|\n| `\"1\"` | Red |\n| `\"2\"` | Orange |\n| `\"3\"` | Yellow |\n| `\"4\"` | Green |\n| `\"5\"` | Cyan |\n| `\"6\"` | Purple |\n\nNote: Specific color values for presets are intentionally undefined, allowing applications to use their own brand colors.\n\n## Complete Examples\n\n### Simple Canvas with Text and Connections\n\n```json\n{\n  \"nodes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8a9b0c1d2e3f4a5b\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 0,\n      \"y\": 0,\n      \"width\": 300,\n      \"height\": 150,\n      \"text\": \"# Main Idea\\n\\nThis is the central concept.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 400,\n      \"y\": -100,\n      \"width\": 250,\n      \"height\": 100,\n      \"text\": \"## Supporting Point A\\n\\nDetails here.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 400,\n      \"y\": 100,\n      \"width\": 250,\n      \"height\": 100,\n      \"text\": \"## Supporting Point B\\n\\nMore details.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"edges\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"8a9b0c1d2e3f4a5b\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"right\",\n      \"toNode\": \"1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b\",\n      \"toSide\": \"left\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"8a9b0c1d2e3f4a5b\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"right\",\n      \"toNode\": \"2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c\",\n      \"toSide\": \"left\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Project Board with Groups\n\n```json\n{\n  \"nodes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f\",\n      \"type\": \"group\",\n      \"x\": 0,\n      \"y\": 0,\n      \"width\": 300,\n      \"height\": 500,\n      \"label\": \"To Do\",\n      \"color\": \"1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6f7a8b9c0d1e2f3a\",\n      \"type\": \"group\",\n      \"x\": 350,\n      \"y\": 0,\n      \"width\": 300,\n      \"height\": 500,\n      \"label\": \"In Progress\",\n      \"color\": \"3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7a8b9c0d1e2f3a4b\",\n      \"type\": \"group\",\n      \"x\": 700,\n      \"y\": 0,\n      \"width\": 300,\n      \"height\": 500,\n      \"label\": \"Done\",\n      \"color\": \"4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8b9c0d1e2f3a4b5c\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 20,\n      \"y\": 50,\n      \"width\": 260,\n      \"height\": 80,\n      \"text\": \"## Task 1\\n\\nImplement feature X\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9c0d1e2f3a4b5c6d\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 370,\n      \"y\": 50,\n      \"width\": 260,\n      \"height\": 80,\n      \"text\": \"## Task 2\\n\\nReview PR #123\",\n      \"color\": \"2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0d1e2f3a4b5c6d7e\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 720,\n      \"y\": 50,\n      \"width\": 260,\n      \"height\": 80,\n      \"text\": \"## Task 3\\n\\n~~Setup CI/CD~~\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"edges\": []\n}\n```\n\n### Research Canvas with Files and Links\n\n```json\n{\n  \"nodes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 300,\n      \"y\": 200,\n      \"width\": 400,\n      \"height\": 200,\n      \"text\": \"# Research Topic\\n\\n## Key Questions\\n\\n- How does X affect Y?\\n- What are the implications?\",\n      \"color\": \"5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a\",\n      \"type\": \"file\",\n      \"x\": 0,\n      \"y\": 0,\n      \"width\": 250,\n      \"height\": 150,\n      \"file\": \"Literature/Paper A.pdf\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b\",\n      \"type\": \"file\",\n      \"x\": 0,\n      \"y\": 200,\n      \"width\": 250,\n      \"height\": 150,\n      \"file\": \"Notes/Meeting Notes.md\",\n      \"subpath\": \"#Key Insights\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"4b5c6d7e8f9a0b1c\",\n      \"type\": \"link\",\n      \"x\": 0,\n      \"y\": 400,\n      \"width\": 250,\n      \"height\": 100,\n      \"url\": \"https://example.com/research\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5c6d7e8f9a0b1c2d\",\n      \"type\": \"file\",\n      \"x\": 750,\n      \"y\": 150,\n      \"width\": 300,\n      \"height\": 250,\n      \"file\": \"Attachments/diagram.png\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"edges\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6d7e8f9a0b1c2d3e\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"right\",\n      \"toNode\": \"1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f\",\n      \"toSide\": \"left\",\n      \"label\": \"supports\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7e8f9a0b1c2d3e4f\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"right\",\n      \"toNode\": \"1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f\",\n      \"toSide\": \"left\",\n      \"label\": \"informs\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8f9a0b1c2d3e4f5a\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"4b5c6d7e8f9a0b1c\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"right\",\n      \"toNode\": \"1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f\",\n      \"toSide\": \"left\",\n      \"toEnd\": \"arrow\",\n      \"color\": \"6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"right\",\n      \"toNode\": \"5c6d7e8f9a0b1c2d\",\n      \"toSide\": \"left\",\n      \"label\": \"visualized by\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Flowchart\n\n```json\n{\n  \"nodes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b7\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 200,\n      \"y\": 0,\n      \"width\": 150,\n      \"height\": 60,\n      \"text\": \"**Start**\",\n      \"color\": \"4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 200,\n      \"y\": 100,\n      \"width\": 150,\n      \"height\": 60,\n      \"text\": \"Step 1:\\nGather data\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 200,\n      \"y\": 200,\n      \"width\": 150,\n      \"height\": 80,\n      \"text\": \"**Decision**\\n\\nIs data valid?\",\n      \"color\": \"3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 400,\n      \"y\": 200,\n      \"width\": 150,\n      \"height\": 60,\n      \"text\": \"Process data\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 0,\n      \"y\": 200,\n      \"width\": 150,\n      \"height\": 60,\n      \"text\": \"Request new data\",\n      \"color\": \"1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a2\",\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"x\": 400,\n      \"y\": 320,\n      \"width\": 150,\n      \"height\": 60,\n      \"text\": \"**End**\",\n      \"color\": \"4\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"edges\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a6b7c8d9e0f1a2b3\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b7\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"bottom\",\n      \"toNode\": \"b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8\",\n      \"toSide\": \"top\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b7c8d9e0f1a2b3c4\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"bottom\",\n      \"toNode\": \"c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9\",\n      \"toSide\": \"top\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8d9e0f1a2b3c4d5\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"right\",\n      \"toNode\": \"d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0\",\n      \"toSide\": \"left\",\n      \"label\": \"Yes\",\n      \"color\": \"4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d9e0f1a2b3c4d5e6\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"left\",\n      \"toNode\": \"e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1\",\n      \"toSide\": \"right\",\n      \"label\": \"No\",\n      \"color\": \"1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e0f1a2b3c4d5e6f7\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"top\",\n      \"fromEnd\": \"none\",\n      \"toNode\": \"b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8\",\n      \"toSide\": \"left\",\n      \"toEnd\": \"arrow\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8\",\n      \"fromNode\": \"d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0\",\n      \"fromSide\": \"bottom\",\n      \"toNode\": \"f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a2\",\n      \"toSide\": \"top\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## ID Generation\n\nNode and edge IDs must be unique strings. Obsidian generates 16-character hexadecimal IDs:\n\n```json\n\"id\": \"6f0ad84f44ce9c17\"\n\"id\": \"a3b2c1d0e9f8g7h6\"\n\"id\": \"1234567890abcdef\"\n```\n\nThis format is a 16-character lowercase hex string (64-bit random value).\n\n## Layout Guidelines\n\n### Positioning\n\n- Coordinates can be negative (canvas extends infinitely)\n- `x` increases to the right\n- `y` increases downward\n- Position refers to top-left corner of node\n\n### Recommended Sizes\n\n| Node Type | Suggested Width | Suggested Height |\n|-----------|-----------------|------------------|\n| Small text | 200-300 | 80-150 |\n| Medium text | 300-450 | 150-300 |\n| Large text | 400-600 | 300-500 |\n| File preview | 300-500 | 200-400 |\n| Link preview | 250-400 | 100-200 |\n| Group | Varies | Varies |\n\n### Spacing\n\n- Leave 20-50px padding inside groups\n- Space nodes 50-100px apart for readability\n- Align nodes to grid (multiples of 10 or 20) for cleaner layouts\n\n## Validation Rules\n\n1. All `id` values must be unique across nodes and edges\n2. `fromNode` and `toNode` must reference existing node IDs\n3. Required fields must be present for each node type\n4. `type` must be one of: `text`, `file`, `link`, `group`\n5. `backgroundStyle` must be one of: `cover`, `ratio`, `repeat`\n6. `fromSide`, `toSide` must be one of: `top`, `right`, `bottom`, `left`\n7. `fromEnd`, `toEnd` must be one of: `none`, `arrow`\n8. Color presets must be `\"1\"` through `\"6\"` or valid hex color\n\n## References\n\n- [JSON Canvas Spec 1.0](https://jsoncanvas.org/spec/1.0/)\n- [JSON Canvas GitHub](https://github.com/obsidianmd/jsoncanvas)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:43:03.803Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Visualization Agents needing to create and edit valid JSON Canvas files for utility network inspections in Obsidian.","zh":"非常适合需要创建和编辑有效的JSON画布文件以进行奥比斯坦公用事业网络检查的数据可视化代理。","ja":"オビシアンでのユーティリティネットワークの検査のために有効なJSONキャンバスファイルを作成および編集する必要があるデータ視覚化エージェントに最適です。","ko":"오비시안에서 유틸리티 네트워크 검사를 위해 유효한 JSON 캔버스 파일을 생성 및 편집해야 하는 데이터 시각화 에이전트에게 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de visualización de datos que necesitan crear y editar archivos de lienzo JSON válidos para inspecciones de redes de servicios en Obsidian.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de visualisation de données ayant besoin de créer et de modifier des fichiers de canevas JSON valides pour les inspections de réseaux de services dans Obsidian.","de":"Perfekt für Data-Visualisierungs-Agents, die gültige JSON-Canvas-Dateien für Utility-Netzwerk-Inspektionen in Obsidian erstellen und bearbeiten müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Visualização de Dados que precisam criar e editar arquivos de canvas JSON válidos para inspeções de redes de utilidade no Obsidian.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов визуализации данных, которым необходимо создавать и редактировать действительные файлы JSON Canvas для осмотров коммунальных сетей в Obsidian.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات مراقبة الوكلاء التي تحتاج إلى إنشاء وتحرير ملفات JSON Canvas صالحة لتفقيدات شبكات المرافق في Obsidian."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate and manipulate infinite canvas data using the JSON Canvas Spec 1.0, enabling advanced data visualization and synchronization capabilities with Obsidian as the database and frontend, and supporting file formats like .canvas.","zh":"使代理能够使用JSON画布规范1.0生成和操作无限画布数据，从而实现高级数据可视化和与奥比斯坦作为数据库和前端的同步功能，并支持类似.canvas的文件格式。","ja":"エージェントがJSONキャンバス仕様1.0を使用して無限のキャンバスデータを生成および操作できるようにし、高度なデータ視覚化とオビシアンをデータベースおよびフロントエンドとして使用した同期機能を可能にし、.canvasなどのファイル形式をサポートします。","ko":"에이전트가 JSON 캔버스 사양 1.0을 사용하여 무한 캔버스 데이터를 생성 및 조작할 수 있게 해주어 고급 데이터 시각화 및 오비시안을 데이터베이스 및 프론트엔드로 사용한同步기능을 가능하게 하며, .canvas와 같은 파일 형식을 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar y manipular datos de lienzo infinito utilizando la especificación JSON Canvas 1.0, lo que permite capacidades avanzadas de visualización y sincronización de datos con Obsidian como base de datos y frontend, y admite formatos de archivo como .canvas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer et de manipuler des données de canevas infinies en utilisant la spécification JSON Canvas 1.0, ce qui permet des capacités de visualisation et de synchronisation de données avancées avec Obsidian en tant que base de données et interface frontend, et prend en charge des formats de fichiers tels que .canvas.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, endlose Canvas-Daten mithilfe der JSON-Canvas-Spezifikation 1.0 zu generieren und zu manipulieren, wodurch erweiterte Datenvisualisierungs- und Synchronisierungsfunktionen mit Obsidian als Datenbank und Frontend ermöglicht werden, und unterstützt Dateiformate wie .canvas.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar e manipular dados de canvas infinitos usando a Especificação JSON Canvas 1.0, permitindo capacidades avançadas de visualização de dados e sincronização com o Obsidian como banco de dados e frontend, e suportando formatos de arquivo como .canvas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать и манипулировать данными бесконечного холста с использованием спецификации JSON Canvas 1.0, что обеспечивает расширенные возможности визуализации данных и синхронизации с Obsidian в качестве базы данных и frontend, а также поддержку форматов файлов, таких как .canvas.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من توليد وتنويع بيانات الشبكة غير المحدودة باستخدام مواصفات JSON Canvas 1.0، مما يُمكّن من إمكانيات متقدمة للرؤية البصرية والتنسيق مع Obsidian كقاعدة بيانات وواجهة أمامية، ودعم صيغ الملفات مثل .canvas."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating and editing JSON Canvas files for network inspections","Generating valid JSON data for infinite canvas applications","Synchronizing canvas data with Obsidian for seamless utility network visualization"],"zh":["为网络检查创建和编辑JSON画布文件","为无限画布应用程序生成有效的JSON数据","将画布数据与奥比斯坦同步以实现无缝的公用事业网络可视化"],"ja":["ネットワークの検査のためにJSONキャンバスファイルを作成および編集する","無限のキャンバスアプリケーション用に有効なJSONデータを生成する","キャンバスデータをオビシアンと同期してシームレスなユーティリティネットワークの視覚化を実現する"],"ko":["네트워크 검사를 위해 JSON 캔버스 파일을 생성 및 편집","무한 캔버스 애플리케이션을 위한 유효한 JSON 데이터를 생성","캔버스 데이터를 오비시안과 동기화하여 무결점 유틸리티 네트워크 시각화를 구현"],"es":["Crear y editar archivos de lienzo JSON para inspecciones de redes","Generar datos JSON válidos para aplicaciones de lienzo infinito","Sincronizar datos de lienzo con Obsidian para una visualización de redes de servicios sin problemas"],"fr":["Créer et modifier des fichiers de canevas JSON pour les inspections de réseaux","Générer des données JSON valides pour les applications de canevas infinies","Synchroniser les données de canevas avec Obsidian pour une visualisation de réseaux de services sans interruption"],"de":["Erstellen und Bearbeiten von JSON-Canvas-Dateien für Utility-Netzwerk-Inspektionen","Generieren von gültigen JSON-Daten für endlose Canvas-Anwendungen","Synchronisieren von Canvas-Daten mit Obsidian für eine nahtlose Visualisierung von Utility-Netzwerken"],"pt":["Criar e editar arquivos JSON Canvas para inspeções de rede","Gerar dados JSON válidos para aplicativos de canvas infinito","Sincronizar dados de canvas com o Obsidian para visualização de rede de utilidade sem interrupções"],"ru":["Создание и редактирование файлов JSON Canvas для осмотров сетей","Генерация действительных JSON-данных для приложений бесконечного холста","Синхронизация данных холста с Obsidian для бесперебойной визуализации коммунальных сетей"],"ar":["إنشاء وتحرير ملفات JSON Canvas لتفقيدات الشبكة","توليد بيانات JSON صالحة لتطبيقات الشبكة غير المحدودة","تمكين بيانات الشبكة مع Obsidian من أجل رؤية شبكات المرافق دون انقطاع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Obsidian as the database and frontend","Limited to JSON Canvas Spec 1.0 compatibility"],"zh":["需要奥比斯坦作为数据库和前端","仅限于JSON画布规范1.0的兼容性"],"ja":["オビシアンをデータベースおよびフロントエンドとして使用する必要がある","JSONキャンバス仕様1.0との互換性に限定される"],"ko":["오비시안을 데이터베이스 및 프론트엔드로서 사용해야 함","JSON 캔버스 사양 1.0과의 호환성으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere Obsidian como base de datos y frontend","Limitado a la compatibilidad con la especificación JSON Canvas 1.0"],"fr":["Nécessite Obsidian en tant que base de données et interface frontend","Limité à la compatibilité avec la spécification JSON Canvas 1.0"],"de":["Benötigt Obsidian als Datenbank und Frontend","Begrenzt auf die Kompatibilität mit der JSON-Canvas-Spezifikation 1.0"],"pt":["Exige o Obsidian como banco de dados e frontend","Limitado à compatibilidade com a Especificação JSON Canvas 1.0"],"ru":["Требует Obsidian в качестве базы данных и frontend","Ограничен совместимостью со спецификацией JSON Canvas 1.0"],"ar":["يتطلب Obsidian كقاعدة بيانات وواجهة أمامية","محدود بالتوافق مع مواصفات JSON Canvas 1.0"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('jaxxstorm/dnstrace/openspec-onboard', 'community', 'jaxxstorm', 'dnstrace', 'jaxxstorm/dnstrace', 'openspec-onboard', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.450Z', '2026-02-18T06:43:48.813Z', NULL, '{"id":"jaxxstorm/dnstrace/openspec-onboard","name":"openspec-onboard","description":{"zh":"本文将指导您完成OpenSpec的第一个完整工作流程周期，包括初始化、工作流程和代码优化","ja":"OpenSpecの最初の完全なワークフロー周期を実行するためのガイド。初期化、ワークフロー、コード最適化などが含まれます","ko":"OpenSpec의 첫 번째 완전한 워크플로우 사이클을 완료하는 방법에 대한 가이드입니다. 초기화, 워크플로우, 코드 최적화 등이 포함됩니다","es":"Guía para configurar OpenSpec en tu proyecto. Aprende a inicializar y utilizar OpenSpec en tu flujo de trabajo","fr":"Guide pour configurer OpenSpec dans votre projet. Apprenez à initialiser et utiliser OpenSpec dans votre flux de travail","de":"Anleitung zur Konfiguration von OpenSpec in Ihrem Projekt. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie OpenSpec initialisieren und verwenden","pt":"O OpenSpec Onboard é um guia que ajuda a configurar o OpenSpec e iniciar o workflow. Aprenda a melhorar seu código com essa ferramenta","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard — это руководство, которое помогает настроить OpenSpec и начать workflow. Узнайте, как улучшить свой код с помощью этого инструмента","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard هو دليل يساعد في تكوين OpenSpec وبدء العمل. تعلم كيفية تحسين رمزك باستخدام أداة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"OpenSpec入门指南","ja":"OpenSpecの使い方","ko":"OpenSpec 시작하기","es":"Onboarding con OpenSpec","fr":"Premiers pas avec OpenSpec","de":"OpenSpec-Onboarding","pt":"OpenSpec Onboard: Guia de Inicialização","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard: Руководство по началу работы","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard: دليل الإعداد الأولي","en":"openspec-onboard"},"description":{"zh":"本文将指导您完成OpenSpec的第一个完整工作流程周期，包括初始化、工作流程和代码优化","ja":"OpenSpecの最初の完全なワークフロー周期を実行するためのガイド。初期化、ワークフロー、コード最適化などが含まれます","ko":"OpenSpec의 첫 번째 완전한 워크플로우 사이클을 완료하는 방법에 대한 가이드입니다. 초기화, 워크플로우, 코드 최적화 등이 포함됩니다","es":"Guía para configurar OpenSpec en tu proyecto. Aprende a inicializar y utilizar OpenSpec en tu flujo de trabajo","fr":"Guide pour configurer OpenSpec dans votre projet. Apprenez à initialiser et utiliser OpenSpec dans votre flux de travail","de":"Anleitung zur Konfiguration von OpenSpec in Ihrem Projekt. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie OpenSpec initialisieren und verwenden","pt":"O OpenSpec Onboard é um guia que ajuda a configurar o OpenSpec e iniciar o workflow. Aprenda a melhorar seu código com essa ferramenta","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard — это руководство, которое помогает настроить OpenSpec и начать workflow. Узнайте, как улучшить свой код с помощью этого инструмента","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard هو دليل يساعد في تكوين OpenSpec وبدء العمل. تعلم كيفية تحسين رمزك باستخدام أداة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["OpenSpec初始化","工作流程指导","代码优化","开发效率提高","代码质量保证"],"ja":["OpenSpecの初期化","ワークフローのガイド","コード最適化","開発効率の向上","コード品質の保証"],"ko":["OpenSpec 초기화","워크플로우 가이드","코드 최적화","개발 효율성 향상","코드 품질 보장"],"es":["Inicialización de OpenSpec","Configuración del flujo de trabajo","Ejecución de comandos de OpenSpec","Verificación del estado de OpenSpec","Integración con el código del proyecto"],"fr":["Initialisation d''OpenSpec","Configuration du flux de travail","Exécution des commandes OpenSpec","Vérification de l''état d''OpenSpec","Intégration avec le code du projet"],"de":["Initialisierung von OpenSpec","Konfiguration des Arbeitsablaufs","Ausführung von OpenSpec-Befehlen","Überprüfung des OpenSpec-Status","Integration mit dem Projektcod"],"pt":["Configuração do OpenSpec","Iniciação do workflow","Melhoria do código","Guia passo a passo","Verificação de inicialização"],"ru":["Настройка OpenSpec","Запуск workflow","Улучшение кода","Пошаговое руководство","Проверка инициализации"],"ar":["تكوين OpenSpec","بدء العمل","تحسين الرمز","دليل خطوة بخطوة","فحص الإعداد الأولي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["OpenSpec","代码规范","代码优化","开发效率","代码质量","工作流程"],"ja":["OpenSpec","コード規範","コード最適化","開発効率","コード品質","ワークフロー"],"ko":["OpenSpec","코드 표준","코드 최적화","개발 효율성","코드 품질","워크플로우"],"es":["OpenSpec","onboarding","configuración","flujo de trabajo","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo","introducción a OpenSpec","tutorial OpenSpec"],"fr":["OpenSpec","onboarding","configuration","flux de travail","développement de logiciels","outils de développement","introduction à OpenSpec","didacticiel OpenSpec"],"de":["OpenSpec","Onboarding","Konfiguration","Arbeitsablauf","Softwareentwicklung","Entwicklungstools","Einführung in OpenSpec","OpenSpec-Tutorial"],"pt":["OpenSpec","Onboard","Guia de inicialização","Configuração","Workflow","Melhoria do código","Desenvolvimento de software","Ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["OpenSpec","Onboard","Руководство по началу работы","Настройка","Workflow","Улучшение кода","Разработка программного обеспечения","Инструменты разработки"],"ar":["OpenSpec","Onboard","دليل الإعداد الأولي","تكوين","العمل","تحسين الرمز","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"jaxxstorm","repo":"dnstrace","repoPath":"jaxxstorm/dnstrace","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.450Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-onboard","description":"Guided onboarding for OpenSpec - walk through a complete workflow cycle with narration and real codebase work.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay","body":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay:\n\n```\n## Welcome to OpenSpec!\n\nI''ll walk you through a complete change cycle—from idea to implementation—using a real task in your codebase. Along the way, you''ll learn the workflow by doing it.\n\n**What we''ll do:**\n1. Pick a small, real task in your codebase\n2. Explore the problem briefly\n3. Create a change (the container for our work)\n4. Build the artifacts: proposal → specs → design → tasks\n5. Implement the tasks\n6. Archive the completed change\n\n**Time:** ~15-20 minutes\n\nLet''s start by finding something to work on.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Task Selection\n\n### Codebase Analysis\n\nScan the codebase for small improvement opportunities. Look for:\n\n1. **TODO/FIXME comments** - Search for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `HACK`, `XXX` in code files\n2. **Missing error handling** - `catch` blocks that swallow errors, risky operations without try-catch\n3. **Functions without tests** - Cross-reference `src/` with test directories\n4. **Type issues** - `any` types in TypeScript files (`: any`, `as any`)\n5. **Debug artifacts** - `console.log`, `console.debug`, `debugger` statements in non-debug code\n6. **Missing validation** - User input handlers without validation\n\nAlso check recent git activity:\n```bash\ngit log --oneline -10 2>/dev/null || echo \"No git history\"\n```\n\n### Present Suggestions\n\nFrom your analysis, present 3-4 specific suggestions:\n\n```\n## Task Suggestions\n\nBased on scanning your codebase, here are some good starter tasks:\n\n**1. [Most promising task]**\n   Location: `src/path/to/file.ts:42`\n   Scope: ~1-2 files, ~20-30 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**2. [Second task]**\n   Location: `src/another/file.ts`\n   Scope: ~1 file, ~15 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**3. [Third task]**\n   Location: [location]\n   Scope: [estimate]\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**4. Something else?**\n   Tell me what you''d like to work on.\n\nWhich task interests you? (Pick a number or describe your own)\n```\n\n**If nothing found:** Fall back to asking what the user wants to build:\n> I didn''t find obvious quick wins in your codebase. What''s something small you''ve been meaning to add or fix?\n\n### Scope Guardrail\n\nIf the user picks or describes something too large (major feature, multi-day work):\n\n```\nThat''s a valuable task, but it''s probably larger than ideal for your first OpenSpec run-through.\n\nFor learning the workflow, smaller is better—it lets you see the full cycle without getting stuck in implementation details.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Slice it smaller** - What''s the smallest useful piece of [their task]? Maybe just [specific slice]?\n2. **Pick something else** - One of the other suggestions, or a different small task?\n3. **Do it anyway** - If you really want to tackle this, we can. Just know it''ll take longer.\n\nWhat would you prefer?\n```\n\nLet the user override if they insist—this is a soft guardrail.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Explore Demo\n\nOnce a task is selected, briefly demonstrate explore mode:\n\n```\nBefore we create a change, let me quickly show you **explore mode**—it''s how you think through problems before committing to a direction.\n```\n\nSpend 1-2 minutes investigating the relevant code:\n- Read the file(s) involved\n- Draw a quick ASCII diagram if it helps\n- Note any considerations\n\n```\n## Quick Exploration\n\n[Your brief analysis—what you found, any considerations]\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│   [Optional: ASCII diagram if helpful]  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nExplore mode (`/opsx:explore`) is for this kind of thinking—investigating before implementing. You can use it anytime you need to think through a problem.\n\nNow let''s create a change to hold our work.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user acknowledgment before proceeding.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Create the Change\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Creating a Change\n\nA \"change\" in OpenSpec is a container for all the thinking and planning around a piece of work. It lives in `openspec/changes/<name>/` and holds your artifacts—proposal, specs, design, tasks.\n\nLet me create one for our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the change with a derived kebab-case name:\n```bash\nopenspec new change \"<derived-name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nCreated: `openspec/changes/<name>/`\n\nThe folder structure:\n```\nopenspec/changes/<name>/\n├── proposal.md    ← Why we''re doing this (empty, we''ll fill it)\n├── design.md      ← How we''ll build it (empty)\n├── specs/         ← Detailed requirements (empty)\n└── tasks.md       ← Implementation checklist (empty)\n```\n\nNow let''s fill in the first artifact—the proposal.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Proposal\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## The Proposal\n\nThe proposal captures **why** we''re making this change and **what** it involves at a high level. It''s the \"elevator pitch\" for the work.\n\nI''ll draft one based on our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft the proposal content (don''t save yet):\n\n```\nHere''s a draft proposal:\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n[1-2 sentences explaining the problem/opportunity]\n\n## What Changes\n\n[Bullet points of what will be different]\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n- `<capability-name>`: [brief description]\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n<!-- If modifying existing behavior -->\n\n## Impact\n\n- `src/path/to/file.ts`: [what changes]\n- [other files if applicable]\n\n---\n\nDoes this capture the intent? I can adjust before we save it.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user approval/feedback.\n\nAfter approval, save the proposal:\n```bash\nopenspec instructions proposal --change \"<name>\" --json\n```\nThen write the content to `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`.\n\n```\nProposal saved. This is your \"why\" document—you can always come back and refine it as understanding evolves.\n\nNext up: specs.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Specs\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Specs\n\nSpecs define **what** we''re building in precise, testable terms. They use a requirement/scenario format that makes expected behavior crystal clear.\n\nFor a small task like this, we might only need one spec file.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the spec file:\n```bash\nmkdir -p openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability-name>\n```\n\nDraft the spec content:\n\n```\nHere''s the spec:\n\n---\n\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: <Name>\n\n<Description of what the system should do>\n\n#### Scenario: <Scenario name>\n\n- **WHEN** <trigger condition>\n- **THEN** <expected outcome>\n- **AND** <additional outcome if needed>\n\n---\n\nThis format—WHEN/THEN/AND—makes requirements testable. You can literally read them as test cases.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability>/spec.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Design\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Design\n\nThe design captures **how** we''ll build it—technical decisions, tradeoffs, approach.\n\nFor small changes, this might be brief. That''s fine—not every change needs deep design discussion.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft design.md:\n\n```\nHere''s the design:\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\n[Brief context about the current state]\n\n## Goals / Non-Goals\n\n**Goals:**\n- [What we''re trying to achieve]\n\n**Non-Goals:**\n- [What''s explicitly out of scope]\n\n## Decisions\n\n### Decision 1: [Key decision]\n\n[Explanation of approach and rationale]\n\n---\n\nFor a small task, this captures the key decisions without over-engineering.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Tasks\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Tasks\n\nFinally, we break the work into implementation tasks—checkboxes that drive the apply phase.\n\nThese should be small, clear, and in logical order.\n```\n\n**DO:** Generate tasks based on specs and design:\n\n```\nHere are the implementation tasks:\n\n---\n\n## 1. [Category or file]\n\n- [ ] 1.1 [Specific task]\n- [ ] 1.2 [Specific task]\n\n## 2. Verify\n\n- [ ] 2.1 [Verification step]\n\n---\n\nEach checkbox becomes a unit of work in the apply phase. Ready to implement?\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user to confirm they''re ready to implement.\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 9: Apply (Implementation)\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Implementation\n\nNow we implement each task, checking them off as we go. I''ll announce each one and occasionally note how the specs/design informed the approach.\n```\n\n**DO:** For each task:\n\n1. Announce: \"Working on task N: [description]\"\n2. Implement the change in the codebase\n3. Reference specs/design naturally: \"The spec says X, so I''m doing Y\"\n4. Mark complete in tasks.md: `- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n5. Brief status: \"✓ Task N complete\"\n\nKeep narration light—don''t over-explain every line of code.\n\nAfter all tasks:\n\n```\n## Implementation Complete\n\nAll tasks done:\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n- [x] ...\n\nThe change is implemented! One more step—let''s archive it.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 10: Archive\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Archiving\n\nWhen a change is complete, we archive it. This moves it from `openspec/changes/` to `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`.\n\nArchived changes become your project''s decision history—you can always find them later to understand why something was built a certain way.\n```\n\n**DO:**\n```bash\nopenspec archive \"<name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nArchived to: `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`\n\nThe change is now part of your project''s history. The code is in your codebase, the decision record is preserved.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 11: Recap & Next Steps\n\n```\n## Congratulations!\n\nYou just completed a full OpenSpec cycle:\n\n1. **Explore** - Thought through the problem\n2. **New** - Created a change container\n3. **Proposal** - Captured WHY\n4. **Specs** - Defined WHAT in detail\n5. **Design** - Decided HOW\n6. **Tasks** - Broke it into steps\n7. **Apply** - Implemented the work\n8. **Archive** - Preserved the record\n\nThis same rhythm works for any size change—a small fix or a major feature.\n\n---\n\n## Command Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems before/during work |\n| `/opsx:new` | Start a new change, step through artifacts |\n| `/opsx:ff` | Fast-forward: create all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue` | Continue working on an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply` | Implement tasks from a change |\n| `/opsx:verify` | Verify implementation matches artifacts |\n| `/opsx:archive` | Archive a completed change |\n\n---\n\n## What''s Next?\n\nTry `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff` on something you actually want to build. You''ve got the rhythm now!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Graceful Exit Handling\n\n### User wants to stop mid-way\n\nIf the user says they need to stop, want to pause, or seem disengaged:\n\n```\nNo problem! Your change is saved at `openspec/changes/<name>/`.\n\nTo pick up where we left off later:\n- `/opsx:continue <name>` - Resume artifact creation\n- `/opsx:apply <name>` - Jump to implementation (if tasks exist)\n\nThe work won''t be lost. Come back whenever you''re ready.\n```\n\nExit gracefully without pressure.\n\n### User just wants command reference\n\nIf the user says they just want to see the commands or skip the tutorial:\n\n```\n## OpenSpec Quick Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems (no code changes) |\n| `/opsx:new <name>` | Start a new change, step by step |\n| `/opsx:ff <name>` | Fast-forward: all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue <name>` | Continue an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply <name>` | Implement tasks |\n| `/opsx:verify <name>` | Verify implementation |\n| `/opsx:archive <name>` | Archive when done |\n\nTry `/opsx:new` to start your first change, or `/opsx:ff` if you want to move fast.\n```\n\nExit gracefully.\n\n---\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- **Follow the EXPLAIN → DO → SHOW → PAUSE pattern** at key transitions (after explore, after proposal draft, after tasks, after archive)\n- **Keep narration light** during implementation—teach without lecturing\n- **Don''t skip phases** even if the change is small—the goal is teaching the workflow\n- **Pause for acknowledgment** at marked points, but don''t over-pause\n- **Handle exits gracefully**—never pressure the user to continue\n- **Use real codebase tasks**—don''t simulate or use fake examples\n- **Adjust scope gently**—guide toward smaller tasks but respect user choice\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:43:48.813Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing guided workflow cycles and codebase interaction, specifically those utilizing OpenSpec","zh":"非常适合需要指导的工作流程周期和代码库交互的开发代理，特别是那些使用OpenSpec的代理","ja":"OpenSpecを使用する開発エージェントがガイド付きのワークフロー周期とコードベースの相互作用を必要とする場合に最適","ko":"OpenSpec를 사용하는 개발 에이전트가 안내된 워크플로 사이클 및 코드베이스와의 상호 작용을 필요로 할 때 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan ciclos de flujo de trabajo guiados y la interacción con el código base, específicamente aquellos que utilizan OpenSpec","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin de cycles de workflow guidés et d''interaction avec la base de code, en particulier ceux qui utilisent OpenSpec","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die einen geleiteten Workflow-Zyklus und eine Interaktion mit dem Codebase benötigen, insbesondere solche, die OpenSpec verwenden","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de ciclos de fluxo de trabalho orientados e interação com o código-fonte, especificamente aqueles que utilizam OpenSpec","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым требуются управляемые циклы рабочих процессов и взаимодействие с кодовой базой, в частности те, которые используют OpenSpec","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى دورات عمل إرشادية وتفاعل مع قاعدة الشفرة، ولا سيما أولئك الذين يستخدمون OpenSpec"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to execute a complete OpenSpec workflow cycle, including initialization checks via `openspec status --json` and setup with `openspec init`, directly interacting with the user''s codebase and explaining each step of the process, leveraging JSON output for status checks","zh":"赋予代理执行完整的OpenSpec工作流程周期的能力，包括通过`openspec status --json`进行初始化检查和通过`openspec init`进行设置，直接与用户的代码库交互并解释该过程的每一步，利用JSON输出进行状态检查","ja":"`openspec status --json`による初期化チェックと`openspec init`によるセットアップを含む、OpenSpecの完全なワークフロー周期を実行するエージェントの能力を付与し、ユーザーのコードベースと直接やり取りし、プロセスの各ステップを説明し、JSON出力を使用してステータスチェックを実行する","ko":"에이전트가 완전한 OpenSpec 워크플로 사이클을 실행할 수 있는 능력을 부여함으로써, `openspec status --json`를 통한 초기화 확인 및 `openspec init`를 통한 설정을 포함하며, 사용자의 코드베이스와 직접 상호 작용하고, 과정의 각 단계를 설명하며, JSON 출력을 사용하여 상태 확인을 수행함","es":"Permite a los agentes ejecutar un ciclo de workflow de OpenSpec completo, incluyendo comprobaciones de inicialización a través de `openspec status --json` y configuración con `openspec init`, interactuando directamente con la base de código del usuario y explicando cada paso del proceso, aprovechando la salida JSON para comprobaciones de estado","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter un cycle de workflow OpenSpec complet, y compris les vérifications d''initialisation via `openspec status --json` et la configuration avec `openspec init`, en interactuant directement avec la base de code de l''utilisateur et en expliquant chaque étape du processus, en exploitant la sortie JSON pour les vérifications d''état","de":"Ermöglicht es den Mitteln, einen vollständigen OpenSpec-Workflow-Zyklus auszuführen, einschließlich Initialisierungsprüfungen über `openspec status --json` und Einrichtung mit `openspec init`, direkt mit dem Codebase des Benutzers interagierend und jeden Schritt des Prozesses erläuternd, wobei die JSON-Ausgabe für Statusprüfungen genutzt wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar um ciclo de trabalho completo do OpenSpec, incluindo verificações de inicialização via `openspec status --json` e configuração com `openspec init`, interagindo diretamente com a base de código do usuário e explicando cada etapa do processo, utilizando a saída JSON para verificações de status","ru":"Позволяет агентам выполнить полный цикл рабочего процесса OpenSpec, включая проверки инициализации через `openspec status --json` и настройку с помощью `openspec init`, напрямую взаимодействуя с кодовой базой пользователя и объясняя каждый шаг процесса, используя вывод JSON для проверок состояния","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تنفيذ دورة عمل كاملة من OpenSpec، بما في ذلك عمليات التحقق من الإعداد عبر `openspec status --json` وإعدادات مع `openspec init`، وتفاعل مباشر مع قاعدة الشفرة للمستخدم وشرح كل خطوة في العملية، واستخدام الإخراج JSON للتحقق من الحالة"},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing OpenSpec in new projects","Guiding users through their first OpenSpec workflow","Debugging OpenSpec setup issues with `openspec status` commands"],"zh":["在新项目中初始化OpenSpec","引导用户完成第一次OpenSpec工作流程","使用`openspec status`命令调试OpenSpec设置问题"],"ja":["新しいプロジェクトでOpenSpecを初期化する","ユーザーが最初のOpenSpecワークフローを完了するのを支援する","`openspec status`コマンドを使用してOpenSpecのセットアップの問題をデバッグする"],"ko":["새 프로젝트에서 OpenSpec 초기화","사용자가 첫 번째 OpenSpec 워크플로를 완료하도록 안내","`openspec status` 명령을 사용하여 OpenSpec 설정 문제 디버깅"],"es":["Inicializar OpenSpec en nuevos proyectos","Guía a los usuarios a través de su primer flujo de trabajo de OpenSpec","Depurar problemas de configuración de OpenSpec con comandos `openspec status`"],"fr":["Initialiser OpenSpec dans de nouveaux projets","Guider les utilisateurs à travers leur premier workflow OpenSpec","Déboguer les problèmes de configuration OpenSpec avec des commandes `openspec status`"],"de":["OpenSpec in neuen Projekten initialisieren","Benutzer durch ihren ersten OpenSpec-Workflow führen","OpenSpec-Setup-Probleme mit `openspec status`-Befehlen debuggen"],"pt":["Inicializar OpenSpec em novos projetos","Orientar os usuários por meio de seu primeiro fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec","Depurar problemas de configuração do OpenSpec com comandos `openspec status`"],"ru":["Инициализировать OpenSpec в новых проектах","Направлять пользователей через их первый рабочий процесс OpenSpec","Отладить проблемы настройки OpenSpec с помощью команд `openspec status`"],"ar":["ت 초기 OpenSpec في مشاريع جديدة","إرشاد المستخدمين خلال دورتهم الأولى من OpenSpec","تصحيح مشاكل إعداد OpenSpec باستخدام أوامر `openspec status`"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires OpenSpec to be installed and accessible via the command line","Must be run in a project directory where OpenSpec can be initialized or is already set up"],"zh":["需要OpenSpec已安装并可以通过命令行访问","必须在OpenSpec可以初始化或已设置的项目目录中运行"],"ja":["OpenSpecがインストールされ、コマンドラインからアクセス可能である必要がある","OpenSpecを初期化できる、または既に設定されているプロジェクトディレクトリで実行する必要がある"],"ko":["OpenSpec가 설치되고 명령줄에서 액세스 할 수 있어야 함","OpenSpec를 초기화하거나 이미 설정된 프로젝트 디렉토리에서 실행해야 함"],"es":["Requiere que OpenSpec esté instalado y sea accesible a través de la línea de comandos","Debe ejecutarse en un directorio de proyecto donde OpenSpec pueda ser inicializado o ya esté configurado"],"fr":["Nécessite que OpenSpec soit installé et accessible via la ligne de commande","Doit être exécuté dans un répertoire de projet où OpenSpec peut être initialisé ou est déjà configuré"],"de":["Benötigt, dass OpenSpec installiert ist und über die Befehlszeile zugänglich ist","Muss in einem Projektmittelverzeichnis ausgeführt werden, in dem OpenSpec initialisiert werden kann oder bereits eingerichtet ist"],"pt":["Requer que o OpenSpec esteja instalado e acessível via linha de comando","Deve ser executado em um diretório de projeto onde o OpenSpec possa ser inicializado ou já esteja configurado"],"ru":["Требует, чтобы OpenSpec был установлен и доступен через командную строку","Должен быть запущен в директории проекта, где OpenSpec может быть инициализирован или уже настроен"],"ar":["يتطلب أن يكون OpenSpec مثبتًا ويمكن الوصول إليه عبر سطر الأوامر","يجب تشغيله في دليل مشروع حيث يمكن 초기 OpenSpec أو تم إعدادها بالفعل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('MichaelvanLaar/n8n-nodes-defuddle/openspec-archive-change', 'community', 'MichaelvanLaar', 'n8n-nodes-defuddle', 'MichaelvanLaar/n8n-nodes-defuddle', 'openspec-archive-change', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.450Z', '2026-02-18T06:44:04.341Z', NULL, '{"id":"MichaelvanLaar/n8n-nodes-defuddle/openspec-archive-change","name":"openspec-archive-change","description":{"zh":"openspec-archive-change 是 n8n 社区节点，利用 Defuddle 库从网页中提取主要内容，用于实验工作流的存档","ja":"openspec-archive-change は n8n コミュニティノードで、Defuddle ライブラリを使用して Web ページから主要コンテンツを抽出します","ko":"openspec-archive-change는 n8n 커뮤니티 노드로 Defuddle 라이브러리를 사용하여 웹페이지에서 주요 콘텐츠를 추출","es":"El nodo de la comunidad n8n openspec-archive-change extrae el contenido principal de las páginas web y archiva los cambios en el flujo de trabajo experimental","fr":"Le nœud de la communauté n8n openspec-archive-change extrait le contenu principal des pages web et archive les modifications dans le flux de travail expérimental","de":"Der Community-Knoten n8n openspec-archive-change extrahiert den Hauptinhalt von Webseiten und archiviert Änderungen im experimentellen Workflow","pt":"O openspec-archive-change é um nó da comunidade n8n que usa a biblioteca Defuddle para extrair o conteúdo principal de páginas web.","ru":"Openspec-archive-change - это узел сообщества n8n, который использует библиотеку Defuddle для извлечения основного содержания веб-страниц.","ar":"openspec-archive-change هو عقدة المجتمع n8n التي تستخدم مكتبة Defuddle لاستخراج المحتوى الرئيسي من صفحات الويب.","en":"n8n community node for extracting main content from webpages using Defuddle library"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"openspec-archive-change 技术文档","ja":"openspec-archive-change 技術ドキュメント","ko":"openspec-archive-change 기술 문서","es":"Archivo de cambios con openspec-archive-change","fr":"Archivage de modifications avec openspec-archive-c