анных","разработка программного обеспечения","фреймворки разработки","предотвращение атак","защита данных","интеграция систем","техническая документация","техническая поддержка"],"ar":["تحقق من مدخلات الخلفية","أمان البيانات","تطوير البرمجيات","إطارات التطوير","منع الهجمات","حماية البيانات","تكامل النظم","توثيق فني","دعم فني"]}},"owner":"willyu1007","repo":"MyTrader","repoPath":"willyu1007/MyTrader","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.450Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"validate-backend-inputs","description":"Validate backend HTTP inputs (params, query, body) with schemas and return consistent 4xx errors for invalid requests.","bodyPreview":"# validate-backend-inputs (entry)\n\nCanonical source: `.ai/skills/backend/validation/validate-backend-inputs/`\n\nOpen `.ai/skills/backend/validation/validate-backend-inputs/SKILL.md` and any supporting files referenced there (for example `reference.md`, `examples.md`, `scripts/`, `templates/`).\n\n> **Note**: The frontmatter above is identical to the canonical source except for `ssot_path` and `category` which are added for navigation. After opening the source file, skip re-reading the description t","body":"# validate-backend-inputs (entry)\n\nCanonical source: `.ai/skills/backend/validation/validate-backend-inputs/`\n\nOpen `.ai/skills/backend/validation/validate-backend-inputs/SKILL.md` and any supporting files referenced there (for example `reference.md`, `examples.md`, `scripts/`, `templates/`).\n\n> **Note**: The frontmatter above is identical to the canonical source except for `ssot_path` and `category` which are added for navigation. After opening the source file, skip re-reading the description to avoid redundant token usage.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:47:19.447Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Business Logic Agents needing robust backend input validation for daily trades.","zh":"非常适合需要强大的后端输入验证的业务逻辑代理，每天进行交易。","ja":"ビジネスロジックエージェントが毎日の取引にロバストなバックエンド入力検証を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"일일 거래를 위한 강력한 백엔드 입력 유효성을 필요로 하는 비즈니스 로직 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Lógica de Negocio que necesitan una validación de entrada de backend robusta para operaciones diarias.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de logique métier nécessitant une validation robuste des entrées de backend pour les échanges quotidiens.","de":"Perfekt für Business-Logik-Agents, die eine robuste Backend-Eingabevalidierung für tägliche Trades benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Lógica de Negócios que necessitam de validação robusta de entrada de backend para negociações diárias.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов бизнес-логики, которым требуется надежная проверка входных данных бэкэнда для ежедневных сделок.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات comercial المنطقية التي تحتاج إلى تحقق قوي من الإدخال الخلفي للمعاملات اليومية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to validate and sanitize backend inputs using canonical sources, ensuring secure and personalized trades through protocols like JSON and data formats such as CSV, while providing reference materials and script templates for customized validation.","zh":"赋予代理验证和清理后端输入的能力，使用规范源，确保通过JSON和CSV等协议以及数据格式等来进行安全和个性化的交易，同时提供参考材料和脚本模板用于自定义验证。","ja":"エージェントがバックエンド入力を検証およびサニタイズすることができるようにし、規範的な情報源を使用してJSONやCSVなどのプロトコルおよびデータ形式を介した安全でパーソナライズされた取引を保証し、カスタム検証のためのリファレンス資料やスクリプトテンプレートを提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 백엔드 입력을 검증 및 정제할 수 있도록 하며, 표준 소스를 사용하여 JSON 및 CSV와 같은 프로토콜 및 데이터 형식을 통해 보안 및 개인화된 거래를 보장하며, 사용자 지정 유효성을 위한 참고 자료 및 스크립트 템플릿을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a validar y sanear las entradas de backend utilizando fuentes canónicas, asegurando operaciones seguras y personalizadas a través de protocolos como JSON y formatos de datos como CSV, mientras proporciona materiales de referencia y plantillas de scripts para validaciones personalizadas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de valider et de nettoyer les entrées de backend en utilisant des sources canoniques, assurant des échanges sécurisés et personnalisés via des protocoles tels que JSON et des formats de données tels que CSV, tout en fournissant des documents de référence et des modèles de scripts pour des validations personnalisées.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Backend-Eingaben mithilfe kanonischer Quellen zu validieren und zu säubern, um sichere und personalisierte Trades durch Protokolle wie JSON und Datenformate wie CSV sicherzustellen, während es Referenzmaterialien und Skriptvorlagen für angepasste Validierungen bereitstellt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a validar e sanitizar entradas de backend usando fontes canônicas, garantindo negociações seguras e personalizadas por meio de protocolos como JSON e formatos de dados como CSV, além de fornecer materiais de referência e modelos de script para validação personalizada.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проверять и очищать входные данные бэкэнда с использованием канонических источников, обеспечивая безопасные и персонализированные сделки посредством протоколов, таких как JSON, и форматов данных, таких как CSV, а также предоставляет справочные материалы и шаблоны скриптов для настраиваемой проверки.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من التحقق من صحة المدخلات الخلفية وتنظيفها باستخدام المصادر القانونية، مما يضمن معاملات آمنة وersonalized من خلال بروتوكولات مثل JSON وتنسيقات البيانات مثل CSV، بالإضافة إلى توفير مواد مرجعية وقوالب نصية مخصصة للتحقق."},"useCases":{"en":["Validating user inputs for trade customization","Sanitizing backend data for secure transactions","Generating validation scripts for daily trade workflows"],"zh":["验证用户输入以自定义交易","清理后端数据以进行安全交易","为每日交易工作流生成验证脚本"],"ja":["取引のカスタマイズのためのユーザー入力を検証する","セキュアな取引のためのバックエンドデータをサニタイズする","毎日の取引ワークフロー用の検証スクリプトを生成する"],"ko":["거래 사용자 지정 위한 사용자 입력 유효성 검사","보안 거래를 위한 백엔드 데이터 정제","일일 거래 워크플로우를 위한 유효성 검사 스크립트 생성"],"es":["Validar entradas de usuario para la personalización de operaciones","Sanear datos de backend para transacciones seguras","Generar scripts de validación para flujos de trabajo de operaciones diarias"],"fr":["Valider les entrées utilisateur pour la personnalisation des échanges","Nettoyer les données de backend pour des transactions sécurisées","Générer des scripts de validation pour les flux de travail d''échanges quotidiens"],"de":["Validierung von Benutzereingaben für die Anpassung von Trades","Säubern von Backend-Daten für sichere Transaktionen","Generieren von Validierungsskripten für tägliche Handelsworkflows"],"pt":["Validar entradas de usuário para personalização de negociações","Sanitizar dados de backend para transações seguras","Gerar scripts de validação para fluxos de trabalho de negociações diárias"],"ru":["Проверка пользовательского ввода для настройки сделок","Очистка данных бэкэнда для безопасных транзакций","Генерация скриптов проверки для рабочих процессов ежедневных сделок"],"ar":["التحقق من المدخلات المستخدمة لتحديد معاملات","تنقية بيانات الخلفية للمعاملات الآمنة","إنتاج نصوص التحقق من صحة سير عمل المعاملات اليومية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to canonical source files","Limited to validation of backend inputs only"],"zh":["需要访问规范源文件","仅限于后端输入的验证"],"ja":["規範的な情報源ファイルへのアクセスが必要","バックエンド入力の検証のみに限定される"],"ko":["표준 소스 파일에 대한 액세스가 필요","백엔드 입력의 유효성 검사만으로 제한"],"es":["Requiere acceso a archivos de fuentes canónicas","Limitado a la validación de entradas de backend solo"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès à des fichiers de sources canoniques","Limité à la validation des entrées de backend uniquement"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf kanonische Quelldateien","Begrenzt auf die Validierung von Backend-Eingaben nur"],"pt":["Requer acesso a arquivos de fonte canônicos","Limitado à validação de entradas de backend apenas"],"ru":["Требует доступа к каноническим файлам-источникам","Ограничен только проверкой входных данных бэкэнда"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الملفات القانونية للمصدر","محدود بالتحقق من المدخلات الخلفية فقط"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('marcusgoll/Spec-Flow/anti-duplication', 'community', 'marcusgoll', 'Spec-Flow', 'marcusgoll/Spec-Flow', 'anti-duplication', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.451Z', '2026-02-18T06:47:30.629Z', NULL, '{"id":"marcusgoll/Spec-Flow/anti-duplication","name":"anti-duplication","description":{"zh":"anti-duplication 技术通过强制 DRY 原则，防止代码重复，减少维护负担","ja":"反復コード防止技術は、DRY 原則を強制し、コードの重複を防ぎます","ko":"중복방지 기술은 DRY 원칙을 강제하여 코드 중복을 방지","es":"La habilidad anti-duplication aplica el principio DRY para prevenir la duplicación de código","fr":"La compétence anti-duplication applique le principe DRY pour prévenir la duplication de code","de":"Die Anti-Duplizierung-Fähigkeit wendet das DRY-Prinzip an, um Code-Duplizierung zu vermeiden","pt":"A habilidade anti-duplication ajuda a evitar a duplicação de código, reduzindo a manutenção e melhorando a reutilização do código","ru":"Навык анти-дублирования помогает избегать дублирования кода, уменьшая поддержку и улучшая повторное использование кода","ar":"تساعد مهارة مكافحة التكرار على تجنب تكرار الكود، وتقلل من الصيانة وتحسن إعادة استخدام الكود","en":"Turn product ideas into production launches with Spec-Driven Development. Repeatable Claude Code workflows with quality gates, token budgets, and auditable artifacts."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"anti-duplication 技术","ja":"反復コード防止","ko":"중복방지 기술","es":"Anti-duplicación de código","fr":"Anti-duplication de code","de":"Anti-Duplizierung von Code","pt":"Anti-Duplication: Evite Código Duplicado","ru":"Анти-Дублирование: Избегайте Дублирования Код","ar":"مكافحة التكرار: قلل من重複 الكود","en":"anti-duplication"},"description":{"zh":"anti-duplication 技术通过强制 DRY 原则，防止代码重复，减少维护负担","ja":"反復コード防止技術は、DRY 原則を強制し、コードの重複を防ぎます","ko":"중복방지 기술은 DRY 원칙을 강제하여 코드 중복을 방지","es":"La habilidad anti-duplication aplica el principio DRY para prevenir la duplicación de código","fr":"La compétence anti-duplication applique le principe DRY pour prévenir la duplication de code","de":"Die Anti-Duplizierung-Fähigkeit wendet das DRY-Prinzip an, um Code-Duplizierung zu vermeiden","pt":"A habilidade anti-duplication ajuda a evitar a duplicação de código, reduzindo a manutenção e melhorando a reutilização do código","ru":"Навык анти-дублирования помогает избегать дублирования кода, уменьшая поддержку и улучшая повторное использование кода","ar":"تساعد مهارة مكافحة التكرار على تجنب تكرار الكود، وتقلل من الصيانة وتحسن إعادة استخدام الكود","en":"Turn product ideas into production launches with Spec-Driven Development. Repeatable Claude Code workflows with quality gates, token budgets, and auditable a..."},"definition":{"en":"Turn product ideas into production launches with Spec-Driven Development. Repeatable Claude Code workflows with quality gates, token budgets, and auditable artifacts."},"features":{"zh":["强制 DRY 原则","防止代码重复","减少维护负担","提高代码复用率","简化代码维护","提高开发效率"],"ja":["DRY 原則を強制","コードの重複を防止","メンテナンスの負担を軽減","コードの再利用率を向上","コードメンテナンスを簡素化","開発効率を向上"],"ko":["DRY 원칙 강제","코드 중복 방지","유지 보수 비용 감소","코드 재사용률 향상","코드 유지 보수簡素化","개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["Aplica el principio DRY","Evita la duplicación de código","Reduce la carga de mantenimiento","Promueve la reutilización de código","Mejora la consistencia del código"],"fr":["Applique le principe DRY","Évitez la duplication de code","Réduisez la charge de maintenance","Promouvez la réutilisation de code","Améliorez la cohérence du code"],"de":["Wendet das DRY-Prinzip an","Vermeidet Code-Duplizierung","Reduziert die Wartungsbelastung","Fördert die Wiederverwendung von Code","Verbessert die Konsistenz des Codes"],"pt":["Evita a duplicação de código","Reduz a manutenção","Melhora a reutilização do código","Aplica o princípio DRY","Reduz o tamanho do código","Facilita a refatoração"],"ru":["Избегает дублирование кода","Уменьшает поддержку","Улучшает повторное использование кода","Применяет принцип DRY","Уменьшает размер кода","Облегчает рефакторинг"],"ar":["تمنع تكرار الكود","تقلل من الصيانة","تحسن إعادة استخدام الكود","تطبيق مبدأ DRY","تقلل من حجم الكود","تسهل إعادة الهيكلة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["anti-duplication","DRY 原则","代码复用","维护负担","开发效率","代码重复","中间件开发","软件开发","编码规范"],"ja":["反復コード防止","DRY 原則","コードの再利用","メンテナンスの負担","開発効率","コードの重複","ミドルウェア開発","ソフトウェア開発","コーディング規約"],"ko":["중복방지","DRY 원칙","코드 재사용","유지 보수 비용","개발 효율성","코드 중복","미들웨어 개발","소프트웨어 개발","코딩 규약"],"es":["anti-duplicación","principio DRY","duplicación de código","mantenimiento de código","reutilización de código","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["anti-duplication","principe DRY","duplication de code","maintenance de code","réutilisation de code","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Anti-Duplizierung","DRY-Prinzip","Code-Duplizierung","Code-Wartung","Code-Wiederverwendung","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["anti-duplication","DRY","duplicação de código","manutenção de código","reutilização de código","desenvolvimento de software","princípios de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["анти-дублирование","DRY","дублирование кода","поддержка кода","повторное использование кода","разработка программного обеспечения","принципы разработки"],"ar":["مكافحة التكرار","DRY","تكرار الكود","صيانة الكود","إعادة استخدام الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","مبادئ التطوير"]}},"owner":"marcusgoll","repo":"Spec-Flow","repoPath":"marcusgoll/Spec-Flow","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.451Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"anti-duplication","description":"Before implementing new code (endpoints, components, services, models), search the codebase for existing patterns to reuse. Prevent code duplication by finding and suggesting similar implementations. Auto-trigger when user asks to create, implement, add, or build new functionality.","bodyPreview":"<objective>\nThe anti-duplication skill enforces the DRY (Don''t Repeat Yourself) principle by proactively searching the codebase for existing patterns before writing new code. This prevents code duplication, reduces maintenance burden, and promotes code reuse.\n\nCode duplication creates maintenance nightmares:\n- Bug fixes must be applied in multiple places\n- Features evolve inconsistently across duplicates\n- Refactoring becomes exponentially harder\n- Codebase grows unnecessarily large\n- Onboarding","body":"<objective>\nThe anti-duplication skill enforces the DRY (Don''t Repeat Yourself) principle by proactively searching the codebase for existing patterns before writing new code. This prevents code duplication, reduces maintenance burden, and promotes code reuse.\n\nCode duplication creates maintenance nightmares:\n- Bug fixes must be applied in multiple places\n- Features evolve inconsistently across duplicates\n- Refactoring becomes exponentially harder\n- Codebase grows unnecessarily large\n- Onboarding takes longer (more code to learn)\n\nThis skill transforms \"implement X\" requests into a two-phase workflow:\n1. **Search phase**: Find existing similar implementations (endpoints, components, services, models)\n2. **Reuse or justify**: Either reuse/extend existing code OR justify why new implementation is necessary\n\nThe result: Codebases stay DRY, maintainable, and consistent.\n</objective>\n\n<quick_start>\n<trigger_pattern>\nWhen user says \"create\", \"implement\", \"add\", or \"build\" new functionality, **IMMEDIATELY** search for existing similar code before writing anything new.\n\n**Trigger phrases**:\n- \"Create a new API endpoint for...\"\n- \"Implement a component that...\"\n- \"Add a service to handle...\"\n- \"Build a model for...\"\n- \"Write a function that...\"\n</trigger_pattern>\n\n<basic_workflow>\n**Step 1**: Extract search keywords from request\n- User: \"Create an API endpoint to fetch user profile\"\n- Keywords: \"API endpoint\", \"fetch\", \"user\", \"profile\", \"GET\"\n\n**Step 2**: Search codebase for similar patterns\n- Grep for: \"router.get\", \"app.get\", \"/api/user\", \"profile\"\n- Glob for: \"**/*user*.ts\", \"**/*profile*.ts\", \"**/routes/**\"\n\n**Step 3**: Analyze findings\n- Found 3 similar endpoints: GET /api/user/:id, GET /api/user/settings, GET /api/admin/users\n- All use same auth middleware, validation pattern, error handling\n\n**Step 4**: Present reuse options\n- **Option A**: Extend existing GET /api/user/:id to include profile data\n- **Option B**: Create new endpoint using same patterns as existing user endpoints\n- **Option C**: Justify why completely new approach is needed\n\n**Step 5**: Implement chosen option (with existing patterns as template)\n</basic_workflow>\n\n<immediate_value>\n**Before anti-duplication skill**:\nUser: \"Create an API endpoint to update user email\"\nClaude: *Writes new endpoint from scratch with different auth, validation, error handling*\nResult: 5th variation of similar endpoint, inconsistent patterns\n\n**After anti-duplication skill**:\nUser: \"Create an API endpoint to update user email\"\nClaude: *Searches codebase, finds 4 existing user endpoints with consistent patterns*\nClaude: \"Found 4 similar user endpoints. They all use: authMiddleware, validateUserInput, standardErrorHandler. I''ll create the new endpoint following this established pattern.\"\nResult: Consistent implementation, reused middleware, maintainable code\n</immediate_value>\n</quick_start>\n\n<workflow>\n<step number=\"1\">\n**Parse the implementation request**\n\nExtract key information:\n- **Type**: What are they building? (endpoint, component, service, model, function, utility)\n- **Domain**: What business domain? (user, product, order, payment, auth)\n- **Operation**: What action? (create, read, update, delete, fetch, validate, transform)\n- **Technology**: What stack? (React, Express, TypeScript, SQL, GraphQL)\n\nExample parsing:\n```\nRequest: \"Create a React component to display product details\"\n\nParsed:\n- Type: React component\n- Domain: Product\n- Operation: Display/render\n- Technology: React, TypeScript (likely)\n```\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"2\">\n**Generate search strategies**\n\nCreate multiple search approaches to maximize coverage:\n\n**A. Keyword-based searches** (Grep):\n- Core domain terms: \"product\", \"Product\", \"PRODUCT\"\n- Operation terms: \"display\", \"render\", \"show\", \"view\"\n- Technology patterns: \"React.FC\", \"function Component\", \"const.*=.*=>\"\n\n**B. File pattern searches** (Glob):\n- Domain files: \"**/*product*.tsx\", \"**/*Product*.tsx\"\n- Location patterns: \"**/components/**/*Detail*.tsx\", \"**/components/**/Product*\"\n- Type-specific: \"**/models/Product*\", \"**/services/product*\"\n\n**C. Structural searches** (Grep with regex):\n- Class definitions: \"class.*Product\"\n- Function exports: \"export (function|const).*product\"\n- API patterns: \"router\\.(get|post|put|delete).*product\"\n\nSee [references/search-strategies.md](references/search-strategies.md) for detailed patterns.\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"3\">\n**Execute searches in parallel**\n\nRun multiple searches concurrently for speed:\n\n**Search batch**:\n1. Grep: \"product\" in **/*.tsx (find all product-related components)\n2. Grep: \"ProductDetail\" (find similar detail components)\n3. Glob: \"**/components/**/Product*.tsx\" (find product component files)\n4. Grep: \"interface.*Product\" (find product type definitions)\n5. Grep: \"display.*product.*props\" (find rendering logic)\n\nAll 5 searches run in parallel (see parallel-execution-optimizer skill).\n\n**Time**: ~5-10 seconds for comprehensive search across large codebase.\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"4\">\n**Analyze search results**\n\nCategorize findings:\n\n**Exact matches**: Nearly identical implementations\n- Example: Found ProductDetailCard, ProductSummaryCard, ProductPreviewCard\n- All render product data with similar structure\n\n**Close matches**: Similar domain, different operation\n- Example: Found ProductList (renders multiple products)\n- Could extract shared rendering logic\n\n**Pattern matches**: Similar operation, different domain\n- Example: Found UserDetailCard, OrderDetailCard\n- Consistent pattern: DetailCard component for entities\n\n**Anti-patterns**: What NOT to do\n- Example: Found ProductView with 500-line monolithic component\n- Shows what to avoid when implementing new component\n\nRank by relevance:\n1. Exact matches (highest reuse potential)\n2. Close matches (partial reuse)\n3. Pattern matches (pattern consistency)\n4. Anti-patterns (learn from mistakes)\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"5\">\n**Present reuse options**\n\nProvide user with informed choices:\n\n**Option A: Reuse existing implementation**\n\"Found ProductDetailCard component that already displays product details. Can we use this directly or does your use case differ?\"\n\n**Option B: Extend existing implementation**\n\"Found ProductSummaryCard (displays basic product info). We can extend it to show full details rather than creating a new component.\"\n\n**Option C: Extract shared pattern**\n\"Found 3 similar DetailCard components (Product, User, Order). We can create a generic DetailCard<T> and use it for products.\"\n\n**Option D: Follow established pattern**\n\"Found consistent pattern across User/Order detail components. I''ll create ProductDetailCard following the same structure for consistency.\"\n\n**Option E: Justify new approach**\n\"Existing ProductView is a 500-line monolith with poor separation of concerns. I''ll create a new modular ProductDetailCard instead. Here''s why the new approach is necessary: [justification]\"\n\nAlways present Options A-D before suggesting new implementation.\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"6\">\n**Implement with reuse**\n\nBased on chosen option:\n\n**If reusing**: Import and use existing code\n```typescript\nimport { ProductDetailCard } from ''@/components/products/ProductDetailCard'';\n\n// Use directly\n<ProductDetailCard product={product} />\n```\n\n**If extending**: Modify existing component\n```typescript\n// Extend ProductSummaryCard with additional fields\n// Before: Shows name, price\n// After: Shows name, price, description, images\n```\n\n**If extracting pattern**: Create generic abstraction\n```typescript\n// Create DetailCard<T> generic component\n// Reuse for Product, User, Order\n```\n\n**If following pattern**: Use existing as template\n```typescript\n// Copy structure from UserDetailCard\n// Adapt for Product domain\n// Maintain consistency (same props pattern, same styling, same error handling)\n```\n\n**If new approach**: Document justification\n```typescript\n/**\n * ProductDetailCard\n *\n * NEW IMPLEMENTATION (does not reuse ProductView)\n *\n * Justification:\n * - Existing ProductView is 500-line monolith\n * - Poor separation of concerns (mixing data fetching, rendering, business logic)\n * - Hard to test and maintain\n *\n * This implementation:\n * - Separates concerns (presentational component only)\n * - Reusable across product catalog and cart\n * - Follows established DetailCard pattern from User/Order\n */\n```\n</step>\n</workflow>\n\n<search_strategies>\n<by_artifact_type>\nDifferent artifact types require different search strategies.\n\n**API Endpoints** (Express, Fastify, NestJS):\n```\nKeywords: router.get, router.post, app.get, @Get, @Post, /api/\nPatterns: HTTP methods + route paths + domain terms\nFiles: **/routes/**, **/controllers/**, **/api/**\n\nExample search for \"user profile endpoint\":\n- Grep: \"router\\.(get|put).*profile\" in **/*routes*.ts\n- Grep: \"/api/user\" in **/*.ts\n- Glob: \"**/routes/**/user*.ts\"\n- Grep: \"getUserProfile|updateUserProfile\" (common naming)\n```\n\n**React Components** (functional, class):\n```\nKeywords: React.FC, function Component, class.*extends React\nPatterns: export function ComponentName, const ComponentName =\nFiles: **/components/**, **/*.tsx, **/*.jsx\n\nExample search for \"product card component\":\n- Grep: \"function.*Product.*Card\" in **/*.tsx\n- Grep: \"ProductCard.*=.*=>\" in **/*.tsx\n- Glob: \"**/components/**/Product*.tsx\"\n- Grep: \"export.*ProductCard\" in **/*.tsx\n```\n\n**Services/Business Logic**:\n```\nKeywords: class.*Service, export.*service, provide, inject\nPatterns: Service naming convention, dependency injection\nFiles: **/services/**, **/lib/**, **/utils/**\n\nExample search for \"email service\":\n- Grep: \"class.*Email.*Service\" in **/*.ts\n- Grep: \"sendEmail|emailService\" in **/*.ts\n- Glob: \"**/services/**/*email*.ts\"\n- Grep: \"nodemailer|sendgrid|aws-ses\" (common email libs)\n```\n\n**Database Models** (Prisma, TypeORM, Sequelize):\n```\nKeywords: model, schema, entity, @Entity, interface.*Model\nPatterns: Database column definitions, relationships\nFiles: **/models/**, **/entities/**, **/schema/**\n\nExample search for \"user model\":\n- Grep: \"model User\" in **/*.prisma\n- Grep: \"@Entity.*User|class User.*extends\" in **/*.ts\n- Glob: \"**/models/**/user*.ts\"\n- Grep: \"interface User.*{\" in **/*.ts\n```\n\nSee [references/search-strategies.md](references/search-strategies.md) for comprehensive patterns.\n</by_artifact_type>\n\n<domain_specific_searches>\nSearch within business domains to find related code:\n\n**E-commerce domains**:\n- User: authentication, profile, preferences\n- Product: catalog, details, inventory\n- Order: cart, checkout, payment\n- Shipping: address, tracking, fulfillment\n\n**Search strategy**: Start with domain term, expand to related terms\n```\nDomain: Product\nPrimary: \"product\", \"Product\", \"PRODUCT\"\nRelated: \"item\", \"catalog\", \"inventory\", \"SKU\"\nOperations: \"addProduct\", \"getProduct\", \"updateProduct\", \"deleteProduct\"\n```\n\n**Cross-domain patterns**:\nLook for similar operations across different domains:\n```\nOperation: \"Detail view\"\nSearch: \"*DetailCard\", \"*DetailView\", \"*Detail.tsx\"\nFinds: UserDetailCard, ProductDetailCard, OrderDetailCard\nPattern: Consistent structure for entity detail components\n```\n</domain_specific_searches>\n\n<technology_specific_searches>\nTailor searches to technology stack:\n\n**TypeScript**:\n```\n- \"interface Product\" (type definitions)\n- \"type Product = \" (type aliases)\n- \"Product extends \" (inheritance)\n- \"as Product\" (type assertions)\n```\n\n**GraphQL**:\n```\n- \"type Product\" (schema definitions)\n- \"Query.product\" (query resolvers)\n- \"Mutation.createProduct\" (mutation resolvers)\n- \"gql\\`.*product\" (query strings)\n```\n\n**SQL/Prisma**:\n```\n- \"model Product\" (Prisma schema)\n- \"CREATE TABLE product\" (SQL migrations)\n- \"SELECT.*FROM product\" (raw queries)\n- \"prisma.product.findMany\" (Prisma client)\n```\n\n**React Query/SWR**:\n```\n- \"useQuery.*product\" (data fetching hooks)\n- \"useMutation.*product\" (mutation hooks)\n- \"queryKey:.*product\" (cache keys)\n```\n</technology_specific_searches>\n</search_strategies>\n\n<auto_trigger_conditions>\n<when_to_trigger>\nAutomatically apply anti-duplication search when detecting these phrases:\n\n**Explicit creation intent**:\n- \"Create a new [artifact]\"\n- \"Implement a [artifact]\"\n- \"Add a [artifact]\"\n- \"Build a [artifact]\"\n- \"Write a [artifact]\"\n- \"Generate a [artifact]\"\n\n**Examples**:\n- \"Create a new API endpoint to fetch orders\"\n- \"Implement a login component\"\n- \"Add a service to handle payments\"\n- \"Build a User model with email and password\"\n- \"Write a function to validate user input\"\n\n**Implicit creation** (inferred from context):\n- \"I need to [do something]\" → May require new code\n- \"How do I [accomplish task]\" → May require new implementation\n- \"Can you [build feature]\" → Definitely requires code\n\n**During /implement phase**:\n- Every task that involves writing new code\n- Before writing first line of implementation\n- Even for \"simple\" tasks (search takes <10 seconds)\n</when_to_trigger>\n\n<when_not_to_trigger>\nSkip anti-duplication search when:\n\n**User explicitly requests new approach**:\n- \"Create a new implementation (don''t reuse existing)\"\n- \"I know there''s X, but I want a different approach\"\n- \"Ignore existing code and start fresh\"\n\n**Modifying existing code**:\n- \"Update the UserController to add validation\"\n- \"Fix the bug in ProductCard component\"\n- \"Refactor the OrderService to use async/await\"\n\n**Non-code tasks**:\n- \"Explain how authentication works\"\n- \"Review the ProductCard component\"\n- \"Run the test suite\"\n\n**Configuration/data files**:\n- \"Add a new npm package\"\n- \"Update the .env file\"\n- \"Create a migration file\" (different from creating models)\n</when_not_to_trigger>\n\n<proactive_trigger_logic>\nWhen user says \"Create an API endpoint to update user email\":\n\n1. **Immediately pause** before writing any code\n2. **Announce search**: \"Before implementing, let me search for existing user endpoints to ensure consistency...\"\n3. **Run searches** (5-10 seconds)\n4. **Present findings**: \"Found 4 existing user endpoints following a consistent pattern. I''ll use the same structure.\"\n5. **Implement** using discovered pattern\n\nThis becomes automatic—user doesn''t need to ask for the search, it happens proactively.\n</proactive_trigger_logic>\n</auto_trigger_conditions>\n\n<reuse_decision_framework>\n<decision_tree>\nAfter search completes, use this decision tree:\n\n**Q1: Found exact match?**\n- YES → Reuse directly (Option A)\n- NO → Go to Q2\n\n**Q2: Found close match (same domain, similar operation)?**\n- YES → Can we extend it? (Option B)\n  - If yes → Extend existing\n  - If no → Go to Q3\n- NO → Go to Q3\n\n**Q3: Found pattern match (similar structure, different domain)?**\n- YES → Extract generic abstraction? (Option C)\n  - If yes → Create generic version\n  - If abstraction too complex → Follow pattern (Option D)\n- NO → Go to Q4\n\n**Q4: Existing implementations are anti-patterns?**\n- YES → Justify new approach (Option E) + document why existing code should be refactored\n- NO → Follow established patterns if any, otherwise implement new\n\n**Final check**: Before implementing new code, answer:\n- \"Why can''t we reuse existing code?\"\n- \"What makes this implementation different?\"\n- \"Will this create duplication?\"\n</decision_tree>\n\n<reuse_threshold>\n**High reuse potential** (≥80% similar):\n→ Reuse directly or extend\n\n**Medium reuse potential** (50-79% similar):\n→ Extract shared logic into utility/helper\n→ Adapt existing pattern\n\n**Low reuse potential** (30-49% similar):\n→ Follow established patterns for consistency\n→ Document differences\n\n**No reuse potential** (<30% similar):\n→ Implement new, but document why it''s different\n→ Consider if this signals missing abstraction\n</reuse_threshold>\n</reuse_decision_framework>\n\n<examples>\n<example name=\"api-endpoint-duplication-prevented\">\n**Request**: \"Create an API endpoint to update user email\"\n\n**Search phase**:\n```\nSearches:\n1. Grep \"router\\.(put|patch).*user\" → Found 3 endpoints\n2. Grep \"/api/user.*email\" → Found 1 endpoint (GET /api/user/email)\n3. Glob \"**/routes/**/user*.ts\" → Found routes/user.ts\n\nResults:\n- PATCH /api/user/profile (updates name, bio)\n- PATCH /api/user/password (updates password)\n- PUT /api/user/settings (updates preferences)\n```\n\n**Analysis**:\nAll 3 endpoints follow same pattern:\n```typescript\nrouter.patch(''/api/user/:field'',\n  authMiddleware,           // JWT authentication\n  validateUserInput,        // Schema validation\n  userController.update,    // Controller method\n  standardErrorHandler      // Error handling\n);\n```\n\n**Recommendation**:\n\"Found 3 existing user update endpoints. They all use:\n- authMiddleware (JWT auth)\n- validateUserInput (Joi schema validation)\n- userController.update (centralized controller)\n- standardErrorHandler (consistent errors)\n\n**Option A**: Extend userController.update to handle email updates\n**Option B**: Create new endpoint following the same pattern\n\nI recommend **Option A** (extend existing controller) to avoid endpoint proliferation. The controller already handles profile/password/settings updates, email fits the same pattern.\"\n\n**Implementation** (Option A):\n```typescript\n// userController.ts (extend existing)\nasync update(req, res) {\n  const { field } = req.params;\n  const allowedFields = [''profile'', ''password'', ''settings'', ''email'']; // ADD email\n\n  if (!allowedFields.includes(field)) {\n    return res.status(400).json({ error: ''Invalid field'' });\n  }\n\n  // Add email-specific validation\n  if (field === ''email'') {\n    await this.validateEmail(req.body.email);\n  }\n\n  // Existing update logic\n  await this.userService.update(req.user.id, field, req.body);\n  res.json({ success: true });\n}\n```\n\n**Duplication prevented**: No new endpoint created, reused existing pattern, consistent auth/validation.\n\nSee [examples/api-endpoint-reuse.md](examples/api-endpoint-reuse.md) for full example.\n</example>\n\n<example name=\"component-pattern-extraction\">\n**Request**: \"Create a React component to display product details\"\n\n**Search phase**:\n```\nSearches:\n1. Grep \"ProductDetail|ProductCard\" in **/*.tsx → Found 2 components\n2. Glob \"**/components/**/Product*.tsx\" → Found 5 product components\n3. Grep \"function.*Detail.*Card\" in **/*.tsx → Found 8 DetailCard components\n\nResults:\n- UserDetailCard: Displays user info in card layout\n- OrderDetailCard: Displays order info in card layout\n- ProductSummaryCard: Displays product summary (not full details)\n- ProductListItem: Displays product in list (minimal info)\n```\n\n**Analysis**:\nFound **pattern**: All \"DetailCard\" components share structure:\n```typescript\ninterface DetailCardProps<T> {\n  data: T;\n  loading?: boolean;\n  onEdit?: () => void;\n  onDelete?: () => void;\n}\n\nfunction DetailCard<T>({ data, loading, onEdit, onDelete }) {\n  if (loading) return <Skeleton />;\n\n  return (\n    <Card>\n      <CardHeader>\n        {/* Title */}\n      </CardHeader>\n      <CardBody>\n        {/* Fields */}\n      </CardBody>\n      <CardActions>\n        {onEdit && <Button onClick={onEdit}>Edit</Button>}\n        {onDelete && <Button onClick={onDelete}>Delete</Button>}\n      </CardActions>\n    </Card>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Recommendation**:\n\"Found consistent DetailCard pattern used for User and Order entities. Rather than creating ProductDetailCard from scratch, I''ll extract the pattern into a generic DetailCard<T> component.\"\n\n**Implementation** (Option C - Extract pattern):\n```typescript\n// components/common/DetailCard.tsx (NEW generic component)\ninterface DetailCardProps<T> {\n  data: T;\n  fields: Array<{ label: string; key: keyof T; render?: (value: any) => ReactNode }>;\n  loading?: boolean;\n  onEdit?: () => void;\n  onDelete?: () => void;\n}\n\nexport function DetailCard<T>({ data, fields, loading, onEdit, onDelete }: DetailCardProps<T>) {\n  if (loading) return <Skeleton />;\n\n  return (\n    <Card>\n      <CardBody>\n        {fields.map(field => (\n          <div key={String(field.key)}>\n            <label>{field.label}</label>\n            <div>{field.render ? field.render(data[field.key]) : data[field.key]}</div>\n          </div>\n        ))}\n      </CardBody>\n      <CardActions>\n        {onEdit && <Button onClick={onEdit}>Edit</Button>}\n        {onDelete && <Button onClick={onDelete}>Delete</Button>}\n      </CardActions>\n    </Card>\n  );\n}\n\n// components/products/ProductDetailCard.tsx (USE generic)\nexport function ProductDetailCard({ product, loading, onEdit, onDelete }: Props) {\n  return (\n    <DetailCard\n      data={product}\n      loading={loading}\n      fields={[\n        { label: ''Name'', key: ''name'' },\n        { label: ''Price'', key: ''price'', render: (val) => `$${val}` },\n        { label: ''Description'', key: ''description'' },\n        { label: ''Stock'', key: ''stock'', render: (val) => `${val} units` },\n      ]}\n      onEdit={onEdit}\n      onDelete={onDelete}\n    />\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Duplication prevented**:\n- No duplicate DetailCard implementations\n- Generic component reusable for all entities\n- Consistent UI/UX across User, Order, Product\n- Refactored existing UserDetailCard and OrderDetailCard to use generic\n\nSee [examples/component-pattern-extraction.md](examples/component-pattern-extraction.md) for full example.\n</example>\n\n<example name=\"service-reuse\">\n**Request**: \"Add a service to send password reset emails\"\n\n**Search phase**:\n```\nSearches:\n1. Grep \"sendEmail|emailService\" → Found EmailService class\n2. Grep \"nodemailer|sendgrid\" → Found nodemailer setup\n3. Glob \"**/services/**/*email*.ts\" → Found services/EmailService.ts\n\nResults:\n- EmailService class with sendEmail() method\n- Already sends: welcome emails, order confirmations, notifications\n- Uses nodemailer + AWS SES\n```\n\n**Analysis**:\nEmailService already exists and is well-structured:\n```typescript\nclass EmailService {\n  async sendEmail(to: string, subject: string, template: string, data: any) {\n    const html = this.renderTemplate(template, data);\n    await this.transporter.sendMail({ to, subject, html });\n  }\n\n  async sendWelcomeEmail(user: User) { ... }\n  async sendOrderConfirmation(order: Order) { ... }\n}\n```\n\n**Recommendation**:\n\"Found existing EmailService that already sends 3 types of emails. Rather than creating a new service, I''ll add a sendPasswordResetEmail method to the existing service.\"\n\n**Implementation** (Option B - Extend existing):\n```typescript\n// services/EmailService.ts (extend existing class)\nclass EmailService {\n  // ... existing methods ...\n\n  async sendPasswordResetEmail(user: User, resetToken: string) {\n    const resetUrl = `${process.env.APP_URL}/reset-password?token=${resetToken}`;\n\n    await this.sendEmail(\n      user.email,\n      ''Password Reset Request'',\n      ''password-reset'',  // template name\n      { userName: user.name, resetUrl, expiresIn: ''1 hour'' }\n    );\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Duplication prevented**:\n- No new email service created\n- Reused existing nodemailer configuration\n- Reused template rendering logic\n- Consistent email sending across app\n\nSee [examples/service-extension.md](examples/service-extension.md) for full example.\n</example>\n</examples>\n\n<anti_patterns>\n<anti_pattern name=\"skipping-search\">\n**Problem**: Implementing without searching first\n\n**Bad approach**:\n```\nUser: \"Create an API endpoint to update user email\"\nClaude: *Immediately writes new endpoint from scratch*\n```\n\nResult: Duplicate endpoint with different auth, validation, error handling from existing user endpoints.\n\n**Correct approach**:\n```\nUser: \"Create an API endpoint to update user email\"\nClaude: \"Let me search for existing user endpoints first...\"\nClaude: *Finds 3 similar endpoints*\nClaude: \"Found existing pattern. I''ll follow it for consistency.\"\n```\n\n**Rule**: ALWAYS search before implementing. Takes 5-10 seconds, prevents hours of refactoring later.\n</anti_pattern>\n\n<anti_pattern name=\"ignoring-search-results\">\n**Problem**: Finding existing code but implementing new anyway\n\n**Bad approach**:\n```\nSearch: Found ProductSummaryCard component\nClaude: \"Found ProductSummaryCard, but I''ll create ProductDetailCard from scratch\"\n*Creates duplicate card component with different styling, props, structure*\n```\n\nResult: Two similar components that should be one, inconsistent UI, double maintenance.\n\n**Correct approach**:\n```\nSearch: Found ProductSummaryCard component\nClaude: \"Found ProductSummaryCard showing basic info. Should we extend it to show full details, or do you need a separate component? The summary version could potentially be enhanced rather than creating a duplicate.\"\n```\n\n**Rule**: When search finds similar code, default to reuse/extend. Only create new if justified.\n</anti_pattern>\n\n<anti_pattern name=\"shallow-search\">\n**Problem**: Searching only for exact matches, missing similar patterns\n\n**Bad approach**:\n```\nRequest: \"Create endpoint GET /api/products/:id\"\nSearch: Only \"GET /api/products\" (too specific)\nMisses: All other GET endpoints with similar structure\n```\n\nResult: Misses established patterns for GET /:id endpoints across User, Order, etc.\n\n**Correct approach**:\n```\nRequest: \"Create endpoint GET /api/products/:id\"\nSearches:\n- \"router.get.*:id\" (find all parameterized GET endpoints)\n- \"/api/.*/:id\" (find all resource-by-id patterns)\n- \"products\" (find all product-related code)\n```\n\n**Rule**: Use multiple search strategies (keywords, patterns, files). Cast wide net, filter results.\n</anti_pattern>\n\n<anti_pattern name=\"copy-paste-without-understanding\">\n**Problem**: Copying existing code without understanding it\n\n**Bad approach**:\n```\nFound: Complex UserDetailCard with 15 props, internal state, side effects\nClaude: *Copies entire component, renames User → Product*\nResult: Cargo-culted complexity, unnecessary props, confusing code\n```\n\n**Correct approach**:\n```\nFound: Complex UserDetailCard\nClaude: \"This component is complex (15 props, internal state). Let me analyze what''s actually needed for Product use case...\"\nClaude: \"Product details only need 5 props. I''ll create simplified version following the core pattern but without unnecessary complexity.\"\n```\n\n**Rule**: Understand existing code before reusing. Don''t cargo-cult complexity.\n</anti_pattern>\n\n<anti_pattern name=\"premature-abstraction\">\n**Problem**: Creating generic abstraction after finding only 1-2 similar pieces\n\n**Bad approach**:\n```\nFound: UserDetailCard, ProductDetailCard (2 components)\nClaude: \"Let me create DetailCard<T> generic component with 20 configuration options to handle all possible cases...\"\n```\n\nResult: Over-engineered abstraction that''s harder to use than copying code.\n\n**Correct approach**:\n```\nFound: UserDetailCard, ProductDetailCard (2 components)\nClaude: \"Found 2 similar components. They''re simple enough that keeping them separate is fine for now. If we add a 3rd entity (Order), then we''ll extract the pattern.\"\n```\n\n**Rule**: Abstraction requires 3+ similar pieces (Rule of Three). Two instances don''t justify generic abstraction yet.\n</anti_pattern>\n</anti_patterns>\n\n<validation>\n<success_indicators>\nAnti-duplication skill successfully applied when:\n\n1. **Search executed before implementation**: Every \"create/implement\" request triggers search first\n2. **Results presented to user**: User sees what was found and why reuse is/isn''t appropriate\n3. **Reuse justified**: If reusing, explain what''s being reused. If not, explain why not.\n4. **Patterns maintained**: New code follows established patterns in codebase\n5. **Duplication avoided**: No near-identical code exists in multiple places\n6. **Abstractions appropriate**: Generic code created only when 3+ similar pieces exist (Rule of Three)\n</success_indicators>\n\n<metrics>\nTrack anti-duplication effectiveness:\n\n**Process metrics**:\n- % of \"create\" requests that trigger search (target: 100%)\n- Average search time (target: <10 seconds)\n- % of searches that find relevant results (target: >60%)\n\n**Outcome metrics**:\n- % of implementations that reuse existing code (target: >40%)\n- % of implementations that follow existing patterns (target: >80%)\n- Lines of code prevented (compared to from-scratch implementation)\n\n**Quality metrics**:\n- Consistency score: How similar are similar artifacts? (target: >80% structural similarity)\n- DRY violations: How many near-duplicates exist? (target: <3 copies of any pattern)\n- Refactoring burden: How often do bug fixes need to be applied in multiple places? (target: declining)\n</metrics>\n\n<validation_checklist>\nBefore completing implementation, verify:\n\n- [ ] Search was executed (not skipped)\n- [ ] Search covered multiple strategies (keywords, files, patterns)\n- [ ] Results were analyzed (exact, close, pattern matches identified)\n- [ ] Reuse options were considered (A, B, C, D, E)\n- [ ] If reusing: Existing code was understood (not blindly copied)\n- [ ] If extending: Extension fits naturally (not forced)\n- [ ] If new: Justification documented (why existing code doesn''t work)\n- [ ] Patterns followed: New code consistent with existing similar code\n- [ ] Abstraction appropriate: Generic code only if 3+ similar pieces\n</validation_checklist>\n</validation>\n\n<reference_guides>\nFor deeper topics, see reference files:\n\n**Search strategies**: [references/search-strategies.md](references/search-strategies.md)\n- Comprehensive search patterns by artifact type\n- Technology-specific search strategies\n- Domain-driven search approaches\n- Advanced regex patterns\n\n**Reuse patterns**: [references/reuse-patterns.md](references/reuse-patterns.md)\n- When to reuse directly vs extend\n- Extracting shared logic\n- Creating generic abstractions\n- Refactoring for reusability\n\n**Decision framework**: [references/decision-framework.md](references/decision-framework.md)\n- Decision tree for reuse vs new implementation\n- Calculating similarity scores\n- Justifying new code\n- Documenting decisions\n\n**Integration with phases**: [references/phase-integration.md](references/phase-integration.md)\n- Using anti-duplication in /plan phase\n- Using anti-duplication in /implement phase\n- Updating plan.md with discovered patterns\n- Documenting reuse decisions in NOTES.md\n</reference_guides>\n\n<success_criteria>\nThe anti-duplication skill is successfully applied when:\n\n1. **Proactive search**: Search triggered automatically before any \"create/implement\" request\n2. **Comprehensive coverage**: Multiple search strategies used (keywords, files, patterns, domain, technology)\n3. **Results analyzed**: Findings categorized (exact, close, pattern matches) and relevance scored\n4. **Reuse prioritized**: Options A-D (reuse, extend, extract, follow pattern) considered before Option E (new)\n5. **Patterns maintained**: New implementations follow established codebase patterns\n6. **Justification documented**: If creating new code despite similar existing code, justification clearly stated\n7. **DRY principle upheld**: No unnecessary duplication introduced\n8. **Abstractions appropriate**: Generic code created only when justified (Rule of Three: 3+ similar pieces)\n9. **User informed**: User understands what was found and why reuse is/isn''t happening\n10. **Time efficient**: Search completes in <10 seconds, doesn''t slow down development\n</success_criteria>\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:47:30.629Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Generation Agents like Claude Code, seeking to enforce the DRY principle and prevent code duplication through Spec-Driven Development.","zh":"适用于 Claude Code 等代码生成代理，旨在通过规范驱动开发强制执行 DRY 原则并防止代码重复。","ja":"Claude Code などのコード生成エージェントに適しており、Spec-Driven Development を通じて DRY 原則を強制し、コードの重複を防ぐことを目指しています。","ko":"클라우드 코드와 같은 코드 생성 에이전트에 적합하며, 규약 주도 개발을 통해 DRY 원칙을 강제하고 코드 중복을 방지하려는 목표를 가지고 있습니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de generación de código como Claude Code, que buscan hacer cumplir el principio DRY y prevenir la duplicación de código a través del desarrollo dirigido por especificaciones.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de génération de code tels que Claude Code, qui cherchent à faire respecter le principe DRY et à prévenir la duplication de code via le développement piloté par spécifications.","de":"Ideal für Code-Generierungsagenten wie Claude Code, die das DRY-Prinzip durchsetzen und Code-Duplizierung durch spezifikationsgetriebene Entwicklung verhindern möchten.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Geração de Código como Claude Code, que buscam impor o princípio DRY e prevenir a duplicação de código por meio do Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Especificações.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов генерации кода, таких как Claude Code, стремящихся обеспечить соблюдение принципа DRY и предотвратить дублирование кода посредством разработки, управляемой спецификациями.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء مولد أكواد مثل Claude Code، الذين يسعون إلى فرض مبدأ DRY ومنع تكرار الكود من خلال التطوير الموجه بالمواصفات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to proactively search codebases for existing patterns, utilizing quality gates, token budgets, and auditable artifacts to prevent maintenance nightmares and promote code reuse, all while working within repeatable workflows.","zh":"赋予代理主动搜索代码库中现有的模式的能力，利用质量门、令牌预算和可审计的工件来防止维护噩梦并促进代码重用，同时在可重复的工作流中工作。","ja":"コードベース内の既存のパターンを主に検索するエージェントの能力を提供し、メンテナンスの悪夢を防ぎ、コードの再利用を促進するために、品質ゲート、トークンバジェット、および監査可能なアーティファクトを利用し、繰り返し可能なワークフロー内で作業します。","ko":"에이전트가 코드베이스에서 기존 패턴을 주도적으로 검색할 수 있는 기능을 제공하여, 품질 게이트, 토큰 예산 및 감사 가능한 아티팩트를 활용하여 유지 보수 악몽을 방지하고 코드 재사용을 촉진하는 동시에 반복 가능한 워크플로에서 작업할 수 있습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes buscar proactivamente patrones existentes en las bases de código, utilizando puertas de calidad, presupuestos de tokens y artefactos auditables para prevenir pesadillas de mantenimiento y promover la reutilización de código, todo mientras trabajan dentro de flujos de trabajo repetibles.","fr":"Permet aux agents de rechercher proactivement des modèles existants dans les bases de code, en utilisant des portes de qualité, des budgets de jetons et des artefacts auditable pour prévenir les cauchemars de maintenance et promouvoir la réutilisation de code, le tout en travaillant dans des flux de travail répétitifs.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Codebasen proaktiv nach bestehenden Mustern zu durchsuchen, wobei Qualitätsprüfungen, Token-Budgets und überprüfbare Artefakte verwendet werden, um Wartungs-Albträume zu verhindern und Code-Wiederverwendung zu fördern, und zwar innerhalb wiederholbarer Workflows.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a procurar proativamente padrões existentes em repositórios de código, utilizando portas de qualidade, orçamentos de tokens e artefatos auditáveis para prevenir pesadelos de manutenção e promover a reutilização de código, tudo isso trabalhando dentro de fluxos de trabalho repetíveis.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проактивно искать существующие шаблоны в кодовых базах, используя ворота качества, бюджет токенов и аудиторские артефакты для предотвращения проблем с обслуживанием и содействия повторному использованию кода, все это происходит в рамках повторяющихся рабочих процессов.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من البحث بنشاط عن الأنماط الحالية في قواعد البيانات الرئيسية، باستخدام بوابات الجودة وميزانيات الرموز والتحقق من صحة الوثائق لمنع كوابيس الصيانة وتعزيز إعادة استخدام الكود، كل ذلك ضمن سير عمل متكرر."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code reviews for duplication","Generating refactoring plans to reduce codebase size","Debugging inconsistent feature evolution across duplicates"],"zh":["自动化代码审查以防止重复","生成重构计划以减少代码库大小","调试不一致的功能演化跨重复"],"ja":["重複を防ぐためのコードレビューの自動化","コードベースのサイズを減らすためのリファクタリングプランの生成","重複を跨ぐ機能の不一致な進化のデバッグ"],"ko":["중복을 방지하기 위한 코드 리뷰 자동화","코드베이스 크기를 줄이기 위한 리팩토링 계획 생성","중복을 가로지르는 기능의 불일치한 진화 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de revisiones de código para duplicados","Generación de planes de refactorización para reducir el tamaño de la base de código","Depuración de la evolución inconsistente de características en duplicados"],"fr":["Automatisation des examens de code pour les doublons","Génération de plans de refactoring pour réduire la taille de la base de code","Débogage de l''évolution inconsistante des fonctionnalités sur les doublons"],"de":["Automatisierung von Code-Reviews für Duplikate","Erzeugung von Refactoring-Plänen zur Reduzierung der Codebasen-Größe","Fehlersuche bei inkonsistenter Feature-Evolution in Duplikaten"],"pt":["Automatizar revisões de código para duplicação","Gerar planos de reestruturação para reduzir o tamanho da base de código","Depurar evolução de recursos inconsistentes em cópias"],"ru":["Автоматизировать проверку кода на дублирование","Генерировать планы рефакторинга для уменьшения размера кодовой базы","Отладить несоответствующую эволюцию функций в дубликатах"],"ar":["ت 자동 hóa استعراض أكواد للتكرار","توليد خطط لإعادة هيكلة لتقليل حجم قاعدة البيانات","تصحيح آفات التطور الغير متناسق في النسخ"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires integration with codebase management systems","Dependent on quality gate and token budget configurations"],"zh":["需要与代码库管理系统集成","依赖于质量门和令牌预算配置"],"ja":["コードベース管理システムとの統合が必要","品質ゲートおよびトークンバジェットの構成に依存"],"ko":["코드베이스 관리 시스템との 통합이 필요","품질 게이트 및 토큰 예산 구성에 의존"],"es":["Requiere integración con sistemas de gestión de código","Dependiente de configuraciones de puertas de calidad y presupuestos de tokens"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec des systèmes de gestion de code","Dépend des configurations de portes de qualité et de budgets de jetons"],"de":["Benötigt Integration mit Codebasen-Management-Systemen","Abhängig von Qualitätsprüfungs- und Token-Budget-Konfigurationen"],"pt":["Requer integração com sistemas de gerenciamento de repositórios de código","Dependente de configurações de portas de qualidade e orçamentos de tokens"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с системами управления кодовыми базами","Зависит от конфигураций ворот качества и бюджетов токенов"],"ar":["يتطلب تكاملًا مع أنظمة إدارة قواعد البيانات الرئيسية","يعتمد على تكوينات بوابات الجودة وميزانيات الرموز"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('gakonst/dotfiles/preferences', 'community', 'gakonst', 'dotfiles', 'gakonst/dotfiles', 'preferences', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.451Z', '2026-02-18T06:48:01.011Z', NULL, '{"id":"gakonst/dotfiles/preferences","name":"preferences","description":{"zh":"保持一致的 Git 和 GitHub 工作流，使用 Georgios 的配置文件和脚本","ja":"Georgios の設定ファイルとスクリプトを使用して一貫性のある Git と GitHub のワークフローを実現","ko":"Georgios 의 설정 파일 및 스크립트를 사용하여 일관된 Git 및 GitHub 워크플로우를 유지","es":"Preferencias de desarrollo para Git y GitHub que ayudan a mantener la consistencia en los repositorios","fr":"Préférences de développement pour Git et GitHub qui aident à maintenir la cohérence dans les dépôts","de":"Entwicklereinstellungen für Git und GitHub, die helfen, die Konsistenz in den Repositories aufrechtzuerhalten","pt":"As preferências de desenvolvimento com Git e GitHub ajudam a manter a consistência no seu fluxo de trabalho","ru":"Настройки разработки с Git и GitHub помогают поддерживать последовательность в вашем рабочем процессе","ar":"تفضيلات التطوير مع Git و GitHub تساعد على الحفاظ على الاتساق في تدفق العمل الخاص بك","en":"My dotfiles along with a script to deploy them to your environment."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Git 配置文件和工作流","ja":"Git と GitHub の設定とワークフロー","ko":"Git 및 GitHub 설정 및 워크플로우","es":"Preferencias de desarrollo con Git y GitHub","fr":"Préférences de développement avec Git et GitHub","de":"Entwicklereinstellungen mit Git und GitHub","pt":"Preferências de Desenvolvimento com Git e GitHub","ru":"Настройки разработки с Git и GitHub","ar":"تفضيلات التطوير مع Git و GitHub","en":"preferences"},"description":{"zh":"保持一致的 Git 和 GitHub 工作流，使用 Georgios 的配置文件和脚本","ja":"Georgios の設定ファイルとスクリプトを使用して一貫性のある Git と GitHub のワークフローを実現","ko":"Georgios 의 설정 파일 및 스크립트를 사용하여 일관된 Git 및 GitHub 워크플로우를 유지","es":"Preferencias de desarrollo para Git y GitHub que ayudan a mantener la consistencia en los repositorios","fr":"Préférences de développement pour Git et GitHub qui aident à maintenir la cohérence dans les dépôts","de":"Entwicklereinstellungen für Git und GitHub, die helfen, die Konsistenz in den Repositories aufrechtzuerhalten","pt":"As preferências de desenvolvimento com Git e GitHub ajudam a manter a consistência no seu fluxo de trabalho","ru":"Настройки разработки с Git и GitHub помогают поддерживать последовательность в вашем рабочем процессе","ar":"تفضيلات التطوير مع Git و GitHub تساعد على الحفاظ على الاتساق في تدفق العمل الخاص بك","en":"My dotfiles along with a script to deploy them to your environment."},"definition":{"en":"My dotfiles along with a script to deploy them to your environment."},"features":{"zh":["使用 gh 进行认证、克隆、PR 和问题跟踪","保持一致的 Git 和 GitHub 工作流","自动化 CI 和 CD 流程","支持 Rust、Python、TypeScript 和 Vercel 预览","简化 Git 和 GitHub 的使用"],"ja":["gh を使用して認証、クローン、PR、issue を実行","一貫性のある Git と GitHub のワークフローを実現","CI と CD プロセスを自動化","Rust、Python、TypeScript、Vercel プレビューをサポート","Git と GitHub の使用を簡素化"],"ko":["gh를 사용하여 인증, 클론, PR 및 이슈 추적","일관된 Git 및 GitHub 워크플로우를 유지","CI 및 CD 프로세스를 자동화","Rust, Python, TypeScript, Vercel 미리 보기 지원","Git 및 GitHub 사용을 단순화"],"es":["Uso de gh para autenticación y clonación","Convenciones para commits y solicitudes de extracción","Configuración de GitHub Actions para Rust, Python y TypeScript","Previsualizaciones de Vercel","Mantenimiento de la consistencia en los repositorios"],"fr":["Utilisation de gh pour l''authentification et le clonage","Conventions pour les commits et les demandes d''extraction","Configuration de GitHub Actions pour Rust, Python et TypeScript","Aperçus de Vercel","Maintenance de la cohérence dans les dépôts"],"de":["Verwendung von gh für Authentifizierung und Klonen","Konventionen für Commits und Pull-Requests","Konfiguration von GitHub Actions für Rust, Python und TypeScript","Vorschauen von Vercel","Aufrechterhaltung der Konsistenz in den Repositories"],"pt":["Uso de `gh` para autenticação e gerenciamento de repositórios","Padronização de commits e preparação de pull requests","Integração com GitHub Actions para automação de tarefas","Manutenção de repositórios prontos para automação","Uso de convenções para evitar quebras em ferramentas estabelecidas"],"ru":["Использование `gh` для аутентификации и управления репозиториями","Стандартизация коммитов и подготовка пулл-реквестов","Интеграция с GitHub Actions для автоматизации задач","Поддержание репозиториев в готовности для автоматизации","Использование соглашений для предотвращения нарушений в установленных инструментах"],"ar":["استخدام `gh` للتحقق من الصحة والإدارة المخازن","توحيد التعليقات والاستعداد لطلبات السحب","التكامل مع إجراءات GitHub للautomatización من المهام","الحفاظ على المخازن جاهزة للautomatización","استخدام الاتفاقيات لتجنب الكسور في الأدوات المعتمدة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Git 配置文件","GitHub 脚本","CI/CD 自动化","Rust","Python","TypeScript","Vercel 预览","Git 工作流","GitHub 工作流"],"ja":["Git 設定ファイル","GitHub スクリプト","CI/CD 自動化","Rust","Python","TypeScript","Vercel プレビュー","Git ワークフロー","GitHub ワークフロー"],"ko":["Git 설정 파일","GitHub 스크립트","CI/CD 자동화","Rust","Python","TypeScript","Vercel 미리 보기","Git 워크플로우","GitHub 워크플로우"],"es":["preferencias de desarrollo","Git","GitHub","gh","autenticación","clonación","commits","solicitudes de extracción","GitHub Actions","Rust","Python","TypeScript","Vercel"],"fr":["préférences de développement","Git","GitHub","gh","authentification","clonage","commits","demandes d''extraction","GitHub Actions","Rust","Python","TypeScript","Vercel"],"de":["Entwicklereinstellungen","Git","GitHub","gh","Authentifizierung","Klonen","Commits","Pull-Requests","GitHub Actions","Rust","Python","TypeScript","Vercel"],"pt":["desenvolvimento com Git","GitHub","preferências de desenvolvimento","autenticação com `gh`","padronização de commits","integração com GitHub Actions"],"ru":["разработка с Git","GitHub","настройки разработки","аутентификация с `gh`","стандартизация коммитов","интеграция с GitHub Actions"],"ar":["التطوير مع Git","GitHub","تفضيلات التطوير","التحقق من الصحة مع `gh`","توحيد التعليقات","التكامل مع إجراءات GitHub"]}},"owner":"gakonst","repo":"dotfiles","repoPath":"gakonst/dotfiles","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.451Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"preferences","description":"Use when aligning with Georgios’s default Git/GitHub conventions—cloning with gh, Conventional Commits, atomic staging, and guarded GitHub Actions for Rust/Python/TypeScript—so work matches his standard workflows.","bodyPreview":"# Preferences (Git & GitHub)\n\n## Overview\nFollow these defaults any time work touches git, GitHub, or CI to stay consistent with Georgios’s workflow and keep repos ready for automation.\n\n## When to Use\n- Cloning or checking out repos/PRs.\n- Writing commits or preparing PRs.\n- Adding or editing GitHub Actions (Rust, Python/uv, TypeScript, Vercel previews).\n- Any task that might break established tooling if conventions drift.\n\n## Core Preferences\n- Use `gh` for auth, cloning, PRs, issues, and API","body":"# Preferences (Git & GitHub)\n\n## Overview\nFollow these defaults any time work touches git, GitHub, or CI to stay consistent with Georgios’s workflow and keep repos ready for automation.\n\n## When to Use\n- Cloning or checking out repos/PRs.\n- Writing commits or preparing PRs.\n- Adding or editing GitHub Actions (Rust, Python/uv, TypeScript, Vercel previews).\n- Any task that might break established tooling if conventions drift.\n\n## Core Preferences\n- Use `gh` for auth, cloning, PRs, issues, and API calls (not raw curl).\n- Standard clone path: `~/github/<owner>/<repo>`; ensure parent exists before cloning.\n- Commit style must be Conventional Commits, one behavior per commit, staged atomically with `git add -p`.\n- PR titles/bodies mirror main commit; keep history clean and reviewable.\n- CI should be path-scoped: run only the stacks whose files changed; add a `changes` job with `dorny/paths-filter`.\n- Language defaults: Rust uses rustfmt/clippy/nextest + sccache/mold; Python uses uv (ruff, mypy, pytest); TypeScript uses pnpm (format:check, lint, test) and caches Playwright when needed; Vercel previews gated on frontend paths.\n- Use concurrency to cancel superseded PR runs; optional `alls-green` aggregator for a single required status.\n- Avoid storing PATs; fetch tokens on demand via `gh auth token`.\n\n## Git & GitHub Workflow\n- Check auth first: `gh auth status`; log in if needed. Export tokens via `gh auth token` when tools expect `GITHUB_TOKEN`.\n- Clone/checkout with `gh repo clone owner/repo ~/github/owner/repo` and `gh pr checkout <num>`.\n- Prefer `gh pr create --fill` for new PRs; reviews via `gh pr review --approve|--request-changes -b \"...\"`\n- For data/scripts, use `gh api ... --paginate` piped to `jq`; avoid unauthenticated curl to api.github.com.\n\n## Commit Rules (Conventional Commits)\n- Subject: `<type>[scope]: <imperative>` (e.g., `feat(auth): add magic link`), ≤72 chars, present/imperative.\n- Types: feat, fix, refactor, chore, test, docs, perf, build, ci, revert.\n- One behavior per commit: stage with `git add -p`; verify `git diff --cached` matches the subject.\n- Body: what/why; footer for issues. No “update/misc” subjects.\n\n## GitHub Actions Expectations\n- Add a `changes` job with `dorny/paths-filter@v3`; gate downstream jobs with `needs: changes` + `if` outputs.\n- Rust job: checkout, `dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable` with fmt/clippy, `rui314/setup-mold`, `mozilla-actions/sccache-action`, `Swatinem/rust-cache`, `cargo fmt -- --check`, `cargo clippy -D warnings`, `taiki-e/install-action@nextest`, `cargo nextest run --no-fail-fast -j num-cpus`.\n- Python job: checkout, `astral-sh/setup-uv@v3`, `uv venv && uv sync --frozen`, `uv run ruff check .`, `uv run mypy .`, `uv run pytest`.\n- TypeScript job: checkout, `actions/setup-node@v4` (node 20, cache=pnpm), `pnpm/action-setup@v4 --run_install`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm test -- --runInBand`, `pnpm format:check`, cache Playwright and install on cache miss.\n- Vercel preview: only when frontend paths change; permissions `contents: read, deployments: write, id-token: write`; use project/org/token secrets.\n- Add `concurrency` to cancel superseded runs; optional `re-actors/alls-green` to aggregate statuses.\n\n## Quick Reference\n- Clone: `dir=~/github/o/r; mkdir -p \"$(dirname \"$dir\")\"; gh repo clone o/r \"$dir\"`\n- Checkout PR: `gh pr checkout <num>`\n- Stage atomically: `git add -p`; verify: `git diff --cached`\n- Commit: `fix(api): guard null author id`\n- Paths-filter job: `uses: dorny/paths-filter@v3` → outputs gate jobs\n- Rust CI trio: fmt + clippy + nextest; with sccache + mold\n- Python CI: uv sync, ruff, mypy, pytest\n- TS CI: pnpm format:check, lint, test; cache Playwright\n- Vercel: gated on TS/frontend paths only\n\n## Red Flags\n- Using `git clone` or raw HTTPS without `gh` (breaks auth/layout).\n- Commit mixes new feature + bugfix or has vague subject.\n- CI runs every job on docs-only PRs (missing paths-filter).\n- Python job uses `pip install` instead of `uv sync --frozen`.\n- Vercel preview runs on every PR regardless of frontend changes.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:48:01.011Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing standardized Git and GitHub workflow integration.","zh":"非常适合需要标准化 Git 和 GitHub 工作流集成的开发代理。","ja":"開発エージェントが標準化された Git と GitHub のワークフロー統合を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"개발 에이전트가 표준화된 Git 및 GitHub 워크플로 통합을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan una integración de flujo de trabajo de Git y GitHub estandarizada.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une intégration de workflow Git et GitHub standardisée.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungssagenten, die eine standardisierte Git- und GitHub-Workflow-Integration benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de integração de fluxo de trabalho do Git e GitHub padronizada.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, которым необходима стандартизированная интеграция рабочего процесса Git и GitHub.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء النمطية الذين يحتاجون إلى دمج عمل معياري Git و GitHub"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to maintain consistent repositories using `gh` for authentication, cloning, and API interactions, ensuring seamless automation and CI/CD pipeline management with GitHub Actions for Rust, Python, TypeScript, and Vercel previews.","zh":"赋予代理维护一致的仓库的能力，使用 `gh` 进行身份验证、克隆和 API 交互，确保与 GitHub Actions 的无缝自动化和 CI/CD 管道管理，支持 Rust、Python、TypeScript 和 Vercel 预览。","ja":"エージェントが一貫したリポジトリを維持できるようにし、`gh` を使用して認証、クローン、API 相互作用を行い、GitHub Actions とのシームレスな自動化と CI/CD パイプライン管理を可能にし、Rust、Python、TypeScript、Vercel プレビューをサポートします。","ko":"에이전트가 일관된 저장소를 유지할 수 있도록 하고, `gh`를 사용하여 인증, 복제 및 API 상호 작용을 수행하여 GitHub Actions와의 자동화 및 CI/CD 파이프라인 관리를 원활하게 하며, Rust, Python, TypeScript 및 Vercel 미리 보기를 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a mantener repositorios consistentes utilizando `gh` para la autenticación, clonación e interacciones de la API, garantizando una automatización y gestión de pipelines de CI/CD sin problemas con GitHub Actions para Rust, Python, TypeScript y vistas previas de Vercel.","fr":"Permet aux agents de maintenir des référentiels cohérents en utilisant `gh` pour l''authentification, le clonage et les interactions de l''API, assurant une automatisation et une gestion de pipelines de CI/CD sans problème avec GitHub Actions pour Rust, Python, TypeScript et aperçus de Vercel.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, konsistente Repositorys mithilfe von `gh` für Authentifizierung, Klonen und API-Interaktionen zu pflegen, wodurch eine nahtlose Automatisierung und Verwaltung von CI/CD-Pipelines mit GitHub Actions für Rust, Python, TypeScript und Vercel-Vorschauen gewährleistet wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a manter repositórios consistentes usando `gh` para autenticação, clonagem e interações de API, garantindo automação sem problemas e gerenciamento de pipelines de CI/CD com GitHub Actions para Rust, Python, TypeScript e pré-visualizações do Vercel.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью поддерживать последовательные репозитории, используя `gh` для аутентификации, клонирования и взаимодействия с API, обеспечивая бесперебойную автоматизацию и управление конвейерами CI/CD с помощью GitHub Actions для Rust, Python, TypeScript и предпросмотров Vercel.","ar":"يُمكّن الوكلاء من الحفاظ على مستودعات متسقة باستخدام `gh` للتحقق من الصحة والاستنساخ وتفاعلات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات، مما يضمن تطبيق تلقائي بدون مشاكل وإدارة أنابيب CI/CD مع GitHub Actions من أجل Rust و Python و TypeScript وتحديدات Vercel"},"useCases":{"en":["Standardizing Git commit messages and PR templates","Automating GitHub repository setup with consistent branching strategies","Debugging CI/CD pipeline issues related to Git and GitHub Actions configuration"],"zh":["标准化 Git 提交消息和 PR 模板","使用一致的分支策略自动化 GitHub 仓库设置","调试与 Git 和 GitHub Actions 配置相关的 CI/CD 管道问题"],"ja":["Git コミットメッセージと PR テンプレートの標準化","一貫したブランチ戦略を使用した GitHub リポジトリの自動設定","Git と GitHub Actions 構成に関連する CI/CD パイプラインの問題のデバッグ"],"ko":["Git 커밋 메시지 및 PR 템플릿 표준화","일관된 분기 전략을 사용하여 GitHub 저장소 자동 설정","Git 및 GitHub Actions 구성과 관련된 CI/CD 파이프라인 문제 디버깅"],"es":["Estandarizar mensajes de commit de Git y plantillas de PR","Automatizar la configuración del repositorio de GitHub con estrategias de ramificación coherentes","Depurar problemas de pipeline de CI/CD relacionados con la configuración de Git y GitHub Actions"],"fr":["Standardiser les messages de commit Git et les modèles de PR","Automatiser la configuration du référentiel GitHub avec des stratégies de branchement cohérentes","Déboguer les problèmes de pipeline de CI/CD liés à la configuration de Git et GitHub Actions"],"de":["Standardisieren von Git-Commit-Meldungen und PR-Vorlagen","Automatisieren der Einrichtung des GitHub-Repositorys mit konsistenten Verzweigungsstrategien","Beheben von Problemen mit der CI/CD-Pipeline im Zusammenhang mit der Konf