ambios de nombre y descripción","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["Approche expérimentale d''artifact-driven","Flexibilité pour décrire ce que vous voulez construire ou réparer","Outil de question à l''utilisateur pour obtenir des informations","Déduction d''un nom en kebab-case à partir de la description","Prise en charge des changements de nom et de description","Intégration avec les outils de développement"],"de":["Experimenteller Ansatz von artifact-driven","Flexibilität, um zu beschreiben, was Sie bauen oder reparieren möchten","Werkzeug zur Frage an den Benutzer, um Informationen zu erhalten","Ableitung eines Namens im kebab-Format aus der Beschreibung","Unterstützung für Namens- und Beschreibungsänderungen","Integration mit Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["Iniciação de nova alteração com abordagem experimental","Uso de artefatos para melhorar o fluxo de trabalho","Derivação de nome em kebab-case a partir da descrição do usuário","Uso da ferramenta AskUserQuestion para solicitar informações ao usuário","Melhoria do fluxo de trabalho de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Запуск нового изменения с экспериментальным подходом","Использование артефактов для улучшения рабочего процесса","Получение имени в kebab-case из описания пользователя","Использование инструмента AskUserQuestion для запроса информации у пользователя","Улучшение рабочего процесса разработки"],"ar":["بدء تغيير جديد باستخدام النهج التجريبي","استخدام المكونات لتحسين تدفق العمل","استخراج اسم بالشكل kebab-case من وصف المستخدم","استخدام أداة AskUserQuestion لطلب معلومات من المستخدم","تحسين تدفق العمل التطويري"]},"keywords":{"zh":["实验性构件驱动方法","新变更","变更名称","kebab-case","AskUserQuestion工具","开发者工具"],"ja":["実験的なアーティファクト駆動アプローチ","新しい変更","変更名","kebab-case","AskUserQuestionツール","開発者ツール"],"ko":["실험적인 아티팩트 주도 접근법","新的 변경","변경 이름","kebab-case","AskUserQuestion工具","개발자 도구"],"es":["OpenSpec","artifact-driven","nuevo cambio","enfoque experimental","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo","integración de herramientas","kebab-case","pregunta al usuario"],"fr":["OpenSpec","artifact-driven","nouveau changement","approche expérimentale","développement de logiciels","outils de développement","intégration d''outils","kebab-case","question à l''utilisateur"],"de":["OpenSpec","artifact-driven","neue Änderung","experimenteller Ansatz","Softwareentwicklung","Entwicklungstools","Tool-Integration","kebab-Format","Benutzerfrage"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de software","abordagem experimental","artefatos","fluxo de trabalho","openspec-new-change","skill de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["разработка программного обеспечения","экспериментальный подход","артефакты","рабочий процесс","openspec-new-change","навык разработки"],"ar":["تطوير البرمجيات","النهج التجريبي","المكونات","تدفق العمل","openspec-new-change","مهارة التطوير"]}},"owner":"jaxxstorm","repo":"landlord","repoPath":"jaxxstorm/landlord","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.451Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-new-change","description":"Start a new OpenSpec change using the experimental artifact workflow. Use when the user wants to create a new feature, fix, or modification with a structured step-by-step approach.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Start a new change using the experimental artifact-driven approach.\n\n**Input**: The user''s request should include a change name (kebab-case) OR a description of what they want to build.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no clear input provided, ask what they want to build**\n\n   Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** (open-ended, no preset options) to ask:\n   > \"What change do you want to work on? Describe what you want to build or fix.\"\n\n   From their description, derive a kebab-case name (e.g., \"add user authentic","body":"Start a new change using the experimental artifact-driven approach.\n\n**Input**: The user''s request should include a change name (kebab-case) OR a description of what they want to build.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no clear input provided, ask what they want to build**\n\n   Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** (open-ended, no preset options) to ask:\n   > \"What change do you want to work on? Describe what you want to build or fix.\"\n\n   From their description, derive a kebab-case name (e.g., \"add user authentication\" → `add-user-auth`).\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT proceed without understanding what the user wants to build.\n\n2. **Determine the workflow schema**\n\n   Use the default schema (omit `--schema`) unless the user explicitly requests a different workflow.\n\n   **Use a different schema only if the user mentions:**\n   - A specific schema name → use `--schema <name>`\n   - \"show workflows\" or \"what workflows\" → run `openspec schemas --json` and let them choose\n\n   **Otherwise**: Omit `--schema` to use the default.\n\n3. **Create the change directory**\n   ```bash\n   openspec new change \"<name>\"\n   ```\n   Add `--schema <name>` only if the user requested a specific workflow.\n   This creates a scaffolded change at `openspec/changes/<name>/` with the selected schema.\n\n4. **Show the artifact status**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\"\n   ```\n   This shows which artifacts need to be created and which are ready (dependencies satisfied).\n\n5. **Get instructions for the first artifact**\n   The first artifact depends on the schema (e.g., `proposal` for spec-driven).\n   Check the status output to find the first artifact with status \"ready\".\n   ```bash\n   openspec instructions <first-artifact-id> --change \"<name>\"\n   ```\n   This outputs the template and context for creating the first artifact.\n\n6. **STOP and wait for user direction**\n\n**Output**\n\nAfter completing the steps, summarize:\n- Change name and location\n- Schema/workflow being used and its artifact sequence\n- Current status (0/N artifacts complete)\n- The template for the first artifact\n- Prompt: \"Ready to create the first artifact? Just describe what this change is about and I''ll draft it, or ask me to continue.\"\n\n**Guardrails**\n- Do NOT create any artifacts yet - just show the instructions\n- Do NOT advance beyond showing the first artifact template\n- If the name is invalid (not kebab-case), ask for a valid name\n- If a change with that name already exists, suggest continuing that change instead\n- Pass --schema if using a non-default workflow\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:49:08.735Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Agile Development Agents needing streamlined project initialization with artifact-driven approaches.","zh":"非常适合需要流线型项目初始化和基于工件的方法的敏捷开发代理。","ja":"Agile開発エージェントがプロジェクトの初期化を効率化し、アーティファクト駆動型アプローチを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"프로젝트 초기화를 효율화하고 아티팩트 기반 접근 방식을 필요로 하는 애자일 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo ágil que necesitan una inicialización de proyecto optimizada con enfoques impulsados por artefactos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement agile ayant besoin d''une initialisation de projet simplifiée avec des approches basées sur les artefacts.","de":"Perfekt für Agile-Entwicklungsagenten, die eine optimierte Projektinitialisierung mit artefaktbasierten Ansätzen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Ágil que necessitam de inicialização de projeto simplificada com abordagens baseadas em artefatos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Agile-разработки, которым необходима упрощенная инициализация проектов с помощью подходов, основанных на артефактах.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التطوير الرشيق الذين يحتاجون إلى تبسيط 초기ه المشروع باستخدام نهج مدفوع بالمنفعة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to derive kebab-case names from user descriptions and initiate new changes using the experimental artifact-driven approach, leveraging tools like the AskUserQuestion tool for open-ended user input.","zh":"赋予代理人从用户描述中推导出短横线命名法名称，并使用实验性的基于工件的方法启动新的更改，利用类似AskUserQuestion工具的工具来获取用户的开放性输入。","ja":"エージェントがユーザーの説明からケバブケースの名前を導出し、AskUserQuestionツールなどのオープンエンドユーザー入力を使用して、実験的なアーティファクト駆動型アプローチで新しい変更を開始できるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 사용자의 설명에서 케밥 케이스 이름을 유추하고 AskUserQuestion 도구와 같은 도구를 사용하여 개방형 사용자 입력을 통해 실험적인 아티팩트 기반 접근 방식으로 새로운 변경을 시작할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a derivar nombres en kebab-case a partir de descripciones de usuarios e iniciar nuevos cambios utilizando el enfoque experimental basado en artefactos, aprovechando herramientas como la herramienta AskUserQuestion para la entrada de usuario de preguntas abiertas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de dériver des noms en kebab-case à partir de descriptions d''utilisateurs et d''initier de nouveaux changements en utilisant l''approche expérimentale basée sur les artefacts, en exploitant des outils comme l''outil AskUserQuestion pour l''entrée utilisateur de questions ouvertes.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, kebab-case-Namen aus Benutzerbeschreibungen abzuleiten und neue Änderungen mithilfe des experimentellen, artefaktbasierten Ansatzes zu initiieren, indem Tools wie das AskUserQuestion-Tool für offene Benutzereingaben genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a derivar nomes em kebab-case a partir de descrições de usuários e iniciar novas alterações usando a abordagem experimental baseada em artefatos, aproveitando ferramentas como a ferramenta AskUserQuestion para entrada de usuário de fim aberto.","ru":"Позволяет агентам получать имена в kebab-случае из описаний пользователей и инициировать новые изменения с помощью экспериментального подхода, основанного на артефактах, используя инструменты, такие как AskUserQuestion, для открытого ввода пользователя.","ar":"يُمكّن الوكلاء من اشتقاق أسماء الحالة الكبаб من описات المستخدمين وبدء تغييرات جديدة باستخدام نهج تجريبي مدفوع بالمنفعة، مستفيداً من أدوات مثل أداة AskUserQuestion لمدخلات المستخدم المفتوحة."},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing new projects with user-defined change names","Deriving kebab-case names from user descriptions","Automating the start of new changes with experimental approaches"],"zh":["使用用户定义的更改名称初始化新项目","从用户描述中推导出短横线命名法名称","使用实验性的方法自动启动新的更改"],"ja":["ユーザー定義の変更名で新しいプロジェクトを初期化する","ユーザーの説明からケバブケースの名前を導出する","実験的なアプローチを使用して新しい変更を自動的に開始する"],"ko":["사용자 정의 변경 이름으로 새로운 프로젝트를 초기화하는 것","사용자의 설명에서 케밥 케이스 이름을 유추하는 것","실험적인 접근 방식을 사용하여 새로운 변경을 자동으로 시작하는 것"],"es":["Inicialización de nuevos proyectos con nombres de cambios definidos por el usuario","Derivación de nombres en kebab-case a partir de descripciones de usuarios","Automatización del inicio de nuevos cambios con enfoques experimentales"],"fr":["Initialisation de nouveaux projets avec des noms de changements définis par l''utilisateur","Déivation de noms en kebab-case à partir de descriptions d''utilisateurs","Automatisation du démarrage de nouveaux changements avec des approches expérimentales"],"de":["Initialisierung neuer Projekte mit benutzerdefinierten Änderungsnamen","Ableitung von kebab-case-Namen aus Benutzerbeschreibungen","Automatisierung des Starts neuer Änderungen mit experimentellen Ansätzen"],"pt":["Inicializar novos projetos com nomes de alterações definidos pelo usuário","Derivar nomes em kebab-case a partir de descrições de usuários","Automatizar o início de novas alterações com abordagens experimentais"],"ru":["Инициализация новых проектов с именами изменений, определенных пользователем","Получение имен в kebab-случае из описаний пользователей","Автоматизация начала новых изменений с помощью экспериментальных подходов"],"ar":["ت初ه مشاريع جديدة بأسماء التغيير المحددة من قبل المستخدم","اشتقاق أسماء الحالة الكباب من وصفات المستخدم","تأتمتة بدء التغييرات الجديدة باستخدام النهج التجريبي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires user input or description of the change","Limited to kebab-case naming convention"],"zh":["需要用户输入或对更改的描述","仅限于短横线命名约定"],"ja":["ユーザーの入力または変更の説明が必要","ケバブケースの命名規則のみに限定される"],"ko":["사용자 입력 또는 변경 설명이 필요함","케밥 케이스 命名 규칙만으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere entrada o descripción de cambio por parte del usuario","Limitado a la convención de nomenclatura en kebab-case"],"fr":["Nécessite une entrée ou une description de changement de l''utilisateur","Limité à la convention de nommage en kebab-case"],"de":["Benötigt Benutzereingabe oder Beschreibung der Änderung","Begrenzt auf die kebab-case-Namenskonvention"],"pt":["Requer entrada ou descrição do usuário da alteração","Limitado à convenção de nomenclatura em kebab-case"],"ru":["Требует ввода или описания пользователя изменения","Ограничен конвенцией именования в kebab-случае"],"ar":["يتطلب مدخلات أو وصف المستخدم للتغيير","محدود بالاتفاقية المسمى-WKEB-حالة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('kks0488/vibe-codex/vc-phase-loop', 'community', 'kks0488', 'vibe-codex', 'kks0488/vibe-codex', 'vc-phase-loop', 0, 0, 80, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.451Z', '2026-02-18T06:48:56.849Z', NULL, '{"id":"kks0488/vibe-codex/vc-phase-loop","name":"vc-phase-loop","description":{"zh":"VC 相位循环是一种快速、零配置的自主编码技术，兼容 Codex 和 OpenCode","ja":"VC フェーズ ループは、高速でゼロセットアップの自律コーディング技術であり、Codex および OpenCode との互換性を持つ","ko":"VC 상위 루프는 빠르고, 零 구성의 자율 코딩 기술이며, Codex 및 OpenCode 와의 호환성을 갖추고 있습니다","es":"El bucle de fase VC es una habilidad de codificación autónoma que ofrece loops rápidos y cero configuración, compatible con Codex y OpenCode","fr":"La boucle de phase VC est une compétence de codage autonome qui offre des boucles rapides et aucune configuration, compatible avec Codex et OpenCode","de":"Die VC-Phase-Schleife ist eine Fähigkeit für autonomes Coden, die schnelle Schleifen und keine Konfiguration bietet, kompatibel mit Codex und OpenCode","pt":"O vc-phase-loop é uma habilidade de codificação autônoma que permite laços rápidos e zero configuração, compatível com Codex e OpenCode.","ru":"Вc-phase-loop - это навык автономного кодирования, который позволяет использовать быстрые циклы и нулевую настройку, совместимый с Codex и OpenCode.","ar":"vc-phase-loop هو مهارة ترميز ذاتي يسمح بطرق معالجة سريعة وبدون إعداد، متوافق مع Codex و OpenCode.","en":"⚡ AI-first skills for autonomous coding. Fast loops, zero-setup, Codex & OpenCode compatible."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"VC 相位循环 - 自主编码加速","ja":"VC フェーズ ループ - 自律コーディングの究極形","ko":"VC 상위 루프 - 자율 코딩의 최종 버전","es":"Bucle de Fase VC - Edición Última","fr":"Boucle de Phase VC - Édition Ultime","de":"VC-Phase-Schleife - Ultimate Edition","pt":"vc-phase-loop: Desenvolvimento Autônomo de Código","ru":"vc-phase-loop: Автономное Кодирование","ar":"vc-phase-loop: الترميز الذاتي","en":"vc-phase-loop"},"description":{"zh":"VC 相位循环是一种快速、零配置的自主编码技术，兼容 Codex 和 OpenCode","ja":"VC フェーズ ループは、高速でゼロセットアップの自律コーディング技術であり、Codex および OpenCode との互換性を持つ","ko":"VC 상위 루프는 빠르고, 零 구성의 자율 코딩 기술이며, Codex 및 OpenCode 와의 호환성을 갖추고 있습니다","es":"El bucle de fase VC es una habilidad de codificación autónoma que ofrece loops rápidos y cero configuración, compatible con Codex y OpenCode","fr":"La boucle de phase VC est une compétence de codage autonome qui offre des boucles rapides et aucune configuration, compatible avec Codex et OpenCode","de":"Die VC-Phase-Schleife ist eine Fähigkeit für autonomes Coden, die schnelle Schleifen und keine Konfiguration bietet, kompatibel mit Codex und OpenCode","pt":"O vc-phase-loop é uma habilidade de codificação autônoma que permite laços rápidos e zero configuração, compatível com Codex e OpenCode.","ru":"Вc-phase-loop - это навык автономного кодирования, который позволяет использовать быстрые циклы и нулевую настройку, совместимый с Codex и OpenCode.","ar":"vc-phase-loop هو مهارة ترميز ذاتي يسمح بطرق معالجة سريعة وبدون إعداد، متوافق مع Codex و OpenCode.","en":"⚡ AI-first skills for autonomous coding. Fast loops, zero-setup, Codex & OpenCode compatible."},"definition":{"en":"⚡ AI-first skills for autonomous coding. Fast loops, zero-setup, Codex & OpenCode compatible."},"features":{"zh":["快速循环","零配置","兼容 Codex 和 OpenCode","自主编码","AI-first 技术","适用于自治编码"],"ja":["高速ループ","ゼロセットアップ","Codex および OpenCode との互換性","自律コーディング","AI-first 技術","自律コーディングに適している"],"ko":["빠른 루프","零 구성","Codex 및 OpenCode 와의 호환성","자율 코딩","AI-첫 번째 기술","자율 코딩에 적합"],"es":["Loops rápidos y autónomos","Cero configuración necesaria","Compatibilidad con Codex y OpenCode","Filosofía de codificación basada en el iron laws","Capacidad de adaptación y reintentos"],"fr":["Boucles rapides et autonomes","Aucune configuration nécessaire","Compatibilité avec Codex et OpenCode","Philosophie de codage basée sur les iron laws","Capacité d''adaptation et de réessais"],"de":["Schnelle und autonome Schleifen","Keine Konfiguration erforderlich","Kompatibilität mit Codex und OpenCode","Codierungsphilosophie basierend auf den iron laws","Fähigkeit zur Anpassung und Wiederholung"],"pt":["Laços rápidos para desenvolvimento autônomo","Zero configuração para iniciar o desenvolvimento","Compatível com Codex e OpenCode","Desenvolvimento de código autônomo","Melhoria da eficiência do desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Быстрые циклы для автономного развития","Нулевая настройка для начала разработки","Совместимый с Codex и OpenCode","Автономное развитие кода","Улучшение эффективности разработки"],"ar":["طرق معالجة سريعة للترميز الذاتي","بدون إعداد لبدء التطوير","متوافق مع Codex و OpenCode","الترميز الذاتي للكود","تحسين كفاءة التطوير"]},"keywords":{"zh":["VC 相位循环","自主编码","AI-first 技术","快速循环","零配置","Codex","OpenCode","自治编码"],"ja":["VC フェーズ ループ","自律コーディング","AI-first 技術","高速ループ","ゼロセットアップ","Codex","OpenCode","自律コーディング"],"ko":["VC 상위 루프","자율 코딩","AI-첫 번째 기술","빠른 루프","零 구성","Codex","OpenCode","자율 코딩"],"es":["bucle de fase vc","codificación autónoma","loops rápidos","cero configuración","codex","opencode","iron laws"],"fr":["boucle de phase vc","codage autonome","boucles rapides","aucune configuration","codex","opencode","iron laws"],"de":["vc-phase-schleife","autonomes coden","schnelle schleifen","keine konfiguration","codex","opencode","iron laws"],"pt":["desenvolvimento autônomo","codificação autônoma","laços rápidos","zero configuração","Codex","OpenCode","desenvolvimento de código","eficiência do desenvolvimento"],"ru":["автономное развитие","автономное кодирование","быстрые циклы","нулевая настройка","Codex","OpenCode","разработка кода","эффективность разработки"],"ar":["الترميز الذاتي","التطوير الذاتي","طرق معالجة سريعة","بدون إعداد","Codex","OpenCode","تطوير الكود","كفاءة التطوير"]}},"owner":"kks0488","repo":"vibe-codex","repoPath":"kks0488/vibe-codex","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.451Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"vc-phase-loop","description":"Ultimate autonomous execution engine. Plan → Execute → Test → Never Stop Until Done. Use when the user wants hands-off completion with no questions, automatic recovery from any failure, and proven results.","bodyPreview":"# VC Phase Loop - ULTIMATE EDITION\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    THE IRON LAWS                            │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                             │\n│  1. NEVER STOP UNTIL PROVEN DONE                            │\n│  2. NEVER ASK - DECIDE AND RECORD                           │\n│  3. NEVER FAIL - ADAPT AND RETRY","body":"# VC Phase Loop - ULTIMATE EDITION\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    THE IRON LAWS                            │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                             │\n│  1. NEVER STOP UNTIL PROVEN DONE                            │\n│  2. NEVER ASK - DECIDE AND RECORD                           │\n│  3. NEVER FAIL - ADAPT AND RETRY                            │\n│  4. NEVER FORGET - TRACK EVERYTHING                         │\n│  5. NEVER ASSUME DONE - VERIFY WITH EVIDENCE                │\n│                                                             │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step Zero: Work Document (MANDATORY)\n\n**BEFORE ANY WORK, create `.vc/work-{timestamp}.md`:**\n\n```markdown\n# Task: {description}\nStarted: {datetime}\nStatus: in_progress\n\n## Phases\n- [ ] Phase 1: {name}\n- [ ] Phase 2: {name}\n...\n\n## Assumptions Log\n| # | Decision | Rationale | Reversible |\n|---|----------|-----------|------------|\n\n## Error Log\n| # | Phase | Error | Attempted Fix | Result |\n|---|-------|-------|---------------|--------|\n\n## Completion Evidence\n{filled when verified complete}\n```\n\n**UPDATE THIS DOCUMENT AFTER EVERY ACTION.**\n\n---\n\n## VC Triggers\n\nActivate with any of these:\n- `vcf: <task>` - **SHORT AND POWERFUL** (recommended)\n- `use vcf: <task>` - equivalent explicit invocation (Codex may output this form)\n- \"vc finish\", \"finish it\", \"take it to the end\"\n- \"plan and execute\", \"hands off\"\n\n---\n\n## The Execution Engine\n\n### Phase Structure\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│              EXECUTION PIPELINE                             │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                             │\n│  STAGE 1: RECONNAISSANCE (Parallel if possible)             │\n│  ├─ Analyze requirements                                    │\n│  ├─ Find related code                                       │\n│  ├─ Identify risks                                          │\n│  └─ Duration: Until complete understanding                  │\n│                                                             │\n│  STAGE 2: PLANNING                                          │\n│  ├─ Create 10-phase plan (20 for large scope)               │\n│  ├─ Define success criteria per phase                       │\n│  ├─ Identify parallel opportunities                         │\n│  └─ Output: Phase list with checkboxes                      │\n│                                                             │\n│  STAGE 3: EXECUTION (Parallel where independent)            │\n│  ├─ Execute phases sequentially or in parallel              │\n│  ├─ On failure: SELF-HEAL (see below)                       │\n│  ├─ Record assumptions with rationale                       │\n│  └─ Update work document after each phase                   │\n│                                                             │\n│  STAGE 4: VERIFICATION                                      │\n│  ├─ Run ALL tests                                           │\n│  ├─ Verify each requirement with evidence                   │\n│  ├─ If fails: LOOP BACK (do not stop)                       │\n│  └─ Output: Completion proof                                │\n│                                                             │\n│  EXIT: ONLY when proven complete                            │\n│                                                             │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## Infinite Retry Engine\n\n**ON ANY FAILURE:**\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│              SELF-HEALING PROTOCOL                          │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                             │\n│  Attempt 1: Standard approach                               │\n│      ↓ FAIL?                                                │\n│  Attempt 2: Alternative method                              │\n│      ↓ FAIL?                                                │\n│  Attempt 3: Decompose into smaller tasks                    │\n│      ↓ FAIL?                                                │\n│  Attempt 4: Deep root cause analysis                        │\n│      ↓ FAIL?                                                │\n│  Attempt 5: Try 3 different approaches in parallel          │\n│      ↓ FAIL?                                                │\n│  Attempt 6: Research external solutions                     │\n│      ↓ FAIL?                                                │\n│  Attempt 7: Create workaround                               │\n│      ↓ FAIL?                                                │\n│  Attempt 8+: Hybrid approach combining all learnings        │\n│      ↓ CONTINUE INDEFINITELY                                │\n│                                                             │\n│  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════    │\n│  THE LOOP NEVER ENDS UNTIL SUCCESS                          │\n│  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════    │\n│                                                             │\n│  On EVERY failure:                                          │\n│  1. Log error with full context                             │\n│  2. Diagnose root cause                                     │\n│  3. Select new strategy                                     │\n│  4. Execute immediately                                     │\n│  5. Record lesson learned                                   │\n│                                                             │\n│  NEVER: Stop and wait for user                              │\n│  NEVER: Give up                                             │\n│  NEVER: Report failure without attempting fix               │\n│                                                             │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## Decision Policy\n\n### Automatic Decisions (No User Input)\n\nMake these decisions automatically and record in Assumptions Log:\n\n| Category | Default Choice | Record |\n|----------|----------------|--------|\n| Code style | Follow existing patterns | Brief note |\n| Library choice | Use what''s already in project | Brief note |\n| File location | Match existing structure | Brief note |\n| Naming | Follow conventions found | Brief note |\n| Error handling | Add try-catch where sensible | Brief note |\n| Testing | Add tests matching existing patterns | Brief note |\n\n### Hard Stops (PAUSE AND ASK)\n\nOnly pause for these HIGH-RISK scenarios:\n- Deleting more than 10 files\n- Modifying production database\n- Actions costing more than $10\n- Security credentials handling\n- Irreversible destructive operations\n\n**Everything else: DECIDE AND CONTINUE.**\n\n---\n\n## Test Discovery & Execution\n\n### Auto-Detection\n\n```\nPriority order:\n1. package.json scripts → npm/yarn/pnpm test\n2. Makefile → make test\n3. pytest.ini/pyproject.toml → pytest\n4. go.mod → go test ./...\n5. Cargo.toml → cargo test\n6. pom.xml → mvn test\n7. build.gradle → ./gradlew test\n8. *.csproj → dotnet test\n```\n\n### If No Tests Found\n\n```\n1. Check for any quality command (lint, typecheck, build)\n2. Run that instead\n3. Note gap: \"No tests found, ran lint/build instead\"\n4. Continue execution (do NOT stop)\n```\n\n### Test Failure Response\n\n```\nTest Failed\n    ↓\nAnalyze failure output\n    ↓\nIdentify root cause\n    ↓\nFix immediately\n    ↓\nRerun tests\n    ↓\nIf still failing: RETRY ENGINE (see above)\n    ↓\nNEVER stop on test failure\n```\n\n---\n\n## Parallelization Rules\n\n### Identify Parallel Opportunities\n\n```\nRULE: If two tasks have NO dependencies, run them in parallel.\n\nExample:\n  Phase 1: Create component A    ─┐\n  Phase 2: Create component B    ─┼─ PARALLEL\n  Phase 3: Create component C    ─┘\n  Phase 4: Integrate A+B+C         → SEQUENTIAL (depends on 1-3)\n  Phase 5: Add tests for A      ─┐\n  Phase 6: Add tests for B      ─┼─ PARALLEL\n  Phase 7: Add tests for C      ─┘\n```\n\n### Background Execution\n\nThese run in background while continuing:\n- `npm install`, `pip install`\n- `npm run build`, `cargo build`\n- Long-running compilations\n- Docker operations\n\n**Check results before depending on them.**\n\n---\n\n## Team Delegation Protocol\n\nWhen coordination overhead grows, use `vc-agent-teams` conventions with file mailboxes:\n\n1. Create team and members:\n   - `vc teams create --name <team>`\n   - `vc teams add-member --team <team> --name <agent>`\n2. Delegate scoped work via direct messages:\n   - `vc teams send --team <team> --type message --from team-lead --recipient <agent> --content \\\"<task>\\\"`\n3. Use broadcast only for milestone updates:\n   - `vc teams send --team <team> --type broadcast --from team-lead --content \\\"<status>\\\"`\n4. Process mailbox responses and mark them read to avoid duplicate execution.\n5. Prune old read traffic periodically:\n   - `vc teams prune --team <team> --days 7`\n\nProtocol message types:\n- `message`\n- `broadcast`\n- `shutdown_request`\n- `shutdown_response`\n- `plan_approval_response`\n\n---\n\n## Sub-Agents (Collaboration Tools)\n\nModern Codex can spawn sub-agents. Use them to **speed up independent work** (recon, analysis, testing), then merge results into a single execution thread.\n\n### When to Spawn Sub-Agents\n\nUse sub-agents when you have **2+ independent threads** such as:\n- Repo reconnaissance (find files, map architecture, identify owners)\n- Documentation lookup / API surface verification\n- Running tests + collecting failure analysis\n- Exploring alternative implementations in parallel\n\n### Sub-Agent Rules (Hard)\n\n- **Max 4 sub-agents** (Codex may cap at 6; stay below it).\n- Each sub-agent gets **one narrow goal** and a **strict deliverable format**.\n- Prefer **read-only** tasks for sub-agents; the main agent owns all writes/patches to avoid conflicts.\n- Keep collaboration depth at **1**: sub-agents should not spawn more agents.\n- If a sub-agent can’t run tools (or `spawn_agent` isn’t available), **fallback to sequential**.\n- Always `close_agent` after harvesting results to avoid resource leaks.\n\n### Agent Role Presets (Recommended)\n\nIf supported, use role presets to make sub-agent behavior more predictable:\n- `explorer`: repo reconnaissance (file map, configs, constraints). **Read-only**.\n- `worker`: testing, repro, alternative approach sketches. Prefer **read-only** unless explicitly told to modify.\n- `default`: general-purpose.\n\n### Dispatch Protocol (Tooling)\n\n1. `spawn_agent` for each independent thread (use `explorer` for recon and `worker` for testing when supported).\n2. Provide:\n   - Goal (1 sentence)\n   - Scope boundaries (what to touch / not touch)\n   - Required output format (bullets/table)\n   - Stop condition (when to reply)\n3. `wait` for results (with timeouts), then `send_input` follow-ups if needed (use `interrupt` to stop/retask a long-running agent).\n4. Integrate outputs into:\n   - Work doc (Phases / Assumptions / Error Log)\n   - A single consolidated plan (main agent)\n5. `close_agent` for each sub-agent.\n\n### Output Format (Required)\n\nEvery sub-agent response must start with:\n- `SUMMARY:` (≤5 bullets)\n- `FINDINGS:` (facts + file paths/commands)\n- `RISKS:` (what could go wrong)\n- `RECOMMENDATION:` (next action)\n\n---\n\n## Completion Proof (REQUIRED)\n\n**Before declaring done, you MUST provide:**\n\n```markdown\n## COMPLETION PROOF\n\n✓ Executed:\n  Command: {actual command}\n  Output: {actual output pasted}\n\n✓ Tests:\n  Command: {test command}\n  Result: {X passed, Y failed}\n\n✓ Requirements Verified:\n  - [Req 1]: {file}:{line} - {evidence}\n  - [Req 2]: {file}:{line} - {evidence}\n\n✓ Quality Checks:\n  - Build: PASS\n  - Lint: PASS (or N errors fixed)\n  - Types: PASS\n\n✓ Work Document: All boxes checked\n```\n\n### Forbidden Completion Phrases\n\nIf you say these, **YOU HAVE NOT COMPLETED**:\n- \"I think it''s done\" → NOT DONE\n- \"Should work\" → NOT DONE\n- \"Looks correct\" → NOT DONE\n- \"I believe\" → NOT DONE\n- \"Probably\" → NOT DONE\n\n**Certainty required. Evidence required.**\n\n---\n\n## Context Management\n\n### For Long Tasks\n\nWhen approaching context limits:\n1. Checkpoint: Update work document with current state\n2. Compress: Summarize completed phases briefly\n3. Focus: Keep only current phase details in context\n4. Reference: Point to work document for history\n\n### Resumption Protocol\n\nIf interrupted:\n1. Read `.vc/work-*.md` to restore state\n2. Find first unchecked item\n3. Continue from there\n4. No re-explanation needed\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\nUse these sections in order:\n\n```markdown\n# Execution Report\n\n## Plan\n{10-20 phases with checkboxes}\n\n## Progress\n{Phase-by-phase execution with timestamps}\n\n## Assumptions\n{Table of decisions made}\n\n## Tests\n{Test execution results}\n\n## Completion Proof\n{Evidence as specified above}\n```\n\n---\n\n## The VC Promise\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                                             │\n│   YOU SET THE GOAL.                                         │\n│                                                             │\n│   WE PLAN IT.                                               │\n│   WE EXECUTE IT.                                            │\n│   WE FIX WHATEVER BREAKS.                                   │\n│   WE RETRY UNTIL SUCCESS.                                   │\n│   WE PROVE IT WORKS.                                        │\n│                                                             │\n│   NO QUESTIONS. NO EXCUSES. NO STOPPING.                    │\n│                                                             │\n│   UNTIL IT''S DONE.                                          │\n│   ACTUALLY DONE.                                            │\n│   PROVEN DONE.                                              │\n│                                                             │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:48:56.849Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for autonomous coding agents requiring relentless iteration and zero-setup execution.","zh":"非常适合需要无休止迭代和零设置执行的自主编码代理。","ja":"リレントレスなイテレーションとゼロセットアップの実行が必要な自律的なコーディングエージェントに最適です。","ko":"영한 설정 실행과 끊임없는 반복이 필요한 자율 코딩 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de codificación autónomos que requieren iteración incansable y ejecución sin configuración.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de codage autonomes nécessitant une itération sans relâche et une exécution sans configuration.","de":"Perfekt für autarke Codierungsagenten, die eine unermüdliche Iteration und eine Null-Konfigurationsausführung erfordern.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes de codificação autônoma que exigem iteração implacável e execução sem configuração.","ru":"Идеально подходит для автономных агентов 