 구조와 성능을 최적화하기 위한 방법입니다","es":"MoonBit Refactoring es una habilidad que mejora el código preservando el comportamiento y minimizando la API pública.","fr":"MoonBit Refactoring est une compétence qui améliore le code en préservant le comportement et en minimisant l''API publique.","de":"MoonBit-Refactoring ist eine Fähigkeit, die den Code verbessert, indem sie das Verhalten bewahrt und die öffentliche API minimiert.","pt":"A refatoração MoonBit é uma habilidade que visa melhorar a eficiência e legibilidade do código, minimizando a API pública e preferindo um estilo declarativo","ru":"Рефакторинг MoonBit — это навык, направленный на улучшение эффективности и читаемости кода, минимизируя публичный API и предпочитая декларативный стиль","ar":"إعادة هيكلة MoonBit هي مهارة تهدف إلى تحسين كفاءة وقابلية قراءة الكود، وتقليل واجهة برمجة التطبيقات العامة وتفضيل نمط إعلاني","en":"port from shiguredo/http11-rs"},"definition":{"en":"port from shiguredo/http11-rs"},"features":{"zh":["优化代码结构","提高性能","减少公共API","使用声明式风格","添加测试和文档"],"ja":["コード構造の最適化","パフォーマンスの向上","公開APIの削減","宣言的スタイルの使用","テストとドキュメントの追加"],"ko":["코드 구조 최적화","성능 향상","공개 API 감소","선언적 스타일 사용","테스트 및 문서 추가"],"es":["Preserva el comportamiento y los contratos públicos","Minimiza la API pública","Preferencia por estilo declarativo y coincidencia de patrones","Uso de tipos de vista para evitar copias","Agrega pruebas y documentación junto con refactorizaciones"],"fr":["Préserve le comportement et les contrats publics","Minimise l''API publique","Préférence pour le style déclaratif et la correspondance de modèles","Utilisation de types de vue pour éviter les copies","Ajoute des tests et de la documentation avec les refactorisations"],"de":["Bewahrt das Verhalten und die öffentlichen Verträge","Minimiert die öffentliche API","Bevorzugt deklarativem Stil und Mustermatching","Verwendung von View-Typen, um Kopien zu vermeiden","Fügt Tests und Dokumentationen hinzu, wenn es um Refactorings geht"],"pt":["Preservação do comportamento e contratos públicos","Minimização da API pública","Preferência por estilo declarativo","Uso de tipos de visualização para evitar cópias","Adição de testes e documentação"],"ru":["Сохранение поведения и публичных контрактов","Минимизация публичного API","Предпочтение декларативному стилю","Использование типов представления для избежания копий","Добавление тестов и документации"],"ar":["الحفاظ على السلوك والاتفاقيات العامة","تقليل واجهة برمجة التطبيقات العامة","التفضيل لنمط إعلاني","استخدام أنواع العرض لتجنب النسخ","إضافة الاختبارات والوثائق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["MoonBit重构","代码优化","性能提升","公共API","声明式风格","测试和文档"],"ja":["MoonBitリファクタリング","コード最適化","パフォーマンス向上","公開API","宣言的スタイル","テストとドキュメント"],"ko":["MoonBit 리팩토링","코드 최적화","성능 향상","공개 API","선언적 스타일","테스트 및 문서"],"es":["refactorización de código","mejora del código","preservar comportamiento","minimizar API pública","estilo declarativo","coincidencia de patrones","tipos de vista"],"fr":["refactoring de code","amélioration du code","préserver le comportement","minimiser l''API publique","style déclaratif","correspondance de modèles","types de vue"],"de":["Code-Refactoring","Code-Optimierung","Verhalten bewahren","öffentliche API minimieren","deklarative Programmierung","Mustermatching","View-Typen"],"pt":["refatoração de código","otimização de código","desenvolvimento de software","programação","legibilidade de código","eficiência de código"],"ru":["рефакторинг кода","оптимизация кода","разработка программного обеспечения","программирование","читаемость кода","эффективность кода"],"ar":["إعادة هيكلة الكود","تحسين الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","البرمجة","قابلية قراءة الكود","كفاءة الكود"]}},"owner":"f4ah6o","repo":"http11.mbt","repoPath":"f4ah6o/http11.mbt","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.451Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"moonbit-refactoring","description":"Refactor MoonBit code to be idiomatic: shrink public APIs, convert functions to methods, use pattern matching with views, add loop invariants, and ensure test coverage without regressions. Use when updating MoonBit packages or refactoring MoonBit APIs, modules, or tests.","bodyPreview":"# MoonBit Refactoring Skill\n\n## Intent\n- Preserve behavior and public contracts unless explicitly changed.\n- Minimize the public API to what callers require.\n- Prefer declarative style and pattern matching over incidental mutation.\n- Use view types (ArrayView/StringView/BytesView) to avoid copies.\n- Add tests and docs alongside refactors.\n\n## Workflow\n**Start broad, then refine locally:**\n\n1. **Architecture first**: Review package structure, dependencies, and API boundaries.\n2. **Inventory** pub","body":"# MoonBit Refactoring Skill\n\n## Intent\n- Preserve behavior and public contracts unless explicitly changed.\n- Minimize the public API to what callers require.\n- Prefer declarative style and pattern matching over incidental mutation.\n- Use view types (ArrayView/StringView/BytesView) to avoid copies.\n- Add tests and docs alongside refactors.\n\n## Workflow\n**Start broad, then refine locally:**\n\n1. **Architecture first**: Review package structure, dependencies, and API boundaries.\n2. **Inventory** public APIs and call sites (`moon doc`, `moon ide find-references`).\n3. **Pick one refactor theme** (API minimization, package splits, pattern matching, loop style).\n4. **Apply the smallest safe change**.\n5. **Update docs/tests** in the same patch.\n6. **Run `moon check`, then `moon test`**.\n7. **Use coverage** to target missing branches.\n\nAvoid local cleanups (renaming, pattern matching) until the high-level structure is sound.\n\n## Improve Package Architecture\n- Keep packages focused: aim for <10k lines per package.\n- Keep files manageable: aim for <2k lines per file.\n- Keep functions focused: aim for <200 lines per function.\n\n### Splitting Files\nTreat files in MoonBit as organizational units; move code freely within a package as long as each file stays focused on one concept.\n\n### Splitting Packages\nWhen spinning off package `A` into `A` and `B`:\n\n1. Create the new package and re-export temporarily:\n   ```mbt\n   // In package B\n   using @A { ... }  // re-export A''s APIs\n   ```\n   Ensure `moon check` passes before proceeding.\n\n2. Find and update all call sites:\n   ```bash\n   moon ide find-references <symbol>\n   ```\n   Replace bare `f` with `@B.f`.\n\n3. Remove the `use` statement once all call sites are updated.\n\n4. Audit and remove newly-unused `pub` APIs from both packages.\n\n### Guidelines\n- Prefer acyclic dependencies: lower-level packages should not import higher-level ones.\n- Only expose what downstream packages actually need.\n- Consider an `internal/` package for helpers that shouldn''t leak.\n\n## Minimize Public API and Modularize\n- Remove `pub` from helpers; keep only required exports.\n- Move helpers into `internal/` packages to block external imports.\n- Split large files by feature; files do not define modules in MoonBit.\n\n## Local refactoring\n\n### Convert Free Functions to Methods + Chaining\n- Move behavior onto the owning type for discoverability.\n- Use `..` for fluent, mutating chains when it reads clearly.\n\nExample:\n```mbt nocheck\n// Before\nfn reader_next(r : Reader) -> Char? { ... }\nlet ch = reader_next(r)\n\n// After\nfn Reader::next(self : Reader) -> Char? { ... }\nlet ch = r.next()\n```\n\nExample (chaining):\n```mbt nocheck\nbuf..write_string(\"#\\\\\")..write_char(ch)\n```\n\n### Prefer Explicit Qualification\n- Use `@pkg.fn` instead of `using` when clarity matters.\n- Keep call sites explicit during wide refactors.\n\nExample:\n```mbt nocheck\nlet n = @parser.parse_number(token)\n```\n\n### Simplify Enum Constructors When Type Is Known\n\nWhen the expected type is known from context, you can omit the full package path for enum constructors:\n\n- **Pattern matching**: Annotate the matched value; constructors need no path.\n- **Nested constructors**: Only the outermost needs the full path.\n- **Return values**: The return type provides context for constructors in the body.\n- **Collections**: Type-annotate the collection; elements inherit the type.\n\nExamples:\n```mbt\n// Pattern matching - annotate the value being matched\nlet tree : @pkga.Tree = ...\nmatch tree {\n  Leaf(x) => x\n  Node(left~, x, right~) => left.sum() + x + right.sum()\n}\n\n// Nested constructors - only outer needs full path\nlet x = @pkga.Tree::Node(left=Leaf(1), x=2, right=Leaf(3))\n\n// Return type provides context\nfn make_tree() -> @pkga.Tree {\n  Node(left=Leaf(1), x=2, right=Leaf(3))\n}\n\n// Collections - type annotation on the array\nlet trees : Array[@pkga.Tree] = [Leaf(1), Node(left=Leaf(2), x=3, right=Leaf(4))]\n```\n\n### Pattern Matching and Views\n- Pattern match arrays directly; the compiler inserts ArrayView implicitly.\n- Use `..` in the middle to match prefix and suffix at once.\n- Pattern match strings directly; avoid converting to `Array[Char]`.\n- `String`/`StringView` indexing yields `UInt16` code units. Use `for ch in s` for Unicode-aware iteration.\n\n#### we prefer pattern matching over small functions\n\nFor example,\n```mbt\n match gen_results.get(0) {\n   Some(value) => Iter::singleton(value)\n   None => Iter::empty()\n }\n```\nWe can pattern match directly, it is more efficient and as readable:\n```mbt\n match gen_results {\n   [value, ..] => Iter::singleton(value)\n   [] => Iter::empty()\n }\n```\nMoonBit pattern matching is pretty expressive, here are some more examples:\n```mbt\nmatch items {\n  [] => ()\n  [head, ..tail] => handle(head, tail)\n  [..prefix, mid, ..suffix] => handle_mid(prefix, mid, suffix)\n}\n```\n\n```mbt\nmatch s {\n  \"\" => ()\n  [..\"let\", ..rest] => handle_let(rest)\n  _ => ()\n}\n```\n#### Char literal matching\n\nUse char literal overloading for `Char`, `UInt16`, and `Int`; the examples below rely on it. This is handy when matching `String` indexing results (`UInt16`) against a char range.\n```mbt\ntest {\n  let a_int : Int = ''b''\n  if (a_int is ''a''..<''z'') { () } else { () }\n  let a_u16 : UInt16 = ''b''\n  if (a_u16 is ''a''..<''z'') { () } else { () }\n  let a_char : Char = ''b''\n  if (a_char is ''a''..<''z'') { () } else { () }\n}\n```\n\n#### Use Nested Patterns and `is`\n\n- Use `is` patterns inside `if`/`guard` to keep branches concise.\n\nExample:\n```mbt\nmatch token {\n  Some(Ident([..\"@\", ..rest])) if process(rest) is Some(x) => handle_at(rest)\n  Some(Ident(name)) => handle_ident(name)\n  None => ()\n}\n```\n\n#### Prefer Range Loops for Simple Indexing\n- Use `for i in start..<end { ... }`, `for i in start..<=end { ... }`, `for i in large>..small`, or `for i in large>=..small` for simple index loops.\n- Keep functional-state `for` loops for algorithms that update state.\n\nExample:\n```mbt\n// Before\nfor i = 0; i < len; {\n  items.push(fill)\n  continue i + 1\n}\n\n// After\nfor i in 0..<len {\n  items.push(fill)\n}\n```\n\n## Loop Specs (Dafny-Style Comments)\n- Add specs for functional-state loops.\n- Skip invariants for simple `for x in xs` loops.\n- Add TODO when a decreases clause is unclear (possible bug).\n\nExample:\n```mbt\nfor i = 0, acc = 0; i < xs.length(); {\n  acc = acc + xs[i]\n  i = i + 1\n} else { acc }\nwhere {\n  invariant: 0 <= i <= xs.length(),\n  reasoning: (\n    #| ... rigorous explanation ...\n    #| ...\n  )\n}\n```\n\n\n### Tests and Docs\n- Prefer black-box tests in `*_test.mbt` or `*.mbt.md`.\n- Add docstring tests with `mbt check` for public APIs.\n\nExample:\n```mbt\n///|\n/// Return the last element of a non-empty array.\n///\n/// # Example\n/// ```mbt check\n/// test {\n///   inspect(last([1, 2, 3]), content=\"3\")\n/// }\n/// ```\npub fn last(xs : Array[Int]) -> Int { ... }\n```\n\n## Coverage-Driven Refactors\n- Use coverage to target missing branches through public APIs.\n- Prefer small, focused tests over white-box checks.\n\nCommands:\n```bash\nmoon coverage analyze -- -f summary\nmoon coverage analyze -- -f caret -F path/to/file.mbt\n```\n\n## Moon IDE Commands\n\n```bash\nmoon doc \"<query>\"\nmoon ide outline <dir|file>\nmoon ide find-references <symbol>\nmoon ide peek-def <symbol>\nmoon ide rename <symbol> -new-name <new_name>\nmoon check\nmoon test\nmoon info\n```\nUse these commands for reliable refactoring.\n\nExample: spinning off `package_b` from `package_a`.\n\nTemporary import in `package_b`:\n```mbt\nusing @package_a { a, type B }\n```\n\nSteps:\n1. Use `moon ide find-references <symbol>` to find all call sites of `a` and `B`.\n2. Replace them with `@package_a.a` and `@package_a.B`.\n3. Remove the `using` statement and run `moon check`.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:51:56.869Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Refactoring Agents needing to preserve behavior and minimize public API in Rust-based projects like shiguredo/http11-rs","zh":"非常适合需要保留行为并最小化公共 API 的 Rust 代码重构代理，尤其适用于像 shiguredo/http11-rs 的 Rust 基础项目","ja":"Rustベースのプロジェクト（例：shiguredo/http11-rs）で動作を保持し、パブリックAPIを最小限に抑えるコードリファクタリングエージェントに最適","ko":"행위는 유지하면서公共 API를 최소화하는 코드 리팩토링 에이전트에게 적합하며, 특히 shiguredo/http11-rs와 같은 Rust 기반 프로젝트에 적합합니다","es":"Perfecto para agentes de refactorización de código que necesitan preservar el comportamiento y minimizar la API pública en proyectos basados en Rust como shiguredo/http11-rs","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de refactoring de code nécessitant de préserver le comportement et de minimiser l''API publique dans des projets basés sur Rust tels que shiguredo/http11-rs","de":"Perfekt für Code-Refactoring-Agents, die das Verhalten erhalten und die öffentliche API in Rust-basierten Projekten wie shiguredo/http11-rs minimieren müssen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Refatoração de Código que precisam preservar o comportamento e minimizar a API pública em projetos baseados em Rust, como shiguredo/http11-rs","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов рефакторинга кода, которым необходимо сохранить поведение и минимизировать публичный API в проектах на основе Rust, таких как shiguredo/http11-rs","ar":"مثالي لعمليات إعادة هيكلة الكود التي تحتاج إلى الحفاظ على السلوك وتقليل واجهة برمجة التطبيقات العامة في مشاريع تستند إلى روست مثل shiguredo/http11-rs"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to refactor code using declarative style and pattern matching, while utilizing view types like ArrayView, StringView, and BytesView to avoid copies, and ensuring tests and documentation are updated alongside refactors using protocols like HTTP/1.1","zh":"赋予代理使用声明式风格和模式匹配来重构代码的能力，同时利用像 ArrayView、StringView 和 BytesView 这样的视图类型来避免副本，并确保在重构过程中使用像 HTTP/1.1 这样的协议来更新测试和文档","ja":"エージェントが宣言的なスタイルとパターンマッチングを使用してコードをリファクタリングする能力を提供し、ArrayView、StringView、BytesView などのビュータイプを使用してコピーを避け、HTTP/1.1などのプロトコルを使用してリファクタリングとともにテストとドキュメントを更新する","ko":"에이전트가 선언적 스타일과 패턴 매칭을 사용하여 코드를 리팩토링할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, ArrayView, StringView 및 BytesView와 같은 뷰 타입을 사용하여 복사본을 피하고, HTTP/1.1과 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 리팩토링과 함께 테스트 및 문서를 업데이트합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a refactorizar el código utilizando un estilo declarativo y coincidencia de patrones, mientras utiliza tipos de vista como ArrayView, StringView y BytesView para evitar copias, y asegurando que las pruebas y la documentación se actualicen junto con los refactors utilizando protocolos como HTTP/1.1","fr":"Permet aux agents de refactoriser le code en utilisant un style déclaratif et la correspondance de modèles, tout en utilisant des types de vue tels que ArrayView, StringView et BytesView pour éviter les copies, et en s''assurant que les tests et la documentation soient mis à jour en parallèle avec les refactors en utilisant des protocoles comme HTTP/1.1","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Code mithilfe eines deklarativen Stils und Mustervergleichs zu refactorisieren, während Typen wie ArrayView, StringView und BytesView verwendet werden, um Kopien zu vermeiden, und sicherzustellen, dass Tests und Dokumentation zusammen mit den Refactors mithilfe von Protokollen wie HTTP/1.1 aktualisiert werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a refatorar o código usando estilo declarativo e correspondência de padrões, utilizando tipos de exibição como ArrayView, StringView e BytesView para evitar cópias, e garantindo que os testes e a documentação sejam atualizados junto com as refatorações usando protocolos como HTTP/1.1","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью рефакторинга кода с использованием декларативного стиля и сопоставления с образцом, используя типы представления, такие как ArrayView, StringView и BytesView, для избежания копирования, и гарантируя, что тесты и документация обновляются вместе с рефакторингом с использованием протоколов, таких как HTTP/1.1","ar":"تمكّن الوكالات من إعادة هيكلة الكود باستخدام أسلوب إعلاني وتماثل الأنماط، واستخدام أنواع العرض مثل ArrayView وStringView وBytesView لتجنب النسخ، وضمان تحديث الاختبارات والتوثيق جنبًا إلى جنب مع إعادة الهيكلة باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل HTTP/1.1"},"useCases":{"en":["Refactoring Rust codebases to improve performance and readability","Minimizing public API for dependencies like http11-rs","Implementing declarative programming principles in existing codebases"],"zh":["重构 Rust 代码库以提高性能和可读性","最小化 http11-rs 等依赖项的公共 API","在现有代码库中实现声明式编程原则"],"ja":["パフォーマンスと可読性を向上させるためにRustコードベースをリファクタリングする","http11-rsなどの依存関係のパブリックAPIを最小限に抑える","既存のコードベースで宣言的なプログラミング原則を実装する"],"ko":["성능과 가독성을 향상시키기 위해 Rust 코드베이스를 리팩토링하는 것","http11-rs와 같은 의존성의 공개 API를 최소화하는 것","기존 코드베이스에서 선언적 프로그래밍 원칙을 구현하는 것"],"es":["Refactorización de bases de código de Rust para mejorar el rendimiento y la legibilidad","Minimización de la API pública para dependencias como http11-rs","Implementación de principios de programación declarativa en bases de código existentes"],"fr":["Refactoring de bases de code Rust pour améliorer les performances et la lisibilité","Minimisation de l''API publique pour des dépendances comme http11-rs","Mise en œuvre de principes de programmation déclarative dans des bases de code existantes"],"de":["Refactoring von Rust-Codebasen zur Verbesserung der Leistung und Lesbarkeit","Minimierung der öffentliche