енежных потоков","Планирование сценариев","Анализ рынка"],"ar":["توقعات الإيرادات","هيكل التكاليف","تحليل التدفق النقدي","تخطيط السيناريوهات","تحليل السوق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["初创金融模型","财务预测","收入预测","现金流分析","场景规划","综合财务分析","AI驱动的财务模型"],"ja":["スタートアップ財務モデル","財務予測","収入予測","キャッシュフロー分析","シナリオプランニング","包括的な財務分析","AI駆動の財務モデル"],"ko":["스타트업 재무 모델","재무 예측","수익 예측","현금 흐름 분석","시나리오 계획","포괄적인 재무 분석","AI 기반 재무 모델"],"es":["modelado financiero","startups","proyecciones de ingresos","análisis de flujo de caja","planificación de escenarios","modelado financiero para startups","creación de modelos financieros","predicción del rendimiento financiero"],"fr":["modélisation financière","startups","projections de revenus","analyse de flux de trésorerie","planification de scénarios","modélisation financière pour les startups","création de modèles financiers","prédiction des performances financières"],"de":["Finanzmodellierung","Startups","Umsatzprognosen","Cash-Flow-Analyse","Szenario-Planung","Finanzmodellierung für Startups","Erstellung von Finanzmodellen","Vorhersage der finanziellen Leistung"],"pt":["modelagem financeira de startup","previsões de receita","estruturas de custos","análise de fluxo de caixa","planejamento de cenários","análise de mercado","finanças de startup"],"ru":["финансовое моделирование стартапа","прогнозы доходов","структура затрат","анализ денежных потоков","планирование сценариев","анализ рынка","финансы стартапа"],"ar":["نمذجة مالية للاستارتيب","توقعات الإيرادات","هيكل التكاليف","تحليل التدفق النقدي","تخطيط السيناريوهات","تحليل السوق","المالية للاستارتيب"]}},"owner":"ANcpLua","repo":"qyl","repoPath":"ANcpLua/qyl","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.452Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"startup-financial-modeling","description":"|","bodyPreview":"## Source Metadata\n\n```yaml\nfrontmatter:\n  version: 1.0.0\nplugin:\n  name: \"startup-business-analyst\"\n  description: \"Comprehensive startup business analysis with market sizing (TAM/SAM/SOM), financial modeling, team planning, and strategic research\"\n  author:\n    name: \"Seth Hobson\"\n    email: \"seth@major7apps.com\"\n```\n\n\n# Startup Financial Modeling\n\nBuild comprehensive 3-5 year financial models with revenue projections, cost structures, cash flow analysis, and scenario planning for early-stage","body":"## Source Metadata\n\n```yaml\nfrontmatter:\n  version: 1.0.0\nplugin:\n  name: \"startup-business-analyst\"\n  description: \"Comprehensive startup business analysis with market sizing (TAM/SAM/SOM), financial modeling, team planning, and strategic research\"\n  author:\n    name: \"Seth Hobson\"\n    email: \"seth@major7apps.com\"\n```\n\n\n# Startup Financial Modeling\n\nBuild comprehensive 3-5 year financial models with revenue projections, cost structures, cash flow analysis, and scenario planning for early-stage startups.\n\n## Overview\n\nFinancial modeling provides the quantitative foundation for startup strategy, fundraising, and operational planning. Create realistic projections using cohort-based revenue modeling, detailed cost structures, and scenario analysis to support decision-making and investor presentations.\n\n## Core Components\n\n### Revenue Model\n\n**Cohort-Based Projections:**\nBuild revenue from customer acquisition and retention by cohort.\n\n**Formula:**\n\n```\nMRR = Σ (Cohort Size × Retention Rate × ARPU)\nARR = MRR × 12\n```\n\n**Key Inputs:**\n\n- Monthly new customer acquisitions\n- Customer retention rates by month\n- Average revenue per user (ARPU)\n- Pricing and packaging assumptions\n- Expansion revenue (upsells, cross-sells)\n\n### Cost Structure\n\n**Operating Expenses Categories:**\n\n1. **Cost of Goods Sold (COGS)**\n   - Hosting and infrastructure\n   - Payment processing fees\n   - Customer support (variable portion)\n   - Third-party services per customer\n\n2. **Sales & Marketing (S&M)**\n   - Customer acquisition cost (CAC)\n   - Marketing programs and advertising\n   - Sales team compensation\n   - Marketing tools and software\n\n3. **Research & Development (R&D)**\n   - Engineering team compensation\n   - Product management\n   - Design and UX\n   - Development tools and infrastructure\n\n4. **General & Administrative (G&A)**\n   - Executive team\n   - Finance, legal, HR\n   - Office and facilities\n   - Insurance and compliance\n\n### Cash Flow Analysis\n\n**Components:**\n\n- Beginning cash balance\n- Cash inflows (revenue, fundraising)\n- Cash outflows (operating expenses, CapEx)\n- Ending cash balance\n- Monthly burn rate\n- Runway (months of cash remaining)\n\n**Formula:**\n\n```\nRunway = Current Cash Balance / Monthly Burn Rate\nMonthly Burn = Monthly Revenue - Monthly Expenses\n```\n\n### Headcount Planning\n\n**Role-Based Hiring Plan:**\nTrack headcount by department and role.\n\n**Key Metrics:**\n\n- Fully-loaded cost per employee\n- Revenue per employee\n- Headcount by department (% of total)\n\n**Typical Ratios (Early-Stage SaaS):**\n\n- Engineering: 40-50%\n- Sales & Marketing: 25-35%\n- G&A: 10-15%\n- Customer Success: 5-10%\n\n## Financial Model Structure\n\n### Three-Scenario Framework\n\n**Conservative Scenario (P10):**\n\n- Slower customer acquisition\n- Lower pricing or conversion\n- Higher churn rates\n- Extended sales cycles\n- Used for cash management\n\n**Base Scenario (P50):**\n\n- Most likely outcomes\n- Realistic assumptions\n- Primary planning scenario\n- Used for board reporting\n\n**Optimistic Scenario (P90):**\n\n- Faster growth\n- Better unit economics\n- Lower churn\n- Used for upside planning\n\n### Time Horizon\n\n**Detailed Projections: 3 Years**\n\n- Monthly detail for Year 1\n- Monthly detail for Year 2\n- Quarterly detail for Year 3\n\n**High-Level Projections: Years 4-5**\n\n- Annual projections\n- Key metrics only\n- Support long-term planning\n\n## Step-by-Step Process\n\n### Step 1: Define Business Model\n\nClarify revenue model and pricing.\n\n**SaaS Model:**\n\n- Subscription pricing tiers\n- Annual vs. monthly contracts\n- Free trial or freemium approach\n- Expansion revenue strategy\n\n**Marketplace Model:**\n\n- GMV projections\n- Take rate (% of transactions)\n- Buyer and seller economics\n- Transaction frequency\n\n**Transactional Model:**\n\n- Transaction volume\n- Revenue per transaction\n- Frequency and seasonality\n\n### Step 2: Build Revenue Projections\n\nUse cohort-based methodology for accuracy.\n\n**Monthly Customer Acquisition:**\nDefine new customers acquired each month.\n\n**Retention Curve:**\nModel customer retention over time.\n\n**Typical SaaS Retention:**\n\n- Month 1: 100%\n- Month 3: 90%\n- Month 6: 85%\n- Month 12: 75%\n- Month 24: 70%\n\n**Revenue Calculation:**\nFor each cohort, calculate retained customers × ARPU for each month.\n\n### Step 3: Model Cost Structure\n\nBreak down costs by category and behavior.\n\n**Fixed vs. Variable:**\n\n- Fixed: Salaries, software, rent\n- Variable: Hosting, payment processing, support\n\n**Scaling Assumptions:**\n\n- COGS as % of revenue\n- S&M as % of revenue (CAC payback)\n- R&D growth rate\n- G&A as % of total expenses\n\n### Step 4: Create Hiring Plan\n\nModel headcount growth by role and department.\n\n**Inputs:**\n\n- Starting headcount\n- Hiring velocity by role\n- Fully-loaded compensation by role\n- Benefits and taxes (typically 1.3-1.4x salary)\n\n**Example:**\n\n```\nEngineer: $150K salary × 1.35 = $202K fully-loaded\nSales Rep: $100K OTE × 1.30 = $130K fully-loaded\n```\n\n### Step 5: Project Cash Flow\n\nCalculate monthly cash position and runway.\n\n**Monthly Cash Flow:**\n\n```\nBeginning Cash\n+ Revenue Collected (consider payment terms)\n- Operating Expenses Paid\n- CapEx\n= Ending Cash\n```\n\n**Runway Calculation:**\n\n```\nIf Ending Cash < 0:\n  Funding Need = Negative Cash Balance\n  Runway = 0\nElse:\n  Runway = Ending Cash / Average Monthly Burn\n```\n\n### Step 6: Calculate Key Metrics\n\nTrack metrics that matter for stage.\n\n**Revenue Metrics:**\n\n- MRR / ARR\n- Growth rate (MoM, YoY)\n- Revenue by segment or cohort\n\n**Unit Economics:**\n\n- CAC (Customer Acquisition Cost)\n- LTV (Lifetime Value)\n- CAC Payback Period\n- LTV / CAC Ratio\n\n**Efficiency Metrics:**\n\n- Burn multiple (Net Burn / Net New ARR)\n- Magic number (Net New ARR / S&M Spend)\n- Rule of 40 (Growth % + Profit Margin %)\n\n**Cash Metrics:**\n\n- Monthly burn rate\n- Runway (months)\n- Cash efficiency\n\n### Step 7: Scenario Analysis\n\nCreate three scenarios with different assumptions.\n\n**Variable Assumptions:**\n\n- Customer acquisition rate (±30%)\n- Churn rate (±20%)\n- Average contract value (±15%)\n- CAC (±25%)\n\n**Fixed Assumptions:**\n\n- Pricing structure\n- Core operating expenses\n- Hiring plan (adjust timing, not roles)\n\n## Business Model Templates\n\n### SaaS Financial Model\n\n**Revenue Drivers:**\n\n- New MRR (customers × ARPU)\n- Expansion MRR (upsells)\n- Contraction MRR (downgrades)\n- Churned MRR (lost customers)\n\n**Key Ratios:**\n\n- Gross margin: 75-85%\n- S&M as % revenue: 40-60% (early stage)\n- CAC payback: < 12 months\n- Net retention: 100-120%\n\n**Example Projection:**\n\n```\nYear 1: $500K ARR, 50 customers, $100K MRR by Dec\nYear 2: $2.5M ARR, 200 customers, $208K MRR by Dec\nYear 3: $8M ARR, 600 customers, $667K MRR by Dec\n```\n\n### Marketplace Financial Model\n\n**Revenue Drivers:**\n\n- GMV (Gross Merchandise Value)\n- Take rate (% of GMV)\n- Net revenue = GMV × Take rate\n\n**Key Ratios:**\n\n- Take rate: 10-30% depending on category\n- CAC for buyers vs. sellers\n- Contribution margin: 60-70%\n\n**Example Projection:**\n\n```\nYear 1: $5M GMV, 15% take rate = $750K revenue\nYear 2: $20M GMV, 15% take rate = $3M revenue\nYear 3: $60M GMV, 15% take rate = $9M revenue\n```\n\n### E-Commerce Financial Model\n\n**Revenue Drivers:**\n\n- Traffic (visitors)\n- Conversion rate\n- Average order value (AOV)\n- Purchase frequency\n\n**Key Ratios:**\n\n- Gross margin: 40-60%\n- Contribution margin: 20-35%\n- CAC payback: 3-6 months\n\n### Services / Agency Financial Model\n\n**Revenue Drivers:**\n\n- Billable hours or projects\n- Hourly rate or project fee\n- Utilization rate\n- Team capacity\n\n**Key Ratios:**\n\n- Gross margin: 50-70%\n- Utilization: 70-85%\n- Revenue per employee\n\n## Fundraising Integration\n\n### Funding Scenario Modeling\n\n**Pre-Money Valuation:**\nBased on metrics and comparables.\n\n**Dilution:**\n\n```\nPost-Money = Pre-Money + Investment\nDilution % = Investment / Post-Money\n```\n\n**Use of Funds:**\nAllocate funding to extend runway and achieve milestones.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```\nRaise: $5M at $20M pre-money\nPost-Money: $25M\nDilution: 20%\n\nUse of Funds:\n- Product Development: $2M (40%)\n- Sales & Marketing: $2M (40%)\n- G&A and Operations: $0.5M (10%)\n- Working Capital: $0.5M (10%)\n```\n\n### Milestone-Based Planning\n\n**Identify Key Milestones:**\n\n- Product launch\n- First $1M ARR\n- Break-even on CAC\n- Series A fundraise\n\n**Funding Amount:**\nEnsure runway to achieve next milestone + 6 months buffer.\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n**Pitfall 1: Overly Optimistic Revenue**\n\n- New startups rarely hit aggressive projections\n- Use conservative customer acquisition assumptions\n- Model realistic churn rates\n\n**Pitfall 2: Underestimating Costs**\n\n- Add 20% buffer to expense estimates\n- Include fully-loaded compensation\n- Account for software and tools\n\n**Pitfall 3: Ignoring Cash Flow Timing**\n\n- Revenue ≠ cash (payment terms)\n- Expenses paid before revenue collected\n- Model cash conversion carefully\n\n**Pitfall 4: Static Headcount**\n\n- Hiring takes time (3-6 months to fill roles)\n- Ramp time for productivity (3-6 months)\n- Account for attrition (10-15% annually)\n\n**Pitfall 5: Not Scenario Planning**\n\n- Single scenario is never accurate\n- Always model conservative case\n- Plan for what you''ll do if base case fails\n\n## Model Validation\n\n**Sanity Checks:**\n\n- [ ] Revenue growth rate is achievable (3x in Year 2, 2x in Year 3)\n- [ ] Unit economics are realistic (LTV/CAC > 3, payback < 18 months)\n- [ ] Burn multiple is reasonable (< 2.0 in Year 2-3)\n- [ ] Headcount scales with revenue (revenue per employee growing)\n- [ ] Gross margin is appropriate for business model\n- [ ] S&M spending aligns with CAC and growth targets\n\n**Benchmark Against Peers:**\nCompare key metrics to similar companies at similar stage.\n\n**Investor Feedback:**\nShare model with advisors or investors for feedback on assumptions.\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n### Reference Files\n\nFor detailed model structures and advanced techniques:\n\n- **`references/model-templates.md`** - Complete financial model templates by business model\n- **`references/unit-economics.md`** - Deep dive on CAC, LTV, payback, and efficiency metrics\n- **`references/fundraising-scenarios.md`** - Modeling funding rounds and dilution\n\n### Example Files\n\nWorking financial models with formulas:\n\n- **`examples/saas-financial-model.md`** - Complete 3-year SaaS model with cohort analysis\n- **`examples/marketplace-model.md`** - Marketplace GMV and take rate projections\n- **`examples/scenario-analysis.md`** - Three-scenario framework with sensitivities\n\n## Quick Start\n\nTo create a startup financial model:\n\n1. **Define business model** - Revenue drivers and pricing\n2. **Project revenue** - Cohort-based with retention\n3. **Model costs** - COGS, S&M, R&D, G&A by month\n4. **Plan headcount** - Hiring by role and department\n5. **Calculate cash flow** - Revenue - expenses = burn/runway\n6. **Compute metrics** - CAC, LTV, burn multiple, runway\n7. **Create scenarios** - Conservative, base, optimistic\n8. **Validate assumptions** - Sanity check and benchmark\n9. **Integrate fundraising** - Model funding rounds and milestones\n\nFor complete templates and formulas, reference the `references/` and `examples/` files.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:58:13.482Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Financial Analysis Agents requiring comprehensive startup financial modeling with revenue projections and cost structures","zh":"适合需要全面启动财务建模、收入预测和成本结构的金融分析代理","ja":"包括収益予測とコスト構造のための包括的なスタートアップ財務モデリングを必要とする金融分析エージェントに適しています","ko":"수익 예측 및 비용 구조에 대한 포괄적인 스타트업 재무 모델링이 필요한 재무 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Análisis Financiero que requieren modelado financiero integral de inicio con proyecciones de ingresos y estructuras de costos","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse financière nécessitant un modèle de démarrage financier complet avec des projections de revenus et des structures de coûts","de":"Ideal für Finanzanalyse-Agents, die umfassendes Finanzmodellierung bei der Gründung mit Umsatzprognosen und Kostenstrukturen erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise Financeira que exigem modelagem financeira de startup abrangente com projeções de receita e estruturas de custos","ru":"Идеально для агентов финансового анализа, требующих комплексной финансовой моделирования стартапов с прогнозами доходов и стоимостью структуры","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل مالي يتطلب نمذجة مالية شاملة لبدء التشغيل مع تقديرات الإيرادات وهيكل التكاليف"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build 3-5 year financial models with scenario planning, cash flow analysis, and market sizing using OTLP ingestion and DuckDB storage, providing semantic conventions for AI telemetry","zh":"赋予代理构建3-5年财务模型的能力，使用场景规划、现金流分析和市场规模估计，利用OTLP摄取和DuckDB存储，提供AI遥测的语义约定","ja":"OTLP取り込みとDuckDBストレージを使用したシナリオプランニング、キャッシュフロー分析、および市場サイズ設定により、エージェントが3〜5年の財務モデルを構築できるようにし、AIテレメトリのためのシマンティック規約を提供する","ko":"OTLP 수집 및 DuckDB 저장소를 사용하여 시나리오 계획, 현금 흐름 분석 및 시장 규모 설정을 통하여 에이전트가 3-5년 재무 모델을 구축할 수 있도록 하며, AI 원격 측정을 위한 의미 규약을 제공합니다","es":"Permite a los agentes crear modelos financieros de 3-5 años con planificación de escenarios, análisis de flujo de efectivo y tamaño de mercado utilizando la ingesta de OTLP y el almacenamiento de DuckDB, proporcionando convenciones semánticas para la telemetría de IA","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des modèles financiers de 3-5 ans avec une planification de scénarios, une analyse de flux de trésorerie et une taille de marché en utilisant l''ingestion OTLP et le stockage DuckDB, en fournissant des conventions sémantiques pour la télémétrie IA","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Finanzmodelle von 3-5 Jahren mit Szenarienplanung, Cashflow-Analyse und Marktgroesse unter Verwendung von OTLP-Eingabe und DuckDB-Speicherung zu erstellen, wodurch semantische Konventionen für die KI-Telemetrie bereitgestellt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir modelos financeiros de 3-5 anos com planejamento de cenários, análise de fluxo de caixa e dimensionamento de mercado usando ingestão OTLP e armazenamento DuckDB, fornecendo convenções semânticas para telemetria de IA","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать финансовые модели на 3-5 лет с планированием сценариев, анализом денежных потоков и размером рынка с использованием ингестии OTLP и хранилища DuckDB, предоставляя семантические конвенции для телеметрии ИИ","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء إمكانية بناء نماذج مالية لمدة 3-5 سنوات مع تخطيط السيناريوهات وتحليل التدفق النقدي وتحجيم السوق باستخدام استهلاك OTLP وتخزين DuckDB ، مع توفير الاتفاقيات الدلالية للتحكم في الحالة الاصطناعية"},"useCases":{"en":["Generating comprehensive financial models for early-stage startups","Analyzing revenue projections and cost structures for strategic planning","Creating scenario plans for different market conditions using TAM/SAM/SOM analysis"],"zh":["为早期创业公司生成全面财务模型","分析收入预测和成本结构以进行战略规划","使用TAM/SAM/SOM分析为不同市场条件创建场景计划"],"ja":["初期のスタートアップ企業のための包括的な財務モデルを生成する","戦略的計画のための収益予測とコスト構造を分析する","TAM/SAM/SOM分析を使用して、さまざまな市場条件のためのシナリオプランを作成する"],"ko":["초기 스타트업 기업을 위한 포괄적인 재무 모델 생성","전략적 계획을 위한 수익 예측 및 비용 구조 분석","TAM/SAM/SOM 분석을 사용하여 다양한 시장 조건에 대한 시나리오 계획 생성"],"es":["Generar modelos financieros integrales para startups en etapas tempranas","Analizar proyecciones de ingresos y estructuras de costos para la planificación estratégica","Crear planes de escenarios para diferentes condiciones de mercado utilizando el análisis de TAM/SAM/SOM"],"fr":["Générer des modèles financiers complets pour les startups en phase de démarrage","Analyser les projections de revenus et les structures de coûts pour la planification stratégique","Créer des plans de scénarios pour différentes conditions de marché en utilisant l''analyse de TAM/SAM/SOM"],"de":["Erstellen von umfassenden Finanzmodellen für Startups in der Frühphase","Analyse von Umsatzprognosen und Kostenstrukturen für die strategische Planung","Erstellen von Szenarienplänen für verschiedene Marktsituationen unter Verwendung der TAM/SAM/SOM-Analyse"],"pt":["Gerar modelos financeiros abrangentes para startups em estágio inicial","Analisar projeções de receita e estruturas de custos para planejamento estratégico","Criar planos de cenários para diferentes condições de mercado usando análise TAM/SAM/SOM"],"ru":["Генерировать комплексные финансовые модели для стартапов на начальном этапе","Анализировать прогнозы доходов и стоимостную структуру для стратегического планирования","Создавать планы сценариев для разных рыночных условий с использованием анализа TAM/SAM/SOM"],"ar":["генерировать نماذج مالية شاملة لبدء التشغيل في مرحلة مبكرة","تحليل تقديرات الإيرادات وهيكل التكاليف للتخطيط الاستراتيجي","إنشاء خطط سيناريو لظروف سوق مختلفة باستخدام تحليل TAM/SAM/SOM"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of financial modeling concepts","Limited to startup financial modeling scope","Dependent on quality of input data for accurate projections"],"zh":["需要了解财务建模概念","仅限于启动财务建模范围","依赖于输入数据的质量以获得准确的预测"],"ja":["財務モデリングの概念を理解する必要がある","スタートアップ財務モデリングの範囲に限定される","正確な予測を得るために、入力データの品質に依存する"],"ko":["재무 모델링 개념을 이해해야 함","스타트업 재무 모델링 범위에만 제한됨","정확한 예측을 얻기 위해 입력 데이터의 품질에 의존함"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de conceptos de modelado financiero","Limitado al alcance del modelado financiero de startups","Dependiente de la calidad de los datos de entrada para proyecciones precisas"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des concepts de modélisation financière","Limité à la portée de la modélisation financière des startups","Dépendant de la qualité des données d''entrée pour des projections précises"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis von Finanzmodellierungskonzepten","Begrenzt auf den Umfang der Finanzmodellierung von Startups","Abhängig von der Qualität der Eingabedaten für genaue Prognosen"],"pt":["Exige compreensão de conceitos de modelagem financeira","Limitado ao escopo de modelagem financeira de startup","Dependente da qualidade dos dados de entrada para projeções precisas"],"ru":["Требует понимания концепций финансового моделирования","Ограничен объемом финансового моделирования стартапов","Зависит от качества входных данных для точных прогнозов"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا لمفاهيم نمذجة مالية","محدود نطاق نمذجة مالية لبدء التشغيل","يعتمد على جودة البيانات المدخلة للحصول على تقديرات دقيقة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
