ar":"تصحيح 系统ي: إيجاد السبب الجذري","en":"systematic-debugging"},"description":{"zh":"系统化调试是一种通过找到技术问题的根源来解决问题的方法，确保不随机修复和新bug","ja":"システム的なデバッグは、テクニカルな問題の根本原因を特定して問題を解決する方法で、ランダムな修正と新しいバグを防ぐ","ko":"시스템적 디버깅은 기술적인 문제의 근본 원인을 식별하여 문제를 해결하는 방법으로 무작위 수정과 새로운 버그를 방지","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque estructurado para identificar y solucionar problemas técnicos de manera eficiente. Siempre encuentra la causa raíz an...","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche structurée pour identifier et résoudre les problèmes techniques de manière efficace. Trouvez toujours la cause prof...","de":"Die systematische Fehlersuche ist ein strukturierter Ansatz, um technische Probleme effizient zu identifizieren und zu lösen. Finden Sie immer die Ursache, b...","pt":"A depuração sistemática é uma abordagem que enfatiza a importância de encontrar a causa raiz dos problemas técnicos antes de propor soluções.","ru":"Системная отладка - это подход, который подчеркивает важность нахождения коренной причины технических проблем перед предложением решений.","ar":"التصحيح النظامي هو نهج يؤكد على أهمية إيجاد السبب الجذري للمشاكل الفنية قبل اقتراح حلول.","en":"Custom agents built for GH copilot"},"definition":{"en":"Custom agents built for GH copilot"},"features":{"zh":["找到技术问题的根源","避免随机修复","防止新bug","提高代码质量","减少调试时间"],"ja":["テクニカルな問題の根本原因を特定","ランダムな修正を避ける","新しいバグを防ぐ","コード品質を向上","デバッグ時間を短縮"],"ko":["기술적인 문제의 근본 원인을 식별","무작위 수정을 방지","新的 버그를 방지","코드 품질을 향상","디버깅 시간을 단축"],"es":["Identifica la causa raíz de los problemas","Evita soluciones temporales","Optimiza el proceso de depuración","Mejora la eficiencia en la resolución de problemas","Reduce el tiempo de depuración"],"fr":["Identifiez la cause profonde des problèmes","Évitez les solutions temporaires","Optimisez le processus de débogage","Améliorez l''efficacité dans la résolution de problèmes","Réduisez le temps de débogage"],"de":["Identifizieren Sie die Ursache von Problemen","Vermeiden Sie temporäre Lösungen","Optimieren Sie den Fehlersuchprozess","Verbessern Sie die Effizienz bei der Problemlösung","Reduzieren Sie die Fehlersuchzeit"],"pt":["Encontra a causa raiz dos problemas","Evita soluções superficiais","Melhora a eficácia da depuração","Reduz o tempo de resolução de problemas","Aumenta a qualidade do código"],"ru":["Находит коренную причину проблем","Избегает поверхностных решений","Улучшает эффективность отладки","Сокращает время решения проблем","Повышает качество кода"],"ar":["تجد السبب الجذري للمشاكل","تتجنب الحلول السطحية","تحسن فعالية التصحيح","تقلل من وقت حل المشاكل","تزيد من جودة الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["系统化调试","技术问题","根源","软件开发","调试技术","代码质量","bug防止"],"ja":["システム的なデバッグ","テクニカルな問題","根本原因","ソフトウェア開発","デバッグ技術","コード品質","バグ防止"],"ko":["시스템적 디버깅","기술적인 문제","근본 원인","소프트웨어 개발","디버깅 기술","코드 품질","버그 방지"],"es":["depuración sistemática","desarrollo de software","resolución de problemas","eficiencia en la depuración","causa raíz","soluciones temporales","proceso de depuración"],"fr":["débogage systématique","développement de logiciels","résolution de problèmes","efficacité dans la débogage","cause profonde","solutions temporaires","processus de débogage"],"de":["systematische Fehlersuche","Softwareentwicklung","Problemlösung","Effizienz in der Fehlersuche","Ursache","temporäre Lösungen","Fehlersuchprozess"],"pt":["depuração sistemática","causa raiz","resolução de problemas","desenvolvimento de software","qualidade do código","eficácia da depuração"],"ru":["системная отладка","коренная причина","решение проблем","разработка программного обеспечения","качество кода","эффективность отладки"],"ar":["التصحيح النظامي","السبب الجذري","حل المشاكل","تطوير البرمجيات","جودة الكود","فعالية التصحيح"]}},"owner":"AlabamaMike","repo":"copilot-agents","repoPath":"AlabamaMike/copilot-agents","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.453Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"systematic-debugging","description":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes - four-phase framework (root cause investigation, pattern analysis, hypothesis testing, implementation) that ensures understanding before attempting solutions","bodyPreview":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs","body":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs in production\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Performance problems\n- Build failures\n- Integration issues\n\n**Use this ESPECIALLY when:**\n- Under time pressure (emergencies make guessing tempting)\n- \"Just one quick fix\" seems obvious\n- You''ve already tried multiple fixes\n- Previous fix didn''t work\n- You don''t fully understand the issue\n\n**Don''t skip when:**\n- Issue seems simple (simple bugs have root causes too)\n- You''re in a hurry (rushing guarantees rework)\n- Manager wants it fixed NOW (systematic is faster than thrashing)\n\n## The Four Phases\n\nYou MUST complete each phase before proceeding to the next.\n\n### Phase 1: Root Cause Investigation\n\n**BEFORE attempting ANY fix:**\n\n1. **Read Error Messages Carefully**\n   - Don''t skip past errors or warnings\n   - They often contain the exact solution\n   - Read stack traces completely\n   - Note line numbers, file paths, error codes\n\n2. **Reproduce Consistently**\n   - Can you trigger it reliably?\n   - What are the exact steps?\n   - Does it happen every time?\n   - If not reproducible → gather more data, don''t guess\n\n3. **Check Recent Changes**\n   - What changed that could cause this?\n   - Git diff, recent commits\n   - New dependencies, config changes\n   - Environmental differences\n\n4. **Gather Evidence in Multi-Component Systems**\n\n   **WHEN system has multiple components (CI → build → signing, API → service → database):**\n\n   **BEFORE proposing fixes, add diagnostic instrumentation:**\n   ```\n   For EACH component boundary:\n     - Log what data enters component\n     - Log what data exits component\n     - Verify environment/config propagation\n     - Check state at each layer\n\n   Run once to gather evidence showing WHERE it breaks\n   THEN analyze evidence to identify failing component\n   THEN investigate that specific component\n   ```\n\n   **Example (multi-layer system):**\n   ```bash\n   # Layer 1: Workflow\n   echo \"=== Secrets available in workflow: ===\"\n   echo \"IDENTITY: ${IDENTITY:+SET}${IDENTITY:-UNSET}\"\n\n   # Layer 2: Build script\n   echo \"=== Env vars in build script: ===\"\n   env | grep IDENTITY || echo \"IDENTITY not in environment\"\n\n   # Layer 3: Signing script\n   echo \"=== Keychain state: ===\"\n   security list-keychains\n   security find-identity -v\n\n   # Layer 4: Actual signing\n   codesign --sign \"$IDENTITY\" --verbose=4 \"$APP\"\n   ```\n\n   **This reveals:** Which layer fails (secrets → workflow ✓, workflow → build ✗)\n\n5. **Trace Data Flow**\n\n   **WHEN error is deep in call stack:**\n\n   **REQUIRED SUB-SKILL:** Use superpowers:root-cause-tracing for backward tracing technique\n\n   **Quick version:**\n   - Where does bad value originate?\n   - What called this with bad value?\n   - Keep tracing up until you find the source\n   - Fix at source, not at symptom\n\n### Phase 2: Pattern Analysis\n\n**Find the pattern before fixing:**\n\n1. **Find Working Examples**\n   - Locate similar working code in same codebase\n   - What works that''s similar to what''s broken?\n\n2. **Compare Against References**\n   - If implementing pattern, read reference implementation COMPLETELY\n   - Don''t skim - read every line\n   - Understand the pattern fully before applying\n\n3. **Identify Differences**\n   - What''s different between working and broken?\n   - List every difference, however small\n   - Don''t assume \"that can''t matter\"\n\n4. **Understand Dependencies**\n   - What other components does this need?\n   - What settings, config, environment?\n   - What assumptions does it make?\n\n### Phase 3: Hypothesis and Testing\n\n**Scientific method:**\n\n1. **Form Single Hypothesis**\n   - State clearly: \"I think X is the root cause because Y\"\n   - Write it down\n   - Be specific, not vague\n\n2. **Test Minimally**\n   - Make the SMALLEST possible change to test hypothesis\n   - One variable at a time\n   - Don''t fix multiple things at once\n\n3. **Verify Before Continuing**\n   - Did it work? Yes → Phase 4\n   - Didn''t work? Form NEW hypothesis\n   - DON''T add more fixes on top\n\n4. **When You Don''t Know**\n   - Say \"I don''t understand X\"\n   - Don''t pretend to know\n   - Ask for help\n   - Research more\n\n### Phase 4: Implementation\n\n**Fix the root cause, not the symptom:**\n\n1. **Create Failing Test Case**\n   - Simplest possible reproduction\n   - Automated test if possible\n   - One-off test script if no framework\n   - MUST have before fixing\n   - **REQUIRED SUB-SKILL:** Use superpowers:test-driven-development for writing proper failing tests\n\n2. **Implement Single Fix**\n   - Address the root cause identified\n   - ONE change at a time\n   - No \"while I''m here\" improvements\n   - No bundled refactoring\n\n3. **Verify Fix**\n   - Test passes now?\n   - No other tests broken?\n   - Issue actually resolved?\n\n4. **If Fix Doesn''t Work**\n   - STOP\n   - Count: How many fixes have you tried?\n   - If < 3: Return to Phase 1, re-analyze with new information\n   - **If ≥ 3: STOP and question the architecture (step 5 below)**\n   - DON''T attempt Fix #4 without architectural discussion\n\n5. **If 3+ Fixes Failed: Question Architecture**\n\n   **Pattern indicating architectural problem:**\n   - Each fix reveals new shared state/coupling/problem in different place\n   - Fixes require \"massive refactoring\" to implement\n   - Each fix creates new symptoms elsewhere\n\n   **STOP and question fundamentals:**\n   - Is this pattern fundamentally sound?\n   - Are we \"sticking with it through sheer inertia\"?\n   - Should we refactor architecture vs. continue fixing symptoms?\n\n   **Discuss with your human partner before attempting more fixes**\n\n   This is NOT a failed hypothesis - this is a wrong architecture.\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Follow Process\n\nIf you catch yourself thinking:\n- \"Quick fix for now, investigate later\"\n- \"Just try changing X and see if it works\"\n- \"Add multiple changes, run tests\"\n- \"Skip the test, I''ll manually verify\"\n- \"It''s probably X, let me fix that\"\n- \"I don''t fully understand but this might work\"\n- \"Pattern says X but I''ll adapt it differently\"\n- \"Here are the main problems: [lists fixes without investigation]\"\n- Proposing solutions before tracing data flow\n- **\"One more fix attempt\" (when already tried 2+)**\n- **Each fix reveals new problem in different place**\n\n**ALL of these mean: STOP. Return to Phase 1.**\n\n**If 3+ fixes failed:** Question the architecture (see Phase 4.5)\n\n## your human partner''s Signals You''re Doing It Wrong\n\n**Watch for these redirections:**\n- \"Is that not happening?\" - You assumed without verifying\n- \"Will it show us...?\" - You should have added evidence gathering\n- \"Stop guessing\" - You''re proposing fixes without understanding\n- \"Ultrathink this\" - Question fundamentals, not just symptoms\n- \"We''re stuck?\" (frustrated) - Your approach isn''t working\n\n**When you see these:** STOP. Return to Phase 1.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Issue is simple, don''t need process\" | Simple issues have root causes too. Process is fast for simple bugs. |\n| \"Emergency, no time for process\" | Systematic debugging is FASTER than guess-and-check thrashing. |\n| \"Just try this first, then investigate\" | First fix sets the pattern. Do it right from the start. |\n| \"I''ll write test after confirming fix works\" | Untested fixes don''t stick. Test first proves it. |\n| \"Multiple fixes at once saves time\" | Can''t isolate what worked. Causes new bugs. |\n| \"Reference too long, I''ll adapt the pattern\" | Partial understanding guarantees bugs. Read it completely. |\n| \"I see the problem, let me fix it\" | Seeing symptoms ≠ understanding root cause. |\n| \"One more fix attempt\" (after 2+ failures) | 3+ failures = architectural problem. Question pattern, don''t fix again. |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Phase | Key Activities | Success Criteria |\n|-------|---------------|------------------|\n| **1. Root Cause** | Read errors, reproduce, check changes, gather evidence | Understand WHAT and WHY |\n| **2. Pattern** | Find working examples, compare | Identify differences |\n| **3. Hypothesis** | Form theory, test minimally | Confirmed or new hypothesis |\n| **4. Implementation** | Create test, fix, verify | Bug resolved, tests pass |\n\n## When Process Reveals \"No Root Cause\"\n\nIf systematic investigation reveals issue is truly environmental, timing-dependent, or external:\n\n1. You''ve completed the process\n2. Document what you investigated\n3. Implement appropriate handling (retry, timeout, error message)\n4. Add monitoring/logging for future investigation\n\n**But:** 95% of \"no root cause\" cases are incomplete investigation.\n\n## Integration with Other Skills\n\n**This skill requires using:**\n- **root-cause-tracing** - REQUIRED when error is deep in call stack (see Phase 1, Step 5)\n- **test-driven-development** - REQUIRED for creating failing test case (see Phase 4, Step 1)\n\n**Complementary skills:**\n- **defense-in-depth** - Add validation at multiple layers after finding root cause\n- **condition-based-waiting** - Replace arbitrary timeouts identified in Phase 2\n- **verification-before-completion** - Verify fix worked before claiming success\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging sessions:\n- Systematic approach: 15-30 minutes to fix\n- Random fixes approach: 2-3 hours of thrashing\n- First-time fix rate: 95% vs 40%\n- New bugs introduced: Near zero vs common\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T06:59:19.700Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced Debugging Agents requiring a systematic approach to identifying root causes of technical issues","zh":"适用于需要系统方法来识别技术问题根因的高级调试代理","ja":"高度なデバッグエージェントが技術的な問題の根本原因を体系的に特定するために必要なアプローチに最適","ko":"기술적인 문제의 근본 원인을 체계적으로 식별해야 하는 고급 디버깅 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de depuración avanzada que requieren un enfoque sistemático para identificar las causas raíz de los problemas técnicos","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de débogage avancés nécessitant une approche systématique pour identifier les causes profondes des problèmes techniques","de":"Ideal für erweiterte Debugging-Agents, die einen systematischen Ansatz für die Identifizierung der Ursachen von technischen Problemen erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Depuração Avançada que requerem uma abordagem sistemática para identificar as causas raiz de problemas técnicos","ru":"Идеально для продвинутых агентов отладки, требующих системного подхода к выявлению коренных причин технических проблем","ar":"مثالي لعميل تصحيح الأخطاء المتقدم الذي يتطلب نهجًا منهجيًا لتحديد الأسباب الجذرية للمشكلات الفنية"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to apply the Iron Law of systematic debugging, ensuring NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST, thereby preventing quick patches that mask underlying issues and promoting thorough investigation of test failures and bugs","zh":"赋予代理应用系统调试的铁律，确保在调查根本原因之前不进行修复，从而防止掩盖潜在问题的快速补丁，并促进对测试失败和错误的彻底调查","ja":"エージェントが体系的なデバッグの鉄則を適用できるようにし、根本原因の調査を先行させることで、根本原因のない修正は行わないことを保証し、根本的な問題を隠すパッチを防ぎ、テストの失敗やバグの徹底的な調査を促進する","ko":"에이전트가 체계적인 디버깅의 철칙을 적용할 수 있도록 하여, 근본 원인 조사를 먼저 수행함으로써 수정을 먼저 적용하지 않음을 보장하고, 근본적인 문제를 가리는 패치를 방지하며, 테스트 실패와 버그에 대한 철저한 조사를 촉진","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar la Ley de Hierro de la depuración sistemática, garantizando NO HAY REPARACIONES SIN INVESTIGACIÓN DE LA CAUSA RAÍZ PRIMERO, lo que evita arreglos rápidos que ocultan problemas subyacentes y promueve una investigación exhaustiva de los fallos de prueba y errores","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer la Loi de Fer du débogage systématique, garantissant AUCUNE CORRECTION SANS ENQUÊTE SUR LA CAUSE PROFONDE D''ABORD, ce qui empêche les correctifs rapides qui masquent les problèmes sous-jacents et promeut une enquête approfondie sur les défaillances de test et les bogues","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, das eisernes Gesetz der systematischen Fehlersuche anzuwenden, sodass NO FIXES OHNE URSACHENFORSCHUNG ZUERST sichergestellt ist, wodurch schnelle Flickschustereien, die zugrunde liegende Probleme verdecken, verhindert und eine gründliche Untersuchung von Testfehlern und Fehlern gefördert wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aplicar a Lei de Ferro da depuração sistemática, garantindo NENHUMA CORREÇÃO SEM INVESTIGAÇÃO DA CAUSA RAIZ EM PRIMEIRO LUGAR, prevenindo assim patches rápidos que mascaram problemas subjacentes e promovendo uma investigação aprofundada de falhas de teste e bugs","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью применять Железный Закон системной отладки, гарантируя НИКАКИХ ИСПРАВЛЕНИЙ БЕЗ РАССЛЕДОВАНИЯ КОРЕННОЙ ПРИЧИНЫ СНАЧАЛА, тем самым предотвращая быстрые патчи, которые маскируют основные проблемы и продвигая тщательное расследование тестовых неудач и ошибок","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من تطبيق قانون الحديد للتصحيح المنهجي، مما يضمن عدم وجود إصلاحات بدون التحقيق في السبب الجذري أولاً، ومنع بذلك التصحيحات السريعة التي تخفي المشكلات الكامنة وتعزيز التحقيق الشامل لأخطاء الاختبار والعيوب"},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging complex test failures","Investigating and resolving bugs using a systematic approach","Applying the core principle of finding root causes before proposing fixes"],"zh":["调试复杂的测试失败","使用系统方法调查和解决错误","应用找到根本原因之前提出修复的核心原则"],"ja":["複雑なテストの失敗をデバッグする","体系的なアプローチを使用してバグを調査して解決する","根本原因を先に特定するという原則を適用する"],"ko":["복잡한 테스트 실패를 디버깅하는 것","체계적인 접근 방식을 사용하여 버그를 조사하고 해결하는 것","근본 원인을 먼저 식별하는 핵심 원칙을 적용"],"es":["Depuración de fallos de prueba complejos","Investigación y resolución de errores utilizando un enfoque sistemático","Aplicación del principio fundamental de encontrar las causas raíz antes de proponer soluciones"],"fr":["Débogage de défaillances de test complexes","Enquête et résolution de bogues en utilisant une approche systématique","Application du principe fondamental de recherche des causes profondes avant de proposer des correctifs"],"de":["Fehlersuche bei komplexen Testfehlern","Untersuchung und Behebung von Fehlern unter Verwendung eines systematischen Ansatzes","Anwendung des Grundprinzips, Ursachen vor der Vorschlag von Lösungen zu finden"],"pt":["Depuração de falhas de teste complexas","Investigação e resolução de bugs usando uma abordagem sistemática","Aplicação do princípio fundamental de encontrar causas raiz antes de propor correções"],"ru":["Отладка сложных тестовых неудач","Расследование и решение ошибок с помощью системного подхода","Применение основного принципа нахождения коренной причины до предложения исправлений"],"ar":["تصحيح أخطاء الاختبار المعقدة","تحقيق وتصحيح العيوب باستخدام نهج منهجي","تطبيق المبدأ الأساسي لإيجاد السبب الجذري قبل اقتراح الإصلاحات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to the systematic debugging process","Violating the letter of this process is considered violating the spirit of debugging"],"zh":["需要遵循系统调试过程","违反此过程的字母精神被认为是违反调试的精神"],"ja":["体系的なデバッグプロセスに従う必要がある","このプロセスの文字を違反することはデバッグの精神を違反することとみなされる"],"ko":["체계적인 디버깅 프로세스를 따라야 함","이 프로세스의 문자를 위반하는 것은 디버깅의 정신을 위반하는 것으로 간주됨"],"es":["Requiere adherencia al proceso de depuración sistemática","Violación de la letra de este proceso se considera violación del espíritu de la depuración"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion au processus de débogage systématique","La violation de la lettre de ce processus est considérée comme une violation de l''esprit du débogage"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung des systematischen Fehlersuchprozesses","Verletzung des Wortlautes dieses Prozesses gilt als Verletzung des Geistes der Fehlersuche"],"pt":["Exige adesão ao processo de depuração sistemática","Violar a letra deste processo é considerado violar o espírito da depuração"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения системного процесса отладки","Нарушение буквы этого процесса считается нарушением духа отладки"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بعملية التصحيح المنهجي","مخالفة حرف هذا البروتوكول تعتبر مخالفة لروح التصحيح"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
