のガイダンスを提供します","ko":"스킬 생성기는 개발자에게 효과적인 스킬을 생성하는 방법에 대한 가이드를 제공하여 Claude의 능력을 확장합니다","es":"El skill-creator proporciona orientación para crear habilidades efectivas que extienden las capacidades de Claude.","fr":"Le skill-creator fournit des conseils pour créer des compétences efficaces qui étendent les capacités de Claude.","de":"Der Skill-Ersteller bietet Anleitung zur Erstellung effektiver Fähigkeiten, die die Fähigkeiten von Claude erweitern.","pt":"O skill-creator é uma ferramenta para criar habilidades personalizadas para Claude, permitindo que os desenvolvedores estendam as capacidades do agente com c...","ru":"Skill-creator - это инструмент для создания индивидуальных навыков для Claude, позволяющий разработчикам расширить возможности агента с помощью специализиров...","ar":"skill-creator هو أداة لإنشاء مهارات مخصصة لبرنامج Claude، مما يسمح للمطورين بتوسيع إمكانيات الوكيل باستخدام المعرفة المتخصصة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["提供创建有效技能的指导","帮助开发者扩展Claude的能力","支持多种工作流","提供专门的知识和工具","能够将Claude转换为专门的代理","支持开发者的特定需求"],"ja":["効果的なスキルを作成するためのガイダンスを提供","開発者がClaudeの能力を拡張するためのサポート","複数のワークフローをサポート","専門の知識とツールを提供","Claudeを専門のエージェントに変換する能力","開発者の特定のニーズをサポート"],"ko":["효과적인 스킬을 생성하는 방법에 대한 가이드를 제공","개발자가 Claude의 능력을 확장하는 것을 지원","다중 작업 흐름을 지원","전문적인 지식과 도구를 제공","Claude를 전문적인 에이전트로 전환하는 능력","개발자의 특정需求을 지원"],"es":["Guía para crear habilidades efectivas","Extiende las capacidades de Claude","Permite la creación de flujos de trabajo especializados","Mejora la experiencia del usuario","Facilita la integración con Claude","Ofrece herramientas y conocimientos especializados"],"fr":["Guide pour créer des compétences efficaces","Étend les capacités de Claude","Permet la création de flux de travail spécialisés","Améliore l''expérience utilisateur","Facilite l''intégration avec Claude","Offre des outils et des connaissances spécialisés"],"de":["Anleitung zur Erstellung effektiver Fähigkeiten","Erweitert die Fähigkeiten von Claude","Ermöglicht die Erstellung spezialisierter Arbeitsabläufe","Verbessert die Benutzererfahrung","Vereinfacht die Integration mit Claude","Bietet spezialisierte Tools und Kenntnisse"],"pt":["Criação de habilidades personalizadas","Extensão das capacidades do agente","Conhecimento especializado","Fluxos de trabalho especializados","Transformação de Claude em agente especializado"],"ru":["Создание индивидуальных навыков","Расширение возможностей агента","Специализированные знания","Специализированные рабочие процессы","Преобразование Claude в специализированного агента"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات مخصصة","توسيع إمكانيات الوكيل","معرفة متخصصة","عمليات عمل مخصصة","تحويل برنامج Claude إلى وكيل متخصص"]},"keywords":{"zh":["技能创作者","创建技能","开发指南","Claude扩展","工作流支持","开发者工具","专门知识","代理转换","开发需求"],"ja":["スキルクリエーター","スキル作成","開発ガイド","Claude拡張","ワークフロー対応","開発者ツール","専門知識","エージェント変換","開発ニーズ"],"ko":["스킬 생성기","스킬 생성","개발 가이드","Claude 확장","작업 흐름 지원","개발자 도구","전문 지식","에이전트 전환","개발需求"],"es":["desarrollo de habilidades","creador de habilidades","Claude","desarrollo de software","integración de habilidades","flujos de trabajo especializados","experiencia del usuario","herramientas de desarrollo","conocimientos especializados"],"fr":["développement de compétences","créateur de compétences","Claude","développement de logiciels","intégration de compétences","flux de travail spécialisés","expérience utilisateur","outils de développement","connaissances spécialisées"],"de":["Fähigkeitsentwicklung","Skill-Ersteller","Claude","Softwareentwicklung","Fähigkeitsintegration","spezialisierte Arbeitsabläufe","Benutzererfahrung","Entwicklungstools","spezialisierte Kenntnisse"],"pt":["skill-creator","criação de habilidades","extensão de capacidades","conhecimento especializado","fluxos de trabalho","desenvolvimento de agentes","tecnologia de IA"],"ru":["skill-creator","создание навыков","расширение возможностей","специализированные знания","специализированные рабочие процессы","разработка агентов","технология ИИ"],"ar":["skill-creator","إنشاء مهارات","توسيع إمكانيات","معرفة متخصصة","عمليات عمل مخصصة","تطوير الوكلاء","تقنية الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"mandpd","repo":"screen-steps","repoPath":"mandpd/screen-steps","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.453Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Concise is Key\n\nThe context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with everything else Claude needs: system prompt, conversation history, other Skills'' metadata, and the actual user request.\n\n**Default assumption: Claude is already very smart.** Only add context Claude doesn''t already have. Challenge each piece of information: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this paragraph justify its token cost?\"\n\nPrefer concise examples over verbose explanations.\n\n### Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom\n\nMatch the level of specificity to the task''s fragility and variability:\n\n**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach.\n\n**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration affects behavior.\n\n**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific sequence must be followed.\n\nThink of Claude as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many routes (high freedom).\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   ├── description: (required)\n│   │   └── compatibility: (optional, rarely needed)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\nEvery SKILL.md consists of:\n\n- **Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields (required), plus optional fields like `license`, `metadata`, and `compatibility`. Only `name` and `description` are read by Claude to determine when the skill triggers, so be clear and comprehensive about what the skill is and when it should be used. The `compatibility` field is for noting environment requirements (target product, system packages, etc.) but most skills don''t need it.\n- **Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all).\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n#### What to Not Include in a Skill\n\nA skill should only contain essential files that directly support its functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files, including:\n\n- README.md\n- INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md\n- QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n- CHANGELOG.md\n- etc.\n\nThe skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to do the job at hand. It should not contain auxilary context about the process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just adds clutter and confusion.\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window)\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure Patterns\n\nKeep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them.\n\n**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks, or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, configuration) into separate reference files.\n\n**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**\n\n```markdown\n# PDF Processing\n\n## Quick start\n\nExtract text with pdfplumber:\n[code example]\n\n## Advanced features\n\n- **Form filling**: See [FORMS.md](FORMS.md) for complete guide\n- **API reference**: See [REFERENCE.md](REFERENCE.md) for all methods\n- **Examples**: See [EXAMPLES.md](EXAMPLES.md) for common patterns\n```\n\nClaude loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed.\n\n**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**\n\nFor Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid loading irrelevant context:\n\n```\nbigquery-skill/\n├── SKILL.md (overview and navigation)\n└── reference/\n    ├── finance.md (revenue, billing metrics)\n    ├── sales.md (opportunities, pipeline)\n    ├── product.md (API usage, features)\n    └── marketing.md (campaigns, attribution)\n```\n\nWhen a user asks about sales metrics, Claude only reads sales.md.\n\nSimilarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, organize by variant:\n\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + provider selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md (AWS deployment patterns)\n    ├── gcp.md (GCP deployment patterns)\n    └── azure.md (Azure deployment patterns)\n```\n\nWhen the user chooses AWS, Claude only reads aws.md.\n\n**Pattern 3: Conditional details**\n\nShow basic content, link to advanced content:\n\n```markdown\n# DOCX Processing\n\n## Creating documents\n\nUse docx-js for new documents. See [DOCX-JS.md](DOCX-JS.md).\n\n## Editing documents\n\nFor simple edits, modify the XML directly.\n\n**For tracked changes**: See [REDLINING.md](REDLINING.md)\n**For OOXML details**: See [OOXML.md](OOXML.md)\n```\n\nClaude reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those features.\n\n**Important guidelines:**\n\n- **Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md.\n- **Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, include a table of contents at the top so Claude can see the full scope when previewing.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nSkill creation involves these steps:\n\n1. Understand the skill with concrete examples\n2. Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)\n3. Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)\n4. Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)\n5. Package the skill (run package_skill.py)\n6. Iterate based on real usage\n\nFollow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Include information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Learn Proven Design Patterns\n\nConsult these helpful guides based on your skill''s needs:\n\n- **Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential workflows and conditional logic\n- **Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-patterns.md for template and example patterns\n\nThese files contain established best practices for effective skill design.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAdded scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion.\n\nAny example files and directories not needed for the skill should be deleted. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form.\n\n##### Frontmatter\n\nWrite the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:\n\n- `name`: The skill name\n- `description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, and helps Claude understand when to use the skill.\n  - Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when to use it.\n  - Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections in the body are not helpful to Claude.\n  - Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n\nDo not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter.\n\n##### Body\n\nWrite instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a .skill file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.skill`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution. The .skill file is a zip file with a .skill extension.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:02:06.596Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Claude needing specialized knowledge and workflow extensions","zh":"非常适合需要专门知识和工作流扩展的AI代理，如Claude","ja":"Claudeのような特殊な知識とワークフローの拡張が必要なAIエージェントに最適","ko":"클라우드와 같은 전문 지식과 워크플로 확장이 필요한 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Claude que necesitan conocimientos especializados y extensiones de flujo de trabajo","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''IA comme Claude nécessitant des connaissances spécialisées et des extensions de workflow","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agenten wie Claude, die spezialisierte Kenntnisse und Workflow-Erweiterungen benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA como Claude que necessitam de conhecimento especializado e extensões de fluxo de trabalho","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude, которым требуются специализированные знания и расширения рабочих процессов","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude الذين يحتاجون إلى معرفة متخصصة وتوسيعات سير العمل"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized entities equipped with procedural knowledge, providing modular and self-contained packages that extend capabilities through specialized workflows and tools, utilizing multi-step processes","zh":"赋予代理人转化为具有过程知识的专门实体的能力，提供模块化和自包含的软件包，以扩展通过专门的工作流程和工具的功能，利用多步骤的过程","ja":"エージェントが手順知識を備えた専門エンティティに変身することを可能にし、能力を拡張するためのモジュラーで自己完結したパッケージを提供し、特殊なワークフローとツールを使用してマルチステッププロセスで機能を拡張する","ko":"에이전트가 절차 지식을 갖춘 전문 엔티티로 변신할 수 있도록 해주고, 기능을 확장하기 위한 모듈화되고 자체적으로 완결된 소프트웨어 패키지를 제공하여, 특수한 워크플로와 도구를 사용하여 다단계 프로세스를 통해 기능을 확장합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformarse en entidades especializadas equipadas con conocimientos procedimentales, proporcionando paquetes modulares y autocontenidos que amplían las capacidades a través de flujos de trabajo y herramientas especializados, utilizando procesos multietapa","fr":"Permet aux agents de se transformer en entités spécialisées équipées de connaissances procédurales, fournissant des packages modulaires et autocontenus qui étendent les capacités grâce à des flux de travail et des outils spécialisés, en utilisant des processus multietapes","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, sich in spezialisierte Einheiten mit prozeduralem Wissen zu verwandeln, indem modulare und selbstenthaltene Pakete bereitgestellt werden, die die Fähigkeiten durch spezialisierte Workflows und Tools erweitern, unter Verwendung von Mehrschrittprozessen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a se transformarem em entidades especializadas equipadas com conhecimento procedural, fornecendo pacotes modulares e autocontidos que estendem as capacidades por meio de fluxos de trabalho e ferramentas especializados, utilizando processos em várias etapas","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью трансформироваться в специализированные сущности, оснащенные процедурными знаниями, предоставляя модульные и самодостаточные пакеты, которые расширяют возможности посредством специализированных рабочих процессов и инструментов, используя многоступенчатые процессы","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من التحول إلى كيانات متخصصة مجهزة بالمعرفة الإجرائية، وتوفر حزمًا متجانسة ومكتفية ذاتيًا توسع القدرات من خلال سير عمل وأدوات متخصصة، باستخدام عمليات متعددة المراحل"},"useCases":{"en":["Creating domain-specific onboarding guides","Developing procedural knowledge for tasks","Extending agent capabilities with modular packages"],"zh":["创建特定领域的入门指南","为任务开发过程知识","通过模块化软件包扩展代理人功能"],"ja":["特定ドメインのオンボーディングガイドの作成","タスクの手順知識の開発","エージェントの機能をモジュール化されたパッケージで拡張"],"ko":["도메인별 온보딩 가이드 만들기","작업을 위한 절차 지식 개발","에이전트 기능을 모듈화된 패키지로 확장"],"es":["Creación de guías de incorporación específicas del dominio","Desarrollo de conocimientos procedimentales para tareas","Ampliación de las capacidades de los agentes con paquetes modulares"],"fr":["Création de guides d''intégration spécifiques au domaine","Développement de connaissances procédurales pour les tâches","Extension des capacités des agents avec des packages modulaires"],"de":["Erstellung von domänenspezifischen Onboardingleitfäden","Entwicklung von prozeduralem Wissen für Aufgaben","Erweiterung der Agentenfähigkeiten mit modularen Paketen"],"pt":["Criar guias de integração específicos de domínio","Desenvolver conhecimento procedural para tarefas","Estender as capacidades dos agentes com pacotes modulares"],"ru":["Создание руководств по интеграции для конкретных доменов","Разработка процедурных знаний для задач","Расширение возможностей агентов с помощью модульных пакетов"],"ar":["إنشاء دلالات دمج محددة للنطاق","تطوير معرفة إجرائية للمهام","توسيع قدرات الوكلاء مع الحزم المتنقلة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Claude''s capabilities as a foundation","Limited to domains and tasks with available specialized knowledge"],"zh":["需要Claude的功能作为基础","仅限于具有可用专门知识的领域和任务"],"ja":["Claudeの機能を基盤として必要","利用可能な専門知識を持つドメインとタスクに限定"],"ko":["클라우드의 기능을 기반으로 필요","사용 가능한 전문 지식을 갖춘 도메인 및 작업에 제한"],"es":["Requiere las capacidades de Claude como base","Limitado a dominios y tareas con conocimientos especializados disponibles"],"fr":["Nécessite les capacités de Claude comme base","Limité aux domaines et tâches avec des connaissances spécialisées disponibles"],"de":["Benötigt die Fähigkeiten von Claude als Grundlage","Begrenzt auf Domänen und Aufgaben mit verfügbarem spezialisiertem Wissen"],"pt":["Exige as capacidades do Claude como base","Limitado a domínios e tarefas com conhecimento especializado disponível"],"ru":["Требует возможностей Claude в качестве основы","Ограничен доменами и задачами с доступными специализированными знаниями"],"ar":["يتطلب قدرات Claude كقاعدة","محدود بالنطاقات والمهام التي تتوفر فيها معرفة متخصصة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('bakwankawa/lazy-code-skill/skill-creator', 'community', 'bakwankawa', 'lazy-code-skill', 'bakwankawa/lazy-code-skill', 'skill-creator', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.453Z', '2026-02-18T07:01:50.213Z', NULL, '{"id":"bakwankawa/lazy-code-skill/skill-creator","name":"skill-creator","description":{"zh":"Skill Creator提供了创建有效技能的指南，帮助开发者开发出能够提升Claude能力的技能","ja":"スキルクリエーターは、開発者がClaudeの能力を高めるスキルを開発するためのガイドを提供する","ko":"스킬 크리에이터는 개발자가 클라우드의 능력을 향상시키는 스킬을 개발하는 데 필요한 가이드를 제공하는 기술","es":"El creador de habilidades proporciona orientación para crear habilidades efectivas que amplían las capacidades de Claude.","fr":"Le créateur de compétences fournit des conseils pour créer des compétences efficaces qui étendent les capacités de Claude.","de":"Der Fähigkeits-Ersteller bietet Anleitung zur Erstellung effektiver Fähigkeiten, die die Fähigkeiten von Claude erweitern.","pt":"O Criador de Habilidades fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes que estendam as capacidades de Claude com conhecimento especializado e workflows","ru":"Создатель Навыков предоставляет руководство по созданию эффективных навыков, которые расширяют возможности Claude с помощью специализированного знания и рабочих процессов","ar":"مبدع المهارات يقدم إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة تمتد قدرات Claude مع معرفة متخصصة وسير عمل","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Skill Creator 技术指南","ja":"スキルクリエーター開発者向けガイド","ko":"스킬 크리에이터 개발자 가이드","es":"Creador de habilidades para desarrolladores","fr":"Créateur de compétences pour développeurs","de":"Fähigkeits-Ersteller für Entwickler","pt":"Criador de Habilidades: Desenvolva Extensões para Claude","ru":"Создатель Навыков: Разработка Расширений для Claude","ar":"مبدع المهارات: تطوير امتدادات ل Claude","en":"skill-creator"},"description":{"zh":"Skill Creator提供了创建有效技能的指南，帮助开发者开发出能够提升Claude能力的技能","ja":"スキルクリエーターは、開発者がClaudeの能力を高めるスキルを開発するためのガイドを提供する","ko":"스킬 크리에이터는 개발자가 클라우드의 능력을 향상시키는 스킬을 개발하는 데 필요한 가이드를 제공하는 기술","es":"El creador de habilidades proporciona orientación para crear habilidades efectivas que amplían las capacidades de Claude.","fr":"Le créateur de compétences fournit des conseils pour créer des compétences efficaces qui étendent les capacités de Claude.","de":"Der Fähigkeits-Ersteller bietet Anleitung zur Erstellung effektiver Fähigkeiten, die die Fähigkeiten von Claude erweitern.","pt":"O Criador de Habilidades fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes que estendam as capacidades de Claude com conhecimento especializado e workflows","ru":"Создатель Навыков предоставляет руководство по созданию эффективных навыков, которые расширяют возможности Claude с помощью специализированного знания и рабо...","ar":"مبدع المهارات يقدم إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة تمتد قدرات Claude مع معرفة متخصصة وسير عمل","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["提供创建有效技能的指南","帮助开发者开发出能够提升Claude能力的技能","支持多种工作流","提供专业知识和工具"],"ja":["効果的なスキルを開発するためのガイドを提供","開発者がClaudeの能力を高めるスキルを開発するのを支援","複数のワークフローをサポート","専門知識とツールを提供"],"ko":["효과적인 스킬을 개발하는 데 필요한 가이드를 제공","개발자가 클라우드의 능력을 향상시키는 스킬을 개발하는 것을 지원","여러 가지 워크플ロー 지원","전문 지식과 도구 제공"],"es":["Flujos de trabajo especializados","Conocimientos procedimentales para tareas específicas","Herramientas y workflows personalizables","Integración con Claude para capacidades avanzadas","Creación de habilidades modulares y reutilizables"],"fr":["Flux de travail spécialisés","Connaissances procédurales pour tâches spécifiques","Outils et flux de travail personnalisables","Intégration avec Claude pour des capacités avancées","Création de compétences modulaires et réutilisables"],"de":["Spezialisierte Arbeitsabläufe","Prozedurales Wissen für spezifische Aufgaben","Anpassbare Tools und Arbeitsabläufe","Integration mit Claude für erweiterte Fähigkeiten","Erstellung modulare und wiederverwendbarer Fähigkeiten"],"pt":["Fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes","Estende as capacidades de Claude com conhecimento especializado","Permite a criação de workflows personalizados","Oferece conhecimento procedural para tarefas específicas","Transforma Claude em um agente especializado","Permite a integração com outros serviços e ferramentas"],"ru":["Предоставляет руководство по созданию эффективных навыков","Расширяет возможности Claude с помощью специализированного знания","Позволяет создавать индивидуальные рабочие процессы","Предлагает процедурные знания для конкретных задач","Преобразует Claude в специализированного агента","Позволяет интегрироваться с другими сервисами и инструментами"],"ar":["يقدم إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة","تمتد قدرات Claude مع معرفة متخصصة","يمكن إنشاء سير عمل مخصصة","يقدم معرفة إجرائية لمهام محددة","يحول Claude إلى وكيل متخصص","يمكن التكامل مع خدمات وأدوات أخرى"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Skill Creator","创建有效技能","开发者指南","Claude能力提升","工作流支持","专业知识和工具"],"ja":["スキルクリエーター","効果的なスキル開発","開発者ガイド","Claudeの能力高める","ワークフローサポート","専門知識とツール"],"ko":["스킬 크리에이터","효과적인 스킬 개발","개발자 가이드","클라우드 능력 향상","워크플로 지원","전문 지식과 도구"],"es":["creador de habilidades","desarrollo de habilidades","Claude","flujos de trabajo especializados","conocimientos procedimentales","herramientas de desarrollo","integración con IA"],"fr":["créateur de compétences","développement de compétences","Claude","flux de travail spécialisés","connaissances procédurales","outils de développement","intégration avec l''IA"],"de":["Fähigkeits-Ersteller","Fähigkeits-Entwicklung","Claude","spezialisierte Arbeitsabläufe","prozedurales Wissen","Entwicklungstools","Integration mit KI"],"pt":["criador de habilidades","desenvolvimento de habilidades","extensões para Claude","workflows personalizados","conhecimento especializado","procedural knowledge","desenvolvimento de software","inteligência artificial"],"ru":["создатель навыков","разработка навыков","расширения для Claude","индивидуальные рабочие процессы","специализированное знание","процедурные знания","разработка программного обеспечения","искусственный интеллект"],"ar":["مبدع المهارات","تطوير المهارات","امتدادات ل Claude","سير عمل مخصصة","معرفة متخصصة","معرفة إجرائية","تطوير البرمجيات","الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"bakwankawa","repo":"lazy-code-skill","repoPath":"bakwankawa/lazy-code-skill","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.453Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Concise is Key\n\nThe context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with everything else Claude needs: system prompt, conversation history, other Skills'' metadata, and the actual user request.\n\n**Default assumption: Claude is already very smart.** Only add context Claude doesn''t already have. Challenge each piece of information: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this paragraph justify its token cost?\"\n\nPrefer concise examples over verbose explanations.\n\n### Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom\n\nMatch the level of specificity to the task''s fragility and variability:\n\n**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach.\n\n**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration affects behavior.\n\n**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific sequence must be followed.\n\nThink of Claude as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many routes (high freedom).\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   ├── description: (required)\n│   │   └── compatibility: (optional, rarely needed)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\nEvery SKILL.md consists of:\n\n- **Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields (required), plus optional fields like `license`, `metadata`, and `compatibility`. Only `name` and `description` are read by Claude to determine when the skill triggers, so be clear and comprehensive about what the skill is and when it should be used. The `compatibility` field is for noting environment requirements (target product, system packages, etc.) but most skills don''t need it.\n- **Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all).\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n#### What to Not Include in a Skill\n\nA skill should only contain essential files that directly support its functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files, including:\n\n- README.md\n- INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md\n- QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n- CHANGELOG.md\n- etc.\n\nThe skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to do the job at hand. It should not contain auxilary context about the process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just adds clutter and confusion.\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window)\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure Patterns\n\nKeep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them.\n\n**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks, or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, configuration) into separate reference files.\n\n**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**\n\n```markdown\n# PDF Processing\n\n## Quick start\n\nExtract text with pdfplumber:\n[code example]\n\n## Advanced features\n\n- **Form filling**: See [FORMS.md](FORMS.md) for complete guide\n- **API reference**: See [REFERENCE.md](REFERENCE.md) for all methods\n- **Examples**: See [EXAMPLES.md](EXAMPLES.md) for common patterns\n```\n\nClaude loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed.\n\n**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**\n\nFor Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid loading irrelevant context:\n\n```\nbigquery-skill/\n├── SKILL.md (overview and navigation)\n└── reference/\n    ├── finance.md (revenue, billing metrics)\n    ├── sales.md (opportunities, pipeline)\n    ├── product.md (API usage, features)\n    └── marketing.md (campaigns, attribution)\n```\n\nWhen a user asks about sales metrics, Claude only reads sales.md.\n\nSimilarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, organize by variant:\n\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + provider selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md (AWS deployment patterns)\n    ├── gcp.md (GCP deployment patterns)\n    └── azure.md (Azure deployment patterns)\n```\n\nWhen the user chooses AWS, Claude only reads aws.md.\n\n**Pattern 3: Conditional details**\n\nShow basic content, link to advanced content:\n\n```markdown\n# DOCX Processing\n\n## Creating documents\n\nUse docx-js for new documents. See [DOCX-JS.md](DOCX-JS.md).\n\n## Editing documents\n\nFor simple edits, modify the XML directly.\n\n**For tracked changes**: See [REDLINING.md](REDLINING.md)\n**For OOXML details**: See [OOXML.md](OOXML.md)\n```\n\nClaude reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those features.\n\n**Important guidelines:**\n\n- **Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md.\n- **Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, include a table of contents at the top so Claude can see the full scope when previewing.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nSkill creation involves these steps:\n\n1. Understand the skill with concrete examples\n2. Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)\n3. Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)\n4. Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)\n5. Package the skill (run package_skill.py)\n6. Iterate based on real usage\n\nFollow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Include information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Learn Proven Design Patterns\n\nConsult these helpful guides based on your skill''s needs:\n\n- **Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential workflows and conditional logic\n- **Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-patterns.md for template and example patterns\n\nThese files contain established best practices for effective skill design.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAdded scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion.\n\nAny example files and directories not needed for the skill should be deleted. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form.\n\n##### Frontmatter\n\nWrite the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:\n\n- `name`: The skill name\n- `description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, and helps Claude understand when to use the skill.\n  - Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when to use it.\n  - Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections in the body are not helpful to Claude.\n  - Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n\nDo not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter.\n\n##### Body\n\nWrite instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a .skill file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.skill`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution. The .skill file is a zip file with a .skill extension.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:01:50.213Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Advanced AI Agents like Claude, needing specialized knowledge and workflow extensions through modular skills.","zh":"非常适合像Claude这样的高级AI代理，需要通过模块化技能获取专业知识和扩展工作流程。","ja":"Claudeのような高度なAIエージェントに最適で、モジュラー式スキルを通じた専門知識とワークフローの拡張を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"Claude와 같은 고급 AI 에이전트에 완벽하게 적합하며, 모듈식 스킬을 통해 전문 지식과 워크플로 확장이 필요한 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfect for Advanced AI Agents like Claude, needing specialized knowledge and workflow extensions through modular skills.","fr":"Perfect for Advanced AI Agents like Claude, needing specialized knowledge and workflow extensions through modular skills.","de":"Perfect for Advanced AI Agents like Claude, needing specialized knowledge and workflow extensions through modular skills.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avançados como o Claude, que necessitam de conhecimento especializado e extensões de fluxo de trabalho através de habilidades modulares.","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых ИИ-агентов, таких как Claude, которым требуются специализированные знания и расширения рабочих процессов с помощью модульных навыков.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المتقدمين مثل Claude، الذين يحتاجون إلى معرفة متخصصة وتوسيع سير العمل من خلال المهارات المعيارية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized entities equipped with procedural knowledge, utilizing modular self-contained packages that provide specialized workflows and tools, effectively extending their capabilities through onboarding guides for specific domains or tasks.","zh":"使代理能够转变为配备程序性知识的专业实体，利用提供专业工作流程和工具的模块化自包含包，通过特定领域或任务的上手指南有效扩展其能力。","ja":"手続き型知識を備えた専門的なエンティティにエージェントを変革させ、専門的なワークフローとツールを提供するモジュラー式の自己完結型パッケージを利用し、特定のドメインやタスクのオンボーディングガイドを通じて能力を効果的に拡張します。","ko":"모듈식 자체 포함 패키지를 활용하여 전문적인 워크플로와 도구를 제공함으로써 절차적 지식을 갖춘 전문 엔티티로 에이전트를 변환시키며, 특정 도메인이나 작업에 대한 온보딩 가이드를 통해 기능을 효과적으로 확장합니다.","es":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized entities equipped with procedural knowledge, utilizing modular self-contained packages that provide specialized workflows and tools, effectively extending their capabilities through onboarding guides for specific domains or tasks.","fr":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized entities equipped with procedural knowledge, utilizing modular self-contained packages that provide specialized workflows and tools, effectively extending their capabilities through onboarding guides for specific domains or tasks.","de":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized entities equipped with procedural knowledge, utilizing modular self-contained packages that provide specialized workflows and tools, effectively extending their capabilities through onboarding guides for specific domains or tasks.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a se transformarem em entidades especializadas equipadas com conhecimento procedural, utilizando pacotes modulares autônomos que fornecem fluxos de trabalho e ferramentas especializadas, estendendo efetivamente suas capacidades por meio de guias de integração para domínios ou tarefas específicas.","ru":"Позволяет агентам превращаться в специализированные сущности, оснащенные процедурными знаниями, используя модульные самодостаточные пакеты, которые предоставляют специализированные рабочие процессы и инструменты, эффективно расширяя их возможности с помощью руководств по внедрению для конкретных доменов или задач.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من التحول إلى كيانات متخصصة مجهزة بمعرفة إجرائية، باستخدام حزم معيارية مستقلة توفر سير عمل وأدوات متخصصة، مما يمتد بشكل فعال بقدراتهم من خلال أدلات الإدماج لمجالات أو مهام محددة."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating domain-specific skills for Claude","Developing procedural knowledge modules","Extending agent capabilities with specialized workflows"],"zh":["为Claude创建领域特定技能","开发程序性知识模块","通过专业工作流程扩展代理能力"],"ja":["Claudeのためのドメイン固有スキルの作成","手続き型知識モジュールの開発","専門的なワークフローによるエージェント機能の拡張"],"ko":["Claude를 위한 도메인 특화 스킬 생성","절차적 지식 모듈 개발","전문적인 워크플로로 에이전트 기능 확장"],"es":["Creating domain-specific skills for Claude","Developing procedural knowledge modules","Extending agent capabilities with specialized workflows"],"fr":["Creating domain-specific skills for Claude","Developing procedural knowledge modules","Extending agent capabilities with specialized workflows"],"de":["Creating domain-specific skills for Claude","Developing procedural knowledge modules","Extending agent capabilities with specialized workflows"],"pt":["Criação de habilidades específicas de domínio para o Claude","Desenvolvimento de módulos de conhecimento procedural","Extensão das capacidades do agente com fluxos de trabalho especializados"],"ru":["Создание навыков для конкретных доменов для Claude","Разработка модулей процедурных знаний","Расширение возможностей агента с помощью специализированных рабочих процессов"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات خاصة بمجال محدد لـ Claude","تطوير وحدات المعرفة الإجرائية","توسيع قدرات الوكيل بسير عمل متخصص"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Claude''s ecosystem for skill integration","Modular packages must be self-contained"],"zh":["需要Claude的生态系统进行技能集成","模块化包必须是自包含的"],"ja":["スキル統合にはClaudeのエコシステムが必要","モジュラー式パッケージは自己完結型でなければならない"],"ko":["스킬 통합을 위해 Claude의 생태계가 필요함","모듈식 패키지는 자체 포함되어야 함"],"es":["Requires Claude''s ecosystem for skill integration","Modular packages must be self-contained"],"fr":["Requires Claude''s ecosystem for skill integration","Modular packages must be self-contained"],"de":["Requires Claude''s ecosystem for skill integration","Modular packages must be self-contained"],"pt":["Requer o ecossistema do Claude para integração de habilidades","Os pacotes modulares devem ser autônomos"],"ru":["Требуется экосистема Claude для интеграции навыков","Модульные пакеты должны быть самодостаточными"],"ar":["يتطلب نظام Claude البيئي لدمج المهارات","يجب أن تكون الحزم المعيارية مستقلة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('fmbp1981-hash/prospect-pulse-54/vercel-react-best-practices', 'community', 'fmbp1981-hash', 'prospect-pulse-54', 'fmbp1981-hash/prospect-pulse-54', 'vercel-react-best-practices', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.453Z', '2026-02-18T07:02:19.572Z', NULL, '{"id":"fmbp1981-hash/prospect-pulse-54/vercel-react-best-practices","name":"vercel-react-best-practices","description":{"zh":"Vercel React 最佳实践指南是 React 和 Next.js 应用的综合性能优化指南，包含 57 条规则，分为 8 类","ja":"Vercel React ベストプラクティスガイドは、React と Next.js アプリの包括的なパフォーマンス最適化ガイドで、57 のルールを 8 つのカテゴリに分類","ko":"Vercel React 최적화 가이드는 React와 Next.js 애플리케이션을 위한 포괄적인 성능 최적화 가이드로, 57개의 규칙을 8개의 카테고리로 분류","es":"Guía de optimización de rendimiento para aplicaciones React y Next.js, con 57 reglas para mejorar el código","fr":"Guide de optimisation des performances pour les applications React et Next.js, avec 57 règles pour améliorer le code","de":"Leitfaden für Leistungsoptimierung für React- und Next.js-Anwendungen, mit 57 Regeln zur Verbesserung des Codes","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Vercel React 最佳实践指南","ja":"Vercel React ベストプラクティスガイド","ko":"Vercel React 최적화 가이드","es":"Mejores prácticas de Vercel para React","fr":"Meilleures pratiques Vercel pour React","de":"Vercel React Best Practices","en":"vercel-react-best-practices"},"description":{"zh":"Vercel React 最佳实践指南是 React 和 Next.js 应用的综合性能优化指南，包含 57 条规则，分为 8 类","ja":"Vercel React ベストプラクティスガイドは、React と Next.js アプリの包括的なパフォーマンス最適化ガイドで、57 のルールを 8 つのカテゴリに分類","ko":"Vercel React 최적화 가이드는 React와 Next.js 애플리케이션을 위한 포괄적인 성능 최적화 가이드로, 57개의 규칙을 8개의 카테고리로 분류","es":"Guía de optimización de rendimiento para aplicaciones React y Next.js, con 57 reglas para mejorar el código","fr":"Guide de optimisation des performances pour les applications React et Next.js, avec 57 règles pour améliorer le code","de":"Leitfaden für Leistungsoptimierung für React- und Next.js-Anwendungen, mit 57 Regeln zur Verbesserung des Codes","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["57 条性能优化规则","8 个优化类别","自动重构和代码生成","适用于 React 和 Next.js 应用"],"ja":["57 のパフォーマンス最適化ルール","8 つの最適化カテゴリ","自動リファクタリングとコード生成","React と Next.js アプリに対応"],"ko":["57개의 성능 최적화 규칙","8개의 최적화 카테고리","자동 리팩토링과 코드 생성","React와 Next.js 애플리케이션 지원"],"es":["57 reglas para optimizar el código","8 categorías para mejorar el rendimiento","Guía para la refactorización automática","Optimización de la carga de datos","Mejora del rendimiento de la aplicación","Compatibilidad con React y Next.js"],"fr":["57 règles pour optimiser le code","8 catégories pour améliorer les performances","Guide pour la refactoring automatisée","Optimisation du chargement des données","Amélioration des performances de l''application","Compatibilité avec React et Next.js"],"de":["57 Regeln zur Optimierung des Codes","8 Kategorien zur Leistungsverbesserung","Leitfaden für die automatisierte Refactoring","Optimierung der Datenaufbereitung","Verbesserung der Leistung der Anwendung","Kompatibilität mit React und Next.js"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Vercel React","React 最佳实践","Next.js 优化","性能优化","自动重构","代码生成"],"ja":["Vercel React","React ベストプラクティス","Next.js 最適化","パフォーマンス最適化","自動リファクタリング","コード生成"],"ko":["Vercel React","React 최적화 가이드","Next.js 최적화","성능 최적화","자동 리팩토링","코드 생성"],"es":["Vercel React","mejores prácticas","optimización de rendimiento","React","Next.js","desarrollo de aplicaciones","rendimiento","código eficiente"],"fr":["Vercel React","meilleures pratiques","optimisation des performances","React","Next.js","développement d''applications","performances","code efficace"],"de":["Vercel React","beste Praktiken","Leistungsoptimierung","React","Next.js","Anwendungsentwicklung","Leistung","effizienter Code"]}},"owner":"fmbp1981-hash","repo":"prospect-pulse-54","repoPath":"fmbp1981-hash/prospect-pulse-54","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.453Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"vercel-react-best-practices","description":"React and Next.js performance optimization guidelines from Vercel Engineering. This skill should be used when writing, reviewing, or refactoring React/Next.js code to ensure optimal performance patterns. Triggers on tasks involving React components, Next.js pages, data fetching, bundle optimization, or performance improvements.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Vercel React Best Practices\n\nComprehensive performance optimization guide for React and Next.js applications, maintained by Vercel. Contains 57 rules across 8 categories, prioritized by impact to guide automated refactoring and code generation.\n\n## When to Apply\n\nReference these guidelines when:\n- Writing new React components or Next.js pages\n- Implementing data fetching (client or server-side)\n- Reviewing code for performance issues\n- Refactoring existing React/Next.js code\n- Optimizing bundl","body":"# Vercel React Best Practices\n\nComprehensive performance optimization guide for React and Next.js applications, maintained by Vercel. Contains 57 rules across 8 categories, prioritized by impact to guide automated refactoring and code generation.\n\n## When to Apply\n\nReference these guidelines when:\n- Writing new React components or Next.js pages\n- Implementing data fetching (client or server-side)\n- Reviewing code for performance issues\n- Refactoring existing React/Next.js code\n- Optimizing bundle size or load times\n\n## Rule Categories by Priority\n\n| Priority | Category | Impact | Prefix |\n|----------|----------|--------|--------|\n| 1 | Eliminating Waterfalls | CRITICAL | `async-` |\n| 2 | Bundle Size Optimization | CRITICAL | `bundle-` |\n| 3 | Server-Side Performance | HIGH | `server-` |\n| 4 | Client-Side Data Fetching | MEDIUM-HIGH | `client-` |\n| 5 | Re-render Optimization | MEDIUM | `rerender-` |\n| 6 | Rendering Performance | MEDIUM | `rendering-` |\n| 7 | JavaScript Performance | LOW-MEDIUM | `js-` |\n| 8 | Advanced Patterns | LOW | `advanced-` |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### 1. Eliminating Waterfalls (CRITICAL)\n\n- `async-defer-await` - Move await into branches where actually used\n- `async-parallel` - Use Promise.all() for independent operations\n- `async-dependencies` - Use better-all for partial dependencies\n- `async-api-routes` - Start promises early, await late in API routes\n- `async-suspense-boundaries` - Use Suspense to stream content\n\n### 2. Bundle Size Optimization (CRITICAL)\n\n- `bundle-barrel-imports` - Import directly, avoid barrel files\n- `bundle-dynamic-imports` - Use next/dynamic for heavy components\n- `bundle-defer-third-party` - Load analytics/logging after hydration\n- `bundle-conditional` - Load modules only when feature is activated\n- `bundle-preload` - Preload on hover/focus for perceived speed\n\n### 3. Server-Side Performance (HIGH)\n\n- `server-auth-actions` - Authenticate server actions like API routes\n- `server-cache-react` - Use React.cache() for per-request deduplication\n- `server-cache-lru` - Use LRU cache for cross-request caching\n- `server-dedup-props` - Avoid duplicate serialization in RSC props\n- `server-serialization` - Minimize data passed to client components\n- `server-parallel-fetching` - Restructure components to parallelize fetches\n- `server-after-nonblocking` - Use after() for non-blocking operations\n\n### 4. Client-Side Data Fetching (MEDIUM-HIGH)\n\n- `client-swr-dedup` - Use SWR for automatic request deduplication\n- `client-event-listeners` - Deduplicate global event listeners\n- `client-passive-event-listeners` - Use passive listeners for scroll\n- `client-localstorage-schema` - Version and minimize localStorage data\n\n### 5. Re-render Optimization (MEDIUM)\n\n- `rerender-defer-reads` - Don''t subscribe to state only used in callbacks\n- `rerender-memo` - Extract expensive work into memoized components\n- `rerender-memo-with-default-value` - Hoist default non-primitive props\n- `rerender-dependencies` - Use primitive dependencies in effects\n- `rerender-derived-state` - Subscribe to derived booleans, not raw values\n- `rerender-derived-state-no-effect` - Derive state during render, not effects\n- `rerender-functional-setstate` - Use functional setState for stable callbacks\n- `rerender-lazy-state-init` - Pass function to useState for expensive values\n- `rerender-simple-expression-in-memo` - Avoid memo for simple primitives\n- `rerender-move-effect-to-event` - Put interaction logic in event handlers\n- `rerender-transitions` - Use startTransition for non-urgent updates\n- `rerender-use-ref-transient-values` - Use refs for transient frequent values\n\n### 6. Rendering Performance (MEDIUM)\n\n- `rendering-animate-svg-wrapper` - Animate div wrapper, not SVG element\n- `rendering-content-visibility` - Use content-visibility for long lists\n- `rendering-hoist-jsx` - Extract static JSX outside components\n- `rendering-svg-precision` - Reduce SVG coordinate precision\n- `rendering-hydration-no-flicker` - Use inline script for client-only data\n- `rendering-hydration-suppress-warning` - Suppress expected mismatches\n- `rendering-activity` - Use Activity component for show/hide\n- `rendering-conditional-render` - Use ternary, not && for conditionals\n- `rendering-usetransition-loading` - Prefer useTransition for loading state\n\n### 7. JavaScript Performance (LOW-MEDIUM)\n\n- `js-batch-dom-css` - Group CSS changes via classes or cssText\n- `js-index-maps` - Build Map for repeated lookups\n- `js-cache-property-access` - Cache object properties in loops\n- `js-cache-function-results` - Cache function results in module-level Map\n- `js-cache-storage` - Cache localStorage/sessionStorage reads\n- `js-combine-iterations` - Combine multiple filter/map into one loop\n- `js-length-check-first` - Check array length before expensive comparison\n- `js-early-exit` - Return early from functions\n- `js-hoist-regexp` - Hoist RegExp creation outside loops\n- `js-min-max-loop` - Use loop for min/max instead of sort\n- `js-set-map-lookups` - Use Set/Map for O(1) lookups\n- `js-tosorted-immutable` - Use toSorted() for immutability\n\n### 8. Advanced Patterns (LOW)\n\n- `advanced-event-handler-refs` - Store event handlers in refs\n- `advanced-init-once` - Initialize app once per app load\n- `advanced-use-latest` - useLatest for stable callback refs\n\n## How to Use\n\nRead individual rule files for detailed explanations and code examples:\n\n```\nrules/async-parallel.md\nrules/bundle-barrel-imports.md\n```\n\nEach rule file contains:\n- Brief explanation of why it matters\n- Incorrect code example with explanation\n- Correct code example with explanation\n- Additional context and references\n\n## Full Compiled Document\n\nFor the complete guide with all rules expanded: `AGENTS.md`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:02:19.572Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for React and Next.js Development Agents optimizing application performance and bundle size.","zh":"适用于React和Next.js开发代理，优化应用程序性能和包大小。","ja":"ReactとNext.js開発エージェントに不可欠で、アプリケーションのパフォーマンスとバンドルサイズを最適化します。","ko":"리액트 및 넥스트.js 개발 에이전트에 필수적인 애플리케이션 성능 및 번들 크기 최적화에 사용됩니다.","es":"Esencial para los agentes de desarrollo de React y Next.js que optimizan el rendimiento de la aplicación y el tamaño del paquete.","fr":"Essentiel pour les agents de développement React et Next.js qui optimisent les performances de l''application et la taille du paquet.","de":"Wesentlich für React- und Next.js-Entwicklungsagenten, die die Anwendungsleistung und die Paketgröße optimieren.","pt":"Essencial para agentes de desenvolvimento React e Next.js que otimizam o desempenho da aplicação e o tamanho do pacote.","ru":"Необходим для агентов разработки React и Next.js, оптимизирующих производительность приложения и размер пакета.","ar":"ضروري لموكلات تطوير React و Next.js التي تحسن أداء التطبيق وحجم الحزمة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables automated code refactoring and generation following Vercel''s 57 prioritized rules across 8 performance categories, including client/server-side data fetching, component optimization, and bundling strategies for React/Next.js applications.","zh":"实现自动化代码重构和生成，遵循Vercel的57个优先规则，跨8个性能类别，包括客户端/服务器端数据获取、组件优化和React/Next.js应用程序的打包策略。","ja":"Vercelの57の優先順位付けされたルールに従って自動化されたコードのリファクタリングと生成を可能にし、クライアント/サーバーサイドのデータフェッチ、コンポーネントの最適化、React/Next.jsアプリケーションのバンドル戦略など、8つのパフォーマンスカテゴリを跨ぐ。","ko":"버셀의 57개 우선 순위 규칙을 따르는 자동화된 코드 리팩토링 및 생성을 가능하게 하며, 클라이언트/서버 측 데이터 가져오기, 구성 요소 최적화 및 리액트/넥스트.js 애플리케이션의 번들링 전략 등을 포함한 8개의 성능 범주에 걸쳐 있습니다.","es":"Permite la refactorización y generación de código automatizadas siguiendo las 57 reglas prioritarias de Vercel en 8 categorías de rendimiento, incluida la recuperación de datos del lado del cliente y del servidor, la optimización de componentes y las estrategias de empaquetado para aplicaciones React/Next.js.","fr":"Permet la refactorisation et la génération de code automatisées en suivant les 57 règles prioritaires de Vercel dans 8 catégories de performances, notamment la récupération de données côté client et serveur, l''optimisation de composants et les stratégies de regroupement pour les applications React/Next.js.","de":"Ermöglicht die automatisierte Code-Refaktorierung und -generierung unter Einhaltung von Vercels 57 priorisierten Regeln in 8 Leistungskategorien, einschließlich Client-/Server-seitigem Datenabruf, Komponentenoptimierung und Bündelungsstrategien für React-/Next.js-Anwendungen.","pt":"Permite a refatoração de código automatizada e geração seguindo as 57 regras priorizadas da Vercel em 8 categorias de desempenho, incluindo busca de dados cliente/servidor, otimização de componentes e estratégias de empacotamento para aplicações React/Next.js.","ru":"Позволяет выполнять автоматическую рефакторинг кода и генерацию, следующую 57 приоритизированным правилам Vercel в 8 категориях производительности, включая клиент-/серверную загрузку данных, оптимизацию компонентов и стратегии пакетирования для приложений React/Next.js.","ar":"تمكن من إعادة هيكلة التعليمات البرمجية التلقائية وتوليد متابعة 57 قاعدة مرتكزة على الأولوية من Vercel في 8 فئات للأداء، بما في ذلك استرجاع البيانات على جانب العميل والخادم وتحسين المكونات واستراتيجيات الحزم لمواقع React/Next.js."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating performance-focused code reviews","Generating optimized React components and Next.js pages","Refactoring existing codebases for bundle optimization","Implementing best-practice data fetching patterns"],"zh":["自动化性能为中心的代码审查","生成优化的React组件和Next.js页面","重构现有的代码库以优化包大小","实施最佳实践的数据获取模式"],"ja":["パフォーマンスに焦点を当てたコードレビューの自動化","最適化されたReactコンポーネントとNext.jsページの生成","バンドルサイズの最適化のために既存のコードベースをリファクタリング","ベストプラクティスのデータ取得パターンの実装"],"ko":["성능 중심 코드 리뷰 자동화","최적화된 리액트 구성 요소 및 넥스트.js 페이지 생성","번들 크기 최적화를 위한 기존 코드베이스 리팩토링","최선의 데이터 가져오기 패턴 구현"],"es":["Automatización de revisiones de código centradas en el rendimiento","Generación de componentes de React y páginas de Next.js optimizados","Reestructuración de bases de código existentes para la optimización de paquetes","Implementación de patrones de recuperación de datos de buenas prácticas"],"fr":["Automatisation des examens de code axés sur les performances","Génération de composants React et de pages Next.js optimisés","Réorganisation de bases de code existantes pour l''optimisation des paquets","Mise en œuvre de modèles de récupération de données de bonnes pratiques"],"de":["Automatisierung von leistungsorientierten Code-Reviews","Generierung von optimierten React-Komponenten und Next.js-Seiten","Neustrukturierung bestehender Codebasen für die Optimierung von Paketen","Implementierung von Datenabrufmustern mit bewährten Verfahren"],"pt":["Automatizar revisões de código focadas no desempenho","Gerar componentes React e páginas Next.js otimizados","Refatorar bases de código existentes para otimização de pacotes","Implementar padrões de busca de dados de melhor prática"],"ru":["Автоматизировать обзоры кода, ориентированные на производительность","Генерировать оптимизированные компоненты React и страницы Next.js","Рефакторить существующие кодовые базы для оптимизации пакетов","Реализовывать лучшие практики поиска данных"],"ar":["تأتمتات المراجعة التلقائية للتعليمات البرمجية التي تركز على الأداء","توليد مكونات React ومواقع Next.js المُحسّنة","إعادة هيكلة قواعد التعليمات البرمجية الحالية لتحسين الحزم","تنفيذ أنماط بحث البيانات لأفضل الممارسات"]},"limitations":{"en":["React/Next.js specific (not framework agnostic)","Requires existing codebase for refactoring scenarios","Performance impact prioritization requires context awareness"],"zh":["仅适用于React/Next.js（不是框架不可知的）","重构场景需要现有的代码库","性能影响优先级需要上下文感知"],"ja":["React/Next.js専用（フレームワーク非依存ではない）","リファクタリングシナリオでは既存のコードベースが必要","パフォーマンスへの影響の優先順位付けにはコンテキストの認識が必要"],"ko":["리액트/넥스트.js 전용(프레임워크 비의존 아님)","리팩토링 시나리오에는 기존 코드베이스가 필요합니다","성능에 대한 영향의 우선 순위에는 컨텍스트 인식이 필요합니다"],"es":["Específico de React/Next.js (no agnóstico de marco de trabajo)","Requiere una base de código existente para escenarios de reestructuración","La priorización del impacto en el rendimiento requiere conciencia del contexto"],"fr":["Spécifique à React/Next.js (pas agnostique du framework)","Nécessite une base de code existante pour les scénarios de réorganisation","La priorisation de l''impact sur les performances nécessite une conscience du contexte"],"de":["React/Next.js-spezifisch (nicht framework-agnostisch)","Benötigt eine bestehende Codebasis für Refaktorierungsszenarien","Die Priorisierung der Leistungsbeeinträchtigung erfordert Kontextbewusstsein"],"pt":["Específico para React/Next.js (não agnóstico de estrutura)","Requer base de código existente para cenários de refatoração","Priorização do impacto de desempenho requer conscientização contextual"],"ru":["Спецефичный для React/Next.js (не фреймворк-агностичный)","Требует существующей кодовой базы для сценариев рефакторинга","Приоритезация влияния на производительность требует контекстного осознания"],"ar":["محدد لموكلات React/Next.js (غير محايد لل_framework)","يتطلب قاعدة التعليمات البرمجية الحالية لمحاكات إعادة الهيكلة","التحديد الأولوي للآثار على الأداء يتطلب دراية سياقية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
