entellem Artefakt-Ansatz","pt":"Inicie uma Nova Alteração com Abordagem Experimental","ru":"Начните новое изменение с помощью экспериментального подхода","ar":"ابدأ bằng تغيير جديد باستخدام النهج التجريبي","en":"openspec-new-change"},"description":{"zh":"openspec-new-change技能允许开发者使用实验性构建方法启动新的变更，提高开发效率和质量","ja":"openspec-new-changeスキルは、開発者が実験的なアプローチで新しい変更を開始し、開発効率と品質を向上させることを可能にします","ko":"openspec-new-change 스킬을 통해 개발자는 실험적 아티팩트 기반 접근법으로 새로운 변경을 시작하여 개발 효율성과 품질을 향상시킬 수 있습니다","es":"La función de cambio experimental permite a los usuarios iniciar un nuevo cambio proporcionando un nombre o describiendo lo que desean construir.","fr":"La fonctionnalité de changement expérimentale permet aux utilisateurs de démarrer un nouveau changement en fournissant un nom ou en décrivant ce qu''ils souha...","de":"Die experimentelle Änderungsfunktion ermöglicht es Benutzern, eine neue Änderung zu starten, indem sie einen Namen angeben oder beschreiben, was sie erstelle...","pt":"Inicie uma nova alteração usando a abordagem experimental baseada em artefatos. Forneça um nome de alteração em kebab-case ou uma descrição do que você desej...","ru":"Начните новое изменение с помощью экспериментального подхода, основанного на артефактах. Предоставьте имя изменения в kebab-case или описание того, что вы хо...","ar":"ابدأ bằng تغيير جديد باستخدام النهج التجريبي القائم على المكونات. قدم اسم التغيير بالشكل kebab-case أو وصف ما تريد بناؤه","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["实验性构建方法","启动新的变更","提高开发效率","改进代码质量","增强协作功能"],"ja":["実験的なアプローチ","新しい変更の開始","開発効率の向上","コード品質の改善","コラボレーションの強化"],"ko":["실험적 아티팩트 기반 접근법","새로운 변경의 시작","개발 효율성의 향상","코드 품질의 개선","협업 기능의 강화"],"es":["Inicia un nuevo cambio con un nombre o descripción","Utiliza la herramienta de pregunta al usuario para obtener más información","Deriva un nombre en kebab-case a partir de la descripción del usuario","Permite a los usuarios describir lo que desean construir o arreglar","Utiliza un enfoque de artefactos experimentales"],"fr":["Démarrez un nouveau changement avec un nom ou une description","Utilisez l''outil de question à l''utilisateur pour obtenir plus d''informations","Déduisez un nom en kebab-case à partir de la description de l''utilisateur","Permet aux utilisateurs de décrire ce qu''ils souhaitent construire ou réparer","Utilise une approche expérimentale d''artefacts"],"de":["Starten Sie eine neue Änderung mit einem Namen oder einer Beschreibung","Verwenden Sie das Tool zur Benutzerfrage, um mehr Informationen zu erhalten","Leiten Sie einen Namen in kebab-case aus der Benutzerbeschreibung ab","Ermöglichen Sie es Benutzern, zu beschreiben, was sie erstellen oder reparieren möchten","Verwenden Sie einen experimentellen Artefakt-Ansatz"],"pt":["Inicie novas alterações com facilidade","Use a abordagem experimental baseada em artefatos","Forneça nomes de alteração em kebab-case","Descreva o que você deseja construir","Use a ferramenta AskUserQuestion para obter informações","Derive nomes de alteração a partir de descrições"],"ru":["Начните новые изменения с легкостью","Используйте экспериментальный подход, основанный на артефактах","Предоставьте имена изменений в kebab-case","Опишите, что вы хотите построить","Используйте инструмент AskUserQuestion для получения информации","Выведите имена изменений из описаний"],"ar":["ابدأ bằng تغييرات جديدة بسهولة","استخدم النهج التجريبي القائم على المكونات","قدم أسماء التغيير بالشكل kebab-case","أوصف ما تريد بناؤه","استخدم أداة AskUserQuestion للاستعلام","استخرج أسماء التغيير من الوصف"]},"keywords":{"zh":["openspec-new-change","实验性构建方法","开发效率","代码质量","协作功能","开发工具","软件开发"],"ja":["openspec-new-change","実験的なアプローチ","開発効率","コード品質","コラボレーション","開発ツール","ソフトウェア開発"],"ko":["openspec-new-change","실험적 아티팩트 기반 접근법","개발 효율성","코드 품질","협업 기능","개발 도구","소프트웨어 개발"],"es":["cambio experimental","artefactos experimentales","herramienta de cambio","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software","metodologías ágiles","desarrollo de aplicaciones"],"fr":["changement expérimental","artefacts expérimentaux","outil de changement","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de logiciels","méthodologies agiles","développement d''applications"],"de":["experimentelle Änderung","experimentelle Artefakte","Änderungstool","Softwareentwicklung","Softwareingenieurwesen","agile Methoden","Anwendungsentwicklung"],"pt":["abordagem experimental","iniciar novas alterações","artefatos","kebab-case","AskUserQuestion","desenvolvimento de projetos","gerenciamento de alterações"],"ru":["экспериментальный подход","начало новых изменений","артефакты","kebab-case","AskUserQuestion","разработка проектов","управление изменениями"],"ar":["النهج التجريبي","بدء تغييرات جديدة","المكونات","kebab-case","AskUserQuestion","تطوير المشاريع","إدارة التغييرات"]}},"owner":"jaxxstorm","repo":"dnstrace","repoPath":"jaxxstorm/dnstrace","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.453Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-new-change","description":"Start a new OpenSpec change using the experimental artifact workflow. Use when the user wants to create a new feature, fix, or modification with a structured step-by-step approach.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Start a new change using the experimental artifact-driven approach.\n\n**Input**: The user''s request should include a change name (kebab-case) OR a description of what they want to build.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no clear input provided, ask what they want to build**\n\n   Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** (open-ended, no preset options) to ask:\n   > \"What change do you want to work on? Describe what you want to build or fix.\"\n\n   From their description, derive a kebab-case name (e.g., \"add user authentic","body":"Start a new change using the experimental artifact-driven approach.\n\n**Input**: The user''s request should include a change name (kebab-case) OR a description of what they want to build.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no clear input provided, ask what they want to build**\n\n   Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** (open-ended, no preset options) to ask:\n   > \"What change do you want to work on? Describe what you want to build or fix.\"\n\n   From their description, derive a kebab-case name (e.g., \"add user authentication\" → `add-user-auth`).\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT proceed without understanding what the user wants to build.\n\n2. **Determine the workflow schema**\n\n   Use the default schema (omit `--schema`) unless the user explicitly requests a different workflow.\n\n   **Use a different schema only if the user mentions:**\n   - A specific schema name → use `--schema <name>`\n   - \"show workflows\" or \"what workflows\" → run `openspec schemas --json` and let them choose\n\n   **Otherwise**: Omit `--schema` to use the default.\n\n3. **Create the change directory**\n   ```bash\n   openspec new change \"<name>\"\n   ```\n   Add `--schema <name>` only if the user requested a specific workflow.\n   This creates a scaffolded change at `openspec/changes/<name>/` with the selected schema.\n\n4. **Show the artifact status**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\"\n   ```\n   This shows which artifacts need to be created and which are ready (dependencies satisfied).\n\n5. **Get instructions for the first artifact**\n   The first artifact depends on the schema (e.g., `proposal` for spec-driven).\n   Check the status output to find the first artifact with status \"ready\".\n   ```bash\n   openspec instructions <first-artifact-id> --change \"<name>\"\n   ```\n   This outputs the template and context for creating the first artifact.\n\n6. **STOP and wait for user direction**\n\n**Output**\n\nAfter completing the steps, summarize:\n- Change name and location\n- Schema/workflow being used and its artifact sequence\n- Current status (0/N artifacts complete)\n- The template for the first artifact\n- Prompt: \"Ready to create the first artifact? Just describe what this change is about and I''ll draft it, or ask me to continue.\"\n\n**Guardrails**\n- Do NOT create any artifacts yet - just show the instructions\n- Do NOT advance beyond showing the first artifact template\n- If the name is invalid (not kebab-case), ask for a valid name\n- If a change with that name already exists, suggest continuing that change instead\n- Pass --schema if using a non-default workflow\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:03:24.596Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring agile project initialization and experimental artifact-driven approaches.","zh":"适合需要敏捷项目初始化和实验性基于构件的方法的开发代理。","ja":"アジャイルなプロジェクトの初期化や実験的なアーティファクト駆動型アプローチを必要とする開発エージェントに適しています。","ko":"敏捷한 프로젝트 초기화 및 실험적인 아티팩트 기반 접근 방식을 요구하는 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que requieren una inicialización de proyecto ágil y enfoques experimentales impulsados por artefactos.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant une initialisation de projet agile et des approches expérimentales axées sur les artefacts.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungssagenten, die eine agile Projekterstellung und experimentelle, an Artefakten orientierte Ansätze erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que requerem inicialização de projeto ágil e abordagens experimentais baseadas em artefatos.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, требующих гибкой инициализации проекта и экспериментальных подходов, основанных на артефактах.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الذي يتطلب 초기 التطبيق المرونة والنهج التجريبي القائم على القطعة الفنية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to derive kebab-case names from user descriptions and initiate new changes using the AskUserQuestion tool, facilitating open-ended user interactions and artifact-driven development with tools like AskUserQuestion.","zh":"赋予代理从用户描述中推导出短横线命名法的名称，并使用 AskUserQuestion 工具启动新的更改，从而促进开放式用户交互和使用 AskUserQuestion 等工具的基于构件的开发。","ja":"エージェントがユーザーの説明からケバブケースの名前を導き出し、AskUserQuestionツールを使用して新しい変更を開始できるようにし、AskUserQuestionなどのツールを使用したオープンエンドのユーザーインタラクションとアーティファクト駆動型開発を促進します。","ko":"에이전트가 사용자 설명에서 케밥 케이스 이름을 도출하고 AskUserQuestion 도구를 사용하여 새로운 변경을 시작할 수 있도록 하여 AskUserQuestion 등의 도구를 사용한 개방형 사용자 상호 작용 및 아티팩트 기반 개발을 촉진합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a derivar nombres en kebab-case a partir de descripciones de usuario y a iniciar nuevos cambios utilizando la herramienta AskUserQuestion, lo que facilita las interacciones de usuario abiertas y el desarrollo impulsado por artefactos con herramientas como AskUserQuestion.","fr":"Permet aux agents de dériver des noms en kebab-case à partir de descriptions d''utilisateur et d''initier de nouveaux changements en utilisant l''outil AskUserQuestion, facilitant ainsi les interactions utilisateur ouvertes et le développement axé sur les artefacts avec des outils comme AskUserQuestion.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, kebab-case-Namen aus Benutzerbeschreibungen abzuleiten und mit dem Tool AskUserQuestion neue Änderungen zu initiieren, wodurch offene Benutzerinteraktionen und eine an Artefakten orientierte Entwicklung mit Tools wie AskUserQuestion erleichtert werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a derivar nomes em kebab-case a partir de descrições do usuário e iniciar novas alterações usando a ferramenta AskUserQuestion, facilitando interações abertas do usuário e desenvolvimento baseado em artefatos com ferramentas como AskUserQuestion.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью получать имена в kebab-case из описаний пользователя и инициировать новые изменения с помощью инструмента AskUserQuestion, что облегчает открытые взаимодействия пользователя и разработку на основе артефактов с помощью инструментов типа AskUserQuestion.","ar":"يتمكن الوكيل من اشتقاق أسماء كباب الحالة من وصف المستخدم والبدء في تغييرات جديدة باستخدام أداة AskUserQuestion، ويسهم في تفاعلات المستخدم المفتوحة والتنمية القائمة على القطعة الفنية بأدوات مثل AskUserQuestion."},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing new projects with experimental approaches","Deriving kebab-case names from user input","Facilitating open-ended user interactions for project planning"],"zh":["使用实验性方法初始化新项目","从用户输入中推导出短横线命名法的名称","促进开放式用户交互以进行项目规划"],"ja":["実験的なアプローチを使用して新しいプロジェクトを初期化する","ユーザーの入力からケバブケースの名前を導き出す","プロジェクト計画のためのオープンエンドのユーザーインタラクションを促進する"],"ko":["실험적인 접근 방식을 사용하여 새로운 프로젝트를 초기화하는 것","사용자 입력에서 케밥 케이스 이름을 도출하는 것","프로젝트 계획을 위한 개방형 사용자 상호 작용을 촉진하는 것"],"es":["Inicialización de nuevos proyectos con enfoques experimentales","Derivación de nombres en kebab-case a partir de la entrada del usuario","Facilitación de interacciones de usuario abiertas para la planificación de proyectos"],"fr":["Initialisation de nouveaux projets avec des approches expérimentales","Déivation de noms en kebab-case à partir de la saisie de l''utilisateur","Facilitation d''interactions utilisateur ouvertes pour la planification de projet"],"de":["Initialisierung neuer Projekte mit experimentellen Ansätzen","Ableitung von kebab-case-Namen aus der Benutzereingabe","Erleichterung offener Benutzerinteraktionen für die Projektplanung"],"pt":["Inicialização de novos projetos com abordagens experimentais","Derivação de nomes em kebab-case a partir da entrada do usuário","Facilitação de interações abertas do usuário para planejamento de projetos"],"ru":["Инициализация новых проектов с экспериментальными подходами","Получение имен в kebab-case из входных данных пользователя","Облегчение открытых взаимодействий пользователя при планировании проектов"],"ar":["تأسيس مشاريع جديدة بالنهج التجريبي","استخراج أسماء كباب الحالة من مدخلات المستخدم","تسهيل تفاعلات المستخدم المفتوحة لتخطيط المشاريع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires user input or description for change initialization","Limited to kebab-case naming convention"],"zh":["需要用户输入或描述来初始化更改","仅限于短横线命名约定"],"ja":["変更の初期化にはユーザーの入力または説明が必要","ケバブケースの命名規則のみに限定される"],"ko":["변경 초기화를 위해 사용자 입력 또는 설명이 필요함","케밥 케이스命名 규칙에만 한정됨"],"es":["Requiere una entrada o descripción del usuario para la inicialización de cambios","Limitado a la convención de nomenclatura en kebab-case"],"fr":["Nécessite une saisie ou une description de l''utilisateur pour l''initialisation des changements","Limité à la convention de nommage en kebab-case"],"de":["Benötigt eine Benutzereingabe oder -beschreibung für die Initialisierung von Änderungen","Begrenzt auf die Namenskonvention in kebab-case"],"pt":["Requer entrada ou descrição do usuário para inicialização de alterações","Limitado à convenção de nomenclatura em kebab-case"],"ru":["Требует ввода или описания пользователя для инициализации изменений","Ограничен конвенцией именования в kebab-case"],"ar":["يتطلب إدخال أو وصف المستخدم لمبادرة التغيير","محدود بالاتفاقية اشتقاق كباب الحالة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('f4ah6o/noraft.mbt/moonbit-refactoring', 'community', 'f4ah6o', 'noraft.mbt', 'f4ah6o/noraft.mbt', 'moonbit-refactoring', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.453Z', '2026-02-18T07:03:14.608Z', NULL, '{"id":"f4ah6o/noraft.mbt/moonbit-refactoring","name":"moonbit-refactoring","description":{"zh":"MoonBit 重构技巧提供了 Rust 最小化 Raft 实现，减少依赖，提高代码质量","ja":"MoonBit リファクタリングスキルは、Rust 最小の Raft 実装を提供し、依存関係を減らし、コード品質を向上させます","ko":"MoonBit 리팩토링 기술은 러스트 최소한의 Raft 구현을 제공하여 의존성을 줄이고 코드 품질을 향상시킵니다","es":"MoonBit es un enfoque de refactorización minimalista para Rust que mantiene el comportamiento y los contratos públicos","fr":"MoonBit est une approche de refactoring minimaliste pour Rust qui préserve le comportement et les contrats publics","de":"MoonBit ist ein minimalistischer Ansatz für die Refaktorierung von Rust-Code, der das Verhalten und die öffentlichen Verträge beibehält","pt":"A habilidade de refatoração Moonbit é uma abordagem minimalista para melhorar o código Rust, focando na preservação do comportamento e na minimização da API pública.","ru":"Навык рефакторинга Moonbit - это минималистский подход к улучшению кода Rust, направленный на сохранение поведения и минимизацию публичного API.","ar":"مهارة إعادة هيكلة Moonbit هي نهج محسّن لتحسين رمز الرست، مع التركيز على الحفاظ على السلوك وتقليل واجهة برمجة التطبيقات العامة.","en":"Minimal, feature-complete Raft for Rust — no I/O, no dependencies"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"MoonBit 重构技巧 - Rust 最小化 Raft 实现","ja":"MoonBit リファクタリングスキル - Rust 最小の Raft 実装","ko":"MoonBit 리팩토링 기술 - 러스트 최소한의 Raft 구현","es":"Refactorización MoonBit: Minimalista y Eficiente","fr":"Refactoring MoonBit: Minimaliste et Efficace","de":"MoonBit Refactoring: Minimalistisch und Effizient","pt":"Moonbit Refactoring: Otimização de Código Rust","ru":"Moonbit Рефакторинг: Оптимизация Код Rust","ar":"moonbit إعادة هيكلة: تحسين رمز الرست","en":"moonbit-refactoring"},"description":{"zh":"MoonBit 重构技巧提供了 Rust 最小化 Raft 实现，减少依赖，提高代码质量","ja":"MoonBit リファクタリングスキルは、Rust 最小の Raft 実装を提供し、依存関係を減らし、コード品質を向上させます","ko":"MoonBit 리팩토링 기술은 러스트 최소한의 Raft 구현을 제공하여 의존성을 줄이고 코드 품질을 향상시킵니다","es":"MoonBit es un enfoque de refactorización minimalista para Rust que mantiene el comportamiento y los contratos públicos","fr":"MoonBit est une approche de refactoring minimaliste pour Rust qui préserve le comportement et les contrats publics","de":"MoonBit ist ein minimalistischer Ansatz für die Refaktorierung von Rust-Code, der das Verhalten und die öffentlichen Verträge beibehält","pt":"A habilidade de refatoração Moonbit é uma abordagem minimalista para melhorar o código Rust, focando na preservação do comportamento e na minimização da API ...","ru":"Навык рефакторинга Moonbit - это минималистский подход к улучшению кода Rust, направленный на сохранение поведения и минимизацию публичного API.","ar":"مهارة إعادة هيكلة Moonbit هي نهج محسّن لتحسين رمز الرست، مع التركيز على الحفاظ على السلوك وتقليل واجهة برمجة التطبيقات العامة.","en":"Minimal, feature-complete Raft for Rust — no I/O, no dependencies"},"definition":{"en":"Minimal, feature-complete Raft for Rust — no I/O, no dependencies"},"features":{"zh":["最小化 Raft 实现","减少依赖","提高代码质量","使用声明式风格和模式匹配","添加测试和文档"],"ja":["最小の Raft 実装","依存関係の削減","コード品質の向上","宣言式スタイルとパターンマッチングの使用","テストとドキュメントの追加"],"ko":["최소한의 Raft 구현","의존성 감소","코드 품질 향상","선언식 스타일과 패턴 매칭 사용","테스트 및 문서 추가"],"es":["Minimiza la API pública","Prefiere el estilo declarativo","Utiliza tipos de vista para evitar copias","Agrega pruebas y documentación","Mantiene el comportamiento y los contratos públicos"],"fr":["Minimise l''API publique","Préfère le style déclaratif","Utilise des types de vue pour éviter les copies","Ajoute des tests et de la documentation","Préserve le comportement et les contrats publics"],"de":["Minimiert die öffentliche API","Bevorzugt den deklarativen Stil","Verwendet Ansichtstypen, um Kopien zu vermeiden","Fügt Tests und Dokumentation hinzu","Beibehält das Verhalten und die öffentlichen Verträge"],"pt":["Preservação do comportamento e contratos públicos","Minimização da API pública","Preferência por estilo declarativo e correspondência de padrões","Uso de tipos de visão para evitar cópias","Adição de testes e documentação ao lado da refatoração"],"ru":["Сохранение поведения и публичных контрактов","Минимизация публичного API","Предпочтение декларативному стилю и сопоставлению с образцом","Использование типов представления для избежания копий","Добавление тестов и документации рядом с рефакторингом"],"ar":["الحفاظ على السلوك والاتفاقيات العامة","تقليل واجهة برمجة التطبيقات العامة","الاعتماد على نمط إعلاني وتطابق الأنماط","استخدام أنواع العرض لتجنب النسخ","إضافة الاختبارات والوثائق إلى جانب إعادة الهيكلة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Rust","Raft","重构","优化","依赖","性能","代码质量"],"ja":["Rust","Raft","リファクタリング","最適化","依存関係","パフォーマンス","コード品質"],"ko":["러스트","Raft","리팩토링","최적화","의존성","성능","코드 품질"],"es":["refactorización","rust","minimalista","API pública","estilo declarativo","tipos de vista","pruebas","documentación"],"fr":["refactoring","rust","minimaliste","API publique","style déclaratif","types de vue","tests","documentation"],"de":["refaktorierung","rust","minimalistisch","öffentliche API","deklarativer Stil","Ansichtstypen","Tests","Dokumentation"],"pt":["refatoração de código","otimização de desempenho","Rust","programação","desenvolvimento de software","melhoria de código","preservação de comportamento","minimização de API"],"ru":["рефакторинг кода","оптимизация производительности","Rust","программирование","разработка программного обеспечения","улучшение кода","сохранение поведения","минимизация API"],"ar":["إعادة هيكلة الرمز","تحسين الأداء","الرست","البرمجة","تطوير البرمجيات","تحسين الرمز","الحفاظ على السلوك","تقليل واجهة برمجة التطبيقات"]}},"owner":"f4ah6o","repo":"noraft.mbt","repoPath":"f4ah6o/noraft.mbt","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.453Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"moonbit-refactoring","description":"Refactor MoonBit code to be idiomatic: shrink public APIs, convert functions to methods, use pattern matching with views, add loop invariants, and ensure test coverage without regressions. Use when updating MoonBit packages or refactoring MoonBit APIs, modules, or tests.","bodyPreview":"# MoonBit Refactoring Skill\n\n## Intent\n- Preserve behavior and public contracts unless explicitly changed.\n- Minimize the public API to what callers require.\n- Prefer declarative style and pattern matching over incidental mutation.\n- Use view types (ArrayView/StringView/BytesView) to avoid copies.\n- Add tests and docs alongside refactors.\n\n## Workflow\n**Start broad, then refine locally:**\n\n1. **Architecture first**: Review package structure, dependencies, and API boundaries.\n2. **Inventory** pub","body":"# MoonBit Refactoring Skill\n\n## Intent\n- Preserve behavior and public contracts unless explicitly changed.\n- Minimize the public API to what callers require.\n- Prefer declarative style and pattern matching over incidental mutation.\n- Use view types (ArrayView/StringView/BytesView) to avoid copies.\n- Add tests and docs alongside refactors.\n\n## Workflow\n**Start broad, then refine locally:**\n\n1. **Architecture first**: Review package structure, dependencies, and API boundaries.\n2. **Inventory** public APIs and call sites (`moon doc`, `moon ide find-references`).\n3. **Pick one refactor theme** (API minimization, package splits, pattern matching, loop style).\n4. **Apply the smallest safe change**.\n5. **Update docs/tests** in the same patch.\n6. **Run `moon check`, then `moon test`**.\n7. **Use coverage** to target missing branches.\n\nAvoid local cleanups (renaming, pattern matching) until the high-level structure is sound.\n\n## Improve Package Architecture\n- Keep packages focused: aim for <10k lines per package.\n- Keep files manageable: aim for <2k lines per file.\n- Keep functions focused: aim for <200 lines per function.\n\n### Splitting Files\nTreat files in MoonBit as organizational units; move code freely within a package as long as each file stays focused on one concept.\n\n### Splitting Packages\nWhen spinning off package `A` into `A` and `B`:\n\n1. Create the new package and re-export temporarily:\n   ```mbt\n   // In package B\n   using @A { ... }  // re-export A''s APIs\n   ```\n   Ensure `moon check` passes before proceeding.\n\n2. Find and update all call sites:\n   ```bash\n   moon ide find-references <symbol>\n   ```\n   Replace bare `f` with `@B.f`.\n\n3. Remove the `use` statement once all call sites are updated.\n\n4. Audit and remove newly-unused `pub` APIs from both packages.\n\n### Guidelines\n- Prefer acyclic dependencies: lower-level packages should not import higher-level ones.\n- Only expose what downstream packages actually need.\n- Consider an `internal/` package for helpers that shouldn''t leak.\n\n## Minimize Public API and Modularize\n- Remove `pub` from helpers; keep only required exports.\n- Move helpers into `internal/` packages to block external imports.\n- Split large files by feature; files do not define modules in MoonBit.\n\n## Local refactoring\n\n### Convert Free Functions to Methods + Chaining\n- Move behavior onto the owning type for discoverability.\n- Use `..` for fluent, mutating chains when it reads clearly.\n\nExample:\n```mbt nocheck\n// Before\nfn reader_next(r : Reader) -> Char? { ... }\nlet ch = reader_next(r)\n\n// After\nfn Reader::next(self : Reader) -> Char? { ... }\nlet ch = r.next()\n```\n\nExample (chaining):\n```mbt nocheck\nbuf..write_string(\"#\\\\\")..write_char(ch)\n```\n\n### Prefer Explicit Qualification\n- Use `@pkg.fn` instead of `using` when clarity matters.\n- Keep call sites explicit during wide refactors.\n\nExample:\n```mbt nocheck\nlet n = @parser.parse_number(token)\n```\n\n### Simplify Enum Constructors When Type Is Known\n\nWhen the expected type is known from context, you can omit the full package path for enum constructors:\n\n- **Pattern matching**: Annotate the matched value; constructors need no path.\n- **Nested constructors**: Only the outermost needs the full path.\n- **Return values**: The return type provides context for constructors in the body.\n- **Collections**: Type-annotate the collection; elements inherit the type.\n\nExamples:\n```mbt\n// Pattern matching - annotate the value being matched\nlet tree : @pkga.Tree = ...\nmatch tree {\n  Leaf(x) => x\n  Node(left~, x, right~) => left.sum() + x + right.sum()\n}\n\n// Nested constructors - only outer needs full path\nlet x = @pkga.Tree::Node(left=Leaf(1), x=2, right=Leaf(3))\n\n// Return type provides context\nfn make_tree() -> @pkga.Tree {\n  Node(left=Leaf(1), x=2, right=Leaf(3))\n}\n\n// Collections - type annotation on the array\nlet trees : Array[@pkga.Tree] = [Leaf(1), Node(left=Leaf(2), x=3, right=Leaf(4))]\n```\n\n### Pattern Matching and Views\n- Pattern match arrays directly; the compiler inserts ArrayView implicitly.\n- Use `..` in the middle to match prefix and suffix at once.\n- Pattern match strings directly; avoid converting to `Array[Char]`.\n- `String`/`StringView` indexing yields `UInt16` code units. Use `for ch in s` for Unicode-aware iteration.\n\n#### we prefer pattern matching over small functions\n\nFor example,\n```mbt\n match gen_results.get(0) {\n   Some(value) => Iter::singleton(value)\n   None => Iter::empty()\n }\n```\nWe can pattern match directly, it is more efficient and as readable:\n```mbt\n match gen_results {\n   [value, ..] => Iter::singleton(value)\n   [] => Iter::empty()\n }\n```\nMoonBit pattern matching is pretty expressive, here are some more examples:\n```mbt\nmatch items {\n  [] => ()\n  [head, ..tail] => handle(head, tail)\n  [..prefix, mid, ..suffix] => handle_mid(prefix, mid, suffix)\n}\n```\n\n```mbt\nmatch s {\n  \"\" => ()\n  [..\"let\", ..rest] => handle_let(rest)\n  _ => ()\n}\n```\n#### Char literal matching\n\nUse char literal overloading for `Char`, `UInt16`, and `Int`; the examples below rely on it. This is handy when matching `String` indexing results (`UInt16`) against a char range.\n```mbt\ntest {\n  let a_int : Int = ''b''\n  if (a_int is ''a''..<''z'') { () } else { () }\n  let a_u16 : UInt16 = ''b''\n  if (a_u16 is ''a''..<''z'') { () } else { () }\n  let a_char : Char = ''b''\n  if (a_char is ''a''..<''z'') { () } else { () }\n}\n```\n\n#### Use Nested Patterns and `is`\n\n- Use `is` patterns inside `if`/`guard` to keep branches concise.\n\nExample:\n```mbt\nmatch token {\n  Some(Ident([..\"@\", ..rest])) if process(rest) is Some(x) => handle_at(rest)\n  Some(Ident(name)) => handle_ident(name)\n  None => ()\n}\n```\n\n#### Prefer Range Loops for Simple Indexing\n- Use `for i in start..<end { ... }`, `for i in start..<=end { ... }`, `for i in large>..small`, or `for i in large>=..small` for simple index loops.\n- Keep functional-state `for` loops for algorithms that update state.\n\nExample:\n```mbt\n// Before\nfor i = 0; i < len; {\n  items.push(fill)\n  continue i + 1\n}\n\n// After\nfor i in 0..<len {\n  items.push(fill)\n}\n```\n\n## Loop Specs (Dafny-Style Comments)\n- Add specs for functional-state loops.\n- Skip invariants for simple `for x in xs` loops.\n- Add TODO when a decreases clause is unclear (possible bug).\n\nExample:\n```mbt\nfor i = 0, acc = 0; i < xs.length(); {\n  acc = acc + xs[i]\n  i = i + 1\n} else { acc }\nwhere {\n  invariant: 0 <= i <= xs.length(),\n  reasoning: (\n    #| ... rigorous explanation ...\n    #| ...\n  )\n}\n```\n\n\n### Tests and Docs\n- Prefer black-box tests in `*_test.mbt` or `*.mbt.md`.\n- Add docstring tests with `mbt check` for public APIs.\n\nExample:\n```mbt\n///|\n/// Return the last element of a non-empty array.\n///\n/// # Example\n/// ```mbt check\n/// test {\n///   inspect(last([1, 2, 3]), content=\"3\")\n/// }\n/// ```\npub fn last(xs : Array[Int]) -> Int { ... }\n```\n\n## Coverage-Driven Refactors\n- Use coverage to target missing branches through public APIs.\n- Prefer small, focused tests over white-box checks.\n\nCommands:\n```bash\nmoon coverage analyze -- -f summary\nmoon coverage analyze -- -f caret -F path/to/file.mbt\n```\n\n## Moon IDE Commands\n\n```bash\nmoon doc \"<query>\"\nmoon ide outline <dir|file>\nmoon ide find-references <symbol>\nmoon ide peek-def <symbol>\nmoon ide rename <symbol> -new-name <new_name>\nmoon check\nmoon test\nmoon info\n```\nUse these commands for reliable refactoring.\n\nExample: spinning off `package_b` from `package_a`.\n\nTemporary import in `package_b`:\n```mbt\nusing @package_a { a, type B }\n```\n\nSteps:\n1. Use `moon ide find-references <symbol>` to find all call sites of `a` and `B`.\n2. Replace them with `@package_a.a` and `@package_a.B`.\n3. Remove the `using` statement and run `moon check`.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:03:14.608Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Rust-based AI Agents needing efficient code refactoring and minimal public API exposure.","zh":"适用于需要高效代码重构和最小化公共API暴露的Rust-based AI Agent。","ja":"RustベースのAIエージェントが効率的なコードのリファクタリングと最小限のパブリックAPIの公開を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"효율적인 코드 리팩토링과 최소한의 공개 API 노출이 필요한 러스트 기반 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA basados en Rust que necesitan un refactorizado de código eficiente y una exposición mínima de la API pública.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA basés sur Rust qui nécessitent un refactorisation de code efficace et une exposition minimale de l''API publique.","de":"Perfekt für auf Rust basierende KI-Agents, die eine effiziente Code-Refaktorisierung und eine minimale öffentliche API-Exposition benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA baseados em Rust que necessitam de refatoração de código eficiente e exposição mínima de API pública.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ на основе Rust, которым требуется эффективная рефакторинг кода и минимальное暴露 публичного API.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل الذكية القائمة على روست التي تحتاج إلى إعادة هيكلة الكود الفعالة وتقليل التعرض ل واجهة برمجة التطبيقات العامة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to refactor Rust code using a declarative style, pattern matching, and view types like ArrayView, StringView, and BytesView, while preserving behavior and public contracts, and minimizing dependencies.","zh":"赋予代理以声明式风格、模式匹配和视图类型（如ArrayView、StringView和BytesView）重构Rust代码的能力，同时保留行为和公共契约，并最小化依赖。","ja":"ArrayView、StringView、BytesViewなどのビュータイプを使用して、宣言的なスタイル、パターンマッチング、およびビュータイプを使用してRustコードをリファクタリングする能力をエージェントに与え、動作とパブリック契約を維持し、依存関係を最小限に抑える。","ko":"에이전트가 선언적 스타일, 패턴 매칭 및 ArrayView, StringView 및 BytesView와 같은 뷰 타입을 사용하여 러스트 코드를 리팩터링 할 수 있는 능력을 부여함으로써 동작 및 공개 계약을 유지하고 의존성을 최소화한다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a refactorizar el código de Rust utilizando un estilo declarativo, coincidencia de patrones y tipos de vista como ArrayView, StringView y BytesView, preservando el comportamiento y los contratos públicos, y minimizando las dependencias.","fr":"Permet aux agents de refactoriser le code Rust en utilisant un style déclaratif, la correspondance de modèles et des types de vue tels que ArrayView, StringView et BytesView, tout en préservant le comportement et les contrats publics, et en minimisant les dépendances.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agents, Rust-Code mithilfe eines deklarativen Stils, Mustervergleichs und Ansichtstypen wie ArrayView, StringView und BytesView zu refaktorisieren, während das Verhalten und die öffentlichen Verträge erhalten und die Abhängigkeiten minimiert werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a refatorar o código Rust usando um estilo declarativo, correspondência de padrões e tipos de visualização como ArrayView, StringView e BytesView, preservando o comportamento e os contratos públicos e minimizando as dependências.","ru":"Позволяет агентам рефакторить код Rust, используя декларативный стиль, сопоставление с образцом и типы представления, такие как ArrayView, StringView и BytesView, сохраняя поведение и публичные контракты и минимизируя зависимости.","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من إعادة هيكلة رمز روست باستخدام نمط إعلاني والتعرف على الأنماط وأنواع العرض مثل ArrayView و StringView و BytesView، مع الحفاظ على السلوك والعقود العامة وتقليل الاعتماديات."},"useCases":{"en":["Refactoring Rust code for minimal public API","Implementing declarative style and pattern matching","Optimizing code using view types to avoid copies"],"zh":["重构Rust代码以最小化公共API","实现声明式风格和模式匹配","使用视图类型优化代码以避免复制"],"ja":["パブリックAPIを最小限に抑えるためにRustコードをリファクタリングする","宣言的なスタイルとパターンマッチングを実装する","ビュータイプを使用してコードを最適化し、コピーを回避する"],"ko":["공개 API를 최소화하기 위해 러스트 코드를 리팩터링한다","선언적 스타일 및 패턴 매칭을 구현한다","뷰 타입을 사용하여 코드를 최적화하고 복사를 피한다"],"es":["Refactorización de código Rust para una API pública mínima","Implementación de un estilo declarativo y coincidencia de patrones","Optimización de código utilizando tipos de vista para evitar copias"],"fr":["Refactorisation de code Rust pour une API publique minimale","Mise en œuvre d''un style déclaratif et de la correspondance de modèles","Optimisation de code en utilisant des types de vue pour éviter les copies"],"de":["Refaktorisierung von Rust-Code für eine minimale öffentliche API","Implementierung eines deklarativen Stils und Mustervergleichs","Optimierung von Code unter Verwendung von Ansichtstypen, um Kopien zu vermeiden"],"pt":["Refatoração de código Rust para API pública mínima","Implementação de estilo declarativo e correspondência de padrões","Otimização de código usando tipos de visualização para evitar cópias"],"ru":["Рефакторинг кода Rust для минимального публичного API","Реализация декларативного стиля и сопоставления с образцом","Оптимизация кода с помощью типов представления для避ания копий"],"ar":["إعادة هيكلة رمز روست من أجل واجهة برمجة التطبيقات العامة الأقل","تنفيذ نمط الإعلان والتعرف على الأنماط","تحسين الكود باستخدام أنواع العرض لتجنب النسخ"]},"limitations":{"en":["Rust-only compatibility","No I/O operations supported","No external dependencies allowed"],"zh":["仅兼容Rust","不支持I/O操作","不允许外部依赖"],"ja":["Rustのみとの互換性","I/O操作はサポートされていない","外部依存は許可されていない"],"ko":["러스트만 호환","입출력 연산 지원 안함","외부 의존성 허용 안함"],"es":["Compatibilidad solo con Rust","No se admiten operaciones de E/S","No se permiten dependencias externas"],"fr":["Compatibilité uniquement avec Rust","Aucune opération d''E/S prise en charge","Aucune dépendance externe autorisée"],"de":["Nur Kompatibilität mit Rust","Keine E/A-Operationen unterstützt","Keine externen Abhängigkeiten erlaubt"],"pt":["Compatibilidade apenas com Rust","Nenhuma operação de E/S suportada","Nenhuma dependência externa permitida"],"ru":["Совместимость только с Rust","Нет поддержки операций ввода/вывода","Нет внешних зависимостей"],"ar":["التوافق مع روست فقط","لا تدعم عمليات الإدخال/الإخراج","لا يسمح بالاعتماديات الخارجية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
