issen","Bewertungsrahmen für Agentsysteme","Leistungsanalyse von Agentsystemen","Erweiterte Bewertungstechniken"],"pt":["Construção de estruturas de avaliação","Avaliação de sistemas de agentes","Abordagens não tradicionais","Decisões dinâmicas","Não determinismo","Múltiplas respostas corretas"],"ru":["Построение оценочных рамок","Оценка систем агентов","Нетрадиционные подходы","Динамические решения","Неопределенность","Несколько правильных ответов"],"ar":["بناء هياكل تقييم","تقييم أنظمة الوكلاء","أساليب غير تقليدية","قرارات ديناميكية","الغير محددة","إجابات متعددة صحيحة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Evaluation 技术","智能代理系统","评估框架","动态决策","非确定性","代理系统评估"],"ja":["エヴァリュエーションスキル","エージェントシステム","評価フレームワーク","動的決定","非決定性","エージェントシステム評価"],"ko":["평가 기술","에이전트 시스템","평가 프레임워크","동적 결정","비결정성","에이전트 시스템 평가"],"es":["evaluación de sistemas de agentes","decisiones dinámicas","resultados no determinísticos","marco de evaluación","análisis de rendimiento","técnicas de evaluación avanzadas","sistemas de agentes","inteligencia artificial"],"fr":["évaluation des systèmes d''agents","décisions dynamiques","résultats non déterministes","cadre d''évaluation","analyse des performances","techniques d''évaluation avancées","systèmes d''agents","intelligence artificielle"],"de":["Bewertung von Agentsystemen","dynamische Entscheidungen","nicht-deterministische Ergebnisse","Bewertungsrahmen","Leistungsanalyse","erweiterte Bewertungstechniken","Agentsysteme","künstliche Intelligenz"],"pt":["avaliação de sistemas de agentes","construção de estruturas de avaliação","abordagens não tradicionais","decisões dinâmicas","sistemas de agentes","eficácia e eficiência","técnicas de avaliação","desenvolvimento de sistemas de agentes"],"ru":["оценка систем агентов","построение оценочных рамок","нетрадиционные подходы","динамические решения","системы агентов","эффективность и производительность","техники оценки","разработка систем агентов"],"ar":["تقييم أنظمة الوكلاء","بناء هياكل تقييم","أساليب غير تقليدية","قرارات ديناميكية","أنظمة الوكلاء","فعالية وكفاءة","تقنيات تقييم","تطوير أنظمة الوكلاء"]}},"owner":"pCruvinel","repo":"antig","repoPath":"pCruvinel/antig","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"evaluation","description":"Build evaluation frameworks for agent systems","bodyPreview":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nBuild evaluation frameworks for agent systems\n\nUse this skill when working with build evaluation frameworks for agent systems.\n# Evaluation Methods for Agent Systems\n\nEvaluation of agent systems requires different approaches than traditional software or even standard language model applications. Agents make dynamic decisions, are non-deterministic between runs, and often lack single correct answers. Effective evaluation must account for these characteristics while prov","body":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nBuild evaluation frameworks for agent systems\n\nUse this skill when working with build evaluation frameworks for agent systems.\n# Evaluation Methods for Agent Systems\n\nEvaluation of agent systems requires different approaches than traditional software or even standard language model applications. Agents make dynamic decisions, are non-deterministic between runs, and often lack single correct answers. Effective evaluation must account for these characteristics while providing actionable feedback. A robust evaluation framework enables continuous improvement, catches regressions, and validates that context engineering choices achieve intended effects.\n\n## When to Activate\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- Testing agent performance systematically\n- Validating context engineering choices\n- Measuring improvements over time\n- Catching regressions before deployment\n- Building quality gates for agent pipelines\n- Comparing different agent configurations\n- Evaluating production systems continuously\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nAgent evaluation requires outcome-focused approaches that account for non-determinism and multiple valid paths. Multi-dimensional rubrics capture various quality aspects: factual accuracy, completeness, citation accuracy, source quality, and tool efficiency. LLM-as-judge provides scalable evaluation while human evaluation catches edge cases.\n\nThe key insight is that agents may find alternative paths to goals—the evaluation should judge whether they achieve right outcomes while following reasonable processes.\n\n**Performance Drivers: The 95% Finding**\nResearch on the BrowseComp evaluation (which tests browsing agents'' ability to locate hard-to-find information) found that three factors explain 95% of performance variance:\n\n| Factor | Variance Explained | Implication |\n|--------|-------------------|-------------|\n| Token usage | 80% | More tokens = better performance |\n| Number of tool calls | ~10% | More exploration helps |\n| Model choice | ~5% | Better models multiply efficiency |\n\nThis finding has significant implications for evaluation design:\n- **Token budgets matter**: Evaluate agents with realistic token budgets, not unlimited resources\n- **Model upgrades beat token increases**: Upgrading to Claude Sonnet 4.5 or GPT-5.2 provides larger gains than doubling token budgets on previous versions\n- **Multi-agent validation**: The finding validates architectures that distribute work across agents with separate context windows\n\n## Detailed Topics\n\n### Evaluation Challenges\n\n**Non-Determinism and Multiple Valid Paths**\nAgents may take completely different valid paths to reach goals. One agent might search three sources while another searches ten. They might use different tools to find the same answer. Traditional evaluations that check for specific steps fail in this context.\n\nThe solution is outcome-focused evaluation that judges whether agents achieve right outcomes while following reasonable processes.\n\n**Context-Dependent Failures**\nAgent failures often depend on context in subtle ways. An agent might succeed on simple queries but fail on complex ones. It might work well with one tool set but fail with another. Failures may emerge only after extended interaction when context accumulates.\n\nEvaluation must cover a range of complexity levels and test extended interactions, not just isolated queries.\n\n**Composite Quality Dimensions**\nAgent quality is not a single dimension. It includes factual accuracy, completeness, coherence, tool efficiency, and process quality. An agent might score high on accuracy but low in efficiency, or vice versa.\n\nEvaluation rubrics must capture multiple dimensions with appropriate weighting for the use case.\n\n### Evaluation Rubric Design\n\n**Multi-Dimensional Rubric**\nEffective rubrics cover key dimensions with descriptive levels:\n\nFactual accuracy: Claims match ground truth (excellent to failed)\n\nCompleteness: Output covers requested aspects (excellent to failed)\n\nCitation accuracy: Citations match claimed sources (excellent to failed)\n\nSource quality: Uses appropriate primary sources (excellent to failed)\n\nTool efficiency: Uses right tools reasonable number of times (excellent to failed)\n\n**Rubric Scoring**\nConvert dimension assessments to numeric scores (0.0 to 1.0) with appropriate weighting. Calculate weighted overall scores. Determine passing threshold based on use case requirements.\n\n### Evaluation Methodologies\n\n**LLM-as-Judge**\nLLM-based evaluation scales to large test sets and provides consistent judgments. The key is designing effective evaluation prompts that capture the dimensions of interest.\n\nProvide clear task description, agent output, ground truth (if available), evaluation scale with level descriptions, and request structured judgment.\n\n**Human Evaluation**\nHuman evaluation catches what automation misses. Humans notice hallucinated answers on unusual queries, system failures, and subtle biases that automated evaluation misses.\n\nEffective human evaluation covers edge cases, samples systematically, tracks patterns, and provides contextual understanding.\n\n**End-State Evaluation**\nFor agents that mutate persistent state, end-state evaluation focuses on whether the final state matches expectations rather than how the agent got there.\n\n### Test Set Design\n\n**Sample Selection**\nStart with small samples during development. Early in agent development, changes have dramatic impacts because there is abundant low-hanging fruit. Small test sets reveal large effects.\n\nSample from real usage patterns. Add known edge cases. Ensure coverage across complexity levels.\n\n**Complexity Stratification**\nTest sets should span complexity levels: simple (single tool call), medium (multiple tool calls), complex (many tool calls, significant ambiguity), and very complex (extended interaction, deep reasoning).\n\n### Context Engineering Evaluation\n\n**Testing Context Strategies**\nContext engineering choices should be validated through systematic evaluation. Run agents with different context strategies on the same test set. Compare quality scores, token usage, and efficiency metrics.\n\n**Degradation Testing**\nTest how context degradation affects performance by running agents at different context sizes. Identify performance cliffs where context becomes problematic. Establish safe operating limits.\n\n### Continuous Evaluation\n\n**Evaluation Pipeline**\nBuild evaluation pipelines that run automatically on agent changes. Track results over time. Compare versions to identify improvements or regressions.\n\n**Monitoring Production**\nTrack evaluation metrics in production by sampling interactions and evaluating randomly. Set alerts for quality drops. Maintain dashboards for trend analysis.\n\n## Practical Guidance\n\n### Building Evaluation Frameworks\n\n1. Define quality dimensions relevant to your use case\n2. Create rubrics with clear, actionable level descriptions\n3. Build test sets from real usage patterns and edge cases\n4. Implement automated evaluation pipelines\n5. Establish baseline metrics before making changes\n6. Run evaluations on all significant changes\n7. Track metrics over time for trend analysis\n8. Supplement automated evaluation with human review\n\n### Avoiding Evaluation Pitfalls\n\nOverfitting to specific paths: Evaluate outcomes, not specific steps.\nIgnoring edge cases: Include diverse test scenarios.\nSingle-metric obsession: Use multi-dimensional rubrics.\nNeglecting context effects: Test with realistic context sizes.\nSkipping human evaluation: Automated evaluation misses subtle issues.\n\n## Examples\n\n**Example 1: Simple Evaluation**\n```python\ndef evaluate_agent_response(response, expected):\n    rubric = load_rubric()\n    scores = {}\n    for dimension, config in rubric.items():\n        scores[dimension] = assess_dimension(response, expected, dimension)\n    overall = weighted_average(scores, config[\"weights\"])\n    return {\"passed\": overall >= 0.7, \"scores\": scores}\n```\n\n**Example 2: Test Set Structure**\n\nTest sets should span multiple complexity levels to ensure comprehensive evaluation:\n\n```python\ntest_set = [\n    {\n        \"name\": \"simple_lookup\",\n        \"input\": \"What is the capital of France?\",\n        \"expected\": {\"type\": \"fact\", \"answer\": \"Paris\"},\n        \"complexity\": \"simple\",\n        \"description\": \"Single tool call, factual lookup\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"medium_query\",\n        \"input\": \"Compare the revenue of Apple and Microsoft last quarter\",\n        \"complexity\": \"medium\",\n        \"description\": \"Multiple tool calls, comparison logic\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"multi_step_reasoning\",\n        \"input\": \"Analyze sales data from Q1-Q4 and create a summary report with trends\",\n        \"complexity\": \"complex\",\n        \"description\": \"Many tool calls, aggregation, analysis\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"research_synthesis\",\n        \"input\": \"Research emerging AI technologies, evaluate their potential impact, and recommend adoption strategy\",\n        \"complexity\": \"very_complex\",\n        \"description\": \"Extended interaction, deep reasoning, synthesis\"\n    }\n]\n```\n\n## Guidelines\n\n1. Use multi-dimensional rubrics, not single metrics\n2. Evaluate outcomes, not specific execution paths\n3. Cover complexity levels from simple to complex\n4. Test with realistic context sizes and histories\n5. Run evaluations continuously, not just before release\n6. Supplement LLM evaluation with human review\n7. Track metrics over time for trend detection\n8. Set clear pass/fail thresholds based on use case\n\n## Integration\n\nThis skill connects to all other skills as a cross-cutting concern:\n\n- context-fundamentals - Evaluating context usage\n- context-degradation - Detecting degradation\n- context-optimization - Measuring optimization effectiveness\n- multi-agent-patterns - Evaluating coordination\n- tool-design - Evaluating tool effectiveness\n- memory-systems - Evaluating memory quality\n\n## References\n\nInternal reference:\n- [Metrics Reference](./references/metrics.md) - Detailed evaluation metrics and implementation\n\n## References\n\nInternal skills:\n- All other skills connect to evaluation for quality measurement\n\nExternal resources:\n- LLM evaluation benchmarks\n- Agent evaluation research papers\n- Production monitoring practices\n\n---\n\n## Skill Metadata\n\n**Created**: 2025-12-20\n**Last Updated**: 2025-12-20\n**Author**: Agent Skills for Context Engineering Contributors\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:06:18.092Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT requiring dynamic evaluation frameworks for agent systems","zh":"适用于 Claude Code 和 AutoGPT 等高级 AI 代理，需要动态评估框架的代理系统","ja":"Claude Code や AutoGPT などの高度な AI エージェントに適しており、エージェント システムに必要な動的評価フレームワークを必要とする","ko":"클라우드 코드 및 오토 GPT와 같은 고급 AI 에이전트에 적합하며 에이전트 시스템에 필요한 동적 평가 프레임워크를 필요로 함","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA avanzados como Claude Code y AutoGPT que requieren marcos de evaluación dinámicos para sistemas de agentes","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA avancés comme Claude Code et AutoGPT nécessitant des cadres d''évaluation dynamiques pour les systèmes d''agents","de":"Ideal für fortschrittliche KI-Agenten wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die dynamische Bewertungsframeworks für Agentsysteme erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avançados como Claude Code e AutoGPT que requerem estruturas de avaliação dinâmicas para sistemas de agentes","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, требующих динамических рамок оценки для систем агентов","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكلاء الذكية المتقدمة مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT التي تتطلب إطارات تقييم ديناميكية لأنظمة الوكلاء"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build and utilize non-deterministic evaluation methods, accounting for dynamic decision-making and the lack of single correct answers in agent systems, leveraging protocols and frameworks tailored for agent evaluation","zh":"赋予代理构建和利用非确定性评估方法的能力，考虑到代理系统中的动态决策和缺乏单一正确答案，利用为代理评估量身定制的协议和框架","ja":"エージェントに非決定性評価方法を構築して利用する能力を与え、エージェント システムにおける動的意思決定と単一の正解がないことに対応し、エージェントの評価に特化したプロトコルとフレームワークを活用する","ko":"에이전트가 비결정적 평가 방법을 구축하고 사용할 수 있는 기능을 제공하여 에이전트 시스템에서 동적 의사 결정 및 단일 올바른 답이 없는 것을 고려하고 에이전트 평가를 위한 프로토콜 및 프레임워크를 활용함","es":"Permite a los agentes crear y utilizar métodos de evaluación no deterministas, teniendo en cuenta la toma de decisiones dinámicas y la falta de respuestas correctas únicas en los sistemas de agentes, aprovechando protocolos y marcos adaptados para la evaluación de agentes","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer et d''utiliser des méthodes d''évaluation non déterministes, en tenant compte de la prise de décision dynamique et de l''absence de réponses correctes uniques dans les systèmes d''agents, en exploitant les protocoles et les cadres adaptés pour l''évaluation des agents","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, nicht-deterministische Bewertungsmethoden zu erstellen und zu nutzen, wobei die dynamische Entscheidungsfindung und das Fehlen eindeutiger richtiger Antworten in Agentsystemen berücksichtigt werden, indem Protokolle und Frameworks für die Agentenbewertung genutzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir e utilizar métodos de avaliação não determinísticos, considerando a tomada de decisões dinâmicas e a falta de respostas corretas únicas em sistemas de agentes, aproveitando protocolos e estruturas personalizadas para avaliação de agentes","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать и использовать неопределенные методы оценки, учитывая динамическое принятие решений и отсутствие единственно правильных ответов в системах агентов, используя протоколы и рамки, адаптированные для оценки агентов","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من بناء واستخدام أساليب تقييم غير محددة، مع مراعاة اتخاذ القرارات الديناميكي وعدم وجود إجابات صحيحة فريدة في أنظمة الوكلاء، واستغلال البروتوكولات والإطارات المخصصة لتقييم الوكلاء"},"useCases":{"en":["Building evaluation frameworks for agent systems","Assessing non-deterministic agent performance","Developing dynamic decision-making metrics"],"zh":["为代理系统构建评估框架","评估非确定性代理性能","开发动态决策指标"],"ja":["エージェント システムの評価フレームワークを構築する","非決定性エージェントのパフォーマンスを評価する","動的意思決定メトリックを開発する"],"ko":["에이전트 시스템을 위한 평가 프레임워크 구축","비결정적 에이전트 성능 평가","동적 의사 결정 메트릭 개발"],"es":["Creación de marcos de evaluación para sistemas de agentes","Evaluación del rendimiento no determinista de los agentes","Desarrollo de métricas de toma de decisiones dinámicas"],"fr":["Création de cadres d''évaluation pour les systèmes d''agents","Évaluation de la performance non déterministe des agents","Développement de métriques de prise de décision dynamique"],"de":["Erstellung von Bewertungsframeworks für Agentsysteme","Bewertung der nicht-deterministischen Leistung von Agenten","Entwicklung von Metriken für dynamische Entscheidungsfindung"],"pt":["Construir estruturas de avaliação para sistemas de agentes","Avaliar o desempenho não determinístico dos agentes","Desenvolver métricas de tomada de decisões dinâmicas"],"ru":["Построение рамок оценки для систем агентов","Оценка неопределенного поведения агентов","Разработка метрик динамического принятия решений"],"ar":["بناء إطارات تقييم لأنظمة الوكلاء","تقييم أداء الوكلاء غير المحدد","تطوير مقاييس اتخاذ القرارات الديناميكي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of agent systems'' unique characteristics","May need customization for specific agent architectures"],"zh":["需要了解代理系统的独特特征","可能需要针对特定代理架构的定制"],"ja":["エージェント システムの独自の特性を理解する必要がある","特定のエージェント アーキテクチャに合わせたカスタマイズが必要になる可能性がある"],"ko":["에이전트 시스템의 고유한 특성을 이해해야 함","특정 에이전트 아키텍처에 맞춘 사용자 정의가 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de las características únicas de los sistemas de agentes","Puede necesitar personalización para arquitecturas de agentes específicas"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des caractéristiques uniques des systèmes d''agents","Peut nécessiter une personnalisation pour des architectures d''agents spécifiques"],"de":["Erfordert Verständnis der einzigartigen Eigenschaften von Agentsystemen","Kann Anpassung für spezifische Agentenarchitekturen erfordern"],"pt":["Exige compreensão das características únicas dos sistemas de agentes","Pode precisar de personalização para arquiteturas de agentes específicas"],"ru":["Требует понимания уникальных характеристик систем агентов","Может потребовать настройки для конкретных архитектур агентов"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا للخصائص الفريدة لأنظمة الوكلاء","يمكن أن يحتاج إلى تخصيص لعمليات بناء الوكلاء المحددة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
