estion de modèles","Gestion de prix","Suivi d''utilisation","API de plateforme","Intégration avec les projets de développement","Modèles et guides pour l''utilisation de la plateforme"],"de":["Modellmanagement","Preisgestaltung","Nutzungsnachverfolgung","Plattform-API","Integration mit Entwicklungsprojekten","Muster und Anleitungen für die Verwendung der Plattform"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de modelos","Precificação","Rastreamento de uso","APIs para integração","Padrões para desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Управление моделями","Ценообразование","Отслеживание использования","API для интеграции","Шаблоны для разработки"],"ar":["إدارة النماذج","التصفية","التتبع","واجهات برمجة التطبيقات للدمج","نماذج لتصميم التطبيقات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Fal 平台技能","模型管理","定价和费用跟踪","使用情况跟踪","平台 API","代码示例","开发者指南"],"ja":["Fal プラットフォームスキル","モデル管理","価格設定とコストの追跡","使用状況の追跡","プラットフォーム API","コード例","開発者ガイド"],"ko":["Fal 플랫폼 스킬","모델 관리","가격 책정 및 비용 추적","사용량 추적","플랫폼 API","코드 예시","개발자 가이드"],"es":["plataforma fal","gestión de modelos","precios","seguimiento de uso","api de plataforma","desarrollo de software","integración de plataforma","patrones de desarrollo","guías de desarrollo"],"fr":["plateforme fal","gestion de modèles","prix","suivi d''utilisation","api de plateforme","développement de logiciels","intégration de plateforme","modèles de développement","guides de développement"],"de":["fal-plattform","modellmanagement","preisgestaltung","nutzungsnachverfolgung","plattform-api","software-entwicklung","plattform-integration","entwicklungs-muster","entwicklungs-anleitungen"],"pt":["fal platform","gerenciamento de modelos","precificação","rastreamento de uso","api","desenvolvimento de software","integração de sistemas"],"ru":["платформа fal","управление моделями","ценообразование","отслеживание использования","api","разработка программного обеспечения","интеграция систем"],"ar":["منصة فال","إدارة النماذج","التصفية","التتبع","واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","تصميم التطبيقات","دمج الأنظمة"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"fal-platform","description":"Platform APIs for model management, pricing, and usage tracking","bodyPreview":"# Fal Platform\n\n## Overview\n\nPlatform APIs for model management, pricing, and usage tracking\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to work with platform apis for model management, pricing, and usage tracking.\n\n## Instructions\n\nThis skill provides guidance and patterns for platform apis for model management, pricing, and usage tracking.\n\nFor more information, see the [source repository](https://github.com/fal-ai-community/skills/blob/main/skills/claude.ai/fal-platform/SKILL.md)","body":"# Fal Platform\n\n## Overview\n\nPlatform APIs for model management, pricing, and usage tracking\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to work with platform apis for model management, pricing, and usage tracking.\n\n## Instructions\n\nThis skill provides guidance and patterns for platform apis for model management, pricing, and usage tracking.\n\nFor more information, see the [source repository](https://github.com/fal-ai-community/skills/blob/main/skills/claude.ai/fal-platform/SKILL.md).\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:08:21.026Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code, AutoGPT, and LangChain needing comprehensive model management, pricing, and usage tracking capabilities via platform APIs.","zh":"适用于像 Claude Code、AutoGPT 和 LangChain 等需要通过平台 API 进行全面模型管理、定价和使用情况跟踪能力的 AI 代理。","ja":"Claude Code、AutoGPT、LangChain などの、プラットフォーム API を介した包括的なモデル管理、価格設定、および使用状況追跡機能を必要とする AI エージェントに適しています。","ko":"클라우드 코드, 오토지피티, 랭체인 등의 플랫폼 API를 통한 종합적인 모델 관리, 가격 설정, 사용량 추적 기능이 필요한 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Claude Code, AutoGPT y LangChain que necesitan capacidades de gestión de modelos, precios y seguimiento de uso completas a través de API de plataforma.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Claude Code, AutoGPT et LangChain nécessitant une gestion de modèle, des prix et des capacités de suivi d''utilisation complètes via des API de plateforme.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Claude Code, AutoGPT und LangChain, die umfassende Modellverwaltungs-, Preis- und Nutzungsverfolgungsfunktionen über Plattform-APIs benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Claude Code, AutoGPT e LangChain que necessitam de capacidades de gerenciamento de modelo, precificação e rastreamento de uso abrangentes por meio de APIs de plataforma.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code, AutoGPT и LangChain, которым необходимы всесторонние возможности управления моделью, ценообразования и отслеживания использования через платформенные API.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT و LangChain الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات إدارة نموذجية و تسعير و تتبع استخدام شاملة من خلال واجهات برمجة تطبيقات المنصة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage models, track usage, and optimize pricing strategies using platform APIs, leveraging APIs for model management, pricing, and usage tracking, and providing guidance on patterns for these APIs.","zh":"赋予代理管理模型、跟踪使用情况和优化定价策略的能力，使用平台 API 进行模型管理、定价和使用情况跟踪，并为这些 API 的模式提供指导。","ja":"エージェントがモデルを管理し、使用状況を追跡し、価格戦略を最適化する能力を提供します。プラットフォーム API を使用してモデル管理、価格設定、使用状況追跡を行い、これらの API のパターンに関するガイダンスを提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 모델을 관리하고 사용량을 추적하며 가격 전략을 최적화 할 수 있는 능력을 제공합니다. 플랫폼 API를 사용하여 모델 관리, 가격 설정, 사용량 추적을 수행하며, 이러한 API의 패턴에 대한 가이드를 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar modelos, realizar un seguimiento del uso y optimizar las estrategias de precios utilizando API de plataforma, aprovechando las API para la gestión de modelos, precios y seguimiento de uso, y brindando orientación sobre patrones para estas API.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer les modèles, de suivre l''utilisation et d''optimiser les stratégies de prix en utilisant les API de plateforme, en exploitant les API pour la gestion de modèles, les prix et le suivi d''utilisation, et en fournissant des conseils sur les modèles pour ces API.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Modelle zu verwalten, den Nutzen zu verfolgen und Preisstrategien mit Hilfe von Plattform-APIs zu optimieren, indem es APIs für Modellverwaltung, Preise und Nutzungsverfolgung nutzt und Anleitungen zu Mustern für diese APIs bietet.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar modelos, rastrear o uso e otimizar estratégias de precificação usando APIs de plataforma, aproveitando as APIs para gerenciamento de modelo, precificação e rastreamento de uso e fornecendo orientação sobre padrões para essas APIs.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять моделями, отслеживать использование и оптимизировать стратегии ценообразования с помощью платформенных API, используя API для управления моделью, ценообразования и отслеживания использования, и предоставляя рекомендации по шаблонам для этих API.","ar":"يتمكن العملاء من إدارة النماذج وتتبع الاستخدام وضبط استراتيجيات التسعير باستخدام واجهات برمجة تطبيقات المنصة، واستخدام واجهات برمجة تطبيقات إدارة النموذج والتسعير وتتبع الاستخدام، وتقديم إرشادات حول أنماط لهذه واجهات برمجة التطبيقات."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating model deployment and tracking","Generating pricing strategies based on usage data","Optimizing model performance through usage analytics"],"zh":["自动化模型部署和跟踪","根据使用数据生成定价策略","通过使用分析优化模型性能"],"ja":["モデルデプロイと追跡の自動化","使用データに基づく価格戦略の生成","使用分析によるモデル性能の最適化"],"ko":["모델 배포 및 추적 자동화","사용량 데이터에 기반한 가격 전략 생성","사용량 분석을 통한 모델 성능 최적화"],"es":["Automatizar la implementación y el seguimiento de modelos","Generar estrategias de precios en función de los datos de uso","Optimizar el rendimiento del modelo a través de análisis de uso"],"fr":["Automatiser le déploiement et le suivi des modèles","Générer des stratégies de prix en fonction des données d''utilisation","Optimiser les performances du modèle via l''analyse d''utilisation"],"de":["Automatisieren der Modellbereitstellung und -nachverfolgung","Erzeugen von Preisstrategien auf der Grundlage von Nutzungsdaten","Optimieren der Modellleistung durch Nutzungsanalyse"],"pt":["Automatizar a implantação de modelos e o rastreamento","Gerar estratégias de precificação com base em dados de uso","Otimizar o desempenho do modelo por meio de análise de uso"],"ru":["Автоматизация развертывания моделей и отслеживания","Генерация стратегий ценообразования на основе данных об использовании","Оптимизация производительности модели посредством анализа использования"],"ar":["تأتمتة نشر النماذج وتتبعها","توليد استراتيجيات التسعير根据 بيانات الاستخدام","تحسين أداء النموذج من خلال تحليل الاستخدام"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to platform APIs","Limited to model management, pricing, and usage tracking functionalities"],"zh":["需要访问平台 API","仅限模型管理、定价和使用情况跟踪功能"],"ja":["プラットフォーム API へのアクセスが必要","モデル管理、価格設定、使用状況追跡機能のみ"],"ko":["플랫폼 API에 대한 액세스가 필요함","모델 관리, 가격 설정, 사용량 추적 기능만 제공"],"es":["Requiere acceso a las API de la plataforma","Limitado a funcionalidades de gestión de modelos, precios y seguimiento de uso"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès aux API de plateforme","Limité aux fonctionnalités de gestion de modèles, de prix et de suivi d''utilisation"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf Plattform-APIs","Begrenzt auf Funktionalitäten für Modellverwaltung, Preise und Nutzungsverfolgung"],"pt":["Exige acesso às APIs de plataforma","Limitado a funcionalidades de gerenciamento de modelo, precificação e rastreamento de uso"],"ru":["Требует доступа к платформенным API","Ограничен функциональностью управления моделью, ценообразования и отслеживания использования"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى واجهات برمجة تطبيقات المنصة","محدود بوظائف إدارة النموذج والتسعير وتتبع الاستخدام"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('YPYT1/All-skills/fp-ts-react', 'community', 'YPYT1', 'All-skills', 'YPYT1/All-skills', 'fp-ts-react', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z', '2026-02-18T07:08:23.826Z', NULL, '{"id":"YPYT1/All-skills/fp-ts-react","name":"fp-ts-react","description":{"zh":"fp-ts-react 提供了实用的函数式编程模式，用于构建 React 应用，确保类型安全和高效状态管理。","ja":"fp-ts-react は、React アプリの構築に役立つ実用的関数型プログラミングパターンを提供し、型安全性と効率的な状態管理を保証します。","ko":"fp-ts-react는 리액트 애플리케이션을 구축하는 데 도움이 되는 실제 함수형 프로그래밍 패턴을 제공하며, 타입 안전성과 효율적인 상태 관리를 보장합니다.","es":"fp-ts-react ofrece patrones prácticos para aplicaciones React con fp-ts para una gestión de estado segura","fr":"fp-ts-react propose des modèles pratiques pour les applications React avec fp-ts pour une gestion d''état sécurisée","de":"fp-ts-react bietet praktische Muster für React-Anwendungen mit fp-ts für eine sichere Zustandsverwaltung","pt":"fp-ts-react é uma coleção de padrões práticos para aplicativos React, focando em gerenciamento de estado seguro e funcional","ru":"fp-ts-react - это коллекция практических шаблонов для приложений React, ориентированных на безопасное функциональное управление состоянием","ar":"fp-ts-react هي مجموعة من الأنماط العملية لتطبيقات React، تركز على إدارة الحالة الوظيفية الآمنة","en":"集合了所有的openclaw,claudecode,open等各个平台所有的skills"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"fp-ts-react：React 中的函数式编程","ja":"fp-ts-react：React の関数型プログラミング","ko":"fp-ts-react: 리액트의 함수형 프로그래밍","es":"fp-ts-react: Patrones funcionales para React","fr":"fp-ts-react : Modèles fonctionnels pour React","de":"fp-ts-react: Funktionale Muster für React","pt":"fp-ts-react: Padrões Práticos para Aplicativos React","ru":"fp-ts-react: Практические шаблоны для приложений React","ar":"fp-ts-react: أنماط عملية لتطبيقات React","en":"fp-ts-react"},"description":{"zh":"fp-ts-react 提供了实用的函数式编程模式，用于构建 React 应用，确保类型安全和高效状态管理。","ja":"fp-ts-react は、React アプリの構築に役立つ実用的関数型プログラミングパターンを提供し、型安全性と効率的な状態管理を保証します。","ko":"fp-ts-react는 리액트 애플리케이션을 구축하는 데 도움이 되는 실제 함수형 프로그래밍 패턴을 제공하며, 타입 안전성과 효율적인 상태 관리를 보장합니다.","es":"fp-ts-react ofrece patrones prácticos para aplicaciones React con fp-ts para una gestión de estado segura","fr":"fp-ts-react propose des modèles pratiques pour les applications React avec fp-ts pour une gestion d''état sécurisée","de":"fp-ts-react bietet praktische Muster für React-Anwendungen mit fp-ts für eine sichere Zustandsverwaltung","pt":"fp-ts-react é uma coleção de padrões práticos para aplicativos React, focando em gerenciamento de estado seguro e funcional","ru":"fp-ts-react - это коллекция практических шаблонов для приложений React, ориентированных на безопасное функциональное управление состоянием","ar":"fp-ts-react هي مجموعة من الأنماط العملية لتطبيقات React، تركز على إدارة الحالة الوظيفية الآمنة","en":"集合了所有的openclaw,claudecode,open等各个平台所有的skills"},"definition":{"en":"集合了所有的openclaw,claudecode,open等各个平台所有的skills"},"features":{"zh":["类型安全状态管理","函数式编程模式","实用数据获取和错误处理","表单验证和错误积累","支持 React 18/19 和 Next.js 14/15"],"ja":["型安全な状態管理","関数型プログラミングパターン","実用データ取得とエラー処理","フォームバリデーションとエラーアキュム","React 18/19 と Next.js 14/15 のサポート"],"ko":["타입 안전 상태 관리","함수형 프로그래밍 패턴","실제 데이터 가져오기 및 오류 처리","폼 유효성 검사 및 오류 누적","리액트 18/19 및 넥스트.js 14/15 지원"],"es":["Gestión de estado segura con fp-ts","Patrones funcionales para aplicaciones React","Manejo de estados de carga/error/éxito en la recuperación de datos","Implementación de validación de formularios con acumulación de errores","Compatibilidad con React 18/19 y Next.js 14/15"],"fr":["Gestion d''état sécurisée avec fp-ts","Modèles fonctionnels pour les applications React","Gestion des états de chargement/erreur/succès dans la récupération de données","Implémentation de la validation de formulaires avec accumulation d''erreurs","Compatibilité avec React 18/19 et Next.js 14/15"],"de":["Sichere Zustandsverwaltung mit fp-ts","Funktionale Muster für React-Anwendungen","Verwaltung von Lade-/Fehler-/Erfolgszuständen bei der Datenabfrage","Implementierung der Formularvalidierung mit Fehlerakkumulation","Kompatibilität mit React 18/19 und Next.js 14/15"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de estado seguro com fp-ts","Padrões funcionais práticos para aplicativos React","Suporte a React 18/19 e Next.js 14/15","Implementação de validação de formulários com acumulação de erros","Manipulação de estados de carregamento/erro/sucesso em busca de dados"],"ru":["Безопасное управление состоянием с помощью fp-ts","Практические функциональные шаблоны для приложений React","Поддержка React 18/19 и Next.js 14/15","Реализация валидации форм с накоплением ошибок","Обработка состояний загрузки/ошибки/успеха при получении данных"],"ar":["إدارة الحالة الآمنة مع fp-ts","أنماط وظيفية عملية لتطبيقات React","دعم React 18/19 و Next.js 14/15","تنفيذ التحقق من صحة النماذج مع تراكم الأخطاء","معالجة حالات التحميل/الخطأ/النجاح في استرجاع البيانات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["fp-ts-react","React 函数式编程","类型安全状态管理","函数式编程模式","数据获取和错误处理","表单验证和错误积累"],"ja":["fp-ts-react","React 関数型プログラミング","型安全な状態管理","関数型プログラミングパターン","データ取得とエラー処理","フォームバリデーションとエラーアキュム"],"ko":["fp-ts-react","리액트 함수형 프로그래밍","타입 안전 상태 관리","함수형 프로그래밍 패턴","데이터 가져오기 및 오류 처리","폼 유효성 검사 및 오류 누적"],"es":["fp-ts-react","patrones funcionales","React","gestión de estado","fp-ts","validación de formularios","recuperación de datos","Next.js"],"fr":["fp-ts-react","modèles fonctionnels","React","gestion d''état","fp-ts","validation de formulaires","récupération de données","Next.js"],"de":["fp-ts-react","funktionale Muster","React","Zustandsverwaltung","fp-ts","Formularvalidierung","Datenabfrage","Next.js"],"pt":["fp-ts-react","React","fp-ts","gerenciamento de estado","padrões funcionais","validação de formulários","busca de dados","Next.js","React 18/19"],"ru":["fp-ts-react","React","fp-ts","управление состоянием","функциональные шаблоны","валидация форм","получение данных","Next.js","React 18/19"],"ar":["fp-ts-react","React","fp-ts","إدارة الحالة","أنماط وظيفية","تحقق من صحة النماذج","استرجاع البيانات","Next.js","React 18/19"]}},"owner":"YPYT1","repo":"All-skills","repoPath":"YPYT1/All-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"fp-ts-react","description":"Practical patterns for using fp-ts with React - hooks, state, forms, data fetching. Use when building React apps with functional programming patterns. Works with React 18/19, Next.js 14/15.","bodyPreview":"# Functional Programming in React\n\nPractical patterns for React apps. No jargon, just code that works.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- When building React apps with fp-ts for type-safe state management\n- When handling loading/error/success states in data fetching\n- When implementing form validation with error accumulation\n- When using React 18/19 or Next.js 14/15 with functional patterns\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Pattern | Use When |\n|---------|----------|\n| `Option` | Value might be missing (us","body":"# Functional Programming in React\n\nPractical patterns for React apps. No jargon, just code that works.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- When building React apps with fp-ts for type-safe state management\n- When handling loading/error/success states in data fetching\n- When implementing form validation with error accumulation\n- When using React 18/19 or Next.js 14/15 with functional patterns\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Pattern | Use When |\n|---------|----------|\n| `Option` | Value might be missing (user not loaded yet) |\n| `Either` | Operation might fail (form validation) |\n| `TaskEither` | Async operation might fail (API calls) |\n| `RemoteData` | Need to show loading/error/success states |\n| `pipe` | Chaining multiple transformations |\n\n---\n\n## 1. State with Option (Maybe It''s There, Maybe Not)\n\nUse `Option` instead of `null | undefined` for clearer intent.\n\n### Basic Pattern\n\n```typescript\nimport { useState } from ''react''\nimport * as O from ''fp-ts/Option''\nimport { pipe } from ''fp-ts/function''\n\ninterface User {\n  id: string\n  name: string\n  email: string\n}\n\nfunction UserProfile() {\n  // Option says \"this might not exist yet\"\n  const [user, setUser] = useState<O.Option<User>>(O.none)\n\n  const handleLogin = (userData: User) => {\n    setUser(O.some(userData))\n  }\n\n  const handleLogout = () => {\n    setUser(O.none)\n  }\n\n  return pipe(\n    user,\n    O.match(\n      // When there''s no user\n      () => <button onClick={() => handleLogin({ id: ''1'', name: ''Alice'', email: ''alice@example.com'' })}>\n        Log In\n      </button>,\n      // When there''s a user\n      (u) => (\n        <div>\n          <p>Welcome, {u.name}!</p>\n          <button onClick={handleLogout}>Log Out</button>\n        </div>\n      )\n    )\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Chaining Optional Values\n\n```typescript\nimport * as O from ''fp-ts/Option''\nimport { pipe } from ''fp-ts/function''\n\ninterface Profile {\n  user: O.Option<{\n    name: string\n    settings: O.Option<{\n      theme: string\n    }>\n  }>\n}\n\nfunction getTheme(profile: Profile): string {\n  return pipe(\n    profile.user,\n    O.flatMap(u => u.settings),\n    O.map(s => s.theme),\n    O.getOrElse(() => ''light'') // default\n  )\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Form Validation with Either\n\nEither is perfect for validation: `Left` = errors, `Right` = valid data.\n\n### Simple Form Validation\n\n```typescript\nimport * as E from ''fp-ts/Either''\nimport * as A from ''fp-ts/Array''\nimport { pipe } from ''fp-ts/function''\n\n// Validation functions return Either<ErrorMessage, ValidValue>\nconst validateEmail = (email: string): E.Either<string, string> =>\n  email.includes(''@'')\n    ? E.right(email)\n    : E.left(''Invalid email address'')\n\nconst validatePassword = (password: string): E.Either<string, string> =>\n  password.length >= 8\n    ? E.right(password)\n    : E.left(''Password must be at least 8 characters'')\n\nconst validateName = (name: string): E.Either<string, string> =>\n  name.trim().length > 0\n    ? E.right(name.trim())\n    : E.left(''Name is required'')\n```\n\n### Collecting All Errors (Not Just First One)\n\n```typescript\nimport * as E from ''fp-ts/Either''\nimport { sequenceS } from ''fp-ts/Apply''\nimport { getSemigroup } from ''fp-ts/NonEmptyArray''\nimport { pipe } from ''fp-ts/function''\n\n// This collects ALL errors, not just the first one\nconst validateAll = sequenceS(E.getApplicativeValidation(getSemigroup<string>()))\n\ninterface SignupForm {\n  name: string\n  email: string\n  password: string\n}\n\ninterface ValidatedForm {\n  name: string\n  email: string\n  password: string\n}\n\nfunction validateForm(form: SignupForm): E.Either<string[], ValidatedForm> {\n  return pipe(\n    validateAll({\n      name: pipe(validateName(form.name), E.mapLeft(e => [e])),\n      email: pipe(validateEmail(form.email), E.mapLeft(e => [e])),\n      password: pipe(validatePassword(form.password), E.mapLeft(e => [e])),\n    })\n  )\n}\n\n// Usage in component\nfunction SignupForm() {\n  const [form, setForm] = useState({ name: '''', email: '''', password: '''' })\n  const [errors, setErrors] = useState<string[]>([])\n\n  const handleSubmit = () => {\n    pipe(\n      validateForm(form),\n      E.match(\n        (errs) => setErrors(errs),     // Show all errors\n        (valid) => {\n          setErrors([])\n          submitToServer(valid)         // Submit valid data\n        }\n      )\n    )\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <form onSubmit={e => { e.preventDefault(); handleSubmit() }}>\n      <input\n        value={form.name}\n        onChange={e => setForm(f => ({ ...f, name: e.target.value }))}\n        placeholder=\"Name\"\n      />\n      <input\n        value={form.email}\n        onChange={e => setForm(f => ({ ...f, email: e.target.value }))}\n        placeholder=\"Email\"\n      />\n      <input\n        type=\"password\"\n        value={form.password}\n        onChange={e => setForm(f => ({ ...f, password: e.target.value }))}\n        placeholder=\"Password\"\n      />\n\n      {errors.length > 0 && (\n        <ul style={{ color: ''red'' }}>\n          {errors.map((err, i) => <li key={i}>{err}</li>)}\n        </ul>\n      )}\n\n      <button type=\"submit\">Sign Up</button>\n    </form>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Field-Level Errors (Better UX)\n\n```typescript\ntype FieldErrors = Partial<Record<keyof SignupForm, string>>\n\nfunction validateFormWithFieldErrors(form: SignupForm): E.Either<FieldErrors, ValidatedForm> {\n  const errors: FieldErrors = {}\n\n  pipe(validateName(form.name), E.mapLeft(e => { errors.name = e }))\n  pipe(validateEmail(form.email), E.mapLeft(e => { errors.email = e }))\n  pipe(validatePassword(form.password), E.mapLeft(e => { errors.password = e }))\n\n  return Object.keys(errors).length > 0\n    ? E.left(errors)\n    : E.right({ name: form.name.trim(), email: form.email, password: form.password })\n}\n\n// In component\n{errors.email && <span className=\"error\">{errors.email}</span>}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Fetching with TaskEither\n\nTaskEither = async operation that might fail. Perfect for API calls.\n\n### Basic Fetch Hook\n\n```typescript\nimport { useState, useEffect } from ''react''\nimport * as TE from ''fp-ts/TaskEither''\nimport * as E from ''fp-ts/Either''\nimport { pipe } from ''fp-ts/function''\n\n// Wrap fetch in TaskEither\nconst fetchJson = <T>(url: string): TE.TaskEither<Error, T> =>\n  TE.tryCatch(\n    async () => {\n      const res = await fetch(url)\n      if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}`)\n      return res.json()\n    },\n    (err) => err instanceof Error ? err : new Error(String(err))\n  )\n\n// Custom hook\nfunction useFetch<T>(url: string) {\n  const [data, setData] = useState<T | null>(null)\n  const [error, setError] = useState<Error | null>(null)\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true)\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    setLoading(true)\n    setError(null)\n\n    pipe(\n      fetchJson<T>(url),\n      TE.match(\n        (err) => {\n          setError(err)\n          setLoading(false)\n        },\n        (result) => {\n          setData(result)\n          setLoading(false)\n        }\n      )\n    )()\n  }, [url])\n\n  return { data, error, loading }\n}\n\n// Usage\nfunction UserList() {\n  const { data, error, loading } = useFetch<User[]>(''/api/users'')\n\n  if (loading) return <div>Loading...</div>\n  if (error) return <div>Error: {error.message}</div>\n  return (\n    <ul>\n      {data?.map(user => <li key={user.id}>{user.name}</li>)}\n    </ul>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Chaining API Calls\n\n```typescript\n// Fetch user, then fetch their posts\nconst fetchUserWithPosts = (userId: string) => pipe(\n  fetchJson<User>(`/api/users/${userId}`),\n  TE.flatMap(user => pipe(\n    fetchJson<Post[]>(`/api/users/${userId}/posts`),\n    TE.map(posts => ({ ...user, posts }))\n  ))\n)\n```\n\n### Parallel API Calls\n\n```typescript\nimport { sequenceT } from ''fp-ts/Apply''\n\n// Fetch multiple things at once\nconst fetchDashboardData = () => pipe(\n  sequenceT(TE.ApplyPar)(\n    fetchJson<User>(''/api/user''),\n    fetchJson<Stats>(''/api/stats''),\n    fetchJson<Notifications[]>(''/api/notifications'')\n  ),\n  TE.map(([user, stats, notifications]) => ({\n    user,\n    stats,\n    notifications\n  }))\n)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. RemoteData Pattern (The Right Way to Handle Async State)\n\nStop using `{ data, loading, error }` booleans. Use a proper state machine.\n\n### The Pattern\n\n```typescript\n// RemoteData has exactly 4 states - no impossible combinations\ntype RemoteData<E, A> =\n  | { _tag: ''NotAsked'' }                    // Haven''t started yet\n  | { _tag: ''Loading'' }                     // In progress\n  | { _tag: ''Failure''; error: E }           // Failed\n  | { _tag: ''Success''; data: A }            // Got it!\n\n// Constructors\nconst notAsked = <E, A>(): RemoteData<E, A> => ({ _tag: ''NotAsked'' })\nconst loading = <E, A>(): RemoteData<E, A> => ({ _tag: ''Loading'' })\nconst failure = <E, A>(error: E): RemoteData<E, A> => ({ _tag: ''Failure'', error })\nconst success = <E, A>(data: A): RemoteData<E, A> => ({ _tag: ''Success'', data })\n\n// Pattern match all states\nfunction fold<E, A, R>(\n  rd: RemoteData<E, A>,\n  onNotAsked: () => R,\n  onLoading: () => R,\n  onFailure: (e: E) => R,\n  onSuccess: (a: A) => R\n): R {\n  switch (rd._tag) {\n    case ''NotAsked'': return onNotAsked()\n    case ''Loading'': return onLoading()\n    case ''Failure'': return onFailure(rd.error)\n    case ''Success'': return onSuccess(rd.data)\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Hook with RemoteData\n\n```typescript\nfunction useRemoteData<T>(fetchFn: () => Promise<T>) {\n  const [state, setState] = useState<RemoteData<Error, T>>(notAsked())\n\n  const execute = async () => {\n    setState(loading())\n    try {\n      const data = await fetchFn()\n      setState(success(data))\n    } catch (err) {\n      setState(failure(err instanceof Error ? err : new Error(String(err))))\n    }\n  }\n\n  return { state, execute }\n}\n\n// Usage\nfunction UserProfile({ userId }: { userId: string }) {\n  const { state, execute } = useRemoteData(() =>\n    fetch(`/api/users/${userId}`).then(r => r.json())\n  )\n\n  useEffect(() => { execute() }, [userId])\n\n  return fold(\n    state,\n    () => <button onClick={execute}>Load User</button>,\n    () => <Spinner />,\n    (err) => <ErrorMessage message={err.message} onRetry={execute} />,\n    (user) => <UserCard user={user} />\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Why RemoteData Beats Booleans\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ BAD: Impossible states are possible\ninterface BadState {\n  data: User | null\n  loading: boolean\n  error: Error | null\n}\n// Can have: { data: user, loading: true, error: someError } - what does that mean?!\n\n// ✅ GOOD: Only valid states exist\ntype GoodState = RemoteData<Error, User>\n// Can only be: NotAsked | Loading | Failure | Success\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Referential Stability (Preventing Re-renders)\n\nfp-ts values like `O.some(1)` create new objects each render. React sees them as \"changed\".\n\n### The Problem\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ BAD: Creates new Option every render\nfunction BadComponent() {\n  const [value, setValue] = useState(O.some(1))\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    // This runs EVERY render because O.some(1) !== O.some(1)\n    console.log(''value changed'')\n  }, [value])\n}\n```\n\n### Solution 1: useMemo\n\n```typescript\n// ✅ GOOD: Memoize Option creation\nfunction GoodComponent() {\n  const [rawValue, setRawValue] = useState<number | null>(1)\n\n  const value = useMemo(\n    () => O.fromNullable(rawValue),\n    [rawValue]  // Only recreate when rawValue changes\n  )\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    // Now this only runs when rawValue actually changes\n    console.log(''value changed'')\n  }, [rawValue])  // Depend on raw value, not Option\n}\n```\n\n### Solution 2: fp-ts-react-stable-hooks\n\n```bash\nnpm install fp-ts-react-stable-hooks\n```\n\n```typescript\nimport { useStableO, useStableEffect } from ''fp-ts-react-stable-hooks''\nimport * as O from ''fp-ts/Option''\nimport * as Eq from ''fp-ts/Eq''\n\nfunction StableComponent() {\n  // Uses fp-ts equality instead of reference equality\n  const [value, setValue] = useStableO(O.some(1))\n\n  // Effect that understands Option equality\n  useStableEffect(\n    () => { console.log(''value changed'') },\n    [value],\n    Eq.tuple(O.getEq(Eq.eqNumber))  // Custom equality\n  )\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Dependency Injection with Context\n\nUse ReaderTaskEither for testable components with injected dependencies.\n\n### Setup Dependencies\n\n```typescript\nimport * as RTE from ''fp-ts/ReaderTaskEither''\nimport { pipe } from ''fp-ts/function''\nimport { createContext, useContext, ReactNode } from ''react''\n\n// Define what services your app needs\ninterface AppDependencies {\n  api: {\n    getUser: (id: string) => Promise<User>\n    updateUser: (id: string, data: Partial<User>) => Promise<User>\n  }\n  analytics: {\n    track: (event: string, data?: object) => void\n  }\n}\n\n// Create context\nconst DepsContext = createContext<AppDependencies | null>(null)\n\n// Provider\nfunction AppProvider({ deps, children }: { deps: AppDependencies; children: ReactNode }) {\n  return <DepsContext.Provider value={deps}>{children}</DepsContext.Provider>\n}\n\n// Hook to use dependencies\nfunction useDeps(): AppDependencies {\n  const deps = useContext(DepsContext)\n  if (!deps) throw new Error(''Missing AppProvider'')\n  return deps\n}\n```\n\n### Use in Components\n\n```typescript\nfunction UserProfile({ userId }: { userId: string }) {\n  const { api, analytics } = useDeps()\n  const [user, setUser] = useState<RemoteData<Error, User>>(notAsked())\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    setUser(loading())\n    api.getUser(userId)\n      .then(u => {\n        setUser(success(u))\n        analytics.track(''user_viewed'', { userId })\n      })\n      .catch(e => setUser(failure(e)))\n  }, [userId, api, analytics])\n\n  // render...\n}\n```\n\n### Testing with Mock Dependencies\n\n```typescript\nconst mockDeps: AppDependencies = {\n  api: {\n    getUser: jest.fn().mockResolvedValue({ id: ''1'', name: ''Test User'' }),\n    updateUser: jest.fn().mockResolvedValue({ id: ''1'', name: ''Updated'' }),\n  },\n  analytics: {\n    track: jest.fn(),\n  },\n}\n\ntest(''loads user on mount'', async () => {\n  render(\n    <AppProvider deps={mockDeps}>\n      <UserProfile userId=\"1\" />\n    </AppProvider>\n  )\n\n  await screen.findByText(''Test User'')\n  expect(mockDeps.api.getUser).toHaveBeenCalledWith(''1'')\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. React 19 Patterns\n\n### use() for Promises (React 19+)\n\n```typescript\nimport { use, Suspense } from ''react''\n\n// Instead of useEffect + useState for data fetching\nfunction UserProfile({ userPromise }: { userPromise: Promise<User> }) {\n  const user = use(userPromise)  // Suspends until resolved\n  return <div>{user.name}</div>\n}\n\n// Parent provides the promise\nfunction App() {\n  const userPromise = fetchUser(''1'')  // Start fetching immediately\n\n  return (\n    <Suspense fallback={<Spinner />}>\n      <UserProfile userPromise={userPromise} />\n    </Suspense>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### useActionState for Forms (React 19+)\n\n```typescript\nimport { useActionState } from ''react''\nimport * as E from ''fp-ts/Either''\n\ninterface FormState {\n  errors: string[]\n  success: boolean\n}\n\nasync function submitForm(\n  prevState: FormState,\n  formData: FormData\n): Promise<FormState> {\n  const data = {\n    email: formData.get(''email'') as string,\n    password: formData.get(''password'') as string,\n  }\n\n  // Use Either for validation\n  const result = pipe(\n    validateForm(data),\n    E.match(\n      (errors) => ({ errors, success: false }),\n      async (valid) => {\n        await saveToServer(valid)\n        return { errors: [], success: true }\n      }\n    )\n  )\n\n  return result\n}\n\nfunction SignupForm() {\n  const [state, formAction, isPending] = useActionState(submitForm, {\n    errors: [],\n    success: false\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <form action={formAction}>\n      <input name=\"email\" type=\"email\" />\n      <input name=\"password\" type=\"password\" />\n\n      {state.errors.map(e => <p key={e} className=\"error\">{e}</p>)}\n\n      <button disabled={isPending}>\n        {isPending ? ''Submitting...'' : ''Sign Up''}\n      </button>\n    </form>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### useOptimistic for Instant Feedback (React 19+)\n\n```typescript\nimport { useOptimistic } from ''react''\n\nfunction TodoList({ todos }: { todos: Todo[] }) {\n  const [optimisticTodos, addOptimisticTodo] = useOptimistic(\n    todos,\n    (state, newTodo: Todo) => [...state, { ...newTodo, pending: true }]\n  )\n\n  const addTodo = async (text: string) => {\n    const newTodo = { id: crypto.randomUUID(), text, done: false }\n\n    // Immediately show in UI\n    addOptimisticTodo(newTodo)\n\n    // Actually save (will reconcile when done)\n    await saveTodo(newTodo)\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <ul>\n      {optimisticTodos.map(todo => (\n        <li key={todo.id} style={{ opacity: todo.pending ? 0.5 : 1 }}>\n          {todo.text}\n        </li>\n      ))}\n    </ul>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Common Patterns Cheat Sheet\n\n### Render Based on Option\n\n```typescript\n// Pattern 1: match\npipe(\n  maybeUser,\n  O.match(\n    () => <LoginButton />,\n    (user) => <UserMenu user={user} />\n  )\n)\n\n// Pattern 2: fold (same as match)\nO.fold(\n  () => <LoginButton />,\n  (user) => <UserMenu user={user} />\n)(maybeUser)\n\n// Pattern 3: getOrElse for simple defaults\nconst name = pipe(\n  maybeUser,\n  O.map(u => u.name),\n  O.getOrElse(() => ''Guest'')\n)\n```\n\n### Render Based on Either\n\n```typescript\npipe(\n  validationResult,\n  E.match(\n    (errors) => <ErrorList errors={errors} />,\n    (data) => <SuccessMessage data={data} />\n  )\n)\n```\n\n### Safe Array Rendering\n\n```typescript\nimport * as A from ''fp-ts/Array''\n\n// Get first item safely\nconst firstUser = pipe(\n  users,\n  A.head,\n  O.map(user => <Featured user={user} />),\n  O.getOrElse(() => <NoFeaturedUser />)\n)\n\n// Find specific item\nconst adminUser = pipe(\n  users,\n  A.findFirst(u => u.role === ''admin''),\n  O.map(admin => <AdminBadge user={admin} />),\n  O.toNullable  // or O.getOrElse(() => null)\n)\n```\n\n### Conditional Props\n\n```typescript\n// Add props only if value exists\nconst modalProps = {\n  isOpen: true,\n  ...pipe(\n    maybeTitle,\n    O.map(title => ({ title })),\n    O.getOrElse(() => ({}))\n  )\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## When to Use What\n\n| Situation | Use |\n|-----------|-----|\n| Value might not exist | `Option<T>` |\n| Operation might fail (sync) | `Either<E, A>` |\n| Async operation might fail | `TaskEither<E, A>` |\n| Need loading/error/success UI | `RemoteData<E, A>` |\n| Form with multiple validations | `Either` with validation applicative |\n| Dependency injection | Context + `ReaderTaskEither` |\n| Prevent re-renders with fp-ts | `useMemo` or `fp-ts-react-stable-hooks` |\n\n---\n\n## Libraries\n\n- **[fp-ts](https://github.com/gcanti/fp-ts)** - Core library\n- **[fp-ts-react-stable-hooks](https://github.com/mblink/fp-ts-react-stable-hooks)** - Stable hooks\n- **[@devexperts/remote-data-ts](https://github.com/devexperts/remote-data-ts)** - RemoteData\n- **[io-ts](https://github.com/gcanti/io-ts)** - Runtime type validation\n- **[zod](https://github.com/colinhacks/zod)** - Schema validation (works great with fp-ts)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:08:23.826Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing type-safe state management in React applications with fp-ts","zh":"非常适合需要在 React 应用中使用 fp-ts 进行类型安全状态管理的前端代理","ja":"React アプリケーションで fp-ts を使用した型安全なステート管理が必要なフロントエンド エージェントに最適","ko":"React 애플리케이션에서 fp-ts를 사용한 타입 안전한 상태 관리가 필요한 프론트엔드 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes frontend que necesitan administración de estado segura con tipos en aplicaciones de React con fp-ts","fr":"Parfait pour les agents frontend ayant besoin d''une gestion d''état sécurisée par type dans les applications React avec fp-ts","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agents, die eine typsichere Zustandsverwaltung in React-Anwendungen mit fp-ts benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que necessitam de gerenciamento de estado com segurança de tipo em aplicações React com fp-ts","ru":"Идеально для фронтенд-агентов, которым требуется управление состоянием с безопасностью типов в приложениях React с fp-ts","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم الذي يحتاج إلى إدارة حالة آمنة في تطبيقات React مع fp-ts"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to handle loading, error, and success states in data fetching using fp-ts, and implement form validation with error accumulation in React 18/19 or Next.js 14/15, leveraging functional patterns and libraries like Option for robust state management","zh":"赋予代理处理使用 fp-ts 进行数据获取的加载、错误和成功状态，并在 React 18/19 或 Next.js 14/15 中使用功能模式和库（如 Option）实现表单验证和错误积累，以实现强