rung der Konvertierung","Erstellung von personalisierten und effektiven Popups","Verbesserung der Benutzererfahrung","Integration mit Marketing-Tools","Analyse und Verfolgung von Ergebnissen"],"pt":["Otimização de popup para conversão","Criação de popups personalizados","Análise de desempenho de popup","Otimização para dispositivos móveis","Integração com marketing de produto"],"ru":["Оптимизация попап для конверсии","Создание индивидуальных попапов","Анализ производительности попап","Оптимизация для мобильных устройств","Интеграция с маркетингом продукта"],"ar":["تحسين نافذة.pop-up للتحويل","إنشاء نافذة.pop-up مخصصة","تحليل أداء نافذة.pop-up","تحسين للجهاز المحمول","التكامل مع تسويق المنتج"]},"keywords":{"zh":["弹出式转化率优化","弹出式窗口设计","转化率优化","品牌知名度提高","用户体验优化","弹出式窗口推荐","弹出式窗口分析","网站优化","数字营销"],"ja":["ポップアップCRO","ポップアップデザイン","変換率最適化","ブランド認知度向上","ユーザーエクスペリエンス最適化","ポップアップ推奨","ポップアップ分析","ウェブサイト最適化","デジタルマーケティング"],"ko":["팝업 전환률 최적화","팝업 디자인","전환률 최적화","브랜드 인지도 향상","사용자 경험 최적화","팝업 추천","팝업 분석","웹사이트 최적화","디지털 마케팅"],"es":["popup CRO","optimización de popups","conversión","experiencia del usuario","desarrollo web","marketing digital","popups personalizados","análisis de resultados"],"fr":["popup CRO","optimisation des popups","conversion","expérience utilisateur","développement web","marketing numérique","popups personnalisés","analyse des résultats"],"de":["Popup CRO","Optimierung von Popups","Konvertierung","Benutzererfahrung","Webentwicklung","Digitales Marketing","Personalisierte Popups","Ergebnisanalyse"],"pt":["popup CRO","otimização de popup","conversão de popup","marketing de produto","análise de desempenho","otimização para dispositivos móveis"],"ru":["попап CRO","оптимизация попап","конверсия попап","маркетинг продукта","анализ производительности","оптимизация для мобильных устройств"],"ar":["عنوان CRO","تحسين نافذة.pop-up","تحويل نافذة.pop-up","تسويق المنتج","تحليل الأداء","تحسين للجهاز المحمول"]}},"owner":"jtordoya-dev","repo":"Antigravity_setup","repoPath":"jtordoya-dev/Antigravity_setup","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"popup-cro","description":"When the user wants to create or optimize popups, modals, overlays, slide-ins, or banners for conversion purposes. Also use when the user mentions exit intent, popup conversions, modal optimization, lead capture popup, email popup, announcement banner, or overlay. For forms outside of popups, see form-cro. For general page conversion optimization, see page-cro.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Popup CRO\n\nYou are an expert in popup and modal optimization. Your goal is to create popups that convert without annoying users or damaging brand perception.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore providing recommendations, understand:\n\n1. **Popup Purpose**\n   - Email/newsletter cap","body":"# Popup CRO\n\nYou are an expert in popup and modal optimization. Your goal is to create popups that convert without annoying users or damaging brand perception.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore providing recommendations, understand:\n\n1. **Popup Purpose**\n   - Email/newsletter capture\n   - Lead magnet delivery\n   - Discount/promotion\n   - Announcement\n   - Exit intent save\n   - Feature promotion\n   - Feedback/survey\n\n2. **Current State**\n   - Existing popup performance?\n   - What triggers are used?\n   - User complaints or feedback?\n   - Mobile experience?\n\n3. **Traffic Context**\n   - Traffic sources (paid, organic, direct)\n   - New vs. returning visitors\n   - Page types where shown\n\n---\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. Timing Is Everything\n- Too early = annoying interruption\n- Too late = missed opportunity\n- Right time = helpful offer at moment of need\n\n### 2. Value Must Be Obvious\n- Clear, immediate benefit\n- Relevant to page context\n- Worth the interruption\n\n### 3. Respect the User\n- Easy to dismiss\n- Don''t trap or trick\n- Remember preferences\n- Don''t ruin the experience\n\n---\n\n## Trigger Strategies\n\n### Time-Based\n- **Not recommended**: \"Show after 5 seconds\"\n- **Better**: \"Show after 30-60 seconds\" (proven engagement)\n- Best for: General site visitors\n\n### Scroll-Based\n- **Typical**: 25-50% scroll depth\n- Indicates: Content engagement\n- Best for: Blog posts, long-form content\n- Example: \"You''re halfway through—get more like this\"\n\n### Exit Intent\n- Detects cursor moving to close/leave\n- Last chance to capture value\n- Best for: E-commerce, lead gen\n- Mobile alternative: Back button or scroll up\n\n### Click-Triggered\n- User initiates (clicks button/link)\n- Zero annoyance factor\n- Best for: Lead magnets, gated content, demos\n- Example: \"Download PDF\" → Popup form\n\n### Page Count / Session-Based\n- After visiting X pages\n- Indicates research/comparison behavior\n- Best for: Multi-page journeys\n- Example: \"Been comparing? Here''s a summary...\"\n\n### Behavior-Based\n- Add to cart abandonment\n- Pricing page visitors\n- Repeat page visits\n- Best for: High-intent segments\n\n---\n\n## Popup Types\n\n### Email Capture Popup\n**Goal**: Newsletter/list subscription\n\n**Best practices:**\n- Clear value prop (not just \"Subscribe\")\n- Specific benefit of subscribing\n- Single field (email only)\n- Consider incentive (discount, content)\n\n**Copy structure:**\n- Headline: Benefit or curiosity hook\n- Subhead: What they get, how often\n- CTA: Specific action (\"Get Weekly Tips\")\n\n### Lead Magnet Popup\n**Goal**: Exchange content for email\n\n**Best practices:**\n- Show what they get (cover image, preview)\n- Specific, tangible promise\n- Minimal fields (email, maybe name)\n- Instant delivery expectation\n\n### Discount/Promotion Popup\n**Goal**: First purchase or conversion\n\n**Best practices:**\n- Clear discount (10%, $20, free shipping)\n- Deadline creates urgency\n- Single use per visitor\n- Easy to apply code\n\n### Exit Intent Popup\n**Goal**: Last-chance conversion\n\n**Best practices:**\n- Acknowledge they''re leaving\n- Different offer than entry popup\n- Address common objections\n- Final compelling reason to stay\n\n**Formats:**\n- \"Wait! Before you go...\"\n- \"Forget something?\"\n- \"Get 10% off your first order\"\n- \"Questions? Chat with us\"\n\n### Announcement Banner\n**Goal**: Site-wide communication\n\n**Best practices:**\n- Top of page (sticky or static)\n- Single, clear message\n- Dismissable\n- Links to more info\n- Time-limited (don''t leave forever)\n\n### Slide-In\n**Goal**: Less intrusive engagement\n\n**Best practices:**\n- Enters from corner/bottom\n- Doesn''t block content\n- Easy to dismiss or minimize\n- Good for chat, support, secondary CTAs\n\n---\n\n## Design Best Practices\n\n### Visual Hierarchy\n1. Headline (largest, first seen)\n2. Value prop/offer (clear benefit)\n3. Form/CTA (obvious action)\n4. Close option (easy to find)\n\n### Sizing\n- Desktop: 400-600px wide typical\n- Don''t cover entire screen\n- Mobile: Full-width bottom or center, not full-screen\n- Leave space to close (visible X, click outside)\n\n### Close Button\n- Always visible (top right is convention)\n- Large enough to tap on mobile\n- \"No thanks\" text link as alternative\n- Click outside to close\n\n### Mobile Considerations\n- Can''t detect exit intent (use alternatives)\n- Full-screen overlays feel aggressive\n- Bottom slide-ups work well\n- Larger touch targets\n- Easy dismiss gestures\n\n### Imagery\n- Product image or preview\n- Face if relevant (increases trust)\n- Minimal for speed\n- Optional—copy can work alone\n\n---\n\n## Copy Formulas\n\n### Headlines\n- Benefit-driven: \"Get [result] in [timeframe]\"\n- Question: \"Want [desired outcome]?\"\n- Command: \"Don''t miss [thing]\"\n- Social proof: \"Join [X] people who...\"\n- Curiosity: \"The one thing [audience] always get wrong about [topic]\"\n\n### Subheadlines\n- Expand on the promise\n- Address objection (\"No spam, ever\")\n- Set expectations (\"Weekly tips in 5 min\")\n\n### CTA Buttons\n- First person works: \"Get My Discount\" vs \"Get Your Discount\"\n- Specific over generic: \"Send Me the Guide\" vs \"Submit\"\n- Value-focused: \"Claim My 10% Off\" vs \"Subscribe\"\n\n### Decline Options\n- Polite, not guilt-trippy\n- \"No thanks\" / \"Maybe later\" / \"I''m not interested\"\n- Avoid manipulative: \"No, I don''t want to save money\"\n\n---\n\n## Frequency and Rules\n\n### Frequency Capping\n- Show maximum once per session\n- Remember dismissals (cookie/localStorage)\n- 7-30 days before showing again\n- Respect user choice\n\n### Audience Targeting\n- New vs. returning visitors (different needs)\n- By traffic source (match ad message)\n- By page type (context-relevant)\n- Exclude converted users\n- Exclude recently dismissed\n\n### Page Rules\n- Exclude checkout/conversion flows\n- Consider blog vs. product pages\n- Match offer to page context\n\n---\n\n## Compliance and Accessibility\n\n### GDPR/Privacy\n- Clear consent language\n- Link to privacy policy\n- Don''t pre-check opt-ins\n- Honor unsubscribe/preferences\n\n### Accessibility\n- Keyboard navigable (Tab, Enter, Esc)\n- Focus trap while open\n- Screen reader compatible\n- Sufficient color contrast\n- Don''t rely on color alone\n\n### Google Guidelines\n- Intrusive interstitials hurt SEO\n- Mobile especially sensitive\n- Allow: Cookie notices, age verification, reasonable banners\n- Avoid: Full-screen before content on mobile\n\n---\n\n## Measurement\n\n### Key Metrics\n- **Impression rate**: Visitors who see popup\n- **Conversion rate**: Impressions → Submissions\n- **Close rate**: How many dismiss immediately\n- **Engagement rate**: Interaction before close\n- **Time to close**: How long before dismissing\n\n### What to Track\n- Popup views\n- Form focus\n- Submission attempts\n- Successful submissions\n- Close button clicks\n- Outside clicks\n- Escape key\n\n### Benchmarks\n- Email popup: 2-5% conversion typical\n- Exit intent: 3-10% conversion\n- Click-triggered: Higher (10%+, self-selected)\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Popup Design\n- **Type**: Email capture, lead magnet, etc.\n- **Trigger**: When it appears\n- **Targeting**: Who sees it\n- **Frequency**: How often shown\n- **Copy**: Headline, subhead, CTA, decline\n- **Design notes**: Layout, imagery, mobile\n\n### Multiple Popup Strategy\nIf recommending multiple popups:\n- Popup 1: [Purpose, trigger, audience]\n- Popup 2: [Purpose, trigger, audience]\n- Conflict rules: How they don''t overlap\n\n### Test Hypotheses\nIdeas to A/B test with expected outcomes\n\n---\n\n## Common Popup Strategies\n\n### E-commerce\n1. Entry/scroll: First-purchase discount\n2. Exit intent: Bigger discount or reminder\n3. Cart abandonment: Complete your order\n\n### B2B SaaS\n1. Click-triggered: Demo request, lead magnets\n2. Scroll: Newsletter/blog subscription\n3. Exit intent: Trial reminder or content offer\n\n### Content/Media\n1. Scroll-based: Newsletter after engagement\n2. Page count: Subscribe after multiple visits\n3. Exit intent: Don''t miss future content\n\n### Lead Generation\n1. Time-delayed: General list building\n2. Click-triggered: Specific lead magnets\n3. Exit intent: Final capture attempt\n\n---\n\n## Experiment Ideas\n\n### Placement & Format Experiments\n\n**Banner Variations**\n- Top bar vs. banner below header\n- Sticky banner vs. static banner\n- Full-width vs. contained banner\n- Banner with countdown timer vs. without\n\n**Popup Formats**\n- Center modal vs. slide-in from corner\n- Full-screen overlay vs. smaller modal\n- Bottom bar vs. corner popup\n- Top announcements vs. bottom slideouts\n\n**Position Testing**\n- Test popup sizes on desktop and mobile\n- Left corner vs. right corner for slide-ins\n- Test visibility without blocking content\n\n---\n\n### Trigger Experiments\n\n**Timing Triggers**\n- Exit intent vs. 30-second delay vs. 50% scroll depth\n- Test optimal time delay (10s vs. 30s vs. 60s)\n- Test scroll depth percentage (25% vs. 50% vs. 75%)\n- Page count trigger (show after X pages viewed)\n\n**Behavior Triggers**\n- Show based on user intent prediction\n- Trigger based on specific page visits\n- Return visitor vs. new visitor targeting\n- Show based on referral source\n\n**Click Triggers**\n- Click-triggered popups for lead magnets\n- Button-triggered vs. link-triggered modals\n- Test in-content triggers vs. sidebar triggers\n\n---\n\n### Messaging & Content Experiments\n\n**Headlines & Copy**\n- Test attention-grabbing vs. informational headlines\n- \"Limited-time offer\" vs. \"New feature alert\" messaging\n- Urgency-focused copy vs. value-focused copy\n- Test headline length and specificity\n\n**CTAs**\n- CTA button text variations\n- Button color testing for contrast\n- Primary + secondary CTA vs. single CTA\n- Test decline text (friendly vs. neutral)\n\n**Visual Content**\n- Add countdown timers to create urgency\n- Test with/without images\n- Product preview vs. generic imagery\n- Include social proof in popup\n\n---\n\n### Personalization Experiments\n\n**Dynamic Content**\n- Personalize popup based on visitor data\n- Show industry-specific content\n- Tailor content based on pages visited\n- Use progressive profiling (ask more over time)\n\n**Audience Targeting**\n- New vs. returning visitor messaging\n- Segment by traffic source\n- Target based on engagement level\n- Exclude already-converted visitors\n\n---\n\n### Frequency & Rules Experiments\n\n- Test frequency capping (once per session vs. once per week)\n- Cool-down period after dismissal\n- Test different dismiss behaviors\n- Show escalating offers over multiple visits\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What''s the primary goal for this popup?\n2. What''s your current popup performance (if any)?\n3. What traffic sources are you optimizing for?\n4. What incentive can you offer?\n5. Are there compliance requirements (GDPR, etc.)?\n6. Mobile vs. desktop traffic split?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **form-cro**: For optimizing the form inside the popup\n- **page-cro**: For the page context around popups\n- **email-sequence**: For what happens after popup conversion\n- **ab-test-setup**: For testing popup variations\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:09:26.428Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Marketing Agents needing advanced popup and modal optimization capabilities for enhanced user experience.","zh":"非常适合需要高级弹出窗口和模态优化功能以增强用户体验的营销代理。","ja":"マーケティングエージェントが高度なポップアップとモーダル最適化機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 팝업과 모달 최적화 기능이 필요한 마케팅 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de marketing que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de optimización de ventanas emergentes y modales para una experiencia de usuario mejorada.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de marketing qui ont besoin de capacités avancées d''optimisation des fenêtres contextuelles et des modales pour améliorer l''expérience utilisateur.","de":"Perfekt für Marketing-Agenten, die erweiterte Funktionen zur Optimierung von Popups und Modals für eine verbesserte Benutzererfahrung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Marketing que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de otimização de popups e modais para uma experiência do usuário aprimorada.","ru":"Идеально для агентов по маркетингу, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности оптимизации всплывающих окон и модальных окон для улучшения пользовательского опыта.","ar":"مثالي لوسائل إعلانية التسويقية التي تحتاج إلى возможيات متقدمة لتحسين النوافذ المنبثقة والتحسين المودالي لتجربة المستخدم المحسنة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create targeted popups that convert without annoying users, utilizing product marketing context from `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` and optimizing for email/newsletter capture, all while preserving brand perception.","zh":"赋予代理创建有针对性的弹出窗口的能力，这些弹出窗口可以在不打扰用户的情况下转化，利用来自 `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` 的产品营销背景，并优化电子邮件/新闻稿捕获，同时保持品牌认知。","ja":"エージェントがユーザーを刺激せずにコンバージョンを実現するターゲットを絞ったポップアップを作成できるようにし、`.claude/product-marketing-context.md` からの製品マーケティングコンテキストを利用し、電子メール/ニュースレターのキャプチャを最適化し、ブランド認知を維持します。","ko":"에이전트가 사용자를 방해하지 않고 전환을 달성할 수 있는 대상별 팝업을 생성할 수 있도록 하며, `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`에서 제품 마케팅 컨텍스트를 활용하여 이메일/뉴스레터 캡처를 최적화하고 브랜드 인식을 유지합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear ventanas emergentes dirigidas que conviertan sin molestar a los usuarios, utilizando el contexto de marketing de productos de `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` y optimizando para la captura de correo electrónico/boletín, todo mientras se mantiene la percepción de la marca.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des fenêtres contextuelles ciblées qui convertissent sans ennuyer les utilisateurs, en utilisant le contexte de marketing de produits de `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` et en optimisant pour la capture d''e-mail/lettre d''information, le tout en préservant la perception de la marque.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, gezielte Popups zu erstellen, die ohne die Nutzer zu belästigen, konvertieren, unter Verwendung des Produktmarketing-Kontexts von `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` und Optimierung für die Erfassung von E-Mail/Newsletter, während die Markenwahrnehmung erhalten bleibt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar popups direcionados que convertem sem irritar os usuários, utilizando o contexto de marketing de produtos de `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` e otimizando para captura de e-mail/boletim, ao mesmo tempo em que preserva a percepção da marca.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать целевые всплывающие окна, которые конвертируют без раздражения пользователей, используя контекст маркетинга продукта из `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` и оптимизируя для захвата электронной почты/новостей,，同时 сохраняя восприятие бренда.","ar":"يتمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء نوافذ منبثقة مستهدفة تُحوّل دون إزعاج المستخدمين، باستخدام سياق تسويق المنتج من `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` وتحسينه لالتقاط البريد الإلكتروني/النشرة الإخبارية، مع الحفاظ على تصور العلامة التجارية في الوقت نفسه."},"useCases":{"en":["Optimizing popup placement for maximum conversion","Generating targeted modal content for specific user segments","Analyzing user interaction with popups to improve brand perception"],"zh":["为最大转化率优化弹出窗口位置","为特定用户段生成目标模态内容","分析用户与弹出窗口的交互以提高品牌认知"],"ja":["最大コンバージョン率のためにポップアップの配置を最適化する","特定のユーザーセグメントに対してターゲットを絞ったモーダルコンテンツを生成する","ブランド認知を向上させるためにユーザーとポップアップの相互作用を分析する"],"ko":["최대 전환율을 위해 팝업 배치 최적화","특정 사용자 세그먼트를 위한 대상 모달 콘텐츠 생성","브랜드 인식을 향상시키기 위한 사용자와 팝업의 상호작용 분석"],"es":["Optimización de la colocación de ventanas emergentes para una mayor conversión","Generación de contenido de modal dirigido para segmentos de usuarios específicos","Análisis de la interacción del usuario con las ventanas emergentes para mejorar la percepción de la marca"],"fr":["Optimisation du placement des fenêtres contextuelles pour une conversion maximale","Génération de contenu de modal ciblé pour des segments d''utilisateurs spécifiques","Analyse de l''interaction de l''utilisateur avec les fenêtres contextuelles pour améliorer la perception de la marque"],"de":["Optimierung der Platzierung von Popups für eine maximale Konversion","Generierung von gezieltem Modal-Inhalt für bestimmte Benutzersegmente","Analyse der Benutzerinteraktion mit Popups, um die Markenwahrnehmung zu verbessern"],"pt":["Otimizando a colocação de popups para conversão máxima","Gerando conteúdo de modal direcionado para segmentos de usuário específicos","Analysando a interação do usuário com popups para melhorar a percepção da marca"],"ru":["Оптимизация размещения всплывающих окон для максимальной конверсии","Генерация целевого модального контента для конкретных сегментов пользователей","Анализ взаимодействия пользователя с всплывающими окнами для улучшения восприятия бренда"],"ar":["تحسين وضع النوافذ المنبثقة لتحقيق أقصى تحويل","генерация محتوى مودالي مستهدف لفئات مستخدم محددة","تحليل تفاعل المستخدم مع النوافذ المنبثقة لتحسين تصور العلامة التجارية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires product marketing context from `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` for optimal performance","Limited to popup and modal optimization"],"zh":["需要来自 `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` 的产品营销背景以实现最佳性能","仅限弹出窗口和模态优化"],"ja":["`.claude/product-marketing-context.md` からの製品マーケティングコンテキストが最適なパフォーマンスを実現するために必要","ポップアップとモーダルの最適化のみに限定"],"ko":["`.claude/product-marketing-context.md`에서 제품 마케팅 컨텍스트가 최적의 성능을实现하는 데 필요","팝업 및 모달 최적화에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere contexto de marketing de productos de `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` para un rendimiento óptimo","Limitado a la optimización de ventanas emergentes y modales"],"fr":["Nécessite un contexte de marketing de produits de `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` pour des performances optimales","Limité à l''optimisation des fenêtres contextuelles et des modales"],"de":["Benötigt Produktmarketing-Kontext von `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` für optimale Leistung","Begrenzt auf die Optimierung von Popups und Modals"],"pt":["Requer contexto de marketing de produtos de `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` para desempenho ótimo","Limitado à otimização de popups e modais"],"ru":["Требует контекста маркетинга продукта из `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` для оптимальной производительности","Ограничен оптимизацией всплывающих окон и модальных окон"],"ar":["يتطلب سياق تسويق المنتج من `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` للأداء الأمثل","محدود بتحسين النوافذ المنبثقة والتحسين المودالي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('malue-ai/dazee-small/trend-spotter', 'community', 'malue-ai', 'dazee-small', 'malue-ai/dazee-small', 'trend-spotter', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z', '2026-02-18T07:09:14.112Z', NULL, '{"id":"malue-ai/dazee-small/trend-spotter","name":"trend-spotter","description":{"zh":"趋势发现工具帮助您从多个数据源中找到最新的热点话题和趋势","ja":"トレンド分析ツールは、複数のデータソースから最新のホットトピックとトレンドを発見するのに役立ちます","ko":"트렌드 분석 도구는 여러 데이터 소스에서 최신 핫 이슈와 트렌드를 발견하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"El detectador de tendencias analiza noticias, redes sociales y datos de búsqueda para identificar las últimas tendencias y temas de actualidad","fr":"Le repéreur de tendances analyse les actualités, les médias sociaux et les données de recherche pour identifier les dernières tendances et sujets d''actualité","de":"Der Trend-Spotter analysiert Nachrichten, soziale Medien und Suchdaten, um die neuesten Trends und Themen zu identifizieren","pt":"O Descobridor de Tendências é uma ferramenta que ajuda a encontrar novas tendências e tópicos quentes em diferentes fontes de dados","ru":"Тренд-споттер - это инструмент, который помогает обнаружить новые тенденции и горячие темы в различных источниках данных","ar":"كاشف الاتجاهات هو أداة تساعد في العثور على اتجاهات جديدة ومواضيع ساخنة في مصادر بيانات مختلفة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"趋势发现工具 - Latest 热点话题分析","ja":"トレンド分析ツール - 最新のホットトピックを発見","ko":"트렌드 분석 도구 - 최신 핫 이슈 발견","es":"Detectador de tendencias: análisis de noticias y redes so...","fr":"Repéreur de tendances: analyse de l''actualité et des médi...","de":"Trend-Spotter: Analyse von Nachrichten und sozialen Medien","pt":"Descobridor de Tendências: Encontre Novas Oportunidades","ru":"Тренд-споттер: Раскройте новые возможности","ar":"كاشف الاتجاهات: اختراق الفرص الجديدة","en":"trend-spotter"},"description":{"zh":"趋势发现工具帮助您从多个数据源中找到最新的热点话题和趋势","ja":"トレンド分析ツールは、複数のデータソースから最新のホットトピックとトレンドを発見するのに役立ちます","ko":"트렌드 분석 도구는 여러 데이터 소스에서 최신 핫 이슈와 트렌드를 발견하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"El detectador de tendencias analiza noticias, redes sociales y datos de búsqueda para identificar las últimas tendencias y temas de actualidad","fr":"Le repéreur de tendances analyse les actualités, les médias sociaux et les données de recherche pour identifier les dernières tendances et sujets d''actualité","de":"Der Trend-Spotter analysiert Nachrichten, soziale Medien und Suchdaten, um die neuesten Trends und Themen zu identifizieren","pt":"O Descobridor de Tendências é uma ferramenta que ajuda a encontrar novas tendências e tópicos quentes em diferentes fontes de dados","ru":"Тренд-споттер - это инструмент, который помогает обнаружить новые тенденции и горячие темы в различных источниках данных","ar":"كاشف الاتجاهات هو أداة تساعد في العثور على اتجاهات جديدة ومواضيع ساخنة في مصادر بيانات مختلفة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["从Google Trends获取实时热搜数据","分析新闻和社交媒体中的热点话题","提供行业动向和市场趋势分析","支持多语言和多地区的数据分析","帮助内容创作者找到热门话题"],"ja":["Google Trendsからリアルタイムのホット検索データを取得","ニュースとソーシャルメディアのホットトピックを分析","業界動向と市場トレンドの分析を提供","多言語と多地域のデータ分析をサポート","コンテンツクリエイターがホットトピックを発見するのを助ける"],"ko":["Google Trends에서 실시간 핫 검색 데이터를 가져옵니다","뉴스와 소셜 미디어의 핫 이슈를 분석합니다","업계 동향과 시장 트렌드 분석을 제공합니다","다중 언어와 다중 지역의 데이터 분석을 지원합니다","콘텐츠 제작자가 핫 이슈를 발견하는 데 도움이 됩니다"],"es":["Análisis de noticias y redes sociales","Identificación de tendencias y patrones","Análisis de datos de búsqueda","Descubrimiento de temas de actualidad","Integración con Google Trends"],"fr":["Analyse des actualités et des médias sociaux","Identification de tendances et de modèles","Analyse des données de recherche","Découverte de sujets d''actualité","Intégration avec Google Trends"],"de":["Analyse von Nachrichten und sozialen Medien","Identifizierung von Trends und Mustern","Analyse von Suchdaten","Entdeckung von Themen","Integration mit Google Trends"],"pt":["Análise de tendências em tempo real","Identificação de tópicos quentes em noticias e mídias sociais","Integração com dados de busca do Google","Filtragem de resultados por localização geográfica","Análise de dados em diferentes idiomas"],"ru":["Анализ тенденций в реальном времени","Определение горячих тем в новостях и социальных сетях","Интеграция с данными поиска Google","Фильтрация результатов по географическому местоположению","Анализ данных на разных языках"],"ar":["تحليل الاتجاهات في الوقت الحقيقي","تحديد المواضيع الساخنة في الأخبار والوسائط الاجتماعية","التكامل مع بيانات بحث جوجل","تصفية النتائج حسب الموقع الجغرافي","تحليل البيانات بلغات مختلفة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["趋势发现","热点话题分析","Google Trends","新闻分析","社交媒体分析","搜索数据分析","内容创作","产品管理"],"ja":["トレンド分析","ホットトピック分析","Google Trends","ニュース分析","ソーシャルメディア分析","検索データ分析","コンテンツ制作","製品管理"],"ko":["트렌드 분석","핫 이슈 분석","Google Trends","뉴스 분석","소셜 미디어 분석","검색 데이터 분석","콘텐츠 제작","제품 관리"],"es":["detectador de tendencias","análisis de noticias","redes sociales","datos de búsqueda","tendencias","patrones","Google Trends"],"fr":["repéreur de tendances","analyse des actualités","médias sociaux","données de recherche","tendances","modèles","Google Trends"],"de":["Trend-Spotter","Nachrichtenanalyse","soziale Medien","Suchdaten","Trends","Muster","Google Trends"],"pt":["tendências em tempo real","análise de dados","tópicos quentes","noticias e mídias sociais","dados de busca do Google","ferramentas de análise de dados"],"ru":["тенденции в реальном времени","анализ данных","горячие темы","новости и социальные сети","данные поиска Google","инструменты анализа данных"],"ar":["اتجاهات في الوقت الحقيقي","تحليل البيانات","مواضيع ساخنة","أخبار ووسائط اجتماعية","بيانات بحث جوجل","أدوات تحليل البيانات"]}},"owner":"malue-ai","repo":"dazee-small","repoPath":"malue-ai/dazee-small","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"trend-spotter","description":"Discover emerging trends and hot topics from news, social media, and search data. Generate trend analysis reports.","bodyPreview":"# 趋势与热点发现\n\n从新闻、社交媒体和搜索数据中发现新兴趋势和热门话题。\n\n## 使用场景\n\n- 用户说「最近 AI 领域有什么新趋势」「今天有什么热点」\n- 内容创作者需要找热门话题\n- 产品经理需要了解行业动向\n\n## 数据来源\n\n### 1. Google Trends（搜索趋势）\n\n```bash\n# 实时热搜（中国）\ncurl -s \"https://trends.google.com/trends/trendingsearches/daily/rss?geo=CN\" | python3 -c \"\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\nimport sys\ntree = ET.parse(sys.stdin)\nroot = tree.getroot()\nns = {''ht'': ''https://trends.google.com/trends/trendingsearches/daily''}\nfor item in root.findall(''.//item'')[:10]:\n    title = item.find(''title'').tex","body":"# 趋势与热点发现\n\n从新闻、社交媒体和搜索数据中发现新兴趋势和热门话题。\n\n## 使用场景\n\n- 用户说「最近 AI 领域有什么新趋势」「今天有什么热点」\n- 内容创作者需要找热门话题\n- 产品经理需要了解行业动向\n\n## 数据来源\n\n### 1. Google Trends（搜索趋势）\n\n```bash\n# 实时热搜（中国）\ncurl -s \"https://trends.google.com/trends/trendingsearches/daily/rss?geo=CN\" | python3 -c \"\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\nimport sys\ntree = ET.parse(sys.stdin)\nroot = tree.getroot()\nns = {''ht'': ''https://trends.google.com/trends/trendingsearches/daily''}\nfor item in root.findall(''.//item'')[:10]:\n    title = item.find(''title'').text\n    traffic = item.find(''ht:approx_traffic'', ns)\n    traffic_text = traffic.text if traffic is not None else ''?''\n    print(f''🔥 {title} ({traffic_text})'')\n\"\n```\n\n### 2. 新闻聚合\n\n```bash\n# 通过公开 RSS 获取行业新闻\n# 配合 blogwatcher Skill 使用\n\n# 或直接用 curl 获取新闻 API（免费的如 NewsAPI 有限额）\ncurl -s \"https://newsapi.org/v2/top-headlines?country=cn&category=technology&apiKey=$NEWS_API_KEY&pageSize=10\"\n```\n\n### 3. GitHub Trending\n\n```bash\n# 获取 GitHub 趋势项目\ncurl -s \"https://api.github.com/search/repositories?q=stars:>100+pushed:>$(date -v-7d +%Y-%m-%d)&sort=stars&order=desc&per_page=10\" | python3 -c \"\nimport json, sys\ndata = json.load(sys.stdin)\nfor repo in data.get(''items'', [])[:10]:\n    name = repo[''full_name'']\n    stars = repo[''stargazers_count'']\n    desc = (repo.get(''description'') or '''')[:60]\n    print(f''⭐ {name} ({stars} stars)'')\n    print(f''   {desc}'')\n\"\n```\n\n### 4. Hacker News 热门\n\n```bash\ncurl -s \"https://hacker-news.firebaseio.com/v0/topstories.json\" | python3 -c \"\nimport json, sys, urllib.request\nids = json.load(sys.stdin)[:10]\nfor id in ids:\n    url = f''https://hacker-news.firebaseio.com/v0/item/{id}.json''\n    item = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(url).read())\n    title = item.get(''title'', '''')\n    score = item.get(''score'', 0)\n    print(f''📰 [{score}分] {title}'')\n\"\n```\n\n## 报告格式\n\n```markdown\n## 趋势报告 — {领域}\n**日期**: 2025-02-07\n\n### 🔥 热门话题 Top 5\n1. **话题名** — 简要描述 + 热度指标\n2. ...\n\n### 📈 上升趋势\n- 趋势 A：过去 7 天搜索量增长 200%\n- 趋势 B：GitHub 相关项目 Star 数激增\n\n### 💡 洞察\n- 行业正在向 XX 方向发展\n- 值得关注的新技术/产品：XX\n\n### 📌 内容创作建议\n- 热门选题：XX\n- 最佳发布时间：XX\n```\n\n## 输出规范\n\n- 数据附带来源和时间\n- 区分「热点」（短期爆发）和「趋势」（持续上升）\n- 给出可行动的建议（写什么内容、关注什么方向）\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:09:14.112Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Analysis Agents needing real-time trend detection from Google Trends and social media data.","zh":"非常适合需要从Google Trends和社交媒体数据中实时检测趋势的数据分析代理。","ja":"Google Trendsおよびソーシャルメディアデータからリアルタイムのトレンド検出が必要なデータ分析エージェントに最適です。","ko":"구글 트렌드 및 소셜 미디어 데이터의 실시간 트렌드 감지를 필요로 하는 데이터 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis de Datos que necesitan detección de tendencias en tiempo real desde Google Trends y datos de redes sociales.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de données ayant besoin de détection de tendances en temps réel à partir de Google Trends et de données de réseaux sociaux.","de":"Perfekt für Datenanalyse-Agenten, die Echtzeit-Trend-Erkennung von Google Trends und sozialen Medien benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Dados que precisam de detecção de tendências em tempo real dos Google Trends e dados de mídia social.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа данных, которым требуется обнаружение тенденций в режиме реального времени из Google Trends и данных социальных сетей.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تحليل البيانات التي تحتاج إلى كشف الاتجاهات في الوقت الفعلي من جوجل ترندز وبيانات وسائل الإعلام الاجتماعية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to discover emerging trends and hot topics using XML parsing and Python''s xml.etree.ElementTree library, providing real-time insights from Google Trends and other data sources like news and social media.","zh":"使代理能够使用XML解析和Python的xml.etree.ElementTree库来发现新兴趋势和热点话题，提供来自Google Trends和其他数据源（如新闻和社交媒体）的实时洞察。","ja":"XMLの解析とPythonのxml.etree.ElementTreeライブラリを使用して、エージェントが新たなトレンドやホットトピックを発見できるようにし、Google Trendsやニュース、ソーシャルメディアなどの他のデータソースからリアルタイムの洞察を提供します。","ko":"XML 파싱 및 Python의 xml.etree.ElementTree 라이브러리를 사용하여 에이전트가 새로운 트렌드 및 핫 토픽을 발견할 수 있도록 하여 구글 트렌드 및 뉴스, 소셜 미디어 등의 다른 데이터 소스에서 실시간으로洞察력을 제공합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes descubrir tendencias emergentes y temas de actualidad utilizando el análisis de XML y la biblioteca xml.etree.ElementTree de Python, proporcionando información en tiempo real desde Google Trends y otras fuentes de datos como noticias y redes sociales.","fr":"Permet aux agents de découvrir des tendances émergentes et des sujets chauds en utilisant l''analyse XML et la bibliothèque xml.etree.ElementTree de Python, fournissant des informations en temps réel à partir de Google Trends et d''autres sources de données comme les actualités et les réseaux sociaux.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, aufkommende Trends und heiße Themen mithilfe von XML-Parsing und der xml.etree.ElementTree-Bibliothek von Python zu entdecken, wodurch Echtzeit-Einblicke aus Google Trends und anderen Datenquellen wie Nachrichten und sozialen Medien bereitgestellt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a descobrirem tendências emergentes e tópicos quentes usando análise de XML e a biblioteca xml.etree.ElementTree do Python, fornecendo insights em tempo real dos Google Trends e outras fontes de dados como notícias e mídia social.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обнаруживать новые тенденции и горячие темы с помощью парсинга XML и библиотеки xml.etree.ElementTree для Python, обеспечивая получение информации в реальном времени из Google Trends и других источников данных, таких как новости и социальные сети.","ar":"يتمكن العميل من اكتشاف الاتجاهات الناشئة والمواضيع الساخنة باستخدام تحليل XML ومكتبة xml.etree.ElementTree لغة بايثون، مما يوفر رؤى في الوقت الفعلي من جوجل ترندز ومصادر بيانات أخرى مثل الأخبار ووسائل الإعلام الاجتماعية."},"useCases":{"en":["Monitoring daily trending searches on Google Trends","Identifying hot topics for content creation","Analyzing industry trends for product managers"],"zh":["监控Google Trends每日热门搜索","为内容创作确定热门话题","为产品经理分析行业趋势"],"ja":["Google Trendsの毎日のトレンド検索を監視する","コンテンツ作成のためのホットトピックを特定する","製品マネージャー向けの業界トレンド分析"],"ko":["구글 트렌드의 일일 인기 검색어 모니터링","컨텐츠 제작을 위한 핫 토픽 식별","제품 매니저를 위한 산업 트렌드 분석"],"es":["Monitoreo de búsquedas diarias en tendencias de Google","Identificación de temas de actualidad para la creación de contenido","Análisis de tendencias de la industria para gestores de productos"],"fr":["Suivi des recherches quotidiennes dans les tendances de Google","Identification des sujets chauds pour la création de contenu","Analyse des tendances de l''industrie pour les responsables de produits"],"de":["Überwachung täglicher Trends bei Google-Suchen","Identifizierung von heißen Themen für die Inhaltserschaffung","Analyse von Branchentrends für Produktmanager"],"pt":["Monitoramento de pesquisas diárias em tendência no Google Trends","Identificação de tópicos quentes para criação de conteúdo","Análise de tendências de indústria para gerentes de produto"],"ru":["Мониторинг ежедневных трендов поиска в Google Trends","Определение горячих тем для создания контента","Анализ тенденций отрасли для менеджеров продукта"],"ar":["مراقبة عمليات البحث اليومية الشائعة في جوجل ترندز","تحديد المواضيع الساخنة لإنشاء المحتوى","تحليل اتجاهات الصناعة لمديري المنتجات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires internet connection for data retrieval","Limited to Google Trends data for Chinese region (geo=CN)"],"zh":["需要互联网连接来检索数据","仅限于中国地区（geo=CN）的Google Trends数据"],"ja":["データの取得にはインターネット接続が必要","中国地域（geo=CN）でのみ利用可能なGoogle Trendsデータ"],"ko":["데이터检索를 위해 인터넷 연결이 필요","중국 지역(geo=CN)에서만 사용 가능한 구글 트렌드 데이터"],"es":["Requiere conexión a Internet para la recuperación de datos","Limitado a datos de Google Trends para la región china (geo=CN)"],"fr":["Nécessite une connexion Internet pour la récupération de données","Limité aux données de Google Trends pour la région chinoise (geo=CN)"],"de":["Benötigt Internetverbindung für die Datenabruf","Begrenzt auf Google-Trends-Daten für die chinesische Region (geo=CN)"],"pt":["Requer conexão com a internet para recuperação de dados","Limitado a dados do Google Trends para região chinesa (geo=CN)"],"ru":["Требуется подключение к интернету для извлечения данных","Ограничен данными Google Trends для китайского региона (geo=CN)"],"ar":["يتطلب الاتصال بالإنترنت لاسترجاع البيانات","محدود ببيانات جوجل ترندز لمنطقة الصين (geo=CN)"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/start', 'community', 'majiayu000', 'claude-skill-registry', 'majiayu000/claude-skill-registry', 'start', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z', '2026-02-18T07:09:59.467Z', NULL, '{"id":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/start","name":"start","description":{"zh":"Claude Code技能注册中心提供了一个全面而强大的自动化迭代和任务管理平台","ja":"Claude Codeスキルレジストリセンターは、包括的で強力な自動化イテレーションとタスク管理プラットフォームを提供","ko":"클로드 코드 스킬 등록 센터는 종합적이고 강력한 자동화 반복과 태스크 관리 플랫폼을 제공","es":"El bucle autónomo es un proceso de iteración que continúa hasta que se satisfacen las especificaciones o se alcanzan los límites. Aprende a configurarlo","fr":"La boucle autonome est un processus d''itération qui continue jusqu''à ce que les spécifications soient satisfaites ou les limites atteintes. Découvrez comment la configurer","de":"Die autonome Schleife ist ein Prozess der Iteration, der bis zur Erfüllung der Spezifikationen oder Erreichung der Grenzen fortgesetzt wird. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie sie konfigurieren","pt":"O Loop é uma iteração autônoma que continua até que as especificações sejam atendidas ou os limites sejam alcançados. Aprenda a utilizá-lo.","ru":"Петля - это автономная итерация, которая продолжается до тех пор, пока спецификации не будут выполнены или пределы не будут достигнуты. Узнайте, как ею пользоваться.","ar":"الحلقة هي تكرار ذاتي يستمر حتى تتم 충족 المواصفات أو تصل الحدود. تعلم كيفية استخدامها.","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":" Claude Code技能注册中心","ja":"Claude Codeスキルレジストリ","ko":"클로드 코드 스킬 등록 센터","es":"Inicio de Bucle Autónomo: Especificaciones y Pasos","fr":"Début de la Boucle Autonome: Spécifications et Étapes","de":"Starte Autonome Schleife: Spezifikationen und Schritte","pt":"Inicie o Loop: Iteração Autônoma para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Запуск Петли: Автономная Итерация для Разработчиков","ar":"ابدأ الحلقة: التكرار الذاتي للمطورين","en":"start"},"description":{"zh":"Claude Code技能注册中心提供了一个全面而强大的自动化迭代和任务管理平台","ja":"Claude Codeスキルレジストリセンターは、包括的で強力な自動化イテレーションとタスク管理プラットフォームを提供","ko":"클로드 코드 스킬 등록 센터는 종합적이고 강력한 자동화 반복과 태스크 관리 플랫폼을 제공","es":"El bucle autónomo es un proceso de iteración que continúa hasta que se satisfacen las especificaciones o se alcanzan los límites. Aprende a configurarlo","fr":"La boucle autonome est un processus d''itération qui continue jusqu''à ce que les spécifications soient satisfaites ou les limites atteintes. Découvrez comment...","de":"Die autonome Schleife ist ein Prozess der Iteration, der bis zur Erfüllung der Spezifikationen oder Erreichung der Grenzen fortgesetzt wird. Erfahren Sie, wi...","pt":"O Loop é uma iteração autônoma que continua até que as especificações sejam atendidas ou os limites sejam alcançados. Aprenda a utilizá-lo.","ru":"Петля - это автономная итерация, которая продолжается до тех пор, пока спецификации не будут выполнены или пределы не будут достигнуты. Узнайте, как ею польз...","ar":"الحلقة هي تكرار ذاتي يستمر حتى تتم 충족 المواصفات أو تصل الحدود. تعلم كيفية استخدامها.","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["自动化迭代","任务管理","状态 schema","循环状态管理","成功标准提取"],"ja":["自動化イテレーション","タスク管理","状態スキーマ","ループ状態管理","成功基準抽出"],"ko":["자동화 반복","태스크 관리","상태 스키마","반복 상태 관리","성공 기준 추출"],"es":["Evaluación de especificaciones","Creación de tareas con esquema de estado","Definición de criterios de éxito","Descomposición en pasos concretos","Anuncio de inicio de bucle"],"fr":["Évaluation des spécifications","Création de tâches avec schéma d''état","Définition des critères de succès","Décomposition en étapes concrètes","Annonce de démarrage de la boucle"],"de":["Evaluierung von Spezifikationen","Erstellung von Aufgaben mit Zustandschema","Definition von Erfolgskriterien","Zerlegung in konkrete Schritte","Ankündigung des Startes der Schleife"],"pt":["Iteração autônoma","Especificações personalizáveis","Limites configuráveis","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento","Otimização de produtividade"],"ru":["Автономная итерация","Пользовательские спецификации","Конфигурируемые пределы","Интеграция с инструментами разработки","Оптимизация производительности"],"ar":["التكرار الذاتي","المواصفات المخصصة","الحدود القابلية للتهيئة","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير","تحسين الإنتاجية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Claude Code","自动化迭代","任务管理","状态 schema","循环状态管理","成功标准提取","开发工具"],"ja":["Claude Code","自動化イテレーション","タスク管理","状態スキーマ","ループ状態管理","成功基準抽出","開発ツール"],"ko":["클로드 코드","자동화 반복","태스크 관리","상태 스키마","반복 상태 관리","성공 기준 추출","개발 도구"],"es":["bucle autónomo","especificaciones","tareas","estado","criterios de éxito","descomposición","anuncio de inicio"],"fr":["boucle autonome","spécifications","tâches","état","critères de succès","décomposition","annonce de démarrage"],"de":["autonome Schleife","Spezifikationen","Aufgaben","Zustand","Erfolgskriterien","Zerlegung","Ankündigung des Startes"],"pt":["loop de iteração","desenvolvimento de software","produtividade de desenvolvedores","automatização de tarefas","ferramentas de desenvolvimento","otimização de código"],"ru":["петля итерации","разработка программного обеспечения","производительность разработчиков","автоматизация задач","инструменты разработки","оптимизация кода"],"ar":["حلقة التكرار","تطوير البرمجيات","إنتاجية المطورين","توفير المهام","أدوات التطوير","تحسين الكود"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"start","description":"Start autonomous iteration loop OR explain how Loop works. Triggers on loop, keep going, dont stop, continue until done, until tests pass, implement full feature, fix all problems, make better, what is loop, how does loop work, loop help, or any persistence pattern. Executes multi-step tasks without stopping until complete or limits reached.","bodyPreview":"# Loop\n\nAutonomous iteration that continues until spec is satisfied or limits reached.\n\n## Before You Start (Required Checklist)\n\n□ Score the spec (use rubric below)\n□ Determine shape (Tool ≥8, Colleague 5-7, Intent <5)\n□ Classify reversibility (see below)\n□ Extract success criteria from spec (explicit list)\n□ Decompose into concrete steps\n□ Create task with state schema\n□ Write `.loop/state.json` with criteria array\n□ Announce: `[LOOP] Starting | Shape: X | Workflow: [A/B/C] | Steps: N | Budget","body":"# Loop\n\nAutonomous iteration that continues until spec is satisfied or limits reached.\n\n## Before You Start (Required Checklist)\n\n□ Score the spec (use rubric below)\n□ Determine shape (Tool ≥8, Colleague 5-7, Intent <5)\n□ Classify reversibility (see below)\n□ Extract success criteria from spec (explicit list)\n□ Decompose into concrete steps\n□ Create task with state schema\n□ Write `.loop/state.json` with criteria array\n□ Announce: `[LOOP] Starting | Shape: X | Workflow: [A/B/C] | Steps: N | Budget: $Y`\n\n**If any checkbox is unclear, STOP and clarify before proceeding.**\n\n### Reversibility Classification\n\n| Type | Rollback | Examples | Action |\n|------|----------|----------|--------|\n| **2A** | < 1 min | Config changes, renames | Execute freely |\n| **2B** | < 5 min | Dependencies, refactors | Checkpoint each step |\n| **1** | Hours+ | Schema changes, public APIs | Require [adversarial pre-check](../../hope/skills/soul/references/adversarial-precheck.md) |\n\nSee [fit-decision.md](../../hope/skills/soul/references/fit-decision.md) for full delegation scoring.\n\n### SHAPE.md Integration\n\nIf `.loop/shape/SHAPE.md` exists (generated by `/hope:shape`), extract:\n\n1. **criteria:** → Add to criteriaStatus initialization\n2. **mustNot:** → Add as circuit breaker triggers\n3. **verification:** → Map to verification types per criterion\n\n```json\n{\n  \"criteriaStatus\": {\n    \"tests pass\": {\"met\": false, \"verification\": \"execution output\"},\n    \"API returns 200\": {\"met\": false, \"verification\": \"execution output\"},\n    \"UI renders\": {\"met\": false, \"verification\": \"observation\"}\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**mustNot Circuit Breaker:** If any `mustNot` condition becomes true during execution → pause immediately.\n\n**Exit Blocked:** If any criterion has `verification: \"assumption\"`, exit_signal cannot be true.\n\n---\n\n## Spec Clarity Rubric (Inline)\n\nScore on 5 dimensions (0-2 each, max 10):\n\n| Dimension | 0 | 1 | 2 |\n|-----------|---|---|---|\n| **Outcome** | \"Make it better\" | \"Improve performance\" | \"p95 latency <100ms\" |\n| **Scope** | \"Fix the app\" | \"Fix auth\" | \"Fix /api/auth/token\" |\n| **Constraints** | None stated | \"Use existing stack\" | \"No new deps, <500 LOC\" |\n| **Success** | None stated | \"Tests pass\" | \"All tests + manual QA\" |\n| **Done** | Implied | \"When it works\" | \"PR merged to main\" |\n\n**Decision:**\n- **≥8:** Tool-shaped — execute silently, report on completion\n- **5-7:** Colleague-shaped — check in after each iteration\n- **<5:** Run `/hope:intent` first\n\n---\n\n## Workflow Type Detection\n\nAfter scoring spec, detect workflow type from content:\n\n| Workflow | Indicators | Gate |\n|----------|------------|------|\n| **A (Build)** | \"add\", \"implement\", \"create\", \"new feature\" | Library search required |\n| **B (Debug)** | \"fix\", \"debug\", \"broken\", \"error\", \"failing\" | Root cause before workaround |\n| **C (Refactor)** | \"refactor\", \"clean up\", \"reorganize\", \"migrate\" | Deletion before redesign |\n\nUpdate announcement to include workflow: `[LOOP] Starting | Shape: X | Workflow: [A/B/C] | Steps: N`\n\nReference [hope/skills/soul](../../hope/skills/soul/SKILL.md) for workflow details.\n\n---\n\n## Confirmation Gates by Shape\n\n### Tool-Shaped (≥8)\n\nExecute autonomously. No confirmation gates.\n\n```\n[LOOP] Starting | Shape: Tool (9/10) | Workflow: A | Steps: 5\n... executes all steps without pausing ...\n<loop-complete>\n```\n\n### Colleague-Shaped (5-7)\n\nPause at three checkpoints:\n\n| Gate | When | Question |\n|------|------|----------|\n| **G1** | After spec decomposition | \"Here are N steps. Proceed?\" |\n| **G2** | After each iteration | \"Step X complete. Continue?\" |\n| **G3** | Before completion claim | \"All criteria met. Confirm done?\" |\n\n```\n[LOOP] Starting | Shape: Colleague (6/10) | Workflow: B | Steps: 4\n\nG1: Decomposed into 4 steps:\n1. Identify failing test\n2. Add instrumentation\n3. Fix root cause\n4. Verify fix\nProceed? [Y/n]\n```\n\n**Skip gates:** User says \"proceed without confirmation\" to run uninterrupted.\n\n### Intent-Required (<5)\n\nBlock and route to `/hope:intent` before proceeding.\n\n---\n\n## State File Schema (CRITICAL)\n\n**Transparency:** Loop writes `.loop/state.json` to track progress.\n\nOn loop start, disclose: \"Writing state to `.loop/state.json`. Delete after session? [Y/n]\"\n\n**Cleanup:** State files auto-delete on `/loop cancel` unless user opts to keep.\n\nWrite `.loop/state.json` at loop start and update after EVERY iteration:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"spec\": \"original user request verbatim\",\n  \"criteria\": [\"tests pass\", \"all routes refactored\", \"no lint errors\"],\n  \"criteriaStatus\": {\n    \"tests pass\": false,\n    \"all routes refactored\": false,\n    \"no lint errors\": true\n  },\n  \"exit_signal\": false,\n  \"steps\": [\"step1\", \"step2\", \"step3\"],\n  \"completedSteps\": [\"step1\"],\n  \"remainingSteps\": [\"step2\", \"step3\"],\n  \"iteration\": 2,\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"circuitBreaker\": {\n    \"stuckCount\": 0,\n    \"lastUnmet\": \"tests pass\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**The stop hook reads this file to decide whether to continue.**\n\n---\n\n## Dual-Condition Exit (CRITICAL)\n\nThe stop hook requires BOTH conditions to stop:\n\n1. **All `criteriaStatus` values are `true`**\n2. **`exit_signal` is `true`**\n\nIf either condition is false, the loop continues.\n\n### Why Dual-Condition?\n\nPrevents premature stops. Claude must:\n1. Actually verify each criterion (tests pass, lint clean, etc.)\n2. Explicitly signal completion intent\n\n---\n\n## Iteration Protocol\n\n```\n1. TaskGet → Retrieve current state\n2. Read .loop/state.json if exists (recovery case)\n3. Announce → [LOOP] Iteration N/max | Cost: $X | Step: [name]\n4. Execute → Do ONE logical unit of work\n5. Verify → Run verification commands for affected criteria\n6. Update state → Write .loop/state.json with updated criteriaStatus\n7. Check circuit breaker → Increment stuckCount if same criteria unmet\n8. Output status block → ---LOOP_STATUS--- (required)\n9. TaskUpdate → Save to Tasks API (backup)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Status Block (REQUIRED)\n\nAfter EACH iteration, output this exact format:\n\n```\n---LOOP_STATUS---\nEXIT_SIGNAL: false\nCRITERIA: {\"tests pass\": false, \"lint clean\": true}\nSTUCK_COUNT: 0\nNEXT: Fix failing tests\n---END_STATUS---\n```\n\n**Rules:**\n- `EXIT_SIGNAL: true` ONLY when ALL criteria verified true\n- `CRITERIA` must match `criteriaStatus` in state file\n- `STUCK_COUNT` increments when same criteria remain unmet\n- `NEXT` describes the next action\n\n---\n\n## State Update Protocol\n\nAfter each iteration:\n\n1. **Run verification commands** for criteria you worked on\n2. **Update `criteriaStatus`** based on actual verification results\n3. **Check for stuck state:**\n   - If same criteria unmet as last iteration, increment `circuitBreaker.stuckCount`\n   - If different criteria unmet, reset `stuckCount` to 0\n4. **Set `exit_signal`:**\n   - `true` ONLY if ALL criteriaStatus values are true\n   - `false` otherwise\n5. **Write updated state** to `.loop/state.json`\n6. **Output status block**\n\n---\n\n## Circuit Breakers\n\n| Trigger | Threshold | Action |\n|---------|-----------|--------|\n| Same criteria unmet | 5x consecutive | Stop hook opens circuit |\n| Same error | 3x consecutive | Pause, request help |\n| Same file edits | 5x in one iteration | Pause, likely thrashing |\n| Budget exceeded | $25 default | Pause, offer continue |\n| Iteration limit | 10 default | Pause, offer continue |\n\nThe stop hook checks `circuitBreaker.stuckCount >= 5` and returns `{ok: true}` to stop.\n\n---\n\n## Announcements\n\n### Before Each Iteration\n\n```\n[LOOP] Iteration N/max | Cost: $X/$budget | Step: [current step]\n```\n\n### After Each Iteration\n\n```\n[LOOP] ✓ [step name] complete | Progress: N/total | Next: [next step]\n```\n\n### On Completion\n\n```\n<loop-complete>\nAll success criteria satisfied:\n- [criterion 1]: ✓\n- [criterion 2]: ✓\n- [criterion 3]: ✓\n</loop-complete>\n```\n\nOutput `<loop-complete>` ONLY after:\n1. All criteriaStatus values are true\n2. exit_signal set to true in state file\n\n**Quality Footer Required:** After `<loop-complete>`, include a verdict box:\n\n```\n╭─ 🟢 SHIP ──────────────────────────╮\n│ Verified: [execution output/observation/measurement] │\n│ Checklist: N/N criteria verified    │\n│ Subjective: ~X% · Type 2A/2B · Npt  │\n├────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ ↳ Alt: [alternative approach]       │\n│ ↳ Risk: [key assumption]            │\n╰────────────────────────────────────╯\n```\n\nMap loop outcomes to verdicts:\n- **🟢 SHIP:** All criteria verified with execution output/observation/measurement\n- **🟡 MONITOR:** Criteria passed but verification was code review only\n- **🔴 RESEARCH:** Any criterion verified by assumption only\n\nSee [quality-footer.md](../../hope/skills/soul/references/quality-footer.md) for format details.\n\n### On Pause\n\n```\n[LOOP] ⏸ Paused: [reason]\nProgress: N steps complete, M remaining\nResume: /loop continue\n```\n\n---\n\n## Commands\n\n| Command | Effect |\n|---------|--------|\n| `/loop [spec]` | Start new loop |\n| `/loop continue` | Resume paused loop |\n| `/loop continue --budget=25` | Add budget and resume |\n| `/loop cancel` | Terminate and clean up |\n| `/loop status` | Show current state |\n\n---\n\n## Cost Controls\n\n| Protection | Default | Max | Override |\n|------------|---------|-----|----------|\n| Budget cap | $25 | $100 | `--budget=N` |\n| Iterations | 10 | 50 | `--iterations=N` |\n\n**Principle:** Pause, don''t kill. User can always continue.\n\n---\n\n## Example\n\nUser: \"loop - refactor all API routes to use validation middleware\"\n\n```\n[LOOP] Starting | Shape: Colleague (7/10) | Steps: 4 | Budget: $25\n\nSpec scoring:\n- Outcome: 2 (clear refactor)\n- Scope: 2 (API routes)\n- Constraints: 1 (middleware implied)\n- Success: 1 (implicit: works)\n- Done: 1 (implicit: all routes)\nTotal: 7/10 → Colleague-shaped\n\n[LOOP] Iteration 1/10 | Cost: $0.50/$25 | Step: Refactor /api/users\n... work happens ...\n[LOOP] ✓ /api/users complete | Progress: 1/4 | Next: /api/auth\n\n---LOOP_STATUS---\nEXIT_SIGNAL: false\nCRITERIA: {\"/api/users refactored\": true, \"/api/auth refactored\": false, \"tests pass\": false}\nSTUCK_COUNT: 0\nNEXT: Refactor /api/auth\n---END_STATUS---\n\nContinue? [Y/n]\n```\n\nOn completion:\n```\n---LOOP_STATUS---\nEXIT_SIGNAL: true\nCRITERIA: {\"/api/users refactored\": true, \"/api/auth refactored\": true, \"tests pass\": true}\nSTUCK_COUNT: 0\nNEXT: none\n---END_STATUS---\n\n<loop-complete>\nAll success criteria satisfied:\n- /api/users refactored: ✓\n- /api/auth refactored: ✓\n- /api/products refactored: ✓\n- /api/orders refactored: ✓\n- All tests pass: ✓\n</loop-complete>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Boundary\n\n**Loop executes, never decides.**\n\n- User controls what gets built — loop executes the spec, doesn''t expand it\n- User controls persistence — state files disclosed, cleanup offered\n- User controls continuation — pause is always honored, \"cancel\" is immediate\n\nLoop must not do work the user should learn. If same pattern repeats 3+ times, suggest: \"This is a learnable pattern. Want the steps to run yourself?\"\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n- `references/loop-mechanics.md` — Command-based stop hook, state schema, circuit breaker\n- `references/spec-rubric.md` — Scoring examples\n- `references/cost-controls.md` — Override syntax, continuation\n- `references/headless.md` — CI/CD integration\n- `references/prd-mode.md` — PRD execution mode for pre-decomposed tasks\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:09:59.467Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Autonomous Agents like Claude Code, AutoGPT, and LangChain requiring iterative workflow management and state tracking.","zh":"适用于像 Claude Code、AutoGPT 和 LangChain 这样的自主代理，需要迭代工作流管理和状态跟踪。","ja":"Claude Code、AutoGPT、LangChain などの自治エージェントに適しており、イテレーション ワークフロー管理と状態追跡が必要です。","ko":"Claude Code, AutoGPT, LangChain 등의 자율 에이전트에 적합하며, 반복적 워크플ロー 관리 및 상태 추적이 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes Autónomos como Claude Code, AutoGPT y LangChain que requieren gestión de flujos de trabajo iterativos y seguimiento de estado.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents Autonomes comme Claude Code, AutoGPT et LangChain nécessitant une gestion de flux de travail itératifs et un suivi d''état.","de":"Ideal für autonome Agenten wie Claude Code, AutoGPT und LangChain, die eine iterative Workflow-Verwaltung und Zustandsverfolgung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Autônomos como Claude Code, AutoGPT e LangChain que exigem gestão de fluxo de trabalho iterativo e rastreamento de estado.","ru":"Идеально подходит для автономных агентов, таких как Claude Code, AutoGPT и LangChain, требующих итеративного управления рабочим процессом и отслеживания состояния.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المستقلين مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT و LangChain الذين يتطلبون إدارة تدفق العمل المتكرر وتعقب الحالة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to execute autonomous iteration with spec satisfaction or limits, utilizing .loop/state.json and state schema for workflow management, and announcing loop initiation with criteria array and budget.","zh":"赋予代理执行自主迭代的能力，具有规范满足或限制，利用 .loop/state.json 和状态模式进行工作流管理，并在循环启动时宣布标准数组和预算。","ja":"エージェントに自律的なイテレーションを実行する力を与え、仕様の満足または制限を利用し、.loop/state.json と状態スキーマを使用してワークフロー管理を行い、ループ開始時に基準配列と予算を発表します。","ko":"에이전트가 자율적으로 반복 작업을 수행할 수 있도록 하며, 규격 만족 또는 제한을 사용하여 .loop/state.json 및 상태 스키마를 활용한 워크플ロー 관리 및 루프 시작 시 기준 배열 및 예산을 公告합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a ejecutar iteraciones autónomas con satisfacción de especificaciones o límites, utilizando .loop/state.json y esquema de estado para la gestión de flujos de trabajo, y anunciando la iniciación del bucle con matriz de criterios y presupuesto.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter des itérations autonomes avec satisfaction des spécifications ou des limites, en utilisant .loop/state.json et schéma d''état pour la gestion de flux de travail, et en annonçant l''initiation de la boucle avec un tableau de critères et un budget.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, autonome Iterationen mit Spezifikationserfüllung oder Grenzen auszuführen, indem .loop/state.json und Zustandsschema für die Workflow-Verwaltung verwendet werden und die Initiierung der Schleife mit Kriterienarray und Budget angekündigt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar iterações autônomas com satisfação de especificações ou limites, utilizando .loop/state.json e esquema de estado para gestão de fluxo de trabalho, e anunciando a inicialização do loop com array de critérios e orçamento.","ru":"Позволяет агентам выполнять автономные итерации с удовлетворением спецификаций или ограничений, используя .loop/state.json и схему состояния для управления рабочим процессом, и объявляя инициацию цикла с массивом критериев и бюджетом.","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء تنفيذ التكرارات المستقلة مع إرضاء المواصفات أو الحدود، باستخدام .loop/state.json و مخطط الحالة لإدارة تدفق العمل، و الإعلان عن بدء الحلقة مع مصفوفة المعايير والميزانية."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating iterative tasks with spec-driven termination","Creating and managing loop workflows with state schema","Debugging loop iterations with explicit success criteria and reversibility classification"],"zh":["使用规范驱动的终止进行自动化的迭代任务","使用状态模式创建和管理循环工作流","使用显式的成功标准和可逆性分类进行循环迭代的调试"],"ja":["仕様駆動の終了を使用したイテレーションタスクの自動化","状態スキーマを使用したループワークフローの作成と管理","明示的な成功基準と可逆性分類を使用したループイテレーションのデバッグ"],"ko":["규격 구동 종료를 사용한 반복 작업의 자동화","상태 스키마를 사용한 루프 워크플로의 생성 및 관리","명시적인 성공 기준 및 가역성 분류를 사용한 루프 반복의 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de tareas iterativas con terminación dirigida por especificaciones","Creación y gestión de flujos de trabajo de bucle con esquema de estado","Depuración de iteraciones de bucle con criterios de éxito explícitos y clasificación de reversibilidad"],"fr":["Automatisation de tâches itératives avec terminaison pilotée par des spécifications","Création et gestion de flux de travail de boucle avec schéma d''état","Débogage des itérations de boucle avec des critères de succès explicites et une classification de réversibilité"],"de":["Automatisierung von iterativen Aufgaben mit spezifikationsgesteuerter Beendigung","Erstellung und Verwaltung von Schleifen-Workflows mit Zustandsschema","Fehlerbehebung von Schleifen-Iterationen mit expliziten Erfolgskriterien und Reversibilitätsklassifizierung"],"pt":["Automatizar tarefas iterativas com término dirigido por especificações","Criar e gerenciar fluxos de trabalho de loop com esquema de estado","Depurar iterações de loop com critérios de sucesso explícitos e classificação de reversibilidade"],"ru":["Автоматизация итеративных задач с завершением, управляемым спецификациями","Создание и управление рабочими процессами цикла со схемой состояния","Отладка итераций цикла с явными критериями успеха и классификацией обратимости"],"ar":["تأتمتة المهام المتكررة مع إنهاء موجه بالمواصفات","إنشاء وإدارة تدفقات العمل للحلقات مع مخطط الحالة","تصحيح أخطاء التكرارات الحلقية مع معايير النجاح الصريحة وتصنيف الإمكانية العكسية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires explicit spec scoring and shape determination","Needs success criteria extraction and decomposition into concrete steps","Mandatory creation of .loop/state.json file with criteria array"],"zh":["需要显式的规范评分和形状确定","需要成功标准的提取和分解为具体步骤","必须创建 .loop/state.json 文件，包含标准数组"],"ja":["明示的な仕様スコアリングと形状決定が必要","成功基準の抽出と具体的なステップへの分解が必要",".loop/state.json ファイルの作成が必須であり、基準配列を含む"],"ko":["명시적인 규격 점수화 및 형상 결정이 필요","성공 기준의 추출 및 구체적인 단계로의 분해가 필요",".loop/state.json 파일의 생성이 필수이며, 기준 배열을 포함"],"es":["Requiere puntuación de especificaciones explícitas y determinación de forma","Necesita extracción de criterios de éxito y descomposición en pasos concretos","Creación obligatoria del archivo .loop/state.json con matriz de criterios"],"fr":["Nécessite une notation de spécifications explicites et une détermination de forme","Nécessite une extraction de critères de réussite et une décomposition en étapes concrètes","Création obligatoire du fichier .loop/state.json avec un tableau de critères"],"de":["Erfordert explizite Spezifikationsbewertung und Formbestimmung","Benötigt Erfolgskriterien-Extraktion und Zerlegung in konkrete Schritte","Obligatorische Erstellung der Datei .loop/state.json mit Kriterienarray"],"pt":["Exige pontuação de especificações explícitas e determinação de forma","Necessita extração de critérios de sucesso e decomposição em etapas concretas","Criação obrigatória do arquivo .loop/state.json com array de critérios"],"ru":["Требует явной оценки спецификаций и определения формы","Требует извлечения критериев успеха и декомпозиции в конкретные шаги","Обязательное создание файла .loop/state.json с массивом критериев"],"ar":["يتطلب تقييمًا صريحًا للمواصفات و تحديد الشكل","يحتاج إلى استخراج معايير النجاح و تحليلها إلى خطوات ملموسة","إنشاء файл .loop/state.json إلزامي مع مصفوفة المعايير"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/fixup', 'community', 'majiayu000', 'claude-skill-registry', 'majiayu000/claude-skill-registry', 'fixup', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z', '2026-02-18T07:10:42.505Z', NULL, '{"id":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/fixup","name":"fixup","description":{"zh":"Fixup 是一种交互式 Rebase 技能，用于优化 Git 提交。通过 Fixup，开发者可以创建修复提交，简化提交历史","ja":"Fixup はインタラクティブ Rebase スキルであり、Git コミットを最適化するために使用される。Fixup では、開発者は修正コミットを作成し、コミット履歴を簡素化できる","ko":"Fixup은 인터랙티브 Rebase 스킬로 Git 커밋을 최적화하는 데 사용된다. Fixup을 통해 개발자는 수정 커밋을 생성하여 커밋 기록을 간소화할 수 있다","es":"Fixup es una habilidad para corregir commits existentes mediante rebase interactivo, mejorando así tu flujo de trabajo Git.","fr":"Fixup est une compétence pour corriger les commits existants à l''aide du rebase interactif, améliorant ainsi votre flux de travail Git.","de":"Fixup ist eine Fähigkeit, um bestehende Commits mittels interaktivem Rebase zu korrigieren und so Ihren Git-Arbeitsablauf zu verbessern.","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Fixup 效果：交互式 Rebase 优化","ja":"Fixup 効果：インタラクティブ Rebase 最適化","ko":"Fixup 효과: 인터랙티브 Rebase 최적화","es":"Fixup: Corrección de Commits con Rebase Interactivo","fr":"Fixup: Correction de Commits avec Rebase Interactif","de":"Fixup: Korrektur von Commits mit interaktivem Rebase","en":"fixup"},"description":{"zh":"Fixup 是一种交互式 Rebase 技能，用于优化 Git 提交。通过 Fixup，开发者可以创建修复提交，简化提交历史","ja":"Fixup はインタラクティブ Rebase スキルであり、Git コミットを最適化するために使用される。Fixup では、開発者は修正コミットを作成し、コミット履歴を簡素化できる","ko":"Fixup은 인터랙티브 Rebase 스킬로 Git 커밋을 최적화하는 데 사용된다. Fixup을 통해 개발자는 수정 커밋을 생성하여 커밋 기록을 간소화할 수 있다","es":"Fixup es una habilidad para corregir commits existentes mediante rebase interactivo, mejorando así tu flujo de trabajo Git.","fr":"Fixup est une compétence pour corriger les commits existants à l''aide du rebase interactif, améliorant ainsi votre flux de travail Git.","de":"Fixup ist eine Fähigkeit, um bestehende Commits mittels interaktivem Rebase zu korrigieren und so Ihren Git-Arbeitsablauf zu verbessern.","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["交互式 Rebase","创建修复提交","简化提交历史","优化 Git 提交","提高开发效率"],"ja":["インタラクティブ Rebase","修正コミットの作成","コミット履歴の簡素化","Git コミットの最適化","開発効率の向上"],"ko":["인터랙티브 Rebase","수정 커밋 생성","커밋 기록 간소화","Git 커밋 최적화","개발 효율 향상"],"es":["Corrección de commits existentes","Rebase interactivo","Mejora del flujo de trabajo Git","Identificación de commits para corrección","Creación de commits de corrección"],"fr":["Correction de commits existants","Rebase interactif","Amélioration du flux de travail Git","Identification de commits à corriger","Création de commits de correction"],"de":["Korrektur bestehender Commits","Interaktives Rebase","Verbesserung des Git-Arbeitsablaufs","Identifizierung von Commits zur Korrektur","Erstellung von Korrektur-Commits"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Fixup","Git","交互式 Rebase","提交优化","开发效率","Git 技能","版本控制"],"ja":["Fixup","Git","インタラクティブ Rebase","コミット最適化","開発効率","Git スキル","バージョン管理"],"ko":["Fixup","Git","인터랙티브 Rebase","커밋 최적화","개발 효율","Git 스킬","버전 관리"],"es":["fixup","rebase interactivo","corrección de commits","flujo de trabajo Git","git status","git fetch","git log"],"fr":["fixup","rebase interactif","correction de commits","flux de travail Git","git status","git fetch","git log"],"de":["fixup","interaktives Rebase","Korrektur von Commits","Git-Arbeitsablauf","git status","git fetch","git log"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"fixup","description":"Create a fixup commit and autosquash rebase","bodyPreview":"# Fixup\n\nYou are assisting with fixing up an existing commit using interactive rebase. Follow these steps:\n\n## 1. Initial Assessment\n\n- Run `git status` to see if there are uncommitted changes\n- Run `git fetch origin` to get latest remote updates\n- Display existing commits with `git log origin/main..HEAD --oneline`\n\n## 2. Create Fixup Commit\n\nIf there are uncommitted changes:\n\n1. Show the commit history\n2. Ask user which commit hash to fixup (or identify it based on context)\n3. Stage changes wit","body":"# Fixup\n\nYou are assisting with fixing up an existing commit using interactive rebase. Follow these steps:\n\n## 1. Initial Assessment\n\n- Run `git status` to see if there are uncommitted changes\n- Run `git fetch origin` to get latest remote updates\n- Display existing commits with `git log origin/main..HEAD --oneline`\n\n## 2. Create Fixup Commit\n\nIf there are uncommitted changes:\n\n1. Show the commit history\n2. Ask user which commit hash to fixup (or identify it based on context)\n3. Stage changes with `git add .` or ask which files to stage\n4. Create a fixup commit:\n\n   ```bash\n   git commit --fixup=<commit-hash>\n   ```\n\n## 3. Autosquash Rebase\n\nRun non-interactive rebase with autosquash:\n\n```bash\ngit rebase --autosquash origin/main\n```\n\n## 4. Commit Message Review\n\nAfter rebase completes, verify the commit message matches the changes:\n\n1. Display the rebased commit:\n\n   ```bash\n   git show HEAD --stat\n   ```\n\n2. Compare the commit message body with the actual changes\n\n3. If the message is inaccurate or incomplete:\n   - Draft a corrected commit message following the `commit-message` rule\n   - Explain what needs to be updated and why\n   - Update with `git commit --amend`\n\n## 5. Post-Rebase Actions\n\nAfter message review:\n\n1. Display the final commit history:\n\n   ```bash\n   git log origin/main..HEAD --oneline\n   ```\n\n2. Inform the user to run `/publish` to push changes and update the PR\n\n## Key Principles\n\n- Use `--fixup=<hash>` to create fixup commits targeting specific commits\n- `--autosquash` automatically merges fixup commits during rebase\n- Review commit messages after rebase - compare with actual changes\n- Update messages with `git commit --amend` when they don''t accurately reflect the changes\n- Commit messages follow the `commit-message` rule\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:10:42.505Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Version Control Agents needing interactive rebase and commit management capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要交互式重新提交和提交管理功能的版本控制代理。","ja":"バージョン管理エージェントが対話型のリベースとコミット管理機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"대화형 재기반 및 커밋 관리 기능이 필요한 버전 제어 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de control de versiones que necesitan capacidades de rebasing interactivo y gestión de commits.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de contrôle de version nécessitant des capacités de rebasage interactif et de gestion de commit.","de":"Perfekt für Version Control Agents, die interaktive Rebase- und Commit-Management-Funktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes de controle de versão que precisam de capacidades de rebase interativo e gerenciamento de commit.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов контроля версий, требующих интерактивного ребейза и управления коммитами.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات مراقبة الإصدار التي تحتاج إلى إعادة قاعدة تفاعلية وإدارة الالتزام"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform interactive rebasing using git, creating fixup commits, and staging changes with precision, leveraging `git status`, `git fetch`, and `git log` commands.","zh":"赋予代理使用git进行交互式重新提交、创建修复提交、使用`git status`、`git fetch`和`git log`命令来精确暂存更改的能力。","ja":"エージェントがgitを使用して対話型のリベースを実行し、修正コミットを作成し、`git status`、`git fetch`、`git log`コマンドを使用して変更を正確にステージングできるようにします。","ko":"에이전트가 git을 사용하여 대화형 재기반을 수행하고 수정 커밋을 생성하며 `git status`, `git fetch`, `git log` 명령을 사용하여 변경 사항을 정확하게 스테이징할 수 있는 기능을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar rebasado interactivo utilizando git, creando commits de fixup y preparando cambios con precisión, aprovechando los comandos `git status`, `git fetch` y `git log`.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''effectuer un rebasage interactif en utilisant git, en créant des commits de correction et en mettant en scène les modifications avec précision, en exploitant les commandes `git status`, `git fetch` et `git log`.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, interaktives Rebasen mit git durchzuführen, Fixup-Commits zu erstellen und Änderungen mit Präzision zu staging, indem die Befehle `git status`, `git fetch` und `git log` genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar rebasamento interativo usando git, criar commits de fixup e estagiar alterações com precisão, aproveitando os comandos `git status`, `git fetch` e `git log`.","ru":"Позволяет агентам выполнять интерактивный ребейз с помощью git, создавать коммиты исправления и ставить изменения с точностью, используя команды `git status`, `git fetch` и `git log`.","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من إجراء إعادة قاعدة تفاعلية باستخدام git، وإنشاء التزامات إصلاح وتحديد التغييرات بدقة، مستفيدا من أوامر `git status` و `git fetch` و `git log`"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating fixup commit creation","Managing uncommitted changes with `git status`","Identifying commit hashes for rebasing"],"zh":["自动创建修复提交","使用`git status`管理未提交的更改","识别重新提交的提交哈希"],"ja":["修正コミットの自動作成","`git status`を使用した未コミットの変更の管理","リベースのコミットハッシュの識別"],"ko":["수정 커밋 자동 생성","`git status`를 사용한 커밋되지 않은 변경 사항 관리","재기반을 위한 커밋 해시 식별"],"es":["Automatización de la creación de commits de fixup","Gestión de cambios no comprometidos con `git status`","Identificación de hashes de commit para rebasado"],"fr":["Automation de la création de commits de correction","Gestion des modifications non validées avec `git status`","Identification des hashes de commit pour le rebasage"],"de":["Automatisierung der Erstellung von Fixup-Commits","Verwaltung nicht committeter Änderungen mit `git status`","Identifizierung von Commit-Hashes für Rebasen"],"pt":["Automatização da criação de commits de fixup","Gerenciamento de alterações não comprometidas com `git status`","Identificação de hashes de commit para rebasamento"],"ru":["Автоматизация создания коммитов исправления","Управление незакоммиченными изменениями с помощью `git status`","Определение хешей коммитов для ребейза"],"ar":["التنفيذ الآلي لإنشاء التزامات الإصلاح","إدارة التغييرات غير الملتزمة بـ `git status`","تحديد hashes الالتزامات لإعادة القاعدة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires git installation","Needs access to remote repository with `git fetch origin`","Limited to interactive rebase workflows"],"zh":["需要git安装","需要使用`git fetch origin`访问远程仓库","仅限交互式重新提交工作流"],"ja":["gitのインストールが必要","`git fetch origin`を使用してリモートリポジトリにアクセスする必要があり","対話型のリベースワークフローに限定"],"ko":["git 설치가 필요","`git fetch origin`을 사용하여 원격 저장소에 액세스해야 함","대화형 재기반 워크플로에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere instalación de git","Necesita acceso al repositorio remoto con `git fetch origin`","Limitado a flujos de trabajo de rebasado interactivo"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de git","Besoin d''accès au référentiel distant avec `git fetch origin`","Limité aux flux de travail de rebasage interactif"],"de":["Benötigt git-Installation","Benötigt Zugriff auf Remote-Repository mit `git fetch origin`","Begrenzt auf interaktive Rebase-Workflows"],"pt":["Requer instalação do git","Necessita acesso ao repositório remoto com `git fetch origin`","Limitado a fluxos de trabalho de rebase interativo"],"ru":["Требуется установка git","Требуется доступ к удаленному репозиторию с помощью `git fetch origin`","Ограничен рабочими процессами интерактивного ребейза"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت git","يحتاج إلى الوصول إلى المستودع البعيد مع `git fetch origin`","محدود بعمليات العمل لإعادة قاعدة تفاعلية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/xfeed', 'community', 'majiayu000', 'claude-skill-registry', 'majiayu000/claude-skill-registry', 'xfeed', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z', '2026-02-18T07:10:14.656Z', NULL, '{"id":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/xfeed","name":"xfeed","description":{"zh":"XFeed技能允许您根据兴趣定义筛选X时间线，获取相关的推文和技术新闻","ja":"XFeedスキルは、Xタイムラインをフィルタリングして関連するツイートやテクノロジーニュースを取得します","ko":"XFeed 기술은 관심 정의에 따라 X 타임라인을 필터링하여 관련된 트윗과 기술 뉴스를 가져옵니다","es":"xfeed es una habilidad que filtra tu timeline de X según tus intereses. Obtiene noticias relevantes de AI/ML y tecnología.","fr":"xfeed est une compétence qui filtre votre timeline X en fonction de vos intérêts. Obtenez des actualités pertinentes sur l''IA/ML et la technologie.","de":"xfeed ist eine Fähigkeit, die Ihre X-Timeline nach Ihren Interessen filtert. Erhalten Sie relevante Nachrichten zu AI/ML und Technologie.","pt":"O xfeed é uma ferramenta que filtra sua linha do tempo do Twitter com base em seus interesses, fornecendo notícias relevantes de AI/ML e tecnologia.","ru":"xfeed — это инструмент, который фильтрует вашу ленту Twitter на основе ваших интересов, предоставляя актуальные новости AI/ML и технологий.","ar":"xfeed هو أداة تصفية سجل تويتر الخاص بك بناءً على اهتماماتك، وتقديم الأخبار ذات الصلة عن الذكاء الاصطناعي وتكنولوجيا المعلومات","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"XFeed技能：筛选X时间线","ja":"XFeedスキル：Xタイムラインのフィルタリング","ko":"XFeed 기술: X 타임라인 필터링","es":"xfeed: Filtrado de timeline de X","fr":"xfeed: Filtrage de la timeline X","de":"xfeed: Gefilterte X-Timeline","pt":"xfeed: Filtragem de Linha do Tempo do Twitter","ru":"xfeed: Фильтрация ленты Twitter","ar":"xfeed: تصفية سجل تويتر","en":"xfeed"},"description":{"zh":"XFeed技能允许您根据兴趣定义筛选X时间线，获取相关的推文和技术新闻","ja":"XFeedスキルは、Xタイムラインをフィルタリングして関連するツイートやテクノロジーニュースを取得します","ko":"XFeed 기술은 관심 정의에 따라 X 타임라인을 필터링하여 관련된 트윗과 기술 뉴스를 가져옵니다","es":"xfeed es una habilidad que filtra tu timeline de X según tus intereses. Obtiene noticias relevantes de AI/ML y tecnología.","fr":"xfeed est une compétence qui filtre votre timeline X en fonction de vos intérêts. Obtenez des actualités pertinentes sur l''IA/ML et la technologie.","de":"xfeed ist eine Fähigkeit, die Ihre X-Timeline nach Ihren Interessen filtert. Erhalten Sie relevante Nachrichten zu AI/ML und Technologie.","pt":"O xfeed é uma ferramenta que filtra sua linha do tempo do Twitter com base em seus interesses, fornecendo notícias relevantes de AI/ML e tecnologia.","ru":"xfeed — это инструмент, который фильтрует вашу ленту Twitter на основе ваших интересов, предоставляя актуальные новости AI/ML и технологий.","ar":"xfeed هو أداة تصفية سجل تويتر الخاص بك بناءً على اهتماماتك، وتقديم الأخبار ذات الصلة عن الذكاء الاصطناعي وتكنولوجيا المعلومات","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["筛选X时间线","根据兴趣定义","获取相关推文","获取技术新闻","支持X/Twitter"],"ja":["Xタイムラインのフィルタリング","興味の定義に基づく","関連するツイートの取得","テクノロジーニュースの取得","X/Twitterのサポート"],"ko":["X 타임라인 필터링","관심 정의에 따른","관련된 트윗 가져오기","기술 뉴스 가져오기","X/Twitter 지원"],"es":["Filtrado de timeline de X","Noticias relevantes de AI/ML","Noticias de tecnología","Configuración personalizable","Integración con la línea de comandos xfeed"],"fr":["Filtrage de la timeline X","Actualités pertinentes sur l''IA/ML","Actualités de la technologie","Configuration personnalisable","Intégration avec la ligne de commande xfeed"],"de":["Gefilterte X-Timeline","Relevante Nachrichten zu AI/ML","Technologienachrichten","Anpassbare Konfiguration","Integration mit der xfeed-Kommandozeile"],"pt":["Filtragem de linha do tempo do Twitter","Notícias relevantes de AI/ML e tecnologia","Configuração personalizada com ~/.xfeed/objectives.md","Integração com o CLI do xfeed","Atualizações em tempo real"],"ru":["Фильтрация ленты Twitter","Актуальные новости AI/ML и технологий","Пользовательская настройка с ~/.xfeed/objectives.md","Интеграция с CLI xfeed","Обновления в реальном времени"],"ar":["تصفية سجل تويتر","أخبار حديثة عن الذكاء الاصطناعي وتكنولوجيا المعلومات","تخصيص الإعدادات باستخدام ~/.xfeed/objectives.md","التكامل مع واجهة سطر الأوامر xfeed","تحديثات في الوقت الفعلي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["XFeed","X时间线","筛选","推文","技术新闻","AI新闻","Twitter"],"ja":["XFeed","Xタイムライン","フィルタリング","ツイート","テクノロジーニュース","AIニュース","Twitter"],"ko":["XFeed","X 타임라인","필터링","트윗","기술 뉴스","AI 뉴스","Twitter"],"es":["xfeed","timeline de X","filtrado de contenido","noticias de AI/ML","noticias de tecnología","desarrollo de software","línea de comandos xfeed"],"fr":["xfeed","timeline X","filtrage de contenu","actualités IA/ML","actualités de la technologie","développement de logiciels","ligne de commande xfeed"],"de":["xfeed","X-Timeline","Inhaltsfilterung","AI/ML-Nachrichten","Technologienachrichten","Softwareentwicklung","xfeed-Kommandozeile"],"pt":["xfeed","twitter","linha do tempo","filtragem","AI/ML","tecnologia","notícias","desenvolvedores","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["xfeed","twitter","лента","фильтрация","AI/ML","технологии","новости","разработчики","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["xfeed","تويتر","سجل","تصفية","الذكاء الاصطناعي","تكنولوجيا المعلومات","أخبار","مطورون","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"xfeed","description":"Fetch and display filtered X (Twitter) timeline based on your interests. Shows AI/ML research, developer tools, and technical content while filtering out noise, rage bait, and irrelevant posts. Uses Claude Haiku to score relevance against your objectives.","bodyPreview":"# XFeed - Filtered X Timeline\n\nFetch your X timeline and filter it based on your interests defined in ~/.xfeed/objectives.md.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when users want to:\n- Check their X/Twitter timeline\n- See filtered, relevant tweets\n- Catch up on AI/ML news and research\n- See what''s happening in tech without the noise\n\n**Trigger keywords:** twitter, x feed, timeline, tweets, what''s happening, tech news, AI news\n\n## Requirements\n\nThe xfeed CLI must be installed and configured","body":"# XFeed - Filtered X Timeline\n\nFetch your X timeline and filter it based on your interests defined in ~/.xfeed/objectives.md.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when users want to:\n- Check their X/Twitter timeline\n- See filtered, relevant tweets\n- Catch up on AI/ML news and research\n- See what''s happening in tech without the noise\n\n**Trigger keywords:** twitter, x feed, timeline, tweets, what''s happening, tech news, AI news\n\n## Requirements\n\nThe xfeed CLI must be installed and configured:\n- Logged into X (twitter.com) in Chrome\n- Anthropic API key\n\n## Commands\n\n### Fetch Filtered Timeline\n```bash\nxfeed fetch --count 30\n```\n\n### Fetch More Tweets\n```bash\nxfeed fetch --count 50\n```\n\n### Fetch with Lower Threshold (More Results)\n```bash\nxfeed fetch --count 30 --threshold 5\n```\n\n### View Raw Unfiltered Feed\n```bash\nxfeed fetch --count 20 --raw\n```\n\n### View Current Objectives\n```bash\nxfeed objectives\n```\n\n### Check Configuration\n```bash\nxfeed config --show\n```\n\n## How It Works\n\n1. Uses your Chrome session to access X\n2. Fetches your home timeline with Playwright\n3. Sends tweets to Claude Haiku for relevance scoring\n4. Displays tweets scoring above threshold (default: 7/10)\n5. Shows relevance reason for each tweet\n\n## Objectives\n\nYour interests are defined in `~/.xfeed/objectives.md`. Current focus:\n- AI/ML research and breakthroughs\n- Model releases and benchmarks\n- AI safety and alignment\n- Developer tools and productivity\n- Major news (real events only)\n\nExclusions: rage bait, crypto promotion, engagement farming, political tribalism\n\n## Output Format\n\nEach tweet shows:\n- Author and handle\n- Time ago\n- Relevance score [X/10]\n- Tweet content\n- Engagement metrics\n- Why it''s relevant\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n**\"Not logged in\"**: Log into x.com in Chrome first\n**\"Not logged in\"**: Your X session expired, log in again in Chrome\n**API errors**: Check Anthropic API key in `.env`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:10:14.656Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Social Media Analysis Agents needing filtered Twitter timeline access and AI/ML news curation.","zh":"非常适合需要过滤 Twitter 时间线访问和 AI/ML 新闻策划的社交媒体分析代理。","ja":"Twitter タイムラインのフィルタリングと AI/ML ニュースのキュレーションが必要なソーシャルメディア分析エージェントに最適です。","ko":"필터링된 Twitter 타임라인 액세스 및 AI/ML 뉴스 큐레이션이 필요한 소셜 미디어 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis de Medios Sociales que necesitan acceso a la línea de tiempo de Twitter filtrada y curación de noticias de IA/ML.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents d''Analyse des Médias Sociaux ayant besoin d''un accès à la ligne de temps Twitter filtrée et d''une curation de nouvelles d''IA/ML.","de":"Perfekt für Social Media Analyse Agenten, die Zugriff auf die gefilterte Twitter-Zeitleiste und AI/ML-Nachrichtenkuratierung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Mídia Social que precisam de acesso à linha do tempo do Twitter filtrada e curadoria de notícias de IA/ML.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа социальных медиа, которым требуется доступ к фильтрованной ленте Twitter и курирование новостей ИИ/МЛ.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل وسائل الإعلام الاجتماعية الذي يحتاج إلى الوصول إلى جدول زمني تويتر المُرشّح وتنقيح أخبار الذكاء الاصطناعي والتعلم الآلي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to fetch and filter X/Twitter timelines based on custom objectives defined in ~/.xfeed/objectives.md, utilizing the xfeed CLI for personalized tech news and research updates, all while leveraging Twitter API for real-time data.","zh":"使代理能够根据 ~/.xfeed/objectives.md 中定义的自定义目标检索和过滤 X/Twitter 时间线，利用 xfeed CLI 进行个性化的技术新闻和研究更新，同时利用 Twitter API 进行实时数据处理。","ja":"エージェントが ~/.xfeed/objectives.md で定義されたカスタム目標に基づいて X/Twitter タイムラインを取得してフィルタリングできるようにし、xfeed CLI を使用してパーソナライズされたテクノロジーニュースと研究の更新を提供し、同時に Twitter API を使用してリアルタイムデータを処理します。","ko":"에이전트가 ~/.xfeed/objectives.md에서 정의된 사용자 지정 목표를 기준으로 X/Twitter 타임라인을 가져와 필터링할 수 있도록 하며, xfeed CLI를 사용하여 개인화된 기술 뉴스 및 연구 업데이트를 제공하며, 동시에 Twitter API를 사용하여 실시간 데이터를 처리합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a recuperar y filtrar líneas de tiempo de X/Twitter basadas en objetivos personalizados definidos en ~/.xfeed/objectives.md, utilizando la CLI de xfeed para actualizaciones personalizadas de noticias y investigación tecnológica, todo mientras aprovecha la API de Twitter para datos en tiempo real.","fr":"Permet aux agents de récupérer et de filtrer les lignes de temps X/Twitter basées sur des objectifs personnalisés définis dans ~/.xfeed/objectives.md, en utilisant la CLI xfeed pour des mises à jour personnalisées de nouvelles et de recherche technologique, le tout en exploitant l''API Twitter pour des données en temps réel.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, X/Twitter-Zeitleisten basierend auf benutzerdefinierten Zielen abzurufen und zu filtern, die in ~/.xfeed/objectives.md definiert sind, unter Verwendung der xfeed-CLI für personalisierte Techniknachrichten- und Forschungsaktualisierungen, während die Twitter-API für Echtzeitdaten genutzt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a buscar e filtrar linhas do tempo do X/Twitter com base em objetivos personalizados definidos em ~/.xfeed/objectives.md, utilizando a CLI xfeed para atualizações de notícias e pesquisas personalizadas, tudo isso aproveitando a API do Twitter para dados em tempo real.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью извлекать и фильтровать ленты X/Twitter на основе пользовательских целей, определенных в ~/.xfeed/objectives.md, используя CLI xfeed для персонализированных обновлений технологических новостей и исследований, все это при использовании Twitter API для данных в режиме реального времени.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على استرجاع وتنقية جداول زمنية X/تويتر بناءً على أهداف مخصصة محددة في ~/.xfeed/objectives.md، باستخدام واجهة سطر الأوامر xfeed للحصول على تحديثات الأخبار والبحوث المخصصة، مع الاستفادة من واجهة برمجة تطبيقات تويتر للحصول على بيانات في الوقت الفعلي."},"useCases":{"en":["Filtering Twitter timelines for relevant AI/ML news","Automating tech news updates for agent awareness","Debugging X/Twitter API connectivity issues"],"zh":["过滤 Twitter 时间线以获取相关的 AI/ML 新闻","自动化技术新闻更新以提高代理意识","调试 X/Twitter API 连接问题"],"ja":["関連する AI/ML ニュースを取得するために Twitter タイムラインをフィルタリング","エージェントの認識を高めるためにテクノロジーニュースの更新を自動化","X/Twitter API 接続の問題をデバッグ"],"ko":["관련된 AI/ML 뉴스를 얻기 위해 Twitter 타임라인을 필터링","에이전트의 인식度를 높이기 위해 기술 뉴스 업데이트를 자동화","X/Twitter API 연결 문제를 디버깅"],"es":["Filtrado de líneas de tiempo de Twitter para noticias relevantes de IA/ML","Automatización de actualizaciones de noticias tecnológicas para la conciencia del agente","Depuración de problemas de conectividad de la API de X/Twitter"],"fr":["Filtrage des lignes de temps Twitter pour des nouvelles pertinentes d''IA/ML","Automatisation des mises à jour des nouvelles technologiques pour la conscience de l''agent","Débogage des problèmes de connectivité de l''API X/Twitter"],"de":["Filtern von Twitter-Zeitleisten für relevante AI/ML-Nachrichten","Automatisierung von Techniknachrichten-Updates für die Agentenkenntnis","Fehlerbehebung bei der Konnektivität der X/Twitter-API"],"pt":["Filtragem de linhas do tempo do Twitter para notícias relevantes de IA/ML","Automação de atualizações de notícias de tecnologia para conscientização do agente","Depuração de problemas de conectividade da API do X/Twitter"],"ru":["Фильтрация лент Twitter для получения релевантных новостей ИИ/МЛ","Автоматизация обновлений технологических новостей для осведомленности агента","Отладка проблем подключения к API X/Twitter"],"ar":["ترشيح جداول زمنية تويتر للحصول على أخبار ذكاء اصطناعي وتعلم آلي ذات صلة","تأتميم تحديثات الأخبار الفنية لتوعية الوكيل","تصحيح مشاكل الاتصال بواجهة برمجة تطبيقات X/تويتر"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires xfeed CLI installation and configuration","Needs ~/.xfeed/objectives.md for custom filtering"],"zh":["需要 xfeed CLI 的安装和配置","需要 ~/.xfeed/objectives.md 进行自定义过滤"],"ja":["xfeed CLI のインストールと設定が必要","~/.xfeed/objectives.md がカスタムフィルタリングに必要"],"ko":["xfeed CLI의 설치 및 구성이 필요","~/.xfeed/objectives.md가 사용자 지정 필터링에 필요"],"es":["Requiere instalación y configuración de la CLI de xfeed","Necesita ~/.xfeed/objectives.md para filtrado personalizado"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation et la configuration de la CLI xfeed","Nécessite ~/.xfeed/objectives.md pour un filtrage personnalisé"],"de":["Benötigt xfeed-CLI-Installation und -Konfiguration","Benötigt ~/.xfeed/objectives.md für benutzerdefiniertes Filtern"],"pt":["Exige instalação e configuração da CLI xfeed","Necessita de ~/.xfeed/objectives.md para filtragem personalizada"],"ru":["Требует установки и конфигурации CLI xfeed","Требует ~/.xfeed/objectives.md для пользовательской фильтрации"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت وتهيئة واجهة سطر الأوامر xfeed","يتطلب ~/.xfeed/objectives.md للترشيح المخصص"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/app-pages', 'community', 'majiayu000', 'claude-skill-registry', 'majiayu000/claude-skill-registry', 'app-pages', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z', '2026-02-18T07:10:29.425Z', NULL, '{"id":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/app-pages","name":"app-pages","description":{"zh":"应用程序页面是展示在应用程序中的顶级视图。开发人员可以通过特定的代码和组件来创建这些页面","ja":"アプリページはアプリケーションで表示されるトップレベルのビューです。開発者は特定のコードとコンポーネントを使用してこれらのページを作成できます","ko":"애플리케이션 페이지는 애플리케이션에서 표시되는 최상위 뷰입니다. 개발자는 특정 코드와 컴포넌트를 사용하여 이러한 페이지를 생성할 수 있습니다","es":"Las páginas de aplicaciones son vistas de nivel superior que se muestran en la aplicación. Aprende a definir y personalizar estas páginas.","fr":"Les pages d''applications sont des vues de niveau supérieur affichées dans l''application. Découvrez comment les définir et les personnaliser.","de":"Anwendungsseiten sind oberste Ebenen, die in der Anwendung angezeigt werden. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie diese Seiten definieren und anpassen können.","pt":"O recurso app-pages permite criar páginas de aplicativos personalizadas. As páginas são vistas de nível superior que exibimos no aplicativo","ru":"Функция app-pages позволяет создавать собственные страницы приложений. Страницы являются верхнеуровневыми представлениями, которые отображаются в приложении","ar":"تسمح ميزة app-pages بإنشاء صفحات تطبيقات مخصصة. الصفحات هي معروضات من المستوى الأعلى التي تعرضها في التطبيق","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"应用程序页面开发指南","ja":"アプリページ開発ガイド","ko":"애플리케이션 페이지 개발 가이드","es":"Páginas de Aplicaciones: Guía Técnica para Desarrolladores","fr":"Pages d''Applications : Guide Technique pour Développeurs","de":"App-Seiten: Technische Anleitung für Entwickler","pt":"Desenvolvimento de Páginas de Aplicativos com app-pages","ru":"Разработка страниц приложений с помощью app-pages","ar":"تطوير صفحات التطبيقات باستخدام app-pages","en":"app-pages"},"description":{"zh":"应用程序页面是展示在应用程序中的顶级视图。开发人员可以通过特定的代码和组件来创建这些页面","ja":"アプリページはアプリケーションで表示されるトップレベルのビューです。開発者は特定のコードとコンポーネントを使用してこれらのページを作成できます","ko":"애플리케이션 페이지는 애플리케이션에서 표시되는 최상위 뷰입니다. 개발자는 특정 코드와 컴포넌트를 사용하여 이러한 페이지를 생성할 수 있습니다","es":"Las páginas de aplicaciones son vistas de nivel superior que se muestran en la aplicación. Aprende a definir y personalizar estas páginas.","fr":"Les pages d''applications sont des vues de niveau supérieur affichées dans l''application. Découvrez comment les définir et les personnaliser.","de":"Anwendungsseiten sind oberste Ebenen, die in der Anwendung angezeigt werden. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie diese Seiten definieren und anpassen können.","pt":"O recurso app-pages permite criar páginas de aplicativos personalizadas. As páginas são vistas de nível superior que exibimos no aplicativo","ru":"Функция app-pages позволяет создавать собственные страницы приложений. Страницы являются верхнеуровневыми представлениями, которые отображаются в приложении","ar":"تسمح ميزة app-pages بإنشاء صفحات تطبيقات مخصصة. الصفحات هي معروضات من المستوى الأعلى التي تعرضها في التطبيق","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["顶级视图的创建","页面名称和组件位置的定义","特定代码和组件的使用","应用程序页面的开发指南","页面间的导航和交互"],"ja":["トップレベルのビューの作成","ページ名とコンポーネントの位置の定義","特定のコードとコンポーネントの使用","アプリページの開発ガイド","ページ間のナビゲーションとインタラクション"],"ko":["최상위 뷰의 생성","페이지 이름과 컴포넌트 위치의 정의","특정 코드와 컴포넌트의 사용","애플리케이션 페이지의 개발 가이드","페이지 간의 네비게이션과 상호작용"],"es":["Definir nombres de páginas en src/store/types.ts","Crear componentes personalizados para cada página","Seguir un patrón similar al de src/components/SearchResultsView","Personalizar la experiencia del usuario en cada página","Utilizar el archivo src/App.tsx como página principal"],"fr":["Définir les noms de pages dans src/store/types.ts","Créer des composants personnalisés pour chaque page","Suivre un modèle similaire à celui de src/components/SearchResultsView","Personnaliser l''expérience utilisateur sur chaque page","Utiliser le fichier src/App.tsx comme page principale"],"de":["Seitennamen in src/store/types.ts definieren","Benutzerdefinierte Komponenten für jede Seite erstellen","Ein Muster ähnlich wie src/components/SearchResultsView folgen","Die Benutzererfahrung auf jeder Seite anpassen","Die Datei src/App.tsx als Hauptseite verwenden"],"pt":["Criação de páginas de aplicativos personalizadas","Definição de nomes de páginas em src/store/types.ts","Padrão de estrutura de página semelhante ao SearchResultsView","Integração com o componente principal do aplicativo","Melhoria da experiência do usuário com páginas personalizadas"],"ru":["Создание собственных страниц приложений","Определение имен страниц в src/store/types.ts","Шаблон структуры страницы, аналогичный SearchResultsView","Интеграция с основным компонентом приложения","Улучшение опыта пользователя с помощью индивидуальных страниц"],"ar":["إنشاء صفحات تطبيقات مخصصة","تحديد أسماء الصفحات في src/store/types.ts","نمط هيكل الصفحة الشبيه بالعرض البحثية","التكامل مع المكون الرئيسي للتطبيق","تحسين تجربة المستخدم مع صفحات مخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["应用程序页面开发","顶级视图","页面名称","组件位置","代码实现","应用程序开发","前端开发","页面间导航"],"ja":["アプリページ開発","トップレベルのビュー","ページ名","コンポーネントの位置","コード実装","アプリケーション開発","フロントエンド開発","ページ間ナビゲーション"],"ko":["애플리케이션 페이지 개발","최상위 뷰","페이지 이름","컴포넌트 위치","코드 구현","애플리케이션 개발","프론트엔드 개발","페이지 간 네비게이션"],"es":["páginas de aplicaciones","desarrollo de aplicaciones","experiencia del usuario","personalización de páginas","src/store/types.ts","src/App.tsx","componentes personalizados"],"fr":["pages d''applications","développement d''applications","expérience utilisateur","personnalisation de pages","src/store/types.ts","src/App.tsx","composants personnalisés"],"de":["Anwendungsseiten","Anwendungsentwicklung","Benutzererfahrung","Seitenanpassung","src/store/types.ts","src/App.tsx","benutzerdefinierte Komponenten"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de aplicativos","páginas de aplicativos","app-pages","criação de páginas personalizadas","experiência do usuário","componentes de aplicativos","src/store/types.ts","SearchResultsView"],"ru":["разработка приложений","страницы приложений","app-pages","создание индивидуальных страниц","опыт пользователя","компоненты приложений","src/store/types.ts","SearchResultsView"],"ar":["تطوير التطبيقات","صفحات التطبيقات","app-pages","إنشاء صفحات مخصصة","تجربة المستخدم","مكونات التطبيقات","src/store/types.ts","SearchResultsView"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"app-pages","description":"Pattern for application pages","bodyPreview":"# Instructions\n\n## Page Name and Component Location\n\nPages are the different top level views (aka panels) that we display in the application. Their names are defined in file `src/store/types.ts` in the following line of code.\n\n```\nexport type AppView = ''browser'' | ''search-results'' | ''settings'';\n```\n\nThe ''browser'' one is the main default application `src/App.tsx`, but any pages other than the main (browser) page should follow a pattern similar to what you find in `src/components/SearchResultsView","body":"# Instructions\n\n## Page Name and Component Location\n\nPages are the different top level views (aka panels) that we display in the application. Their names are defined in file `src/store/types.ts` in the following line of code.\n\n```\nexport type AppView = ''browser'' | ''search-results'' | ''settings'';\n```\n\nThe ''browser'' one is the main default application `src/App.tsx`, but any pages other than the main (browser) page should follow a pattern similar to what you find in `src/components/SearchResultsView.tsx`\n\n## Tab Navigation\n\nEach page has a corresponding tab button in the tab panel at the top of the screen (Browse, Search, Settings). When the user clicks a tab button, we update the `currentView` in the global `AppState`, and that causes the page to display at next render.\n\n## React Global State Management\n\nExample: `setCurrentView(''search-results'');`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:10:29.425Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing to manage and customize application pages with TypeScript and React.","zh":"非常适合需要使用TypeScript和React管理和自定义应用程序页面的前端代理。","ja":"TypeScriptとReactを使用してアプリケーションページを管理およびカスタマイズする必要があるフロントエンドエージェントに最適です。","ko":"TypeScript와 React를 사용하여 애플리케이션 페이지를 관리하고 사용자 정의하는 프론트엔드 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes Frontend que necesitan gestionar y personalizar páginas de aplicaciones con TypeScript y React.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend qui ont besoin de gérer et de personnaliser des pages d''applications avec TypeScript et React.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agenten, die Anwendungsseiten mit TypeScript und React verwalten und anpassen müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que precisam gerenciar e personalizar páginas de aplicativos com TypeScript e React.","ru":"Идеально для агентов Frontend, которым необходимо управлять и настраивать страницы приложений с помощью TypeScript и React.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأماميين الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة وتخصيص صفحات التطبيقات باستخدام TypeScript و React."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create and navigate between different top-level views, such as ''browser'', ''search-results'', and ''settings'' pages, using defined AppView types in TypeScript and component-based architecture with React, facilitating seamless integration with Vercel for web deployment.","zh":"赋予代理创建和导航不同顶级视图的能力，例如使用TypeScript中的定义的AppView类型和基于React的组件架构，实现与Vercel的无缝集成以进行Web部署，例如''浏览器''、''搜索结果''和''设置''页面。","ja":"TypeScriptの定義されたAppViewタイプとReactベースのコンポーネントアーキテクチャを使用して、エージェントが異なるトップレベルビューを作成およびナビゲートできるようにし、Vercelとのシームレスな統合を実現してWebデプロイメントを行うことができるため、たとえば''ブラウザ''、''検索結果''、''設定''ページなど。","ko":"에이전트가 TypeScript에서 정의된 AppView 유형과 React 기반 구성 요소 아키텍처를 사용하여 다양한 최상위 보기(예: ''브라우저'', ''검색 결과'', ''설정'' 페이지)를 생성 및 탐색할 수 있도록 하여 Vercel과 무縫 통합을 통해 웹 배포를 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear y navegar entre diferentes vistas de nivel superior, como páginas ''navegador'', ''resultados de búsqueda'' y ''ajustes'', utilizando tipos de AppView definidos en TypeScript y arquitectura basada en componentes con React, lo que facilita una integración sin problemas con Vercel para la implementación web.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer et de naviguer entre différentes vues de niveau supérieur, telles que des pages ''navigateur'', ''résultats de recherche'' et ''paramètres'', en utilisant des types AppView définis dans TypeScript et une architecture basée sur des composants avec React, ce qui facilite une intégration transparente avec Vercel pour le déploiement web.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, unterschiedliche Top-Level-Ansichten wie ''Browser'', ''Suchergebnisse'' und ''Einstellungen'' zu erstellen und zu navigieren, indem sie definierte AppView-Typen in TypeScript und eine komponentenbasierte Architektur mit React verwenden, was eine nahtlose Integration mit Vercel für die Webbereitstellung ermöglicht.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar e navegar entre diferentes visualizações de nível superior, como páginas ''navegador'', ''resultados de pesquisa'' e ''configurações'', usando tipos de AppView definidos em TypeScript e arquitetura baseada em componentes com React, facilitando a integração perfeita com o Vercel para implantação na web.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать и перемещаться между различными представлениями верхнего уровня, такими как страницы ''браузер'', ''результаты поиска'' и ''настройки'', используя определенные типы AppView в TypeScript и компонентную архитектуру с React, что облегчает беспрепятственную интеграцию с Vercel для веб-развертывания.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء التنقل بين مختلف العروض من المستوى الأعلى، مثل صفحات ''المتصفح'' و ''نتائج البحث'' و ''الإعدادات''، باستخدام أنواع AppView المحددة في TypeScript وعمارة مكونات مع React، مما يسهل التكامل السلس مع Vercel لنشر الويب."},"useCases":{"en":["Configuring application page layouts","Implementing navigation between pages","Customizing page components with React"],"zh":["配置应用程序页面布局","实现页面之间的导航","使用React自定义页面组件"],"ja":["アプリケーションページレイアウトの構成","ページ間のナビゲーションの実装","Reactを使用したページコンポーネントのカスタマイズ"],"ko":["애플리케이션 페이지 레이아웃 구성","페이지 간 탐색 구현","React를 사용한 페이지 구성 요소 사용자 정의"],"es":["Configuración de diseños de páginas de aplicaciones","Implementación de la navegación entre páginas","Personalización de componentes de página con React"],"fr":["Configuration des dispositions de pages d''applications","Mise en œuvre de la navigation entre les pages","Personnalisation des composants de page avec React"],"de":["Konfiguration von Anwendungsseitenlayouts","Implementierung der Navigation zwischen Seiten","Anpassung von Seitenkomponenten mit React"],"pt":["Configurar layouts de páginas de aplicativos","Implementar navegação entre páginas","Personalizar componentes de página com React"],"ru":["Настройка макетов страниц приложений","Реализация навигации между страницами","Настройка компонентов страниц с помощью React"],"ar":["تكوين تخطيطات صفحات التطبيقات","تنفيذ التنقل بين الصفحات","تخصيص مكونات الصفحة باستخدام React"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of TypeScript and React","Limited to predefined AppView types"],"zh":["需要TypeScript和React的知识","仅限于预定义的AppView类型"],"ja":["TypeScriptとReactの知識が必要","事前に定義されたAppViewタイプに限定される"],"ko":["TypeScript와 React에 대한 지식이 필요합니다.","사전에 정의된 AppView 유형으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de TypeScript y React","Limitado a tipos de AppView predefinidos"],"fr":["Requiert des connaissances en TypeScript et React","Limité à des types AppView prédéfinis"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse in TypeScript und React","Begrenzt auf vordefinierte AppView-Typen"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento de TypeScript e React","Limitado a tipos de AppView predefinidos"],"ru":["Требует знания TypeScript и React","Ограничен предопределенными типами AppView"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة TypeScript و React","محدود بنوع AppView المحدد مسبقًا"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/done', 'community', 'majiayu000', 'claude-skill-registry', 'majiayu000/claude-skill-registry', 'done', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z', '2026-02-18T07:10:36.157Z', NULL, '{"id":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/done","name":"done","description":{"zh":"任务完成工作流是一套用于完成开发任务的步骤，包括提交更改、重新基线和创建拉取请求","ja":"タスク完了ワークフローは、開発タスクを完了するための手順です。変更のコミット、リベース、プルリクエストの作成が含まれます","ko":"작업 완료 워크플로는 개발 작업을 완료하는 데 사용되는 일련의 단계로 변경 사항을 커밋하고 재배치 및 풀 요청을 생성합니다","es":"El flujo de trabajo de finalización de tareas de desarrollo implica comprobar el código, confirmar cambios y crear solicitudes de extracción","fr":"Le workflow de finition de tâches de développement implique la vérification du code, la confirmation des modifications et la création de demandes d''extraction","de":"Der Entwicklungs-Aufgabenabschluss-Workflow umfasst die Überprüfung des Codes, das Bestätigen von Änderungen und das Erstellen von Pull-Requests","pt":"Este fluxo de trabalho ajuda a concluir tarefas de desenvolvimento, garantindo commits e pull requests de alta qualidade","ru":"Этот поток работы помогает завершать задачи разработки, обеспечивая высокое качество коммитов и пулл-реквестов","ar":"يساعد هذا التدفق في إكمال المهام التطويرية، مع ضمان جودة عالية لالتزامات وطلبات السحب","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"任务完成工作流 - Claude Code 技能","ja":"タスク完了ワークフロー - Claude Code スキル","ko":"작업 완료 워크플ロー - Claude Code 스킬","es":"Flujo de trabajo de finalización de tareas de desarrollo","fr":"Workflow de finition de tâches de développement","de":"Entwicklungs-Aufgabenabschluss-Workflow","pt":"Fluxo de Trabalho de Conclusão de Tarefas","ru":"Поток завершения задач","ar":"تدفق إكمال المهام","en":"done"},"description":{"zh":"任务完成工作流是一套用于完成开发任务的步骤，包括提交更改、重新基线和创建拉取请求","ja":"タスク完了ワークフローは、開発タスクを完了するための手順です。変更のコミット、リベース、プルリクエストの作成が含まれます","ko":"작업 완료 워크플로는 개발 작업을 완료하는 데 사용되는 일련의 단계로 변경 사항을 커밋하고 재배치 및 풀 요청을 생성합니다","es":"El flujo de trabajo de finalización de tareas de desarrollo implica comprobar el código, confirmar cambios y crear solicitudes de extracción","fr":"Le workflow de finition de tâches de développement implique la vérification du code, la confirmation des modifications et la création de demandes d''extraction","de":"Der Entwicklungs-Aufgabenabschluss-Workflow umfasst die Überprüfung des Codes, das Bestätigen von Änderungen und das Erstellen von Pull-Requests","pt":"Este fluxo de trabalho ajuda a concluir tarefas de desenvolvimento, garantindo commits e pull requests de alta qualidade","ru":"Этот поток работы помогает завершать задачи разработки, обеспечивая высокое качество коммитов и пулл-реквестов","ar":"يساعد هذا التدفق في إكمال المهام التطويرية، مع ضمان جودة عالية لالتزامات وطلبات السحب","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["提交更改","重新基线","创建拉取请求","遵循传统的提交格式"],"ja":["変更のコミット","リベース","プルリクエストの作成","従来のコミット形式に従う"],"ko":["변경 사항을 커밋","재배치","풀 요청 생성","従来의 커밋 형식 준수"],"es":["Comprobación de código","Confirmación de cambios","Creación de solicitudes de extracción","Seguimiento de historial de Git","Formato de confirmación convencional"],"fr":["Vérification du code","Confirmation des modifications","Création de demandes d''extraction","Suivi de l''historique Git","Format de confirmation conventionnel"],"de":["Code-Überprüfung","Änderungsbestätigung","Erstellung von Pull-Requests","Git-Historie-Verfolgung","Konventionelles Commit-Format"],"pt":["Verificação de pré-voo","Commits e pull requests de alta qualidade","Rebase no branch main","Seguimento de convenções de commit","Histórico de git que aparece como autorizado por humanos","Inclusão de descrições claras e concisas"],"ru":["Предполетные проверки","Коммиты и пулл-реквесты высокого качества","Ребейз на ветке main","Следование конвенциям коммитов","История гита, которая выглядит как созданная человеком","Включение четких и кратких описаний"],"ar":["فحص ما قبل الطيران","التزامات وطلبات سحب ذو جودة عالية","إعادة Основ على الفرع الرئيسي","التزام بمواصفات الالتزام","تاريخ جيت يبدو وكأنه مصدره إنسان","إدراج وصفات واضحة وموجزة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["任务完成工作流","开发流程","代码审查","提交更改","重新基线","创建拉取请求"],"ja":["タスク完了ワークフロー","開発プロセス","コードレビュー","変更のコミット","リベース","プルリクエストの作成"],"ko":["작업 완료 워크플로우","개발 프로세스","코드 리뷰","변경 사항을 커밋","재배치","풀 요청 생성"],"es":["desarrollo de software","flujo de trabajo de desarrollo","finalización de tareas"," Git","confirmación de cambios","solicitudes de extracción","codificación eficiente"],"fr":["développement de logiciels","workflow de développement","finition de tâches","Git","confirmation des modifications","demandes d''extraction","codage efficace"],"de":["Software-Entwicklung","Entwicklungs-Workflow","Aufgabenabschluss","Git","Änderungsbestätigung","Pull-Requests","effizientes Codieren"],"pt":["fluxo de trabalho de desenvolvimento","conclusão de tarefas","commits de alta qualidade","pull requests","rebase no main","convenções de commit","git history","desenvolvimento de software","práticas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["поток разработки","завершение задач","коммиты высокого качества","пулл-реквесты","ребейз на мейн","конвенции коммитов","история гита","разработка программного обеспечения","практики разработки"],"ar":["تدفق التطوير","إكمال المهام","التزامات ذو جودة عالية","طلبات السحب","إعادة الفرع الرئيسي","مواصفات الالتزام","تاريخ جيت","تطوير البرمجيات","ممارسات التطوير"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"done","description":"Finish a task by committing changes, rebasing on main, and creating a PR","bodyPreview":"# Task Completion Workflow\n\nYou are finishing a development task. Follow these steps in order to commit changes, rebase on main, and create a pull request.\n\n## CRITICAL RULES\n\n- **NEVER** include AI tool references in commits, PRs, or code comments\n- **NO** \"Co-Authored-By: Claude\" or similar AI attributions\n- All git history must appear human-authored\n- Follow conventional commit format: `<type>: <description>`\n\n## Step 1: Pre-flight Checks\n\nRun these checks **sequentially**:\n\n1. Verify in git","body":"# Task Completion Workflow\n\nYou are finishing a development task. Follow these steps in order to commit changes, rebase on main, and create a pull request.\n\n## CRITICAL RULES\n\n- **NEVER** include AI tool references in commits, PRs, or code comments\n- **NO** \"Co-Authored-By: Claude\" or similar AI attributions\n- All git history must appear human-authored\n- Follow conventional commit format: `<type>: <description>`\n\n## Step 1: Pre-flight Checks\n\nRun these checks **sequentially**:\n\n1. Verify in git repository:\n   ```bash\n   git rev-parse --git-dir\n   ```\n\n2. Get current branch:\n   ```bash\n   git branch --show-current\n   ```\n\n3. Check for changes:\n   ```bash\n   git status --porcelain\n   ```\n\n**Stop conditions:**\n- If not in git repo → **Error**: \"Not in a git repository\"\n- If on `main` branch → **Error**: \"Cannot commit directly to main branch. Create a feature branch first.\"\n- If no changes (empty output) → **Error**: \"No changes to commit\"\n\nIf all checks pass, proceed to Step 2.\n\n## Step 2: Analyze and Commit Changes\n\n### 2.1 Review Changes\n\nRun these commands to understand what changed:\n\n```bash\ngit status\ngit diff HEAD\n```\n\nIf there are already staged files, also check:\n```bash\ngit diff --staged\n```\n\n### 2.2 Analyze Changes\n\nBased on the diff output, determine:\n\n- **Commit type**: Choose from:\n  - `feat` - New feature\n  - `fix` - Bug fix\n  - `refactor` - Code restructuring without behavior change\n  - `docs` - Documentation only\n  - `style` - Formatting, whitespace, missing semicolons\n  - `test` - Adding or updating tests\n  - `chore` - Build process, dependencies, tooling\n\n- **Description**: Write a concise summary (< 72 characters) that completes the sentence: \"This commit will...\"\n  - Good: \"add user authentication middleware\"\n  - Good: \"fix null pointer dereference in login handler\"\n  - Bad: \"changes\" or \"updates stuff\"\n\n- **Body** (optional): Add if the change is complex and needs explanation\n\n### 2.3 Security Check\n\nCheck if any changed files match sensitive patterns:\n```bash\ngit status --porcelain | grep -E ''\\.(env|key|pem)|credentials|secrets''\n```\n\nIf matches found:\n- **Warn the user**: \"Detected potential sensitive files: [list]. Are you sure you want to commit these?\"\n- **Wait for user confirmation** before proceeding\n- If user declines, stop here\n\n### 2.4 Stage Files\n\nPrefer staging specific files rather than using `git add .`:\n\n```bash\ngit add <file1> <file2> <file3>\n```\n\nOnly use `git add .` if justified (many files changed, all safe to commit).\n\n### 2.5 Create Commit\n\n**If $ARGUMENTS is provided**: Use it as the commit message directly:\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"$ARGUMENTS\"\n```\n\n**Otherwise**: Generate the commit message using the format:\n```\n<type>: <description>\n```\n\nExample:\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"feat: add user authentication middleware\"\n```\n\n**CRITICAL**: Do NOT add any Co-Authored-By or AI attribution trailers.\n\n### 2.6 Verify Commit\n\nCheck the commit was created:\n```bash\ngit log -1 --oneline\n```\n\nIf commit failed (pre-commit hooks, etc.):\n- Show the error message to the user\n- **STOP**: Let the user fix the issue\n- User can run `/done` again after fixing\n\n## Step 3: Rebase on origin/main\n\n### 3.1 Fetch Latest\n\nUpdate the remote tracking branches:\n```bash\ngit fetch origin\n```\n\n### 3.2 Rebase\n\nRebase current branch onto origin/main:\n```bash\ngit rebase origin/main\n```\n\n### 3.3 Handle Rebase Result\n\n**If rebase succeeds**: Proceed to Step 4.\n\n**If conflicts are detected** (non-zero exit code):\n\n**STOP** and inform the user:\n\n```\nRebase conflicts detected. To resolve:\n\n1. Check conflict status:\n   git status\n\n2. Open conflicted files and resolve conflicts (look for <<<<<<< markers)\n\n3. Stage resolved files:\n   git add <resolved-file>\n\n4. Continue the rebase:\n   git rebase --continue\n\n5. After resolving all conflicts, run /done again to create the PR\n\nTo abort the rebase:\n   git rebase --abort\n```\n\n**DO NOT** attempt automatic conflict resolution. This requires human judgment.\n\n## Step 4: Create Pull Request\n\n### 4.1 Gather Context\n\nGet branch and commit information:\n\n```bash\n# Current branch name\ngit branch --show-current\n\n# All commits in this branch (not in main)\ngit log origin/main..HEAD --oneline\n\n# Full commit details\ngit log origin/main..HEAD\n\n# Summary of changed files\ngit diff origin/main...HEAD --stat\n```\n\n### 4.2 Analyze Commits\n\nReview ALL commits in the branch to understand the overall change:\n- If **single commit**: PR title = commit message (which already includes the type prefix)\n- If **multiple commits**: Summarize the overall feature/fix with appropriate type prefix (feat, fix, refactor, etc.)\n\n### 4.3 Generate PR Title\n\n- **MUST** start with conventional commit type prefix: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `style:`, `test:`, or `chore:`\n- Use clear, concise language after the prefix\n- Keep under 72 characters total\n- No AI attribution\n\nExample titles:\n- \"feat: add user authentication middleware\"\n- \"fix: null pointer dereference in login handler\"\n- \"refactor: session management for improved performance\"\n- \"docs: add API documentation for auth endpoints\"\n- \"chore: update dependencies to latest versions\"\n\n### 4.4 Generate PR Body\n\nUse this format:\n\n```markdown\n## Summary\n\n- [Key change 1]\n- [Key change 2]\n- [Key change 3]\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] [Test scenario 1]\n- [ ] [Test scenario 2]\n- [ ] [Test scenario 3]\n```\n\nGuidelines:\n- 3-5 bullet points in Summary\n- Focus on \"what\" and \"why\", not implementation details\n- Test plan should be actionable checklist items\n- **NO** \"Generated with Claude Code\" or AI attribution footer\n\n### 4.5 Push Branch (if needed)\n\nBefore creating the PR, check if the branch has been pushed:\n\n```bash\ngit rev-parse --abbrev-ref --symbolic-full-name @{u} 2>/dev/null\n```\n\n**If this command fails** (no upstream branch set):\n\nPush the branch and set upstream:\n```bash\ngit push -u origin <branch-name>\n```\n\n**If this command succeeds** (upstream branch exists):\n\nCheck if local is ahead of remote:\n```bash\ngit status -sb\n```\n\nIf the output shows `[ahead N]` or `[ahead N, behind M]`:\n- After rebase, the branch needs a force push\n- Run: `git push --force-with-lease`\n\n### 4.6 Create PR\n\nUse heredoc for proper formatting:\n\n```bash\ngh pr create --title \"PR title here\" --body \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n## Summary\n\n- Key change 1\n- Key change 2\n- Key change 3\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] Test scenario 1\n- [ ] Test scenario 2\n- [ ] Test scenario 3\nEOF\n)\" --base main\n```\n\n### 4.7 Handle PR Creation Result\n\n**If successful**:\n- Display the PR URL to the user\n\n**If PR already exists**:\n- Show error message\n- If possible, extract and display the existing PR URL from the error\n- Inform user: \"A PR already exists for this branch\"\n\n**If GitHub CLI not found**:\n- Show installation instructions:\n  ```\n  GitHub CLI (gh) not found. Install it:\n  - macOS: brew install gh\n  - Linux: See https://github.com/cli/cli#installation\n\n  After installation, authenticate: gh auth login\n  ```\n\n## Error Handling\n\nFor any command that fails:\n1. Show the **exact error message** from the command\n2. Provide **actionable next steps** for the user\n3. **DO NOT** proceed to the next phase\n4. User can fix the issue and run `/done` again\n\n## Notes\n\n- The workflow automatically handles pushing the branch if needed (Step 4.5)\n- Prefer clear, atomic commits over large batch commits\n- The PR description should help reviewers understand the context quickly\n- If pre-commit hooks modify files, they''ll need to be staged and committed again\n- After rebase, force push with `--force-with-lease` is safer than `--force` (protects against overwriting others'' work)\n\n## Usage Examples\n\n**Basic usage (auto-generated commit message):**\n```\n/done\n```\n\n**With custom commit message:**\n```\n/done \"feat: add new authentication feature\"\n```\n\n**With multi-line commit message:**\n```\n/done \"feat: add authentication\n\nImplements OAuth2 flow with JWT tokens.\nIncludes session management and refresh tokens.\"\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:10:36.157Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing streamlined task completion workflows with git.","zh":"非常适合需要简化任务完成工作流的开发代理，特别是与 git 相关的工作流。","ja":"開発エージェントがタスクの完了ワークフローを効率化する必要がある場合に最適です。特に Git に関連するワークフローです。","ko":"개발 에이전트가 작업 완료 워크플ロー 를 간소화해야 하는 경우에 적합합니다. 특히 Git와 관련된 워크플로우의 경우입니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollo que necesitan flujos de trabajo de finalización de tareas optimizados con git.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin de flux de travail de finalisation de tâches simplifiés avec git.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die optimierte Arbeitsabläufe für die Aufgabenvervollständigung mit git benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de fluxos de trabalho de conclusão de tarefas simplificados com git.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, которым необходимы упрощенные рабочие процессы выполнения задач с git.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الناشئين الذين يحتاجون إلى سير عمل簡略ة لإنجاز المهام مع جيت."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage git repositories effectively, ensuring conventional commit formats and adherence to critical rules such as excluding AI tool references and maintaining a human-authored git history, all while utilizing protocols like rebasing on main and creating pull requests.","zh":"赋予代理管理 git 仓库的能力，确保遵守传统的提交格式和关键规则，如排除 AI 工具引用并保持人工编写的 git 历史记录，同时利用诸如在主分支上重置基线和创建拉取请求之类的协议。","ja":"エージェントが Git リポジトリを効果的に管理できるようにし、従来のコミット形式に従い、AI ツールの参照を除外し、人間が書き込んだ Git の履歴を維持するなどの重要なルールを遵守することを保証する。また、メインブランチでのリベースやプルリクエストの作成などのプロトコルを使用します。","ko":"에이전트가 git 저장소를 효과적으로 관리할 수 있도록 하여 전통적인 커밋 형식과 중요한 규칙을 준수하도록하며, AI 도구 참조를 제외하고 인가가 작성한 git 기록을 유지하며, rebasing on main 및 풀 요청 생성과 같은 프로토콜을 사용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar repositorios de git de manera efectiva, asegurando formatos de compromiso convencionales y el cumplimiento de reglas críticas como la exclusión de referencias a herramientas de inteligencia artificial y el mantenimiento de un historial de git creado por humanos, todo mientras se utilizan protocolos como rebase en main y la creación de solicitudes de extracción.","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer des référentiels git de manière efficace, en garantissant des formats de commit conventionnels et le respect de règles critiques telles que l''exclusion des références aux outils d''IA et le maintien d''un historique git rédigé par l''homme, le tout en utilisant des protocoles tels que le rebase sur main et la création de demandes d''extraction.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, git-Repositorys effektiv zu verwalten, indem konventionelle Commit-Formate sichergestellt und kritische Regeln wie das Ausschließen von AI-Tool-Referenzen und die Aufrechterhaltung einer von Menschen erstellten git-Historie eingehalten werden, und zwar unter Nutzung von Protokollen wie Rebase auf Main und Erstellung von Pull-Anfragen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar repositórios git de forma eficaz, garantindo formatos de commit convencionais e adesão a regras críticas, como excluir referências de ferramentas de IA e manter um histórico de git autorado por humanos, tudo isso utilizando protocolos como rebase na main e criação de pull requests.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью эффективно управлять репозиториями git, обеспечивая соблюдение стандартных форматов коммитов и соблюдение критически важных правил, таких как исключение ссылок на инструменты ИИ и сохранение истории git, созданной человеком, все это при использовании протоколов, таких как ребейзинг на главной ветке и создание запросов на включение.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إدارة مستودعات جيت بفعالية، وضمان تنسيقات التزامات التقليدية والامتثال للقواعد الحاسمة، مثل استبعاد المراجع لأدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي والحفاظ على تاريخ جيت مكتوب من قبل الإنسان، وكل ذلك باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل إعادة التأسيس على الرأس الرئيسي وإنشاء طلبات السحب."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating commit and rebasing processes","Generating compliant pull requests","Enforcing conventional commit formats"],"zh":["自动化提交和重置基线过程","生成符合规定的拉取请求","强制执行传统的提交格式"],"ja":["コミットとリベースのプロセスを自動化する","規則に準拠したプルリクエストを生成する","従来のコミット形式を強制する"],"ko":["커밋 및 리베이스 프로세스 자동화","규정 준수 풀 요청 생성","전통적인 커밋 형식 적용"],"es":["Automatización de procesos de commit y rebase","Generación de solicitudes de extracción conformes","Aplicación de formatos de commit convencionales"],"fr":["Automatisation des processus de commit et de rebase","Génération de demandes d''extraction conformes","Application de formats de commit conventionnels"],"de":["Automatisierung von Commit- und Rebase-Prozessen","Erzeugung konformer Pull-Anfragen","Durchsetzung konventioneller Commit-Formate"],"pt":["Automatizar processos de commit e rebase","Gerar solicitações de pull conformes","Fazer cumprir formatos de commit convencionais"],"ru":["Автоматизировать процессы коммита и ребейзинга","Генерировать запросы на включение, соответствующие стандартам","Применять стандартные форматы коммитов"],"ar":["التحكم الآلي في عمليات التزام والتعديل","توليد طلبات السحب المتوافقة","فرض تنسيقات التزامات التقليدية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires git access","Must adhere to specific commit and PR formatting rules","No AI attributions allowed in commits or code comments"],"zh":["需要 git 访问权限","必须遵守特定的提交和 PR 格式化规则","提交或代码注释中不允许有 AI 属性"],"ja":["Git アクセスが必要","特定のコミットと PR の形式規則に従う必要がある","コミットまたはコードコメントに AI 属性を含めることはできない"],"ko":["git 접근 권한 필요","특정 커밋 및 PR 형식 규칙을 따라야 함","커밋 또는 코드 주석에 AI 속성을 허용할 수 없음"],"es":["Requiere acceso a git","Debe cumplir con reglas de formato de commit y PR específicas","No se permiten atribuciones de IA en commits o comentarios de código"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à git","Doit respecter des règles de formatage de commit et de PR spécifiques","Les attributions d''IA ne sont pas autorisées dans les commits ou les commentaires de code"],"de":["Erfordert git-Zugriff","Muss spezifischen Commit- und PR-Formatierungsregeln entsprechen","Keine AI-Attributionen in Commits oder Code-Kommentaren erlaubt"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao git","Deve aderir a regras específicas de formatação de commit e PR","Não são permitidas atribuições de IA em commits ou comentários de código"],"ru":["Требует доступа к git","Должно соблюдать специальные правила форматирования коммитов и PR","Не допускаются атрибуты ИИ в коммитах или комментариях кода"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى جيت","يجب اتباع قواعد محددة لتنسيق التزامات وطلبات السحب","لا يسمح بسمات الذكاء الاصطناعي في التزامات أو تعليقات الشفرة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/reviewing-Objectstar', 'community', 'majiayu000', 'claude-skill-registry', 'majiayu000/claude-skill-registry', 'reviewing-Objectstar', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z', '2026-02-18T07:10:26.254Z', NULL, '{"id":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/reviewing-Objectstar","name":"reviewing-Objectstar","description":{"zh":"Objectstar 是一种基于规则的 4GL 主机平台，使用条件象限代替 IF/THEN/ELSE，表格代替对象，规则代替程序。该技能帮助开发者识别和理解 Objectstar 代码，分析数据流和规则结构。","ja":"Objectstar はルールベースの 4GL メインフレーム プラットフォームで、IF/THEN/ELSE の代わりに条件象限、オブジェクトの代わりにテーブル、プログラムの代わりにルールを使用します。このスキルは、開発者が Objectstar コードを識別して理解し、データ フローとルール構造を分析するのに役立ちます。","ko":"Objectstar는 규칙 기반의 4GL 메인프레임 플랫폼으로, IF/THEN/ELSE 대신 조건 사분면, 객체 대신 테이블, 프로그램 대신 규칙을 사용합니다. 이 스킬은 개발자가 Objectstar 코드를 식별하고 이해하며, 데이터 흐름과 규칙 구조를 분석하는 데 도움이 됩니다.","es":"Objectstar es una plataforma de desarrollo 4GL que utiliza cuadrantes de condiciones y reglas en lugar de programas","fr":"Objectstar est une plateforme de développement 4GL qui utilise des quadrants de conditions et des règles au lieu de programmes","de":"Objectstar ist eine 4GL-Entwicklungsplattform, die Bedingungsquadranten und Regeln anstelle von Programmen verwendet","pt":"Objectstar é uma plataforma de regras de 4ª geração que utiliza quadrantes de condição e tabelas em vez de objetos e programas","ru":"Objectstar - это правилаоснованная платформа 4GL, которая использует условные квадранты и таблицы вместо объектов и программ","ar":"Objectstar هي منصة قواعد لغة الجيل الرابع التي تستخدم مربعات الشروط والجداول بدلاً من الكائنات والبرامج","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Objectstar 代码审查技能","ja":"Objectstar コードレビュースキル","ko":"Objectstar 코드 리뷰 스킬","es":"Revisión de Objectstar: Análisis de código 4GL","fr":"Révision Objectstar : Analyse de code 4GL","de":"Objectstar-Überprüfung: Analyse von 4GL-Code","pt":"Revisão de Objectstar: Plataforma de Regras de 4ª Geração","ru":"Обзор Objectstar: Правилаоснованная платформа 4GL","ar":"مراجعة Objectstar: منصة قواعد لغة الجيل الرابع","en":"reviewing-Objectstar"},"description":{"zh":"Objectstar 是一种基于规则的 4GL 主机平台，使用条件象限代替 IF/THEN/ELSE，表格代替对象，规则代替程序。该技能帮助开发者识别和理解 Objectstar 代码，分析数据流和规则结构。","ja":"Objectstar はルールベースの 4GL メインフレーム プラットフォームで、IF/THEN/ELSE の代わりに条件象限、オブジェクトの代わりにテーブル、プログラムの代わりにルールを使用します。このスキルは、開発者が Objectstar コードを識別して理解し、データ フローとルール構造を分析するのに役...","ko":"Objectstar는 규칙 기반의 4GL 메인프레임 플랫폼으로, IF/THEN/ELSE 대신 조건 사분면, 객체 대신 테이블, 프로그램 대신 규칙을 사용합니다. 이 스킬은 개발자가 Objectstar 코드를 식별하고 이해하며, 데이터 흐름과 규칙 구조를 분석하는 데 도움이 됩니다.","es":"Objectstar es una plataforma de desarrollo 4GL que utiliza cuadrantes de condiciones y reglas en lugar de programas","fr":"Objectstar est une plateforme de développement 4GL qui utilise des quadrants de conditions et des règles au lieu de programmes","de":"Objectstar ist eine 4GL-Entwicklungsplattform, die Bedingungsquadranten und Regeln anstelle von Programmen verwendet","pt":"Objectstar é uma plataforma de regras de 4ª geração que utiliza quadrantes de condição e tabelas em vez de objetos e programas","ru":"Objectstar - это правилаоснованная платформа 4GL, которая использует условные квадранты и таблицы вместо объектов и программ","ar":"Objectstar هي منصة قواعد لغة الجيل الرابع التي تستخدم مربعات الشروط والجداول بدلاً من الكائنات والبرامج","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["识别 Objectstar 代码","理解规则结构","分析数据流","支持条件象限和 FORALL 循环","支持参数化表格和规则"],"ja":["Objectstar コードの識別","ルール構造の理解","データ フローの分析","条件象限と FORALL ループのサポート","パラメータ化テーブルとルールのサポート"],"ko":["Objectstar 코드 식별","규칙 구조 이해","데이터 흐름 분석","조건 사분면과 FORALL 루프 지원","파라미터화된 테이블과 규칙 지원"],"es":["Análisis de código Objectstar","Identificación de cuadrantes de condiciones","Comprensión de la estructura de reglas","Análisis de flujo de datos","Soporte para FORALL loops y tablas parametrizadas"],"fr":["Analyse de code Objectstar","Identification de quadrants de conditions","Compréhension de la structure de règles","Analyse de flux de données","Prise en charge des boucles FORALL et des tableaux paramétrés"],"de":["Analyse von Objectstar-Code","Identifizierung von Bedingungsquadranten","Verständnis der Regelsstruktur","Analyse des Datenflusses","Unterstützung für FORALL-Schleifen und parametrierte Tabellen"],"pt":["Utiliza quadrantes de condição em vez de IF/THEN/ELSE","Emprega tabelas em vez de objetos","Suporta regras em vez de programas","Possui fluxo de trabalho de revisão de código","Permite análise de fluxo de dados","Oferece suporte estendido até 30 de março de 2027"],"ru":["Использует условные квадранты вместо IF/THEN/ELSE","Использует таблицы вместо объектов","Поддерживает правила вместо программ","Имеет рабочий процесс просмотра кода","Позволяет анализировать поток данных","Предоставляет расширенную поддержку до 30 марта 2027 года"],"ar":["تستخدم مربعات الشروط بدلاً من IF/THEN/ELSE","تستخدم الجداول بدلاً من الكائنات","تدعم القواعد بدلاً من البرامج","تمتلك تدفق عمل لمراجعة الكود","تسمح بتحليل تدفق البيانات","توفر دعمًا موسعًا حتى 30 مارس 2027"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Objectstar","4GL","主机平台","规则","条件象限","FORALL 循环","参数化表格","代码审查"],"ja":["Objectstar","4GL","メインフレーム プラットフォーム","ルール","条件象限","FORALL ループ","パラメータ化テーブル","コードレビュー"],"ko":["Objectstar","4GL","메인프레임 플랫폼","규칙","조건 사분면","FORALL 루프","파라미터화된 테이블","코드 리뷰"],"es":["Objectstar","4GL","análisis de código","desarrollo de software","reglas de negocio","cuadrantes de condiciones","FORALL loops","tablas parametrizadas"],"fr":["Objectstar","4GL","analyse de code","développement de logiciels","règles métier","quadrants de conditions","boucles FORALL","tableaux paramétrés"],"de":["Objectstar","4GL","Code-Analyse","Software-Entwicklung","Geschäftsregeln","Bedingungsquadranten","FORALL-Schleifen","parametrierte Tabellen"],"pt":["Objectstar","plataforma de regras","desenvolvimento de software","revisão de código","análise de fluxo de dados","quadrantes de condição","tabelas","regras","programas","suporte estendido"],"ru":["Objectstar","правилаоснованная платформа","разработка программного обеспечения","просмотр кода","анализ потока данных","условные квадранты","таблицы","правила","программы","расширенная поддержка"],"ar":["Objectstar","منصة قواعد","تطوير البرمجيات","مراجعة الكود","تحليل تدفق البيانات","مربعات الشروط","الجداول","القواعد","البرامج","دعم موسع"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.454Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"reviewing-Objectstar","description":"Analyze, refactor, and migrate TIBCO Objectstar (Object Service Broker) legacy mainframe applications. Use when working with Objectstar/OSB source code files, rules, screen definitions, or table definitions. Triggers on .osr, .osb file extensions, or code containing Objectstar patterns like condition quadrants (Y N columns), FORALL loops, TRANSFERCALL, parameterized tables, or rules with LOCAL declarations.","bodyPreview":"# Objectstar Language Skill\n\nObjectstar is a rules-based 4GL mainframe platform using condition quadrants instead of IF/THEN/ELSE, tables instead of objects, and rules instead of programs. Extended support ends March 30, 2027.\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n1. **Identify Objectstar code** → Look for condition quadrants, FORALL loops, parameterized tables\n2. **Understand rule structure** → Parse the four-section format (declaration, conditions, actions, handlers)\n3. **Analyze data flow** → Track LOCAL variab","body":"# Objectstar Language Skill\n\nObjectstar is a rules-based 4GL mainframe platform using condition quadrants instead of IF/THEN/ELSE, tables instead of objects, and rules instead of programs. Extended support ends March 30, 2027.\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n1. **Identify Objectstar code** → Look for condition quadrants, FORALL loops, parameterized tables\n2. **Understand rule structure** → Parse the four-section format (declaration, conditions, actions, handlers)\n3. **Analyze data flow** → Track LOCAL variable scope (visible in descendant rules)\n4. **For refactoring** → Apply patterns from [patterns.md](references/patterns.md)\n5. **For migration** → Map constructs using [migration.md](references/migration.md)\n\n## Rule Structure (Fundamental Unit)\n\nEvery Objectstar rule has four sections:\n\n```\nRULE_NAME(arg1, arg2);              -- 1. Declaration\nLOCAL var1, var2;                   -- Local variables (untyped)\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ncondition1;                         | Y N N    -- 2. Conditions (Y/N columns)\ncondition2;                         |   Y N\n------------------------------------------------------------+---------------\naction1;                            | 1        -- 3. Actions (numbered sequence)\naction2;                            |   1\naction3;                            |     1\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nON exception_name:                             -- 4. Exception handlers\n    handler_statement;\n```\n\n**Condition quadrant logic**: Conditions evaluate top-to-bottom. The Y/N pattern in each column determines which action column executes. Numbers indicate execution order within a column.\n\n## Critical Language Rules\n\n### Variable Scoping (Non-Standard)\nLOCAL variables are visible in the declaring rule AND all descendant rules (rules called from within). This breaks encapsulation—track carefully during migration.\n\n### No Traditional Loops\n- **No WHILE/FOR** — Use `FORALL` for iteration over table occurrences\n- **No IF/THEN/ELSE** — Use condition quadrant Y/N patterns\n- Loop termination via `UNTIL exception:` pattern\n\n### Data Types Are Dual-Classified\nSemantic types (C=Count, D=Date, I=Identifier, L=Logical, Q=Quantity, S=String) define meaning. Syntax types (B=Binary, C=Char, P=Packed, V=Variable, F=Float, UN=Unicode) define storage. Variables inherit type from assigned values.\n\n### Everything Is a Table\nScreens, reports, data stores, even rule storage—all tables. Table types: TDS (permanent), SCR (screen), TEM (temporary), SES (session), MAP (memory mapping), SUB (subview).\n\n### OTP vs Batch Contexts\n\nObjectstar rules run in two distinct contexts with different patterns:\n\n| Aspect | OTP (Online Transaction Processing) | Batch Processing |\n|--------|-------------------------------------|------------------|\n| **Interface** | 3270 terminal screens | Job streams (JCL/scripts) |\n| **User interaction** | Interactive, screen-driven | Unattended, scheduled |\n| **Data passing** | Screen tables (SCR) | Session tables (SES), parameters |\n| **Transaction model** | Short, user-paced commits | Long-running, periodic commits |\n| **Error handling** | SCREENMSG for user feedback | MSGLOG for logging |\n| **Typical patterns** | DISPLAY loops, TRANSFERCALL | FORALL with COMMIT windows |\n\n**OTP Pattern** (screen-driven):\n```\nUNTIL EXIT_DISPLAY DISPLAY ORDER_SCREEN:\n    CALL VALIDATE_ORDER;\n    CALL SAVE_ORDER;\nEND;\nON EXIT_DISPLAY:\n    CALL CLEANUP;\n```\n\n**Batch Pattern** (commit window):\n```\nLOCAL COUNT;\nCOUNT = 0;\nFORALL INVOICES UNTIL GETFAIL:\n    CALL PROCESS_INVOICE;\n    COUNT = COUNT + 1;\n    COUNT >= 1000;                      | Y N\n    ----------------------------------------+-----\n    COMMIT;                             | 1\n    COUNT = 0;                          | 2\nEND;\nCOMMIT;  -- Final commit\n```\n\n**Migration implications**:\n- OTP rules → Web controllers with form handling\n- Batch rules → Scheduled jobs, message queues, or streaming APIs\n- Classify rules early (OTP/Batch/Shared utility) before migration\n\n## Essential Syntax Quick Reference\n\n### Rule Invocation\n```\nCALL rule(args);                    -- Same transaction, returns\nEXECUTE IN UPDATE rule(args);       -- Child transaction\nSCHEDULE TO QUEUE rule(args);       -- Async batch\nTRANSFERCALL rule(args);            -- Transfer control, no return\n```\n\n### Data Operations\n```\nGET TABLE WHERE field = value;\nGET TABLE(param) ORDERED DESCENDING field WITH MINLOCK;\nINSERT TABLE;\nREPLACE TABLE;\nDELETE TABLE WHERE field = value;\n```\n\n### Iteration\n```\nFORALL TABLE(param) WHERE condition\n    ORDERED ASCENDING field\n    UNTIL GETFAIL:\n    -- process each occurrence\nEND;\n\nUNTIL EXIT_DISPLAY DISPLAY SCREEN:\n    -- process until exit\nEND;\n```\n\n### WHERE Clause Operators\n```\n=, >, <, >=, <=       -- Comparison\n¬= or NOT =           -- Not equal\n& or AND              -- Conjunction\n| or OR               -- Disjunction\n¬ or NOT              -- Negation\nLIKE ''ABC*''           -- * matches any string\nLIKE ''AB?D''           -- ? matches single char\n```\n\n### Exception Handling\n```\nON GETFAIL:           -- Record not found\nON GETFAIL TABLE:     -- Table-specific\nON ACCESSFAIL:        -- Any access failure\nON ERROR:             -- Catch-all (use last)\nSIGNAL CUSTOM_ERR;    -- Raise exception\n```\n\n### String Operations\n```\nstr1 || str2                        -- Concatenation\nLENGTH(s), SUBSTRING(s,start,len)\nUPPERCASE(s), LOWERCASE(s)\nMATCH(s, pattern), PAD(s,len,char,just)\n```\n\n## Reserved Keywords\n\n```\nAND        ASCENDING    BROWSE      CALL        COMMIT      CONTINUE\nDELETE     DESCENDING   DISPLAY     END         EXECUTE     FORALL\nGET        IN           INSERT      LIKE        LOCAL       NOT\nNULL       ON           OR          ORDERED     PRINT       REPLACE\nRETURN     ROLLBACK     SCHEDULE    SIGNAL      TO          TRANSFERCALL\nUNTIL      UPDATE       WHERE\n```\n\n## Common Exception Hierarchy\n\n```\nERROR (catch-all)\n├── ACCESSFAIL\n│   ├── GETFAIL, INSERTFAIL, REPLACEFAIL, DELETEFAIL\n│   └── DISPLAYFAIL, SERVERFAIL\n├── INTEGRITYFAIL\n│   ├── COMMITLIMIT, LOCKFAIL, VALIDATEFAIL\n└── RULEFAIL\n    ├── ZERODIVIDE, OVERFLOW, CONVERSION\n    └── NULLVALUE, STRINGSIZE, SECURITYFAIL\n```\n\n## Workflow Checklists\n\nCopy these checklists to track progress on complex tasks.\n\n### Code Analysis Workflow\n\n```\n## Objectstar Analysis Progress\n\n### 1. Structure Identification\n- [ ] Locate rule declaration and arguments\n- [ ] Identify LOCAL variables\n- [ ] Map condition quadrant columns\n- [ ] List action sequence numbers\n\n### 2. Data Flow Analysis\n- [ ] Trace LOCAL variable scope chain (which descendant rules use them?)\n- [ ] Document table access patterns (GET/REPLACE/INSERT/DELETE)\n- [ ] Identify parameterized table usage (e.g., `TABLE(REGION)`)\n\n### 3. Control Flow Analysis\n- [ ] Map condition quadrant to equivalent branching logic\n- [ ] Document FORALL iteration patterns and termination conditions\n- [ ] Note TRANSFERCALL usage (breaks return flow)\n- [ ] List all CALL/EXECUTE dependencies\n\n### 4. Exception Analysis\n- [ ] List all exception handlers (ON statements)\n- [ ] Check handler specificity (table-specific before generic)\n- [ ] Identify SIGNAL statements and custom exceptions\n- [ ] Verify catch-all ON ERROR has proper handling\n\n### 5. Documentation\n- [ ] Summarize rule purpose\n- [ ] Document non-obvious business logic\n- [ ] Note migration concerns\n```\n\n### Migration Workflow\n\n```\n## Objectstar Migration Progress\n\n### Phase 1: Inventory\n- [ ] Extract complete MetaStor (tables, rules, screens)\n- [ ] Classify rules: OTP screen logic vs batch vs shared utility\n- [ ] Document all parameterized tables\n- [ ] Map CALL/EXECUTE/TRANSFERCALL dependencies\n\n### Phase 2: Schema Migration\n- [ ] Map TDS tables to relational schema\n- [ ] Convert parameterized tables to composite keys\n- [ ] Define foreign key relationships\n- [ ] Create JPA entities\n\n### Phase 3: Logic Migration (per rule)\n- [ ] Convert condition quadrants to decision logic\n- [ ] Map LOCAL variables to typed Java fields\n- [ ] Handle scope chain with context objects\n- [ ] Convert FORALL to repository queries + streams\n\n### Phase 4: Exception Handling\n- [ ] Map Objectstar exceptions to Java exceptions\n- [ ] Convert ON handlers to try-catch blocks\n- [ ] Implement transaction boundaries (@Transactional)\n\n### Phase 5: UI Migration (if OTP)\n- [ ] Convert screens to web forms (MVC)\n- [ ] Map screen tables to DTOs\n- [ ] Implement validation rules\n\n### Phase 6: Validation\n- [ ] Create test cases from existing behavior\n- [ ] Run → Compare outputs → Fix discrepancies → Repeat\n- [ ] Verify transaction semantics preserved\n```\n\n### Refactoring Feedback Loop\n\nFor iterative improvement, use this pattern:\n\n```\n1. Identify anti-pattern (see patterns.md)\n2. Apply refactoring\n3. Verify rule still compiles/runs\n4. Test affected functionality\n5. If issues found → revert and retry with different approach\n6. Document changes made\n```\n\n## Refactoring Guidelines\n\n1. **Simplify condition quadrants** — Consolidate redundant Y/N columns\n2. **Extract common patterns** — Repeated FORALL/GET sequences → separate rules\n3. **Standardize exception handling** — Table-specific before generic\n4. **Document scope dependencies** — LOCAL variables used across rule calls\n5. **Add Browse hints** — Use Browse Mode for read-only operations\n\nFor anti-patterns to avoid during refactoring, see [pitfalls.md](references/pitfalls.md).\n\n## Migration Priorities\n\nFor Java migration, address these semantic gaps (see [migration.md](references/migration.md) for details):\n\n1. **Untyped LOCAL variables** → Type inference or wrapper classes\n2. **Descendant scope visibility** → Custom scope chain management\n3. **Parameterized tables** → Composite keys + filtered queries\n4. **Condition quadrants** → Decision tables or switch expressions\n5. **TRANSFERCALL** → Explicit control flow refactoring\n\n## Reference Files\n\n- [syntax.md](references/syntax.md) — Complete syntax reference with all data types\n- [patterns.md](references/patterns.md) — Common code patterns with examples\n- [pitfalls.md](references/pitfalls.md) — Anti-patterns and common mistakes to avoid\n- [migration.md](references/migration.md) — Java migration mappings and strategies\n- [tools.md](references/tools.md) — Built-in shareable tools reference\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:10:26.254Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Legacy System Agents needing expertise in rules-based 4GL mainframe platforms like Objectstar","zh":"非常适合需要在基于规则的4GL主机平台（如Objectstar）上拥有专业知识的遗留系统代理","ja":"ルールベースの4GLメインフレームプラットフォーム（例：Objectstar）で専門知識を必要とするレガシーシステムエージェントに最適","ko":"규칙 기반 4GL 메인프레임 플랫폼(예: Objectstar)에서 전문 지식을 필요로 하는 레거시 시스템 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Sistemas Legados que necesitan experiencia en plataformas de mainframe basadas en reglas de 4GL como Objectstar","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de systèmes hérités ayant besoin d''expertise sur les plates-formes de mainframe à base de règles 4GL comme Objectstar","de":"Perfekt für Legacy-System-Agents, die Expertenwissen auf Regeln basierenden 4GL-Mainframe-Plattformen wie Objectstar benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Sistemas Legados que necessitam de especialização em plataformas de mainframe baseadas em regras de 4GL, como o Objectstar","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов старых систем, которым необходимы знания в области платформ основанных на правилах 4GL мейнфреймов, таких как Objectstar","ar":"مثالي لعميل نظام التراث الذي يحتاج إلى خبرة في منصات مين فريم 4GL القائمة على القواعد مثل Objectstar"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to parse condition quadrants, analyze data flow using LOCAL variables, and understand rule structures in the four-section format, leveraging tables instead of objects and rules instead of programs","zh":"赋予代理分析条件象限、使用LOCAL变量分析数据流并了解四部分格式中的规则结构的能力，利用表格代替对象，规则代替程序","ja":"エージェントが条件象限を解析し、LOCAL変数を使用してデータフローを分析し、4部構成形式のルール構造を理解する能力を与え、テーブルを使用してオブジェクトを置き換え、ルールを使用してプログラムを置き換える","ko":"에이전트가 조건 사분면을 분석하고 로컬 변수를 사용하여 데이터 흐름을 분석하고 4부분 구성 형식의 규칙 구조를 이해할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 표를 사용하여 객체를 대체하고 규칙을 사용하여 프로그램을 대체","es":"Habilita a los agentes para analizar cuadrantes de condiciones, analizar el flujo de datos utilizando variables LOCAL, y comprender estructuras de reglas en el formato de cuatro secciones, utilizando tablas en lugar de objetos y reglas en lugar de programas","fr":"Permet aux agents d''analyser les quadrants de conditions, d''analyser le flux de données à l''aide de variables LOCAL, et de comprendre les structures de règles dans le format à quatre sections, en utilisant des tableaux au lieu d''objets et des règles au lieu de programmes","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Bedingungsquadranten zu analysieren, den Datenfluss unter Verwendung von LOCAL-Variablen zu analysieren und Regelframeworks im Vierabschnittsformat zu verstehen, indem Tabellen anstelle von Objekten und Regeln anstelle von Programmen eingesetzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a analisar quadrantes de condição, analisar o fluxo de dados usando variáveis LOCAL, e entender estruturas de regras no formato de quatro seções, utilizando tabelas em vez de objetos e regras em vez de programas","ru":"Позволяет агентам анализировать квадранты условий, анализировать поток данных с использованием локальных переменных и понимать структуры правил в четырехсекционном формате, используя таблицы вместо объектов и правила вместо программ","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من تحليل رباعيات الشروط، و تحليل تدفق البيانات باستخدام المتغيرات المحلية، وفهم هياكل القواعد في تنسيق الأقسام الأربعة، باستخدام الجداول بدلاً من الكائنات والقواعد بدلاً من البرامج"},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing Objectstar code for migration purposes","Debugging rule structures in Objectstar applications","Optimizing data flow in legacy mainframe systems"],"zh":["出于迁移目的分析Objectstar代码","调试Objectstar应用程序中的规则结构","优化遗留主机系统中的数据流"],"ja":["移行のためにObjectstarコードを分析する","Objectstarアプリケーションのルール構造をデバッグする","レガシーメインフレームシステムのデータフローを最適化する"],"ko":["이동을 위해 Objectstar 코드를 분석","Objectstar 애플리케이션의 규칙 구조를 디버깅","레거시 메인프레임 시스템의 데이터 흐름을 최적화"],"es":["Análisis de código Objectstar para fines de migración","Depuración de estructuras de reglas en aplicaciones Objectstar","Optimización del flujo de datos en sistemas de mainframe legados"],"fr":["Analyse du code Objectstar à des fins de migration","Débogage des structures de règles dans les applications Objectstar","Optimisation du flux de données dans les systèmes de mainframe hérités"],"de":["Analyse von Objectstar-Code für Migrationszwecke","Fehlerbehebung von Regelframeworks in Objectstar-Anwendungen","Optimierung des Datenflusses in Legacy-Mainframe-Systemen"],"pt":["Analisar código Objectstar para fins de migração","Depurar estruturas de regras em aplicações Objectstar","Otimizar fluxo de dados em sistemas de mainframe legados"],"ru":["Анализ кода Objectstar для целей миграции","Отладка структур правил в приложениях Objectstar","Оптимизация потока данных в устаревших системах мейнфрейма"],"ar":["تحليل رمز Objectstar لأغراض الهجرة","تصحيح أخطاء هياكل القواعد في تطبيقات Objectstar","تحسين تدفق البيانات في أنظمة المينفريم التقليدية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Extended support ends March 30, 2027","Requires knowledge of condition quadrants and FORALL loops","Objectstar platform specific"],"zh":["延长支持于2027年3月30日结束","需要条件象限和FORALL循环的知识","特定于Objectstar平台"],"ja":["延長サポートは2027年3月30日に終了","条件象限とFORALLループの知識が必要","Objectstarプラットフォーム専用"],"ko":["연장 지원은 2027년 3월 30일에 종료","조건 사분면과 FORALL 루프에 대한 지식이 필요","Objectstar 플랫폼 전용"],"es":["El soporte extendido finaliza el 30 de marzo de 2027","Requiere conocimiento de cuadrantes de condiciones y bucles FORALL","Específico de la plataforma Objectstar"],"fr":["Le support étendu se termine le 30 mars 2027","Nécessite une connaissance des quadrants de conditions et des boucles FORALL","Spécifique à la plate-forme Objectstar"],"de":["Das erweiterte Support endet am 30. März 2027","Benötigt Kenntnisse von Bedingungsquadranten und FORALL-Schleifen","Spezifisch für die Objectstar-Plattform"],"pt":["Suporte estendido termina em 30 de março de 2027","Requer conhecimento de quadrantes de condição e loops FORALL","Específico da plataforma Objectstar"],"ru":["Расширенная поддержка заканчивается 30 марта 2027 года","Требуется знание квадрантов условий и циклов FORALL","Специфичен для платформы Objectstar"],"ar":["ينتهي الدعم الممتد في 30 مارس 2027","يتطلب معرفة رباعيات الشروط وأشكال FORALL","محدد لمنصة Objectstar"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
