 domaine de Cynefin","Analyse de situations complexes","Choix de la réponse appropriée","Application de l''approche de réponse","Reconnaissance de la complexité des problèmes"],"de":["Identifizierung des Cynefin-Bereichs","Analyse komplexer Situationen","Wahl der geeigneten Reaktion","Anwendung des Reaktionsansatzes","Anerkennung der Komplexität von Problemen"],"pt":["Identificação do domínio do problema","Aplicação da abordagem de resposta apropriada","Análise de situações complexas","Escolha de respostas adequadas","Flexibilidade para reconhecer partes de problemas em múltiplos domínios"],"ru":["Определение домена проблемы","Применение подходящего подхода к ответу","Анализ сложных ситуаций","Выбор подходящих ответов","Гибкость для признания частей проблем в нескольких доменах"],"ar":["تحديد مجال المشكلة","تطبيق نهج الاستجابة المناسب","تحليل المواقف المعقدة","اختيار الاستجابات المناسبة","المرونة لتسليم أجزاء المشكلات في مجالات متعددة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Cynefin 框架","问题分析","应对策略","复杂性评估","不确定性评估","决策支持","软件开发","项目管理"],"ja":["Cynefin フレームワーク","問題分析","対応戦略","複雑性評価","不確実性評価","意思決定支援","ソフトウェア開発","プロジェクト管理"],"ko":["Cynefin 프레임워크","문제 분석","대응 전략","복잡성 평가","불확실성 평가","의사결정 지원","소프트웨어 개발","프로젝트 관리"],"es":["análisis Cynefin","marco de decisión","problemas complejos","dominio de Cynefin","respuesta adecuada","desarrollo de software","análisis de situaciones"],"fr":["analyse Cynefin","cadre de décision","problèmes complexes","domaine de Cynefin","réponse appropriée","développement de logiciels","analyse de situations"],"de":["Cynefin-Analyse","Entscheidungsrahmen","komplexe Probleme","Cynefin-Bereich","geeignete Reaktion","Software-Entwicklung","Situationsanalyse"],"pt":["análise Cynefin","problemas complexos","respostas adequadas","domínio do problema","abordagem de resposta","análise de situações","desenvolvimento de software","metodologias ágeis"],"ru":["анализ Cynefin","сложные проблемы","подходящие ответы","домен проблемы","подход к ответу","анализ ситуаций","разработка программного обеспечения","гибкие методологии"],"ar":["تحليل Cynefin","مشكلات معقدة","استجابات مناسبة","مجال المشكلة","نهج الاستجابة","تحليل المواقف","تطوير البرمجيات","منهجيات مرنة"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.455Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"cynefin","description":"Cynefin sense-making framework categorizing problems as Simple, Complicated, Complex, Chaotic, or Confused to select the right approach. Use when unsure how to tackle a problem.","bodyPreview":"# Cynefin Analysis\n\nAnalyze a situation through the Cynefin framework to understand what type of problem it is and choose the appropriate response.\n\n## Instructions\n\nDetermine which Cynefin domain the problem belongs to, then apply the appropriate response approach. Be willing to recognize that parts of a problem may span multiple domains.\n\n### Output Format\n\n**Situation**: [What we''re analyzing]\n\n---\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Characteristics Check**\n\n| Characteristic | Yes/No/Maybe | Evidence |","body":"# Cynefin Analysis\n\nAnalyze a situation through the Cynefin framework to understand what type of problem it is and choose the appropriate response.\n\n## Instructions\n\nDetermine which Cynefin domain the problem belongs to, then apply the appropriate response approach. Be willing to recognize that parts of a problem may span multiple domains.\n\n### Output Format\n\n**Situation**: [What we''re analyzing]\n\n---\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Characteristics Check**\n\n| Characteristic | Yes/No/Maybe | Evidence |\n|---------------|--------------|----------|\n| Cause and effect are clear and predictable | | |\n| Experts can analyze and determine the answer | | |\n| Outcomes can only be understood in hindsight | | |\n| The situation is unstable/in crisis | | |\n| We genuinely don''t know what kind of problem this is | | |\n\n---\n\n## Domain Classification\n\n**Primary Domain**: [Simple/Complicated/Complex/Chaotic/Confused]\n\n**Why this domain?**\n[Reasoning for the classification]\n\n---\n\n## Domain-Appropriate Response\n\n### If SIMPLE/OBVIOUS\n*Sense → Categorize → Respond*\n\n**Best Practice to Apply**: [The established approach]\n\n### If COMPLICATED\n*Sense → Analyze → Respond*\n\n**Experts Needed**: [Who has the expertise?]\n**Analysis Required**: [What to investigate?]\n\n### If COMPLEX\n*Probe → Sense → Respond*\n\n**Safe-to-Fail Experiments**:\n| Probe | What We''d Learn | Amplify if... | Dampen if... |\n|-------|-----------------|---------------|---------------|\n| [experiment] | [insight] | [success indicators] | [failure indicators] |\n\n**Key Mindset**: Don''t try to predict. Try things, observe, adapt.\n\n### If CHAOTIC\n*Act → Sense → Respond*\n\n**Immediate Stabilization**: [What action do we take right now?]\n\n### If CONFUSED\n*Break down, then categorize*\n\n| Sub-problem | Likely Domain | Why |\n|-------------|---------------|-----|\n| [sub-problem] | [domain] | [reasoning] |\n\n---\n\n## Boundary Warnings\n\n| Transition | Warning Signs | What to Do |\n|------------|--------------|------------|\n| Simple → Chaotic | Complacency | Challenge assumptions |\n| Complicated → Complex | Analysis not converging | Try probes instead |\n| Complex → Chaotic | Loss of control | Stabilize fast |\n\n---\n\n## Recommended Approach\n\n**Given this is a [DOMAIN] problem, we should:**\n1. [Primary approach]\n2. [Supporting action]\n\n## Guidelines\n\n- Most people default to Complicated (analysis) when Complex (probes) is needed\n- \"Best practice\" is only valid in Simple domain\n- In Complex, you can''t predict—you can only experiment and adapt\n- In Chaotic, act first, think later\n\n$ARGUMENTS\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:14:34.356Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Complex Problem-Solving Agents needing advanced decision-making frameworks like Cynefin.","zh":"非常适合需要像Cynefin这样的高级决策框架的复杂问题解决代理","ja":"Cynefinのような高度な意思決定フレームワークを必要とする複雑な問題解決エージェントに最適","ko":"Cynefin과 같은 고급 의사결정 프레임워크가 필요한 복잡한 문제 해결 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de resolución de problemas complejos que necesitan marcos de toma de decisiones avanzados como Cynefin.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de résolution de problèmes complexes nécessitant des cadres de prise de décision avancés comme Cynefin.","de":"Perfekt für komplexe Problemlösungsagenten, die erweiterte Entscheidungsfindungsframeworks wie Cynefin benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Resolução de Problemas Complexos que necessitam de estruturas de tomada de decisão avançadas como o Cynefin.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов, решающих сложные проблемы, которым необходимы продвинутые рамки принятия решений, такие как Cynefin.","ar":"مثالي للعاملين الذكيين لحل المشكلات المعقدة الذين يحتاجون إلى إطارات اتخاذ قرار متقدمة مثل Cynefin."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to categorize problems into Cynefin domains, applying appropriate response approaches through situational analysis and characteristic checks, utilizing frameworks like the Cynefin matrix.","zh":"赋予代理将问题分类到Cynefin域，并通过情况分析和特征检查应用适当的响应方法，利用像Cynefin矩阵这样的框架","ja":"エージェントが状況分析と特性チェックを通じてCynefinドメインに問題を分類し、適切な対応アプローチを適用することを可能にし、Cynefinマトリックスなどのフレームワークを利用する","ko":"에이전트가 상황 분석과 특성 점검을 통해 문제를 Cynefin 도메인으로 분류하고 적절한 응답 접근 방식을 적용할 수 있도록 하며, Cynefin 매트릭스와 같은 프레임워크를 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a categorizar problemas en dominios de Cynefin, aplicando enfoques de respuesta adecuados a través del análisis situacional y las comprobaciones de características, utilizando frameworks como la matriz de Cynefin.","fr":"Permet aux agents de catégoriser les problèmes en domaines Cynefin, en appliquant des approches de réponse appropriées à travers l''analyse situationnelle et les vérifications de caractéristiques, en utilisant des frameworks comme la matrice Cynefin.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Probleme in Cynefin-Domänen zu kategorisieren und geeignete Reaktionsansätze durch situative Analyse und Charakteristikprüfungen anzuwenden, indem Frameworks wie die Cynefin-Matrix verwendet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a categorizar problemas em domínios Cynefin, aplicando abordagens de resposta apropriadas por meio de análise situacional e verificações de características, utilizando estruturas como a matriz Cynefin.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью категоризировать проблемы в домены Cynefin, применяя подходящие подходы к ответу через ситуационный анализ и проверки характеристик, используя рамки, такие как матрица Cynefin.","ar":"يسمح للعاملين بتصنيف المشكلات إلى مجالات Cynefin، وتطبيق نهج إجابة مناسبة من خلال التحليل المواقفي والفحوصات المميزة، باستخدام الإطارات مثل مصفوفة Cynefin."},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing complex situations through the Cynefin framework","Determining problem domains for informed decision-making","Applying context-dependent responses to dynamic situations"],"zh":["通过Cynefin框架分析复杂情况","确定问题域以进行明智的决策","将上下文依赖的响应应用于动态情况"],"ja":["Cynefinフレームワークを使用した複雑な状況の分析","情報に基づいた意思決定のための問題ドメインの決定","動的状況へのコンテキスト依存のレスポンスの適用"],"ko":["Cynefin 프레임워크를 사용한 복잡한 상황 분석","알려진 의사결정을 위한 문제 도메인의 결정","동적 상황에 대한 문맥 종속 응답의 적용"],"es":["Análisis de situaciones complejas a través del marco de Cynefin","Determinación de dominios de problemas para una toma de decisiones informada","Aplicación de respuestas dependientes del contexto a situaciones dinámicas"],"fr":["Analyse de situations complexes à travers le cadre Cynefin","Détermination des domaines de problèmes pour une prise de décision éclairée","Application de réponses dépendantes du contexte à des situations dynamiques"],"de":["Analyse komplexer Situationen durch den Cynefin-Rahmen","Bestimmung von Problemdomänen für eine informierte Entscheidungsfindung","Anwendung von kontextabhängigen Reaktionen auf dynamische Situationen"],"pt":["Analisar situações complexas por meio da estrutura Cynefin","Determinar domínios de problemas para tomada de decisão informada","Aplicar respostas dependentes de contexto a situações dinâmicas"],"ru":["Анализ сложных ситуаций с помощью рамки Cynefin","Определение доменов проблем для информированного принятия решений","Применение контекстно-зависимых ответов к динамическим ситуациям"],"ar":["تحليل الحالات المعقدة من خلال إطار Cynefin","تحديد مجالات المشكلات لاتخاذ القرارات المستنيرة","تطبيق استجابات تعتمد على السياق للحالات الديناميكية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Cynefin framework and its domains","May need iterative analysis for accurate domain determination"],"zh":["需要了解Cynefin框架及其域","可能需要迭代分析以确定准确的域"],"ja":["Cynefinフレームワークとそのドメインの理解が必要","正確なドメインの決定には反復分析が必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["Cynefin 프레임워크와 그 도메인에 대한 이해가 필요","정확한 도메인 결정에는 반복 분석이 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión del marco de Cynefin y sus dominios","Puede necesitar un análisis iterativo para una determinación precisa del dominio"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension du cadre Cynefin et de ses domaines","Peut nécessiter une analyse itérative pour une détermination précise du domaine"],"de":["Erfordert das Verständnis des Cynefin-Rahmens und seiner Domänen","Kann ein iteratives Analyseverfahren für eine genaue Domänenbestimmung erfordern"],"pt":["Exige compreensão da estrutura Cynefin e seus domínios","Pode precisar de análise iterativa para determinação precisa do domínio"],"ru":["Требует понимания рамки Cynefin и ее доменов","Может потребовать итеративного анализа для точного определения домена"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم إطار Cynefin ومجالاته","يمكن أن يحتاج إلى تحليل تكراري لتحديد الدومين بدقة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/queries', 'community', 'majiayu000', 'claude-skill-registry', 'majiayu000/claude-skill-registry', 'queries', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.455Z', '2026-02-18T07:15:19.605Z', NULL, '{"id":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/queries","name":"queries","description":{"zh":"Drizzle Cube 查询技能帮助您构建和执行语义查询，用于检索分析数据。它结合了措施、维度、过滤器和时间维度来检索数据","ja":"Drizzle Cube クエリースキルは、分析データを取得するためのセマンティック クエリを構築して実行するのに役立ちます。 Measurements、Dimensions、Filters、Time Dimensions を組み合わせてデータを取得します","ko":"드릴즈 큐브 쿼리 스킬은 분석 데이터를检索하는 의미 쿼리를 구축 및 실행하는 데 도움이 됩니다. 측정, 차원, 필터 및 시간 차원을 결합하여 데이터를检索합니다","es":"Esta habilidad te permite construir y ejecutar consultas semánticas utilizando la API de Drizzle Cube, combinando medidas, dimensiones, filtros y dimensiones de tiempo.","fr":"Cette compétence vous permet de construire et d''exécuter des requêtes sémantiques en utilisant l''API Drizzle Cube, en combinant mesures, dimensions, filtres et dimensions de temps.","de":"Diese Fähigkeit ermöglicht es Ihnen, semantische Abfragen mit der Drizzle Cube-API zu erstellen und auszuführen, indem Sie Maße, Dimensionen, Filter und Zeitdimensionen kombinieren.","pt":"O skill de consultas do Drizzle Cube permite construir e executar consultas semânticas para obter dados analíticos. As consultas combinam medidas, dimensões, filtros e dimensões de tempo.","ru":"Навык запросов Drizzle Cube позволяет строить и выполнять семантические запросы для получения аналитических данных. Запросы объединяют меры, размерности, фильтры и временные размерности.","ar":"المهارة الاستعلامية ل Drizzle Cube تسمح ببناء وتنفيذ استعلامات семантиكية لاستخراج بيانات تحليلية. الاستعلامات تجمع بين المقاييس والأبعاد والمرشحات وأبعاد الوقت.","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Drizzle Cube 查询技能","ja":"Drizzle Cube クエリースキル","ko":"드릴즈 큐브 쿼리 스킬","es":"Consultas de Drizzle Cube: construye y ejecuta queries se...","fr":"Requêtes Drizzle Cube : construisez et exécutez des requê...","de":"Drizzle Cube Abfragen: erstellen und ausführen Sie semant...","pt":"Consultas de Dados com Drizzle Cube","ru":"Запросы данных с Drizzle Cube","ar":"استعلامات البيانات مع Drizzle Cube","en":"queries"},"description":{"zh":"Drizzle Cube 查询技能帮助您构建和执行语义查询，用于检索分析数据。它结合了措施、维度、过滤器和时间维度来检索数据","ja":"Drizzle Cube クエリースキルは、分析データを取得するためのセマンティック クエリを構築して実行するのに役立ちます。 Measurements、Dimensions、Filters、Time Dimensions を組み合わせてデータを取得します","ko":"드릴즈 큐브 쿼리 스킬은 분석 데이터를检索하는 의미 쿼리를 구축 및 실행하는 데 도움이 됩니다. 측정, 차원, 필터 및 시간 차원을 결합하여 데이터를检索합니다","es":"Esta habilidad te permite construir y ejecutar consultas semánticas utilizando la API de Drizzle Cube, combinando medidas, dimensiones, filtros y dimensiones...","fr":"Cette compétence vous permet de construire et d''exécuter des requêtes sémantiques en utilisant l''API Drizzle Cube, en combinant mesures, dimensions, filtres ...","de":"Diese Fähigkeit ermöglicht es Ihnen, semantische Abfragen mit der Drizzle Cube-API zu erstellen und auszuführen, indem Sie Maße, Dimensionen, Filter und Zeit...","pt":"O skill de consultas do Drizzle Cube permite construir e executar consultas semânticas para obter dados analíticos. As consultas combinam medidas, dimensões,...","ru":"Навык запросов Drizzle Cube позволяет строить и выполнять семантические запросы для получения аналитических данных. Запросы объединяют меры, размерности, фил...","ar":"المهارة الاستعلامية ل Drizzle Cube تسمح ببناء وتنفيذ استعلامات семантиكية لاستخراج بيانات تحليلية. الاستعلامات تجمع بين المقاييس والأبعاد والمرشحات وأبعاد ال...","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["构建和执行语义查询","结合措施、维度、过滤器和时间维度","检索分析数据","使用 Drizzle Cube 查询 API","支持时间维度和过滤"],"ja":["セマンティック クエリの構築と実行","Measurements、Dimensions、Filters、Time Dimensions の組み合わせ","アナリティクス データの取得","Drizzle Cube クエリ API の使用","Time Dimensions とフィルタリングのサポート"],"ko":["의미 쿼리의 구축 및 실행","측정, 차원, 필터 및 시간 차원의 결합","분석 데이터의检索","드릴즈 큐브 쿼리 API의 사용","시간 차원 및 필터링의 지원"],"es":["Construye consultas semánticas con la API de Drizzle Cube","Combina medidas, dimensiones, filtros y dimensiones de tiempo","Recupera datos analíticos con precisión","Especifica condiciones de filtro y agrupación","Ordena los resultados según tus necesidades"],"fr":["Construisez des requêtes sémantiques avec l''API Drizzle Cube","Combinez mesures, dimensions, filtres et dimensions de temps","Récupérez des données analytiques avec précision","Spécifiez des conditions de filtre et de regroupement","Triez les résultats selon vos besoins"],"de":["Erstellen Sie semantische Abfragen mit der Drizzle Cube-API","Kombinieren Sie Maße, Dimensionen, Filter und Zeitdimensionen","Rufen Sie Analyse-Daten mit Genauigkeit ab","Spezifizieren Sie Filter- und Gruppierungsbedingungen","Ordnen Sie die Ergebnisse nach Ihren Bedürfnissen"],"pt":["Construção de consultas semânticas","Combinação de medidas, dimensões, filtros e dimensões de tempo","Recuperação de dados analíticos","Uso da API de consulta do Drizzle Cube","Agrupamento e filtragem de dados"],"ru":["Строительство семантических запросов","Объединение мер, размерностей, фильтров и временных размерностей","Получение аналитических данных","Использование API запросов Drizzle Cube","Группировка и фильтрация данных"],"ar":["بناء استعلامات семантиكية","جمع المقاييس والأبعاد والمرشحات وأبعاد الوقت","استخراج بيانات تحليلية","استخدام واجهة برمجة تطبيقات استعلام Drizzle Cube","تجميع وفرز البيانات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Drizzle Cube 查询","语义查询","分析数据","查询 API","时间维度","过滤器","措施","维度"],"ja":["Drizzle Cube クエリ","セマンティック クエリ","アナリティクス データ","クエリ API","Time Dimensions","フィルタリング","Measurements","Dimensions"],"ko":["드릴즈 큐브 쿼리","의미 쿼리","분석 데이터","쿼리 API","시간 차원","필터링","측정","차원"],"es":["consultas semánticas","Drizzle Cube","API de Drizzle Cube","medidas","dimensiones","filtros","dimensiones de tiempo","datos analíticos"],"fr":["requêtes sémantiques","Drizzle Cube","API Drizzle Cube","mesures","dimensions","filtres","dimensions de temps","données analytiques"],"de":["semantische Abfragen","Drizzle Cube","Drizzle Cube-API","Maße","Dimensionen","Filter","Zeitdimensionen","Analyse-Daten"],"pt":["consultas semânticas","drizzle cube","api de consulta","dados analíticos","medidas","dimensões","filtros","dimensões de tempo"],"ru":["семантические запросы","drizzle cube","api запросов","аналитические данные","меры","размерности","фильтры","временные размерности"],"ar":["استعلامات семантиكية","drizzle cube","واجهة برمجة تطبيقات استعلام","بيانات تحليلية","مقاييس","أبعاد","مرشحات","أبعاد زمنية"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.455Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"queries","description":"Build and execute semantic queries with filters, time dimensions, aggregations, and ordering in drizzle-cube. Use when querying analytics data, filtering results, working with date ranges, aggregating measures, or building reports with drizzle-cube.","bodyPreview":"# Drizzle Cube Queries\n\nThis skill helps you build and execute semantic queries using Drizzle Cube''s query API. Queries combine measures, dimensions, filters, and time dimensions to retrieve analytics data.\n\n## Core Concept\n\nA **query** in Drizzle Cube specifies:\n- **Measures** - What to aggregate (counts, sums, averages, etc.)\n- **Dimensions** - How to group/categorize the results\n- **TimeDimensions** - Time-based filtering and grouping\n- **Filters** - Conditions to filter the data\n- **Order**","body":"# Drizzle Cube Queries\n\nThis skill helps you build and execute semantic queries using Drizzle Cube''s query API. Queries combine measures, dimensions, filters, and time dimensions to retrieve analytics data.\n\n## Core Concept\n\nA **query** in Drizzle Cube specifies:\n- **Measures** - What to aggregate (counts, sums, averages, etc.)\n- **Dimensions** - How to group/categorize the results\n- **TimeDimensions** - Time-based filtering and grouping\n- **Filters** - Conditions to filter the data\n- **Order** - Sorting of results\n- **Limit/Offset** - Pagination\n\n## Basic Query Structure\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''CubeName.measureName''],\n  dimensions: [''CubeName.dimensionName''],\n  timeDimensions: [{\n    dimension: ''CubeName.timeDimension'',\n    granularity: ''day'',\n    dateRange: [''2024-01-01'', ''2024-12-31'']\n  }],\n  filters: [{\n    member: ''CubeName.field'',\n    operator: ''equals'',\n    values: [''value'']\n  }],\n  order: { ''CubeName.field'': ''asc'' },\n  limit: 100,\n  offset: 0\n}\n\n// Execute the query\nconst result = await semanticLayer.execute(query, securityContext)\n```\n\n## Measures\n\nMeasures are aggregated values calculated across your data.\n\n### Single Measure\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count'']\n}\n\n// Result: Total employee count\n```\n\n### Multiple Measures\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [\n    ''Employees.count'',\n    ''Employees.avgSalary'',\n    ''Employees.totalSalary''\n  ]\n}\n\n// Result: Multiple aggregations in one query\n```\n\n### Cross-Cube Measures\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [\n    ''Employees.count'',\n    ''Departments.count'',\n    ''Projects.count''\n  ]\n}\n\n// Result: Aggregations from multiple cubes (automatic JOINs)\n```\n\n## Dimensions\n\nDimensions categorize and group your data.\n\n### Single Dimension\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  dimensions: [''Employees.department'']\n}\n\n// Result: Employee count grouped by department\n```\n\n### Multiple Dimensions\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  dimensions: [\n    ''Employees.department'',\n    ''Employees.isActive''\n  ]\n}\n\n// Result: Employee count grouped by department and active status\n```\n\n### Cross-Cube Dimensions\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  dimensions: [\n    ''Employees.name'',\n    ''Departments.name'' // Dimension from joined cube\n  ]\n}\n\n// Result: Uses automatic JOIN to include department name\n```\n\n## Time Dimensions\n\nTime dimensions enable temporal filtering and grouping.\n\n### Basic Time Dimension\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  timeDimensions: [{\n    dimension: ''Employees.createdAt'',\n    granularity: ''day'' // Group by day\n  }]\n}\n```\n\n### Time Granularities\n\n```typescript\n// Supported granularities:\nconst granularities = [\n  ''second'',\n  ''minute'',\n  ''hour'',\n  ''day'',\n  ''week'',\n  ''month'',\n  ''quarter'',\n  ''year''\n]\n\n// Example: Monthly grouping\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  timeDimensions: [{\n    dimension: ''Employees.createdAt'',\n    granularity: ''month''\n  }]\n}\n```\n\n### Date Range Filtering with Time Grouping\n\nTime dimensions with `dateRange` filter AND group data by time. The dimension appears in the output grouped by the specified granularity.\n\n```typescript\n// Absolute date range (array format)\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  timeDimensions: [{\n    dimension: ''Employees.createdAt'',\n    granularity: ''week'',\n    dateRange: [''2024-01-01'', ''2024-12-31'']\n  }]\n}\n// Result: Weekly employee counts from Jan 1 to Dec 31, 2024\n\n// Single date (becomes full day range)\nconst query2 = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  timeDimensions: [{\n    dimension: ''Employees.createdAt'',\n    granularity: ''hour'',\n    dateRange: ''2024-01-15''\n  }]\n}\n// Result: Hourly counts for January 15, 2024\n\n// Relative date range\nconst query3 = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  timeDimensions: [{\n    dimension: ''Employees.createdAt'',\n    granularity: ''day'',\n    dateRange: ''last 30 days''\n  }]\n}\n// Result: Daily counts for the last 30 days\n```\n\n**All Supported Date Range Patterns:**\n\n```typescript\n// Fixed relative ranges\nconst fixedRanges = [\n  ''today'',              // Current day\n  ''yesterday'',          // Previous day\n  ''this week'',          // Current week (Monday-Sunday)\n  ''this month'',         // Current month\n  ''this quarter'',       // Current quarter (Q1-Q4)\n  ''this year'',          // Current year\n  ''last week'',          // Previous week\n  ''last month'',         // Previous month\n  ''last quarter'',       // Previous quarter\n  ''last year'',          // Previous year\n  ''last 7 days'',        // Last 7 days from now\n  ''last 30 days'',       // Last 30 days from now\n  ''last 12 months''      // Last 12 months from now\n]\n\n// Flexible relative ranges (N can be any number)\nconst flexibleRanges = [\n  ''last N days'',        // e.g., ''last 45 days'', ''last 90 days''\n  ''last N weeks'',       // e.g., ''last 8 weeks'', ''last 12 weeks''\n  ''last N months'',      // e.g., ''last 3 months'', ''last 18 months''\n  ''last N quarters'',    // e.g., ''last 2 quarters'', ''last 4 quarters''\n  ''last N years''        // e.g., ''last 2 years'', ''last 5 years''\n]\n\n// Examples of flexible patterns\nconst examples = {\n  measures: [''Sales.revenue''],\n  timeDimensions: [{\n    dimension: ''Sales.date'',\n    granularity: ''week'',\n    dateRange: ''last 12 weeks''  // Last 12 weeks grouped by week\n  }]\n}\n\n// All patterns are case-insensitive\n''Last 30 Days'' === ''last 30 days'' === ''LAST 30 DAYS''\n```\n\n### Time Dimension with Granularity and Range\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  timeDimensions: [{\n    dimension: ''Employees.createdAt'',\n    granularity: ''week'',\n    dateRange: ''last 90 days''\n  }]\n}\n\n// Result: Weekly employee counts for the last 90 days\n```\n\n## Filters\n\nFilters restrict which data is included in the query.\n\n### Simple Filters\n\n#### Equals Filter\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  filters: [{\n    member: ''Employees.department'',\n    operator: ''equals'',\n    values: [''Engineering'']\n  }]\n}\n```\n\n#### Multiple Values (IN clause)\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  filters: [{\n    member: ''Employees.department'',\n    operator: ''equals'',\n    values: [''Engineering'', ''Sales'', ''Marketing'']\n  }]\n}\n```\n\n### String Operators\n\n```typescript\n// Contains\n{\n  member: ''Employees.name'',\n  operator: ''contains'',\n  values: [''John'']\n}\n\n// Not contains\n{\n  member: ''Employees.email'',\n  operator: ''notContains'',\n  values: [''@competitor.com'']\n}\n\n// Starts with\n{\n  member: ''Employees.name'',\n  operator: ''startsWith'',\n  values: [''Dr.'']\n}\n\n// Ends with\n{\n  member: ''Employees.email'',\n  operator: ''endsWith'',\n  values: [''@company.com'']\n}\n\n// Not equals\n{\n  member: ''Employees.status'',\n  operator: ''notEquals'',\n  values: [''terminated'']\n}\n```\n\n### Numeric Operators\n\n```typescript\n// Greater than\n{\n  member: ''Employees.salary'',\n  operator: ''gt'',\n  values: [100000]\n}\n\n// Greater than or equal\n{\n  member: ''Employees.salary'',\n  operator: ''gte'',\n  values: [50000]\n}\n\n// Less than\n{\n  member: ''Employees.yearsOfService'',\n  operator: ''lt'',\n  values: [5]\n}\n\n// Less than or equal\n{\n  member: ''Employees.age'',\n  operator: ''lte'',\n  values: [65]\n}\n\n// Between (range)\n{\n  member: ''Employees.salary'',\n  operator: ''between'',\n  values: [50000, 150000]\n}\n```\n\n### Null/Empty Operators\n\n```typescript\n// Is set (not null)\n{\n  member: ''Employees.departmentId'',\n  operator: ''set''\n}\n\n// Not set (is null)\n{\n  member: ''Employees.terminationDate'',\n  operator: ''notSet''\n}\n\n// Is empty (null or empty string)\n{\n  member: ''Employees.middleName'',\n  operator: ''isEmpty''\n}\n\n// Is not empty\n{\n  member: ''Employees.email'',\n  operator: ''isNotEmpty''\n}\n```\n\n### Date Operators\n\n```typescript\n// In date range\n{\n  member: ''Employees.createdAt'',\n  operator: ''inDateRange'',\n  values: [''2024-01-01'', ''2024-12-31'']\n}\n\n// Before date\n{\n  member: ''Employees.createdAt'',\n  operator: ''beforeDate'',\n  values: [''2024-06-01'']\n}\n\n// After date\n{\n  member: ''Employees.createdAt'',\n  operator: ''afterDate'',\n  values: [''2023-01-01'']\n}\n```\n\n### Date Range Filters (Filter Without Time Grouping)\n\n**NEW**: Use `dateRange` in filters to filter by date WITHOUT adding time dimensions to the output. This is perfect for KPI cards, summaries, and any query where you want to filter by time period but don''t need time-series data.\n\n**Key Differences from timeDimensions:**\n- **filters.dateRange**: Filters data only, NO time columns in output\n- **timeDimensions.dateRange**: Filters AND groups data, time columns appear in output\n\n#### Basic Filter with dateRange\n\n```typescript\n// Filter employees created in last 30 days\n// Time dimension does NOT appear in output\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count'', ''Employees.avgSalary''],\n  dimensions: [''Employees.department''],\n  filters: [{\n    member: ''Employees.createdAt'',\n    operator: ''inDateRange'',    // REQUIRED operator\n    dateRange: ''last 30 days''   // NEW property\n  }]\n}\n\n// Result: Department-level stats filtered to last 30 days\n// Output columns: department, count, avgSalary (NO createdAt column)\n```\n\n#### All dateRange Formats Work in Filters\n\n```typescript\n// Absolute date range (array)\n{\n  member: ''Orders.createdAt'',\n  operator: ''inDateRange'',\n  dateRange: [''2024-01-01'', ''2024-12-31'']\n}\n\n// Single date (full day)\n{\n  member: ''Orders.createdAt'',\n  operator: ''inDateRange'',\n  dateRange: ''2024-01-15''\n}\n\n// Fixed relative ranges\n{\n  member: ''Orders.createdAt'',\n  operator: ''inDateRange'',\n  dateRange: ''today''\n}\n\n{\n  member: ''Orders.createdAt'',\n  operator: ''inDateRange'',\n  dateRange: ''this month''\n}\n\n{\n  member: ''Orders.createdAt'',\n  operator: ''inDateRange'',\n  dateRange: ''last quarter''\n}\n\n// Flexible relative ranges\n{\n  member: ''Orders.createdAt'',\n  operator: ''inDateRange'',\n  dateRange: ''last 90 days''\n}\n\n{\n  member: ''Orders.createdAt'',\n  operator: ''inDateRange'',\n  dateRange: ''last 12 weeks''\n}\n\n{\n  member: ''Orders.createdAt'',\n  operator: ''inDateRange'',\n  dateRange: ''last 6 months''\n}\n```\n\n#### When to Use filters.dateRange vs timeDimensions.dateRange\n\n**Use filters.dateRange when:**\n- Building KPI cards (total sales this month)\n- Showing summary statistics for a time period\n- You need to filter by date but don''t want time columns in output\n- Creating comparison queries (this month vs last month using separate queries)\n- Dashboard widgets showing single metrics\n\n**Use timeDimensions.dateRange when:**\n- Creating time-series charts (line charts, area charts)\n- Showing trends over time (weekly signups, monthly revenue)\n- Need time dimension in output (day, week, month columns)\n- Comparing periods in a single query with time grouping\n\n#### Comparison Table\n\n| Feature | filters.dateRange | timeDimensions.dateRange |\n|---------|-------------------|--------------------------|\n| **Filters data** | ✅ Yes | ✅ Yes |\n| **Groups by time** | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |\n| **Time column in output** | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |\n| **Requires granularity** | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |\n| **Requires operator** | ✅ `inDateRange` | ❌ N/A |\n| **Best for** | KPIs, summaries | Charts, trends |\n\n#### Practical Examples\n\n```typescript\n// Example 1: KPI Card - Total sales this month (NO time grouping)\nconst thisMonthSales = {\n  measures: [''Orders.totalRevenue'', ''Orders.count''],\n  filters: [{\n    member: ''Orders.createdAt'',\n    operator: ''inDateRange'',\n    dateRange: ''this month''\n  }]\n}\n// Output: { totalRevenue: 150000, count: 342 }\n\n// Example 2: Time-series chart - Daily sales last 30 days (WITH time grouping)\nconst dailySalesChart = {\n  measures: [''Orders.totalRevenue''],\n  timeDimensions: [{\n    dimension: ''Orders.createdAt'',\n    granularity: ''day'',\n    dateRange: ''last 30 days''\n  }]\n}\n// Output: [\n//   { ''Orders.createdAt'': ''2024-01-01'', totalRevenue: 5000 },\n//   { ''Orders.createdAt'': ''2024-01-02'', totalRevenue: 5500 },\n//   ...\n// ]\n\n// Example 3: Department summary for Q1 (NO time grouping)\nconst q1Summary = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count'', ''Employees.avgSalary''],\n  dimensions: [''Employees.department''],\n  filters: [{\n    member: ''Employees.createdAt'',\n    operator: ''inDateRange'',\n    dateRange: ''this quarter''\n  }]\n}\n// Output: [\n//   { department: ''Engineering'', count: 50, avgSalary: 120000 },\n//   { department: ''Sales'', count: 30, avgSalary: 90000 }\n// ]\n\n// Example 4: Combining filters.dateRange with other filters\nconst activeEmployeesLast6Months = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  dimensions: [''Employees.department''],\n  filters: [{\n    and: [\n      {\n        member: ''Employees.createdAt'',\n        operator: ''inDateRange'',\n        dateRange: ''last 6 months''\n      },\n      {\n        member: ''Employees.isActive'',\n        operator: ''equals'',\n        values: [true]\n      },\n      {\n        member: ''Employees.salary'',\n        operator: ''gte'',\n        values: [50000]\n      }\n    ]\n  }]\n}\n```\n\n#### Important Notes\n\n1. **Operator is mandatory**: When using `dateRange` in filters, you MUST use `operator: ''inDateRange''`\n2. **Time dimensions only**: `dateRange` only works with time dimensions (type: ''time''), not regular dimensions\n3. **Precedence**: If both `dateRange` and `values` are provided, `dateRange` takes precedence\n4. **Validation**: Invalid date ranges will throw an error during query execution\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ WRONG: Missing operator\n{\n  member: ''Employees.createdAt'',\n  dateRange: ''last 30 days''\n  // ERROR: Missing operator: ''inDateRange''\n}\n\n// ❌ WRONG: Wrong operator\n{\n  member: ''Employees.createdAt'',\n  operator: ''equals'',\n  dateRange: ''last 30 days''\n  // ERROR: Must use ''inDateRange'' operator with dateRange\n}\n\n// ❌ WRONG: Non-time dimension\n{\n  member: ''Employees.name'',  // String dimension, not time\n  operator: ''inDateRange'',\n  dateRange: ''last 30 days''\n  // ERROR: Can only use dateRange with time dimensions\n}\n\n// ✅ CORRECT\n{\n  member: ''Employees.createdAt'',\n  operator: ''inDateRange'',\n  dateRange: ''last 30 days''\n}\n```\n\n### Compound Filters (AND)\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  filters: [\n    {\n      and: [\n        {\n          member: ''Employees.department'',\n          operator: ''equals'',\n          values: [''Engineering'']\n        },\n        {\n          member: ''Employees.isActive'',\n          operator: ''equals'',\n          values: [true]\n        },\n        {\n          member: ''Employees.salary'',\n          operator: ''gte'',\n          values: [100000]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n// Result: Active engineers making >= $100k\n```\n\n### Compound Filters (OR)\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  filters: [\n    {\n      or: [\n        {\n          member: ''Employees.department'',\n          operator: ''equals'',\n          values: [''Engineering'']\n        },\n        {\n          member: ''Employees.department'',\n          operator: ''equals'',\n          values: [''Data Science'']\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n// Result: Employees in either Engineering or Data Science\n```\n\n### Nested Compound Filters\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  filters: [\n    {\n      and: [\n        {\n          member: ''Employees.isActive'',\n          operator: ''equals'',\n          values: [true]\n        },\n        {\n          or: [\n            {\n              member: ''Employees.salary'',\n              operator: ''gte'',\n              values: [100000]\n            },\n            {\n              member: ''Employees.yearsOfService'',\n              operator: ''gte'',\n              values: [10]\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n// Result: Active employees who either earn >= $100k OR have >= 10 years service\n```\n\n## Ordering\n\nSort query results by dimensions or measures.\n\n### Order by Dimension\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  dimensions: [''Employees.department''],\n  order: {\n    ''Employees.department'': ''asc''\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Order by Measure\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count'', ''Employees.avgSalary''],\n  dimensions: [''Employees.department''],\n  order: {\n    ''Employees.count'': ''desc'' // Sort by employee count descending\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Multiple Order Fields\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  dimensions: [''Employees.department'', ''Employees.isActive''],\n  order: {\n    ''Employees.department'': ''asc'',\n    ''Employees.count'': ''desc''\n  }\n}\n\n// Result: Sorted by department (A-Z), then by count (high to low)\n```\n\n## Pagination\n\nLimit results and implement pagination.\n\n### Limit Results\n\n```typescript\nconst query = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  dimensions: [''Employees.name''],\n  order: { ''Employees.count'': ''desc'' },\n  limit: 10 // Top 10 only\n}\n```\n\n### Pagination with Offset\n\n```typescript\n// Page 1 (first 20 results)\nconst page1 = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  dimensions: [''Employees.name''],\n  order: { ''Employees.name'': ''asc'' },\n  limit: 20,\n  offset: 0\n}\n\n// Page 2 (results 21-40)\nconst page2 = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  dimensions: [''Employees.name''],\n  order: { ''Employees.name'': ''asc'' },\n  limit: 20,\n  offset: 20\n}\n\n// Page 3 (results 41-60)\nconst page3 = {\n  measures: [''Employees.count''],\n  dimensions: [''Employees.name''],\n  order: { ''Employees.name'': ''asc'' },\n  limit: 20,\n  offset: 40\n}\n```\n\n## Complete Query Examples\n\n### Example 1: Sales Report\n\n```typescript\nconst salesReport = {\n  measures: [\n    ''Orders.count'',\n    ''Orders.totalRevenue'',\n    ''Orders.avgOrderValue''\n  ],\n  dimensions: [\n    ''Orders.productCategory'',\n    ''Customers.region''\n  ],\n  timeDimensions: [{\n    dimension: ''Orders.createdAt'',\n    granularity: ''month'',\n    dateRange: ''this year''\n  }],\n  filters: [{\n    and: [\n      {\n        member: ''Orders.status'',\n        operator: ''equals'',\n        values: [''completed'']\n      },\n      {\n        member: ''Orders.totalAmount'',\n        operator: ''gte'',\n        values: [100]\n      }\n    ]\n  }],\n  order: {\n    ''Orders.totalRevenue'': ''desc''\n  },\n  limit: 100\n}\n\nconst result = await semanticLayer.execute(salesReport, securityContext)\n```\n\n### Example 2: Employee Analytics\n\n```typescript\nconst employeeAnalytics = {\n  measures: [\n    ''Employees.count'',\n    ''Employees.avgSalary'',\n    ''Employees.totalSalary''\n  ],\n  dimensions: [\n    ''Departments.name'',\n    ''Employees.seniorityLevel''\n  ],\n  filters: [{\n    and: [\n      {\n        member: ''Employees.isActive'',\n        operator: ''equals'',\n        values: [true]\n      },\n      {\n        member: ''Employees.createdAt'',\n        operator: ''afterDate'',\n        values: [''2020-01-01'']\n      }\n    ]\n  }],\n  order: {\n    ''Departments.name'': ''asc'',\n    ''Employees.avgSalary'': ''desc''\n  }\n}\n\nconst result = await semanticLayer.execute(employeeAnalytics, securityContext)\n```\n\n### Example 3: Growth Metrics\n\n```typescript\nconst growthMetrics = {\n  measures: [\n    ''Users.count'',\n    ''Users.newSignups'',\n    ''Users.activeUsers''\n  ],\n  timeDimensions: [{\n    dimension: ''Users.createdAt'',\n    granularity: ''week'',\n    dateRange: ''last 90 days''\n  }],\n  filters: [{\n    member: ''Users.isVerified'',\n    operator: ''equals'',\n    values: [true]\n  }],\n  order: {\n    ''Users.createdAt'': ''asc''\n  }\n}\n\nconst result = await semanticLayer.execute(growthMetrics, securityContext)\n```\n\n### Example 4: Top Performers\n\n```typescript\nconst topPerformers = {\n  measures: [\n    ''Employees.count'',\n    ''Productivity.avgLinesOfCode'',\n    ''Productivity.totalDeployments''\n  ],\n  dimensions: [\n    ''Employees.name'',\n    ''Departments.name''\n  ],\n  timeDimensions: [{\n    dimension: ''Productivity.date'',\n    dateRange: ''last 30 days''\n  }],\n  filters: [{\n    and: [\n      {\n        member: ''Employees.isActive'',\n        operator: ''equals'',\n        values: [true]\n      },\n      {\n        member: ''Productivity.totalDeployments'',\n        operator: ''gt'',\n        values: [0]\n      }\n    ]\n  }],\n  order: {\n    ''Productivity.totalDeployments'': ''desc''\n  },\n  limit: 10\n}\n\nconst result = await semanticLayer.execute(topPerformers, securityContext)\n```\n\n## Query Execution\n\n### Basic Execution\n\n```typescript\nimport { SemanticLayerCompiler } from ''drizzle-cube''\n\nconst semanticLayer = new SemanticLayerCompiler({ drizzle: db, schema })\nsemanticLayer.registerCube(employeesCube)\n\nconst result = await semanticLayer.execute(query, {\n  organisationId: ''org-123'',\n  userId: ''user-456''\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.data) // Array of result rows\nconsole.log(result.annotation) // Metadata about measures/dimensions\n```\n\n### Result Structure\n\n```typescript\ninterface QueryResult {\n  data: Array<Record<string, any>> // Result rows\n  annotation: {\n    measures: Record<string, MeasureAnnotation>\n    dimensions: Record<string, DimensionAnnotation>\n    timeDimensions: Record<string, TimeDimensionAnnotation>\n  }\n  requestId: string\n  slowQuery: boolean\n  query: any // Transformed query\n}\n\n// Example result\nconst result = {\n  data: [\n    {\n      ''Employees.department'': ''Engineering'',\n      ''Employees.count'': 50,\n      ''Employees.avgSalary'': 125000\n    },\n    {\n      ''Employees.department'': ''Sales'',\n      ''Employees.count'': 30,\n      ''Employees.avgSalary'': 95000\n    }\n  ],\n  annotation: {\n    measures: {\n      ''Employees.count'': { title: ''Employee Count'', type: ''count'' },\n      ''Employees.avgSalary'': { title: ''Average Salary'', type: ''avg'' }\n    },\n    dimensions: {\n      ''Employees.department'': { title: ''Department'', type: ''string'' }\n    }\n  },\n  requestId: ''req-abc123'',\n  slowQuery: false\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Specify only needed fields** - Don''t request all measures/dimensions unnecessarily\n2. **Use filters early** - Apply filters to reduce data processed\n3. **Limit large result sets** - Use `limit` and `offset` for pagination\n4. **Order strategically** - Order by measures for \"top N\" queries\n5. **Combine filters efficiently** - Use AND/OR appropriately to minimize data scanned\n6. **Use time dimensions wisely** - Leverage granularity for time-series analysis\n7. **Test security context** - Always validate multi-tenant isolation\n8. **Choose the right dateRange approach**:\n   - Use `filters.dateRange` for KPIs and summaries (no time grouping needed)\n   - Use `timeDimensions.dateRange` for charts and trends (time grouping needed)\n   - Leverage flexible patterns like `''last 90 days''` instead of hardcoded dates\n9. **Prefer relative date ranges** - Use `''last 30 days''` instead of absolute dates for dynamic reports\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- **Missing security context** - Every query requires a security context\n- **Wrong operator** - Use `equals` not `=`, `gte` not `>=`\n- **Invalid date format** - Use ISO format: `2024-01-01`\n- **Mixing AND/OR incorrectly** - Nested compound filters need careful structure\n- **Performance issues** - Large queries without limits can be slow\n- **Missing `inDateRange` operator** - When using `dateRange` in filters, you MUST specify `operator: ''inDateRange''`\n- **Using dateRange on non-time dimensions** - `dateRange` only works with time dimensions (type: ''time'')\n- **Confusing filters.dateRange vs timeDimensions.dateRange**:\n  - Wrong: Using `timeDimensions.dateRange` for a KPI card (adds unnecessary time column to output)\n  - Wrong: Using `filters.dateRange` for a time-series chart (no time grouping, can''t create chart)\n- **Invalid relative date patterns** - Use exact patterns like `''last 30 days''` not `''past 30 days''` or `''previous 30 days''`\n\n## All Available Filter Operators\n\n```typescript\n// String operators\n''equals'', ''notEquals'', ''contains'', ''notContains'', ''startsWith'', ''endsWith''\n\n// Numeric operators\n''gt'', ''gte'', ''lt'', ''lte'', ''between''\n\n// Array operators\n''in'', ''notIn''\n\n// Null operators\n''set'', ''notSet'', ''isEmpty'', ''isNotEmpty''\n\n// Date operators\n''inDateRange'', ''beforeDate'', ''afterDate''\n\n// Pattern operators\n''like'', ''ilike'', ''regex''\n```\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- Create **charts** from your queries with the chart skills\n- Build **dashboards** with the `dashboard` skill\n- Learn about **cube definitions** with the `cube-definition` skill\n- Set up **server APIs** with the `server-setup` skill\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:15:19.605Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Data Analysis Agents needing advanced semantic query capabilities with Drizzle Cube''s query API.","zh":"非常适合需要使用Drizzle Cube查询API进行高级语义查询能力的数据分析代理。","ja":"Drizzle CubeのクエリAPIを使用した高度なセマンティククエリ機能を必要とするデータ分析エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Drizzle Cube의 쿼리 API를 사용하여 고급 의미 쿼리 기능을 필요로 하는 데이터 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de Análisis de Datos que necesitan capacidades de consulta semántica avanzadas con la API de consulta de Drizzle Cube.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de données nécessitant des capacités de requête sémantique avancées avec l''API de requête Drizzle Cube.","de":"Perfekt für Data-Analytics-Agents, die erweiterte semantische Abfragefunktionen mit der Drizzle-Cube-Abfrage-API benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Dados que necessitam de capacidades de consulta semântica avançadas com a API de consulta do Drizzle Cube.","ru":"Идеально для агентов анализа данных, которым необходимы расширенные возможности семантического запроса с помощью API запросов Drizzle Cube.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات تحليل البيانات التي تحتاج إلى قدرات استعلام семантиك متقدمه مع واجهة برمجة تطبيقات استعلامات كيوب دريزل."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build and execute complex queries using measures, dimensions, filters, and time dimensions, providing robust analytics data retrieval through Drizzle Cube''s API, leveraging concepts like aggregation and filtering.","zh":"赋予代理构建和执行复杂查询的能力，使用度量、维度、过滤器和时间维度，通过Drizzle Cube的API提供强大的分析数据检索，利用聚合和过滤等概念。","ja":"エージェントに、尺度、次元、フィルタ、時間次元を使用して複雑なクエリを構築して実行する能力を付与し、Drizzle CubeのAPIを通じて、集約やフィルタリングなどの概念を利用して、強力な分析データの取得を提供します。","ko":"에이전트에 측정, 차원, 필터, 시간 차원을 사용하여 복잡한 쿼리를 구축하고 실행하는 능력을 부여하여 Drizzle Cube의 API를 통해 집계 및 필터링과 같은 개념을 활용하여 강력한 분석 데이터를 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a construir y ejecutar consultas complejas utilizando medidas, dimensiones, filtros y dimensiones de tiempo, proporcionando una recuperación robusta de datos analíticos a través de la API de Drizzle Cube, aprovechando conceptos como la agregación y el filtrado.","fr":"Permet aux agents de construire et d''exécuter des requêtes complexes en utilisant des mesures, des dimensions, des filtres et des dimensions de temps, fournissant une récupération robuste de données analytiques via l''API Drizzle Cube, en exploitant des concepts tels que l''agrégation et le filtrage.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, komplexe Abfragen zu erstellen und auszuführen, indem sie Maße, Dimensionen, Filter und Zeitdimensionen verwenden, und bietet so eine robuste Analyse-Datenabruf durch die Drizzle-Cube-API, indem Konzepte wie Aggregation und Filterung genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir e executar consultas complexas usando medidas, dimensões, filtros e dimensões de tempo, fornecendo uma recuperação robusta de dados analíticos por meio da API do Drizzle Cube, aproveitando conceitos como agregação e filtragem.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать и выполнять сложные запросы, используя меры, размерности, фильтры и размерности времени, обеспечивая надежную выборку аналитических данных через API Drizzle Cube, используя такие концепции, как агрегация и фильтрация.","ar":"تمكّن العوامل من بناء وتشغيل استعلامات معقدة باستخدام المقاييس والأبعاد والمرشحات وأبعاد الوقت، وتوفير استرجاع بيانات تحليلية قوي من خلال واجهة برمجة تطبيقات كيوب دريزل، واستخدام مفاهيم مثل التجميع والترشيح."},"useCases":{"en":["Building custom analytics dashboards with aggregated measures","Filtering data based on specific conditions and time dimensions","Grouping results by dimensions for in-depth analysis"],"zh":["构建使用聚合度量的自定义分析仪表盘","根据特定条件和时间维度筛选数据","根据维度对结果进行分组以进行深入分析"],"ja":["集約尺度を使用したカスタム分析ダッシュボードの構築","特定の条件と時間次元に基づいてデータをフィルタリング","次元によって結果をグループ化して詳細分析を実施"],"ko":["집계 측정을 사용한 사용자 정의 분석 대시보드 구축","특정 조건 및 시간 차원에 따라 데이터 필터링","차원에 따라 결과를 그룹화하여 심층 분석 수행"],"es":["Construir paneles de análisis personalizados con medidas agregadas","Filtrar datos en función de condiciones y dimensiones de tiempo específicas","Agrupar resultados por dimensiones para un análisis en profundidad"],"fr":["Créer des tableaux de bord d''analyse personnalisés avec des mesures agrégées","Filtrer les données en fonction de conditions et de dimensions de temps spécifiques","Regrouper les résultats par dimensions pour une analyse approfondie"],"de":["Erstellen von benutzerdefinierten Analyse-Dashboards mit aggregierten Maßen","Filtern von Daten basierend auf spezifischen Bedingungen und Zeitdimensionen","Gruppieren von Ergebnissen nach Dimensionen für eine tiefere Analyse"],"pt":["Construir painéis de análise personalizados com medidas agregadas","Filtrar dados com base em condições e dimensões de tempo específicas","Agrupar resultados por dimensões para análise aprofundada"],"ru":["Создание пользовательских панелей аналитики с агрегированными мерами","Фильтрация данных на основе конкретных условий и размерностей времени","Группировка результатов по размерностям для углубленного анализа"],"ar":["بناء لوحات تحليل مخصصة مع مقاييس مجمعة","ترشيح البيانات على основе شروط وأبعاد زمنية محددة","تجميع النتائج حسب الأبعاد للتحليل العميق"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to Drizzle Cube''s query API","Dependent on data structure and schema compatibility"],"zh":["需要访问Drizzle Cube的查询API","依赖于数据结构和模式的兼容性"],"ja":["Drizzle CubeのクエリAPIへのアクセスが必要","データ構造とスキーマの互換性に依存"],"ko":["Drizzle Cube의 쿼리 API에 대한 액세스가 필요","데이터 구조 및 스키마의 호환성에 종속"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la API de consulta de Drizzle Cube","Dependiente de la compatibilidad de la estructura y el esquema de datos"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à l''API de requête Drizzle Cube","Dépend de la compatibilité de la structure et du schéma de données"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Drizzle-Cube-Abfrage-API","Abhängig von der Kompatibilität der Datenstruktur und des Datenschemas"],"pt":["Exige acesso à API de consulta do Drizzle Cube","Dependente da compatibilidade da estrutura e do esquema de dados"],"ru":["Требует доступа к API запросов Drizzle Cube","Зависит от совместимости структуры и схемы данных"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى واجهة برمجة تطبيقات استعلامات كيوب دريزل","يعتمد على توافق هيكل وجدول البيانات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/use-tdd', 'community', 'majiayu000', 'claude-skill-registry', 'majiayu000/claude-skill-registry', 'use-tdd', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.455Z', '2026-02-18T07:16:01.902Z', NULL, '{"id":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/use-tdd","name":"use-tdd","description":{"zh":"TDD, ","ja":"TDD, ","ko":"TDD, ","es":"TDD es una metodología de desarrollo que implica escribir pruebas antes de escribir el código","fr":"Le TDD est une méthodologie de développement qui consiste à écrire des tests avant de rédiger le code","de":"TDD ist eine Entwicklungsmethode, bei der Sie zuerst Tests schreiben, bevor Sie den Code schreiben","pt":"O TDD é uma abordagem de desenvolvimento de software que prioriza a escrita de testes antes do código de produção","ru":"TDD - это подход к разработке программного обеспечения, который отдает приоритет написанию тестов перед кодом производства","ar":"TDD هو نهج في تطوير البرمجيات يؤكد على كتابة الاختبارات قبل كود الإنتاج","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"TDD ","ja":"TDD","ko":"TDD ","es":"TDD: Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas","fr":"TDD: Développement Dirigé par les Tests","de":"TDD: Testgetriebene Entwicklung","pt":"TDD: Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes","ru":"TDD: Разработка через тестирование","ar":"TDD: التطوير الموجه بواسطة الاختبار","en":"use-tdd"},"description":{"zh":"TDD, ","ja":"TDD, ","ko":"TDD, ","es":"TDD es una metodología de desarrollo que implica escribir pruebas antes de escribir el código","fr":"Le TDD est une méthodologie de développement qui consiste à écrire des tests avant de rédiger le code","de":"TDD ist eine Entwicklungsmethode, bei der Sie zuerst Tests schreiben, bevor Sie den Code schreiben","pt":"O TDD é uma abordagem de desenvolvimento de software que prioriza a escrita de testes antes do código de produção","ru":"TDD - это подход к разработке программного обеспечения, который отдает приоритет написанию тестов перед кодом производства","ar":"TDD هو نهج في تطوير البرمجيات يؤكد على كتابة الاختبارات قبل كود الإنتاج","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["TDD","Red-Green-Refactor","",""],"ja":["TDD","Red-Green-Refactor","",""],"ko":["TDD","Red-Green-Refactor","",""],"es":["Escribe pruebas antes de escribir el código","Verifica que las pruebas fallen antes de escribir el código","Escribe el código mínimo necesario para pasar la prueba","Refactoriza el código para mejorar su calidad","Repite el ciclo de pruebas y refactorización"],"fr":["Écrivez des tests avant de rédiger le code","Vérifiez que les tests échouent avant de rédiger le code","Écrivez le code minimal nécessaire pour passer le test","Réfactorisez le code pour améliorer sa qualité","Répétez le cycle de tests et de refactorisation"],"de":["Schreiben Sie Tests, bevor Sie den Code schreiben","Überprüfen Sie, ob die Tests fehlschlagen, bevor Sie den Code schreiben","Schreiben Sie den minimalen Code, der erforderlich ist, um den Test zu bestehen","Refaktorisieren Sie den Code, um seine Qualität zu verbessern","Wiederholen Sie den Test- und Refaktorisierungszyklus"],"pt":["Escrita de testes antes do código de produção","Ciclo de desenvolvimento Red-Green-Refactor","Garantia de qualidade do código","Desenvolvimento incremental","Melhoria da confiabilidade do código"],"ru":["Написание тестов перед кодом производства","Цикл разработки Red-Green-Refactor","Гарантия качества кода","Инкрементная разработка","Улучшение надежности кода"],"ar":["كتابة الاختبارات قبل كود الإنتاج","دورة التطوير Red-Green-Refactor","ضمان جودة الكود","التطوير المتزايد","تحسين موثوقية الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["TDD","Test-Driven Development","Red-Green-Refactor","","","TDD"],"ja":["TDD","Test-Driven Development","Red-Green-Refactor","","","TDD"],"ko":["TDD","Test-Driven Development","Red-Green-Refactor","","","TDD"],"es":["TDD","Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas","Pruebas automatizadas","Calidad del código","Desarrollo de software","Metodologías de desarrollo"],"fr":["TDD","Développement Dirigé par les Tests","Tests automatisés","Qualité du code","Développement de logiciels","Méthodologies de développement"],"de":["TDD","Testgetriebene Entwicklung","Automatisierte Tests","Code-Qualität","Softwareentwicklung","Entwicklungsmethoden"],"pt":["TDD","Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes","Testes unitários","Ciclo de desenvolvimento","Garantia de qualidade","Desenvolvimento de software","Melhoria da confiabilidade"],"ru":["TDD","Разработка через тестирование","Юнит-тесты","Цикл разработки","Гарантия качества","Разработка программного обеспечения","Улучшение надежности"],"ar":["TDD","التطوير الموجه بواسطة الاختبار","اختبارات الوحدة","دورة التطوير","ضمان الجودة","تطوير البرمجيات","تحسين الموثوقية"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.455Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"use-tdd","description":"Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code","bodyPreview":"Write the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch the test fail, you don''t know if it tests the right thing.\n\n# The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO PRODUCTION CODE WITHOUT A FAILING TEST FIRST\n```\n\nWrite code before the test? Delete it. Start over.\n\n**No exceptions:**\n- Don''t keep it as \"reference\"\n- Don''t \"adapt\" it while writing tests\n- Delete means delete\n\n# Red-Green-Refactor\n\n## RED - Write Failing Test\n\nWrite one minimal test showing what should hap","body":"Write the test first. Watch it fail. Write minimal code to pass.\n\n**Core principle:** If you didn''t watch the test fail, you don''t know if it tests the right thing.\n\n# The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO PRODUCTION CODE WITHOUT A FAILING TEST FIRST\n```\n\nWrite code before the test? Delete it. Start over.\n\n**No exceptions:**\n- Don''t keep it as \"reference\"\n- Don''t \"adapt\" it while writing tests\n- Delete means delete\n\n# Red-Green-Refactor\n\n## RED - Write Failing Test\n\nWrite one minimal test showing what should happen.\n\n**Requirements:**\n- One behavior\n- Clear name\n- Real code (no mocks unless unavoidable)\n\n## Verify RED - Watch It Fail\n\n**MANDATORY. Never skip.**\n\n```bash\nnpm test path/to/test.test.ts\n```\n\nConfirm:\n- Test fails (not errors)\n- Failure message is expected\n- Fails because feature missing (not typos)\n\n**Test passes?** You''re testing existing behavior. Fix test.\n\n## GREEN - Minimal Code\n\nWrite simplest code to pass the test.\n\nDon''t add features, refactor other code, or \"improve\" beyond the test.\n\n## Verify GREEN - Watch It Pass\n\n**MANDATORY.**\n\n```bash\nnpm test path/to/test.test.ts\n```\n\nConfirm:\n- Test passes\n- Other tests still pass\n- Output pristine (no errors, warnings)\n\n**Test fails?** Fix code, not test.\n\n## REFACTOR - Clean Up\n\nAfter green only:\n- Remove duplication\n- Improve names\n- Extract helpers\n\nKeep tests green. Don''t add behavior.\n\n# Why Order Matters\n\n**\"I''ll write tests after to verify it works\"**\n\nTests written after code pass immediately. Passing immediately proves nothing:\n- Might test wrong thing\n- Might test implementation, not behavior\n- Might miss edge cases you forgot\n\nTest-first forces you to see the test fail, proving it actually tests something.\n\n**\"I already manually tested all the edge cases\"**\n\nManual testing is ad-hoc:\n- No record of what you tested\n- Can''t re-run when code changes\n- Easy to forget cases under pressure\n\nAutomated tests are systematic and run the same way every time.\n\n**\"Deleting X hours of work is wasteful\"**\n\nSunk cost fallacy. Your choice now:\n- Delete and rewrite with TDD (X more hours, high confidence)\n- Keep it and add tests after (30 min, low confidence, likely bugs)\n\nThe \"waste\" is keeping code you can''t trust.\n\n**\"TDD is dogmatic, being pragmatic means adapting\"**\n\nTDD IS pragmatic:\n- Finds bugs before commit (faster than debugging after)\n- Prevents regressions (tests catch breaks immediately)\n- Documents behavior (tests show how to use code)\n- Enables refactoring (change freely, tests catch breaks)\n\n**\"Tests after achieve the same goals - it''s spirit not ritual\"**\n\nNo. Tests-after answer \"What does this do?\" Tests-first answer \"What should this do?\"\n\nTests-after are biased by your implementation. You test what you built, not what''s required.\n\nTests-first force edge case brainstorm before implementing.\n\n# Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Too simple to test\" | Simple code breaks. Test takes 30 seconds. |\n| \"I''ll test after\" | Tests passing immediately prove nothing. |\n| \"Tests after achieve same goals\" | Tests-after = \"what does this do?\" Tests-first = \"what should this do?\" |\n| \"Already manually tested\" | Ad-hoc ≠ systematic. No record, can''t re-run. |\n| \"Deleting X hours is wasteful\" | Sunk cost fallacy. Keeping unverified code is technical debt. |\n| \"Keep as reference\" | You''ll adapt it. That''s testing after. Delete means delete. |\n| \"Need to explore first\" | Fine. Throw away exploration, start with TDD. |\n| \"Test hard = design unclear\" | Listen to test. Hard to test = hard to use. |\n\n# Red Flags - STOP\n\n- Code before test\n- Test after implementation\n- Test passes immediately\n- Can''t explain why test failed\n- Tests added \"later\"\n- \"I already manually tested it\"\n- \"Tests after achieve the same purpose\"\n- \"Keep as reference\" or \"adapt existing code\"\n- \"Already spent X hours, deleting is wasteful\"\n\n**All of these mean: Delete code. Start over with TDD.**\n\n# Verification Checklist\n\nBefore marking work complete:\n\n- [ ] Every new function/method has a test\n- [ ] Watched each test fail before implementing\n- [ ] Each test failed for expected reason (feature missing, not typo)\n- [ ] Wrote minimal code to pass each test\n- [ ] All tests pass\n- [ ] Output pristine (no errors, warnings)\n- [ ] Tests use real code (mocks only if unavoidable)\n- [ ] Edge cases and errors covered\n\nCan''t check all boxes? You skipped TDD. Start over.\n\n# Final Rule\n\n```\nProduction code → test exists and failed first\nOtherwise → not TDD\n```\n\nNo exceptions without your human partner''s permission.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:16:01.902Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing rigorous testing and validation through Test-Driven Development (TDD)","zh":"非常适合需要通过测试驱动开发（TDD）进行严格测试和验证的开发代理","ja":"開発エージェントが厳格なテストと検証を必要とする場合に最適であり、テスト駆動開発（TDD）を通じて実現される","ko":"개발 에이전트가 테스트 주도 개발(TDD)을 통해 엄격한 테스트와 검증을 필요로 하는 경우에 적합함","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan pruebas y validación rigurosas a través del Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas (TDD)","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin de tests et de validation rigoureux via le Développement Piloté par les Tests (TDD)","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die strenge Tests und Validierung durch testgetriebene Entwicklung (TDD) benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de testes e validação rigorosos por meio do Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Testes (TDD)","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, требующих строгого тестирования и валидации с помощью Тест-ориентированного развития (TDD)","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى اختبار وتحقق صارم من خلال التطوير الموجه بالاختبار (TDD)"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write robust code by enforcing the Red-Green-Refactor cycle, ensuring production code is always backed by a failing test, utilizing principles like the Iron Law and minimizing code through iterative testing and refactoring","zh":"通过强制执行红绿重构周期，确保生产代码始终由失败的测试支持，利用铁律等原则，并通过迭代测试和重构来最小化代码，从而使代理能够编写强健的代码","ja":"Red-Green-Refactorサイクルを強制実行することで、常に失敗したテストによって裏付けられた生産コードを保証し、鉄の法則などの原則を利用し、イテレーティブなテストとリファクタリングによってコードを最小限に抑えることで、エージェントが堅牢なコードを書くことを可能にしている","ko":"에이전트가 강건한 코드를 작성할 수 있도록紅绿重构 주기를 강제하여, 항상 실패한 테스트에 의한 생산 코드를 뒷받침하고 철의 법칙 등의 원칙을 활용하며, 반복 테스트와 리팩토링을 통해 코드를 최소화하는 것을 권장함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a escribir código robusto al aplicar el ciclo Rojo-Verde-Refactor, asegurando que el código de producción esté respaldado por una prueba fallida, utilizando principios como la Ley de Hierro y minimizando el código a través de pruebas y refactorización iterativas","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire du code robuste en appliquant le cycle Rouge-Vert-Refactor, en garantissant que le code de production est toujours étayé par un test en échec, en utilisant des principes comme la Loi de Fer et en minimisant le code via des tests et une refactoring itératifs","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, robusten Code zu schreiben, indem sie den Rot-Grün-Refactor-Zyklus durchsetzen, sicherstellen, dass der Produktionscode immer von einem fehlgeschlagenen Test unterstützt wird, unter Verwendung von Prinzipien wie dem Eisernen Gesetz und minimieren den Code durch iterative Tests und Refactoring","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escrever código robusto, aplicando o ciclo Red-Green-Refactor, garantindo que o código de produção seja sempre respaldado por um teste com falha, utilizando princípios como a Lei de Ferro e minimizando o código por meio de testes e refatoração iterativos","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью писать прочный код, применяя цикл Red-Green-Refactor, гарантируя, что производственный код всегда поддерживается неудачным тестом, используя принципы, такие как Железный закон, и минимизируя код посредством итеративного тестирования и рефакторинга","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على كتابة код متين من خلال تطبيق دورة اختبار-إصلاح-إعادة هيكلة، وضمان أن يكون код الإنتاج دائمًا مدعومًا باختبار فاشل، واستخدام مبادئ مثل قانون الحديد وتقليل الكود من خلال الاختبار والتحسين الإ_teratif"},"useCases":{"en":["Writing minimal code to pass tests","Debugging existing codebases with TDD","Implementing the Red-Green-Refactor cycle for new feature development"],"zh":["编写最小代码以通过测试","使用TDD调试现有代码库","为新功能开发实施红绿重构周期"],"ja":["テストに合格するための最小限のコードの記述","TDDを使用して既存のコードベースをデバッグする","新機能開発のためのRed-Green-Refactorサイクルの実施"],"ko":["테스트를 통과하기 위한 최소한의 코드 작성","TDD를 사용하여 기존 코드베이스 디버깅","새로운 기능 개발을 위한 红绿重构 주기 구현"],"es":["Escribir código mínimo para pasar pruebas","Depurar código existente con TDD","Implementar el ciclo Rojo-Verde-Refactor para el desarrollo de nuevas características"],"fr":["Écrire un code minimal pour passer les tests","Déboguer les bases de code existantes avec le TDD","Mettre en œuvre le cycle Rouge-Vert-Refactor pour le développement de nouvelles fonctionnalités"],"de":["Minimale Code zum Bestehen von Tests schreiben","Bestehenden Code mit TDD debuggen","Den Rot-Grün-Refactor-Zyklus für die Entwicklung neuer Funktionen implementieren"],"pt":["Escrever código mínimo para passar nos testes","Depurar código existente com TDD","Implementar o ciclo Red-Green-Refactor para desenvolvimento de novas funcionalidades"],"ru":["Написание минимального кода для прохождения тестов","Отладка существующего кода с помощью TDD","Реализация цикла Red-Green-Refactor для разработки новых функций"],"ar":["كتابة код mínimo لاجتياز الاختبارات","تصحيح الأخطاء في رمز موجود باستخدام TDD","تنفيذ دورة اختبار-إصلاح-إعادة هيكلة لتطوير ميزات جديدة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to the Iron Law of no production code without a failing test first","Demands a strict Red-Green-Refactor development cycle"],"zh":["需要遵守铁律，即没有失败的测试就不允许有生产代码","要求严格的红绿重构开发周期"],"ja":["失敗したテストなしに生産コードを許可しない鉄の法則に従う必要がある","厳格なRed-Green-Refactor開発サイクルを要求する"],"ko":["실패한 테스트 없이 생산 코드를 허용하지 않는 철의 법칙을遵守해야 함","엄격한 红绿重构 개발 주기를 요구함"],"es":["Requiere adherirse a la Ley de Hierro de no tener código de producción sin una prueba fallida primero","Exige un ciclo de desarrollo estricto de Rojo-Verde-Refactor"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion à la Loi de Fer de pas de code de production sans un test en échec d''abord","Exige un cycle de développement strict Rouge-Vert-Refactor"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung des Eisernen Gesetzes, keine Produktionscode ohne einen fehlgeschlagenen Test zuerst","Fordert einen strengen Rot-Grün-Refactor-Entwicklungszyklus"],"pt":["Exige adesão à Lei de Ferro de não ter código de produção sem um teste com falha primeiro","Exige um ciclo de desenvolvimento rigoroso Red-Green-Refactor"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения Железного закона о том, что нет производственного кода без неудачного теста сначала","Требует строгого цикла разработки Red-Green-Refactor"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بقانون الحديد بحيث لا يكون هناك رمز إنتاج بدون اختبار فاشل أولا","يتطلب دورة تطوير صارمة اختبار-إصلاح-إعادة هيكلة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
