tica","Implementação de padrões de codificação","Suporte a aplicações Rails","Baseado no Guia de Estilo de Ruby da comunidade","Melhoria da qualidade do código"],"ru":["Статический анализ кода","Автоматическое форматирование кода","Реализация стандартов кодирования","Поддержка приложений Rails","Основан на руководстве по стилю Ruby сообщества","Улучшение качества кода"],"ar":["تحليل الشفرة الثابت","تنسيق الشفرة التلقائي","تنفيذ معايير التشفير","دعم تطبيقات ريلز","يستند إلى دليل أسلوب روبي المجتمعي","تحسين جودة الشفرة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["RuboCop","Ruby代码分析","代码格式化","Ruby风格指南","静态代码分析","代码优化","Rails应用程序"],"ja":["RuboCop","Rubyコード解析","コードフォーマット","Rubyスタイルガイド","静的コード解析","コード最適化","Railsアプリケーション"],"ko":["RuboCop","루비 코드 분석","코드 포맷팅","루비 스타일 가이드","정적 코드 분석","코드 최적화","Rails 애플리케이션"],"es":["RuboCop","análisis de código","formato de código","Guía de Estilos de Ruby","Rails","calidad del código","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["RuboCop","analyse de code","formatage de code","Guide de style Ruby","Rails","qualité du code","développement de logiciels","outils de développement"],"de":["RuboCop","Code-Analyse","Code-Formatierung","Ruby-Style-Guide","Rails","Code-Qualität","Software-Entwicklung","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["RuboCop","análise de código estático","formatação de código","Ruby","Guia de Estilo de Ruby","qualidade do código","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["RuboCop","статический анализ кода","форматирование кода","Ruby","руководство по стилю Ruby","качество кода","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["محول شفرة روبي","تحليل الشفرة الثابت","تنسيق الشفرة","روبي","دليل أسلوب روبي","جودة الشفرة","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.455Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"rubocop","description":">-","bodyPreview":"# RuboCop Code Analysis & Formatting\n\nRuboCop is Ruby''s premier static code analyzer (linter) and formatter, based on the community-driven Ruby Style Guide. This skill enables comprehensive code analysis, automatic formatting, and enforcement of coding standards across Ruby projects including Rails applications.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nClaude automatically uses this skill when users:\n\n- Ask to \"check\", \"lint\", \"analyze\", or \"review\" Ruby code\n- Request code formatting or style improvements\n-","body":"# RuboCop Code Analysis & Formatting\n\nRuboCop is Ruby''s premier static code analyzer (linter) and formatter, based on the community-driven Ruby Style Guide. This skill enables comprehensive code analysis, automatic formatting, and enforcement of coding standards across Ruby projects including Rails applications.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nClaude automatically uses this skill when users:\n\n- Ask to \"check\", \"lint\", \"analyze\", or \"review\" Ruby code\n- Request code formatting or style improvements\n- Want to enforce coding standards or style guidelines\n- Need to detect potential bugs or code smells\n- Ask about RuboCop configuration or setup\n- Request Rails, RSpec, or performance-specific analysis\n- Want to run autocorrections on Ruby code\n\n## Core Capabilities\n\n**Code Analysis & Linting**\n- Detects style violations, bugs, and code smells across all cop departments\n- Supports Rails, RSpec, Performance, and custom cop extensions\n- Provides detailed offense reports with line numbers and descriptions\n\n**Automatic Code Correction**\n- Safe autocorrection (`-a`) for guaranteed-safe fixes\n- Unsafe autocorrection (`-A`) for broader but riskier corrections\n- Layout-only fixes (`-x`) for formatting without logic changes\n\n**Configuration & Customization**\n- Flexible `.rubocop.yml` configuration\n- Per-project and per-directory configuration inheritance\n- Selective cop enabling/disabling and severity adjustment\n- Custom cop development support\n\n**Extension Integration**\n- **rubocop-rails**: Rails best practices and conventions\n- **rubocop-rspec**: RSpec-specific analysis\n- **rubocop-performance**: Performance optimization checks\n\n## Quick Analysis Workflow\n\n### Run Basic Analysis\n\n```bash\n# Analyze current directory\nrubocop\n\n# Analyze specific files/directories\nrubocop app spec lib/important_file.rb\n\n# Show only correctable offenses\nrubocop --display-only-correctable\n```\n\n### Apply Corrections\n\n```bash\n# Safe autocorrection only (recommended)\nrubocop -a\n\n# All corrections including unsafe\nrubocop -A\n\n# Layout/formatting corrections only\nrubocop -x\n\n# Autocorrect specific cops\nrubocop -a --only Style/StringLiterals,Layout/TrailingWhitespace\n```\n\n### Targeted Analysis\n\n```bash\n# Run only specific cops\nrubocop --only Style/StringLiterals,Naming/MethodName\n\n# Run all cops except specified\nrubocop --except Metrics/MethodLength\n\n# Run only lint cops\nrubocop --lint\n\n# Check only Rails-specific issues\nrubocop --only Rails\n```\n\n## Configuration Essentials\n\n### Basic .rubocop.yml Setup\n\n```yaml\n# Enable extensions\nplugins:\n  - rubocop-rails\n  - rubocop-rspec\n  - rubocop-performance\n\nAllCops:\n  TargetRubyVersion: 3.2\n  NewCops: enable  # Auto-enable new cops\n  Exclude:\n    - ''db/schema.rb''\n    - ''vendor/**/*''\n    - ''node_modules/**/*''\n\n# Adjust specific cops\nStyle/StringLiterals:\n  EnforcedStyle: double_quotes\n\nMetrics/MethodLength:\n  Max: 15\n  Exclude:\n    - ''spec/**/*''\n```\n\n### Common Configuration Patterns\n\n**Inherit from shared config:**\n```yaml\ninherit_from:\n  - .rubocop_todo.yml\n  - config/rubocop_defaults.yml\n```\n\n**Rails-specific settings:**\n```yaml\nRails:\n  Enabled: true\n\nRails/ApplicationRecord:\n  Enabled: true\n  Exclude:\n    - ''db/migrate/**''\n```\n\n**RSpec configuration:**\n```yaml\nRSpec/ExampleLength:\n  Max: 10\n\nRSpec/MultipleExpectations:\n  Max: 3\n```\n\n## Analysis Interpretation\n\n### Understanding Offense Output\n\n```\napp/models/user.rb:15:3: C: Style/StringLiterals: Prefer single-quoted strings...\n  name = \"John Doe\"\n         ^^^^^^^^^^\n```\n\n**Format breakdown:**\n- `app/models/user.rb:15:3` - File path, line number, column number\n- `C:` - Severity (C=Convention, W=Warning, E=Error, F=Fatal)\n- `Style/StringLiterals` - Cop department and name\n- Message explains the issue and often suggests fixes\n\n### Severity Levels\n\n- **Convention (C)**: Style/formatting issues\n- **Warning (W)**: Potential problems that should be reviewed\n- **Error (E)**: Definite problems that need fixing\n- **Fatal (F)**: Syntax errors preventing analysis\n\n## Common Workflows\n\n### Initial Project Setup\n\n```bash\n# Generate initial configuration\nrubocop --init\n\n# Generate .rubocop_todo.yml for existing violations\nrubocop --auto-gen-config\n\n# Use todo file to gradually fix issues\n# .rubocop.yml:\ninherit_from: .rubocop_todo.yml\n```\n\n### Pre-commit Integration\n\n```bash\n# Check staged files only\ngit diff --name-only --cached | grep ''\\.rb$'' | xargs rubocop\n\n# With autocorrection\ngit diff --name-only --cached | grep ''\\.rb$'' | xargs rubocop -a\n```\n\n### CI/CD Integration\n\n```bash\n# Exit with error code if offenses found\nrubocop --format progress --fail-level warning\n\n# Generate formatted reports\nrubocop --format json --out rubocop-report.json\nrubocop --format html --out rubocop-report.html\n```\n\n### Parallel Execution\n\n```bash\n# Use all available CPUs (enabled by default)\nrubocop --parallel\n\n# Limit CPU usage\nPARALLEL_PROCESSOR_COUNT=2 rubocop\n```\n\n## Extension-Specific Features\n\n### Rails Analysis\n\nDetects Rails-specific issues:\n- ActiveRecord best practices\n- Controller and routing conventions\n- Migration safety checks\n- SQL injection risks\n\n### RSpec Analysis\n\nEnforces RSpec best practices:\n- Example organization and naming\n- Let vs instance variable usage\n- Expectation patterns\n- Test file structure\n\n### Performance Analysis\n\nIdentifies performance optimizations:\n- Inefficient collection methods\n- String concatenation issues\n- Unnecessary array allocations\n- Regex compilation optimizations\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n**\"Unknown cop\" errors:**\n- Ensure required gems are installed (`rubocop-rails`, `rubocop-rspec`, etc.)\n- Add to `.rubocop.yml`: `plugins: [rubocop-rails]`\n\n**Autocorrection not working:**\n- Some cops don''t support autocorrection\n- Use `-A` for unsafe corrections\n- Check cop is enabled in configuration\n\n**Performance issues:**\n- Use `--parallel` for faster execution\n- Add `UseCache: true` under `AllCops` in config\n- Exclude large generated files\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n- [Configuration Guide](references/configuration_guide.md) - Comprehensive configuration reference\n- [Cop Reference](references/cop_reference.md) - All cop departments and their responsibilities\n- [Extensions Guide](references/extensions_guide.md) - Rails, RSpec, Performance extension details\n- [Autocorrect Guide](references/autocorrect_guide.md) - Safe vs unsafe corrections explained\n- [Custom Cops Guide](references/custom_cops_guide.md) - Creating custom cops for your project\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:16:26.049Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Ruby-focused Agents needing advanced code analysis and formatting capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级代码分析和格式化功能的Ruby专注代理。","ja":"Ruby に焦点を当てたエージェントが高度なコード分析とフォーマット機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 코드 분석 및 형식 지정 기능이 필요한 Ruby 중심 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes centrados en Ruby que necesitan capacidades de análisis y formato de código avanzadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents axés sur Ruby nécessitant des capacités d''analyse et de mise en forme de code avancées.","de":"Perfekt für Ruby-fokussierte Agenten, die erweiterte Codeanalysen- und Formatierungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes focados em Ruby que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de análise e formatação de código.","ru":"Идеально для агентов, ориентированных на Ruby, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности анализа и форматирования кода.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذين يركزون على Ruby و الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة لتحليل وتشكيل الشفرة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce Ruby Style Guide standards, automatically format code, and perform comprehensive static code analysis using RuboCop, enhancing overall code quality and readability with features like linting and style improvements.","zh":"赋予代理执行 Ruby 风格指南标准、自动格式化代码和使用 RuboCop 进行全面静态代码分析，从而通过 linting 和样式改进等功能提高代码质量和可读性。","ja":"エージェントに Ruby スタイル ガイドの標準を適用し、コードを自動でフォーマットし、RuboCop を使用して包括的な静的コード分析を実行する機能を提供し、linting やスタイルの改善などの機能でコードの品質と可読性を向上させます。","ko":"에이전트가 Ruby 스타일 가이드 표준을 적용하고 코드를 자동으로 형식화하며 RuboCop를 사용하여 포괄적인 정적 코드 분석을 수행하여 린팅 및 스타일 개선 등의 기능으로 코드 품질 및 가독성을 향상시킵니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar los estándares de la Guía de estilo de Ruby, a formato de código automático y a realizar un análisis de código estático integral utilizando RuboCop, mejorando la calidad y la legibilidad del código en general con características como la verificación de errores y mejoras de estilo.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer les normes du Guide de style Ruby, de formater automatiquement le code et de réaliser une analyse de code statique complète à l''aide de RuboCop, améliorant ainsi la qualité et la lisibilité globales du code avec des fonctionnalités telles que la vérification des erreurs et les améliorations de style.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Ruby-Style-Guide-Standards durchzusetzen, automatisch Code zu formatieren und eine umfassende statische Codeanalyse mithilfe von RuboCop durchzuführen, wodurch die Gesamtkodqualität und Lesbarkeit durch Funktionen wie Fehlerüberprüfung und Stilverbesserungen verbessert wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impor os padrões do Guia de Estilo Ruby, formatar automaticamente o código e realizar uma análise de código estática abrangente usando RuboCop, melhorando a qualidade geral e a legibilidade do código com recursos como linting e melhorias de estilo.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечивать соблюдение стандартов Руководства по стилю Ruby, автоматически форматировать код и выполнять всесторонний статический анализ кода с помощью RuboCop, улучшая общее качество и читаемость кода с помощью функций, таких как linting и улучшение стиля.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من فرض معايير دليل أسلوب روبي، وتشكيل الشفرة تلقائيًا، وإجراء تحليل شفرة静ي شامل باستخدام روبوكوب، مما يعزز جودة الشفرة وقراءتها بشكل عام مع ميزات مثل linting وتحسين الأسلوب."},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing Ruby code for style and security issues","Automating code formatting for Rails applications","Enforcing coding standards across large Ruby projects"],"zh":["分析 Ruby 代码的样式和安全问题","自动化 Rails 应用程序的代码格式化","跨大型 Ruby 项目执行编码标准"],"ja":["スタイルとセキュリティの問題のために Ruby コードを分析する","Rails アプリケーションのコードの自動フォーマット","大規模な Ruby プロジェクト全体でコーディング規約を適用する"],"ko":["스타일 및 보안 문제에 대한 Ruby 코드 분석","Rails 애플리케이션의 코드 자동 형식화","대형 Ruby 프로젝트 전반에 걸친 코딩 표준 적용"],"es":["Analizar el código Ruby en busca de problemas de estilo y seguridad","Automatizar el formato de código para aplicaciones Rails","Hacer cumplir los estándares de codificación en proyectos Ruby grandes"],"fr":["Analyser le code Ruby pour les problèmes de style et de sécurité","Automatiser le formatage de code pour les applications Rails","Faire respecter les normes de codage dans les grands projets Ruby"],"de":["Ruby-Code auf Stil- und Sicherheitsprobleme analysieren","Codeformatierung für Rails-Anwendungen automatisieren","Codierungsstandards in großen Ruby-Projekten durchsetzen"],"pt":["Analisar o código Ruby para problemas de estilo e segurança","Automatizar a formatação de código para aplicações Rails","Impor padrões de codificação em projetos Ruby grandes"],"ru":["Анализировать код Ruby на наличие проблем со стилем и безопасностью","Автоматизировать форматирование кода для приложений Rails","Обеспечивать соблюдение стандартов кодирования в крупных проектах Ruby"],"ar":["تحليل شفرة روبي للقضايا المتعلقة بالأسلوب والأمان","تutomatizar تشكيل الشفرة لتطبيقات ريلز","فرض معايير الترميز عبر مشاريع روبي كبيرة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Ruby environment","Limited to Ruby and Rails projects"],"zh":["需要 Ruby 环境","仅限 Ruby 和 Rails 项目"],"ja":["Ruby 環境が必要","Ruby と Rails のプロジェクトのみ"],"ko":["Ruby 환경이 필요함","Ruby 및 Rails 프로젝트에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere entorno de Ruby","Limitado a proyectos Ruby y Rails"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Ruby","Limité aux projets Ruby et Rails"],"de":["Benötigt Ruby-Umgebung","Begrenzt auf Ruby- und Rails-Projekte"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Ruby","Limitado a projetos Ruby e Rails"],"ru":["Требуется среда Ruby","Ограничен проектами Ruby и Rails"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة روبي","محدود بمشاريع روبي و ريلز"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/handoff', 'community', 'majiayu000', 'claude-skill-registry', 'majiayu000/claude-skill-registry', 'handoff', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.455Z', '2026-02-18T07:16:18.280Z', NULL, '{"id":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry/handoff","name":"handoff","description":{"zh":"会话交接技能允许开发者创建结构化文档，以实现 Claude 会话间的无缝续性","ja":"セッションハンドオフスキルは、開発者がクールドセッション間のシームレスな継続性を実現するための構造化ドキュメントを作成できるようにします","ko":"세션 핸드오버 스킬을 통해 개발자는 클라우드 세션 간의 무중단 연속성을 위한 구조화된 문서를 만들 수 있습니다","es":"El skill Handoff permite crear documentos estructurados para una continuidad sin fisuras en las sesiones de Claude. Esto permite mejorar la productividad y reducir la pérdida de tiempo.","fr":"Le skill Handoff permet de créer des documents structurés pour une continuité sans faille dans les sessions Claude. Cela permet d''améliorer la productivité et de réduire la perte de temps.","de":"Der Handoff-Skill ermöglicht die Erstellung strukturierter Dokumente für eine nahtlose Fortsetzung in Claude-Sitzungen. Dies ermöglicht eine Steigerung der Produktivität und eine Reduzierung der Zeitverluste.","pt":"O Handoff é um recurso que permite criar documentos estruturados para garantir a continuidade da sessão em Claude.","ru":"Handoff - это функция, которая позволяет создавать структурированные документы для обеспечения передачи сессии в Claude.","ar":"هاندوف هو ميزة تتيح إنشاء وثائق منظمّة لضمان استمرارية الجلسة في كلود.","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":" Claude 代码会话交接","ja":"ク로드コードセッションハンドオフ","ko":"클라우드 코드 세션 핸드오버","es":"Handoff: Continuidad de sesión en Claude","fr":"Handoff : Continuité de session dans Claude","de":"Handoff: Sitzungsübergabe in Claude","pt":"Handoff: Continuidade de Sessão em Claude","ru":"Handoff: Передача сессии в Claude","ar":"هاندوف: استمرارية الجلسة في كلود","en":"handoff"},"description":{"zh":"会话交接技能允许开发者创建结构化文档，以实现 Claude 会话间的无缝续性","ja":"セッションハンドオフスキルは、開発者がクールドセッション間のシームレスな継続性を実現するための構造化ドキュメントを作成できるようにします","ko":"세션 핸드오버 스킬을 통해 개발자는 클라우드 세션 간의 무중단 연속성을 위한 구조화된 문서를 만들 수 있습니다","es":"El skill Handoff permite crear documentos estructurados para una continuidad sin fisuras en las sesiones de Claude. Esto permite mejorar la productividad y r...","fr":"Le skill Handoff permet de créer des documents structurés pour une continuité sans faille dans les sessions Claude. Cela permet d''améliorer la productivité e...","de":"Der Handoff-Skill ermöglicht die Erstellung strukturierter Dokumente für eine nahtlose Fortsetzung in Claude-Sitzungen. Dies ermöglicht eine Steigerung der P...","pt":"O Handoff é um recurso que permite criar documentos estruturados para garantir a continuidade da sessão em Claude.","ru":"Handoff - это функция, которая позволяет создавать структурированные документы для обеспечения передачи сессии в Claude.","ar":"هاندوف هو ميزة تتيح إنشاء وثائق منظمّة لضمان استمرارية الجلسة في كلود.","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["创建结构化文档","实现会话间的无缝续性","支持多个会话阶段","快速评估会话状态","捕获未来会话的状态"],"ja":["構造化ドキュメントの作成","セッション間のシームレスな継続性","複数のセッションフェーズのサポート","セッション状態の迅速な評価","将来のセッションの状態のキャプチャ"],"ko":["구조화된 문서 생성","세션 간의 무중단 연속성","다중 세션 단계 지원","세션 상태의 빠른 평가","미래 세션의 상태 캡처"],"es":["Creación de documentos estructurados","Continuidad sin fisuras en las sesiones","Mejora de la productividad","Reducir la pérdida de tiempo","Captura de estado de sesión","Preparación para futuras sesiones"],"fr":["Création de documents structurés","Continuité sans faille dans les sessions","Amélioration de la productivité","Réduction de la perte de temps","Capture de l''état de session","Préparation pour les futures sessions"],"de":["Erstellung strukturierter Dokumente","Nahtlose Fortsetzung in Sitzungen","Steigerung der Produktivität","Reduzierung der Zeitverluste","Sitzungszustand erfassen","Vorbereitung auf zukünftige Sitzungen"],"pt":["Criação de documentos estruturados","Continuidade de sessão em Claude","Transferência de estado de sessão","Suporte a múltiplos projetos","Capacidade de capturar estado para futuras sessões"],"ru":["Создание структурированных документов","Передача сессии в Claude","Передача состояния сессии","Поддержка нескольких проектов","Возможность захватить состояние для будущих сессий"],"ar":["إنشاء وثائق منظمّة","استمرارية الجلسة في كلود","نقل حالة الجلسة","دعم المشاريع المتعددة","قابلية 捕获 حالة للمجالس المستقبلية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["会话交接","结构化文档","Claude 代码","会话间的无缝续性","开发者工具","代码管理"],"ja":["セッションハンドオフ","構造化ドキュメント","クールドコード","セッション間のシームレスな継続性","開発者ツール","コード管理"],"ko":["세션 핸드오버","구조화된 문서","클라우드 코드","세션 간의 무중단 연속성","개발자 도구","코드 관리"],"es":["Handoff","Sesiones de Claude","Continuidad sin fisuras","Productividad","Documentos estructurados","Captura de estado de sesión","Desarrollo de software","Tecnologías de sesión"],"fr":["Handoff","Sessions Claude","Continuité sans faille","Productivité","Documents structurés","Capture de l''état de session","Développement de logiciels","Technologies de session"],"de":["Handoff","Claude-Sitzungen","Nahtlose Fortsetzung","Produktivität","Strukturierte Dokumente","Sitzungszustand erfassen","Softwareentwicklung","Sitzungstechnologien"],"pt":["handoff","claude","continuidade de sessão","documentos estruturados","transferência de estado","desenvolvimento de software","gestão de projetos"],"ru":["handoff","claude","передача сессии","структурированные документы","передача состояния","разработка программного обеспечения","управление проектами"],"ar":["هاندوف","كلود","استمرارية الجلسة","وثائق منظمّة","نقل حالة","تطوير البرمجيات","إدارة المشاريع"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.455Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"handoff","description":"Create a structured session handoff document for continuity across sessions. Use when ending a work session, switching contexts, or before a break. Captures decisions, progress, code changes, and next steps so a future session can pick up where you left off without losing context.","bodyPreview":"# Session Handoff Skill\n\nCreate structured documents that enable seamless continuity across Claude sessions.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Ending a work session for the day\n- Before taking a break mid-task\n- Switching to a different project temporarily\n- When you want to capture state for a future session\n- Before a context reset you know is coming\n\n## Handoff Process\n\n### Step 1: Assess Session State\n\nQuickly assess:\n\n1. **What phase are we in?** (exploration, planning, implementation, debugging, review)","body":"# Session Handoff Skill\n\nCreate structured documents that enable seamless continuity across Claude sessions.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Ending a work session for the day\n- Before taking a break mid-task\n- Switching to a different project temporarily\n- When you want to capture state for a future session\n- Before a context reset you know is coming\n\n## Handoff Process\n\n### Step 1: Assess Session State\n\nQuickly assess:\n\n1. **What phase are we in?** (exploration, planning, implementation, debugging, review)\n2. **What''s the active task?** (what we''re trying to accomplish)\n3. **How far along are we?** (just started, mid-way, almost done)\n\n### Step 2: Ask What Matters\n\nAsk the user:\n\n> \"I''ll create a handoff document. Is there anything specific you want to make sure I capture? (Key decisions, code snippets, context about the problem, things you''ll forget, etc.)\"\n\n### Step 3: Generate Handoff Document\n\nCreate a structured document:\n\n```markdown\n# Session Handoff: [Brief Description]\n\n**Date:** [YYYY-MM-DD]\n**Project:** [project name/path]\n**Session Duration:** [approximate]\n\n## Current State\n\n**Task:** [What we''re working on]\n**Phase:** [exploration/planning/implementation/debugging/review]\n**Progress:** [where we are - percentage or milestone]\n\n## What We Did\n\n[2-3 sentence summary of the session''s work]\n\n## Decisions Made\n\n- **[Decision]** — [Rationale]\n- **[Decision]** — [Rationale]\n\n## Code Changes\n\n**Files modified:**\n\n- `path/to/file.ts` — [what and why]\n- `path/to/other.ts` — [what and why]\n\n**Key code context:**\n[Critical snippets or patterns to remember]\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- [ ] [Question needing resolution]\n- [ ] [Question needing resolution]\n\n## Blockers / Issues\n\n- [Issue] — [current status]\n\n## Context to Remember\n\n[Important background, constraints, user preferences, domain knowledge - things that would take time to re-establish]\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. [ ] [First thing to do next session]\n2. [ ] [Second thing]\n3. [ ] [Third thing]\n\n## Files to Review on Resume\n\n- `path/to/key/file.ts` — [why it matters]\n```\n\n### Step 4: Write the File\n\nWrite to: `.claude/handoffs/[YYYY-MM-DD]-[brief-description].md`\n\nConfirm location with user:\n\n> \"I''ll save this to `.claude/handoffs/[filename].md`. Want a different location?\"\n\n## What to Capture\n\n### Always Include\n\n1. **Decisions with reasoning** — The \"why\" is often more valuable than the \"what\"\n2. **Code changes** — File paths, what changed, the intent\n3. **Current progress** — Where in the task we stopped\n4. **Next steps** — Clear, actionable items to resume with\n5. **User context** — Constraints, preferences, domain knowledge they shared\n\n### Include When Relevant\n\n- **Errors encountered** — And how they were (or weren''t) resolved\n- **Dead ends** — Approaches tried that didn''t work (saves re-exploration)\n- **Key files** — Files to read to get back up to speed\n- **External dependencies** — APIs, services, tools involved\n\n### Skip\n\n- Verbose tool output (file listings, grep results)\n- Intermediate reasoning that reached conclusions\n- Repeated similar operations\n- Information that''s obvious from the code\n\n## Format Guidelines\n\n- **Bullet points** — Scannable over narrative\n- **File paths** — `src/foo.ts:42` not \"that function\"\n- **Checkboxes for actions** — `- [ ]` for next steps and open questions\n- **Specifics** — \"Added retry logic to fetchUser()\" not \"made improvements\"\n\n## Quality Check\n\nBefore saving, verify:\n\n1. **Could a fresh Claude pick up from this?** — Enough context to continue?\n2. **Are decisions traceable?** — Clear why things were decided?\n3. **Are next steps actionable?** — Know exactly what to do first?\n4. **Is code work clear?** — Know which files matter?\n\n## Using a Handoff Document\n\nWhen starting a new session, the user can:\n\n1. Share the handoff file at session start\n2. Say \"Resume from this handoff: [paste or path]\"\n3. Reference it with @ mention if supported\n\nThe handoff should let you hit the ground running without lengthy re-explanation.\n\n## Example Handoff\n\n```markdown\n# Session Handoff: Auth System Implementation\n\n**Date:** 2025-01-15\n**Project:** /Users/robert/projects/my-api\n**Session Duration:** ~2 hours\n\n## Current State\n\n**Task:** Implementing user authentication for the API\n**Phase:** Implementation\n**Progress:** ~60% - basic flow works, need refresh tokens\n\n## What We Did\n\nBuilt the core JWT authentication flow including token generation, validation middleware, and login/logout endpoints. Hit an issue with key rotation that we resolved by moving to config-based key paths.\n\n## Decisions Made\n\n- **JWT with RS256** — Stateless auth, works with distributed setup\n- **Redis for refresh tokens** — Need revocation capability\n- **15-min access token expiry** — Balance security/UX for mobile app\n\n## Code Changes\n\n**Files modified:**\n\n- `src/auth/jwt.ts` — Token generation and validation logic\n- `src/middleware/auth.ts` — Request authentication middleware\n- `src/routes/auth.ts` — Login/logout endpoints\n- `config/keys/` — RSA key pair storage\n\n**Key code context:**\nToken validation uses RS256. Keys loaded from `config/keys/` based on NODE_ENV.\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- [ ] Automatic vs opt-in refresh token rotation?\n- [ ] Rate limit for login attempts? (User mentioned 10k DAU)\n\n## Context to Remember\n\n- Client is a mobile app - tokens need offline capability\n- User has 10k daily active users - scale matters\n- Using PostgreSQL for user storage\n- User prefers explicit error messages over generic ones\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. [ ] Implement `/auth/refresh` endpoint\n2. [ ] Add rate limiting to `/auth/login`\n3. [ ] Write tests for token expiry edge cases\n4. [ ] Update API docs with auth flow\n\n## Files to Review on Resume\n\n- `src/auth/jwt.ts` — Core token logic\n- `src/routes/auth.ts` — Current endpoint implementation\n```\n\n## Key Reminders\n\n- Ask what matters to the user before generating\n- Decisions need reasoning — capture the \"why\"\n- File paths anchor the work — always include them\n- Next steps should be immediately actionable\n- Better slightly longer and useful than short and vague\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T07:16:18.280Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Claude Code Agents needing seamless session continuity and state capture.","zh":"非常适合需要无缝会话连续性和状态捕获的 Claude Code Agents。","ja":"セッションの連続性と状態のキャプチャが必要な Claude Code エージェントに最適です。","ko":"클라우드 코드 에이전트에서 무중단 세션 연속성 및 상태 캡처가 필요한 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de código Claude que necesitan una continuidad de sesión sin problemas y captura de estado.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de code Claude nécessitant une continuité de session sans interruption et une capture d''état.","de":"Perfekt für Claude-Code-Agents, die eine nahtlose Sitzungsfortsetzung und Zustandserfassung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes Claude Code que necessitam de continuidade de sessão sem interrupções e captura de estado.","ru":"Идеально для агентов Claude Code, которым требуется бесперебойная непрерывность сеанса и захват состояния.","ar":"مثالي لعميل Claude Code الذي يحتاج إلى استمرار دقيق للجلسة و_capture الحالة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create structured documents for effortless handoffs across sessions, utilizing protocols like session state assessment and phase identification, enabling continuity in exploration, planning, implementation, debugging, and review phases.","zh":"赋予代理创建结构化文档的能力，以便在会话之间实现无缝交接，利用会话状态评估和阶段识别等协议，实现探索、规划、实施、调试和审查阶段的连续性。","ja":"エージェントが構造化ドキュメントを作成できるようにし、セッション間の手順を容易にすることで、セッション状態評価や段階識別などのプロトコルを利用して、探索、計画、実装、デバッグ、レビュー段階の連続性を実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 구조화된 문서를 생성하여 세션 간의 손쉬운 인계를 가능하게 하며, 세션 상태 평가 및 단계 식별과 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 탐색, 계획, 구현, 디버깅 및 검토 단계의 연속성을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear documentos estructurados para una entrega sin esfuerzo entre sesiones, utilizando protocolos como evaluación del estado de la sesión e identificación de fases, lo que permite la continuidad en las fases de exploración, planificación, implementación, depuración y revisión.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des documents structurés pour des passes sans effort entre les sessions, en utilisant des protocoles tels que l''évaluation de l''état de la session et l''identification de phases, permettant la continuité dans les phases d''exploration, de planification, de mise en œuvre, de débogage et d''examen.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, strukturierte Dokumente für eine mühelose Übergabe zwischen Sitzungen zu erstellen, indem Protokolle wie Sitzungsstatusbewertung und Phasenidentifizierung verwendet werden, wodurch die Kontinuität in den Phasen der Exploration, Planung, Implementierung, Fehlersuche und Überprüfung ermöglicht wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar documentos estruturados para entregas sem esforço entre as sessões, utilizando protocolos como avaliação do estado 